msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/demonstratedByCompetency|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Names the competency question that pins a gmeow:FlagshipScenario's structure, referenced by IRI (a gmeow:CompetencyQuestion). The competency-question individual lives in the slice's tests/competency.ttl, so this reference is resolved and its gmeow:cqExpectRow expectation confirmed by the native flagship cross-check rather than by SHACL, which never loads the tests dataset."
msgstr "命名固定某个 gmeow:FlagshipScenario 结构的能力问题，通过 IRI 引用（一个 gmeow:CompetencyQuestion）。该能力问题个体位于切片的 tests/competency.ttl 文件中，因此此引用会被解析，其 gmeow:cqExpectRow 预期由原生旗舰交叉核对来确认，而非由从不加载测试数据集的 SHACL 来确认。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/demonstratedByCompetency|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exa:e8Symmetry gmeow:demonstratedByCompetency cq:cqE8RootSystem ."
msgstr "示例：exa:e8Symmetry gmeow:demonstratedByCompetency cq:cqE8RootSystem ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/demonstratedByExample|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Names the worked example that realizes a gmeow:FlagshipScenario, as a SLICE-RELATIVE path string (the same base as gmeow:exampleFile). The referenced *.ttl is the concrete artifact a reader inspects to see the scenario built, and the execution-discharge harness validates it clean."
msgstr "命名实现某个 gmeow:FlagshipScenario 的示例，以切片相对路径字符串形式给出（与 gmeow:exampleFile 相同的基准）。被引用的 *.ttl 是读者查看以看到场景构建过程的具体工件，执行清偿框架会将其验证为干净。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/demonstratedByExample|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exa:e8Symmetry gmeow:demonstratedByExample \"examples/e8-symmetry.ttl\" ."
msgstr "示例：exa:e8Symmetry gmeow:demonstratedByExample \"examples/e8-symmetry.ttl\" ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/demonstratedByProducer|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Names the native producer entrypoint that emits a gmeow:FlagshipScenario's output, as a path-like identifier string (e.g. math::producers::e8_weyl_order, pipeline::stages::lang_form::build_corpus). REQUIRED on every gmeow:FlagshipScenario: a scenario carries this binding if and only if the execution-discharge harness actually runs that producer and pins its output — the acceptance bar is discharged by execution, never by an unrun label."
msgstr "命名发出某个 gmeow:FlagshipScenario 输出的原生生产者入口点，以类似路径的标识符字符串形式给出（例如 math::producers::e8_weyl_order、pipeline::stages::lang_form::build_corpus）。在每个 gmeow:FlagshipScenario 上均为必需：当且仅当执行清偿框架实际运行该生产者并固定其输出时，场景才携带此绑定——验收标准由执行来清偿，绝不由未运行的标签来清偿。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/demonstratedByProducer|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exa:e8Symmetry gmeow:demonstratedByProducer \"math::producers::e8_weyl_order\" ."
msgstr "示例：exa:e8Symmetry gmeow:demonstratedByProducer \"math::producers::e8_weyl_order\" ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/enforcesFailureClass|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Links a gate — a SHACL shape or a gmeow:FlagshipScenario — to the conformance-failure subclass it enforces, so the machine-checked gate and the typed failure vocabulary are cross-referenced: a query can move from a gate to the named failure it raises and back. Carried on a SHACL shape (the shape enforcing that failure) or on a gmeow:FlagshipScenario (the failure its guarding counter-example must raise). An annotation property, never a reasoned axiom; its value is a slice-local <Slice>ConformanceFailure subclass."
msgstr "将一个门（一个 SHACL 形状或一个 gmeow:FlagshipScenario）链接到它所强制执行的一致性失败子类，使机器核对的门与类型化的失败词汇相互交叉引用：查询可从门移动到它所引发的具名失败并返回。它承载于 SHACL 形状（强制该失败的形状）上，或承载于 gmeow:FlagshipScenario（其守护性反例必须引发的失败）上。它是一个注解属性，绝非推理公理；其值是切片本地的 <Slice>ConformanceFailure 子类。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/enforcesFailureClass|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "math:UnsituatedNumberShape gmeow:enforcesFailureClass math:UnsituatedNumber ."
msgstr "示例：math:UnsituatedNumberShape gmeow:enforcesFailureClass math:UnsituatedNumber ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/FlagshipScenario|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A typed acceptance-manifest object reifying one of a grounding slice's flagship acceptance scenarios — its depth bar. Each gmeow:FlagshipScenario binds one scenario to the artifacts that realize and enforce it: the worked example (gmeow:demonstratedByExample), the competency question that pins its structure (gmeow:demonstratedByCompetency), the native producer that emits its output (gmeow:demonstratedByProducer), the counter-example that proves its gate bites (gmeow:guardedByCounterExample), and the named conformance-failure subclass that gate raises (gmeow:enforcesFailureClass). A scenario missing its example, competency, producer, counter-example, or enforcing class, or naming an enforcing class that is not one of the owning slice's conformance-failure subclasses, is unwired and ill-formed (gmeow:UnwiredFlagshipScenario)."
msgstr "一个类型化的验收清单对象，将某个接地切片的旗舰验收场景之一——它的深度标准——予以具体化。每个 gmeow:FlagshipScenario 将一个场景绑定到实现并强制它的工件：示例（gmeow:demonstratedByExample）、固定其结构的能力问题（gmeow:demonstratedByCompetency）、发出其输出的原生生产者（gmeow:demonstratedByProducer）、证明其门有效咬合的反例（gmeow:guardedByCounterExample），以及该门所引发的具名一致性失败子类（gmeow:enforcesFailureClass）。凡缺少其示例、能力、生产者、反例或强制类的场景，或所命名的强制类不属于所属切片一致性失败子类之一的场景，都是未接线且格式错误的（gmeow:UnwiredFlagshipScenario）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/FlagshipScenario|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exa:e8Symmetry a gmeow:FlagshipScenario ; gmeow:demonstratedByExample \"examples/e8-symmetry.ttl\" ; gmeow:demonstratedByCompetency cq:cqE8RootSystem ; gmeow:demonstratedByProducer \"math::producers::e8_weyl_order\" ; gmeow:guardedByCounterExample \"tests/counter-examples/e8-wrong-weyl-order.ttl\" ; gmeow:enforcesFailureClass math:WrongE8WeylOrder ."
msgstr "示例：exa:e8Symmetry a gmeow:FlagshipScenario ; gmeow:demonstratedByExample \"examples/e8-symmetry.ttl\" ; gmeow:demonstratedByCompetency cq:cqE8RootSystem ; gmeow:demonstratedByProducer \"math::producers::e8_weyl_order\" ; gmeow:guardedByCounterExample \"tests/counter-examples/e8-wrong-weyl-order.ttl\" ; gmeow:enforcesFailureClass math:WrongE8WeylOrder ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/FlagshipScenarioWiringConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A closed-world integrity constraint: every gmeow:FlagshipScenario binds at least one worked example, competency question, native producer, counter-example, and enforcing failure class. An acceptance scenario missing any realizing/enforcing artifact is unwired (gmeow:UnwiredFlagshipScenario)."
msgstr "一个闭世界完整性约束：每个 gmeow:FlagshipScenario 至少绑定一个示例、一个能力问题、一个原生生产者、一个反例以及一个强制失败类。缺少任何实现/强制工件的验收场景即为未接线（gmeow:UnwiredFlagshipScenario）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/GmeowClassCompletenessConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A closed-world integrity constraint: every gmeow:-namespaced owl:Class carries at least one rdfs:label, one skos:definition, one rdfs:isDefinedBy, and one gmeow:graphBoxRole."
msgstr "一个闭世界完整性约束：gmeow: 命名空间下的每个 owl:Class 至少携带一个 rdfs:label、一个 skos:definition、一个 rdfs:isDefinedBy 以及一个 gmeow:graphBoxRole。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/GmeowDatatypeCompletenessConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A closed-world integrity constraint: every gmeow:-namespaced rdfs:Datatype carries at least one rdfs:label, one skos:definition, one rdfs:isDefinedBy, and one gmeow:graphBoxRole."
msgstr "一个闭世界完整性约束：gmeow: 命名空间下的每个 rdfs:Datatype 至少携带一个 rdfs:label、一个 skos:definition、一个 rdfs:isDefinedBy 以及一个 gmeow:graphBoxRole。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/GmeowInternalLanguageTagConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A closed-world integrity constraint: every language-tagged literal object of a gmeow:-namespaced predicate must carry a language tag under the private-use x-gmeow-* prefix (case-insensitive ^x-gmeow-[a-z0-9-]+$). Introspects the value's language tag via logic:termHasLang and logic:termLangMatches so the repo-wide localizable-prose convention is enforced by the logic: core, not a hand-authored shape surface."
msgstr "一个闭世界完整性约束：gmeow: 命名空间谓词的每个带语言标签的字面量对象都必须在私有用途 x-gmeow-* 前缀下携带语言标签（不区分大小写，^x-gmeow-[a-z0-9-]+$）。它通过 logic:termHasLang 与 logic:termLangMatches 内省该值的语言标签，使整个仓库范围的可本地化散文约定由 logic: 核心强制执行，而非由手工编写的形状表面执行。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/GmeowOntologyCompletenessConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A closed-world integrity constraint: every gmeow:-namespaced owl:Ontology header carries at least one rdfs:label, one skos:definition, one rdfs:isDefinedBy, and one gmeow:graphBoxRole."
msgstr "一个闭世界完整性约束：gmeow: 命名空间下的每个 owl:Ontology 头部至少携带一个 rdfs:label、一个 skos:definition、一个 rdfs:isDefinedBy 以及一个 gmeow:graphBoxRole。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/GmeowPropertyCompletenessConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A closed-world integrity constraint: every gmeow:-namespaced owl object/datatype/annotation property carries at least one rdfs:label, one skos:definition, one rdfs:isDefinedBy, and one gmeow:graphBoxRole."
msgstr "一个闭世界完整性约束：gmeow: 命名空间下的每个 owl 对象/数据/注解属性至少携带一个 rdfs:label、一个 skos:definition、一个 rdfs:isDefinedBy 以及一个 gmeow:graphBoxRole。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/guardedByCounterExample|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Names the counter-example that proves a gmeow:FlagshipScenario's gate bites, as a SLICE-RELATIVE path string. The referenced tests/counter-examples/*.ttl is the minimal violation that raises the scenario's gmeow:enforcesFailureClass; per the conformance discipline, a rule with no negative fixture is not considered enforced, and the execution-discharge harness runs the fixture and confirms exactly that class fires."
msgstr "命名证明某个 gmeow:FlagshipScenario 的门有效咬合的反例，以切片相对路径字符串形式给出。被引用的 tests/counter-examples/*.ttl 是引发该场景 gmeow:enforcesFailureClass 的最小违例；依据一致性纪律，没有负向夹具的规则不被视为已强制执行，执行清偿框架会运行该夹具并确认恰好是该类被触发。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/guardedByCounterExample|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "exa:e8Symmetry gmeow:guardedByCounterExample \"tests/counter-examples/e8-wrong-weyl-order.ttl\" ."
msgstr "示例：exa:e8Symmetry gmeow:guardedByCounterExample \"tests/counter-examples/e8-wrong-weyl-order.ttl\" ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment"
msgid "Foundation vocabulary for GMEOW Logic. The logic: namespace <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> is the canonical reasoning surface; its terms are declared standalone (no gUFO stereotypes, no rdfs:subClassOf into gmeow: reasoned classes) so the gUFO projection can be generated from them rather than the reverse. The rules, solver, profile machinery, and conformance corpus are minted as the native engine lands; this module mints the term surface."
msgstr "GMEOW Logic 的基础词汇表。logic: 命名空间 <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> 是规范的推理面；其词项以独立方式声明（无 gUFO 构造型，无指向 gmeow: 已推理类的 rdfs:subClassOf），以便可由它们生成 gUFO 投影，而非反向生成。随着原生引擎落地，规则、求解器、配置文件机制以及合规语料库将逐一铸造；本模块铸造词项面。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The GMEOW Logic module — home of the `logic:` reasoning vocabulary. It declares the canonical UFO⁺ foundation (the foundational sorts and relations authored in `logic:`, of which gUFO is a generated down-projection), the semantic profiles every rule set must declare, the world/modal terms, the four distinct quantitative axes (probability, confidence, weight, evidence), and the preservation-polarity vocabulary of the loss ledger. The `logic:` namespace is the canonical foundation; OWL, Datalog, SHACL, Prolog, N3, and the gUFO/BFO/DOLCE upper ontologies are its generated lossy projections (Principle 17). `logic:` terms are STANDALONE: they carry no gUFO parentage, because gUFO is a projection of `logic:`, not its ground. The normative semantics are in `design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md`; the preservation contract is in `design/LOGIC-CONFORMANCE.md`."
msgstr "GMEOW 逻辑模块——`logic:` 推理词汇的所在地。它声明了规范的 UFO⁺ 基础（用 `logic:` 编写的基础种类与关系，gUFO 是其生成的下投影）、每个规则集都必须声明的语义配置、世界/模态词项、四个不同的量化轴（概率、置信度、权重、证据），以及损失账簿的保持极性词汇。`logic:` 命名空间是规范基础；OWL、Datalog、SHACL、Prolog、N3 以及 gUFO/BFO/DOLCE 上层本体都是它生成的有损投影（原则 17）。`logic:` 词项是独立的：它们不携带任何 gUFO 血统，因为 gUFO 是 `logic:` 的投影，而非其根基。规范语义见 `design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md`；保持契约见 `design/LOGIC-CONFORMANCE.md`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/UnwiredFlagshipScenario|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The shared abstract failure class for a gmeow:FlagshipScenario that is not fully wired: it is missing its worked example (gmeow:demonstratedByExample), competency question (gmeow:demonstratedByCompetency), producer (gmeow:demonstratedByProducer), counter-example (gmeow:guardedByCounterExample), or enforcing failure class (gmeow:enforcesFailureClass); or the class it names as enforcing is not one of the owning slice's conformance-failure subclasses. The depth bar is a contract, not a suggestion: an acceptance scenario that does not bind all realizing/enforcing artifacts cannot claim the scenario is met. Each grounding slice's own <Slice>UnwiredFlagshipScenario subclasses ONLY its slice-local <Slice>ConformanceFailure root (never this spec-layer marker, which is never a subclass target); unwired-detection is instead enforced UNIFORMLY across every slice by the shared gmeow:FlagshipScenarioShape, which carries gmeow:enforcesFailureClass gmeow:UnwiredFlagshipScenario, cross-referencing this shared name with the gate that raises it."
msgstr "为未完全接线的 gmeow:FlagshipScenario 提供的共享抽象失败类：它缺少其示例（gmeow:demonstratedByExample）、能力问题（gmeow:demonstratedByCompetency）、生产者（gmeow:demonstratedByProducer）、反例（gmeow:guardedByCounterExample）或强制失败类（gmeow:enforcesFailureClass）；或者它命名为强制的类不属于所属切片一致性失败子类之一。深度标准是契约而非建议：未绑定所有实现/强制工件的验收场景不能声称该场景已满足。每个接地切片各自的 <Slice>UnwiredFlagshipScenario 仅派生自其切片本地的 <Slice>ConformanceFailure 根（绝不派生自这个规范层标记，该标记永不作为子类目标）；未接线检测转而由共享的 gmeow:FlagshipScenarioShape 在每个切片间统一强制执行，它携带 gmeow:enforcesFailureClass gmeow:UnwiredFlagshipScenario，将这个共享名称与引发它的门交叉引用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/UnwiredFlagshipScenario|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "gmeow:FlagshipScenarioShape gmeow:enforcesFailureClass gmeow:UnwiredFlagshipScenario ."
msgstr "示例：gmeow:FlagshipScenarioShape gmeow:enforcesFailureClass gmeow:UnwiredFlagshipScenario ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AbstractIndividual|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "An individual that exists outside spacetime and bears no qualities — a number, a set, a value structure — neither enduring nor perduring nor inhering. The counterpart of gufo:AbstractIndividual; the abstract sibling of the concrete (endurant/perdurant) individuals. Quality values live here (stated in prose, not as a subclass edge)."
msgstr "一个存在于时空之外且不承载任何性质的个体——一个数、一个集合、一个值结构——既不持续存在，也不延展存在，也不内属。它是 gufo:AbstractIndividual 的对应物；是具体（持续体/延展体）个体的抽象同胞。性质值居于此处（以散文表述，而非作为子类边）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AbstractIndividualType|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A logic:Type whose instances are logic:AbstractIndividuals — the type whose extension (via logic:instanceOf) is drawn from individuals outside spacetime (numbers, sets, logic:QualityValues). The counterpart of gufo:AbstractIndividualType. Stated in prose, not as a subclass edge. Contrast logic:ConcreteIndividualType, whose instances are located in spacetime."
msgstr "一个 logic:Type，其实例是 logic:AbstractIndividuals——该类型的外延（经由 logic:instanceOf）取自时空之外的个体（数、集合、logic:QualityValues）。它是 gufo:AbstractIndividualType 的对应物。以散文表述，而非作为子类边。与 logic:ConcreteIndividualType 相对照，后者的实例位于时空之中。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/accessibleFrom|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The generic Kripke accessibility abstraction between worlds: relates a world to a world from which it is reachable, generalizing the standpoint sharpening poset. It exists for uniform traversal and provenance, not for inference — the modal operators are NOT translated over this bare relation. Necessity and possibility are evaluated over the appropriate named, typed accessibility relation (necessity is truth in every accessible context of that type, possibility truth in some), never over the blurred union of all of them. That evaluation is bounded universal quantification because the world set is the finite, materialized contextual index, not the unbounded space of all logically possible worlds. logic:accessibleFrom is the generic superproperty of the six typed accessibility relations — logic:epistemicallyPossible, logic:doxasticallyAccessible, logic:deonticallyIdeal, logic:temporallySucceeds, logic:counterfactuallyCloser, and gmeow:sharpens — but only in prose: these are NOT asserted rdfs:subPropertyOf it, because the generic superproperty licenses no cross-type entailment by itself. An inference may follow a named, typed accessibility relation; it may not conclude anything by walking the bare superproperty across contexts of different types. The one pre-existing typed sub-relation, gmeow:sharpens, carries owl:TransitiveProperty in the standpoint slice, while the five logic: kernel relations assert no OWL characteristics and document their logical character in prose — an intentional asymmetry, not an oversight."
msgstr "世界之间通用的 Kripke 可达性抽象：将一个世界关联到可从中到达它的世界，推广了立场锐化偏序集。它的存在是为了统一遍历与溯源，而非为了推理——模态算子并不在这条裸关系上翻译。必然性与可能性是在恰当的具名、类型化可达性关系上求值的（必然性是在该类型的每个可达语境中为真，可能性是在某个可达语境中为真），绝不在所有关系的模糊并集上求值。该求值是有界全称量化，因为世界集是有限的、已物化的语境索引，而非所有逻辑可能世界的无界空间。logic:accessibleFrom 是六个类型化可达性关系——logic:epistemicallyPossible、logic:doxasticallyAccessible、logic:deonticallyIdeal、logic:temporallySucceeds、logic:counterfactuallyCloser 与 gmeow:sharpens——的通用超属性，但仅在散文层面：这些关系并未被声明为它的 rdfs:subPropertyOf，因为通用超属性本身不授予任何跨类型蕴涵。推理可以沿一条具名、类型化可达性关系前进；它不可通过在不同类型的语境间行走裸超属性而得出任何结论。唯一预先存在的类型化子关系 gmeow:sharpens 在立场切片中携带 owl:TransitiveProperty，而五个 logic: 内核关系不声明任何 OWL 特征，并在散文中记录其逻辑特性——这是有意的不对称，而非疏漏。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AchievementGoal|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:GoalExpressionKind for a goal satisfied once its logic:boundSituationType FIRST obtains at any state along the logic:Path — a one-shot attainment. Contrast logic:MaintenanceGoal (must hold at every state)."
msgstr "用于以下目标的 logic:GoalExpressionKind：一旦其 logic:boundSituationType 沿着 logic:Path 在任一状态首次成立，该目标即得满足——一次性达成。与 logic:MaintenanceGoal 相对照（其必须在每个状态成立）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/actionResource|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ActionSchema to what the action consumes or requires — the seam to the resource-competing goal conflict (logic:competesForResource), where two goals draw on a resource an action schema declares and the supply is insufficient for both. Domain logic:ActionSchema (stated in prose). One of the eight action-theory facets. DISTINCT from logic:resourcePolicy, which is a ReasoningContract→ResourcePolicy engine-budget property — a different concept that must not be conflated with an action's consumable resource."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ActionSchema 关联到该动作所消耗或所需之物——通向资源竞争型目标冲突（logic:competesForResource）的接缝，其中两个目标取用某动作模式所声明的一种资源，而供给不足以同时满足两者。定义域 logic:ActionSchema（以散文表述）。它是八个动作理论侧面之一。它与 logic:resourcePolicy 相区别，后者是 ReasoningContract→ResourcePolicy 的引擎预算属性——一个不同的概念，不可与动作的可消耗资源混为一谈。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ActionSchema|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A named precondition / effect / invariant template that a transaction program may invoke: the reusable unit of state change. Distinct from the concrete transaction program that instantiates it, so a reusable schema is never conflated with a single state-changing run. Punned (OWL 2 DL metamodelling): it is simultaneously the IR node kind AND the class whose instances are specific reusable action schemas — an action occurrence is a gmeow:Event that instantiates one such schema through logic:instantiatesSchema. The structure means–end reasoning reads is declared on a schema by the eight action-theory facets: logic:precondition, logic:effect, logic:invariant, logic:capability, logic:nondeterministicOutcome, logic:observation, logic:compensation, and logic:actionResource."
msgstr "一个具名的前置条件/效果/不变式模板，事务程序可以调用它：状态变更的可复用单元。它区别于实例化它的具体事务程序，因此可复用模式绝不与单次的状态变更运行混为一谈。它带有双关（OWL 2 DL 元建模）：它同时是 IR 节点种类，也是其实例为特定可复用动作模式的类——一次动作发生是一个 gmeow:Event，通过 logic:instantiatesSchema 实例化一个这样的模式。手段-目的推理所读取的结构由八个动作理论侧面在模式上声明：logic:precondition、logic:effect、logic:invariant、logic:capability、logic:nondeterministicOutcome、logic:observation、logic:compensation 与 logic:actionResource。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/activationBasis|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:GovernanceRegime to a constrained state it activates as binding: the regime holds that a logic:DownwardConstraint whose logic:constraintState is this value binds its target (logic:ConstraintBinding) rather than lapsing to logic:ConstraintUnknown. The carrier that makes governance regime-relative — a state in one regime's activation basis and absent from another's receives opposite verdicts with no contradiction. Without a matching basis entry, a constraint over that state is logic:ConstraintUnknown under the regime. The governance analogue of logic:reductionBasis (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "将一个 logic:GovernanceRegime 关联到它激活为具约束力的一个受约束状态：该体制认为，其 logic:constraintState 为此值的 logic:DownwardConstraint 会约束其目标（logic:ConstraintBinding），而不会退化为 logic:ConstraintUnknown。这是使治理相对于体制的载体——某状态若存在于一个体制的激活基础中而缺席于另一个体制的激活基础，则会收到相反的裁决而不构成矛盾。若无匹配的基础条目，则在该体制下针对该状态的约束为 logic:ConstraintUnknown。它是 logic:reductionBasis 的治理类比物（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons 一节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/activeInState|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a support/reified assertion to the path state in which that support was active. The transition oracle uses it to keep retired supports auditable: a `del` records the predecessor state where the support held, then advances to a successor where that support no longer holds."
msgstr "将一个支撑/具体化断言关联到该支撑处于活跃状态的路径状态。转移预言机用它来保持已退役支撑的可审计性：一个 `del` 记录支撑成立的前驱状态，然后前进到该支撑不再成立的后继状态。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/acyclicProperty|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic: property-characteristic marker for acyclicity: a property P whose transitive closure P+ is irreflexive — P(a₁,a₂) ∧ … ∧ P(aₙ,a₁) holds for no chain, so following P never returns to its start. Stronger than logic:irreflexiveProperty (which forbids only the one-step P(a,a)) yet distinct from logic:transitiveProperty ∧ logic:irreflexiveProperty: an acyclic P is deliberately NOT transitive (its successors are the immediate steps, not every reachable node), so the characteristic is enforced by the native coherence gate's internal reachability walk rather than by materialising the closure. Marks a stepwise chain such as gmeow:linkNext that must never cycle."
msgstr "表示无环性的 logic: 属性特征标记：一个属性 P，其传递闭包 P+ 是非自反的——P(a₁,a₂) ∧ … ∧ P(aₙ,a₁) 对任何链都不成立，因此沿 P 前进绝不返回其起点。它比 logic:irreflexiveProperty 更强（后者仅禁止单步 P(a,a)），却又与 logic:transitiveProperty ∧ logic:irreflexiveProperty 相区别：无环的 P 是有意不传递的（其后继是直接步，而非每个可达节点），因此该特征由原生一致性门的内部可达性行走来强制执行，而非通过物化闭包。它标记诸如 gmeow:linkNext 这类绝不可成环的逐步链。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AdmissibleValuationPolicy|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The facet value class of the admissible-valuation (gap/glut) policy: which of the four Belnap values a valuation is ALLOWED to assign. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract. Forbidding the gap, the glut, or both carves the classic sub-logics out of the same logic:BelnapBilattice algebra — it is a FORMAL ERROR to reduce the FDE↔LP difference to the designated-value set, because the two differ precisely in this admissible-valuation set, not in their designated values."
msgstr "可容许赋值（间隙/过盈）策略的侧面值类：赋值被允许指派四个 Belnap 值中的哪些。在 ReasoningContract 上单值。禁止间隙、禁止过盈或两者兼禁，可从同一个 logic:BelnapBilattice 代数中切出经典的子逻辑——将 FDE↔LP 的差异归约到指定值集合是一个形式错误，因为二者恰恰在这个可容许赋值集合上不同，而非在其指定值上不同。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/admissibleValuation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to the logic:AdmissibleValuationPolicy it selects — the gap/glut policy fixing which Belnap values a valuation may assign. Single-valued on the contract. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:AdmissibleValuationPolicy (stated here in prose, matching the module's domain/range convention). It is one of the three independent truth-facet components and must not be conflated with logic:designatedValues."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ReasoningContract 关联到它所选择的 logic:AdmissibleValuationPolicy——确定赋值可指派哪些 Belnap 值的间隙/过盈策略。在契约上单值。定义域 logic:ReasoningContract，值域 logic:AdmissibleValuationPolicy（此处以散文表述，与模块的定义域/值域约定一致）。它是三个独立的真值侧面组件之一，不可与 logic:designatedValues 混为一谈。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AdmitAllFour|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The admissible-valuation policy that permits all four Belnap values — true, false, both (glut), and neither (gap). It carves out First-Degree Entailment (FDE): a valuation may leave an atom under-determined (gap) or over-determined (glut). Reducing the FDE↔LP difference to the designated-value set is a formal error — FDE differs from LP by admitting the gap, not by its designated values."
msgstr "允许全部四个 Belnap 值的可容许赋值策略——真、假、两者（过盈）与皆非（间隙）。它切出一阶蕴涵（FDE）：赋值可将某原子留为欠定（间隙）或超定（过盈）。将 FDE↔LP 的差异归约到指定值集合是形式错误——FDE 与 LP 的区别在于容许间隙，而非在于其指定值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AffineCorrespondence|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A co-projection onto a shared component: the 'similar but not quite' alignment, where source and view agree on a common part but neither embeds in the other. The companion of logic:Prism in the partial-alignment band — a Prism focuses an optional variant, an affine correspondence focuses a shared sub-structure. The correct rung for a logic:Vague logic:Determinacy target, NOT a low-confidence logic:Equiv. Caps: laws on the shared component only."
msgstr "对共享组件的余投影：即“相似但不尽然”的对齐，其中源与视图在一个共同部分上一致，但两者都不嵌入对方。它是 logic:Prism 在部分对齐带中的伙伴——Prism 聚焦一个可选变体，仿射对应聚焦一个共享子结构。它是 logic:Vague logic:Determinacy 目标的正确档位，而非低置信度的 logic:Equiv。上限：定律仅作用于共享组件之上。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AgencyAssessment|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The canonical relational construct of holonic agency: a four-valued assessment of whether a holon exhibits Koestler's two co-equal Janus tendencies — self-assertive (autonomy, as a whole) and integrative (subordination, as a part) — always made relative to a declared logic:HolonicAgencyProfile. Holon integrity is assessed, never asserted — the assessment is reified with the role properties logic:agencyHolon and logic:agencyProfile, and the engine derives its logic:agencyVerdict (logic:HolonIntegral, logic:AutonomyDeficient, logic:IntegrationDeficient, or logic:AgencyUnknown). The two pathologies are the collapse of one tendency: a 'part' with no autonomy (logic:AutonomyDeficient) and a 'whole' that refuses to integrate (logic:IntegrationDeficient); integrity is both present, and neither face is privileged over the other (Principle 9). The convenient unary reading 'this holon is integral' is the lossy projection of this assessment, exactly as logic:Holon projects logic:HolonicPosition and logic:EmergenceAssessment carries emergence (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "全子（holon）能动性的规范关系构造：一个四值评估，判断某全子是否展现 Koestler 的两个同等的 Janus 双面倾向——自我肯定（作为整体的自主性）与整合（作为部分的从属）——始终相对于一个已声明的 logic:HolonicAgencyProfile 作出。全子完整性是被评估的，绝不被断言——该评估通过角色属性 logic:agencyHolon 与 logic:agencyProfile 予以具体化，引擎据此导出其 logic:agencyVerdict（logic:HolonIntegral、logic:AutonomyDeficient、logic:IntegrationDeficient 或 logic:AgencyUnknown）。两种病态是某一倾向的坍缩：无自主性的“部分”（logic:AutonomyDeficient）与拒绝整合的“整体”（logic:IntegrationDeficient）；完整性是两者皆在，且任一面都不优先于另一面（原则 9）。便利的一元读法“这个全子是完整的”是该评估的有损投影，恰如 logic:Holon 投影 logic:HolonicPosition、logic:EmergenceAssessment 承载涌现（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons 一节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/agencyHolon|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The holon role of an logic:AgencyAssessment: the entity whose Janus-faced holonic agency is being assessed — the holon that bears (logic:bearsProperty) the self-assertive and integrative values the profile reasons over. One of the two role properties (with logic:agencyProfile) that reify the agency-assessment relation onto the arity-bounded reasoning surface, mirroring logic:assessmentWhole and the logic:HolonicPosition role properties. It is also a well-formedness existence guard: every verdict rule re-binds it, so a malformed assessment naming no holon receives no verdict (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "一个 logic:AgencyAssessment 的全子角色：其 Janus 双面全子能动性正被评估的实体——承载（logic:bearsProperty）配置所据以推理的自我肯定值与整合值的全子。它是将能动性评估关系具体化到有界元数推理表面上的两个角色属性之一（另一个是 logic:agencyProfile），映照 logic:assessmentWhole 与 logic:HolonicPosition 的角色属性。它同时是良构性存在守卫：每条裁决规则都会重新绑定它，因此未命名任何全子的畸形评估不会收到任何裁决（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons 一节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/agencyProfile|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The profile role of an logic:AgencyAssessment: the logic:HolonicAgencyProfile the assessment is relative to. Holonic agency is never absolute — the verdict (logic:HolonIntegral / logic:AutonomyDeficient / logic:IntegrationDeficient / logic:AgencyUnknown) is read only against this declared profile's logic:selfAssertiveBasis and logic:integrativeBasis. An assessment that omits this role, or whose profile declares no basis at all, cannot evidence either tendency and receives logic:AgencyUnknown. One of the two role properties (with logic:agencyHolon) that reify the agency-assessment relation, mirroring logic:assessmentReductionTheory and logic:constraintRegime (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "一个 logic:AgencyAssessment 的配置角色：该评估所相对的 logic:HolonicAgencyProfile。全子能动性从不是绝对的——裁决（logic:HolonIntegral / logic:AutonomyDeficient / logic:IntegrationDeficient / logic:AgencyUnknown）只针对这个已声明配置的 logic:selfAssertiveBasis 与 logic:integrativeBasis 来读取。省略此角色的评估，或其配置根本未声明任何基础的评估，无法为两种倾向中的任何一种提供证据，故收到 logic:AgencyUnknown。它是将能动性评估关系具体化的两个角色属性之一（另一个是 logic:agencyHolon），映照 logic:assessmentReductionTheory 与 logic:constraintRegime（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons 一节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AgencyUnknown|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The agency-verdict value when neither Janus tendency is evidenced: under the declared logic:HolonicAgencyProfile, the assessed holon bears neither an logic:selfAssertiveBasis value nor an logic:integrativeBasis value, so neither the self-assertive nor the integrative marker can fire and the integrity question has no positive footing. This subsumes the 'cannot pose the question' case: it fires both when the holon bears no basis value and when the profile declares no basis at all (no marker can derive). The first-class fourth value, kept distinct from the two pathologies so that a holon evidencing neither tendency is never silently read as a deficiency of one — failure-to-evidence is not integrity, and a basis-free profile is unknown, not deficient. Mirrors logic:EmergenceUnknown and logic:ConstraintUnknown (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "当两个 Janus 倾向都未获证据时的能动性裁决值：在已声明的 logic:HolonicAgencyProfile 下，被评估的全子既不承载 logic:selfAssertiveBasis 值也不承载 logic:integrativeBasis 值，因此自我肯定标记与整合标记都无法触发，完整性问题没有任何正面立足点。它涵盖“无法提出该问题”的情形：既在全子不承载任何基础值时触发，也在配置根本未声明任何基础时触发（没有任何标记能够导出）。作为头等的第四值，它与两种病态保持区分，从而使不为任何倾向提供证据的全子绝不被默默读作某一倾向的缺陷——未能提供证据不等于完整性，而无基础的配置是未知而非缺陷。它映照 logic:EmergenceUnknown 与 logic:ConstraintUnknown（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons 一节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AgencyVerdict|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The closed class of holonic-agency outcomes: the four-valued result an logic:AgencyAssessment receives via logic:agencyVerdict. Its four named individuals are logic:HolonIntegral (both Janus tendencies present), logic:AutonomyDeficient (a 'part' with no autonomy), logic:IntegrationDeficient (a 'whole' refusing to integrate), and logic:AgencyUnknown (neither tendency evidenced, so the integrity question has no positive footing). The set is closed, so a misspelt verdict names no declared value and is rejected rather than silently accepted, mirroring logic:EmergenceVerdict and logic:ConstraintVerdict (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "全子能动性结果的封闭类：一个 logic:AgencyAssessment 经由 logic:agencyVerdict 收到的四值结果。它的四个具名个体是 logic:HolonIntegral（两个 Janus 倾向皆在）、logic:AutonomyDeficient（无自主性的“部分”）、logic:IntegrationDeficient（拒绝整合的“整体”）与 logic:AgencyUnknown（无任何倾向获证据，故完整性问题没有正面立足点）。该集合是封闭的，因此拼写错误的裁决命名不到任何已声明的值，会被拒绝而非默默接受，映照 logic:EmergenceVerdict 与 logic:ConstraintVerdict（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons 一节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/agencyVerdict|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The engine-derived outcome of an logic:AgencyAssessment: the four-valued logic:AgencyVerdict (logic:HolonIntegral, logic:AutonomyDeficient, logic:IntegrationDeficient, or logic:AgencyUnknown) the foundation lowering entails for it. Never asserted by hand — it is computed by the stratified agency rules from the assessment's holon and declared logic:HolonicAgencyProfile, the convenient OWL-projectable surface of the assessment exactly as logic:assessmentVerdict is for emergence and logic:constraintVerdict for governance. The two pathology values are reached by negation-as-failure over the two co-equal tendency markers, so each verdict is genuinely profile-relative rather than a bare default (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "一个 logic:AgencyAssessment 的引擎导出结果：基础降级为其蕴涵的四值 logic:AgencyVerdict（logic:HolonIntegral、logic:AutonomyDeficient、logic:IntegrationDeficient 或 logic:AgencyUnknown）。从不由人手断言——它由分层的能动性规则从评估的全子与已声明的 logic:HolonicAgencyProfile 计算得出，是评估的便利、可投影为 OWL 的表面，恰如 logic:assessmentVerdict 之于涌现、logic:constraintVerdict 之于治理。两个病态值通过对两个同等倾向标记的失败即否定而达到，因此每个裁决都真正相对于配置，而非一个赤裸的缺省值（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons 一节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/aggComparator|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The relational comparator of a logic:AggregateConstraint's invariant (=, !=, <, <=, >, >=; the Unicode ≠/≤/≥ are accepted). The projected sh:SPARQLConstraint HAVING uses the negation of this operator, because a sh:select returns the VIOLATING focus nodes."
msgstr "一个 logic:AggregateConstraint 不变式的关系比较符（=、!=、<、<=、>、>=；接受 Unicode 的 ≠/≤/≥）。所投影的 sh:SPARQLConstraint 的 HAVING 使用此运算符的否定，因为 sh:select 返回的是违例的焦点节点。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/aggCompareTo|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The right-hand side a logic:AggregateConstraint's aggregate is compared to: an IRI object is a compared PROPERTY of the focus ($this <prop> ?rhs), and a literal is a fixed comparison value."
msgstr "一个 logic:AggregateConstraint 的聚合所比较的右侧：IRI 对象是焦点的一个被比较属性（$this <prop> ?rhs），而字面量是一个固定的比较值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/aggDistinct|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Whether a logic:AggregateConstraint aggregates over DISTINCT values (COUNT(DISTINCT ?x)). Absent means false."
msgstr "一个 logic:AggregateConstraint 是否在去重（DISTINCT）值上聚合（COUNT(DISTINCT ?x)）。缺省即为假。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/aggFunction|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The aggregate function of a logic:AggregateConstraint (COUNT, SUM, MIN, MAX) applied over logic:aggPath. Distinct from logic:aggregateFunction, which carries a reduce RULE's head aggregation; this drives a constraint's GROUP BY/HAVING violation SELECT."
msgstr "一个 logic:AggregateConstraint 的聚合函数（COUNT、SUM、MIN、MAX），作用于 logic:aggPath。它区别于 logic:aggregateFunction（后者承载归约规则的头部聚合）；它驱动约束的 GROUP BY/HAVING 违例 SELECT。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/aggPath|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The predicate a logic:AggregateConstraint aggregates over the focus: the objects of $this <aggPath> ?x are the values logic:aggFunction is applied to."
msgstr "一个 logic:AggregateConstraint 在焦点上聚合的谓词：$this <aggPath> ?x 的对象即 logic:aggFunction 所作用的值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AggregateBalanceConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Compact sugar for a double-entry balance constraint: a logic:onClass target whose postings (logic:balancePostingPredicate) are partitioned by a partition predicate (logic:balancePartitionPredicate) into a debit side (logic:balanceDebitValue) and a credit side (logic:balanceCreditValue), each posting's numeric amount is read via logic:balanceAmountNodePredicate then logic:balanceValuePredicate, and the group key via logic:balanceAmountNodePredicate then logic:balanceGroupPredicate; within every group the two partition-sums must be EQUAL. Generalizes the single-aggregate logic:AggregateConstraint to a partitioned two-sum equality over a value-key group. Expands to a canonical logic:Constraint carrying an honest reified FOL integrity plus a structured balance satellite, lowered to a SELECT $this … GROUP BY $this ?group HAVING(sumDebits != sumCredits) sh:SPARQLConstraint. Frontend-only authoring shortcut."
msgstr "复式记账平衡约束的紧凑语法糖：一个 logic:onClass 目标，其分录（logic:balancePostingPredicate）由一个分区谓词（logic:balancePartitionPredicate）划分为借方（logic:balanceDebitValue）与贷方（logic:balanceCreditValue），每笔分录的数值金额经由 logic:balanceAmountNodePredicate 再经 logic:balanceValuePredicate 读取，组键经由 logic:balanceAmountNodePredicate 再经 logic:balanceGroupPredicate 读取；在每个组内，两个分区之和必须相等。它将单聚合的 logic:AggregateConstraint 推广为在值-键组上的分区双和相等。它展开为一个规范的 logic:Constraint，携带诚实的具体化 FOL 完整性外加一个结构化的平衡卫星，降级为一个 SELECT $this … GROUP BY ?group HAVING(sumDebits != sumCredits) 的 sh:SPARQLConstraint。仅为前端的编写捷径。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AggregateBalanceConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:entryBalances a logic:AggregateBalanceConstraint ; logic:onClass ex:JournalEntry ; logic:balancePostingPredicate ex:posting ; logic:balancePartitionPredicate ex:direction ; logic:balanceDebitValue ex:debit ; logic:balanceCreditValue ex:credit ; logic:balanceAmountNodePredicate ex:amount ; logic:balanceValuePredicate ex:value ; logic:balanceGroupPredicate ex:currency ."
msgstr "示例：ex:entryBalances a logic:AggregateBalanceConstraint ; logic:onClass ex:JournalEntry ; logic:balancePostingPredicate ex:posting ; logic:balancePartitionPredicate ex:direction ; logic:balanceDebitValue ex:debit ; logic:balanceCreditValue ex:credit ; logic:balanceAmountNodePredicate ex:amount ; logic:balanceValuePredicate ex:value ; logic:balanceGroupPredicate ex:currency ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/aggregateComparison|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The reified relation an expanded logic:AggregateConstraint carries as its honest FOL integrity: aggregateComparison(this, function, distinct, path, comparator, rhs). The realized FOL formula core has no aggregate node, so this predication makes the aggregate meaning complete in the FOL canon while the structured satellite drives the real GROUP BY/HAVING SPARQL projection."
msgstr "一个已展开的 logic:AggregateConstraint 作为其诚实 FOL 完整性所携带的具体化关系：aggregateComparison(this, function, distinct, path, comparator, rhs)。已实现的 FOL 公式核心没有聚合节点，因此这一谓述使聚合含义在 FOL 正典中完整，而结构化卫星则驱动真正的 GROUP BY/HAVING SPARQL 投影。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/aggregateFunction|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment"
msgid "Aggregate function of a reduce rule. Default-absent: an ordinary Horn rule carries no aggregation surface, so the existing corpus is byte-identical."
msgstr "归约规则的聚合函数。默认缺省：普通的 Horn 规则不携带任何聚合面，因此现有语料库在字节层面完全一致。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/aggregateFunction|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Names the aggregate function (SUM, COUNT, MIN, MAX, AVG) a logic:Rule applies in its reduce (aggregation) head: the rule binds logic:aggregateResult to this function applied to logic:aggregateVariable over the groups formed by logic:groupKey. This is the canonical logic: representation of the reduce half of the computation surface; it projects to an aggregating Datalog rule and to a SHACL-AF GROUP-BY sub-SELECT (design/LOGIC-SHACL-AF.md). A rule with no logic:aggregateFunction is an ordinary derivation (map) rule."
msgstr "命名一个 logic:Rule 在其归约（聚合）头部所应用的聚合函数（SUM、COUNT、MIN、MAX、AVG）：该规则将 logic:aggregateResult 绑定为此函数作用于 logic:aggregateVariable 在由 logic:groupKey 形成的组上的结果。这是计算表面归约那一半的规范 logic: 表示；它投影为一条聚合的 Datalog 规则以及一个 SHACL-AF 的 GROUP-BY 子 SELECT（design/LOGIC-SHACL-AF.md）。没有 logic:aggregateFunction 的规则是一条普通的派生（map）规则。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/aggregateResult|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment"
msgid "The head variable a reduce rule binds to the aggregate result. Default-absent on ordinary Horn rules."
msgstr "归约规则绑定到聚合结果的头部变量。在普通 Horn 规则上默认缺省。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/aggregateResult|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The head variable (a ?-prefixed string) a reduce rule binds to the value of logic:aggregateFunction applied to logic:aggregateVariable per group. It is the head object the rule derives for each group key, projecting to the SPARQL `(FUNC(?var) AS ?result)` of the SHACL-AF reduce surface."
msgstr "归约规则将其绑定到 logic:aggregateFunction 按组作用于 logic:aggregateVariable 之值的头部变量（一个以 ? 为前缀的字符串）。它是规则为每个组键导出的头部对象，投影为 SHACL-AF 归约表面的 SPARQL `(FUNC(?var) AS ?result)`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Aggregate|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The emergence-verdict value for a part-reducible whole property: under the declared logic:ReductionTheory of an logic:EmergenceAssessment, the whole's property is reconstructible from its proper parts — the theory carries the property in its logic:reductionBasis and a proper part also bears it (logic:bearsProperty) — so the property is a mere aggregate, a sum or closure over parts, not an emergent one. The positive, derivation-grounded verdict, reached by an actual part-reconstruction rather than by negation; contrast logic:Emergent (not part-reducible under the theory) and logic:EmergenceUnknown (the reducibility question cannot be posed) (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "针对可归约于部分的整体属性的涌现裁决值：在一个 logic:EmergenceAssessment 已声明的 logic:ReductionTheory 下，整体的属性可从其真部分重建——该理论在其 logic:reductionBasis 中携带该属性，且某个真部分也承载它（logic:bearsProperty）——因此该属性只是一个聚合，一个在部分之上的求和或闭包，而非涌现的属性。这是正面的、以派生为根基的裁决，经由实际的部分重建而非经由否定达到；与 logic:Emergent（在该理论下不可归约于部分）以及 logic:EmergenceUnknown（可归约性问题无法被提出）相对照（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons 一节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/aggregateVariable|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment"
msgid "The body variable a reduce rule aggregates. Default-absent on ordinary Horn rules."
msgstr "归约规则所聚合的体部变量。在普通 Horn 规则上默认缺省。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/aggregateVariable|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The rule-body variable (a ?-prefixed string) whose bindings logic:aggregateFunction aggregates within each group of a reduce rule. It must be positively bound by the rule body, exactly as a head variable must, so the aggregate ranges over a defined column."
msgstr "logic:aggregateFunction 在归约规则的每个组内对其绑定进行聚合的规则体变量（一个以 ? 为前缀的字符串）。它必须由规则体正向绑定，恰如头部变量所必须那样，从而聚合遍历一个已定义的列。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/aggThreshold|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The fixed literal value the group aggregate of a logic:JoinAggregateConstraint is tested against under logic:aggComparator (e.g. 0 for ∂²=0). Always a literal: the (focus, far-endpoint) group key already consumes the far endpoint, so unlike logic:aggCompareTo there is no per-focus property right-hand side. The projected sh:SPARQLConstraint HAVING negates the comparator, because a sh:select returns the VIOLATING groups."
msgstr "一个 logic:JoinAggregateConstraint 的组聚合在 logic:aggComparator 下所对照测试的固定字面量值（例如对于 ∂²=0 取 0）。始终是字面量：（焦点，远端点）组键已经消费了远端点，因此不同于 logic:aggCompareTo，这里没有按焦点的属性右侧。所投影的 sh:SPARQLConstraint 的 HAVING 会取该比较符的否定，因为 sh:select 返回的是违例的组。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/allValuesFrom|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:teamRestriction logic:allValuesFrom ex:Person ."
msgstr "示例：ex:teamRestriction logic:allValuesFrom ex:Person ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/allValuesFrom|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The condition is vacuously satisfied when the constrained property has no values."
msgstr "当受约束的属性没有任何值时，该条件被平凡地满足。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AndDecomposition|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The decomposition of a gmeow:Goal under which all of its necessary sub-goals must hold together for the parent to be satisfied — a conjunctive node of the and-or goal graph means–end search runs over. It groups the logic:necessaryFor sub-goals of the parent: every grouped sub-goal must be satisfied. The co-equal counterpart of logic:OrDecomposition (any one sufficient sub-goal settles the parent); the two compose into the and-or goal graph. Decomposition carries satisfaction dependency and is typed apart from the generic mereology spine — a sub-goal may be both a gmeow:properPartOf and logic:necessaryFor its parent, yet part-hood alone does not express the satisfaction dependency planning needs."
msgstr "一个 gmeow:Goal 的分解，在此分解下其所有必要子目标必须共同成立，父目标才得满足——这是手段-目的搜索所遍历的与-或目标图的一个合取节点。它对父目标的 logic:necessaryFor 子目标进行分组：每个被分组的子目标都必须得满足。它是 logic:OrDecomposition 的同等对应物（任一充分子目标即可决定父目标）；二者组成与-或目标图。分解承载满足依赖，并与通用的部分学脊柱分开定型——一个子目标可以既是其父目标的 gmeow:properPartOf 又是其 logic:necessaryFor，然而仅凭部分身份并不表达规划所需的满足依赖。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/and|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a conjunction logic:Formula to each of its operand sub-formulae (multi-valued, two or more). Conjunction is commutative and associative, so the canonical identity flattens nested conjunctions and is insensitive to operand order. It is not serial composition of transaction programs, which has state-changing path semantics."
msgstr "将一个合取 logic:Formula 关联到它的每个操作数子公式（多值，两个或更多）。合取是可交换且可结合的，因此规范恒等式会展平嵌套的合取并对操作数顺序不敏感。它不是事务程序的串行组合，后者具有改变状态的路径语义。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/and|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A conjunction node can link the atoms ex:red(x) and ex:round(x) through two logic:and edges."
msgstr "合取节点可以通过两条 logic:and 边连接原子 ex:red(x) 和 ex:round(x)。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/anomalyCycle|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The detected dependency cycle of a logic:SerializationAnomaly, rendered as the canonical sequence of transaction IRIs joined by ' -> ' (rotated to start at the lexicographically smallest member and closed back to it, so the same history always yields the same description). Domain logic:SerializationAnomaly, range xsd:string (stated in prose). It is a human-readable DESCRIPTION of the history-level finding — the conflict-graph cycle that has no equivalent serial order — never a claim of ⊥ within a state; a non-serializable schedule is surfaced with its cycle described here, never silently linearized."
msgstr "一个 logic:SerializationAnomaly 所检测到的依赖环，呈现为由 ' -> ' 连接的事务 IRI 的规范序列（经旋转以从字典序最小的成员起始并闭合回它，使同一历史始终产生同一描述）。定义域 logic:SerializationAnomaly，值域 xsd:string（以散文表述）。它是对历史级发现的人类可读描述——没有任何等价串行顺序的冲突图环——绝非某状态内 ⊥ 的主张；不可串行化的调度会连同此处描述的环一并被呈现，绝不被默默线性化。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/antecedent|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a material-implication logic:Formula to its antecedent (the hypothesis). Paired with logic:consequent; the two name the implication's operands explicitly so the ordered, non-commutative reading never depends on serialization order."
msgstr "将一个实质蕴涵 logic:Formula 关联到它的前件（假设）。它与 logic:consequent 配对；二者显式命名蕴涵的操作数，使这种有序、不可交换的读法绝不依赖序列化顺序。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/antecedent|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "In person(x) implies mortal(x), the person atom is the sole logic:antecedent."
msgstr "在 person(x) implies mortal(x) 中，person 原子是唯一的 logic:antecedent。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/antiConjectureObligationCandidate|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The symmetric anti-conjecture promotion leg: relates a robustly logic:ConjectureRefutedInStandpoint conjecture to a candidate logic:NonEntailmentObligation forbidding its formula — a refuted formula is not merely dropped, it becomes a first-class commitment that the foundation must NEVER draw it. Mirrors logic:conjecturePromotionCandidate (corroborated to axiom candidate) under negation (refuted to non-entailment candidate). Present exactly when the conjecture is refuted-in-standpoint. Domain logic:Conjecture, range logic:NonEntailmentObligation."
msgstr "反猜想提升的对称支路：将一个稳健地 logic:ConjectureRefutedInStandpoint 的猜想关联到一个禁止其公式的候选 logic:NonEntailmentObligation——被驳斥的公式不只是被丢弃，它成为一个头等承诺，规定基础绝不可推出它。它在否定之下映照 logic:conjecturePromotionCandidate（获佐证者提升为公理候选）（被驳斥者提升为非蕴涵候选）。恰在该猜想于立场中被驳斥时出现。定义域 logic:Conjecture，值域 logic:NonEntailmentObligation。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Annotation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The tenth logic:NodeKind: a lifted RDFS/SKOS annotation axiom carried as a first-class IR node. Its subject is the annotated term, its predicate the surface annotation IRI verbatim (rdfs:label, rdfs:comment, skos:definition, skos:prefLabel, skos:altLabel, skos:scopeNote), and its object the literal value on the internal x-gmeow-english carrier tag. Lifting these annotations into the canonical IR — rather than passing them through untouched — is what makes logic: a genuine isSupersetOf SKOS and RDFS: the crisp annotation surface round-trips at logic:ExactPreservation, and the generated SKOS concept-scheme surface is a projection of these axioms rather than an authored second source. Load-bearing prose annotations (skos:definition, rdfs:comment) are marked load-bearing so the put leg preserves them; the display labels are droppable hints (design/LOGIC-META-SEMANTICS.md, the outward-face isSupersetOf row)."
msgstr "第十个 logic:NodeKind：一个作为第一类中间表示节点承载的、被提升的 RDFS/SKOS 注解公理。它的主体是被注解的术语，它的谓词是逐字保留的表层注解 IRI（rdfs:label、rdfs:comment、skos:definition、skos:prefLabel、skos:altLabel、skos:scopeNote），它的对象是带有内部 x-gmeow-english 承载标签的字面值。将这些注解提升进规范中间表示——而非将它们原样放行——正是使 logic: 成为对 SKOS 与 RDFS 真正 isSupersetOf 的原因：清晰的注解表层在 logic:ExactPreservation 处往返，而生成的 SKOS 概念方案表层是这些公理的投影，而非人工撰写的第二来源。承载语义的散文注解（skos:definition、rdfs:comment）被标记为承载，以便 logic:putLeg 分支保留它们；显示标签则是可丢弃的提示（design/LOGIC-META-SEMANTICS.md，外向面的 isSupersetOf 行）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AntiRigidType|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A logic:Type that applies contingently to EVERY one of its instances — for each instance there is a world of existence in which it lacks the type (the anti-rigidity witness; logic:rigidlyAppliesTo holds for none of its instances). The counterpart of gufo:AntiRigidType; the meta-type whose instances are the anti-rigid sorts: logic:Phase and logic:Role (each a logic:AntiRigidType and a logic:Sortal), logic:RoleMixin and logic:PhaseMixin (each a logic:AntiRigidType and a logic:NonSortal). Stated in prose, not as a subclass edge. The discipline that anti-rigid instantiation owes a witness is logic:dischargeObligation. Contrast logic:RigidType."
msgstr "一个 logic:Type，它偶然地适用于其每一个实例——对每个实例都存在一个使其缺乏该类型的存在世界（反刚性见证；logic:rigidlyAppliesTo 对其任何实例都不成立）。它是 gufo:AntiRigidType 的对应物；是其实例为反刚性种类的元类型：logic:Phase 与 logic:Role（各为一个 logic:AntiRigidType 且为 logic:Sortal），logic:RoleMixin 与 logic:PhaseMixin（各为一个 logic:AntiRigidType 且为 logic:NonSortal）。以散文表述，而非作为子类边。反刚性实例化亏欠一个见证的纪律是 logic:dischargeObligation。与 logic:RigidType 相对照。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/anyOf|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A member predicate of a logic:DisjunctiveRequirednessConstraint: at least one of the logic:anyOf predicates must have a value on the focus (a disjunction of existentials)."
msgstr "一个 logic:DisjunctiveRequirednessConstraint 的成员谓词：logic:anyOf 谓词中至少有一个必须在焦点上有值（存在量词的析取）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ArgumentationSemantics|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The facet value class of the argumentation facet: how conflicts among defeasible arguments are resolved. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract. Its individuals range from no argumentation through the grounded and preferred Dung semantics to a policy-specific resolution."
msgstr "论辩侧面的侧面值类：可废止论证之间的冲突如何被消解。在 ReasoningContract 上单值。其个体从无论辩、经由基础语义与优先 Dung 语义，直到某种策略专有的消解。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/argumentation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to the logic:ArgumentationSemantics it selects — how conflicts among defeasible arguments are resolved. Single-valued on the contract. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:ArgumentationSemantics (stated in prose, matching the module's domain/range convention)."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ReasoningContract 关联到它所选择的 logic:ArgumentationSemantics——可废止论证之间的冲突如何被消解。在契约上单值。定义域 logic:ReasoningContract，值域 logic:ArgumentationSemantics（以散文表述，与模块的定义域/值域约定一致）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/argument|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ArgumentStructure — an atomic-predication logic:Formula (over logic:relation) or a logic:FunctionTerm (over logic:functionSymbol) — to one of its argument term-carriers. The SAME property carries both, so a function term's operands reuse the predication argument machinery. Each carrier fixes its position with logic:termIndex and its value with exactly one term-value property (logic:termIri, logic:termVariable, logic:termLiteral, logic:termSequenceMarker, or logic:termApplication), so a variadic argument list — including sequence markers and nested compound function terms — round-trips with its order and term kinds intact. It is not a direct link to the term value and carries no ordering by triple position."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ArgumentStructure——一个原子谓述 logic:Formula（在 logic:relation 上）或一个 logic:FunctionTerm（在 logic:functionSymbol 上）——关联到它的某个论元词项载体。同一个属性承载两者，因此函数项的操作数复用谓述论元机制。每个载体以 logic:termIndex 固定其位置，以恰好一个词项值属性（logic:termIri、logic:termVariable、logic:termLiteral、logic:termSequenceMarker 或 logic:termApplication）固定其值，从而一个可变元论元列表——包括序列标记与嵌套的复合函数项——能在保持其顺序与词项种类完好的情况下往返。它不是通向词项值的直接链接，也不按三元组位置携带任何排序。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/argument|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The atom ex:knows(alice,bob) uses carriers at indices 0 and 1 linked through logic:argument."
msgstr "原子 ex:knows(alice,bob) 使用索引 0 和 1 处的载体，二者通过 logic:argument 相连。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ArgumentStructure|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A node that applies a reified operator to an ordered list of logic:argument term-carriers: an atomic-predication logic:Formula (operator = logic:relation) or a logic:FunctionTerm (operator = logic:functionSymbol). It is the shared rdfs:domain of logic:argument, so the ordered argument-carrier machinery is reused across both without asserting that a function term is a formula or that a formula is a term."
msgstr "一个将具体化算子作用于 logic:argument 词项载体有序列表的节点：一个原子谓述 logic:Formula（算子 = logic:relation）或一个 logic:FunctionTerm（算子 = logic:functionSymbol）。它是 logic:argument 的共享 rdfs:domain，因此有序的论元载体机制在两者间复用，而不断言函数项是公式或公式是词项。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Aspect|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A moment (trope): an endurant that exists only by inhering in a bearer on which it existentially depends — a colour, a belief, a marriage's commitment. The counterpart of gufo:Aspect, covering its intrinsic/extrinsic split (gufo:IntrinsicAspect inheres in a single bearer, gufo:ExtrinsicAspect depends on several): logic: carries that distinction on the inherence/dependence relation rather than as separate classes. The dependent counterpart of logic:Substantial. Qualities and modes are aspects (stated in prose, not as a subclass edge)."
msgstr "一个瞬态（trope）：一个仅通过内属于其存在性依赖的承载者而存在的持续体——一种颜色、一个信念、一桩婚姻的承诺。它是 gufo:Aspect 的对应物，涵盖其内在/外在之分（gufo:IntrinsicAspect 内属于单一承载者，gufo:ExtrinsicAspect 依赖于多个）：logic: 将该区分承载在内属/依赖关系上，而非作为分离的类。它是 logic:Substantial 的依赖性对应物。性质与样式都是方面（以散文表述，而非作为子类边）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/assessedAgent|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The agent role of a logic:CognitiveAssessment: whose cognition is judged. Range gmeow:Agent (stated in prose, matching the module's convention). A well-formedness existence guard — every projection rule re-binds it, so a malformed assessment naming no agent receives no ladder edge."
msgstr "一个 logic:CognitiveAssessment 的智能体角色：被评判的是谁的认知。值域 gmeow:Agent（以散文表述，与模块约定一致）。它是一个良构性存在守卫——每条投影规则都会重新绑定它，因此未命名任何智能体的畸形评估不会收到任何阶梯边。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/assessmentContext|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The task or context a logic:CognitiveAssessment holds for, since competence is context-relative: the same agent may be competent on one task and not on another, so an assessment without a context underdetermines what it claims. Range is left open (stated in prose)."
msgstr "一个 logic:CognitiveAssessment 所适用的任务或语境，因为胜任力是相对于语境的：同一智能体可能在一项任务上胜任而在另一项上不胜任，因此没有语境的评估会欠定它所主张的内容。值域留作开放（以散文表述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AssessmentDimension|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The value-vocabulary class of the factored axis a logic:CognitiveAssessment judges, named via logic:assessmentDimension. An OPEN value vocabulary (individuals, never subclasses): a new dimension is a new individual rather than a reshaping of the construct, the same orthogonal-factorization discipline the foundation applies to claim modality and contextual scope. The dimensions vary independently — an assessment on one says nothing about another — and an assessment names exactly one."
msgstr "一个 logic:CognitiveAssessment 所评判的、经由 logic:assessmentDimension 命名的因子化轴的值词汇类。一个开放的值词汇（是个体，绝非子类）：新的维度是一个新个体，而非对该构造的重塑，这与基础对主张模态与语境范围所施加的正交因子化纪律相同。各维度独立变化——对一个维度的评估对另一个维度不置一词——而一次评估恰好命名一个维度。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/assessmentDimension|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The single factored axis a logic:CognitiveAssessment judges: a logic:AssessmentDimension individual. An assessment names exactly one; the dimensions vary independently. Range logic:AssessmentDimension (stated in prose)."
msgstr "logic:CognitiveAssessment 所评判的单一因子化轴：一个 logic:AssessmentDimension 个体。一次评估恰好命名一个；各维度彼此独立地变化。值域为 logic:AssessmentDimension（以散文形式说明）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/assessmentEvaluator|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Who holds the judgment of a logic:CognitiveAssessment: the standpoint is attributed via gmeow:accordingTo, so a self-assessment (evaluator = assessed agent) and an observer's assessment coexist as two records rather than collapsing into one verdict. Range gmeow:Agent (stated in prose)."
msgstr "谁持有一次 logic:CognitiveAssessment 的判断：立场通过 gmeow:accordingTo 归属，因此自我评估（评估者 = 被评估主体）与旁观者的评估作为两条记录并存，而非坍缩为单一裁决。值域为 gmeow:Agent（以散文形式说明）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/assessmentEvidence|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The reasoning, observations, or recorded episode a logic:CognitiveAssessment rests on — the inference commitments it cites, the gmeow:ModelInvocation that produced the reasoning, the results it grades — so an assessment is auditable against the reasoning it judges rather than standing apart from it. Range is left open (stated in prose)."
msgstr "一次 logic:CognitiveAssessment 所依据的推理、观测或已记录的情节——它援引的推理承诺、产生该推理的 gmeow:ModelInvocation、它所评级的结果——从而使评估可对照它所评判的推理接受审计，而不与之相脱离。值域保持开放（以散文形式说明）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AssessmentLevel|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The value-vocabulary class of an ordinal level on an assessment's scale, the object of logic:assessmentLevel and logic:thresholdLevel when the scale is ordinal. An OPEN, ordered value vocabulary (logic:levelNone ≺ logic:levelEmerging ≺ logic:levelCompetent ≺ logic:levelStrong), ordered by logic:levelAtOrAbove so that 'a level at or above a threshold' is well-defined for the coarse-ladder projection without a numeric comparison (which would force a procedural profile). An assessment whose scale is continuous carries a literal logic:assessmentLevel instead; the ordinal levels are the projection scale."
msgstr "评估尺度上某一序数级别的取值词汇类，当尺度为序数时是 logic:assessmentLevel 与 logic:thresholdLevel 的对象。一个开放且有序的取值词汇（logic:levelNone ≺ logic:levelEmerging ≺ logic:levelCompetent ≺ logic:levelStrong），由 logic:levelAtOrAbove 排序，使得“达到或高于某阈值的级别”对于粗梯级投影而言无需数值比较即可良好定义（数值比较会强制要求过程式配置）。尺度为连续的评估则改为携带一个字面量 logic:assessmentLevel；序数级别即投影尺度。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/assessmentLevel|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The value a logic:CognitiveAssessment takes on its logic:assessmentScale: an ordinal logic:AssessmentLevel individual when the scale is ordinal (the case the coarse-ladder projection reads), or a continuous literal otherwise (a Brier or logarithmic score on a continuous scale). Because the range spans both an individual and a literal it is a plain rdf:Property, not an owl:ObjectProperty (which could not carry the continuous literal) — the same open-range convention the module states in prose elsewhere."
msgstr "一次 logic:CognitiveAssessment 在其 logic:assessmentScale 上所取的值：当尺度为序数时是一个序数 logic:AssessmentLevel 个体（粗梯级投影读取的情形），否则是一个连续字面量（连续尺度上的 Brier 分或对数分）。由于值域同时涵盖个体与字面量，它是一个普通的 rdf:Property 而非 owl:ObjectProperty（后者无法承载连续字面量）——正是该模块在别处以散文所述的同一开放值域约定。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/assessmentMethod|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "How the judgment of a logic:CognitiveAssessment was reached — a test, a review, a scoring rule applied to a forecast series, an introspective report. Range is left open (stated in prose), so the method may be a named procedure or a free description."
msgstr "一次 logic:CognitiveAssessment 的判断如何得出——一次测试、一次评审、应用于预测序列的评分规则、一份内省报告。值域保持开放（以散文形式说明），因此方法可以是一个具名程序或一段自由描述。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/assessmentProperty|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The property role of an logic:EmergenceAssessment: the property-value whose emergence is being assessed — the thing the whole bears (logic:bearsProperty) and whose reducibility to the parts is in question. One of the three role properties (with logic:assessmentWhole and logic:assessmentReductionTheory) that reify the emergence-assessment relation onto the arity-bounded reasoning surface, mirroring the logic:HolonicPosition role properties (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "一次 logic:EmergenceAssessment 的属性角色：其涌现正被评估的属性值——整体所承载（logic:bearsProperty）且其对各部分的可还原性受到质疑之物。三个角色属性之一（与 logic:assessmentWhole 及 logic:assessmentReductionTheory 一起），它们将涌现评估关系具体化到有界元数的推理表面上，镜像 logic:HolonicPosition 的角色属性（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons 章节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/assessmentReductionTheory|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The theory role of an logic:EmergenceAssessment: the logic:ReductionTheory the assessment is relative to. Emergence is never absolute — the verdict (logic:Aggregate / logic:Emergent / logic:EmergenceUnknown) is read only against this declared theory's logic:reductionBasis, and recording it is what lets a stronger theory overturn an logic:Emergent verdict without contradiction. An assessment that omits this role cannot pose the reducibility question and receives logic:EmergenceUnknown. One of the three role properties (with logic:assessmentWhole and logic:assessmentProperty) that reify the emergence-assessment relation (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "一次 logic:EmergenceAssessment 的理论角色：评估所相对的 logic:ReductionTheory。涌现从不是绝对的——裁决（logic:Aggregate / logic:Emergent / logic:EmergenceUnknown）只对照这个已声明理论的 logic:reductionBasis 来读取，而记录它正是让更强的理论能够无矛盾地推翻某个 logic:Emergent 裁决之所在。省略此角色的评估无法提出可还原性问题，因而获得 logic:EmergenceUnknown。三个角色属性之一（与 logic:assessmentWhole 及 logic:assessmentProperty 一起），它们将涌现评估关系具体化（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons 章节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/assessmentScale|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The named scale, ordinal or continuous, on which a logic:CognitiveAssessment's logic:assessmentLevel is read. Range is left open (stated in prose), since a scale may be the native ordinal logic:AssessmentLevel vocabulary or a foreign scale (Bloom's, SOLO, a Brier-scored continuous range)."
msgstr "读取一次 logic:CognitiveAssessment 的 logic:assessmentLevel 所用的具名尺度，序数或连续。值域保持开放（以散文形式说明），因为尺度可以是原生序数词汇 logic:AssessmentLevel，也可以是外来尺度（Bloom's、SOLO、以 Brier 计分的连续范围）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/assessmentSubject|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The subject role of a logic:CognitiveAssessment: what the assessment is about — a single inference, a body of reasoning, a domain of competence, or the agent as a whole. Its grain is carried by logic:subjectGranularity. Range is left open (stated in prose), since the subject may be reasoning, a domain entity, or the reasoner itself."
msgstr "一次 logic:CognitiveAssessment 的主体角色：评估所关乎之物——单一推理、一段推理体、一个能力领域，或整体的主体。其粒度由 logic:subjectGranularity 承载。值域保持开放（以散文形式说明），因为主体可以是推理、领域实体，或推理器自身。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/assessmentVerdict|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The derived outcome of an logic:EmergenceAssessment: the logic:EmergenceVerdict (logic:Aggregate, logic:Emergent, or logic:EmergenceUnknown) the foundation lowering entails for it. Never asserted by hand — it is computed by the stratified emergence rules from the assessment's whole, property, and declared logic:ReductionTheory, the convenient OWL-projectable surface of the assessment exactly as logic:isHolon projects holon-ness. logic:Emergent is reached by negation-as-failure over the aggregate derivation, so the verdict is genuinely theory-relative rather than a bare 'unflagged' default (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "一次 logic:EmergenceAssessment 的派生结果：基础下降为其蕴含的 logic:EmergenceVerdict（logic:Aggregate、logic:Emergent 或 logic:EmergenceUnknown）。绝不手工断言——它由分层涌现规则依据评估的整体、属性及已声明的 logic:ReductionTheory 计算得出，是评估便于投影为 OWL 的表面，恰如 logic:isHolon 投影全子性。logic:Emergent 通过对聚合派生的失败即否定而达成，因此裁决真正相对于理论，而非一个赤裸的“未标记”默认值（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons 章节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/assessmentWhole|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The whole role of an logic:EmergenceAssessment: the entity whose property is being assessed for emergence — the whole that bears the property and stands over the proper parts the reduction is attempted from. One of the three role properties (with logic:assessmentProperty and logic:assessmentReductionTheory) that reify the emergence-assessment relation onto the arity-bounded reasoning surface, mirroring the logic:HolonicPosition role properties (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "一次 logic:EmergenceAssessment 的整体角色：其属性正就涌现受评估的实体——承载该属性并居于尝试还原所自的各真部分之上的整体。三个角色属性之一（与 logic:assessmentProperty 及 logic:assessmentReductionTheory 一起），它们将涌现评估关系具体化到有界元数的推理表面上，镜像 logic:HolonicPosition 的角色属性（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons 章节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/assuresResult|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ResultAssurance to the single logic:ReasoningResult it assesses. Domain logic:ResultAssurance, range logic:ReasoningResult (stated in prose, matching the module's convention)."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ResultAssurance 关联到它所评估的单一 logic:ReasoningResult。定义域为 logic:ResultAssurance，值域为 logic:ReasoningResult（以散文形式说明，符合该模块的约定）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/asymmetricProperty|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic: property-characteristic marker for asymmetry: a property P such that P(a,b) entails ¬P(b,a). The logic: analogue of owl:AsymmetricProperty, minted standalone so it can co-occur with logic:transitiveProperty on the same property — the transitive ∧ asymmetric combination OWL 2 DL bars for decidability but logic: keeps and reasons over (criticism 7)."
msgstr "logic: 中表示非对称性的属性特征标记：一个属性 P 使得 P(a,b) 蕴含 ¬P(b,a)。owl:AsymmetricProperty 的 logic: 类比物，独立铸造，从而可在同一属性上与 logic:transitiveProperty 共现——传递 ∧ 非对称这一组合为可判定性之故被 OWL 2 DL 禁止，但 logic: 予以保留并对其推理（criticism 7）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AtomicGoal|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:GoalExpressionKind for a leaf goal satisfied exactly when its logic:boundSituationType obtains at the relevant state. The base of the compositional algebra; contrast the conjunctive/disjunctive combinators and the temporal kinds."
msgstr "叶子目标的 logic:GoalExpressionKind，当且仅当其 logic:boundSituationType 在相关状态成立时被满足。组合代数的基底；与合取/析取组合子及时序种类相对照。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/attackComponentSelfExclusion|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Asserts that a gmeow:Attack's gmeow:attackSource (a gmeow:Argument) must not aim its gmeow:attackTarget at one of its own components — its conclusion (gmeow:argumentConclusion), a premise use (gmeow:hasPremiseUse), or an inference application (gmeow:hasInferenceApplication): an argument does not attack a part of itself. The native coherence gate raises a violation when the target is a component of the source."
msgstr "断言一个 gmeow:Attack 的 gmeow:attackSource（一个 gmeow:Argument）不得将其 gmeow:attackTarget 指向自身的某个组成部分——它的结论（gmeow:argumentConclusion）、一次前提使用（gmeow:hasPremiseUse）或一次推理应用（gmeow:hasInferenceApplication）：一个论证不攻击自身的某一部分。当目标是源的组成部分时，原生一致性关卡会引发一次违规。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/attackRebutTargetsStandpointClaim|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Asserts that a gmeow:Attack whose gmeow:attackKind is gmeow:attackRebut must aim its gmeow:attackTarget at a conclusion gmeow:StandpointClaim — rebutting attacks the conclusion. The native coherence gate raises a violation when the kind is rebut but the target is not a standpoint claim."
msgstr "断言一个 gmeow:attackKind 为 gmeow:attackRebut 的 gmeow:Attack 必须将其 gmeow:attackTarget 指向一个作为结论的 gmeow:StandpointClaim——反驳攻击的是结论。当种类为 rebut 但目标并非一个立场主张时，原生一致性关卡会引发一次违规。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/attackSelfAttackExclusion|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Asserts that a gmeow:Attack's gmeow:attackSource and gmeow:attackTarget must be distinct: conflict is irreflexive — nothing attacks itself. The native coherence gate raises a violation when they coincide; the generated SHACL constraint surface is its projection."
msgstr "断言一个 gmeow:Attack 的 gmeow:attackSource 与 gmeow:attackTarget 必须相异：冲突是非自反的——没有任何东西攻击自身。当二者重合时，原生一致性关卡会引发一次违规；所生成的 SHACL 约束表面是其投影。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/attackUndercutTargetsInferenceApplication|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Asserts that a gmeow:Attack whose gmeow:attackKind is gmeow:attackUndercut must aim its gmeow:attackTarget at a gmeow:InferenceApplication — undercutting attacks the warrant / inferential link. The native coherence gate raises a violation when the kind is undercut but the target is not an inference application."
msgstr "断言一个 gmeow:attackKind 为 gmeow:attackUndercut 的 gmeow:Attack 必须将其 gmeow:attackTarget 指向一个 gmeow:InferenceApplication——削弱攻击的是保证 / 推理链接。当种类为 undercut 但目标并非一次推理应用时，原生一致性关卡会引发一次违规。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/attackUndermineTargetsPremiseUse|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Asserts that a gmeow:Attack whose gmeow:attackKind is gmeow:attackUndermine must aim its gmeow:attackTarget at a gmeow:PremiseUse — undermining is premise-directed. The native coherence gate raises a violation when the kind is undermine but the target is not a premise use."
msgstr "断言一个 gmeow:attackKind 为 gmeow:attackUndermine 的 gmeow:Attack 必须将其 gmeow:attackTarget 指向一个 gmeow:PremiseUse——瓦解针对的是前提。当种类为 undermine 但目标并非一次前提使用时，原生一致性关卡会引发一次违规。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AutonomyDeficient|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The agency-verdict value for the first Koestlerian pathology — a 'part' with no autonomy: under the declared logic:HolonicAgencyProfile, the holon bears an logic:integrativeBasis value (it subordinates as a part) but bears no logic:selfAssertiveBasis value, so its self-assertive (autonomy-as-a-whole) face has collapsed. Reached by negation-as-failure over the self-assertive marker while the integrative marker holds, so the verdict is profile-relative, never a bare default. The co-equal counterpart of logic:IntegrationDeficient (the opposite collapse); contrast logic:HolonIntegral (both faces) and logic:AgencyUnknown (neither evidenced) (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "第一种柯斯特勒式病态的能动性裁决值——一个没有自主性的“部分”：在已声明的 logic:HolonicAgencyProfile 下，该全子承载一个 logic:integrativeBasis 值（它作为部分而从属）却不承载任何 logic:selfAssertiveBasis 值，因此其自我肯定（作为整体的自主性）之面已坍缩。当整合标记成立时，通过对自我肯定标记的失败即否定而达成，因此裁决相对于配置，绝非赤裸的默认值。logic:IntegrationDeficient 的对等对应物（相反的坍缩）；与 logic:HolonIntegral（两面俱在）及 logic:AgencyUnknown（两者皆无佐证）相对照（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons 章节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AvoidanceGoal|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:GoalExpressionKind for a goal satisfied only while its proscribed logic:boundSituationType NEVER obtains across the interval, violated at the first state it obtains — the dual of logic:MaintenanceGoal. While the window is still open the evaluation is logic:GoalEvaluationUndetermined."
msgstr "一个目标的 logic:GoalExpressionKind，仅当其被禁止的 logic:boundSituationType 在整个区间内从不成立时才被满足，一旦在首个状态成立即被违反——logic:MaintenanceGoal 的对偶。只要窗口仍然开放，评估即为 logic:GoalEvaluationUndetermined。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/awaitingSignal|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a node still blocked on a logic:ExternalSignal to the exact signal it is waiting on — the witness that a notification-wait is pending (the engine has not been told), never silently completed. It appears in two places, both marking the same withheld judgment. (1) On a logic:GateUndetermined logic:GateProbe over a logic:NotificationWaitSchema: the reason the gate is undetermined rather than admitted. (2) On a logic:TransactionOutcome whose executed transaction path HALTED at an un-signalled wait step: the load-bearing distinction between a PENDING (undetermined) outcome and a definite failure — both read logic:transactionSucceeds false, but only the pending one names, through this witness, the signal it still awaits, so a plan blocked on an external notification is never conflated with a genuine precondition failure. Range the awaited logic:ExternalSignal (stated in prose). In every case: the wait can still complete once the signal arrives."
msgstr "将一个仍因某 logic:ExternalSignal 而阻塞的节点关联到它正等待的确切信号——一次通知等待正在进行（引擎尚未被告知）而绝非被静默完成的见证。它出现在两处，二者都标记同一个被搁置的判断。（1）在针对某 logic:NotificationWaitSchema 的 logic:GateUndetermined logic:GateProbe 上：关卡处于未定而非被准入的缘由。（2）在其已执行事务路径于某个未收到信号的等待步骤处停止的 logic:TransactionOutcome 上：一个待定（未定）结果与一次确定失败之间承重的区分——两者的 logic:transactionSucceeds 都读为假，但唯有待定者通过此见证命名它仍在等待的信号，从而使一个因外部通知而阻塞的计划绝不与一次真正的前置条件失败相混淆。值域为所等待的 logic:ExternalSignal（以散文形式说明）。在所有情形下：一旦信号到达，等待仍可完成。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/awaitsSignal|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:NotificationWaitSchema to the logic:ExternalSignal situation whose arrival its completion waits on. Domain logic:NotificationWaitSchema, range a logic:ExternalSignal situation (stated in prose). The wait fires only once this signal obtains in the state; until then it is pending (logic:awaitingSignal), never silently completed."
msgstr "将一个 logic:NotificationWaitSchema 关联到其完成所等待其到达的 logic:ExternalSignal 情境。定义域为 logic:NotificationWaitSchema，值域为一个 logic:ExternalSignal 情境（以散文形式说明）。该等待仅在此信号于状态中成立后才触发；在此之前它处于进行中（logic:awaitingSignal），绝不被静默完成。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/axiomHash|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A content-addressed digest of an axiom set inside the checked bundle, pinning exactly which axioms the coherence outcome ranged over — MULTI-valued, one per certified fragment component. Domain logic:CoherenceCertificate or logic:CoherenceCheckAttestation (stated in prose)."
msgstr "已检查包内某公理集的内容寻址摘要，精确钉定一致性结果所涵盖的公理——多值，每个已认证片段组件一个。定义域为 logic:CoherenceCertificate 或 logic:CoherenceCheckAttestation（以散文形式说明）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/BackwardEvaluation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:EvaluationMode value selecting goal-directed SLG-WFS backward resolution: subsumptive demand-driven answer keying (SLG tabling), structured-term unification over logic:FunctionTerm arguments, explicit proof objects for each derived answer, and three-valued well-founded negation for logic:not-negated body literals. The one evaluation strategy this vocabulary supports today; contrast a future forward-chase member of logic:EvaluationMode over the identical clause set."
msgstr "选择目标导向 SLG-WFS 后向消解的 logic:EvaluationMode 值：包容式、按需驱动的答案键控（SLG 表化）、对 logic:FunctionTerm 参数的结构化词项合一、为每个派生答案提供的显式证明对象，以及针对 logic:not 否定的体文字的三值良基否定。此词汇今天所支持的唯一评估策略；与未来在同一子句集上进行前向追赶的 logic:EvaluationMode 成员相对照。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/backwardSourceHash|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The framed-BLAKE3 digest over the backward goal-resolution SOURCE surface of the engine — the dispatch entry point, the profile gates, the query IR, the fact-source seam, and the whole physical resolution engine — folded into a logic:EngineContract so a pinned consumer detects any change to how a goal query is decided. Because it digests source bytes in a fixed order, a rename or a body edit of any covered file both move it (and the containing logic:engineContractDescriptorHash). Single-valued. Domain logic:EngineContract (stated in prose). NON-CONFLATION with logic:forwardContractHash: the backward surface answers goal queries by resolution, the forward surface materializes consequences by the EL/DL/RL chase; the two source surfaces are independent and MUST NOT alias — a change confined to one moves only its own digest, which is why the descriptor carries both rather than a single blended hash. Authored canonically in crates/logic (Rust); a lossy documentation projection (Principle 17). Normative in design/LOGIC-RUNTIME.md, §The forward materialization ↔ backward resolution seam."
msgstr "对引擎后向目标消解源代码表面的带框 BLAKE3 摘要——派发入口点、配置关卡、查询 IR、事实源接缝，以及整个物理消解引擎——折叠进一个 logic:EngineContract，使被钉定的消费者能检测到目标查询判定方式的任何改动。由于它以固定顺序对源字节做摘要，任何被覆盖文件的重命名或体编辑都会使其移动（连同外层的 logic:engineContractDescriptorHash）。单值。定义域为 logic:EngineContract（以散文形式说明）。与 logic:forwardContractHash 的不相混淆：后向表面通过消解回答目标查询，前向表面通过 EL/DL/RL 追赶物化推论；两个源表面彼此独立且不得别名——限于其一的改动只移动它自己的摘要，这正是描述符同时携带两者而非单一混合摘要的缘由。在 crates/logic（Rust）中规范撰写；一份有损文档投影（原则 17）。规范见 design/LOGIC-RUNTIME.md，§The forward materialization ↔ backward resolution seam。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/balanceAmountNodePredicate|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The predicate of a logic:AggregateBalanceConstraint from a posting to its amount node (?posting <amountNode> ?amount); both the numeric value and the group key hang off this shared amount node, so a value and its group key are always read from the same amount."
msgstr "一个 logic:AggregateBalanceConstraint 从一条分录指向其金额节点的谓词（?posting <amountNode> ?amount）；数值与分组键都挂在这个共享金额节点上，因此一个值与其分组键始终从同一金额读取。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/balanceCreditValue|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:balancePartitionPredicate value marking a CREDIT posting in a logic:AggregateBalanceConstraint."
msgstr "在一个 logic:AggregateBalanceConstraint 中标记一条贷方分录的 logic:balancePartitionPredicate 值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/balancedByGroup|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The reified relation an expanded logic:AggregateBalanceConstraint carries as its honest FOL integrity: balancedByGroup(this, posting, partition, debit, credit, amountNode, value, group). The realized FOL formula core has no aggregate node, so this predication makes the double-entry-balance meaning complete in the FOL canon while the structured satellite drives the real GROUP BY/HAVING SPARQL projection."
msgstr "一个展开的 logic:AggregateBalanceConstraint 作为其诚实 FOL 完整性所携带的具体化关系：balancedByGroup(this, posting, partition, debit, credit, amountNode, value, group)。所实现的 FOL 公式核心没有聚合节点，因此这一谓述使复式记账的平衡含义在 FOL 正典中完整，而结构化卫星则驱动真正的 GROUP BY/HAVING SPARQL 投影。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/balanceDebitValue|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:balancePartitionPredicate value marking a DEBIT posting in a logic:AggregateBalanceConstraint."
msgstr "在一个 logic:AggregateBalanceConstraint 中标记一条借方分录的 logic:balancePartitionPredicate 值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/balanceGroupPredicate|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The predicate of a logic:AggregateBalanceConstraint from the amount node to the group key (?amount <group> ?group); the balance equality is asserted per group (e.g. per currency)."
msgstr "一个 logic:AggregateBalanceConstraint 从金额节点指向分组键的谓词（?amount <group> ?group）；平衡等式按每个组（例如按每种货币）来断言。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/balancePartitionPredicate|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The predicate of a logic:AggregateBalanceConstraint on a posting whose value selects its partition — the debit side (logic:balanceDebitValue) or the credit side (logic:balanceCreditValue)."
msgstr "一个 logic:AggregateBalanceConstraint 作用于某条分录上、其值选择其分区的谓词——借方侧（logic:balanceDebitValue）或贷方侧（logic:balanceCreditValue）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/balancePostingPredicate|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The predicate of a logic:AggregateBalanceConstraint from the focus to each posting aggregated in the balance ($this <posting> ?posting)."
msgstr "一个 logic:AggregateBalanceConstraint 从焦点指向平衡中每条被聚合分录的谓词（$this <posting> ?posting）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/balanceValuePredicate|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The predicate of a logic:AggregateBalanceConstraint from the amount node to its numeric value (?amount <value> ?val), the quantity summed per partition."
msgstr "一个 logic:AggregateBalanceConstraint 从金额节点指向其数值的谓词（?amount <value> ?val），即按每个分区求和的量。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/bearsProperty|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates an entity to a property-value it carries, for the purpose of the emergence calculus: a whole and its proper parts each bearsProperty the values an logic:EmergenceAssessment reasons over. A deliberately thin logic-layer relation — NOT a metaphysical inherence claim; the bearer relation for logic:Modes and dispositions is asserted with their own domain properties (Principle 5), and gufo:inheresIn is never asserted. Whether a borne whole property reduces to the parts that bear it is exactly what logic:EmergenceAssessment decides; crucially, no rule propagates bearsProperty down logic:properPartOf, so an logic:Emergent whole property never reaches its parts (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "将一个实体关联到它所承载的属性值，用于涌现演算：一个整体及其各真部分各自 bearsProperty 某个 logic:EmergenceAssessment 所推理的值。一种有意保持轻薄的逻辑层关系——并非形而上学的内在性主张；logic:Modes 与倾向的承载关系借助它们自身的定义域属性来断言（原则 5），而 gufo:inheresIn 从不被断言。一个被承载的整体属性是否可还原为承载它的各部分，正是 logic:EmergenceAssessment 所判定的；关键在于，没有规则沿 logic:properPartOf 向下传播 bearsProperty，因此一个 logic:Emergent 的整体属性绝不会到达其各部分（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons 章节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/BelnapBilattice|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The four-valued Belnap truth algebra with the values true, false, both (over-determined / glut) and neither (under-determined / gap). The richest truth algebra a ReasoningContract may select; the classic sub-logics (FDE, LP, K3, classical) are carved out of this same algebra by the admissible-valuation policy and the designated-value set, which vary independently of the algebra."
msgstr "四值 Belnap 真值代数，取值为真、假、两者（过定 / 溢出）与两者皆非（欠定 / 空缺）。一个 ReasoningContract 可选择的最丰富真值代数；经典子逻辑（FDE、LP、K3、经典）由容许赋值策略与指定值集合从这同一代数中切分出来，二者与代数彼此独立地变化。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/BindingOptional|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:ColumnBinding value for a column that may be unbound in some rows (e.g. projected from a SPARQL OPTIONAL). Wire value `optional`."
msgstr "用于某些行中可能未绑定的列的 logic:ColumnBinding 值（例如从 SPARQL OPTIONAL 投影而来）。线值 `optional`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/BindingRequired|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:ColumnBinding value for a column bound in every result row. An unbound required column is a hard contract violation. Wire value `required`."
msgstr "用于在每个结果行中都被绑定的列的 logic:ColumnBinding 值。一个未绑定的必需列是一次硬性契约违规。线值 `required`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Blocked|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:FeasibilityStatus value for a goal with no path from the current situation, where the obstruction may yet lift — temporarily unreachable rather than permanently so. Contrast logic:Infeasible (unreachable in every reachable situation) and logic:Feasible (a path exists)."
msgstr "用于从当前情境无路径可达之目标的 logic:FeasibilityStatus 值，其障碍或仍可解除——暂时不可达而非永久如此。与 logic:Infeasible（在每个可达情境中皆不可达）及 logic:Feasible（存在一条路径）相对照。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/boundSituationType|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates an atomic, achievement, maintenance, or avoidance logic:GoalExpression to the logic:Situation type it targets — the situation whose obtaining (via logic:situationObtains at a state along the path) decides the goal. Domain logic:GoalExpression, range logic:Situation (stated in prose). Part of a goal expression's STRUCTURAL identity together with its kind and operands."
msgstr "将一个原子、达成、维持或规避的 logic:GoalExpression 关联到它所针对的 logic:Situation 类型——该情境的成立（沿路径某状态经 logic:situationObtains）判定该目标。定义域为 logic:GoalExpression，值域为 logic:Situation（以散文形式说明）。连同其种类与操作数，构成一个目标表达式结构性身份的一部分。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/branchActionSchema|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a policy branch to the logic:ActionSchema it invokes when selected — the next action the policy takes for this observation. Domain a policy branch, range logic:ActionSchema (stated in prose). The native evaluator surfaces it as logic:nextActionSchema on the policy when the branch's logic:branchGuard matches the observation."
msgstr "将一个策略分支关联到它被选中时所调用的 logic:ActionSchema——策略针对此观测所采取的下一动作。定义域为一个策略分支，值域为 logic:ActionSchema（以散文形式说明）。当该分支的 logic:branchGuard 与观测匹配时，原生求值器将其在策略上呈现为 logic:nextActionSchema。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/branchGuard|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a policy branch to the revealed situation that selects it: when the branch's logic:branchObservation reveals (logic:reveals) this situation, the branch is selected. Domain a policy branch, range the guarding logic:Situation (stated in prose). The guard the native evaluator matches against the observation's revealed situation."
msgstr "将一个策略分支关联到选择它的被揭示情境：当该分支的 logic:branchObservation 揭示（logic:reveals）此情境时，该分支被选中。定义域为一个策略分支，值域为作为守卫的 logic:Situation（以散文形式说明）。即原生求值器用以对照观测所揭示情境的守卫。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/branchObservation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a policy branch to the observation value its selection is conditioned on — the observation whose logic:reveals decides whether this branch fires. Domain a policy branch, range the logic:observation value (stated in prose). What makes a plan's branching observation-conditioned rather than fixed in advance."
msgstr "将一个策略分支关联到其选择所依条件的观测值——其 logic:reveals 判定此分支是否触发的观测。定义域为一个策略分支，值域为 logic:observation 值（以散文形式说明）。使一个计划的分支由观测决定而非事先固定之所在。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/BridgeView|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The floor rung: a commitment-shifting comorphism with NO satisfaction-preservation claim — the alignment to BFO, DOLCE, SUMO or YAMATO. A bridge view carries logic:morphismKind logic:CommitmentShiftingBridge, and the loss ledger refuses to emit owl:equivalentClass for it. Caps: no preservation law; the alignment is a by-reference bridge, never an identity."
msgstr "地板档级：一个转移承诺的余态射，不带任何满足性保持主张——对 BFO、DOLCE、SUMO 或 YAMATO 的对齐。一个桥视图携带 logic:morphismKind logic:CommitmentShiftingBridge，损失账本拒绝为其发出 owl:equivalentClass。上限：无保持律；该对齐是一座按引用的桥，绝非一个恒等。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/BudgetBoundedResource|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The resource execution policy that runs under a declared resource budget or bound: on exhaustion the engine returns a budget-exhausted, incomplete result — sound but incomplete — and never a false answer. The bounded counterpart of logic:CertifiedFragmentResource; a contract may carry both, since resource is an execution policy holding several independent properties together rather than a single complete-vs-bounded toggle."
msgstr "在已声明的资源预算或界限下运行的资源执行策略：耗尽时引擎返回一个预算耗尽的、不完整的结果——可靠但不完整——而绝不返回错误答案。logic:CertifiedFragmentResource 的有界对应物；一个契约可同时携带两者，因为资源是一种同时持有若干独立属性的执行策略，而非单一的完整对有界开关。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/BudgetExhausted|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:EvaluationStatus value for a run that hit a declared resource budget or bound before finishing. Wire value `budget-exhausted`. The specific budget that tripped (answers/inference/depth) is carried alongside as consumed-budget detail so the historical answer-status strings remain a lossless projection."
msgstr "用于在完成前触及已声明资源预算或界限的一次运行的 logic:EvaluationStatus 值。线值 `budget-exhausted`。被触发的具体预算（答案/推理/深度）作为已消耗预算细节一并携带，从而使历史性的答案状态字符串仍为一份无损投影。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/builtinArithmetic|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The native basic-math builtin: derives a value by the arithmetic operations (add, subtract, multiply, divide, compare) over numeric arguments. A derivational builtin (Principle 12, in-logic): the lightweight math a foundation needs, NOT heavy numerical domain computation (n-dimensional vector operations, SLAM, trajectory updates), which stays external by reference. Gated to logic:ProceduralPrologProfile; the closed operator set is evaluated by the native physical reasoning core as binding-pattern-keyed filters and generators. Residual modes (an unbound operand, division by zero, integer overflow) are typed hard failures, never wrong answers or silent approximations."
msgstr "原生基础数学内建：通过对数值参数的算术运算（加、减、乘、除、比较）派生一个值。一个派生型内建（原则 12，逻辑内）：一个基础所需的轻量数学，而非繁重的数值领域计算（n 维向量运算、SLAM、轨迹更新），后者按引用留在外部。受限于 logic:ProceduralPrologProfile；封闭的运算符集由原生物理推理核心作为按绑定模式键控的过滤器与生成器来求值。残余模式（未绑定的操作数、除以零、整数溢出）是带类型的硬失败，绝非错误答案或静默近似。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/builtinBilinearSquaredDistance|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The native metric-form builtin: derives the EXACT squared distance (x − y)ᵀ G (x − y) of two coordinate vectors under an authored symmetric bilinear form (a math:GramMatrix). A derivational builtin (Principle 12, in-logic): the lightweight exact-rational metric a foundation needs to decide a nearest-prototype question, NOT heavy external numerical domain computation. Its operands are IRIs into the math: slice — a math:GramMatrix and two math: vectors, whose exact-rational cells (math:hasEntry/math:hasComponent → math:RationalValue) the vocabulary owns; this builtin never re-authors that math: surface, it reads it. The squared distance is exact over ℚ (no √: the square root stays an output-edge seam, and √ is monotone so squared order equals distance order). Gated to logic:ProceduralPrologProfile; the closed function is evaluated by the native physical reasoning core as a binding-pattern-keyed filter/generator. Positive-definiteness of the form is certified once, off-gate, by the math: reasoned-graph gate; the runtime builtin trusts that certificate. Residual modes (an unbound operand, an absent or malformed form, a coordinate-length mismatch, exact-arithmetic overflow) are typed hard failures, never wrong answers or silent approximations."
msgstr "原生度量形式内建：在一个撰写的对称双线性形式（一个 math:GramMatrix）下派生两个坐标向量的精确平方距离 (x − y)ᵀ G (x − y)。一个派生型内建（原则 12，逻辑内）：一个基础判定最近原型问题所需的轻量精确有理度量，而非繁重的外部数值领域计算。它的操作数是指向 math: 切片的 IRI——一个 math:GramMatrix 和两个 math: 向量，其精确有理单元（math:hasEntry/math:hasComponent → math:RationalValue）由该词汇拥有；此内建从不重新撰写那个 math: 表面，它只读取。平方距离在 ℚ 上是精确的（无 √：平方根留作输出边接缝，且 √ 单调，故平方序等于距离序）。受限于 logic:ProceduralPrologProfile；封闭函数由原生物理推理核心作为按绑定模式键控的过滤器/生成器来求值。该形式的正定性由 math: 已推理图关卡在关卡之外认证一次；运行时内建信任该证书。残余模式（未绑定的操作数、缺失或畸形的形式、坐标长度不匹配、精确算术溢出）是带类型的硬失败，绝非错误答案或静默近似。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/builtinDateDifference|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The native date-arithmetic builtin: derives the difference between two dates, e.g. legalAge = year(now) − year(birth). A derivational builtin (Principle 12, in-logic): the lightweight date arithmetic a foundation needs, NOT heavy temporal-domain computation (calendar/datum transforms), which stays external by reference. Gated to logic:ProceduralPrologProfile; execution is seamed to the engine."
msgstr "原生日期算术内建：派生两个日期之间的差，例如 legalAge = year(now) − year(birth)。一个派生型内建（原则 12，逻辑内）：一个基础所需的轻量日期算术，而非繁重的时间领域计算（历法/基准变换），后者按引用留在外部。受限于 logic:ProceduralPrologProfile；执行被接缝到引擎。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Builtin|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A native computational primitive usable in rule bodies under logic:ProceduralPrologProfile: the registry entry for a derivational builtin such as string concatenation, date arithmetic, or basic math (criticism 8, LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md §OWL 2 criticisms). Builtins are the lightweight derivations a foundation genuinely needs (Principle 12, in-logic); heavy domain computation — geo/datum transforms, relation-algebra composition, vector operations — stays external by reference. The registry is declared here; builtin execution is seamed to the compiler/engine."
msgstr "在 logic:ProceduralPrologProfile 下可用于规则体的原生计算原语：一个派生型内建（如字符串连接、日期算术或基础数学）的注册表条目（criticism 8，LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md §OWL 2 criticisms）。内建是一个基础真正所需的轻量派生（原则 12，逻辑内）；繁重的领域计算——地理/基准变换、关系代数复合、向量运算——按引用留在外部。注册表在此声明；内建的执行被接缝到编译器/引擎。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/builtinStringConcat|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The native string-concatenation builtin: derives a string by joining its arguments, e.g. fullName = firstName + \" \" + lastName. A derivational builtin (Principle 12, in-logic): the lightweight string derivation a foundation needs, NOT heavy domain text processing, which stays external by reference. Gated to logic:ProceduralPrologProfile; execution is seamed to the engine."
msgstr "原生字符串连接内建：通过连接其参数派生一个字符串，例如 fullName = firstName + \" \" + lastName。一个派生型内建（原则 12，逻辑内）：一个基础所需的轻量字符串派生，而非繁重的领域文本处理，后者按引用留在外部。受限于 logic:ProceduralPrologProfile；执行被接缝到引擎。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/bundleHash|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The content-addressed identity (a blake3 digest) of the exact bundle a coherence outcome was checked over. The outcome is invalid for any bundle whose canonical hash differs. Single-valued. Domain logic:CoherenceCertificate or logic:CoherenceCheckAttestation (stated in prose)."
msgstr "某个一致性结果被检查所针对的确切包的内容寻址身份（一个 blake3 摘要）。对于任何其规范摘要不同的包，该结果无效。单值。定义域为 logic:CoherenceCertificate 或 logic:CoherenceCheckAttestation（以散文形式说明）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CandidateAccepted|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The canonical, axiom-bearing lifecycle state: a candidate a reviewer has promoted, reachable only through logic:CandidateUnderReview with a recorded logic:reviewedBy decision. A candidate asserted as accepted without that review is a checked governance violation, not a soft warning. Wire value `accepted`."
msgstr "规范的、承载公理的生命周期状态：一个评审者已晋升的候选，仅可经由带有已记录 logic:reviewedBy 决定的 logic:CandidateUnderReview 到达。一个未经该评审即被断言为已接受的候选是一次受检的治理违规，而非一个软性警告。线值 `accepted`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateBullshitTruthIndifference|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The equivalence-definition formalization candidate governing logic:bullshitTruthIndifference: to carry gmeow:claimModality gmeow:bullshit is exactly to be a gmeow:StandpointClaim held with gmeow:claimTruthDirectedness gmeow:truthIndifferent — Frankfurt's bullshit, neither true nor false under the standpoint. truthIndifferent uniquely selects the bullshit modality among the five, so it is definitional. Realized in the OWL / full-FOL projection (biconditional), non-monotone, disclosed in the loss ledger — NOT natively enforced. Harvested from gmeow:bullshit's skos:definition. Accepted through review with a positive case (logic:cqBullshitIndifferenceHolds) and a negative countermodel (logic:cqBullshitIndifferenceLieRejected)."
msgstr "治理 logic:bullshitTruthIndifference 的等价定义型形式化候选：携带 gmeow:claimModality gmeow:bullshit 恰恰就是成为一个以 gmeow:claimTruthDirectedness gmeow:truthIndifferent 持有的 gmeow:StandpointClaim——Frankfurt 的胡扯，在该立场下既非真亦非假。truthIndifferent 在五种之中唯一地选出胡扯模态，故它是定义性的。在 OWL / 完整 FOL 投影中实现（双条件），非单调，披露于损失账本——并不原生强制。收割自 gmeow:bullshit 的 skos:definition。经评审接受，附一个正面案例（logic:cqBullshitIndifferenceHolds）与一个负面反模型（logic:cqBullshitIndifferenceLieRejected）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateCategory|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:FormalizationCandidate to the logic:FormalizationCategory recording what kind of force its prose carried. Single-valued and REQUIRED: a candidate with no category resolving to the closed set is a hard governance error, never silently bucketed. Domain logic:FormalizationCandidate, range logic:FormalizationCategory."
msgstr "将一个 logic:FormalizationCandidate 关联到记录其散文所携带何种效力的 logic:FormalizationCategory。单值且必需：一个没有可归入封闭集合之类别的候选是一次硬性治理错误，绝不被静默归桶。定义域为 logic:FormalizationCandidate，值域为 logic:FormalizationCategory。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateContract|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:FormalizationCandidate to the logic:ReasoningContract (ME1) its proposed axiom would be interpreted under — the semantics that make 'sound' meaningful for it. Single-valued. Domain logic:FormalizationCandidate, range logic:ReasoningContract."
msgstr "将一个 logic:FormalizationCandidate 关联到其所提议公理将据以被解释的 logic:ReasoningContract（ME1）——使“可靠”对它而言有意义的语义。单值。定义域为 logic:FormalizationCandidate，值域为 logic:ReasoningContract。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateCounterpartNonTransitive|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The deliberate-non-assertion formalization candidate carrying the standing commitment that cross-realm counterpart identity (gmeow:counterpartOf) stays non-transitive: it is symmetric by design but must never chain, so contested, standpoint-indexed, or context-dependent claims are never transitively collapsed into owl:sameAs identity. Realized as the logic:NonEntailmentObligation logic:CounterpartNonTransitivityObligation and enforced by Arm A syntactic reachability over the counterpart rule heads (no rule head produces the predicate). Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation). The semantic risk is core-contaminating: a careless transitivity rule would corrupt the reasoned core by merging entities the design keeps distinct. Its harvest back-link (logic:candidateFormalizes gmeow:counterpartOf, logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition) ties it to the exact prose that commits to non-transitivity, and logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of that skos:definition text so a later edit surfaces as drift."
msgstr "承载“跨域对应物同一性（gmeow:counterpartOf）保持非传递”这一常驻承诺的有意不断言型形式化候选：它按设计是对称的，但绝不可链接，从而使有争议的、按立场索引的或依赖上下文的主张绝不被传递地坍缩为 owl:sameAs 同一性。实现为 logic:NonEntailmentObligation logic:CounterpartNonTransitivityObligation，并由 Arm A 对对应物规则头的句法可达性来强制（没有规则头产生该谓词）。经评审接受（logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation）。其语义风险会污染核心：一条草率的传递性规则会通过合并设计所保持相异的实体而败坏已推理核心。它的收割回链（logic:candidateFormalizes gmeow:counterpartOf，logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition）将其系于承诺非传递性的确切散文，而 logic:candidateSourceHash 是该 skos:definition 文本的 sha256，因此日后的编辑会作为漂移浮现。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateCrossNodeGlut|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The derivation-rule formalization candidate governing logic:ruleCrossNodeGlut: it harvests the cross-node-glut commitment in gmeow:findingAnchor's skos:definition (the anchor is the code-blind join key that lets a reasoner join two different-code findings at one place and detect an opposing-polarity conflict the same-fingerprint merge misses) into an enforced positive-Horn rule with an inequality guard and a non-trivial-anchor guard, materialized natively as logic:ExactPreservation. Because the reified-Horn chase cannot mint a fresh witness node, the glut is carried as the gmeow:crossNodeGlutWith edge rather than a minted gmeow:CrossNodeGlutWitness. Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation) with a positive case (logic:cqCrossNodeGlutHolds) and two countermodels (logic:cqCrossNodeGlutTrivialAnchorRejected, logic:cqCrossNodeGlutSamePolarityRejected). Its harvest back-link (logic:candidateFormalizes gmeow:findingAnchor, logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition) ties it to the exact prose, and logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of that definition text so a later edit surfaces as drift."
msgstr "治理 logic:ruleCrossNodeGlut 的派生规则型形式化候选：它将 gmeow:findingAnchor 的 skos:definition 中的跨节点溢出承诺（锚是对代码无视的连接键，使推理器能在一处连接两个不同代码的发现，并检测到同指纹合并所遗漏的相反极性冲突）收割为一条被强制的正 Horn 规则，配以一个不等式守卫和一个非平凡锚守卫，原生物化为 logic:ExactPreservation。由于具体化 Horn 追赶无法铸造新的见证节点，该溢出由 gmeow:crossNodeGlutWith 边承载，而非一个被铸造的 gmeow:CrossNodeGlutWitness。经评审接受（logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation），附一个正面案例（logic:cqCrossNodeGlutHolds）与两个反模型（logic:cqCrossNodeGlutTrivialAnchorRejected、logic:cqCrossNodeGlutSamePolarityRejected）。它的收割回链（logic:candidateFormalizes gmeow:findingAnchor，logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition）将其系于确切散文，而 logic:candidateSourceHash 是该定义文本的 sha256，因此日后的编辑会作为漂移浮现。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateDeceptionHeldProjectedDivergence|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The necessary-condition formalization candidate governing logic:deceptionHeldProjectedDivergence: every gmeow:eventTypeDeception event carries a gmeow:heldStandpoint and a gmeow:projectedStandpoint doxastic claim whose modalities diverge — the gap is the act, not a truth verdict. A necessary, not sufficient, condition (a licensed-falsehood projection also has a gap yet is not deception; see logic:candidateLicensedFalsehoodNotDeception). Realized in the OWL / full-FOL projection (nested existential with strong negation), non-monotone, disclosed in the loss ledger — NOT natively enforced. Harvested from gmeow:eventTypeDeception's skos:definition, so an edit to that prose surfaces as drift. Accepted through review with a positive case (logic:cqDeceptionDivergenceHolds) and a negative countermodel (logic:cqDeceptionDivergenceGapRejected)."
msgstr "治理 logic:deceptionHeldProjectedDivergence 的必要条件型形式化候选：每一个 gmeow:eventTypeDeception 事件都携带一个 gmeow:heldStandpoint 和一个 gmeow:projectedStandpoint 信念主张，二者的模态相互背离——此鸿沟即行为本身，而非一个真值裁决。一个必要而非充分的条件（一次获许可的虚假投影同样有一道鸿沟却并非欺骗；见 logic:candidateLicensedFalsehoodNotDeception）。在 OWL / 完整 FOL 投影中实现（带强否定的嵌套存在量词），非单调，披露于损失账本——并不原生强制。收割自 gmeow:eventTypeDeception 的 skos:definition，因此对该散文的一次编辑会作为漂移浮现。经评审接受，附一个正面案例（logic:cqDeceptionDivergenceHolds）与一个负面反模型（logic:cqDeceptionDivergenceGapRejected）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateDeliberateNonAssertion|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Marks a logic:FormalizationCandidate as one of the ontology's deliberate-non-assertion boundaries — an intentional refusal to over-assert that the foundation commits to and is held against: a forbidden entailment carried by a logic:NonEntailmentObligation, an integrity constraint whose violation is a finding, or a deliberately preserved class overlap. Its role is enumerability: the marked set IS the deliberate-non-assertion report, and it deliberately cuts across logic:candidateCategory (a boundary may be a logic:CategoryNonEntailmentObligation, a logic:CategoryIntegrityConstraint or a logic:CategoryDeliberateOverlap), so the whole boundary set is queryable as one report rather than inferred from an overloaded category facet (an integrity-constraint boundary is not distinguishable from an ordinary integrity constraint by category alone). Present and true on exactly the guardrail candidates; single-valued, xsd:boolean. Domain logic:FormalizationCandidate."
msgstr "将一个 logic:FormalizationCandidate 标记为本体的蓄意不断言边界之一——一种有意拒绝过度断言的立场,基础对此作出承诺并据以约束自身:由 logic:NonEntailmentObligation 承载的被禁蕴涵、其违背即构成一项发现的完整性约束,或一处被蓄意保留的类重叠。其作用在于可枚举性:被标记的集合即为蓄意不断言报告,并且它有意横跨 logic:candidateCategory(一处边界可能是 logic:CategoryNonEntailmentObligation、logic:CategoryIntegrityConstraint 或 logic:CategoryDeliberateOverlap),因而整个边界集合可作为单一报告被查询,而非从一个负载过重的类别面向推断而来(仅凭类别无法把一处完整性约束边界与一项普通完整性约束区分开)。恰好在护栏候选项上呈现且为真;单值,xsd:boolean。定义域 logic:FormalizationCandidate。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateDiagnosticMetaExtensibility|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The derivation-rule formalization candidate governing logic:ruleRootFinding, the extensibility demonstrator: it harvests the extension-point commitment in gmeow:DiagnosticMetaRule's skos:definition (the reasoner enumerates every gmeow:DiagnosticMetaRule and applies it, so a new meta-finding is added by authoring a new tagged rule with zero engine change) into an enforced positive-Horn rule deriving gmeow:RootFinding, materialized natively as logic:ExactPreservation. Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation) with a positive case (logic:cqRootFindingHolds) and a negative countermodel (logic:cqRootFindingNonRootRejected). Its harvest back-link (logic:candidateFormalizes gmeow:DiagnosticMetaRule, logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition) ties it to the exact prose, and logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of that definition text so a later edit surfaces as drift."
msgstr "该派生规则型形式化候选项规约 logic:ruleRootFinding,即可扩展性演示器:它从 gmeow:DiagnosticMetaRule 的 skos:definition(推理器枚举每一个 gmeow:DiagnosticMetaRule 并加以应用,因此只需撰写一条新的带标签规则、零引擎改动即可添加一个新的元发现)中采集扩展点承诺,形成一条派生 gmeow:RootFinding 的、被强制执行的正 Horn 规则,原生地物化为 logic:ExactPreservation。经审查接受(logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation),配有一个正例(logic:cqRootFindingHolds)和一个负向反模型(logic:cqRootFindingNonRootRejected)。其采集反向链接(logic:candidateFormalizes gmeow:DiagnosticMetaRule,logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition)将其绑定到确切的散文文本,而 logic:candidateSourceHash 是该定义文本的 sha256,因此后续的编辑会以漂移形式显现。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateEndurantPerdurantDisjoint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The formalization candidate that harvests the continuant/occurrent divide from logic:Endurant's skos:definition (which contrasts logic:Perdurant, which has temporal parts) into the enforced logic:Endurant owl:disjointWith logic:Perdurant integrity constraint asserted above. Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation) with a positive case (logic:cqEndurantPerdurantDisjointHolds) and a negative countermodel (logic:cqEndurantPerdurantClashRejected); its harvest back-link (logic:candidateFormalizes logic:Endurant, logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition) ties it to the exact prose, and logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of that definition text so a later edit surfaces as drift. The native DL coherence gate reads the owl:disjointWith directly, forcing a both-endurant-and-perdurant individual to owl:Nothing."
msgstr "该形式化候选项从 logic:Endurant 的 skos:definition(其与 logic:Perdurant 相对照,后者具有时间部分)中采集延续者/发生者的划分,形成上文所断言的、被强制执行的 logic:Endurant owl:disjointWith logic:Perdurant 完整性约束。经审查接受(logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation),配有一个正例(logic:cqEndurantPerdurantDisjointHolds)和一个负向反模型(logic:cqEndurantPerdurantClashRejected);其采集反向链接(logic:candidateFormalizes logic:Endurant,logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition)将其绑定到确切的散文文本,而 logic:candidateSourceHash 是该定义文本的 sha256,因此后续的编辑会以漂移形式显现。原生 DL 一致性门直接读取该 owl:disjointWith,将一个既是延续者又是发生者的个体强制为 owl:Nothing。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateEntitySortalCovering|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The necessary-condition formalization candidate governing the class covering that every gmeow:Entity is one of {gmeow:Agent, gmeow:InformationObject, gmeow:PhysicalObject, gmeow:SocialObject}. Its source is gmeow:Entity's gmeow:howToUse prose, which enumerates the four sortals. The covering is realized ONLY in the OWL projection as an owl:unionOf (a class-covering disjunction); it is NON-monotone and is disclosed in the loss ledger — the native monotone StratifiedNAF chase does NOT enforce a disjunctive head, so this is projection-only, not natively enforced. It carries NO harvest back-link (the covering is a doc-level enumeration, not a single harvestable axiom field). Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation) with a positive case (logic:cqEntitySortalCoveringHolds) and a negative case (logic:cqEntitySortalCoveringGapRejected); logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of that gmeow:howToUse text for drift detection."
msgstr "该必要条件型形式化候选项规约以下类覆盖:每个 gmeow:Entity 都是 {gmeow:Agent, gmeow:InformationObject, gmeow:PhysicalObject, gmeow:SocialObject} 之一。其来源是 gmeow:Entity 的 gmeow:howToUse 散文,其中枚举了这四个 sortal。该覆盖仅在 OWL 投影中以 owl:unionOf(一种类覆盖析取)实现;它是非单调的,并在损失账本中披露——原生的单调 StratifiedNAF 追逐并不强制析取式头部,因此这只属于投影,而非原生强制。它不携带任何采集反向链接(该覆盖是文档层面的枚举,而非单一可采集的公理字段)。经审查接受(logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation),配有一个正例(logic:cqEntitySortalCoveringHolds)和一个负例(logic:cqEntitySortalCoveringGapRejected);logic:candidateSourceHash 是该 gmeow:howToUse 文本的 sha256,用于漂移检测。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateEventSituationDisjoint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The formalization candidate governing the logic:Event owl:disjointWith logic:Situation integrity constraint asserted above: an occurrence that unfolds in time is disjoint from the static configuration a situation records. Unlike the other partition axioms this contrast is NOT stated in a single harvestable annotation field, so the candidate carries NO harvest back-link (neither logic:candidateFormalizes nor logic:candidateSourceField — never a half-link); its provenance records a doc-section/foundation harvest over the occurrent structure instead. Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation) with a positive case (logic:cqEventSituationDisjointHolds) and a negative countermodel (logic:cqEventSituationClashRejected); logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of logic:Event's skos:definition so an edit to that anchor prose surfaces as drift. The native DL coherence gate reads the owl:disjointWith directly, forcing a both-event-and-situation individual to owl:Nothing."
msgstr "该形式化候选项规约上文所断言的 logic:Event owl:disjointWith logic:Situation 完整性约束:一个在时间中展开的事件与情境所记录的静态配置互不相交。与其他划分公理不同,此对照并未在单一可采集的注释字段中表达,因此该候选项不携带任何采集反向链接(既无 logic:candidateFormalizes 也无 logic:candidateSourceField——绝不留半个链接);其出处转而记录一次针对发生者结构的文档章节或基础层面的采集。经审查接受(logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation),配有一个正例(logic:cqEventSituationDisjointHolds)和一个负向反模型(logic:cqEventSituationClashRejected);logic:candidateSourceHash 是 logic:Event 的 skos:definition 的 sha256,因此对该锚定散文的编辑会以漂移形式显现。原生 DL 一致性门直接读取该 owl:disjointWith,将一个既是事件又是情境的个体强制为 owl:Nothing。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateExtractionProvenance|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The provenance of a candidate's extraction — what produced it (an extractor identifier, run, or model invocation reference). Records that an automated extraction is exactly that, so it enters at logic:CandidateProposed and earns no canonical force without review. Single-valued, xsd:string. Domain logic:FormalizationCandidate."
msgstr "某候选项抽取的出处——即产生它的事物(一个抽取器标识、一次运行或一个模型调用引用)。记录一次自动化抽取正是如此,因而它进入 logic:CandidateProposed 状态,并且在未经审查时不获得任何规范效力。单值,xsd:string。定义域 logic:FormalizationCandidate。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateFalsehoodIsRefutedClaim|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The equivalence-definition formalization candidate governing logic:falsehoodIsRefutedClaim: to carry gmeow:claimModality gmeow:refuted is exactly to be a gmeow:StandpointClaim that necessarily denies its proposition (gmeow:polarityDeny ∧ gmeow:modalForceNecessary = □¬). This pins 'falsehood = refuted StandpointClaim' as a frame-relative configuration, never a global truth flag, and ties the legacy five-value modality twin to its canonical axes. Realized in the OWL / full-FOL projection (biconditional), non-monotone, disclosed in the loss ledger — NOT natively enforced. Harvested from gmeow:refuted's skos:definition. Accepted through review with a positive case (logic:cqFalsehoodRefutedHolds) and a negative countermodel (logic:cqFalsehoodRefutedGlobalTruthRejected)."
msgstr "该等价定义型形式化候选项规约 logic:falsehoodIsRefutedClaim:携带 gmeow:claimModality gmeow:refuted,恰恰就是成为一个必然否定其命题的 gmeow:StandpointClaim(gmeow:polarityDeny ∧ gmeow:modalForceNecessary = □¬)。这将「虚假 = 被反驳的 gmeow:StandpointClaim」确定为一种相对于框架的配置,而绝非全局真值标志,并把遗留的五值模态孪生对象绑定到其规范轴。实现于 OWL / 完整 FOL 投影(双条件式),非单调,在损失账本中披露——并非原生强制。采集自 gmeow:refuted 的 skos:definition。经审查接受,配有一个正例(logic:cqFalsehoodRefutedHolds)和一个负向反模型(logic:cqFalsehoodRefutedGlobalTruthRejected)。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateFindingCluster|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The derivation-rule formalization candidate governing logic:ruleFindingCluster, logic:ruleClusterRoot, and logic:ruleFindingClusterType: it harvests the grouping commitment in gmeow:FindingCluster's skos:definition (a grouping of findings that share one gmeow:findingRootCause, its members linked by gmeow:findingCluster and its shared root carried by gmeow:clusterRoot) into three enforced positive-Horn rules over the root-cause output, materialized natively as logic:ExactPreservation. Because fresh-node minting is not expressible in the reified-Horn chase, the cluster is identified by its root finding. Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation) with a positive case (logic:cqFindingClusterHolds) and a negative countermodel (logic:cqFindingClusterDistinctRootsRejected). Its harvest back-link (logic:candidateFormalizes gmeow:FindingCluster, logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition) ties it to the exact prose, and logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of that definition text so a later edit surfaces as drift."
msgstr "该派生规则型形式化候选项规约 logic:ruleFindingCluster、logic:ruleClusterRoot 和 logic:ruleFindingClusterType:它从 gmeow:FindingCluster 的 skos:definition(共享同一 gmeow:findingRootCause 的一组发现,其成员由 gmeow:findingCluster 相连,其共享根由 gmeow:clusterRoot 承载)中采集分组承诺,形成针对根因输出的三条被强制执行的正 Horn 规则,原生地物化为 logic:ExactPreservation。由于在具体化 Horn 追逐中无法表达新节点的铸造,该分组以其根发现来标识。经审查接受(logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation),配有一个正例(logic:cqFindingClusterHolds)和一个负向反模型(logic:cqFindingClusterDistinctRootsRejected)。其采集反向链接(logic:candidateFormalizes gmeow:FindingCluster,logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition)将其绑定到确切的散文文本,而 logic:candidateSourceHash 是该定义文本的 sha256,因此后续的编辑会以漂移形式显现。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateFindingRootCause|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The derivation-rule formalization candidate governing logic:ruleFindingHasAntecedent and logic:ruleFindingRootCause: it harvests the root-cause commitment in gmeow:findingRootCause's skos:definition (the shared root antecedent reached by following gmeow:findingAntecedent transitively up the witness DAG to a childless witness, honestly the shared root and not a dominator) into an enforced stratified-negation rule set, materialized natively as logic:ExactPreservation. The childless test is a negation-as-failure over the derived gmeow:findingHasAntecedent marker, so the contract is logic:StratifiedNAFProfile. Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation) with a positive case (logic:cqFindingRootCauseHolds) and a negative countermodel (logic:cqFindingRootCauseNonRootRejected). Its harvest back-link (logic:candidateFormalizes gmeow:findingRootCause, logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition) ties it to the exact prose, and logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of that definition text so a later edit surfaces as drift."
msgstr "该派生规则型形式化候选项规约 logic:ruleFindingHasAntecedent 和 logic:ruleFindingRootCause:它从 gmeow:findingRootCause 的 skos:definition(通过沿 gmeow:findingAntecedent 传递地向上遍历见证 DAG 直至一个无子见证而到达的共享根前件,如实为共享根而非支配点)中采集根因承诺,形成一组被强制执行的分层否定规则,原生地物化为 logic:ExactPreservation。无子测试是对派生标记 gmeow:findingHasAntecedent 的失败即否定,因此其契约为 logic:StratifiedNAFProfile。经审查接受(logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation),配有一个正例(logic:cqFindingRootCauseHolds)和一个负向反模型(logic:cqFindingRootCauseNonRootRejected)。其采集反向链接(logic:candidateFormalizes gmeow:findingRootCause,logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition)将其绑定到确切的散文文本,而 logic:candidateSourceHash 是该定义文本的 sha256,因此后续的编辑会以漂移形式显现。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateFindingTraces|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The derivation-rule formalization candidate governing logic:ruleFindingTracesBase and logic:ruleFindingTracesStep: it harvests the transitive-reachability commitment in gmeow:findingAntecedent's skos:definition (the reasoner joins UP the witness DAG, following the edge transitively to the root antecedent) into two enforced positive-Horn rules deriving the closure gmeow:findingTraces, materialized natively as logic:ExactPreservation. Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation) with a positive case (logic:cqFindingTracesHolds) and a negative countermodel (logic:cqFindingTracesNonReachRejected). Its harvest back-link (logic:candidateFormalizes gmeow:findingAntecedent, logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition) ties it to the exact prose, and logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of that definition text so a later edit surfaces as drift."
msgstr "该派生规则型形式化候选项规约 logic:ruleFindingTracesBase 和 logic:ruleFindingTracesStep:它从 gmeow:findingAntecedent 的 skos:definition(推理器沿见证 DAG 向上连接,传递地沿该边到达根前件)中采集传递可达性承诺,形成两条派生闭包 gmeow:findingTraces 的、被强制执行的正 Horn 规则,原生地物化为 logic:ExactPreservation。经审查接受(logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation),配有一个正例(logic:cqFindingTracesHolds)和一个负向反模型(logic:cqFindingTracesNonReachRejected)。其采集反向链接(logic:candidateFormalizes gmeow:findingAntecedent,logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition)将其绑定到确切的散文文本,而 logic:candidateSourceHash 是该定义文本的 sha256,因此后续的编辑会以漂移形式显现。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateFormalizes|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The harvest back-link: relates a logic:FormalizationCandidate to the prose-bearing term (a gmeow: or logic: term, stated in prose) whose constraint its axiom formalizes, read together with logic:candidateSourceField (which of that term's annotation fields — skos:definition, gmeow:useWhen or gmeow:avoidWhen). Where logic:candidateSourceHash anchors the candidate to its source text by hash and logic:candidateExtractionProvenance records what produced it, this names the exact ontology term the harvested axiom keeps coherent, so harvest coverage is queryable in both directions. Present exactly when the source IS a term's annotation field (a doc-section source stays recorded in provenance alone, never a fabricated term-link); single-valued. Distinct from logic:formalizes, which bridges a logic: term to a gmeow: concept and is never a reasoned axiom. Domain logic:FormalizationCandidate."
msgstr "采集反向链接:将一个 logic:FormalizationCandidate 关联到承载散文的词项(一个 gmeow: 或 logic: 词项,以散文表述),其公理形式化了该词项的约束,并与 logic:candidateSourceField(该词项的哪个注释字段——skos:definition、gmeow:useWhen 或 gmeow:avoidWhen)一并解读。logic:candidateSourceHash 以哈希把候选项锚定到其源文本,logic:candidateExtractionProvenance 记录产生它的事物,而本属性则指明被采集公理所维系一致的确切本体词项,因而采集覆盖可在两个方向上查询。恰当源确为某词项的注释字段时呈现(文档章节来源仅记录在出处中,绝不伪造词项链接);单值。它有别于 logic:formalizes,后者把一个 logic: 词项桥接到一个 gmeow: 概念,且从不是被推理的公理。定义域 logic:FormalizationCandidate。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateFrameRelativity|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The integrity-constraint formalization candidate that harvests Principle 11 frame-relativity from logic:referenceFrame's skos:definition into the enforced logic:MeasurementFrameMissing constraint: a logic:measuredValue is meaningful only together with the logic:referenceFrame it is expressed in, so a frame-free value is ill-formed and two frame-relative values are never equated frame-free. Violation is a finding, not a derivation, materialized by the existing foundation quality discipline. Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation) with a positive case (logic:cqFrameRelativityHolds — a framed value stays well-formed) and a negative countermodel (logic:cqFrameRelativityFramelessRejected — a frame-free value is the logic:MeasurementFrameMissing violation). Its harvest back-link (logic:candidateFormalizes logic:referenceFrame, logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition) ties it to the exact prose, and logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of that definition text so a later edit surfaces as drift."
msgstr "该完整性约束型形式化候选项从 logic:referenceFrame 的 skos:definition 中采集原则 11 的框架相对性,形成被强制执行的 logic:MeasurementFrameMissing 约束:一个 logic:measuredValue 只有连同其所表达的 logic:referenceFrame 才有意义,因此无框架的值是病态的,两个相对于框架的值绝不会在无框架的情况下被等同。违背是一项发现,而非派生,由基础中既有的质量纪律物化。经审查接受(logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation),配有一个正例(logic:cqFrameRelativityHolds——一个带框架的值仍然良构)和一个负向反模型(logic:cqFrameRelativityFramelessRejected——一个无框架的值即 logic:MeasurementFrameMissing 违背)。其采集反向链接(logic:candidateFormalizes logic:referenceFrame,logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition)将其绑定到确切的散文文本,而 logic:candidateSourceHash 是该定义文本的 sha256,因此后续的编辑会以漂移形式显现。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateFunctionalComplexKindDisjoint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The net-new-enforcement formalization candidate that harvests the pairwise disjointness of the three mereological individuation kinds (logic:Collection, logic:FunctionalComplex, logic:Quantity) from their skos:definition prose into enforced owl:disjointWith integrity constraints: the demonstration that the harvest mechanism creates axioms that did NOT exist before, not merely a link to an already-typed one. None of the three was asserted owl:disjointWith on origin/main; the prose contrasts them as distinct individuation modes (logic:FunctionalComplex's Definition names both other kinds explicitly). Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation) with a positive case (logic:cqFunctionalComplexKindDisjointHolds) and a negative countermodel (logic:cqFunctionalComplexKindDisjointOverlapRejected); its harvest back-link (logic:candidateFormalizes logic:FunctionalComplex, logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition) ties it to the exact prose, and logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of that definition text so a later edit to the prose surfaces as drift. The native DL coherence gate reads the resulting owl:disjointWith directly, forcing a two-kind individual to owl:Nothing."
msgstr "该全新强制型形式化候选项从三种部分论个体化种类(logic:Collection、logic:FunctionalComplex、logic:Quantity)的 skos:definition 散文中采集其两两不相交,形成被强制执行的 owl:disjointWith 完整性约束:此举证明采集机制创造出此前并不存在的公理,而非仅仅链接到一个已被类型化的公理。三者中在 origin/main 上都未被断言 owl:disjointWith;散文将它们对照为不同的个体化模式(logic:FunctionalComplex 的定义明确点出另外两个种类)。经审查接受(logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation),配有一个正例(logic:cqFunctionalComplexKindDisjointHolds)和一个负向反模型(logic:cqFunctionalComplexKindDisjointOverlapRejected);其采集反向链接(logic:candidateFormalizes logic:FunctionalComplex,logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition)将其绑定到确切的散文文本,而 logic:candidateSourceHash 是该定义文本的 sha256,因此后续对散文的编辑会以漂移形式显现。原生 DL 一致性门直接读取由此得到的 owl:disjointWith,将一个属于两种种类的个体强制为 owl:Nothing。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateGateFatalVerdict|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The derivation-rule formalization candidate governing logic:ruleGateFatalVerdict: it harvests the up-set construction documented in gmeow:findingGateVerdict's skos:definition (the verdict is gmeow:gateFatal exactly on the principal up-set ↑(Error, Blocking, Binding), the meet of the severity, blocking-projected category, and standpoint axes) into an enforced positive-Horn derivation rule, materialized natively as logic:ExactPreservation — the RDF-side image of the single Rust gmeow_errors::grade::gate() policy morphism. Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation) with a positive case (logic:cqGateFatalVerdictHolds) and two never-gate countermodels (logic:cqGateFatalAdvisoryNeverFatalRejected, logic:cqGateFatalPermittedConflictNeverFatalRejected). Its harvest back-link (logic:candidateFormalizes gmeow:findingGateVerdict, logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition) ties it to the exact prose, and logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of that definition text so a later edit surfaces as drift."
msgstr "该派生规则型形式化候选项规约 logic:ruleGateFatalVerdict:它从 gmeow:findingGateVerdict 的 skos:definition 所记载的上集构造(裁决恰在主上集 ↑(Error, Blocking, Binding) 上为 gmeow:gateFatal,即严重度、按阻塞投影的类别与立场三轴的下确界)中采集,形成一条被强制执行的正 Horn 派生规则,原生地物化为 logic:ExactPreservation——即单一 Rust 策略态射 gmeow_errors::grade::gate() 在 RDF 侧的映像。经审查接受(logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation),配有一个正例(logic:cqGateFatalVerdictHolds)和两个永不阻断的反模型(logic:cqGateFatalAdvisoryNeverFatalRejected、logic:cqGateFatalPermittedConflictNeverFatalRejected)。其采集反向链接(logic:candidateFormalizes gmeow:findingGateVerdict,logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition)将其绑定到确切的散文文本,而 logic:candidateSourceHash 是该定义文本的 sha256,因此后续的编辑会以漂移形式显现。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateIndirectContributor|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The derivation-rule formalization candidate governing logic:ruleIndirectContributor: it harvests the productive composition documented in gmeow:indirectContributor's skos:definition (indirect contributors are the agents reached by composing gmeow:wasGeneratedBy with gmeow:wasAssociatedWith) into an enforced positive-Horn derivation rule, materialized natively as logic:ExactPreservation. Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation) with a positive case (logic:cqIndirectContributorHolds) and a negative countermodel (logic:cqIndirectContributorDirectAttributionRejected), and bound to the non-entailment obligation logic:IndirectContributorNotAttributionObligation that forbids the derived edge from ever becoming asserted gmeow:wasAttributedTo. Its harvest back-link (logic:candidateFormalizes gmeow:indirectContributor, logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition) ties it to the exact prose, and logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of that definition text so a later edit surfaces as drift."
msgstr "该派生规则型形式化候选项规约 logic:ruleIndirectContributor:它从 gmeow:indirectContributor 的 skos:definition(间接贡献者是通过将 gmeow:wasGeneratedBy 与 gmeow:wasAssociatedWith 复合而到达的施动者)中采集其所记载的能产复合,形成一条被强制执行的正 Horn 派生规则,原生地物化为 logic:ExactPreservation。经审查接受(logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation),配有一个正例(logic:cqIndirectContributorHolds)和一个负向反模型(logic:cqIndirectContributorDirectAttributionRejected),并绑定到非蕴涵义务 logic:IndirectContributorNotAttributionObligation,该义务禁止这条派生边曾成为被断言的 gmeow:wasAttributedTo。其采集反向链接(logic:candidateFormalizes gmeow:indirectContributor,logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition)将其绑定到确切的散文文本,而 logic:candidateSourceHash 是该定义文本的 sha256,因此后续的编辑会以漂移形式显现。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateInstantiatesWork|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The derivation-rule formalization candidate governing logic:ruleInstantiatesWork: it harvests the copy-to-Work composition documented in gmeow:instantiatesWork's skos:definition (an Item instantiates the Work reached by composing gmeow:exemplifies, gmeow:embodies and gmeow:realizes) into an enforced positive-Horn derivation rule, materialized natively as logic:ExactPreservation. Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation) with a positive case (logic:cqInstantiatesWorkHolds) and a negative countermodel (logic:cqInstantiatesWorkBrokenSpineRejected). Its harvest back-link (logic:candidateFormalizes gmeow:instantiatesWork, logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition) ties it to the exact prose, and logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of that definition text so a later edit surfaces as drift."
msgstr "该派生规则型形式化候选项规约 logic:ruleInstantiatesWork:它从 gmeow:instantiatesWork 的 skos:definition(一个 Item 实例化通过复合 gmeow:exemplifies、gmeow:embodies 与 gmeow:realizes 而到达的 Work)中采集其所记载的复本到作品复合,形成一条被强制执行的正 Horn 派生规则,原生地物化为 logic:ExactPreservation。经审查接受(logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation),配有一个正例(logic:cqInstantiatesWorkHolds)和一个负向反模型(logic:cqInstantiatesWorkBrokenSpineRejected)。其采集反向链接(logic:candidateFormalizes gmeow:instantiatesWork,logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition)将其绑定到确切的散文文本,而 logic:candidateSourceHash 是该定义文本的 sha256,因此后续的编辑会以漂移形式显现。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateIntentNotEntailed|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The deliberate-non-assertion formalization candidate carrying the standing commitment that deceptive intent must never be entailed: gmeow:deceptiveIntentClaim is an attributed, defeasible standpoint claim, so a held≠projected structural gap is EVIDENCE, never ENTAILMENT, of intent, and the foundation must never derive the predicate. Realized as the logic:NonEntailmentObligation logic:IntentNotFromDeceptionObligation and enforced by Arm A syntactic reachability over the rule heads plus Arm B finite closure over the materialized derivation graph. Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation). The semantic risk is core-contaminating: a mis-formalization that closed this inference would corrupt the reasoned core with an entailed intent, so the guardrail protects the core, not merely a projection. Its harvest back-link (logic:candidateFormalizes gmeow:deceptiveIntentClaim, logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldAvoidWhen) ties it to the exact prose that forbids the entailment, and logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of that gmeow:avoidWhen text so a later edit surfaces as drift."
msgstr "该蓄意不断言型形式化候选项承载如下长驻承诺:欺骗性意图绝不可被蕴涵:gmeow:deceptiveIntentClaim 是一项被归属的、可废止的立场主张,因此持有≠投影的结构性缺口是意图的证据,而绝非其蕴涵,基础绝不可派生该谓词。它实现为 logic:NonEntailmentObligation logic:IntentNotFromDeceptionObligation,并由 A 臂对规则头部的句法可达性,加上 B 臂对已物化派生图的有限闭包共同强制执行。经审查接受(logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation)。其语义风险会污染核心:若一次错误形式化闭合了此推理,便会以一个被蕴涵的意图腐蚀被推理的核心,因此该护栏保护的是核心,而不仅仅是一个投影。其采集反向链接(logic:candidateFormalizes gmeow:deceptiveIntentClaim,logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldAvoidWhen)将其绑定到禁止该蕴涵的确切散文,而 logic:candidateSourceHash 是该 gmeow:avoidWhen 文本的 sha256,因此后续的编辑会以漂移形式显现。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateLicensedFalsehoodNotDeception|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The necessary-condition formalization candidate governing logic:licensedFalsehoodNotDeception: a gmeow:Event whose projected standpoint is gmeow:veridicalityLicensedFalsehood is excluded from gmeow:eventTypeDeception — the fiction/satire/sarcasm safety property that separates harmless non-truth-asserting frames from deception. Realized in the OWL / full-FOL projection (strong negation), non-monotone, disclosed in the loss ledger — NOT natively enforced. Harvested from gmeow:veridicalityLicensedFalsehood's skos:definition. Accepted through review with a positive case (logic:cqLicensedFalsehoodSafeHolds) and a negative countermodel (logic:cqLicensedFalsehoodDeceptionRejected)."
msgstr "该必要条件型形式化候选项规约 logic:licensedFalsehoodNotDeception:一个投影立场为 gmeow:veridicalityLicensedFalsehood 的 gmeow:Event 被排除于 gmeow:eventTypeDeception 之外——即把无害的、不作真值断言的框架与欺骗区分开的虚构/讽刺/反讽安全性质。实现于 OWL / 完整 FOL 投影(强否定),非单调,在损失账本中披露——并非原生强制。采集自 gmeow:veridicalityLicensedFalsehood 的 skos:definition。经审查接受,配有一个正例(logic:cqLicensedFalsehoodSafeHolds)和一个负向反模型(logic:cqLicensedFalsehoodDeceptionRejected)。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateLifecycle|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:FormalizationCandidate to its current logic:CandidateLifecycleState. Single-valued. logic:CandidateAccepted is the canonical state and is legitimate only with a recorded logic:reviewedBy decision. Domain logic:FormalizationCandidate, range logic:CandidateLifecycleState."
msgstr "将一个 logic:FormalizationCandidate 关联到其当前的 logic:CandidateLifecycleState。单值。logic:CandidateAccepted 是规范状态,仅在带有已记录的 logic:reviewedBy 决定时才合法。定义域 logic:FormalizationCandidate,值域 logic:CandidateLifecycleState。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CandidateLifecycleState|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The closed value class of the logic:candidateLifecycle facet: the four-state machine a logic:FormalizationCandidate moves through. Its individuals are logic:CandidateProposed (entry; every extraction lands here), logic:CandidateUnderReview, logic:CandidateAccepted (canonical, axiom-bearing) and logic:CandidateRejected. logic:CandidateAccepted is reachable only through logic:CandidateUnderReview with a recorded logic:reviewedBy decision, never directly. The set is closed, so a misspelt state names no declared value and is rejected (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, §Typed formalization governance)."
msgstr "logic:candidateLifecycle 面向的封闭取值类:一个 logic:FormalizationCandidate 所经历的四状态机。其个体为 logic:CandidateProposed(入口;每次抽取都落到此处)、logic:CandidateUnderReview、logic:CandidateAccepted(规范的、携带公理的)以及 logic:CandidateRejected。logic:CandidateAccepted 只能经由 logic:CandidateUnderReview 并带有已记录的 logic:reviewedBy 决定而到达,绝不能直接到达。该集合是封闭的,因此一个拼错的状态并不指称任何已声明的取值,会被拒绝(design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md,§Typed formalization governance)。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateNegativeCase|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:FormalizationCandidate to a negative case or countermodel — a gmeow:CompetencyQuestion the axiom must NOT satisfy, recording the boundary the formalization must respect (range gmeow:CompetencyQuestion, stated in prose). Domain logic:FormalizationCandidate."
msgstr "将一个 logic:FormalizationCandidate 关联到一个负例或反模型——一个公理不得满足的 gmeow:CompetencyQuestion,记录形式化须遵守的边界(值域 gmeow:CompetencyQuestion,以散文表述)。定义域 logic:FormalizationCandidate。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateNonEntailment|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:FormalizationCandidate to a logic:NonEntailmentObligation its axiom is required to respect — the forbidden conclusion the formalization must not let the engine draw. Domain logic:FormalizationCandidate, range logic:NonEntailmentObligation."
msgstr "将一个 logic:FormalizationCandidate 关联到其公理须遵守的一项 logic:NonEntailmentObligation——即形式化不得让引擎得出的被禁结论。定义域 logic:FormalizationCandidate,值域 logic:NonEntailmentObligation。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateNoOverTyping|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The integrity-constraint formalization candidate that harvests Principle 9's no-over-typing boundary from logic:MixIden's skos:definition into the enforced identity-overlap discipline: a sortal inherits its principle of identity from exactly one Kind, so an instance tracing to two-or-more disjoint Kinds is the logic:MixIden violation. Violation is a finding, not a derivation, materialized by the existing foundation identity discipline (it wraps logic:MixIden, it does not duplicate it). Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation) with a positive case (logic:cqNoOverTypingHolds — a single-Kind instance is well-formed) and a negative countermodel (logic:cqNoOverTypingTwoKindsRejected — a two-Kind instance is the logic:MixIden violation). Its harvest back-link (logic:candidateFormalizes logic:MixIden, logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition) ties it to the exact prose, and logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of that definition text so a later edit surfaces as drift."
msgstr "该完整性约束型形式化候选项从 logic:MixIden 的 skos:definition 中采集原则 9 的非过度类型化边界,形成被强制执行的身份重叠纪律:一个 sortal 恰从一个 Kind 继承其身份原则,因此一个可追溯到两个或更多不相交 Kind 的实例即 logic:MixIden 违背。违背是一项发现,而非派生,由基础中既有的身份纪律物化(它包裹 logic:MixIden,并不复制之)。经审查接受(logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation),配有一个正例(logic:cqNoOverTypingHolds——一个单 Kind 实例是良构的)和一个负向反模型(logic:cqNoOverTypingTwoKindsRejected——一个双 Kind 实例即 logic:MixIden 违背)。其采集反向链接(logic:candidateFormalizes logic:MixIden,logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition)将其绑定到确切的散文文本,而 logic:candidateSourceHash 是该定义文本的 sha256,因此后续的编辑会以漂移形式显现。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateObjectIndividuationCovering|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The necessary-condition formalization candidate governing the class covering that every logic:Object is one of {logic:Collection, logic:Quantity, logic:FunctionalComplex}. It completes the existing individuation-kind pairwise disjointness (logic:candidateFunctionalComplexKindDisjoint) into a full partition. The covering is realized ONLY in the OWL projection as an owl:unionOf; it is NON-monotone and disclosed in the loss ledger — the native monotone StratifiedNAF chase does NOT enforce a disjunctive head, so this is projection-only, not natively enforced. It carries NO harvest back-link. Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation) with a positive case (logic:cqObjectIndividuationCoveringHolds) and a negative case (logic:cqObjectIndividuationCoveringGapRejected); logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of logic:Object's skos:definition for drift detection."
msgstr "该必要条件型形式化候选项规约以下类覆盖:每个 logic:Object 都是 {logic:Collection, logic:Quantity, logic:FunctionalComplex} 之一。它将既有的个体化种类两两不相交(logic:candidateFunctionalComplexKindDisjoint)补全为一个完整划分。该覆盖仅在 OWL 投影中以 owl:unionOf 实现;它是非单调的,并在损失账本中披露——原生的单调 StratifiedNAF 追逐并不强制析取式头部,因此这只属于投影,而非原生强制。它不携带任何采集反向链接。经审查接受(logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation),配有一个正例(logic:cqObjectIndividuationCoveringHolds)和一个负例(logic:cqObjectIndividuationCoveringGapRejected);logic:candidateSourceHash 是 logic:Object 的 skos:definition 的 sha256,用于漂移检测。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateOrgMembershipPropagation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The derivation-rule formalization candidate governing logic:ruleOrgMembershipPropagation: it harvests the upward membership propagation documented in gmeow:memberOf's skos:definition (membership propagates up the organizational part/whole hierarchy via the property chain with gmeow:subOrganizationOf) into an enforced positive-Horn derivation rule, materialized natively as logic:ExactPreservation. The logic: rule is the native-chase form of the same propagation the gmeow:memberOf owl:propertyChainAxiom carries for the OWL 2 RL closure — one inference formalized across two reasoning engines (the harvest pattern), not a divergent second reading. Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation) with a positive case (logic:cqOrgMembershipPropagationHolds) and a negative countermodel (logic:cqOrgMembershipPropagationDownwardRejected). Its harvest back-link (logic:candidateFormalizes gmeow:memberOf, logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition) ties it to the exact prose, and logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of that definition text so a later edit surfaces as drift."
msgstr "该派生规则型形式化候选项规约 logic:ruleOrgMembershipPropagation:它从 gmeow:memberOf 的 skos:definition(成员关系经由与 gmeow:subOrganizationOf 组成的属性链沿组织的部分/整体层级向上传播)中采集其所记载的向上成员传播,形成一条被强制执行的正 Horn 派生规则,原生地物化为 logic:ExactPreservation。该 logic: 规则是 gmeow:memberOf 的 owl:propertyChainAxiom 为 OWL 2 RL 闭包所承载的同一传播的原生追逐形式——同一推理跨两个推理引擎形式化(采集模式),而非发散的第二种解读。经审查接受(logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation),配有一个正例(logic:cqOrgMembershipPropagationHolds)和一个负向反模型(logic:cqOrgMembershipPropagationDownwardRejected)。其采集反向链接(logic:candidateFormalizes gmeow:memberOf,logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition)将其绑定到确切的散文文本,而 logic:candidateSourceHash 是该定义文本的 sha256,因此后续的编辑会以漂移形式显现。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidatePositiveCase|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:FormalizationCandidate to a positive competency case its proposed axiom must satisfy — a gmeow:CompetencyQuestion whose expected answer the axiom should produce (range gmeow:CompetencyQuestion, stated in prose). Domain logic:FormalizationCandidate."
msgstr "将一个 logic:FormalizationCandidate 关联到其所提出公理必须满足的一个正向能力案例——一个 gmeow:CompetencyQuestion,公理应产出其预期答案(值域 gmeow:CompetencyQuestion,以散文表述)。定义域 logic:FormalizationCandidate。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateProjectionBehavior|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:FormalizationCandidate to the logic:PreservationKind its axiom would carry under projection — how faithfully it survives down-projection to OWL/Datalog/SHACL. Reuses the loss-ledger preservation polarity rather than minting a parallel note. Single-valued. Domain logic:FormalizationCandidate, range logic:PreservationKind."
msgstr "将一个 logic:FormalizationCandidate 关联到其公理在投影下会承载的 logic:PreservationKind——即它向下投影到 OWL/Datalog/SHACL 时保真的程度。它复用损失账本的保持极性,而不铸造一条平行注记。单值。定义域 logic:FormalizationCandidate,值域 logic:PreservationKind。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateProperPartOfAsymmetric|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The worked production formalization candidate that harvests the asymmetry of logic:properPartOf from that term's skos:definition into an enforced strict-order integrity constraint: the keystone demonstration of the prose→axiom harvest mechanism. Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation) with a positive case (logic:cqProperPartAsymmetryHolds) and a negative countermodel (logic:cqProperPartAsymmetrySymmetricPairRejected); its harvest back-link (logic:candidateFormalizes logic:properPartOf, logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition) ties it to the exact prose, and logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of that definition text so a later edit to the prose surfaces as drift."
msgstr "该经充分演练的产出型形式化候选项从 logic:properPartOf 一词的 skos:definition 中采集其反对称性,形成一条被强制执行的严格序完整性约束:即散文→公理采集机制的拱心石示范。经审查接受(logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation),配有一个正例(logic:cqProperPartAsymmetryHolds)和一个负向反模型(logic:cqProperPartAsymmetrySymmetricPairRejected);其采集反向链接(logic:candidateFormalizes logic:properPartOf,logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition)将其绑定到确切的散文文本,而 logic:candidateSourceHash 是该定义文本的 sha256,因此后续对散文的编辑会以漂移形式显现。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CandidateProposed|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The lifecycle entry state: a candidate freshly extracted and not yet reviewed. An LLM extraction ALWAYS enters here; it carries no canonical force. Wire value `proposed`."
msgstr "生命周期的入口状态:一个刚被抽取、尚未审查的候选项。一次 LLM 抽取总是进入此处;它不承载任何规范效力。线值 `proposed`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CandidateRejected|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The terminal lifecycle state for a candidate review declined to formalize — recorded rather than deleted, so the decision (and its negative case) is auditable. Wire value `rejected`."
msgstr "生命周期的终止状态,对应审查拒绝予以形式化的候选项——予以记录而非删除,以便该决定(及其负例)可供审计。线值 `rejected`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateRelatorMediation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The formalization candidate that generalizes the relator-mediation discipline (RelComp) from the hardcoded OntoUML seed relators to every subclass of the logic:Relator category, harvested from logic:Relator's own skos:definition ('A Relator must mediate at least two distinct entities'). The native foundation reasoner confers relator-hood on every class subClassOf logic:Relator and fires logic:violation logic:RelComp on any concrete (leaf) relator that mediates fewer than two distinct relata. Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation) with a positive case (logic:cqRelatorMediationHolds) and a negative countermodel (logic:cqRelatorMediationUnderMediatedRejected); its harvest back-link (logic:candidateFormalizes logic:Relator, logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition) ties it to the exact prose, and logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of that skos:definition text so a later edit surfaces as drift."
msgstr "该形式化候选项将关系体中介纪律(RelComp)从硬编码的 OntoUML 种子关系体推广到 logic:Relator 类别的每一个子类,采集自 logic:Relator 自身的 skos:definition(「一个 Relator 必须中介至少两个不同的实体」)。原生的基础推理器把关系体身份赋予每一个 subClassOf logic:Relator 的类,并对任何中介少于两个不同关系项的具体(叶)关系体触发 logic:violation logic:RelComp。经审查接受(logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation),配有一个正例(logic:cqRelatorMediationHolds)和一个负向反模型(logic:cqRelatorMediationUnderMediatedRejected);其采集反向链接(logic:candidateFormalizes logic:Relator,logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition)将其绑定到确切的散文文本,而 logic:candidateSourceHash 是该 skos:definition 文本的 sha256,因此后续的编辑会以漂移形式显现。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateScope|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The intended scope of a candidate's axiom — the terms, slice, or context it is meant to constrain. Read together with logic:candidateContract (the reasoning semantics it is interpreted under). Single-valued, xsd:string. Domain logic:FormalizationCandidate."
msgstr "某候选项公理的预期范围——它意在约束的词项、切片或上下文。与 logic:candidateContract(它被据以解释的推理语义)一并解读。单值,xsd:string。定义域 logic:FormalizationCandidate。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateSemanticRisk|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:FormalizationCandidate to its logic:SemanticRiskClass — how far a wrong formalization would propagate, which sets how strict the reviewer gate must be. Single-valued. Domain logic:FormalizationCandidate, range logic:SemanticRiskClass."
msgstr "将一个 logic:FormalizationCandidate 关联到其 logic:SemanticRiskClass——即一次错误形式化会传播多远,这决定了审查者门须多严格。单值。定义域 logic:FormalizationCandidate,值域 logic:SemanticRiskClass。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateSocialInformationOverlap|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The deliberate-overlap formalization candidate governing the explicit, reviewed NON-assertion of disjointness between gmeow:SocialObject and gmeow:InformationObject: the one overlap the top-sortal partition preserves so that socially-sustained narratives may carry information content without identity clash (a founding myth is both). Its source is gmeow:SocialObject's skos:definition, which states that no disjointness with InformationObject is asserted for exactly this reason. Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation) with a positive case (logic:cqSocialInformationOverlapHolds — a myth typed as both stays coherent) and a negative countermodel (logic:cqSocialInformationOverlapDisjointRejected — asserting the disjointness would force the myth to owl:Nothing, which is why the overlap must be preserved). Its harvest back-link (logic:candidateFormalizes gmeow:SocialObject, logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition) ties it to the exact prose, and logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of that definition text for drift detection. The risk is advisory: this is a non-assertion, so it contaminates nothing — it records a reviewed decision NOT to constrain."
msgstr "该蓄意重叠型形式化候选项规约 gmeow:SocialObject 与 gmeow:InformationObject 之间不相交这一显式且经审查的不断言:即顶层 sortal 划分所保留的唯一重叠,以便社会性维系的叙事得以承载信息内容而无身份冲突(一个奠基神话二者兼是)。其来源是 gmeow:SocialObject 的 skos:definition,其中陈述正因如此才不断言与 InformationObject 的任何不相交。经审查接受(logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation),配有一个正例(logic:cqSocialInformationOverlapHolds——一个被类型化为二者的神话仍保持一致)和一个负向反模型(logic:cqSocialInformationOverlapDisjointRejected——断言该不相交会把该神话强制为 owl:Nothing,这正是必须保留此重叠的原因)。其采集反向链接(logic:candidateFormalizes gmeow:SocialObject,logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition)将其绑定到确切的散文文本,而 logic:candidateSourceHash 是该定义文本的 sha256,用于漂移检测。此风险为咨询性:这是一项不断言,因而不污染任何东西——它记录了一个经审查的、不予约束的决定。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateSourceField|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Names which annotation field of the logic:candidateFormalizes term a candidate harvested — a logic:ProseField from the closed set (logic:ProseFieldDefinition, logic:ProseFieldUseWhen, logic:ProseFieldAvoidWhen). Together with logic:candidateFormalizes it pins the harvested axiom to the exact source triple. Co-present with logic:candidateFormalizes: a candidate carrying one of the pair without the other is a hard governance error (verify.harvest-link-paired), never a half-link. Single-valued. Domain logic:FormalizationCandidate, range logic:ProseField."
msgstr "指明某候选项采集了 logic:candidateFormalizes 词项的哪个注释字段——来自封闭集合的一个 logic:ProseField(logic:ProseFieldDefinition、logic:ProseFieldUseWhen、logic:ProseFieldAvoidWhen)。它与 logic:candidateFormalizes 一并把被采集公理钉到确切的源三元组。它与 logic:candidateFormalizes 共同呈现:一个候选项只携带这对中的一个而缺另一个,即为一项硬治理错误(verify.harvest-link-paired),绝非半个链接。单值。定义域 logic:FormalizationCandidate,值域 logic:ProseField。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateSourceHash|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The content hash of the source text a logic:FormalizationCandidate was extracted from: the anchor that ties the candidate back to the exact prose it formalizes and detects drift if that prose changes. Single-valued, xsd:string. Domain logic:FormalizationCandidate."
msgstr "某 logic:FormalizationCandidate 被抽取自的源文本的内容哈希:即把候选项回系到其所形式化的确切散文、并在该散文变化时检测漂移的锚点。单值,xsd:string。定义域 logic:FormalizationCandidate。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateTenureClaimSurfacing|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The derivation-rule formalization candidate governing logic:ruleTenureClaimVantage and logic:ruleTenureClaimObservedFeature: it harvests the tenure→claim mapping documented in gmeow:StandpointTenure's skos:definition (the tenureStandpoint maps to the claim's vantage; the tenurePosition maps to the claim's observedFeature) into two enforced positive-Horn derivation rules, materialized natively as logic:ExactPreservation. Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation) with a positive case (logic:cqTenureClaimSurfacingHolds) and a negative countermodel (logic:cqTenureClaimSurfacingSwapRejected). Its harvest back-link (logic:candidateFormalizes gmeow:StandpointTenure, logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition) ties it to the exact prose, and logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of that definition text so a later edit surfaces as drift."
msgstr "该派生规则型形式化候选项规约 logic:ruleTenureClaimVantage 和 logic:ruleTenureClaimObservedFeature:它从 gmeow:StandpointTenure 的 skos:definition(tenureStandpoint 映射到主张的观察位 vantage;tenurePosition 映射到主张的 observedFeature)中采集其所记载的任期→主张映射,形成两条被强制执行的正 Horn 派生规则,原生地物化为 logic:ExactPreservation。经审查接受(logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation),配有一个正例(logic:cqTenureClaimSurfacingHolds)和一个负向反模型(logic:cqTenureClaimSurfacingSwapRejected)。其采集反向链接(logic:candidateFormalizes gmeow:StandpointTenure,logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition)将其绑定到确切的散文文本,而 logic:candidateSourceHash 是该定义文本的 sha256,因此后续的编辑会以漂移形式显现。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateTopSortalDisjoint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The formalization candidate that harvests the pairwise disjointness of the four kernel top sortals from gmeow:PhysicalObject's gmeow:avoidWhen prose (which states the three others are disjoint with PhysicalObject by design) into the enforced owl:disjointWith integrity constraints asserted in the kernel: gmeow:Agent, gmeow:PhysicalObject, gmeow:InformationObject and gmeow:SocialObject are pairwise disjoint EXCEPT the deliberately-preserved SocialObject∩InformationObject overlap. The gmeow:Agent ⊥ gmeow:SocialObject edge is net-new on this branch. Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation) with a positive case (logic:cqTopSortalDisjointHolds) and a negative countermodel (logic:cqTopSortalDisjointClashRejected); its harvest back-link (logic:candidateFormalizes gmeow:PhysicalObject, logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldAvoidWhen) ties it to the exact prose, and logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of that gmeow:avoidWhen text so a later edit surfaces as drift. The native DL coherence gate reads the owl:disjointWith directly, forcing a two-sortal individual to owl:Nothing."
msgstr "该形式化候选项从 gmeow:PhysicalObject 的 gmeow:avoidWhen 散文(其陈述另外三者按设计与 PhysicalObject 不相交)中采集内核四个顶层 sortal 的两两不相交,形成内核中所断言、被强制执行的 owl:disjointWith 完整性约束:gmeow:Agent、gmeow:PhysicalObject、gmeow:InformationObject 与 gmeow:SocialObject 两两不相交,唯独 SocialObject∩InformationObject 这处被蓄意保留的重叠除外。gmeow:Agent ⊥ gmeow:SocialObject 这条边在本分支上是全新的。经审查接受(logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation),配有一个正例(logic:cqTopSortalDisjointHolds)和一个负向反模型(logic:cqTopSortalDisjointClashRejected);其采集反向链接(logic:candidateFormalizes gmeow:PhysicalObject,logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldAvoidWhen)将其绑定到确切的散文文本,而 logic:candidateSourceHash 是该 gmeow:avoidWhen 文本的 sha256,因此后续的编辑会以漂移形式显现。原生 DL 一致性门直接读取该 owl:disjointWith,将一个属于两个 sortal 的个体强制为 owl:Nothing。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CandidateUnderReview|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The lifecycle state of a candidate a reviewer is actively adjudicating — the mandatory waypoint between logic:CandidateProposed and logic:CandidateAccepted. Wire value `under-review`."
msgstr "审查者正在积极裁定的某候选项的生命周期状态——即 logic:CandidateProposed 与 logic:CandidateAccepted 之间的强制途经点。线值 `under-review`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CanonicalProjection|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The projection-target value requesting the answer be rendered in the canonical logic: surface — the orthogonal, lossless form GMEOW reasons over, before any down-projection. The default output request; it never alters which entailments hold."
msgstr "请求将答案呈现在规范 logic: 表面上的投影目标取值——即 GMEOW 据以推理的、在任何向下投影之前的正交且无损形式。默认的输出请求;它绝不改变哪些蕴涵成立。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/capabilityAvailable|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a state to a capability the actor holds at it — the executional capability the gate matches an action schema's logic:capability against. Domain a state, range the available capability (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将一个状态关联到施动者在该状态所持有的一项能力——即门用来与某动作模式的 logic:capability 相匹配的执行能力。定义域为一个状态,值域为可用能力(以散文表述)。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/capability|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ActionSchema to what an agent must be able to do to execute it — the executional precondition on the actor rather than on the state. Domain logic:ActionSchema (stated in prose). One of the eight action-theory facets, distinct from logic:precondition (a precondition on the situation, not the agent)."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ActionSchema 关联到某施动者为执行它所必须能够做到的事——即施加于施动者而非状态之上的执行前置条件。定义域 logic:ActionSchema(以散文表述)。它是动作理论八个面向之一,有别于 logic:precondition(施加于情境而非施动者的前置条件)。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cardinality|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:birthMotherRestriction logic:cardinality 1 ."
msgstr "示例：ex:birthMotherRestriction logic:cardinality 1 ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cardinality|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Exact cardinality combines the corresponding inclusive minimum and maximum over all fillers."
msgstr "精确基数在所有填充项上组合相应的包含式最小值与最大值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/carriesTerminationCertificate|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ChaseAcceptanceWitness to the weak-acyclicity termination-certificate evidence (xsd:string, the ChaseAdmission::WeaklyAcyclic evidence summary) that admits its chase. Domain logic:ChaseAcceptanceWitness (stated in prose). A chase acceptance record with no certificate reports a closure that may never terminate."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ChaseAcceptanceWitness 关联到接纳其追逐的弱无环终止证书证据(xsd:string,即 ChaseAdmission::WeaklyAcyclic 证据摘要)。定义域 logic:ChaseAcceptanceWitness(以散文表述)。一条不带证书的追逐接纳记录所报告的闭包可能永不终止。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CategoryDefeasibleDefault|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:FormalizationCategory for defeasible content a more specific fact may override — default-logic force, distinct from plain typicality. Wire value `defeasible-default`."
msgstr "用于可废止内容(更具体的事实可将其推翻)的 logic:FormalizationCategory——一种默认逻辑效力,有别于单纯的典型性。线值 `defeasible-default`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CategoryDeliberateOverlap|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:FormalizationCategory for a mereological sharing fact deliberately admitted — an intended overlap rather than an accidental one. Wire value `deliberate-overlap`."
msgstr "用于一处被蓄意接纳的部分论共享事实的 logic:FormalizationCategory——一处有意的重叠而非偶然的重叠。线值 `deliberate-overlap`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CategoryDerivationRule|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:FormalizationCategory for a productive rule whose head is entailed — content that adds to the reasoned closure. Wire value `derivation-rule`."
msgstr "用于一条能产规则(其头部被蕴涵)的 logic:FormalizationCategory——即为被推理闭包添加内容的内容。线值 `derivation-rule`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CategoryDocumentationOnly|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:FormalizationCategory for explanatory prose that is NOT to be formalized at all — the category that records a deliberate decision to leave content unaxiomatized. Wire value `documentation-only`."
msgstr "用于完全不予形式化的解释性散文的 logic:FormalizationCategory——即记录一个有意决定、把内容留作未公理化的类别。线值 `documentation-only`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CategoryEquivalenceDefinition|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:FormalizationCategory for prose stating the necessary-and-sufficient identity of a term — a definitional equivalence. Wire value `equivalence-definition`."
msgstr "用于陈述某词项之充要身份的散文的 logic:FormalizationCategory——一种定义性等价。线值 `equivalence-definition`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CategoryIntegrityConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:FormalizationCategory for an integrity condition whose violation is a finding, not a derivation — a CBox constraint rather than a productive rule. Wire value `integrity-constraint`."
msgstr "用于一项完整性条件(其违背是一项发现而非派生)的 logic:FormalizationCategory——一条 CBox 约束而非能产规则。线值 `integrity-constraint`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CategoryNecessaryCondition|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:FormalizationCategory for prose stating a one-directional necessary condition (the term implies the condition). Wire value `necessary-condition`."
msgstr "用于陈述单向必要条件(词项蕴涵该条件)的散文的 logic:FormalizationCategory。线值 `necessary-condition`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CategoryNonEntailmentObligation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:FormalizationCategory for a deliberate non-assertion — prose recording a conclusion the foundation must never draw, realized as a logic:NonEntailmentObligation. Wire value `non-entailment-obligation`."
msgstr "用于一项蓄意不断言的 logic:FormalizationCategory——即记录基础绝不可得出之结论的散文,实现为一个 logic:NonEntailmentObligation。线值 `non-entailment-obligation`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CategoryRecommendation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:FormalizationCategory for advisory content that is never enforced — guidance carried but not reasoned over. Wire value `recommendation`."
msgstr "用于从不强制的咨询性内容的 logic:FormalizationCategory——即被承载但不被推理的指引。线值 `recommendation`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Category|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A rigid non-sortal that classifies instances of several different Kinds by shared essential properties without itself supplying a principle of identity: it dispersively spans Kinds rather than carrying its own identity criterion. Rigid but identity-dispersive; the rigid counterpart of the anti-rigid RoleMixin and PhaseMixin."
msgstr "一个刚性非 sortal,它凭共享的本质属性对若干不同 Kind 的实例进行分类,而自身并不提供身份原则:它以弥散方式横跨各 Kind,而不携带自己的身份判据。刚性但身份弥散;它是反刚性的 RoleMixin 与 PhaseMixin 的刚性对应物。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CategorySufficientCondition|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:FormalizationCategory for prose stating a one-directional sufficient condition (the condition implies the term). Wire value `sufficient-condition`."
msgstr "用于陈述单向充分条件(该条件蕴涵词项)的散文的 logic:FormalizationCategory。线值 `sufficient-condition`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CategoryTypicality|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:FormalizationCategory for generic, what-normally-holds content — kept distinct from logic:CategoryDefeasibleDefault, whose force is override rather than genericity. Wire value `typicality`."
msgstr "用于泛指的、通常成立之内容的 logic:FormalizationCategory——与 logic:CategoryDefeasibleDefault 保持区分,后者的效力在于推翻而非泛指。线值 `typicality`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/causalLinkDistinctness|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Asserts that a gmeow:CausalLink's gmeow:linkAntecedent and gmeow:linkConsequent must be distinct: nothing type-causes itself. The native coherence gate raises a violation when they coincide."
msgstr "断言一个 gmeow:CausalLink 的 gmeow:linkAntecedent 与 gmeow:linkConsequent 必须相异:没有任何东西在类型层面导致自身。当二者重合时,原生一致性门会抛出一项违背。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/causalPartOf|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Causal parthood among perdurants: relates a sub-occurrent that causally contributes to a larger occurrent — the ignition is a causal part of the launch, the infection a causal part of the illness. A specialization of logic:temporalPartOf (stated in prose, not as an rdfs:subPropertyOf edge, matching how the foundation parthood relations are authored): every causal part is also a temporal part of the same whole, but NOT conversely — a merely temporally-nested sub-occurrent need carry no causal contribution (causal subset-of temporal, the YAMATO/Galton occurrent-mereology refinement). Transitive (a causal part of a causal part causally contributes to the whole) but deliberately NOT asymmetric or irreflexive, since causal feedback loops are legal among occurrents — contrast logic:properPartOf, the strict-order endurant parthood. Distinct from the temporal-only nesting carried at the domain level by gmeow:subEventOf."
msgstr "发生者之间的因果部分关系:关联一个对更大发生者作出因果贡献的子发生者——点火是发射的一个因果部分,感染是疾病的一个因果部分。它是 logic:temporalPartOf 的一种特化(以散文表述,而非作为一条 rdfs:subPropertyOf 边,与基础中各部分关系的撰写方式一致):每个因果部分也是同一整体的一个时间部分,但反之不然——一个仅在时间上嵌套的子发生者可以不承载任何因果贡献(因果是时间的子集,即 YAMATO/Galton 的发生者部分论精化)。可传递(因果部分的因果部分对整体作出因果贡献),但被有意设为既不反对称也不非自反,因为因果反馈回路在发生者之间是合法的——与 logic:properPartOf 即严格序的延续者部分关系相对照。它有别于由 gmeow:subEventOf 在领域层面承载的纯时间嵌套。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CertifiedFragmentResource|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The resource execution policy that requires the rule set to lie within a certified-complete, terminating fragment: it guarantees hard termination and a complexity bound, and the result reports complete-for-fragment. The certified counterpart of logic:BudgetBoundedResource; because resource is an execution policy holding independent properties together, a contract may require both a certified fragment and a budget at once."
msgstr "要求规则集处于一个经认证完备且可终止片段之内的资源执行策略:它保证硬终止与一个复杂度界,结果报告为片段内完备。它是 logic:BudgetBoundedResource 的经认证对应物;由于资源是一种把若干独立性质并持的执行策略,一份契约可以同时要求一个经认证片段与一份预算。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/certifiedFragment|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The certified-complete fragment reference backing a logic:CompleteForFragment claim on a logic:ReasoningResult. Single-valued. Domain logic:ReasoningResult (stated in prose)."
msgstr "支撑某 logic:ReasoningResult 上 logic:CompleteForFragment 主张的经认证完备片段引用。单值。定义域 logic:ReasoningResult(以散文表述)。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/characteristicSort|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:PropertyCharacteristicAssertion to the characteristic-sort marker it asserts — one of logic:transitiveProperty, logic:symmetricProperty, logic:irreflexiveProperty, logic:asymmetricProperty or logic:functionalProperty. Co-present with logic:characterizes: a characteristic assertion carrying one without the other names no enforceable characteristic. Domain logic:PropertyCharacteristicAssertion; single-valued."
msgstr "将一个 logic:PropertyCharacteristicAssertion 关联到它所断言的特征分类标记——为 logic:transitiveProperty、logic:symmetricProperty、logic:irreflexiveProperty、logic:asymmetricProperty 或 logic:functionalProperty 之一。它与 logic:characterizes 共同呈现:一条只携带其一而缺另一的特征断言,并不指称任何可强制的特征。定义域 logic:PropertyCharacteristicAssertion;单值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/characterizes|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:PropertyCharacteristicAssertion to the property it characterises (a gmeow: or logic: property, stated in prose). Read together with logic:characteristicSort, it tells the native coherence gate which property bears which characteristic. Domain logic:PropertyCharacteristicAssertion; single-valued."
msgstr "将一个 logic:PropertyCharacteristicAssertion 关联到它所刻画的属性(一个 gmeow: 或 logic: 属性,以散文形式给出)。与 logic:characteristicSort 一并阅读时,它告诉原生一致性门哪个属性承载哪种特征。定义域为 logic:PropertyCharacteristicAssertion;单值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ChaseAcceptanceWitness|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The acceptance record that an existential-rule chase materialization terminated under a weak-acyclicity certificate, executed natively by gmeow_logic::materialize::materialize_existential_rules, which surfaces the ChaseAdmission termination certificate as a first-class gmeow:Finding. It carries, through logic:carriesTerminationCertificate, the certificate evidence. The flagship producer runs the native chase and pins that the surfaced Finding is non-empty and that the derivation carries an explain trace passing gmeow_logic::explain::assert_faithful; this witness is the ontological twin the thin logic:ChaseAcceptanceWitnessShape gates."
msgstr "该接受记录证明一次存在规则 chase 物化在弱无环性证书下终止,由 gmeow_logic::materialize::materialize_existential_rules 原生执行,后者将 ChaseAdmission 终止证书作为一等的 gmeow:Finding 呈现出来。它通过 logic:carriesTerminationCertificate 携带证书证据。旗舰生产者运行原生 chase,并钉住呈现出的 Finding 非空、且推导携带一条通过 gmeow_logic::explain::assert_faithful 的解释轨迹;此见证是纤薄的 logic:ChaseAcceptanceWitnessShape 所把守的本体论孪生体。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ChaseWitnessLeaf|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The narrow, plain leaf class the invented Skolem witness of a logic:ExistentialChaseDemonstrand inhabits — the `D` in the demonstrator's C ⊑ ∃p.D law. It is deliberately a LEAF: it carries no existential obligation of its own, no owl:disjointWith, and no functional or cardinality axiom, and it does NOT reach logic:ExistentialChaseDemonstrand, so a chase-invented null typed into it triggers no further inference, no Skolem ancestor-blocking cycle, and no global inconsistency. Its whole role is to be the harmless target type the ∃demonstratesChaseWitness.ChaseWitnessLeaf obligation is satisfied against, keeping the demonstrator weakly-acyclic and terminating."
msgstr "由 logic:ExistentialChaseDemonstrand 所发明的 Skolem 见证者所栖居的那个狭窄、朴素的叶子类——即演示者 C ⊑ ∃p.D 律中的 `D`。它被刻意设为叶子:它自身不承载任何存在性义务,没有 owl:disjointWith,也没有函数性或基数公理,并且它不触及 logic:ExistentialChaseDemonstrand,因此一个被 chase 发明并归入其中的空值不会触发任何进一步推理、任何 Skolem 祖先阻断环、或任何全局不一致。它的全部职责是充当那个无害的目标类型,让 ∃demonstratesChaseWitness.ChaseWitnessLeaf 义务得以对之满足,从而使演示者保持弱无环且可终止。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ChaseWitnessLeaf|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/skolem/9f2c> a logic:ChaseWitnessLeaf ."
msgstr "示例：<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/skolem/9f2c> a logic:ChaseWitnessLeaf ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/checkIssuedAt|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The xsd:dateTime a coherence outcome was issued. INJECTED, never sampled in the deterministic fold core, so re-running with the same inputs and timestamp is byte-identical. Single-valued. Domain logic:CoherenceCertificate or logic:CoherenceCheckAttestation (stated in prose)."
msgstr "一致性结果被发出的 xsd:dateTime。它是被注入的,绝不在确定性折叠核心中采样,因此以相同输入与时间戳重新运行是逐字节一致的。单值。定义域为 logic:CoherenceCertificate 或 logic:CoherenceCheckAttestation(以散文给出)。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/choiceMode|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The cardinality mode of a logic:ChoiceGroupConstraint: 'exactly-one', 'at-most-one', or 'exactly-one-of-N' (an alias of 'exactly-one')."
msgstr "一个 logic:ChoiceGroupConstraint 的基数模式:'exactly-one'、'at-most-one' 或 'exactly-one-of-N'(即 'exactly-one' 的别名)。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/choicePredicate|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A member predicate of a logic:ChoiceGroupConstraint's choice group. Multi-valued (at least two); the ∃-requiredness of each is combined per logic:choiceMode."
msgstr "一个 logic:ChoiceGroupConstraint 的选择组的成员谓词。多值(至少两个);每个的 ∃-必需性按 logic:choiceMode 组合。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Choice|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The guarded-choice program combinator: selects one of two sub-programs based on whether a guard situation holds at the current state. The left operand (logic:leftOperand) is executed when the guard holds; the right operand (logic:rightOperand) is executed when it does not. The guard is declared through logic:guardSituation, reusing the same property the conditional goal expression reads — a choice combinator is a PROGRAM operator that dispatches on a guard, typed APART from a conditional formula connective that holds at a single state. The two operands are binary, carried by logic:leftOperand and logic:rightOperand (the same properties logic:SerialConjunction uses). A plan whose branches are conditioned on what an earlier observation revealed is a POLICY — a reading of a plan, not a separate class — and its branches are resolved through logic:planBranch, logic:branchGuard, and logic:nextActionSchema; logic:Choice is the structural combinator that expresses the branching operator in the program body. Distinct from goal-level logic:DisjunctiveGoal, which evaluates a truth-at-a-state condition over sub-expressions, not a program that dispatches control to one of two sub-programs."
msgstr "受守卫选择的程序组合子:它根据某个守卫情形在当前状态是否成立,选择两个子程序之一。当守卫成立时执行左操作数(logic:leftOperand);当其不成立时执行右操作数(logic:rightOperand)。守卫通过 logic:guardSituation 声明,复用条件目标表达式所读取的同一属性——选择组合子是一个按守卫分派的程序算子,其类型与在单一状态成立的条件公式连接词区分开来。两个操作数为二元,由 logic:leftOperand 与 logic:rightOperand 携带(即 logic:SerialConjunction 所用的同一属性)。若一个计划的分支以先前某次观察所揭示的内容为条件,则它是一个策略——是对计划的一种解读,而非独立的类——其分支通过 logic:planBranch、logic:branchGuard 与 logic:nextActionSchema 解析;logic:Choice 是在程序体中表达分支算子的结构组合子。它有别于目标层面的 logic:DisjunctiveGoal,后者在子表达式之上求值一个状态处真值的条件,而非将控制分派到两个子程序之一的程序。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ClassicalModelSemantics|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The model-semantics facet value selecting classical first-order entailment: truth in every model. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract; contrast the least-model, well-founded, and stable-model values that select a distinguished model or model set for rule programs."
msgstr "选择经典一阶蕴涵的模型语义面值:在每个模型中为真。在 ReasoningContract 上单值;与最小模型、良基与稳定模型这些为规则程序选定某个特出模型或模型集的取值相对照。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ClassicalTwoValued|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The two-valued truth algebra with only true and false. The degenerate truth algebra a ReasoningContract selects when neither gluts nor gaps are needed; equivalent to selecting the Belnap algebra with logic:ForbidGapAndGlut, offered as a direct value for the common classical case."
msgstr "只含真与假的二值真值代数。当既不需要真值过剩也不需要真值空缺时,某个 ReasoningContract 所选择的退化真值代数;等价于选择配以 logic:ForbidGapAndGlut 的 Belnap 代数,作为常见经典情形的直接取值提供。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/clause|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningProgram to each authored clause: an atomic fact or a Horn rule whose logic:antecedent body atoms entail its logic:consequent head, with any body atom optionally logic:not-negated. Reuses the SAME logic:Formula clause shape the forward relational-core lane already lowers from — there is no separate, program-specific clause language. Multi-valued; a program with no clauses is malformed (logic:ReasoningProgramClauseConstraint)."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ReasoningProgram 关联到每一条撰写的子句:一个原子事实,或一条 Horn 规则,其 logic:antecedent 体原子蕴涵其 logic:consequent 头,任一体原子可选择性地 logic:not-negated。它复用前向关系核心通道已从中下降的同一种 logic:Formula 子句形态——不存在单独的、程序专用的子句语言。多值;没有子句的程序是畸形的(logic:ReasoningProgramClauseConstraint)。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Closed|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The occurrent-boundary value for a completed unitary event: a perdurant whole over a closed temporal interval, finished and no longer able to change — the arrival, the run completed, the executed record. The event half of the YAMATO/Galton action(open)/event(closed) distinction; a Closed occurrent that bears a time-varying logic:Fluent is the logic:OccurrentChangeAsymmetry violation, since a completed whole cannot vary. Contrast logic:Open."
msgstr "已完成的单一事件的历象边界取值:一个跨越闭合时间区间的续存整体,已终结且不再能够变化——那次到达、那次已完成的运行、那条已执行的记录。它是 YAMATO/Galton 的 action(open)/event(closed) 区分中的「事件」一半;一个承载随时间变化的 logic:Fluent 的 Closed 历象构成 logic:OccurrentChangeAsymmetry 违规,因为一个已完成的整体不能变化。与 logic:Open 相对照。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/closedUnder|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Declares a predicate or shape closed within a logic:WorldBoundary: the closed-world-assumption toggle that says, for the named predicate inside the boundary, that the materialized extension is complete and absence may be read as falsity. The per-predicate CWA switch of the hybrid open/closed construct, enforced by the built-in SHACL (the CWA lane); outside any boundary, or for predicates not closed under one, the open-world reading holds. Enforcement is seamed to the engine."
msgstr "在一个 logic:WorldBoundary 内将某谓词或形状声明为封闭:这是封闭世界假设的开关,它就边界内被命名的谓词声明其物化外延是完整的,且缺席可被读作假。它是混合开放/封闭构造的按谓词 CWA 开关,由内建 SHACL(CWA 通道)强制执行;在任何边界之外,或对于未在某边界下被封闭的谓词,开放世界读法成立。执行被接缝到引擎。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ClosedWorldClosure|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The closed-world value of the closure map: for the predicate or context key it is bound to, the materialized extension is complete and absence may be read as falsity. Realized within a logic:WorldBoundary by the built-in SHACL (the CWA lane); it is the per-key value of the closure map, never a global flag — open-world is the default for unlisted keys."
msgstr "闭包映射的封闭世界取值:对于它所绑定的谓词或上下文键,物化外延是完整的,且缺席可被读作假。它在一个 logic:WorldBoundary 内由内建 SHACL(CWA 通道)实现;它是闭包映射的按键取值,绝非全局标志——开放世界是未列出键的默认值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ClosureAcceptanceWitness|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The acceptance record that an EL→RL→DL reasoning closure (gmeow_logic::reason::reason_all) genuinely entailed new atoms: it names, through logic:closureEntailedAtom, at least one atom the closure derived beyond its asserted EDB. The flagship producer runs the native closure and pins that a designated entailed atom is present and absent from the EDB; this witness is the ontological twin the thin logic:ClosureAcceptanceWitnessShape gates."
msgstr "该接受记录证明一次 EL→RL→DL 推理闭包(gmeow_logic::reason::reason_all)确实蕴涵了新原子:它通过 logic:closureEntailedAtom 命名至少一个闭包在其断言的 EDB 之外所导出的原子。旗舰生产者运行原生闭包,并钉住某个指定的被蕴涵原子存在且不在 EDB 中;此见证是纤薄的 logic:ClosureAcceptanceWitnessShape 所把守的本体论孪生体。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/closureEntailedAtom|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ClosureAcceptanceWitness to a serialized atom (xsd:string, e.g. `A subClassOf C`) that the EL→RL→DL closure entails but the asserted EDB does not contain. Domain logic:ClosureAcceptanceWitness (stated in prose). At least one is required: a closure witness that entails nothing beyond its input demonstrates no reasoning."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ClosureAcceptanceWitness 关联到一个序列化原子(xsd:string,例如 `A subClassOf C`),该原子被 EL→RL→DL 闭包蕴涵但断言的 EDB 并不包含。定义域为 logic:ClosureAcceptanceWitness(以散文给出)。至少需要一个:一个在其输入之外不蕴涵任何东西的闭包见证并不展示任何推理。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ClosureEntry|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A reified entry of the Closure facet map: it binds a predicate or context key (logic:closureKey) to an open- or closed-world value (logic:closureValue). The Closure facet is a map, not a global flag; WorldBoundary-scoped closed-world is the per-key value, open-world the default for unlisted keys."
msgstr "Closure 面映射的一个具体化条目:它将一个谓词或上下文键(logic:closureKey)绑定到一个开放世界或封闭世界取值(logic:closureValue)。Closure 面是一个映射,而非全局标志;受 WorldBoundary 界定的封闭世界是按键取值,开放世界是未列出键的默认值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/closureEntry|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to a logic:ClosureEntry — a per-key override of the closure map binding a predicate or context key to an open- or closed-world value. The closure facet is a map, not a global flag: logic:defaultClosure gives the default for unlisted keys, while each logic:closureEntry overrides one key. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:ClosureEntry (stated in prose, matching the module's convention)."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ReasoningContract 关联到一个 logic:ClosureEntry——闭包映射的一个按键覆盖,将谓词或上下文键绑定到开放世界或封闭世界取值。闭包面是一个映射,而非全局标志:logic:defaultClosure 给出未列出键的默认值,而每个 logic:closureEntry 覆盖一个键。定义域为 logic:ReasoningContract,值域为 logic:ClosureEntry(以散文给出,符合模块惯例)。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/closureKey|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ClosureEntry to the predicate-or-context key it scopes: the string key whose closure value the entry fixes. Domain logic:ClosureEntry (stated in prose, matching the module's convention); range xsd:string. The key together with logic:closureValue forms one binding of the closure map."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ClosureEntry 关联到它所界定的谓词或上下文键:即条目为其固定闭包取值的字符串键。定义域为 logic:ClosureEntry(以散文给出,符合模块惯例);值域为 xsd:string。该键与 logic:closureValue 一起构成闭包映射的一个绑定。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ClosureValue|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The facet value class of a single closure setting — open-world or closed-world. It is the per-key value of the closure map (carried as the map default via logic:defaultClosure or as the value of a logic:ClosureEntry), not the closure facet itself, which is a map keyed by predicate or context."
msgstr "单个闭包设置的面值类——开放世界或封闭世界。它是闭包映射的按键取值(作为映射默认值经 logic:defaultClosure 携带,或作为一个 logic:ClosureEntry 的取值),而非闭包面本身,后者是一个按谓词或上下文索引的映射。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/closureValue|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ClosureEntry to the logic:ClosureValue (open- or closed-world) it assigns to its key. Domain logic:ClosureEntry, range logic:ClosureValue (stated in prose, matching the module's convention). Together with logic:closureKey it forms one binding of the closure map."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ClosureEntry 关联到它赋予其键的 logic:ClosureValue(开放或封闭世界)。定义域为 logic:ClosureEntry,值域为 logic:ClosureValue(以散文给出,符合模块惯例)。它与 logic:closureKey 一起构成闭包映射的一个绑定。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/coarserThanTransitivity|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Asserts on the canonical carrier that gmeow:coarserThan is transitive: the partial order on granularity levels its skos:definition names, which makes 'at or above a target level' well-defined. The native coherence gate reads this to close the granularity order."
msgstr "在规范载体上断言 gmeow:coarserThan 是传递的:即其 skos:definition 所命名的粒度层级上的偏序,这使得「处于或高于某目标层级」得以良定义。原生一致性门读取此项以闭合粒度序。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CognitiveAssessment|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The canonical record of how good some reasoning is, or how capable a reasoner is: a reified, vantage-indexed node naming exactly one logic:AssessmentDimension and carrying its assessed agent (logic:assessedAgent), subject and granularity (logic:assessmentSubject with logic:subjectGranularity), task or context (logic:assessmentContext), scale and level (logic:assessmentScale with logic:assessmentLevel), evaluator and standpoint (logic:assessmentEvaluator, attributed via gmeow:accordingTo), evidence (logic:assessmentEvidence), method (logic:assessmentMethod), valid interval (carried by gmeow:duringInterval) and the strength with which the judgment itself is held (carried by logic:confidence). The dimensions vary independently, so a single ordinal familiarity-to-mastery scale collapses exactly the distinctions an assessment exists to draw; the construct keeps them factored. A self-assessment and an observer's assessment of the same agent are two coexisting records, never reconciled into one verdict, and because the node is reified an assessment is itself a subject another assessment can range over — an evaluation of the evaluator — with no new machinery. The convenient ordinal reading is the lossy coarse-ladder projection of this assessment, exactly as logic:AgencyAssessment projects the unary 'this holon is integral'; a reliability assessment is a logic:CognitiveAssessment on the reliability dimension over a series of runs, distinct from the single-run logic:ResultAssurance. Normative in design/LOGIC-COGNITION.md."
msgstr "对某项推理有多好、或某个推理者有多强的规范记录:一个具体化的、按视角索引的节点,恰好命名一个 logic:AssessmentDimension,并携带其被评估主体(logic:assessedAgent)、其对象与粒度(logic:assessmentSubject 及 logic:subjectGranularity)、其任务或上下文(logic:assessmentContext)、其标度与层级(logic:assessmentScale 及 logic:assessmentLevel)、其评估者与立场(logic:assessmentEvaluator,经 gmeow:accordingTo 归属)、其证据(logic:assessmentEvidence)、其方法(logic:assessmentMethod)、其有效区间(由 gmeow:duringInterval 携带)以及判断本身被持守的强度(由 logic:confidence 携带)。各维度独立变化,因此一条从熟悉到精通的单一序数标度恰恰会坍缩一次评估所要刻画的那些区分;该构造使它们保持因子化。对同一主体,自评与观察者的评估是两条并存的记录,绝不被调和为单一裁决,而且由于该节点已具体化,一次评估自身也是另一次评估可遍历的对象——对评估者的评估——无需任何新机构。便利的序数读法是此评估的有损粗阶投影,正如 logic:AgencyAssessment 投射一元的「此全子是完整的」;可靠性评估是可靠性维度上跨一系列运行的 logic:CognitiveAssessment,有别于单次运行的 logic:ResultAssurance。规范见 design/LOGIC-COGNITION.md。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CoherenceCertificate|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The contract-scoped assertion, issued ONLY from a CONCLUSIVE check (the summarized logic:ReasoningResult has logic:EvaluationCompleted, or logic:CompleteForFragment), that over the certified fragment the inspection was COMPLETE and found no forbidden integrity violation and no undisclosed contradiction. Scoped by contract (logic:contractHash on the linked result), fragment (logic:certifiedFragment), budget (logic:consumedBudget) and bundle (logic:bundleHash, logic:axiomHash). Coherence means 'every contradiction present is permitted under the contract and disclosed, or has been reported as a violation' — NEVER 'this bundle contains no contradiction'. A complete check is the only thing entitled to the word certify; a bounded check yields a logic:CoherenceCheckAttestation instead. Carries logic:permittedConflictWitness for disclosed gluts and logic:forbiddenViolationWitness (necessarily empty for an issued certificate). Authored canonically in crates/logic (Rust); a lossy documentation projection (Principle 17). Normative in design/LOGIC-CONFORMANCE.md, §The coherence certificate."
msgstr "契约范围的断言,仅从一次结论性检查发出(被总结的 logic:ReasoningResult 带有 logic:EvaluationCompleted 或 logic:CompleteForFragment),它断定在被认证的片段之上检查是完整的,且未发现任何被禁止的完整性违规、也无任何未披露的矛盾。它由契约(链接结果上的 logic:contractHash)、片段(logic:certifiedFragment)、预算(logic:consumedBudget)与捆绑(logic:bundleHash、logic:axiomHash)界定。一致性意味着「所呈现的每个矛盾要么在契约下被允许并已披露,要么已被报告为违规」——而绝不是「此捆绑不含任何矛盾」。唯有完整检查才有资格使用「认证」一词;有界检查转而产出一个 logic:CoherenceCheckAttestation。它为已披露的过剩携带 logic:permittedConflictWitness,并携带 logic:forbiddenViolationWitness(对已发出的证书必然为空)。在 crates/logic(Rust)中规范撰写;一个有损的文档投影(原则 17)。规范见 design/LOGIC-CONFORMANCE.md,§一致性证书。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CoherenceCheckAttestation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The strictly weaker outcome a BOUNDED or INCOMPLETE coherence check issues (the summarized logic:ReasoningResult has logic:BudgetExhausted, or logic:Incomplete / logic:CompletenessUnknown): it records only that no forbidden integrity violation and no undisclosed contradiction was found WITHIN the completed search. A budget-exhausted run produces an attestation, NEVER a logic:CoherenceCertificate, because it cannot rule out a contradiction it never reached. Honest evidence, not a certification of coherence. Carries the same scoped payload (logic:summarizesResult, logic:bundleHash, logic:contradictionPolicy, logic:checkIssuedAt). Authored canonically in crates/logic (Rust); a lossy documentation projection (Principle 17). Normative in design/LOGIC-CONFORMANCE.md, §The coherence certificate."
msgstr "有界或不完整的一致性检查所发出的严格更弱的结果(被总结的 logic:ReasoningResult 带有 logic:BudgetExhausted,或 logic:Incomplete / logic:CompletenessUnknown):它仅记录在已完成的搜索之内未发现任何被禁止的完整性违规、也无任何未披露的矛盾。预算耗尽的运行产出一份证明,绝不产出 logic:CoherenceCertificate,因为它无法排除一个它从未触及的矛盾。这是诚实的证据,而非对一致性的认证。它携带相同的范围载荷(logic:summarizesResult、logic:bundleHash、logic:contradictionPolicy、logic:checkIssuedAt)。在 crates/logic(Rust)中规范撰写;一个有损的文档投影(原则 17)。规范见 design/LOGIC-CONFORMANCE.md,§一致性证书。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Collection|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A plurality individuated by its members, where the members are themselves the relevant units of the whole — a deck of cards, a committee, a playlist. The counterpart of gufo:Collection; members relate to it via logic:memberOf rather than logic:properPartOf. Contrast logic:Quantity, which is individuated by constitution rather than by member count."
msgstr "一个由其成员个体化的复多,其中成员本身就是整体的相关单位——一副牌、一个委员会、一个播放列表。它是 gufo:Collection 的对应物;成员通过 logic:memberOf 而非 logic:properPartOf 与之关联。与 logic:Quantity 相对照,后者由构成而非成员计数来个体化。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ColumnBinding|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The closed value class of the logic:columnBinding facet: whether a column's variable is bound in every row. Its individuals are logic:BindingRequired and logic:BindingOptional. The set is closed, so a misspelt value names no declared binding and is rejected."
msgstr "logic:columnBinding 面的封闭取值类:即一列的变量是否在每一行都被绑定。其个体为 logic:BindingRequired 与 logic:BindingOptional。该集合是封闭的,因此拼写错误的取值不命名任何已声明的绑定,并被拒绝。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/columnBinding|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ResultColumn to the logic:ColumnBinding it declares — whether the variable is bound in every row. Single-valued. Domain logic:ResultColumn, range logic:ColumnBinding (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ResultColumn 关联到它所声明的 logic:ColumnBinding——即变量是否在每一行都被绑定。单值。定义域为 logic:ResultColumn,值域为 logic:ColumnBinding(以散文给出)。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/columnDatatype|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a literal logic:ResultColumn to the datatype IRI it pins. Single-valued and OPTIONAL: a literal column with no logic:columnDatatype accepts any literal (a declared loosening, not a half-typed column); a non-literal column carries none. Domain logic:ResultColumn, range a datatype IRI (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将一个字面 logic:ResultColumn 关联到它所钉定的数据类型 IRI。单值且可选:一个没有 logic:columnDatatype 的字面列接受任意字面量(这是一种已声明的放宽,而非半类型化的列);非字面列不携带任何此项。定义域为 logic:ResultColumn,值域为一个数据类型 IRI(以散文给出)。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/columnTermKind|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ResultColumn to the logic:TermKind it requires — the mandatory RDF term kind of the column's values. Single-valued. Domain logic:ResultColumn, range logic:TermKind (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ResultColumn 关联到它所要求的 logic:TermKind——即该列取值的强制 RDF 词项种类。单值。定义域为 logic:ResultColumn,值域为 logic:TermKind(以散文给出)。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/columnVariable|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The bare SPARQL variable name (no leading '?') a logic:ResultColumn types. Single-valued, xsd:string. Domain logic:ResultColumn (stated in prose)."
msgstr "一个 logic:ResultColumn 所类型化的裸 SPARQL 变量名(不带前导 '?')。单值,xsd:string。定义域为 logic:ResultColumn(以散文给出)。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/commitmentBeneficiaryDistinctness|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Asserts that a gmeow:Commitment's gmeow:committedAgent and gmeow:commitmentBeneficiary must be distinct: a resolution made purely to oneself is an Intention, not a Commitment. The native coherence gate raises a violation when they coincide."
msgstr "断言一个 gmeow:Commitment 的 gmeow:committedAgent 与 gmeow:commitmentBeneficiary 必须相异:纯粹对自己作出的决意是一个 Intention,而非 Commitment。当二者重合时,原生一致性门抛出一个违规。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CommitmentShiftingBridge|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A bridge that shifts ontological commitment rather than preserving satisfaction: the kind borne by a logic:BridgeView alignment to a top-level ontology (BFO, DOLCE, SUMO, YAMATO). The loss ledger refuses to emit owl:equivalentClass for it; the bridge is adopted by reference (Principle 5), never as an identity collapse."
msgstr "一座转移本体论承诺而非保持可满足性的桥:即一个 logic:BridgeView 对某上层本体(BFO、DOLCE、SUMO、YAMATO)的对齐所承载的那种桥。损失账本拒绝为它发出 owl:equivalentClass;该桥是按引用采纳的(原则 5),绝不作为身份坍缩。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CommittedExecution|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The execution-mode value under which a transaction program's elementary updates are committed — the effects advance the path and persist. The default execution mode; contrast logic:HypotheticalExecution, which discards effects."
msgstr "在其之下事务程序的初等更新被提交的执行模式取值——效果推进路径并持久化。默认执行模式;与 logic:HypotheticalExecution 相对照,后者丢弃效果。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CommonLogicProjection|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The projection-target value requesting the answer be rendered to the ISO Common Logic surface. One of several output targets a single contract may name at once; like every projection target it is a rendering request and never alters which entailments hold."
msgstr "请求将答案渲染到 ISO Common Logic 表面的投影目标取值。它是单个契约可一次性命名的若干输出目标之一;如同每个投影目标,它是一个渲染请求,绝不改变哪些蕴涵成立。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ComparativeRelationshipType|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A logic:RelationshipType whose instances are comparative relations grounded directly in the qualities of their relata, with NO mediating relator (heavier-than, older-than, the same colour as). The counterpart of gufo:ComparativeRelationshipType; the relation holds in virtue of the relata's logic:Quality values standing in an ordering within a logic:QualitySpace, not in virtue of any logic:Relator. Stated in prose, not as a subclass edge. Contrast logic:MaterialRelationshipType, which is relator-founded."
msgstr "一个 logic:RelationshipType,其实例是直接以其关系项的质为根据、没有中介关系子的比较关系(比…重、比…老、与…同色)。它是 gufo:ComparativeRelationshipType 的对应物;该关系凭借关系项的 logic:Quality 取值在某个 logic:QualitySpace 内处于一个序中而成立,而非凭借任何 logic:Relator。以散文给出,而非作为子类边。与 logic:MaterialRelationshipType 相对照,后者以关系子为基。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CompatibilityRule|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A single local rule of the reasoning-contract feature model (constraint graph): it states that two facet values require each other, exclude each other, or together demand a particular resource value or decidability class. The supported-contract set is computed from these rules — a contract is supported iff it violates none. Authored canonically in crates/logic (Rust) and projected here as documentation; the projection is lossy (Principle 17)."
msgstr "推理契约特征模型(约束图)的一条单一局部规则:它陈述两个面值互相要求、互相排斥,或共同要求某个特定的资源取值或可判定性类。受支持契约集由这些规则计算得出——一个契约受支持当且仅当它不违反任何一条。在 crates/logic(Rust)中规范撰写,并在此作为文档投影;该投影是有损的(原则 17)。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/compensation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ActionSchema to the action that undoes this one — the basis for recoverable transactions. Tied to the realized outcome, not the schema as a whole: when the outcome set is nondeterministic each branch names the compensation that recovers from IT, so recovery matches what actually happened rather than applying one generic undo across every branch. Domain logic:ActionSchema (stated in prose). One of the eight action-theory facets."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ActionSchema 关联到撤销此动作的动作——可恢复事务的基础。它系于已实现的结果,而非整体模式:当结果集是非确定的时,每个分支命名从该分支恢复的补偿,因此恢复对应于实际发生的情况,而非在每个分支上套用一个通用撤销。定义域为 logic:ActionSchema(以散文给出)。动作理论八个面之一。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/competesForResource|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates two gmeow:Goals that both draw on a resource an action schema declares (logic:actionResource), where the supply is insufficient for both. Domain gmeow:Goal, range gmeow:Goal (stated in prose). The seam between goal conflict and the action-theory resource facet. One of seven conflict relations between independently-meaningful goals, weaker than gmeow:counterGoal (constitutive opposition)."
msgstr "关联两个都汲取某动作模式所声明的资源(logic:actionResource)的 gmeow:Goal,而该供给不足以同时满足二者。定义域为 gmeow:Goal,值域为 gmeow:Goal(以散文给出)。它是目标冲突与动作理论资源面之间的接缝。这是独立有意义目标之间七种冲突关系之一,比 gmeow:counterGoal(构成性对立)更弱。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/competesWithIrreflexivity|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Asserts on the canonical carrier that gmeow:competesWith is irreflexive: a rival standpoint claim never competes with itself, as its skos:definition states. gmeow:competesWith is symmetric (owl:SymmetricProperty) but irreflexive; irreflexivity is enforced here on the canonical carrier — kept out of OWL to hold the reasoned profile within OWL 2 DL (the deception discipline) — and the native coherence gate raises a violation for a claim asserted to compete with itself; the generated SHACL constraint surface is its projection."
msgstr "在规范载体上断言 gmeow:competesWith 是非自反的:一个竞争性立场主张绝不与自身竞争,正如其 skos:definition 所述。gmeow:competesWith 是对称的(owl:SymmetricProperty)但非自反;非自反性在此于规范载体上强制执行——将其排除在 OWL 之外以把推理剖面维持在 OWL 2 DL 之内(欺骗纪律)——且原生一致性门对一个被断言为与自身竞争的主张抛出违规;生成的 SHACL 约束表面是其投影。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CompleteForFragment|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:CompletenessStatus value for an answer complete for the certified fragment the contract pins — a conclusive evaluation even when the whole run did not otherwise complete. Wire value `complete-for-fragment`."
msgstr "针对某个答案的 logic:CompletenessStatus 取值,该答案相对于契约所钉定的被认证片段是完整的——即使整次运行在其他方面未完成,这也是一次结论性评估。线值 `complete-for-fragment`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CompletenessStatus|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The closed value class of the logic:resultCompleteness field: relative to what is the answer complete? Its individuals are logic:CompleteForFragment, logic:Incomplete, and logic:CompletenessUnknown. The set is closed; a misspelt value is rejected (design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md, §The reasoning result)."
msgstr "logic:resultCompleteness 字段的封闭取值类:答案相对于什么而完整?其个体为 logic:CompleteForFragment、logic:Incomplete 与 logic:CompletenessUnknown。该集合是封闭的;拼写错误的取值被拒绝(design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md,§推理结果)。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CompletenessUnknown|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:CompletenessStatus value when completeness is not a defined question for the request — e.g. a genuine incomparable-entrenchment revision tie. Wire value `unknown`."
msgstr "当完整性对该请求不是一个有定义的问题时的 logic:CompletenessStatus 取值——例如一次真正的不可比较固守度修订平局。线值 `unknown`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CompleteOverApproximation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The projection may overgenerate but does not miss canonical answers: complete but possibly unsound. Every canonical answer appears, alongside possible spurious ones; the dual of logic:SoundUnderApproximation."
msgstr "该投影可能过度生成,但不遗漏规范答案:完整但可能不可靠。每个规范答案都出现,同时伴随可能的虚假答案;它是 logic:SoundUnderApproximation 的对偶。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/complexityClass|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The complexity / decidability class a projection or profile certifies — EL → PTIME, DL → decidable/N2EXPTIME, Datalog → terminating/PTIME-data — recorded alongside the preservation polarity in the loss ledger. Decidability is a projection guarantee bought by projecting down, not a canonical-layer promise: the canonical layer is maximally expressive and only semi-decidable."
msgstr "一个投影或剖面所认证的复杂度 / 可判定性类——EL → PTIME、DL → decidable/N2EXPTIME、Datalog → terminating/PTIME-data——与保持极性一并记录在损失账本中。可判定性是通过向下投影而换得的投影保证,而非规范层的许诺:规范层是最大程度可表达的,且仅是半可判定的。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/compositionExclusionPart|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:RoleCompositionExclusionAssertion to the role whose bound value must not be a component of the whole role's value. Domain logic:RoleCompositionExclusionAssertion; single-valued."
msgstr "将一个 logic:RoleCompositionExclusionAssertion 关联到某个角色,其绑定值不得是整体角色取值的一个组件。定义域为 logic:RoleCompositionExclusionAssertion;单值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/compositionExclusionTarget|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:RoleCompositionExclusionAssertion to the class whose focus nodes it constrains. Domain logic:RoleCompositionExclusionAssertion; single-valued."
msgstr "将一个 logic:RoleCompositionExclusionAssertion 关联到它约束其焦点节点的类。定义域为 logic:RoleCompositionExclusionAssertion;单值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/compositionExclusionVia|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:RoleCompositionExclusionAssertion to a composition property linking the whole role's value to a component. Each asserted value is one step the exclusion ranges over; the native coherence gate raises a violation when the part role coincides with a component reached through any of them. Domain logic:RoleCompositionExclusionAssertion; multi-valued."
msgstr "将一个 logic:RoleCompositionExclusionAssertion 关联到一个把整体角色取值连到某组件的组合属性。每个被断言的取值是排斥所遍历的一步;当部分角色与经由其中任一步所抵达的组件重合时,原生一致性门抛出一个违规。定义域为 logic:RoleCompositionExclusionAssertion;多值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/compositionExclusionWhole|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:RoleCompositionExclusionAssertion to the role binding the WHOLE whose components the part role must not coincide with. Domain logic:RoleCompositionExclusionAssertion; single-valued."
msgstr "将一个 logic:RoleCompositionExclusionAssertion 关联到绑定整体的角色,部分角色不得与该整体的组件重合。定义域为 logic:RoleCompositionExclusionAssertion;单值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/conclusion|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The canonical conclusion text a logic:ReasoningResult's verdict is about — part of the proof certificate. Single-valued. Domain logic:ReasoningResult (stated in prose)."
msgstr "一个 logic:ReasoningResult 的裁决所关涉的规范结论文本——证明证书的一部分。单值。定义域为 logic:ReasoningResult(以散文给出)。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConcreteIndividual|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A logic:Individual located in spacetime — an endurant or a perdurant, something that bears qualities and stands in causal relations. The counterpart of gufo:ConcreteIndividual; the concrete sibling that complements logic:AbstractIndividual within logic:Individual. Every logic:Endurant and every logic:Perdurant is a logic:ConcreteIndividual (stated in prose, not as a subclass edge); it is the instance-level counterpart of logic:ConcreteIndividualType."
msgstr "一个定位于时空中的 logic:Individual——一个持续体或一个续存体,某个承载质并处于因果关系中的东西。它是 gufo:ConcreteIndividual 的对应物;是在 logic:Individual 内补足 logic:AbstractIndividual 的具体同胞。每个 logic:Endurant 与每个 logic:Perdurant 都是一个 logic:ConcreteIndividual(以散文给出,而非作为子类边);它是 logic:ConcreteIndividualType 在实例层面的对应物。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConcreteIndividualType|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A logic:Type whose instances are logic:ConcreteIndividuals — the type whose extension (via logic:instanceOf) is drawn from individuals located in spacetime (endurants and perdurants). The counterpart of gufo:ConcreteIndividualType; the umbrella over logic:EndurantType together with the type-of-perdurants. Stated in prose, not as a subclass edge. Contrast logic:AbstractIndividualType."
msgstr "一个 logic:Type,其实例是 logic:ConcreteIndividual——即其外延(经 logic:instanceOf)取自定位于时空中的个体(持续体与续存体)的类型。它是 gufo:ConcreteIndividualType 的对应物;是覆盖 logic:EndurantType 连同续存体之类型的伞状类。以散文给出,而非作为子类边。与 logic:AbstractIndividualType 相对照。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConcurrencyControlProtocol|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The IMPLEMENTATION MECHANISM that enforces a chosen isolation level — HOW a guarantee is achieved, never the guarantee itself. The closed value class of concurrency-control protocols. Its individuals are logic:StrictTwoPhaseLocking, logic:StrongStrictTwoPhaseLocking, logic:TimestampOrdering, logic:OptimisticValidation, and logic:MultiversionConcurrencyControl. The set is closed; a misspelt value is rejected. This is one of three distinct, separately-declared concurrency concerns that must NOT be conflated: a logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol is a mechanism, a logic:SerializabilityCriterion is a property of a history, and a logic:IsolationLevel is a guarantee strength — a protocol is how a guarantee is achieved, it is never the guarantee itself."
msgstr "强制执行所选隔离级别的实现机制——即保证是如何达成的,绝非保证本身。并发控制协议的封闭取值类。其个体为 logic:StrictTwoPhaseLocking、logic:StrongStrictTwoPhaseLocking、logic:TimestampOrdering、logic:OptimisticValidation 与 logic:MultiversionConcurrencyControl。该集合是封闭的;拼写错误的取值被拒绝。这是三个相异、分别声明、不得混为一谈的并发关切之一:一个 logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol 是一种机制,一个 logic:SerializabilityCriterion 是一段历史的性质,而一个 logic:IsolationLevel 是一种保证强度——协议是保证如何达成的方式,它绝不是保证本身。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/concurrentComposedFrom|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a DERIVED logic:ConcurrentHistory to each of the two transaction-program operands (the logic:leftOperand and logic:rightOperand of the logic:ConcurrentComposition) whose interleaved elementary steps produced its conflict edges. Domain logic:ConcurrentHistory, range a transaction-program node (stated in prose); multi-valued (one link per operand). It is the audit trail from the history back to the authored sub-programs that gave rise to it, kept distinct from logic:precedes (an edge BETWEEN the transactions within the history) — this link points OUT to the programs, not between operations."
msgstr "将一个派生的 logic:ConcurrentHistory 关联到两个事务程序操作数中的每一个(即 logic:ConcurrentComposition 的 logic:leftOperand 与 logic:rightOperand),其交错的初等步骤产生了它的冲突边。定义域为 logic:ConcurrentHistory,值域为一个事务程序节点(以散文给出);多值(每个操作数一条链接)。它是从历史回溯到催生它的所撰写子程序的审计线索,与 logic:precedes(历史内各事务之间的一条边)保持相异——此链接向外指向程序,而非在各操作之间。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConcurrentComposition|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The concurrent-composition program combinator: two sub-programs advance together with their elementary steps interleaved over a shared path. The left sub-program is carried by logic:leftOperand and the right by logic:rightOperand. This is the COMPOSITION OPERATOR that states two programs run concurrently — it is DISTINCT from the three separately-declared concurrency correctness concerns the transaction layer keeps apart: (a) logic:SerializabilityCriterion is a correctness PROPERTY OF A HISTORY (conflict-serializability or view-serializability), (b) logic:IsolationLevel is the declared GUARANTEE STRENGTH a schedule must meet, and (c) logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol is the IMPLEMENTATION MECHANISM enforcing that strength. ConcurrentComposition names the structural operator; whether the resulting history is serializable, what isolation is declared, and which protocol enforces it are separately-declared facets. A logic:ConcurrentHistory carries the conflict edges whose cycle structure logic:SerializationAnomaly detects; logic:ConcurrentComposition names the program that gives rise to such a history. Typed APART from ordinary (at-a-state) conjunction — concurrent programs advance over a shared path segment, while a conjunctive formula holds at a single state."
msgstr "并发组合的程序组合子:两个子程序一同推进,其初等步骤在一条共享路径上交错。左子程序由 logic:leftOperand 携带,右子程序由 logic:rightOperand 携带。这是陈述两个程序并发运行的组合算子——它有别于事务层所分开的三个分别声明的并发正确性关切:(a) logic:SerializabilityCriterion 是一段历史的正确性性质(冲突可串行化或视图可串行化),(b) logic:IsolationLevel 是某调度必须满足的已声明保证强度,以及 (c) logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol 是强制执行该强度的实现机制。ConcurrentComposition 命名结构算子;所得历史是否可串行化、声明了何种隔离、以及哪个协议强制执行它,都是分别声明的面。一个 logic:ConcurrentHistory 携带其环结构由 logic:SerializationAnomaly 检测的冲突边;logic:ConcurrentComposition 命名催生这样一段历史的程序。它的类型与普通的(在某状态处的)合取区分开来——并发程序在一段共享路径区段上推进,而一个合取公式在单一状态成立。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConcurrentHistory|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The transaction history of a concurrent composition: the node that carries the logic:precedes conflict edges whose cycle structure logic:SerializationAnomaly classifies. The native concurrent evaluator DERIVES it from the interleaved execution of a logic:ConcurrentComposition's two legs (it may also be authored directly as a conflict graph). It is a HISTORY-LEVEL property bearer, kept DISTINCT from the logic:ConcurrentComposition PROGRAM that gives rise to it and from the logic:TransactionOutcome VERDICT of running that program — a history records which conflicting operations were ordered against which, not whether a path exists. Its serializability is judged against the logic:serializabilityCriterion it carries (default logic:ConflictSerializability); a cyclic conflict graph is surfaced as a logic:SerializationAnomaly finding, never silently linearized and never a logical contradiction within a state."
msgstr "并发组合的事务历史:承载 logic:precedes 冲突边、其环结构由 logic:SerializationAnomaly 分类的节点。原生并发求值器从一个 logic:ConcurrentComposition 两条腿的交错执行中派生它(它也可直接作为冲突图撰写)。它是一个历史层面的性质承载者,与催生它的 logic:ConcurrentComposition 程序、以及运行该程序的 logic:TransactionOutcome 裁决保持相异——一段历史记录哪些冲突操作相对哪些被排序,而非是否存在某条路径。它的可串行化性依其所携带的 logic:serializabilityCriterion(默认 logic:ConflictSerializability)判定;一个有环的冲突图作为一个 logic:SerializationAnomaly 发现被呈现,绝不被静默线性化,也绝不是某状态内的逻辑矛盾。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConditionalGoal|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:GoalExpressionKind for a goal whose target applies only when its logic:guardSituation holds; when the guard is false the goal prescribes nothing and its evaluation reflects does-not-apply rather than satisfied or violated. The single operand carries the guarded target sub-expression."
msgstr "针对某个目标的 logic:GoalExpressionKind,该目标的靶标仅当其 logic:guardSituation 成立时才适用;当守卫为假时,该目标不规定任何东西,其求值反映「不适用」而非满足或违反。单个操作数携带受守卫的靶标子表达式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConditionalRangeAssertion|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A central record asserting that, on a target class, a focus node whose gmeow:-selector property carries a NAMED value must bind — through a second value property — an instance of a required type. It names the class with logic:conditionalRangeTarget, the discriminant property with logic:conditionalRangeSelector and its triggering value with logic:conditionalRangeSelectorValue, the constrained property with logic:conditionalRangeValue, and the demanded type with logic:conditionalRangeRequiredType; the native coherence gate joins them to raise a violation when the selector matches yet the value is not of the required type. Carries a logic:formalizes back-reference to the domain property whose prose it encodes."
msgstr "一条中心记录,它断言在某个目标类上,凡其 gmeow:-选择器属性携带一个具名值的焦点节点,必须——通过第二个取值属性——绑定一个所需类型的实例。它以 logic:conditionalRangeTarget 命名该类,以 logic:conditionalRangeSelector 命名判别属性、以 logic:conditionalRangeSelectorValue 命名其触发值,以 logic:conditionalRangeValue 命名受约束属性,以 logic:conditionalRangeRequiredType 命名所要求的类型;原生一致性门将它们联接,以在选择器匹配但取值不属于所需类型时抛出一个违规。它携带一个 logic:formalizes 反向引用,指向它所编码其散文的定义域属性。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/conditionalRangeRequiredType|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ConditionalRangeAssertion to the class the constrained value must instantiate when the selector matches. Domain logic:ConditionalRangeAssertion; single-valued."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ConditionalRangeAssertion 关联到当选择器匹配时受约束取值必须实例化的类。定义域为 logic:ConditionalRangeAssertion;单值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/conditionalRangeSelector|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ConditionalRangeAssertion to the discriminant property whose value triggers the condition. Read together with logic:conditionalRangeSelectorValue. Domain logic:ConditionalRangeAssertion; single-valued."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ConditionalRangeAssertion 关联到其取值触发该条件的判别属性。与 logic:conditionalRangeSelectorValue 一并阅读。定义域为 logic:ConditionalRangeAssertion;单值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/conditionalRangeSelectorValue|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ConditionalRangeAssertion to the named value of the discriminant property that triggers the required-type condition. Domain logic:ConditionalRangeAssertion; single-valued."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ConditionalRangeAssertion 关联到判别属性那个触发所需类型条件的具名值。定义域为 logic:ConditionalRangeAssertion;单值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/conditionalRangeTarget|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ConditionalRangeAssertion to the class whose focus nodes it constrains. Domain logic:ConditionalRangeAssertion; single-valued."
msgstr "将 logic:ConditionalRangeAssertion 关联到其约束焦点节点的那个类。定义域 logic:ConditionalRangeAssertion；单值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/conditionalRangeValue|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ConditionalRangeAssertion to the property whose bound value must satisfy the required type when the selector matches. Domain logic:ConditionalRangeAssertion; single-valued."
msgstr "将 logic:ConditionalRangeAssertion 关联到某属性，当选择器匹配时该属性的绑定值必须满足所要求的类型。定义域 logic:ConditionalRangeAssertion；单值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConfConsistent|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The conformance-verdict value when a model exists and the conjecture is NOT entailed: the reduction premises ∧ ¬conclusion is satisfiable, so the axiom set is consistent and the entailment fails. The decided-negative outcome the coarse three-bucket view assigns to the TPTP SZS logic:SzsSatisfiable and logic:SzsCounterSatisfiable statuses and to the W3C mf:NegativeEntailment test kind. One of the two informative meet-elements of the logic:ConformanceVerdict lattice (with logic:ConfInconsistent), below the least-informative join logic:ConfIncomplete; the RDF image of the native runner verdict `consistent`."
msgstr "当存在模型且猜想未被蕴含时的一致性判定值：归约前提 ∧ ¬结论 可满足，故公理集是协调的且蕴含不成立。这是粗略的三桶视图分配给 TPTP SZS logic:SzsSatisfiable 与 logic:SzsCounterSatisfiable 状态以及 W3C mf:NegativeEntailment 测试类别的判定为否的结果。它是 logic:ConformanceVerdict 格的两个有信息量的交元素之一（另一个为 logic:ConfInconsistent），位于信息量最少的并 logic:ConfIncomplete 之下；是原生运行器判定 `consistent` 的 RDF 映像。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/confidence|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Epistemic confidence assigned to a statement by a source or process — how sure the asserter is. Normatively distinct from logic:probability: a confidence score is NOT a probability and MUST NOT be interpreted as one unless an explicit mapping to logic:probability is declared. Also distinct from logic:weight (a solver ranking) and logic:evidenceStrength (evidential warrant)."
msgstr "由某来源或过程赋予某陈述的认知置信度——即断言者的确定程度。它在规范上不同于 logic:probability：置信度分值并非概率，除非声明了到 logic:probability 的显式映射，否则不得将其解释为概率。它也不同于 logic:weight（求解器排名）和 logic:evidenceStrength（证据支持强度）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConfIncomplete|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The conformance-verdict value when the reasoner did not decide the problem — it gave up, exhausted its resource budget, or returned an explicit unknown. The decided-nothing outcome the coarse three-bucket view assigns to the TPTP SZS logic:SzsUnknown, logic:SzsGaveUp, logic:SzsTimeout, and logic:SzsResourceOut statuses. The least-informative join (⊤) of the logic:ConformanceVerdict lattice, above both logic:ConfInconsistent and logic:ConfConsistent, so a genuinely-undecided result is never silently read as a decided one; the RDF image of the native runner verdict `incomplete`. Kept strictly distinct from a native capability gap (an out-of-fragment construct is a hard-fail ledger row, not an incomplete swallowed into agreement)."
msgstr "当推理器未对问题作出裁决时的一致性判定值——它放弃了、耗尽了资源预算，或返回了显式的未知。这是粗略的三桶视图分配给 TPTP SZS logic:SzsUnknown、logic:SzsGaveUp、logic:SzsTimeout 和 logic:SzsResourceOut 状态的未决结果。它是 logic:ConformanceVerdict 格中信息量最少的并（⊤），位于 logic:ConfInconsistent 与 logic:ConfConsistent 二者之上，从而使真正未决的结果绝不会被悄然读作已决；它是原生运行器判定 `incomplete` 的 RDF 映像。它与原生能力缺口严格区分（片段之外的构造是硬失败的账本行，而非被吞入一致性中的一项未决）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConfInconsistent|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The conformance-verdict value when the conjecture is entailed / the axiom set has no model: the reduction premises ∧ ¬conclusion is UNSATISFIABLE. The decided-positive outcome the coarse three-bucket view assigns to the TPTP SZS logic:SzsTheorem, logic:SzsUnsatisfiable, and logic:SzsContradictoryAxioms statuses and to the W3C mf:PositiveEntailment test kind. One of the two informative meet-elements of the logic:ConformanceVerdict lattice (with logic:ConfConsistent), below the least-informative join logic:ConfIncomplete; the RDF image of the native runner verdict `inconsistent`. The coarse bucket is a lossy projection: it does not distinguish logic:SzsContradictoryAxioms from logic:SzsUnsatisfiable, so the verbatim token is preserved as provenance via logic:rawStatusToken (design/LOGIC-CONFORMANCE.md, the external FOL soundness oracle)."
msgstr "当猜想被蕴含 / 公理集无模型时的一致性判定值：归约前提 ∧ ¬结论 不可满足。这是粗略的三桶视图分配给 TPTP SZS logic:SzsTheorem、logic:SzsUnsatisfiable 和 logic:SzsContradictoryAxioms 状态以及 W3C mf:PositiveEntailment 测试类别的判定为真的结果。它是 logic:ConformanceVerdict 格的两个有信息量的交元素之一（另一个为 logic:ConfConsistent），位于信息量最少的并 logic:ConfIncomplete 之下；是原生运行器判定 `inconsistent` 的 RDF 映像。粗略的桶是一种有损投影：它不区分 logic:SzsContradictoryAxioms 与 logic:SzsUnsatisfiable，因此原始记号经由 logic:rawStatusToken 作为来源信息逐字保留下来（design/LOGIC-CONFORMANCE.md，外部 FOL 可靠性判定源）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConflictSerializability|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:SerializabilityCriterion value satisfied when an equivalent serial order exists that is reachable from the history by swapping only non-conflicting operations — no swap of a pair of conflicting operations is required. A history property, not a protocol. Contrast logic:ViewSerializability."
msgstr "当存在一个等价的串行次序、且该次序可通过仅交换互不冲突的操作从历史达到（无需交换任何一对冲突操作）时所满足的 logic:SerializabilityCriterion 值。这是历史的属性，而非协议。与 logic:ViewSerializability 相对照。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConformanceVerdict|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The closed, three-valued lattice of external-corpus conformance outcomes: the result a conformance comparison receives when a native verdict is graded against a community-decided ground truth. Its three named individuals are logic:ConfInconsistent (entailment holds / no model), logic:ConfConsistent (a model exists / entailment fails), and logic:ConfIncomplete (the reasoner did not decide) — the last being the least-informative join (⊤) so an undecided result never masquerades as a decided one. The RDF image of the native runner's verdict-status value, and the target of the SZS-status and W3C manifest-kind alignment; the SZS→verdict collapse is a declared lossy projection (logic:SoundUnderApproximation) that this closed lattice makes machine-checkable. The set is closed, so a misspelt verdict names no declared value and is rejected rather than silently accepted, mirroring logic:EmergenceVerdict and logic:ConstraintVerdict (design/LOGIC-CONFORMANCE.md, the two orthogonal correctness axes)."
msgstr "外部语料一致性结果的封闭三值格：当原生判定相对于社区裁定的基准真值被评级时，一致性比较所获得的结果。其三个具名个体为 logic:ConfInconsistent（蕴含成立 / 无模型）、logic:ConfConsistent（存在模型 / 蕴含不成立）和 logic:ConfIncomplete（推理器未作裁决）——后者是信息量最少的并（⊤），从而使未决结果绝不冒充已决。它是原生运行器判定状态值的 RDF 映像，也是 SZS 状态与 W3C 清单类别对齐的目标；SZS→判定的坍缩是一种已声明的有损投影（logic:SoundUnderApproximation），此封闭格使之可由机器核验。该集合是封闭的，故拼写错误的判定不指称任何已声明的值，会被拒绝而非被悄然接受，与 logic:EmergenceVerdict 和 logic:ConstraintVerdict 相仿（design/LOGIC-CONFORMANCE.md，两个正交的正确性轴）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConjectureCorroborated|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The epistemic state of a conjecture whose formula was Supported (Belnap true) from its standpoint: the symmetric test found for the formula and no counterexample. Corroboration is provisional support, never proof — a corroborated formula becomes eligible for the positive promotion leg (logic:conjecturePromotionCandidate to a canonical-axiom candidate), still gated through review. Wire value `corroborated`."
msgstr "某猜想的认知状态，其公式从其立场看为「被支持」（Belnap 真）：对称检验为该公式找到了支持且无反例。佐证是暂时性的支持，绝非证明——被佐证的公式变得有资格进入正向晋升分支（logic:conjecturePromotionCandidate 通往规范公理候选），仍须经过评审把关。传输值 `corroborated`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/conjectureDischargeVerdict|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Conjecture to the logic:DischargeVerdict carrying its CONCLUSIVENESS — reusing the existing three-value obligation class rather than minting a parallel notion. logic:ObligationDischarged marks a conclusive result (a corroboration or a refutation within a complete fragment, or a conclusive independence for an open conjecture); logic:ObligationUnknown marks a budget-exhausted or fragment-gap run that is carried forward, never 'proved'. An open conjecture carrying logic:ObligationUnknown that is NOT in logic:ConjectureOpen is a hard error (verify.conjecture-open-if-inconclusive): a timeout may never read as refuted. Single-valued. Domain logic:Conjecture, range logic:DischargeVerdict."
msgstr "将 logic:Conjecture 关联到承载其「决定性」的 logic:DischargeVerdict——复用现有的三值义务类，而非铸造一个平行概念。logic:ObligationDischarged 标记决定性结果（在完全片段内的一次佐证或一次反驳，或对开放猜想的一次决定性独立性）；logic:ObligationUnknown 标记预算耗尽或片段缺口的运行，此类运行被向前携带，绝不算作「已证」。携带 logic:ObligationUnknown 却不处于 logic:ConjectureOpen 的开放猜想属于硬错误（verify.conjecture-open-if-inconclusive）：超时绝不可读作已被反驳。单值。定义域 logic:Conjecture，值域 logic:DischargeVerdict。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/conjectureEntails|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The corpus entailment pre-order over conjectures: logic:conjectureEntails relates a formula phi to a formula psi it entails (phi models psi), so a refutation of psi propagates contrapositively to phi (if psi is refuted, phi cannot stand). The relation is a PRE-ORDER in intent (reflexive and transitive), but its full transitive closure is NOT materialized as a stored relation: the vocabulary carries each pairwise edge and the propagation competency query (conjecture-entails-propagation.rq) reasons over those edges directly, so contrapositive propagation is queryable without the corpus-wide closure being computed as a persisted extension. Each edge is itself a conjecture test (that phi genuinely entails psi), not a bare assertion. Domain logic:Conjecture, range logic:Conjecture."
msgstr "语料在猜想上的蕴含预序：logic:conjectureEntails 将公式 phi 关联到它所蕴含的公式 psi（phi 是 psi 的模型），因此对 psi 的反驳会逆否地传播到 phi（若 psi 被反驳，则 phi 不能成立）。该关系在意图上是预序（自反且传递），但其完整的传递闭包并不作为存储关系被物化：词汇表承载每一条成对的边，传播能力查询（conjecture-entails-propagation.rq）直接在这些边上进行推理，因此逆否传播是可查询的，而无需将全语料范围的闭包计算为持久化的外延。每条边本身都是一次猜想检验（即 phi 确实蕴含 psi），而非裸断言。定义域 logic:Conjecture，值域 logic:Conjecture。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/conjectureFormula|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The canonical, alpha-normalized identity of the conjectured formula: the content_key string of the full first-order AST (the alpha-normalized content identity from the full-FOL formula AST), so two conjectures that name the same formula up to bound-variable renaming share one key and cannot be double-counted. Single-valued, xsd:string. Domain logic:Conjecture."
msgstr "被猜想公式的规范化、经 alpha 归一化的身份：完整一阶 AST 的 content_key 字符串（源自完整 FOL 公式 AST 的经 alpha 归一化的内容身份），从而使两个在约束变量重命名意义下指称同一公式的猜想共享同一个键，不会被重复计数。单值，xsd:string。定义域 logic:Conjecture。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConjectureLifecycleState|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The closed four-member value class of the logic:conjectureLifecycleState facet: the EPISTEMIC state a logic:Conjecture occupies, ORTHOGONAL to the GOVERNANCE lifecycle (logic:CandidateLifecycleState) it inherits from the candidate spine — Principle 9 refuses to collapse two distinct axes into one. Its individuals are logic:ConjectureOpen, logic:ConjectureCorroborated, logic:ConjectureRefutedInStandpoint and logic:ConjectureWithdrawn, each projected from a Belnap truth-value origin (Supported becomes Corroborated; Opposed or Both becomes RefutedInStandpoint; Neither-conclusive becomes Open carrying logic:ObligationDischarged; Undetermined or BudgetExhausted becomes Open carrying logic:ObligationUnknown; Withdrawn is an author action, never engine-produced). The set is closed, so a misspelt state names no declared value and is rejected (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the conjecture-and-refutation section)."
msgstr "logic:conjectureLifecycleState 面向的封闭四成员值类：logic:Conjecture 所处的「认知」状态，与它从候选主干继承的「治理」生命周期（logic:CandidateLifecycleState）正交——原则 9 拒绝把两个不同的轴坍缩为一个。其个体为 logic:ConjectureOpen、logic:ConjectureCorroborated、logic:ConjectureRefutedInStandpoint 和 logic:ConjectureWithdrawn，各自从一个 Belnap 真值来源投影而来（被支持变为已佐证；被反对或两者兼具变为在立场中被反驳；两者皆非且决定性的变为开放并携带 logic:ObligationDischarged；未定或预算耗尽变为开放并携带 logic:ObligationUnknown；已撤回是作者行为，绝非引擎产生）。该集合是封闭的，故拼写错误的状态不指称任何已声明的值，会被拒绝（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，猜想与反驳一节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/conjectureLifecycleState|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Conjecture to its current EPISTEMIC logic:ConjectureLifecycleState (open / corroborated / refuted-in-standpoint / withdrawn). Single-valued and REQUIRED. Orthogonal to logic:candidateLifecycle (the GOVERNANCE state inherited from the candidate spine): a conjecture may be governance-accepted yet epistemically open, so the two are never collapsed (Principle 9). Domain logic:Conjecture, range logic:ConjectureLifecycleState."
msgstr "将 logic:Conjecture 关联到其当前的「认知」logic:ConjectureLifecycleState（open / corroborated / refuted-in-standpoint / withdrawn）。单值且必需。与 logic:candidateLifecycle（从候选主干继承的「治理」状态）正交：一个猜想可能在治理上被接受却在认知上开放，故二者绝不坍缩（原则 9）。定义域 logic:Conjecture，值域 logic:ConjectureLifecycleState。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConjectureOpen|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The epistemic state of a conjecture whose symmetric formula / negation test was NOT conclusive in either direction: neither corroborated nor refuted. Two Belnap origins land here and are told apart by the carried logic:conjectureDischargeVerdict — a Neither-conclusive run (formula and negation both genuinely undecided within a complete fragment) carries logic:ObligationDischarged (conclusive independence), while an Undetermined or budget-exhausted run carries logic:ObligationUnknown (not proved absent, carried forward). A timeout NEVER reads as refuted. Wire value `open`."
msgstr "某猜想的认知状态，其对称的公式 / 否定检验在两个方向上均未得出决定性结论：既未被佐证也未被反驳。两个 Belnap 来源汇于此处，并通过所承载的 logic:conjectureDischargeVerdict 加以区分——「两者皆非且决定性」的运行（公式与其否定在完全片段内均真正未决）携带 logic:ObligationDischarged（决定性独立），而未定或预算耗尽的运行携带 logic:ObligationUnknown（并非证明其不成立，而是向前携带）。超时绝不读作已被反驳。传输值 `open`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/conjecturePromotionCandidate|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The POSITIVE promotion leg: relates a logic:ConjectureCorroborated conjecture to the logic:FormalizationCandidate proposing to promote its formula to a canonical axiom. The candidate still runs the ordinary reviewer gate (corroboration is provisional support, never proof), so a corroborated conjecture never becomes a canonical axiom by mere entailment. Present exactly when the conjecture is corroborated. Domain logic:Conjecture, range logic:FormalizationCandidate."
msgstr "「正向」晋升分支：将一个 logic:ConjectureCorroborated 猜想关联到提议将其公式晋升为规范公理的 logic:FormalizationCandidate。该候选仍要通过普通的评审者关卡（佐证是暂时性支持，绝非证明），因此被佐证的猜想绝不会仅凭蕴含就成为规范公理。恰好在猜想被佐证时存在。定义域 logic:Conjecture，值域 logic:FormalizationCandidate。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/conjectureRefinedFrom|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The Lakatos refinement edge: relates a successor conjecture to the refuted conjecture it weakens — the 'monster-barring' move where a refuted conjecture is not abandoned but replaced by a strictly weaker successor that excludes the counterexample. Read together with logic:survivesCounterexample (the witness the successor now excludes). Domain logic:Conjecture, range logic:Conjecture."
msgstr "Lakatos 精化边：将后继猜想关联到它所削弱的被反驳猜想——即「排除怪物」之举，被反驳的猜想不被放弃，而是被一个严格更弱、排除该反例的后继所取代。与 logic:survivesCounterexample（后继如今所排除的见证）一并阅读。定义域 logic:Conjecture，值域 logic:Conjecture。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConjectureRefutationWitnessConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A closed-world integrity constraint: a logic:Conjecture in logic:ConjectureRefutedInStandpoint names at least one logic:conjectureRefutationWitness — the concrete logic:ContradictionWitness backing the refutation."
msgstr "一条封闭世界完整性约束：处于 logic:ConjectureRefutedInStandpoint 的 logic:Conjecture 至少指称一个 logic:conjectureRefutationWitness——即支撑该反驳的具体 logic:ContradictionWitness。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/conjectureRefutationWitness|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a refuted logic:Conjecture to the logic:ContradictionWitness that refutes it — the concrete counterexample naming the individual forced to owl:Nothing, the world, and the premises. Present exactly when the conjecture is logic:ConjectureRefutedInStandpoint (a refuted conjecture with no witness is a hard error, logic:ConjectureShape and verify.conjecture-refutation-witness-required; a witness on a non-refuted conjecture is meaningless). Domain logic:Conjecture, range logic:ContradictionWitness."
msgstr "将被反驳的 logic:Conjecture 关联到反驳它的 logic:ContradictionWitness——即具体的反例，指明被迫归入 owl:Nothing 的个体、世界以及诸前提。恰好在猜想为 logic:ConjectureRefutedInStandpoint 时存在（无见证的被反驳猜想属于硬错误，logic:ConjectureShape 及 verify.conjecture-refutation-witness-required；将见证置于未被反驳的猜想上则毫无意义）。定义域 logic:Conjecture，值域 logic:ContradictionWitness。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConjectureRefutedInStandpoint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The epistemic state of a conjecture whose formula was Opposed or Both (Belnap false or contradictory) from its standpoint: a concrete counterexample was found, forcing some individual to owl:Nothing. The refutation is scoped to the standpoint (Principle 9), never global-false, and MUST name a concrete logic:ContradictionWitness (logic:conjectureRefutationWitness, enforced by logic:ConjectureShape and verify.conjecture-refutation-witness-required). A robustly-refuted formula becomes eligible for the anti-conjecture promotion leg (logic:antiConjectureObligationCandidate to a logic:NonEntailmentObligation candidate forbidding the formula). Wire value `refuted-in-standpoint`."
msgstr "某猜想的认知状态，其公式从其立场看为「被反对」或「两者兼具」（Belnap 假或矛盾）：找到了具体的反例，迫使某个体归入 owl:Nothing。该反驳的范围限定于该立场（原则 9），绝非全局为假，并且必须指称一个具体的 logic:ContradictionWitness（logic:conjectureRefutationWitness，由 logic:ConjectureShape 及 verify.conjecture-refutation-witness-required 强制执行）。被稳健反驳的公式变得有资格进入反猜想晋升分支（logic:antiConjectureObligationCandidate 通往禁止该公式的 logic:NonEntailmentObligation 候选）。传输值 `refuted-in-standpoint`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Conjecture|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A named, standpoint-scoped candidate formula under active epistemic test: the dynamic, testable specialization of the logic:FormalizationCandidate spine (rdfs:subClassOf logic:FormalizationCandidate). Because it subclasses the candidate, a conjecture carries all eight universal candidate carriers (logic:candidateSourceHash, logic:candidateExtractionProvenance, logic:candidateScope, logic:candidateContract, logic:candidateCategory, logic:candidateLifecycle, logic:candidateProjectionBehavior, logic:candidateSemanticRisk); what specializes it is that its positive/negative cases are ENGINE-PRODUCED (via a scoped reasoning run recorded through logic:verdictProvenance) rather than reviewer-asserted. Its verdict is always scoped to a single reified standpoint (logic:conjectureStandpoint, REQUIRED — Principle 9 refuses a global-false verdict), and it carries an EPISTEMIC lifecycle (logic:conjectureLifecycleState: open / corroborated / refuted-in-standpoint / withdrawn) ORTHOGONAL to the GOVERNANCE lifecycle it inherits from the candidate (logic:candidateLifecycle). Conclusiveness reuses the existing logic:DischargeVerdict value class (logic:conjectureDischargeVerdict), never a freshly minted notion: a conclusive independence carries logic:ObligationDischarged, a budget-exhausted or fragment-gap run carries logic:ObligationUnknown. The conjectured formula is tested symmetrically against its constructed strong negation as two INDEPENDENT legs — support for the formula (the standpoint's KB entails it) and support for its negation (the KB refutes it, decided by the inconsistency of asserting the formula) — so a KB that entails BOTH the formula AND its negation from one standpoint yields the Belnap glut logic:InfoBoth, a within-standpoint contradiction LOCALIZED to the candidate proposition (a genuine refutation still carrying a concrete logic:ContradictionWitness), whereas a KB contradictory for reasons UNRELATED to the candidate cannot host a meaningful test at all. A refutation names a concrete logic:ContradictionWitness, and the two symmetric promotion legs feed a corroborated formula back as a canonical-axiom candidate (logic:conjecturePromotionCandidate) and a robustly-refuted formula forward as a logic:NonEntailmentObligation candidate (logic:antiConjectureObligationCandidate) (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the conjecture-and-refutation section)."
msgstr "一个具名的、以立场为范围、处于活跃认知检验之下的候选公式：logic:FormalizationCandidate 主干的动态、可检验的特化（rdfs:subClassOf logic:FormalizationCandidate）。由于它是候选的子类，猜想承载全部八个通用候选载体（logic:candidateSourceHash、logic:candidateExtractionProvenance、logic:candidateScope、logic:candidateContract、logic:candidateCategory、logic:candidateLifecycle、logic:candidateProjectionBehavior、logic:candidateSemanticRisk）；使其特化的是其正/负例由「引擎产生」（经由通过 logic:verdictProvenance 记录的一次以范围限定的推理运行），而非由评审者断言。其判定始终以单一具体化的立场为范围（logic:conjectureStandpoint，必需——原则 9 拒绝全局为假的判定），且它承载一个「认知」生命周期（logic:conjectureLifecycleState：open / corroborated / refuted-in-standpoint / withdrawn），与它从候选继承的「治理」生命周期（logic:candidateLifecycle）正交。决定性复用现有的 logic:DischargeVerdict 值类（logic:conjectureDischargeVerdict），绝非新铸的概念：决定性独立携带 logic:ObligationDischarged，预算耗尽或片段缺口的运行携带 logic:ObligationUnknown。被猜想的公式针对其构造出的强否定被对称地检验，构成两条「独立」分支——对公式的支持（该立场的知识库蕴含它）与对其否定的支持（知识库反驳它，由断言该公式所致的不协调性来判定）——因此，一个从某立场同时蕴含公式「及」其否定的知识库会产生 Belnap 溢余 logic:InfoBoth，即一个「局部化」于该候选命题的立场内矛盾（仍携带具体 logic:ContradictionWitness 的真正反驳），而一个因与该候选「无关」的原因而矛盾的知识库根本无法承载有意义的检验。反驳指称一个具体的 logic:ContradictionWitness，两条对称的晋升分支将被佐证的公式回送为规范公理候选（logic:conjecturePromotionCandidate），并将被稳健反驳的公式前送为 logic:NonEntailmentObligation 候选（logic:antiConjectureObligationCandidate）（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，猜想与反驳一节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/conjectureStandpoint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Conjecture to the reified standpoint its verdict is scoped to — a REQUIRED, single-valued IRI (a gmeow:Standpoint, stated in prose). Standpoint scoping here is REIFICATION, never a named graph: the verdict is 'the formula is refuted FROM THIS standpoint', never a global-false claim (Principle 9). A conjecture with no standpoint has an ill-scoped verdict and is a hard governance error (verify.conjecture-standpoint-scoped). Single-valued. Domain logic:Conjecture."
msgstr "将 logic:Conjecture 关联到其判定所限定范围的具体化立场——一个必需的、单值的 IRI（一个 gmeow:Standpoint，以散文陈述）。此处的立场范围限定是「具体化」，绝非具名图：判定是「该公式从『这个』立场看被反驳」，绝非全局为假的主张（原则 9）。没有立场的猜想具有范围不当的判定，属于硬治理错误（verify.conjecture-standpoint-scoped）。单值。定义域 logic:Conjecture。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/conjectureVerdict|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Conjecture to the content-addressed reasoning-result node its verdict was read from — a logic:ReasoningResult (stated in prose) produced by the scoped reasoning run over the standpoint. Where logic:conjectureLifecycleState and logic:conjectureDischargeVerdict carry the projected epistemic verdict and conclusiveness, this links back to the full result graph the projection was computed from, so the verdict is auditable against its source run. Single-valued. Domain logic:Conjecture."
msgstr "将 logic:Conjecture 关联到其判定所读自的内容寻址推理结果节点——一个 logic:ReasoningResult（以散文陈述），由针对该立场的以范围限定的推理运行产生。logic:conjectureLifecycleState 和 logic:conjectureDischargeVerdict 承载投影后的认知判定与决定性，而此属性回链到投影据以计算的完整结果图，从而使判定可对照其源运行进行审计。单值。定义域 logic:Conjecture。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConjectureWithdrawn|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The terminal epistemic state of a conjecture its author retired — a deliberate authoring action, NEVER an engine-produced verdict (a withdrawn conjecture carries logic:verdictProvenance logic:VerdictReviewerAsserted). Recorded rather than deleted, so the retirement and any partial evidence stay auditable. Distinct from refuted: withdrawal is a human decision to stop testing, not a found counterexample. Wire value `withdrawn`."
msgstr "某猜想被其作者退役后的终态认知状态——一次刻意的撰写行为，绝非引擎产生的判定（被撤回的猜想携带 logic:verdictProvenance logic:VerdictReviewerAsserted）。它被记录而非删除，从而使该退役及任何部分证据保持可审计。与被反驳有别：撤回是停止检验的人类决定，而非找到的反例。传输值 `withdrawn`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConjunctiveGoal|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:GoalExpressionKind for a goal satisfied only when ALL of its logic:operand sub-expressions are satisfied. The conjunctive combinator of the goal algebra; co-equal counterpart of logic:DisjunctiveGoal."
msgstr "用于某目标的 logic:GoalExpressionKind，该目标仅当其全部 logic:operand 子表达式都被满足时才被满足。这是目标代数的合取组合子；与 logic:DisjunctiveGoal 地位对等。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/consequent|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a material-implication logic:Formula to its consequent (the conclusion). Paired with logic:antecedent; their presence marks the node as an implication, distinct from the commutative logic:iff."
msgstr "将一条实质蕴含的 logic:Formula 关联到其后件（结论）。与 logic:antecedent 配对；二者的出现将该节点标记为一个蕴含，区别于可交换的 logic:iff。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/consequent|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "In person(x) implies mortal(x), the mortal atom is the sole logic:consequent."
msgstr "在 person(x) implies mortal(x) 中，mortal 原子是唯一的 logic:consequent。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConstraintBinding|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The constraint-verdict value for a downward constraint that holds upon its target: under the declared logic:GovernanceRegime of a logic:DownwardConstraint, the named target is a proper part of the governing whole and the regime activates the constrained state (logic:activationBasis), and no declared override is borne by the target — so the whole's constraint binds the part. The verdict is strictly regime-relative: it is reached by negation-as-failure over the override derivation while the assessment still binds a declared regime, never as a bare 'unconstrained' default, and a different or stronger logic:GovernanceRegime may activate or quiet the same state under another constraint without contradiction. This is downward constraint, not material causation — the whole limits the part's permissible role/state, it does not produce the part. Contrast logic:ConstraintOverridden and logic:ConstraintUnknown (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "对于一条对其目标成立的下向约束的约束判定值：在 logic:DownwardConstraint 所声明的 logic:GovernanceRegime 之下，具名目标是治理整体的真部分，且该体制激活了受约束状态（logic:activationBasis），并且目标未承载任何已声明的推翻——因此整体的约束绑定该部分。该判定严格相对于体制：它是在评估仍绑定某已声明体制之时、通过对推翻推导的失败即否定而得出，绝非作为裸的「无约束」默认值，且一个不同或更强的 logic:GovernanceRegime 可在另一约束之下激活或平息同一状态而不产生矛盾。这是下向约束，而非物质因果——整体限制部分的可允许角色/状态，它并不产生该部分。与 logic:ConstraintOverridden 及 logic:ConstraintUnknown 相对照（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，类型化与情境化的部分学与全子一节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConstraintOverridden|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The constraint-verdict value for a downward constraint defeated by a declared exception: the logic:DownwardConstraint names an override (logic:constraintOverride) and the constrained target bears that override token (logic:bearsProperty), so the whole's constraint does not bind the part. The positive, derivation-grounded verdict, reached by an actual override-match rather than by negation; it settles before logic:ConstraintBinding so that an overridden constraint is never read as binding. Constraint, not causation: the override quiets a governing limit, it does not unmake a part. Contrast logic:ConstraintBinding (active and not overridden) and logic:ConstraintUnknown (no regime activates the state) (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "对于一条被已声明例外击败的下向约束的约束判定值：logic:DownwardConstraint 指称一个推翻（logic:constraintOverride），且受约束目标承载该推翻记号（logic:bearsProperty），因此整体的约束不绑定该部分。这是正向的、以推导为根据的判定，由一次实际的推翻匹配得出，而非由否定得出；它先于 logic:ConstraintBinding 结算，从而使被推翻的约束绝不被读作绑定。这是约束，而非因果：推翻平息一条治理界限，它并不解除某部分的构成。与 logic:ConstraintBinding（激活且未被推翻）及 logic:ConstraintUnknown（无体制激活该状态）相对照（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，类型化与情境化的部分学与全子一节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/constraintOverride|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The override role of a logic:DownwardConstraint: the declared exception token whose presence on the constrained target defeats the constraint. When the target bears this token (logic:bearsProperty), the constraint receives logic:ConstraintOverridden rather than logic:ConstraintBinding — a structured, declared escape hatch, not an ad-hoc one. An override quiets a governing limit; it never unmakes the part (constraint, not causation). One of the role properties that reify the downward-constraint relation onto the arity-bounded reasoning surface (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "logic:DownwardConstraint 的推翻角色：一个已声明的例外记号，其在受约束目标上的出现会击败该约束。当目标承载此记号（logic:bearsProperty）时，该约束获得 logic:ConstraintOverridden 而非 logic:ConstraintBinding——这是一个结构化的、已声明的逃生口，而非临时的。推翻平息一条治理界限；它绝不解除该部分的构成（约束，而非因果）。它是将下向约束关系具体化到有界元数推理面上的角色属性之一（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，类型化与情境化的部分学与全子一节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/constraintRegime|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The regime role of a logic:DownwardConstraint: the logic:GovernanceRegime the constraint is relative to. Governance is never absolute — the verdict (logic:ConstraintBinding / logic:ConstraintOverridden / logic:ConstraintUnknown) is read only against this declared regime's logic:activationBasis, and recording it is what lets a different regime quiet a binding without contradiction. A constraint that omits this role, or whose constrained state is not in the regime's basis, cannot be shown to bind and receives logic:ConstraintUnknown. One of the role properties (with logic:constraintWhole, logic:constraintTarget, logic:constraintState, and logic:constraintOverride) that reify the downward-constraint relation, mirroring logic:assessmentReductionTheory (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "logic:DownwardConstraint 的体制角色：约束所相对的 logic:GovernanceRegime。治理从不是绝对的——判定（logic:ConstraintBinding / logic:ConstraintOverridden / logic:ConstraintUnknown）只对照此已声明体制的 logic:activationBasis 来读取，而记录它正是让一个不同的体制得以平息某个绑定而不产生矛盾的原因。省略此角色的约束，或其受约束状态不在该体制基底之中的约束，无法被证明为绑定，遂获得 logic:ConstraintUnknown。它是将下向约束关系具体化的角色属性之一（连同 logic:constraintWhole、logic:constraintTarget、logic:constraintState 和 logic:constraintOverride），与 logic:assessmentReductionTheory 相仿（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，类型化与情境化的部分学与全子一节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Constraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "An integrity condition whose violation is a finding, not a derivation: the node kind for a condition that detects bad data rather than producing new facts. Kept distinct from logic:DerivationRule so a check is never mistaken for a productive rule."
msgstr "一条完整性条件，其违反是一项发现，而非一次推导：用于检测坏数据而非产生新事实的条件的节点种类。它与 logic:DerivationRule 保持区分，从而使一次检查绝不会被误认为一条生产性规则。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/constraintState|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The constrained-state role of a logic:DownwardConstraint: the permissible role or state the governing whole limits on the target part — what the part may be or do within the whole. This is typically the part's functional role or gmeow:Goal set in the context of its super-whole: a part's teleological role is fixed relative to the holon it serves, which is exactly the downward face of holonic governance (cf. gmeow:Goal in the teleology slice, linked via rdfs:seeAlso). A constraint binds this state only when the declared logic:GovernanceRegime activates it (logic:activationBasis). One of the role properties that reify the downward-constraint relation onto the arity-bounded reasoning surface (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "logic:DownwardConstraint 的受约束状态角色：治理整体施加于目标部分之上的可允许角色或状态——即该部分在整体之内可以成为什么或做什么。这通常是该部分在其超整体情境中所设定的功能角色或 gmeow:Goal 集合：部分的目的论角色相对于它所服务的全子而固定，这正是全子治理的下向侧面（参见目的论切片中的 gmeow:Goal，经由 rdfs:seeAlso 链接）。仅当已声明的 logic:GovernanceRegime 激活它（logic:activationBasis）时，约束才绑定此状态。它是将下向约束关系具体化到有界元数推理面上的角色属性之一（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，类型化与情境化的部分学与全子一节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/constraintTarget|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The target role of a logic:DownwardConstraint: the proper part the governing whole constrains — the part whose permissible state is limited. The verdict is derived only for this explicitly named target; because the constraint names its target rather than cascading down logic:properPartOf, governance is NON-TRANSITIVE by default (ME9) — a constraint onto a part says nothing automatic about the part's own sub-parts. One of the role properties (with logic:constraintWhole) that reify the downward-constraint relation, mirroring logic:assessmentWhole (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "logic:DownwardConstraint 的目标角色：治理整体所约束的真部分——即其可允许状态受到限制的那个部分。判定仅针对此显式具名的目标而导出；由于约束指称其目标而非沿 logic:properPartOf 级联向下，治理默认「非传递」（ME9）——施于某部分的约束对该部分自身的子部分不作任何自动的断言。它是将下向约束关系具体化的角色属性之一（连同 logic:constraintWhole），与 logic:assessmentWhole 相仿（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，类型化与情境化的部分学与全子一节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConstraintUnknown|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The constraint-verdict value when the binding question cannot be posed: the logic:DownwardConstraint names a target that is a proper part of the governing whole, but no declared logic:GovernanceRegime activates the constrained state (no logic:constraintRegime, or the regime's logic:activationBasis does not carry the state), and no override is borne — so neither a binding (logic:ConstraintBinding) nor an override-defeat (logic:ConstraintOverridden) can be derived. The first-class third value, kept distinct from the other two so that an un-activated constraint is never silently read as binding — failure-to-activate is not constraint, and a regime-free constraint is unknown, not binding (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "当无法提出绑定问题时的约束判定值：logic:DownwardConstraint 指称一个身为治理整体真部分的目标，但没有任何已声明的 logic:GovernanceRegime 激活受约束状态（无 logic:constraintRegime，或该体制的 logic:activationBasis 不承载该状态），且未承载任何推翻——因此既无法导出绑定（logic:ConstraintBinding），也无法导出推翻击败（logic:ConstraintOverridden）。这是头等的第三值，与其余两者保持区分，从而使未被激活的约束绝不被悄然读作绑定——未能激活并非约束，且无体制的约束是未知，而非绑定（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，类型化与情境化的部分学与全子一节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConstraintVerdict|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The closed class of downward-constraint outcomes: the tri-valued result a logic:DownwardConstraint receives via logic:constraintVerdict. Its three named individuals are logic:ConstraintBinding (the whole's constraint holds upon the part under the declared regime), logic:ConstraintOverridden (a declared exception defeats it), and logic:ConstraintUnknown (no regime activates the constrained state). The set is closed, so a misspelt verdict names no declared value and is rejected rather than silently accepted, mirroring logic:EmergenceVerdict and logic:MereologyConstraint (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "下向约束结果的封闭类：logic:DownwardConstraint 经由 logic:constraintVerdict 获得的三值结果。其三个具名个体为 logic:ConstraintBinding（在已声明体制下整体的约束对部分成立）、logic:ConstraintOverridden（一个已声明的例外将其击败）和 logic:ConstraintUnknown（无体制激活受约束状态）。该集合是封闭的，故拼写错误的判定不指称任何已声明的值，会被拒绝而非被悄然接受，与 logic:EmergenceVerdict 和 logic:MereologyConstraint 相仿（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，类型化与情境化的部分学与全子一节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/constraintVerdict|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The engine-derived outcome of a logic:DownwardConstraint: the tri-valued logic:ConstraintVerdict (logic:ConstraintBinding, logic:ConstraintOverridden, or logic:ConstraintUnknown) the reasoner computes for the constraint from its role properties, the holarchy, and the declared logic:GovernanceRegime. Never asserted by hand — it is what the stratified downward-constraint rules conclude — mirroring logic:assessmentVerdict for emergence (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "logic:DownwardConstraint 的引擎导出结果：推理器根据该约束的角色属性、全子层级以及已声明的 logic:GovernanceRegime 为其计算出的三值 logic:ConstraintVerdict（logic:ConstraintBinding、logic:ConstraintOverridden 或 logic:ConstraintUnknown）。绝不手工断言——它是分层的下向约束规则所得出的结论——与用于涌现的 logic:assessmentVerdict 相仿（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，类型化与情境化的部分学与全子一节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/constraintWhole|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The governing-whole role of a logic:DownwardConstraint: the enclosing holon that imposes the constraint — the whole over the proper part named by logic:constraintTarget. The whole bounds the part's permissible state but does not produce it (constraint, not causation). One of the role properties (with logic:constraintTarget, logic:constraintState, logic:constraintRegime, and logic:constraintOverride) that reify the downward-constraint relation, mirroring logic:assessmentWhole and the logic:HolonicPosition role properties (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "logic:DownwardConstraint 的治理整体角色：施加该约束的外围全子——即凌驾于 logic:constraintTarget 所指称真部分之上的整体。整体界定部分的可允许状态，但并不产生它（约束，而非因果）。它是将下向约束关系具体化的角色属性之一（连同 logic:constraintTarget、logic:constraintState、logic:constraintRegime 和 logic:constraintOverride），与 logic:assessmentWhole 及 logic:HolonicPosition 角色属性相仿（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，类型化与情境化的部分学与全子一节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/consumedBudget|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The resource budget a logic:ReasoningResult consumed, against the contract's declared allowance. Single-valued. Domain logic:ReasoningResult (stated in prose)."
msgstr "某 logic:ReasoningResult 相对于合约所声明的配额而消耗的资源预算。单值。定义域 logic:ReasoningResult（以散文陈述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ContextAxis|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The facet value class of one index axis of the multi-dimensional context facet. Context is multi-dimensional: a single result may be indexed simultaneously by world, standpoint, time, and path. Each logic:ContextAxis individual names one such axis; they coexist on one result rather than being alternative values of one slot."
msgstr "多维情境面向的某个索引轴的面向值类。情境是多维的：单个结果可同时按世界、立场、时间和路径被索引。每个 logic:ContextAxis 个体命名一个这样的轴；它们共存于同一个结果之上，而非同一个槽位的可替代取值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/contextAxis|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to a logic:ContextAxis its results are indexed by. The context facet is multi-dimensional, so a contract may carry several logic:contextAxis values (world, standpoint, time, path) that coexist on one result rather than being alternative values of one slot. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:ContextAxis (stated in prose, matching the module's convention)."
msgstr "将 logic:ReasoningContract 关联到其结果所依据索引的 logic:ContextAxis。情境面向是多维的，因此一个合约可承载多个 logic:contextAxis 值（世界、立场、时间、路径），它们共存于同一个结果之上，而非同一个槽位的可替代取值。定义域 logic:ReasoningContract，值域 logic:ContextAxis（以散文陈述，符合该模块的约定）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/contractHash|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The content-addressed identity of the reasoning contract a logic:ReasoningResult was produced under. Single-valued. Domain logic:ReasoningResult (stated in prose)."
msgstr "产生某 logic:ReasoningResult 时所依据的推理合约的内容寻址身份。单值。定义域 logic:ReasoningResult（以散文陈述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/contradictionPolicy|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a coherence outcome to the logic:AdmissibleValuationPolicy that decides, for the governing contract, whether a within-world glut is a forbidden violation (logic:ForbidGlut, logic:ForbidGapAndGlut) or a permitted disclosed conflict (logic:AdmitAllFour, logic:ForbidGap). The pivot that classifies each contradiction witness. Single-valued. Domain logic:CoherenceCertificate or logic:CoherenceCheckAttestation, range logic:AdmissibleValuationPolicy (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将一个融贯性结果关联到 logic:AdmissibleValuationPolicy，后者为治理合约裁定：世界内的溢余究竟是被禁止的违反（logic:ForbidGlut、logic:ForbidGapAndGlut），还是被允许的、已披露的冲突（logic:AdmitAllFour、logic:ForbidGap）。它是对每个矛盾见证进行分类的枢轴。单值。定义域 logic:CoherenceCertificate 或 logic:CoherenceCheckAttestation，值域 logic:AdmissibleValuationPolicy（以散文陈述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ContradictionWitness|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The RDF shape of the runtime refutation witness a conjecture test emits when it refutes the formula: the concrete counterexample that forced an individual to owl:Nothing. It names the offending individual (logic:witnessIndividual), the world IRI the contradiction was found in (logic:witnessWorld), and the set of premises that jointly entailed the contradiction (logic:witnessPremise, one serialized triple each, multi-valued). It is an ABox artifact — a produced fact about a specific reasoning run, not a constraint — and is present exactly when its conjecture is logic:ConjectureRefutedInStandpoint (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the conjecture-and-refutation section)."
msgstr "猜想检验反驳公式时所发出的运行期反驳见证的 RDF 形状：迫使某个体归入 owl:Nothing 的具体反例。它指明违规个体（logic:witnessIndividual）、发现该矛盾所在的世界 IRI（logic:witnessWorld），以及共同蕴含该矛盾的前提集合（logic:witnessPremise，每个为一条序列化的三元组，多值）。它是一个 ABox 制品——关于某次具体推理运行的产生事实，而非约束——并恰好在其猜想为 logic:ConjectureRefutedInStandpoint 时存在（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，猜想与反驳一节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/contradictionWitness|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningResult to a within-world contradiction witness justifying a logic:InfoBoth verdict — MULTI-valued. The witness is local to its world; the base store is never globalized to owl:Nothing. Domain logic:ReasoningResult (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将 logic:ReasoningResult 关联到一个证成 logic:InfoBoth 判定的世界内矛盾见证——多值。该见证局部于其世界；基础存储绝不被全局化为 owl:Nothing。定义域 logic:ReasoningResult（以散文陈述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/contradictoryGoal|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates two gmeow:Goals in contradictory conflict: satisfying one entails violating the other in EVERY world. Domain gmeow:Goal, range gmeow:Goal (stated in prose). One of seven conflict relations between independently-meaningful goals, each WEAKER than gmeow:counterGoal — the strongest, constitutive opposition that partly defines what a goal means. A witnessed conflict is surfaced as a context-indexed finding, never silently resolved."
msgstr "将两个处于矛盾冲突中的 gmeow:Goal 关联起来：满足其一在「每个」世界中都蕴含违反另一。定义域 gmeow:Goal，值域 gmeow:Goal（以散文陈述）。它是独立有意义的目标之间七种冲突关系之一，每一种都比 gmeow:counterGoal 更「弱」——后者是最强的、构成性的对立，部分地定义了一个目标的含义。被见证的冲突会作为按情境索引的发现被显现出来，绝不被悄然消解。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/contraryGoal|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates two gmeow:Goals in contrary conflict: the two cannot both be satisfied, though both may fail. Domain gmeow:Goal, range gmeow:Goal (stated in prose). One of seven conflict relations between independently-meaningful goals, weaker than gmeow:counterGoal (constitutive opposition) and than logic:contradictoryGoal (which also forces one to be violated when the other is satisfied)."
msgstr "将两个处于反对冲突中的 gmeow:Goal 关联起来：二者不能同时被满足，但可以同时落空。定义域 gmeow:Goal，值域 gmeow:Goal（以散文陈述）。它是独立有意义的目标之间七种冲突关系之一，弱于 gmeow:counterGoal（构成性对立）以及 logic:contradictoryGoal（后者还会在一者被满足时迫使另一者被违反）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/contributesTo|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a sub-gmeow:Goal whose satisfaction advances a gmeow:Goal without settling it. Domain gmeow:Goal, range gmeow:Goal (stated in prose). One of the four decomposition relations carrying satisfaction dependency; weaker than logic:necessaryFor (required) and logic:sufficientFor (settles on its own), and distinct from gmeow:properPartOf, which carries only structural part-hood."
msgstr "关联一个子 gmeow:Goal，其满足推进某个 gmeow:Goal 却不使之达成。定义域 gmeow:Goal，值域 gmeow:Goal（以散文陈述）。它是承载满足依赖的四种分解关系之一；弱于 logic:necessaryFor（必需）和 logic:sufficientFor（凭其自身即达成），且不同于 gmeow:properPartOf，后者仅承载结构性的部分从属关系。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ControlFlowEdge|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A reified control-flow edge between two process nodes — the canonical FLOW-GRAPH form of control flow, mediating a source node (logic:flowFrom) and a target node (logic:flowTo). Complementary to, NOT a duplicate of, the structured-program combinators (logic:Choice, logic:Iteration, logic:ConcurrentComposition, logic:Fallback): the combinators are the program-TREE form an interpreter walks, while a logic:ControlFlowEdge is the binary-edge form the DAG-workflow acyclicity certifier runs Tarjan SCC over. A graph carrying a logic:Iteration loop edge (or any back-edge) is outside the DAG fragment. Downstream reified control-flow relators such as gmeow:ControlFlow specialize this class. A Relator mediating two distinct relata (its flowFrom and flowTo nodes), satisfying the relator-mediation discipline."
msgstr "两个过程节点之间的一条具体化控制流边——控制流的规范「流图」形式，中介一个源节点（logic:flowFrom）与一个目标节点（logic:flowTo）。它与结构化程序组合子（logic:Choice、logic:Iteration、logic:ConcurrentComposition、logic:Fallback）互补，而「非」其重复：组合子是解释器所遍历的「程序树」形式，而 logic:ControlFlowEdge 是 DAG 工作流无环性认证器在其上运行 Tarjan SCC 的二元边形式。承载 logic:Iteration 循环边（或任何回边）的图处于 DAG 片段之外。下游具体化的控制流关系子（如 gmeow:ControlFlow）特化此类。一个中介两个不同关系项（其 flowFrom 与 flowTo 节点）的关系子，满足关系子中介规范。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/correlates|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:DependencyModel to a logic:probability-annotated fact (the reified base triple) that participates in the model's explicit joint distribution. The set of correlated facts is the support over which logic:jointOutcome enumerates joint assignments; any logic:probability fact NOT correlated by the model is treated as independent. The range is intentionally left open (no rdfs:range): a correlated fact is a reified logic:probability statement, which carries no dedicated class in this standalone module."
msgstr "将 logic:DependencyModel 关联到一个由 logic:probability 注解的事实（具体化的基础三元组），该事实参与模型的显式联合分布。相关事实的集合是 logic:jointOutcome 据以枚举联合赋值的支撑集；任何未被模型相关联的 logic:probability 事实都被视为独立。值域被有意保持开放（无 rdfs:range）：一个相关事实是一条具体化的 logic:probability 陈述，在此独立模块中它不承载任何专用类。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CorrespondenceLaw|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The closed value class of the lens laws a logic:Correspondence can claim through a logic:LawClaim: logic:GetPut, logic:PutGet, logic:PutPut and logic:SectionLaw. Which laws are claimable is capped by the correspondence's logic:MorphismClass rung, and each claim carries a logic:DischargeVerdict. The set is closed, so a misspelt law names no declared value and is rejected (design/LOGIC-CORRESPONDENCE.md, the ninth-node-kind section)."
msgstr "一个 logic:Correspondence 可经由 logic:LawClaim 主张的透镜律的封闭值类：logic:GetPut、logic:PutGet、logic:PutPut 和 logic:SectionLaw。哪些律可被主张由该对应的 logic:MorphismClass 档级封顶，且每项主张承载一个 logic:DischargeVerdict。该集合是封闭的，故拼写错误的律不指称任何已声明的值，会被拒绝（design/LOGIC-CORRESPONDENCE.md，第九种节点一节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CorrespondenceRelation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The typed, closed value class of a logic:Correspondence's relation, on an ordered lattice rather than a free string: logic:Equiv ⊐ { logic:Subsumes, logic:SubsumedBy } ⊐ logic:Overlaps ⊐ logic:RelatedMatch, with logic:Disjoint the negative pole. From one authored relation the compiler derives the SSSOM predicate, the EDOAL relation symbol and the OWL-alignment-axiom strength, so the generated alignment artifacts cannot drift apart. The set is closed, so a misspelt relation names no declared value and is rejected (design/LOGIC-CORRESPONDENCE.md, the relation-lattice section)."
msgstr "logic:Correspondence 之关系的类型化、封闭值类，位于一个有序格之上而非自由字符串：logic:Equiv ⊐ { logic:Subsumes, logic:SubsumedBy } ⊐ logic:Overlaps ⊐ logic:RelatedMatch，以 logic:Disjoint 为负极。编译器从单一撰写出的关系导出 SSSOM 谓词、EDOAL 关系符号和 OWL 对齐公理的强度，从而使生成的对齐制品无法彼此漂移。该集合是封闭的，故拼写错误的关系不指称任何已声明的值，会被拒绝（design/LOGIC-CORRESPONDENCE.md，关系格一节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/correspondenceRelation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Correspondence to its logic:CorrespondenceRelation on the ordered lattice (equiv ⊐ subsumes / subsumedBy ⊐ overlaps ⊐ relatedMatch, disjoint the negative pole). The single authored relation from which the SSSOM predicate, EDOAL symbol and OWL-alignment strength are derived. Range logic:CorrespondenceRelation (domain stated in prose)."
msgstr "将 logic:Correspondence 关联到其位于有序格上的 logic:CorrespondenceRelation（equiv ⊐ subsumes / subsumedBy ⊐ overlaps ⊐ relatedMatch，disjoint 为负极）。这是唯一撰写出的关系，SSSOM 谓词、EDOAL 符号和 OWL 对齐强度皆由它导出。值域 logic:CorrespondenceRelation（定义域以散文陈述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Correspondence|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A law-bearing, possibly-lossy, possibly-bidirectional alignment between a source pattern and a target pattern: the ninth node kind. It carries its morphism class on an ordered law-spine, its claimed laws with discharge status, the separated quantitative axes, FOL/SOL caveats, and standpoint indexing; its get and put legs are transaction programs while its caveat-and-relation envelope is meta-level and stays meta. It is the single kind cross-ontology alignment compiles into, and from which the SSSOM, EDOAL, FnO, SPARQL, and up-lift surfaces are generated lowerings. Fully specified in design/LOGIC-CORRESPONDENCE.md."
msgstr "源模式与目标模式之间的一种承载律的、可能有损的、可能双向的对齐：第九种节点。它在一个有序的律主干上承载其态射类、其带有履行状态的所主张之律、分离的定量轴、FOL/SOL 附注以及按立场的索引；其 get 与 put 分支是事务程序，而其附注与关系的外壳处于元层级并保持在元层。它是跨本体对齐所编译成的唯一种类，SSSOM、EDOAL、FnO、SPARQL 及上提各表面皆由它生成为下降投影。完整规范见 design/LOGIC-CORRESPONDENCE.md。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/corrSzsToVerdict|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The first-class correspondence recording the SZS-status → logic:ConformanceVerdict collapse as a monotone (Galois) lossy projection. It carries logic:preservationKind logic:SoundUnderApproximation because the three-bucket view drops the logic:SzsContradictoryAxioms/logic:SzsUnsatisfiable and logic:SzsCounterSatisfiable/logic:SzsSatisfiable distinctions (a logic:LossyLens, logic:mnemomorphic false — the coarse verdict cannot recover the source token, which is why logic:rawStatusToken preserves it). Modelling the collapse as a logic:Correspondence rather than a bespoke check means its preservation rung is verified by two concrete mechanisms: the per-correspondence loss-ledger row (the Principle-17 residue that names the dropped logic:SzsContradictoryAxioms/logic:SzsUnsatisfiable and logic:SzsCounterSatisfiable/logic:SzsSatisfiable distinctions as structured actual-drop notes), and the preservation-consistency gate, which reds the build if a non-injective rung such as this logic:LossyLens ever declares logic:ExactPreservation instead of the honest logic:SoundUnderApproximation (design/LOGIC-CORRESPONDENCE.md, the loss ledger and correspondence gates)."
msgstr "记录 SZS 状态 → logic:ConformanceVerdict 坍缩为一个单调（Galois）有损投影的头等对应。它承载 logic:preservationKind logic:SoundUnderApproximation，因为三桶视图丢弃了 logic:SzsContradictoryAxioms/logic:SzsUnsatisfiable 与 logic:SzsCounterSatisfiable/logic:SzsSatisfiable 之间的区分（一个 logic:LossyLens，logic:mnemomorphic 为假——粗略的判定无法恢复源记号，这正是 logic:rawStatusToken 保留它的原因）。将该坍缩建模为一个 logic:Correspondence 而非定制检查，意味着其保持档级由两个具体机制核验：逐对应的损耗账本行（原则 17 的残余，它将被丢弃的 logic:SzsContradictoryAxioms/logic:SzsUnsatisfiable 与 logic:SzsCounterSatisfiable/logic:SzsSatisfiable 区分命名为结构化的实际丢弃注记），以及保持一致性关卡，一旦像此 logic:LossyLens 这样的非单射档级声明 logic:ExactPreservation 而非诚实的 logic:SoundUnderApproximation，该关卡就使构建变红（design/LOGIC-CORRESPONDENCE.md，损耗账本与对应关卡）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CounterfactualAcceptanceWitness|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The acceptance record that a Stratum-C counterfactual world was constructed and resolved to a deterministic outcome, executed natively by gmeow_logic::counterfactual::construct_and_resolve over the entrenchment ordering. It names, through logic:selectedByEntrenchment, the outcome the entrenchment ranking selected. The flagship producer runs the native resolution and pins the deterministic selected binding; this witness is the ontological twin the thin logic:CounterfactualAcceptanceWitnessShape gates."
msgstr "证明某个 Stratum-C 反事实世界已被构造并解析为确定性结果的接受记录，由 gmeow_logic::counterfactual::construct_and_resolve 在固守序上原生执行。它经由 logic:selectedByEntrenchment 指明固守排名所选定的结果。旗舰生产者运行原生解析并钉住确定性选定绑定；此见证是纤薄的 logic:CounterfactualAcceptanceWitnessShape 所把关的本体论孪生。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/counterfactuallyCloser|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The typed counterfactual accessibility relation under a declared closeness ordering (Lewis comparative similarity, a generalized closeness poset over contexts). Counterfactual reasoning is a USE of typed contexts: a counterfactual claim is truth in the counterfactually-closer accessible contexts under the ordering. Closeness is declared data, not a fixed semantics. logic:accessibleFrom is its generic superproperty in prose only — NOT asserted rdfs:subPropertyOf — so what would have been never leaks into what is by walking the bare superproperty."
msgstr "在已声明的接近度序（Lewis 比较相似性，情境上的广义接近度偏序集）之下的类型化反事实可达关系。反事实推理是对类型化情境的一种「使用」：一个反事实主张就是在该序下反事实地更接近的可达情境中的真。接近度是已声明的数据，而非固定的语义。logic:accessibleFrom 仅在散文层面是其通用超属性——「未」断言为 rdfs:subPropertyOf——从而使「本会如此」绝不会因遍历那条裸超属性而泄漏进「实然」。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/counterfactualOf|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a constructed counterfactual world to the base world it minimally revises: the surface for Lewis/Stalnaker counterfactuals, where the antecedent-world is computed by a revision rule rather than asserted and its contents must not leak into the base graph. Closeness is declared data (a generalized sharpening poset), not a fixed semantics; under the default Deterministic Revision Profile a declared entrenchment ordering yields a single revised world, and a genuine tie returns unknown rather than branching."
msgstr "将一个构造出的反事实世界关联到它所最小修订的基础世界：Lewis/Stalnaker 反事实的表面，其中前件世界由修订规则计算得出而非被断言，且其内容不得泄漏进基础图。接近度是已声明的数据（一个广义的锐化偏序集），而非固定的语义；在默认的确定性修订剖面之下，一个已声明的固守序产生单一的修订世界，而一次真正的平局返回未知，而非产生分支。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/counterGoalIrreflexivity|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Asserts on the canonical carrier that gmeow:counterGoal is irreflexive: a goal is never its own shadow, as its skos:definition states. The native coherence gate reads this to raise a violation for a goal asserted to counter itself."
msgstr "在规范载体上断言 gmeow:counterGoal 是非自反的：一个目标绝不是其自身的影子，正如其 skos:definition 所述。原生融贯性关卡读取此断言，为被断言与自身相对的目标引发一项违反。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/counterGoalSymmetry|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Asserts on the canonical carrier that gmeow:counterGoal is symmetric: each pole of a constitutive opposition constitutes the other, as its skos:definition states. The native coherence gate reads this to mirror the opposition."
msgstr "在规范载体上断言 gmeow:counterGoal 是对称的：一种构成性对立的每一极都构成另一极，正如其 skos:definition 所述。原生融贯性关卡读取此断言以镜像该对立。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CounterpartNonTransitivityObligation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The standing non-entailment obligation that cross-realm counterpart identity (gmeow:counterpartOf) stays non-transitive: it is symmetric but deliberately not transitive, so the foundation must never derive it (any derivation, transitive or otherwise, is forbidden — it is assertion-only). Discharged by syntactic reachability over the counterpart rule heads (no rule head produces the predicate). Guards the coreference slice (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, §Typed formalization governance)."
msgstr "关于跨界域对应方身份（gmeow:counterpartOf）保持非传递的常设非蕴含义务：它是对称的但故意不传递，因此基础层绝不可导出它（任何导出，无论传递与否，皆被禁止——它只允许断言）。经由对应方规则头上的句法可达性来履行（无任何规则头产生该谓词）。它守护共指切片（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，§类型化形式化治理）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/counterpartOfSymmetry|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Asserts on the canonical carrier that gmeow:counterpartOf is symmetric: cross-realm counterparts recognise each other both ways, as its skos:definition states. It is deliberately NOT transitive — that non-characteristic is enforced by logic:CounterpartNonTransitivityObligation, so no transitive carrier is authored. The native coherence gate reads this to mirror the counterpart link only."
msgstr "在规范载体上断言 gmeow:counterpartOf 是对称的：跨域的对应物在两个方向上相互识别，正如其 skos:definition 所述。它被刻意设为非传递的——该非特性由 logic:CounterpartNonTransitivityObligation 强制执行，因此不撰写任何传递载体。原生一致性关卡读取此项，仅镜像对应物链接。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqBullshitIndifferenceHolds|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the bullshit-modality equivalence must satisfy: a gmeow:StandpointClaim whose gmeow:claimModality is gmeow:bullshit is exactly one whose gmeow:claimTruthDirectedness is gmeow:truthIndifferent (Frankfurt) — held without regard for correspondence, distinct from a lie's truth-aimed denial. The well-formed case the biconditional admits."
msgstr "bullshit-模态等价必须满足的正向胜任案例：一个 gmeow:StandpointClaim，其 gmeow:claimModality 为 gmeow:bullshit，恰好就是其 gmeow:claimTruthDirectedness 为 gmeow:truthIndifferent（弗兰克福）的那一个——不顾及对应而持有，区别于谎言那种以真为的的否认。双条件所容许的良构案例。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqBullshitIndifferenceLieRejected|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The negative countermodel the bullshit-modality equivalence must respect: conflating gmeow:bullshit with a truth-aimed lie (gmeow:truthAimed) is rejected — bullshit is indifferent to truth, a lie asserts against a believed truth. HONEST SCOPE: the equivalence is realized in the OWL / full-FOL projection; the native monotone chase does not enforce a biconditional, disclosed in the loss ledger."
msgstr "bullshit-模态等价必须尊重的负向反模型：将 gmeow:bullshit 与以真为的的谎言（gmeow:truthAimed）混为一谈将被拒绝——bullshit 对真理漠不关心，而谎言则针对所信的真理作出断言。诚实范围：该等价在 OWL / 全-FOL 投影中实现；原生单调追逐不强制双条件，此点在损失账本中披露。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqCrossNodeGlutHolds|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the cross-node-glut rule must satisfy — 'all cross-node gluts at one anchor': given two distinct findings at one gmeow:NonTrivialAnchor whose categories carry opposing gmeow:categoryPolarity (one logic:InfoSupported, one logic:InfoOpposed), the reasoner must derive gmeow:crossNodeGlutWith linking them — the Supported/Opposed clash across codes the same-fingerprint merge structurally misses."
msgstr "跨节点-glut 规则必须满足的正向胜任案例——'单一锚点处的所有跨节点 glut'：给定位于同一 gmeow:NonTrivialAnchor 的两条不同发现，其类别带有相反的 gmeow:categoryPolarity（一为 logic:InfoSupported，一为 logic:InfoOpposed），推理机必须导出 gmeow:crossNodeGlutWith 将它们相连——即跨代码的 Supported/Opposed 冲突，同指纹合并在结构上会遗漏之。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqCrossNodeGlutSamePolarityRejected|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The second negative countermodel the cross-node-glut rule must respect: two findings at one gmeow:NonTrivialAnchor whose categories carry the SAME gmeow:categoryPolarity (both logic:InfoSupported, say) derive NO gmeow:crossNodeGlutWith — a glut is an OPPOSING Belnap clash (Supported vs Opposed), never an agreement; and findings at DIFFERENT anchors never join at all. The boundary that keeps the edge to genuine coherence conflicts."
msgstr "跨节点-glut 规则必须尊重的第二个负向反模型：位于同一 gmeow:NonTrivialAnchor 的两条发现，其类别带有相同的 gmeow:categoryPolarity（比如都为 logic:InfoSupported），不导出任何 gmeow:crossNodeGlutWith——glut 是一种相反的 Belnap 冲突（Supported 对 Opposed），绝非一致；而位于不同锚点的发现根本不会相连。将此边保留给真正一致性冲突的边界。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqCrossNodeGlutTrivialAnchorRejected|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The first negative countermodel the cross-node-glut rule must respect: two opposing-polarity findings that share an anchor which is NOT a gmeow:NonTrivialAnchor (the default empty anchor locationless findings collapse onto) derive NO gmeow:crossNodeGlutWith — the gmeow:NonTrivialAnchor guard keeps the join off the shared placeholder, so the rule fires only at anchors that name a real source position. The boundary that prevents the false-join over locationless findings."
msgstr "跨节点-glut 规则必须尊重的第一个负向反模型：两条极性相反的发现共享一个并非 gmeow:NonTrivialAnchor 的锚点（无位置发现坍缩到的那个默认空锚点），不导出任何 gmeow:crossNodeGlutWith——gmeow:NonTrivialAnchor 守卫使连接远离共享的占位符，故规则仅在命名真实来源位置的锚点处触发。防止对无位置发现进行虚假连接的边界。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqDeceptionDivergenceGapRejected|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The negative countermodel the deception-divergence axiom must respect: a gmeow:Event typed gmeow:eventTypeDeception whose held and projected standpoints coincide (no divergent claim-state) violates the necessary condition in the OWL / full-FOL projection. HONEST SCOPE: the native monotone StratifiedNAF chase does NOT enforce this existential, negation-bearing condition, so the rejection is realized only in the projection and is disclosed in the loss ledger."
msgstr "欺骗-分歧公理必须尊重的负向反模型：一个被类型化为 gmeow:eventTypeDeception 的 gmeow:Event，若其所持与所投射的立场重合（无分歧的主张状态），则在 OWL / 全-FOL 投影中违反该必要条件。诚实范围：原生单调 StratifiedNAF 追逐不强制这一存在性的、带否定的条件，故该拒绝仅在投影中实现，并在损失账本中披露。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqDeceptionDivergenceHolds|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the deception-divergence necessary-condition must satisfy: a gmeow:Event of gmeow:eventTypeDeception that carries a gmeow:heldStandpoint and a gmeow:projectedStandpoint — both gmeow:DoxasticStandpointClaims — whose claim modalities differ satisfies the axiom. The held/projected gap is the deceptive act; the well-formed case the formula admits."
msgstr "欺骗-分歧必要条件必须满足的正向胜任案例：一个 gmeow:eventTypeDeception 的 gmeow:Event，携带一个 gmeow:heldStandpoint 与一个 gmeow:projectedStandpoint——二者皆为 gmeow:DoxasticStandpointClaims——其主张模态相异，即满足该公理。所持/所投射之间的落差就是欺骗行为；公式所容许的良构案例。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqEndurantPerdurantClashRejected|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The negative countermodel the endurant/perdurant disjointness axiom must respect: an individual typed BOTH logic:Endurant and logic:Perdurant is a violation — the native DL coherence gate forces it to owl:Nothing, because logic:Endurant owl:disjointWith logic:Perdurant is asserted. A thing that is at once wholly present at every moment and composed of temporal parts is not an admissible model. The boundary the continuant/occurrent divide enforces."
msgstr "endurant/perdurant 不相交公理必须尊重的负向反模型：同时被类型化为 logic:Endurant 与 logic:Perdurant 的个体是一个违规——原生 DL 一致性关卡将其逼为 owl:Nothing，因为已断言 logic:Endurant owl:disjointWith logic:Perdurant。一个既在每一时刻完整在场、又由时间部分构成的事物不是可容许的模型。持续者/发生者之分所强制的边界。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqEndurantPerdurantDisjointHolds|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the endurant/perdurant disjointness axiom must satisfy: an individual typed logic:Endurant and NOT logic:Perdurant (a continuant wholly present at each moment) stays coherent — it is not forced to owl:Nothing — because a thing either endures through change or unfolds through it, not both."
msgstr "endurant/perdurant 不相交公理必须满足的正向胜任案例：被类型化为 logic:Endurant 而非 logic:Perdurant 的个体（一个在每一时刻完整在场的持续者）保持一致——它不会被逼为 owl:Nothing——因为一个事物或是历经变化而持续，或是通过变化而展开，二者不可得兼。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqEntitySortalCoveringGapRejected|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The negative countermodel the entity-sortal covering must respect: a gmeow:Entity typed into NONE of the four sortals violates the owl:unionOf covering in the OWL-DL projection — an OWL reasoner rejects the class-covering gap. HONEST SCOPE: the native monotone StratifiedNAF gate does NOT enforce this disjunctive covering (a disjunction in the head is non-Horn), so this rejection is realized only in the OWL projection, not in the native chase, and is disclosed in the loss ledger accordingly."
msgstr "实体-sortal 覆盖必须尊重的负向反模型：未被类型化进四个 sortal 之任一的 gmeow:Entity，在 OWL-DL 投影中违反 owl:unionOf 覆盖——OWL 推理机拒绝该类覆盖缺口。诚实范围：原生单调 StratifiedNAF 关卡不强制这一析取覆盖（头部中的析取为非-Horn），故该拒绝仅在 OWL 投影中实现，而非在原生追逐中，并相应地在损失账本中披露。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqEntitySortalCoveringHolds|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the entity-sortal covering must satisfy: a gmeow:Entity that is one of the four sortals (gmeow:Agent, gmeow:InformationObject, gmeow:PhysicalObject, gmeow:SocialObject) is covered by the owl:unionOf — no gap. Realized in the OWL-DL projection; it is the well-formed case the covering disjunction admits."
msgstr "实体-sortal 覆盖必须满足的正向胜任案例：作为四个 sortal 之一（gmeow:Agent、gmeow:InformationObject、gmeow:PhysicalObject、gmeow:SocialObject）的 gmeow:Entity 被 owl:unionOf 覆盖——无缺口。在 OWL-DL 投影中实现；这是覆盖析取所容许的良构案例。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqEventSituationClashRejected|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The negative countermodel the event/situation disjointness axiom must respect: an individual typed BOTH logic:Event and logic:Situation is a violation — the native DL coherence gate forces it to owl:Nothing, because logic:Event owl:disjointWith logic:Situation is asserted. A thing that is at once an unfolding occurrence and the static configuration a situation records is not an admissible model. The boundary the occurrent/configuration distinction enforces."
msgstr "event/situation 不相交公理必须尊重的负向反模型：同时被类型化为 logic:Event 与 logic:Situation 的个体是一个违规——原生 DL 一致性关卡将其逼为 owl:Nothing，因为已断言 logic:Event owl:disjointWith logic:Situation。一个既是展开中的发生、又是情境所记录的静态配置的事物不是可容许的模型。发生者/配置之别所强制的边界。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqEventSituationDisjointHolds|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the event/situation disjointness axiom must satisfy: an individual typed logic:Event and NOT logic:Situation (a perdurant occurrence composed of temporal parts) stays coherent — it is not forced to owl:Nothing — because an occurrence that unfolds in time is not the static configuration a situation records."
msgstr "event/situation 不相交公理必须满足的正向胜任案例：被类型化为 logic:Event 而非 logic:Situation 的个体（一个由时间部分构成的 perdurant 发生）保持一致——它不会被逼为 owl:Nothing——因为一个在时间中展开的发生并不是情境所记录的静态配置。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqFalsehoodRefutedGlobalTruthRejected|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The negative countermodel the falsehood-as-refuted-claim equivalence must respect: reading gmeow:refuted as a frame-independent isFalse flag on the proposition — rather than as the necessarily-denying stance of one standpoint — is rejected (Principle 11: no global truth verdict). HONEST SCOPE: the equivalence is realized in the OWL / full-FOL projection; the native monotone chase does not enforce a biconditional, so this is disclosed in the loss ledger."
msgstr "虚假-即-被驳斥主张等价必须尊重的负向反模型：将 gmeow:refuted 读作命题之上一个与框架无关的 isFalse 标志——而非某一立场的必然否定姿态——将被拒绝（原则 11：无全局真理裁决）。诚实范围：该等价在 OWL / 全-FOL 投影中实现；原生单调追逐不强制双条件，故此点在损失账本中披露。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqFalsehoodRefutedHolds|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the falsehood-as-refuted-claim equivalence must satisfy: a gmeow:StandpointClaim whose gmeow:claimModality is gmeow:refuted is exactly one whose gmeow:claimPolarity is gmeow:polarityDeny and gmeow:claimModalForce is gmeow:modalForceNecessary (□¬ — settled-false-in-frame). The well-formed case the biconditional admits; there is no separate isFalse flag."
msgstr "虚假-即-被驳斥主张等价必须满足的正向胜任案例：一个 gmeow:StandpointClaim，其 gmeow:claimModality 为 gmeow:refuted，恰好就是其 gmeow:claimPolarity 为 gmeow:polarityDeny 且 gmeow:claimModalForce 为 gmeow:modalForceNecessary（□¬——框架内已定为假）的那一个。双条件所容许的良构案例；并无单独的 isFalse 标志。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqFindingClusterDistinctRootsRejected|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The negative countermodel the cluster rules must respect: findings with DIFFERENT gmeow:findingRootCause values land in different clusters — a finding whose root is R1 is never linked by gmeow:findingCluster to the cluster keyed by a distinct R2, and each cluster node carries only its own root. The boundary that keeps unrelated root-cause groups from merging."
msgstr "簇规则必须尊重的负向反模型：带有不同 gmeow:findingRootCause 值的发现落入不同的簇——根为 R1 的发现绝不会经由 gmeow:findingCluster 连到以不同的 R2 为键的簇，且每个簇节点只携带自身的根。防止无关联的根因组相互合并的边界。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqFindingClusterHolds|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the cluster rules must satisfy — 'all findings sharing root R': given F2 and F3 that each gmeow:findingRootCause the root F1, the reasoner must derive gmeow:findingCluster(F2, F1), gmeow:findingCluster(F3, F1), gmeow:clusterRoot(F1, F1), and rdf:type(F1, gmeow:FindingCluster) — every finding sharing R gathered under the one root-keyed cluster node, which carries R exactly once."
msgstr "簇规则必须满足的正向胜任案例——'共享根 R 的所有发现'：给定 F2 与 F3 各自 gmeow:findingRootCause 根 F1，推理机必须导出 gmeow:findingCluster(F2, F1)、gmeow:findingCluster(F3, F1)、gmeow:clusterRoot(F1, F1) 以及 rdf:type(F1, gmeow:FindingCluster)——每条共享 R 的发现都汇集于以根为键的那一个簇节点之下，而该节点恰携带 R 一次。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqFindingRootCauseHolds|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the root-cause rule must satisfy — 'the root of all findings sharing root R': given F2 and F3 that each gmeow:findingAntecedent the childless F1 (F1 has no antecedent), the reasoner must derive gmeow:findingRootCause(F2, F1) AND gmeow:findingRootCause(F3, F1), and transitively gmeow:findingRootCause(F4, F1) for an F4 that traces to F1 through F2 — the shared childless root, agreeing with the witness-DAG root-cause harvest."
msgstr "根因规则必须满足的正向胜任案例——'共享根 R 的所有发现之根'：给定 F2 与 F3 各自 gmeow:findingAntecedent 无子的 F1（F1 无任何先行者），推理机必须导出 gmeow:findingRootCause(F2, F1) 与 gmeow:findingRootCause(F3, F1)，并传递地对经由 F2 追溯到 F1 的 F4 导出 gmeow:findingRootCause(F4, F1)——即共享的无子之根，与见证-DAG 根因采收相符。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqFindingRootCauseNonRootRejected|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The negative countermodel the root-cause rule must respect: a traced antecedent that ITSELF carries a gmeow:findingAntecedent is never derived a gmeow:findingRootCause — only a childless root qualifies. For F4 → F2 → F1, F4's root cause is F1, NEVER the intermediate F2 (which is a gmeow:findingHasAntecedent of itself); and an independent finding with no antecedent chain derives no root cause at all. The boundary the negation-as-failure over gmeow:findingHasAntecedent keeps."
msgstr "根因规则必须尊重的负向反模型：一个本身携带 gmeow:findingAntecedent 的被追溯先行者绝不会被导出为 gmeow:findingRootCause——只有无子之根才够格。对于 F4 → F2 → F1，F4 的根因是 F1，绝非中间的 F2（它自身是一个 gmeow:findingHasAntecedent 的持有者）；而一个无先行者链的独立发现根本不导出任何根因。基于 gmeow:findingHasAntecedent 之上的失败即否定所保持的边界。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqFindingTracesHolds|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the transitive-closure rules must satisfy — 'every antecedent this finding derives from, directly or transitively': given F4 gmeow:findingAntecedent F2 and F2 gmeow:findingAntecedent F1, the reasoner must derive BOTH gmeow:findingTraces(F4, F2) and gmeow:findingTraces(F4, F1), closing the witness DAG up past the intermediate."
msgstr "传递-闭包规则必须满足的正向胜任案例——'此发现直接或传递地据以派生的每个先行者'：给定 F4 gmeow:findingAntecedent F2 且 F2 gmeow:findingAntecedent F1，推理机必须同时导出 gmeow:findingTraces(F4, F2) 与 gmeow:findingTraces(F4, F1)，将见证 DAG 向上闭合越过中间者。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqFindingTracesNonReachRejected|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The negative countermodel the transitive-closure rules must respect: gmeow:findingTraces is exactly the reachability closure of gmeow:findingAntecedent — a finding with no antecedent chain to another finding never traces to it, and the closure is directed (a root antecedent does not trace DOWN to its downstream witnesses). Two findings in disjoint witness DAGs share no gmeow:findingTraces edge."
msgstr "传递-闭包规则必须尊重的负向反模型：gmeow:findingTraces 恰是 gmeow:findingAntecedent 的可达性闭包——一个没有先行者链通向另一发现的发现绝不会追溯到它，且该闭包是有向的（一个根先行者不会向下追溯到其下游见证）。位于不相交见证 DAG 中的两条发现不共享任何 gmeow:findingTraces 边。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqFrameRelativityFramelessRejected|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The negative countermodel the frame-relativity constraint must respect: a logic:measuredValue asserted with no logic:referenceFrame is the logic:MeasurementFrameMissing violation — a frame-free value collapse the foundation catches as a finding, never admits as a well-formed model. The boundary Principle 11 enforces: a value asserted without its frame is ill-formed, and two frame-relative values are never equated frame-free."
msgstr "框架-相对性约束必须尊重的负向反模型：一个断言时没有 logic:referenceFrame 的 logic:measuredValue 即是 logic:MeasurementFrameMissing 违规——无框架的值坍缩会被基础作为一条发现所捕获，绝不作为良构模型而容许。原则 11 所强制的边界：一个断言时缺其框架的值是病构的，且两个框架-相对的值绝不会在无框架下被等同。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqFrameRelativityHolds|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the frame-relativity constraint must satisfy: a logic:measuredValue expressed together with its logic:referenceFrame is well-formed — it carries no logic:MeasurementFrameMissing violation — because the value is meaningful only paired with the frame it is expressed in (Principle 11)."
msgstr "框架-相对性约束必须满足的正向胜任案例：一个连同其 logic:referenceFrame 一并表达的 logic:measuredValue 是良构的——它不携带任何 logic:MeasurementFrameMissing 违规——因为该值唯有与其所表达于的框架配对时才有意义（原则 11）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqFunctionalComplexKindDisjointHolds|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the individuation-kind disjointness axioms must satisfy: an individual typed logic:FunctionalComplex and NOT also logic:Collection or logic:Quantity stays coherent — it is not forced to owl:Nothing — because a whole is individuated in exactly one of the three modes the prose contrasts."
msgstr "个体化-种类不相交公理必须满足的正向胜任案例：被类型化为 logic:FunctionalComplex 且并非同时为 logic:Collection 或 logic:Quantity 的个体保持一致——它不会被逼为 owl:Nothing——因为一个整体恰按散文所对比的三种模式之一被个体化。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqFunctionalComplexKindDisjointOverlapRejected|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The negative countermodel the individuation-kind disjointness axioms must respect: an individual typed BOTH logic:FunctionalComplex and logic:Collection is a violation — the native DL coherence gate forces it to owl:Nothing — so a whole individuated at once by distinct functional roles and by member count is not an admissible model. The boundary the harvested constraint enforces."
msgstr "个体化-种类不相交公理必须尊重的负向反模型：同时被类型化为 logic:FunctionalComplex 与 logic:Collection 的个体是一个违规——原生 DL 一致性关卡将其逼为 owl:Nothing——因此一个既由不同功能角色、又由成员计数而同时被个体化的整体不是可容许的模型。所采收之约束所强制的边界。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqGateFatalAdvisoryNeverFatalRejected|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The first never-gate countermodel the gate rule must respect: a finding whose gmeow:findingStandpoint is gmeow:standpointAdvisory is NEVER derived gmeow:findingGateVerdict gmeow:gateFatal, no matter how loud its severity or how blocking its category — the standpoint axis is below the Binding top, so the meet cannot reach Fatal. The boundary that keeps advice from ever failing the gate, mirroring Rust gate() returning Collected for every advisory grade."
msgstr "关卡规则必须尊重的第一个永不-致命反模型：一条发现，其 gmeow:findingStandpoint 为 gmeow:standpointAdvisory，绝不会被导出 gmeow:findingGateVerdict gmeow:gateFatal，无论其严重度多么响亮或其类别多么阻断——立场轴处于 Binding 顶之下，故其交（meet）无法抵达 Fatal。使建议永不在关卡处失败的边界，映照 Rust 的 gate() 对每一个咨询等级返回 Collected。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqGateFatalPermittedConflictNeverFatalRejected|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The second never-gate countermodel the gate rule must respect: a finding whose gmeow:findingCategory is logic:FindingPermittedEpistemicConflict — whose gmeow:categoryBlocking projection is gmeow:blockingCoherent — is NEVER derived gmeow:findingGateVerdict gmeow:gateFatal, even at gmeow:severityError and gmeow:standpointBinding, because its Blocking axis is below the Blocking top. The load-bearing boundary that a disclosed, coherent contradiction a glut-admitting contract permits does not fail the gate, mirroring Rust gate() returning Collected for every Coherent-category grade."
msgstr "关卡规则必须尊重的第二个永不-致命反模型：一条发现，其 gmeow:findingCategory 为 logic:FindingPermittedEpistemicConflict——其 gmeow:categoryBlocking 投影为 gmeow:blockingCoherent——绝不会被导出 gmeow:findingGateVerdict gmeow:gateFatal，即便在 gmeow:severityError 与 gmeow:standpointBinding 之下，因为其 Blocking 轴处于 Blocking 顶之下。承重边界如下：一个允许-glut 的契约所许可的、已披露且一致的矛盾并不会在关卡处失败，映照 Rust 的 gate() 对每一个 Coherent-类别等级返回 Collected。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqGateFatalVerdictHolds|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the gate rule must satisfy: given a finding with gmeow:findingSeverity gmeow:severityError, a gmeow:findingCategory whose gmeow:categoryBlocking is gmeow:blockingBlocking (a failure kind), and gmeow:findingStandpoint gmeow:standpointBinding, the reasoner must derive gmeow:findingGateVerdict gmeow:gateFatal — the principal up-set ↑(Error, Blocking, Binding) the harvested prose commits to, agreeing with Rust gate() returning Fatal."
msgstr "关卡规则必须满足的正向胜任案例：给定一条发现，带有 gmeow:findingSeverity gmeow:severityError、一个其 gmeow:categoryBlocking 为 gmeow:blockingBlocking（一种失败种类）的 gmeow:findingCategory，以及 gmeow:findingStandpoint gmeow:standpointBinding，推理机必须导出 gmeow:findingGateVerdict gmeow:gateFatal——即所采收散文所承诺的主上集 ↑(Error, Blocking, Binding)，与 Rust 的 gate() 返回 Fatal 相符。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqIndirectContributorDirectAttributionRejected|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The negative countermodel the indirect-contribution rule must respect: the derived gmeow:indirectContributor edge must never appear as gmeow:wasAttributedTo — deriving direct, asserted responsibility from the generation chain is a violation, the boundary the non-entailment obligation holds the formalization to."
msgstr "间接-贡献规则必须尊重的负向反模型：派生出的 gmeow:indirectContributor 边绝不可作为 gmeow:wasAttributedTo 出现——从生成链派生出直接的、被断言的责任是一个违规，即非蕴含义务将形式化约束于其上的边界。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqIndirectContributorHolds|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the indirect-contribution rule must satisfy: given an entity gmeow:wasGeneratedBy an activity that gmeow:wasAssociatedWith an agent, the reasoner must derive gmeow:indirectContributor from the entity to that agent — the productive composition the harvested prose commits to."
msgstr "间接-贡献规则必须满足的正向胜任案例：给定一个实体 gmeow:wasGeneratedBy 一项活动，而该活动 gmeow:wasAssociatedWith 一个主体，推理机必须从该实体向该主体派生 gmeow:indirectContributor——即所采收散文所承诺的生产性复合。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqInstantiatesWorkBrokenSpineRejected|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The negative countermodel the WEMI-instantiation rule must respect: an Item whose spine is broken — a Manifestation that embodies no Expression, or an Expression that realizes no Work — derives NO gmeow:instantiatesWork edge, because the derivation is the conjunction of all three R-relations. The boundary that keeps the shortcut from short-circuiting an incomplete spine."
msgstr "WEMI-实例化规则必须尊重的负向反模型：脊柱断裂的 Item——一个不体现任何 Expression 的 Manifestation，或一个不实现任何 Work 的 Expression——不派生任何 gmeow:instantiatesWork 边，因为该派生是全部三条 R-关系的合取。防止该捷径对不完整脊柱进行短路的边界。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqInstantiatesWorkHolds|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the WEMI-instantiation rule must satisfy: given an Item that gmeow:exemplifies a Manifestation that gmeow:embodies an Expression that gmeow:realizes a Work, the reasoner must derive gmeow:instantiatesWork from the Item to that Work — the copy-to-Work composition the harvested prose commits to."
msgstr "WEMI-实例化规则必须满足的正向胜任案例：给定一个 Item，它 gmeow:exemplifies 一个 Manifestation，后者 gmeow:embodies 一个 Expression，后者 gmeow:realizes 一个 Work，推理机必须从该 Item 向该 Work 派生 gmeow:instantiatesWork——即所采收散文所承诺的副本-到-Work 复合。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqLicensedFalsehoodDeceptionRejected|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The negative countermodel the licensed-falsehood safety partition must respect: classifying a socially-licensed non-truth-asserting projection (a novel, a satire) as deception is rejected — the audience understands the non-asserting frame. HONEST SCOPE: the exclusion is realized in the OWL / full-FOL projection (strong negation in the head); the native monotone chase does not enforce it, disclosed in the loss ledger."
msgstr "被许可-虚假安全分区必须尊重的负向反模型：将一个受社会许可、不作真理断言的投射（一部小说、一则讽刺作品）归类为欺骗将被拒绝——受众理解其不作断言的框架。诚实范围：该排除在 OWL / 全-FOL 投影中实现（头部中的强否定）；原生单调追逐并不强制它，此点在损失账本中披露。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqLicensedFalsehoodSafeHolds|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the licensed-falsehood safety partition must satisfy: a gmeow:Event whose gmeow:projectedStandpoint carries gmeow:claimVeridicality gmeow:veridicalityLicensedFalsehood (fiction, satire, sarcasm) is NOT a gmeow:eventTypeDeception, even though it carries a held/projected gap. The well-formed case the exclusion admits."
msgstr "被许可-虚假安全分区必须满足的正向胜任案例：一个 gmeow:Event，其 gmeow:projectedStandpoint 携带 gmeow:claimVeridicality gmeow:veridicalityLicensedFalsehood（虚构、讽刺、反讽），并不是一个 gmeow:eventTypeDeception，纵使它携带一个所持/所投射的落差。该排除所容许的良构案例。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqNoOverTypingHolds|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the no-over-typing constraint must satisfy: an object whose sortal traces its principle of identity to exactly one ultimate logic:Kind is well-formed — it carries no logic:MixIden violation — because a Kind supplies a single principle of identity (Principle 9's refusal to over-type)."
msgstr "无-过度类型化约束必须满足的正向胜任案例：一个对象，其 sortal 将其身份原则追溯到恰好一个终极的 logic:Kind，是良构的——它不携带任何 logic:MixIden 违规——因为一个 Kind 供给单一的身份原则（原则 9 对过度类型化的拒绝）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqNoOverTypingTwoKindsRejected|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The negative countermodel the no-over-typing constraint must respect: a sortal tracing its identity to two-or-more disjoint logic:Kinds is the logic:MixIden violation — over-typing the foundation catches as a finding, never admits as a well-formed model. The boundary Principle 9 enforces: co-equal facets are not fused into two disjoint identity-supplying Kinds on one instance."
msgstr "无-过度类型化约束必须尊重的负向反模型：一个将其身份追溯到两个或更多不相交 logic:Kinds 的 sortal 即是 logic:MixIden 违规——过度类型化会被基础作为一条发现所捕获，绝不作为良构模型而容许。原则 9 所强制的边界：对等的诸面向不会在同一实例上被融合为两个不相交的、供给身份的 Kinds。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqObjectIndividuationCoveringGapRejected|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The negative countermodel the object-individuation covering must respect: a logic:Object typed into NONE of the three individuation kinds violates the owl:unionOf covering in the OWL-DL projection — an OWL reasoner rejects the class-covering gap. HONEST SCOPE: the native monotone StratifiedNAF gate does NOT enforce this disjunctive covering, so this rejection is realized only in the OWL projection and is disclosed in the loss ledger."
msgstr "对象-个体化覆盖必须尊重的负向反模型：未被类型化进三种个体化种类之任一的 logic:Object，在 OWL-DL 投影中违反 owl:unionOf 覆盖——OWL 推理机拒绝该类覆盖缺口。诚实范围：原生单调 StratifiedNAF 关卡不强制这一析取覆盖，故该拒绝仅在 OWL 投影中实现，并在损失账本中披露。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqObjectIndividuationCoveringHolds|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the object-individuation covering must satisfy: a logic:Object that is one of the three individuation kinds (logic:Collection, logic:Quantity, logic:FunctionalComplex) is covered by the owl:unionOf — no gap. Realized in the OWL-DL projection; the well-formed case the covering disjunction admits, completing the individuation-kind pairwise disjointness into a partition."
msgstr "对象-个体化覆盖必须满足的正向胜任案例：作为三种个体化种类之一（logic:Collection、logic:Quantity、logic:FunctionalComplex）的 logic:Object 被 owl:unionOf 覆盖——无缺口。在 OWL-DL 投影中实现；这是覆盖析取所容许的良构案例，将个体化-种类的两两不相交补全为一个分区。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqOrgMembershipPropagationDownwardRejected|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The negative countermodel the membership-propagation rule must respect: membership climbs the sub-organization chain UP only — a member of a parent organization is NOT thereby a member of its sub-organizations, and an agent outside the hierarchy gains no derived membership. The direction boundary the frontier-variable rule keeps, deriving parent membership from child membership and never the reverse."
msgstr "成员资格-传播规则必须尊重的负向反模型：成员资格只沿子组织链向上攀升——一个母组织的成员并不因此成为其诸子组织的成员，而处于层级之外的主体不获得任何派生成员资格。边界变量规则所保持的方向边界，即从子成员资格派生母成员资格，绝不反向。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqOrgMembershipPropagationHolds|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the membership-propagation rule must satisfy: given an agent gmeow:memberOf a department that is gmeow:subOrganizationOf a company, the reasoner must derive gmeow:memberOf from the agent to the company — and, recursively, to every further containing organization — the upward propagation the harvested prose commits to."
msgstr "成员资格-传播规则必须满足的正向胜任案例：给定一个主体 gmeow:memberOf 一个部门，而该部门 gmeow:subOrganizationOf 一家公司，推理机必须从该主体向该公司派生 gmeow:memberOf——并递归地向每一个更外层的包含组织——即所采收散文所承诺的向上传播。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqProperPartAsymmetryHolds|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the properPartOf-asymmetry axiom must satisfy: given logic:properPartOf(a,b), the reasoner must not also hold logic:properPartOf(b,a) — the strict-order reading the harvested prose commits to."
msgstr "properPartOf-非对称公理必须满足的正向胜任案例：给定 logic:properPartOf(a,b)，推理机不得同时持有 logic:properPartOf(b,a)——即所采收散文所承诺的严格序读法。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqProperPartAsymmetrySymmetricPairRejected|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The negative countermodel the properPartOf-asymmetry axiom must respect: a purported model asserting both logic:properPartOf(a,b) and logic:properPartOf(b,a) is a violation, not an admissible model — the boundary the formalization must not cross."
msgstr "properPartOf-非对称公理必须尊重的负向反模型：一个宣称同时断言 logic:properPartOf(a,b) 与 logic:properPartOf(b,a) 的模型是一个违规，而非可容许的模型——即形式化不得跨越的边界。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqRelatorMediationHolds|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the relator-mediation discipline (RelComp) must satisfy: a concrete relator that mediates at least two distinct relata stays coherent — it fires no logic:violation logic:RelComp. gmeow:Commitment, which mediates gmeow:committedAgent, gmeow:commitmentBeneficiary and gmeow:intentionGoal, is well-mediated and passes."
msgstr "关系子-中介纪律（RelComp）必须满足的正向胜任案例：一个中介至少两个不同关系项的具体关系子保持一致——它不触发任何 logic:violation logic:RelComp。gmeow:Commitment 中介 gmeow:committedAgent、gmeow:commitmentBeneficiary 与 gmeow:intentionGoal，是良好中介的，予以通过。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqRelatorMediationUnderMediatedRejected|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The negative countermodel the relator-mediation discipline must reject: a concrete relator that mediates fewer than two distinct relata is degenerate and fires logic:violation logic:RelComp — an objectified relation that connects only one entity grounds no material relation, so it is not a relator."
msgstr "关系子-中介纪律必须拒绝的负向反模型：一个中介少于两个不同关系项的具体关系子是退化的，触发 logic:violation logic:RelComp——一个只连接一个实体的对象化关系不接地任何实质关系，故它不是一个关系子。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqRootFindingHolds|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the root-finding rule must satisfy — 'which findings are root causes': given F2 gmeow:findingRootCause F1, the reasoner must derive rdf:type(F1, gmeow:RootFinding); and it must fire through the gmeow:DiagnosticMetaRule class discovery exactly like the other meta-rules, so a consumer selecting rules by that type runs it with no engine change."
msgstr "根-发现规则必须满足的正向胜任案例——'哪些发现是根因'：给定 F2 gmeow:findingRootCause F1，推理机必须导出 rdf:type(F1, gmeow:RootFinding)；并且它必须像其他元规则一样经由 gmeow:DiagnosticMetaRule 类发现而触发，从而一个按该类型选择规则的消费者无需更改引擎即可运行它。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqRootFindingNonRootRejected|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The negative countermodel the root-finding rule must respect: a finding that is NOT the gmeow:findingRootCause of any finding is never typed gmeow:RootFinding — the marker names exactly the witnessed roots, so a downstream witness or an independent finding with no dependents carries no gmeow:RootFinding type."
msgstr "根-发现规则必须尊重的负向反模型：一条并非任何发现之 gmeow:findingRootCause 的发现绝不会被类型化为 gmeow:RootFinding——该标记恰好命名那些被见证的根，故一个下游见证或一个无任何依赖者的独立发现不携带任何 gmeow:RootFinding 类型。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqSocialInformationOverlapDisjointRejected|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The negative countermodel that explains WHY the social/information overlap must be preserved: IF gmeow:SocialObject were wrongly asserted owl:disjointWith gmeow:InformationObject, then a founding myth typed as both would be forced to owl:Nothing by the coherence gate — collapsing a legitimate model. The rejected disjointness is the mistake this deliberate non-assertion guards against; asserting it is the boundary the partition must NOT cross."
msgstr "阐明为何社会/信息重叠必须被保持的负向反模型：倘若 gmeow:SocialObject 被错误地断言为 owl:disjointWith gmeow:InformationObject，那么一个被同时类型化为两者的建国神话就会被一致性关卡逼为 owl:Nothing——从而使一个正当的模型坍缩。被拒绝的不相交性正是这一刻意不作断言所防范的错误；断言它就是该分区不得跨越的边界。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqSocialInformationOverlapHolds|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the deliberate social/information overlap must satisfy: an individual typed BOTH gmeow:SocialObject and gmeow:InformationObject — a founding myth that is at once socially sustained and information-bearing — stays coherent and is NOT forced to owl:Nothing, precisely because no disjointness between the two is asserted. The overlap the top-sortal partition deliberately preserves."
msgstr "刻意的社会/信息重叠必须满足的正向胜任案例：一个被同时类型化为 gmeow:SocialObject 与 gmeow:InformationObject 的个体——一个既由社会维系又承载信息的建国神话——保持一致且不会被逼为 owl:Nothing，恰恰因为两者之间未断言任何不相交性。顶层-sortal 分区刻意保持的重叠。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqTenureClaimSurfacingHolds|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the tenure-claim-surfacing rules must satisfy: given a gmeow:StandpointTenure that gmeow:standpointClaim a claim, gmeow:tenureStandpoint a standpoint, and gmeow:tenurePosition a position, the reasoner must derive gmeow:vantage from the claim to that standpoint AND gmeow:observedFeature from the claim to that position — the tenure→claim mapping the harvested prose commits to."
msgstr "任期-主张浮现规则必须满足的正向胜任案例：给定一个 gmeow:StandpointTenure，它 gmeow:standpointClaim 一个主张、gmeow:tenureStandpoint 一个立场、gmeow:tenurePosition 一个位置，推理机必须从该主张向该立场派生 gmeow:vantage，并从该主张向该位置派生 gmeow:observedFeature——即所采收散文所承诺的 任期→主张 映射。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqTenureClaimSurfacingSwapRejected|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The negative countermodel the tenure-claim-surfacing rules must respect: the mapping is directional and specific — the tenureStandpoint becomes the claim's gmeow:vantage (never its gmeow:observedFeature) and the tenurePosition becomes the claim's gmeow:observedFeature (never its gmeow:vantage), and a tenure with no gmeow:standpointClaim surfaces nothing. The boundary that keeps frame and position from being crossed onto the wrong role."
msgstr "任期-主张浮现规则必须尊重的负向反模型：该映射是有向且特定的——tenureStandpoint 成为主张的 gmeow:vantage（绝非其 gmeow:observedFeature），tenurePosition 成为主张的 gmeow:observedFeature（绝非其 gmeow:vantage），而一个没有 gmeow:standpointClaim 的任期不浮现任何东西。防止框架与位置被交叉到错误角色之上的边界。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqTopSortalDisjointClashRejected|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The negative countermodel the top-sortal disjointness axioms must respect: an individual typed BOTH gmeow:Agent and gmeow:SocialObject is a violation — the native DL coherence gate forces it to owl:Nothing, because gmeow:Agent owl:disjointWith gmeow:SocialObject is asserted (net-new on this branch). A thing that both acts and bears responsibility yet exists purely by social convention is not an admissible model. The boundary the disjointness enforces."
msgstr "顶层-sortal 不相交公理必须尊重的负向反模型：同时被类型化为 gmeow:Agent 与 gmeow:SocialObject 的个体是一个违规——原生 DL 一致性关卡将其逼为 owl:Nothing，因为已断言 gmeow:Agent owl:disjointWith gmeow:SocialObject（本分支上全新引入）。一个既行动又承担责任、却纯粹凭社会约定而存在的事物不是可容许的模型。该不相交性所强制的边界。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqTopSortalDisjointHolds|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the top-sortal disjointness axioms must satisfy: an individual typed into exactly one of the four kernel top sortals (gmeow:Agent, gmeow:InformationObject, gmeow:PhysicalObject, gmeow:SocialObject) stays coherent — it is not forced to owl:Nothing — because each thing is individuated under a single top sortal (save the deliberately-preserved social∩information overlap)."
msgstr "顶层-sortal 不相交公理必须满足的正向胜任案例：被类型化进四个内核顶层 sortal（gmeow:Agent、gmeow:InformationObject、gmeow:PhysicalObject、gmeow:SocialObject）之恰好一个的个体保持一致——它不会被逼为 owl:Nothing——因为每个事物皆在单一顶层 sortal 之下被个体化（刻意保持的 社会∩信息 重叠除外）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Crisp|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The target relationship is ontically sharp: the alignment either holds or does not, with no borderline cases. The determinacy of an equivalence or a clean subsumption."
msgstr "目标关系在本体上是明锐的：对齐或是成立或是不成立，没有边界情形。一个等价或一个干净的包摄所具有的确定性。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/criterionPoleDistinctness|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Asserts that a gmeow:Criterion's gmeow:rewardPole and gmeow:penaltyPole must be distinct: one pole is no axis. The native coherence gate raises a violation when they coincide."
msgstr "断言一个 gmeow:Criterion 的 gmeow:rewardPole 与 gmeow:penaltyPole 必须相异：单一的极点不构成轴。当二者重合时，原生一致性关卡会引发一个违规。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/crossMode|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The mode of a logic:CrossNodeConstraint: 'co-occur' (the two roles must be present together) or 'differ' (the two roles must never bind the same value)."
msgstr "一个 logic:CrossNodeConstraint 的模式：'co-occur'（两个角色必须一同在场）或 'differ'（两个角色绝不可绑定同一值）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/dagCycleWitness|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates an `unsupported` DAG-workflow verdict to a disclosed offending edge or cycle member — the back-edge or logic:Iteration that places a plan outside the certified acyclic fragment — MULTI-valued (a graph may carry several cycles). Mirrors the witness-disclosure discipline of logic:forbiddenViolationWitness: the certifier never silently truncates a cyclic plan, it surfaces exactly which edges break acyclicity while the plan stays valid under a non-DAG contract. Domain a reasoning result or coherence outcome carrying the `unsupported` evaluation status, range a flow edge or process node (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将一个 `unsupported` 的 DAG-工作流裁决关联到一条被披露的违规边或环成员——即把计划置于已认证无环片段之外的回边或 logic:Iteration——多值（一个图可携带若干环）。映照 logic:forbiddenViolationWitness 的见证-披露纪律：认证器绝不静默截断一个有环计划，而是精确浮现出哪些边打破无环性，同时该计划在非-DAG 契约下仍然有效。定义域为携带 `unsupported` 求值状态的一个推理结果或一致性结局，值域为一条流边或一个进程节点（以散文陈述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DagWorkflowContract|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The named ReasoningContract that requests the DAG-workflow resource policy (logic:resourcePolicy logic:DagWorkflowResource), under which a loop-free logic:Plan is topologically schedulable and complete-for-fragment. It is a CONTRACT (a standing request on the Resource facet), NOT a logic:ReasoningPreset: a preset bundles a model-semantics selection, whereas this fixes only the execution-discipline (Resource) facet — the contract-not-profile doctrine, applied so the resource discipline is a facet a contract requests, not a semantic profile. The dogfooded build pipeline runs logic:executedUnderContract this contract; a cyclic plan resolves to `unsupported` with its offending edge named rather than being approximated to a nearby supported semantics."
msgstr "请求 DAG-工作流资源策略（logic:resourcePolicy logic:DagWorkflowResource）的具名 ReasoningContract，在该策略下，一个无环路的 logic:Plan 是可拓扑排程且片段-完备的。它是一个契约（对 Resource 面向的常设请求），而非一个 logic:ReasoningPreset：一个预设捆绑了模型-语义选择，而这一个只固定执行-纪律（Resource）面向——即契约-非-剖面的教义，如此施用使得资源纪律成为一个契约所请求的面向，而非一个语义剖面。自食其狗粮的构建流水线以 logic:executedUnderContract 在此契约下运行；一个有环计划会解析为 `unsupported` 并命名其违规边，而不是被近似到某个邻近的受支持语义。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DagWorkflowResource|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The resource execution policy of the DAG-workflow profile: it requires the plan's control/dataflow graph to be a loop-free (acyclic) DAG — no logic:Iteration and an acyclic logic:dataflowConsumes / flow-edge closure — so the schedule is a topological order with a hard termination guarantee, and the result reports logic:CompleteForFragment. Acyclicity is the universal structural guarantee certified here; a typed terminal discipline such as the build pipeline's single gmeow:kindSink is an additional per-surface constraint, not part of this graph-level certification. A specialization of the certified-fragment discipline of logic:CertifiedFragmentResource applied to process control flow rather than rule recursion; because resource is an execution policy holding independent properties together, a contract may carry both a DAG-workflow requirement and a budget at once. A plan outside the acyclic fragment is still valid canonically but resolves to `unsupported` under this policy, the offending edge disclosed by logic:dagCycleWitness — never silently truncated."
msgstr "DAG-工作流剖面的资源执行策略：它要求计划的控制/数据流图为一个无环路（无环）的 DAG——没有 logic:Iteration 且有一个无环的 logic:dataflowConsumes / 流边闭包——从而排程是一个带有硬性终止保证的拓扑序，且结果报告 logic:CompleteForFragment。无环性是此处所认证的普遍结构保证；诸如构建流水线单一 gmeow:kindSink 之类的具类型终端纪律是一项额外的、逐-表面的约束，并不属于这一图-层级认证。它是 logic:CertifiedFragmentResource 的已认证-片段纪律的一个特化，施用于进程控制流而非规则递归；因为资源是一个把独立属性维系在一起的执行策略，一个契约可同时携带一个 DAG-工作流要求与一个预算。一个处于无环片段之外的计划在规范上仍然有效，但在此策略下解析为 `unsupported`，其违规边由 logic:dagCycleWitness 披露——绝不静默截断。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/dataflowConsumes|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a process node — a logic:Plan step, a pipeline stage, or a procedure step — to an upstream node whose product it reads: the canonical binary dataflow dependency, oriented consumer -> producer (an executor inverts it to schedule producers first). The transitive closure must be acyclic for the DAG-workflow profile (logic:DagWorkflowResource); a cycle takes the plan out of the certified acyclic fragment and is disclosed through logic:dagCycleWitness, never silently dropped. Domain and range a process node (stated in prose, matching the module's convention). The reified FLOW-GRAPH counterpart is logic:DataFlowEdge; downstream surfaces such as gmeow:dataflowConsumes specialize this property."
msgstr "将一个进程节点——一个 logic:Plan 步骤、一个流水线阶段或一个过程步骤——关联到一个上游节点，即它读取其产物的那个节点：规范的二元数据流依赖，取向为 consumer -> producer（一个执行器将其反转以先排程生产者）。对于 DAG-工作流剖面（logic:DagWorkflowResource），其传递闭包必须是无环的；一个环会把计划带出已认证无环片段，并经由 logic:dagCycleWitness 披露，绝不静默丢弃。定义域与值域皆为一个进程节点（以散文陈述，符合本模块的约定）。其具体化的流-图对应物是 logic:DataFlowEdge；诸如 gmeow:dataflowConsumes 之类的下游表面对此属性作特化。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DataFlowEdge|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A reified dataflow edge between two process nodes — the FLOW-GRAPH counterpart of the logic:dataflowConsumes property, mediating a source (producer) node via logic:flowFrom and a target (consumer) node via logic:flowTo. Use the property form (logic:dataflowConsumes) for a bare binary dependency and this reified form when an edge must carry its own attributes (the flowing entity, a guard, an order). Downstream reified dataflow relators such as gmeow:DataFlow specialize this class. A Relator mediating two distinct relata, satisfying the relator-mediation discipline."
msgstr "两个流程节点之间的一条具体化数据流边——logic:dataflowConsumes 属性的流图对应物,通过 logic:flowFrom 中介一个源(生产者)节点、通过 logic:flowTo 中介一个目标(消费者)节点。对于裸的二元依赖采用属性形式(logic:dataflowConsumes),而当一条边必须携带其自身属性(流动的实体、一个守卫、一个次序)时采用此具体化形式。下游的具体化数据流关系子(如 gmeow:DataFlow)特化此类。一个中介两个不同 relata 的关系子,满足关系子中介纪律。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/dataflowProduces|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The inverse of logic:dataflowConsumes: relates a process node to a downstream node that reads its product (producer -> consumer). The canonical authored direction is logic:dataflowConsumes, so this inverse is normally left to be inferred rather than asserted. Domain and range a process node (stated in prose)."
msgstr "logic:dataflowConsumes 的逆:将一个流程节点关联到读取其产物的下游节点(生产者 -> 消费者)。规范的编写方向是 logic:dataflowConsumes,因此此逆通常留待推断而非断言。定义域与值域为一个流程节点(以散文陈述)。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DatalogFragment|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The formula-fragment facet value selecting the function-free, range-restricted Datalog class of formulae. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract; the decidable, terminating fragment more restrictive than logic:HornFragment (no function symbols) and the projection target for which least-model semantics is PTIME-data."
msgstr "选择无函数、值域受限的 Datalog 公式类的公式片段侧面值。在 ReasoningContract 上单值;比 logic:HornFragment 更受限(无函数符号)的可判定、可终止片段,也是最小模型语义为 PTIME-data 的投影目标。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DatalogProjection|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The projection-target value requesting the answer be rendered to a Datalog surface. One of several output targets a single contract may name at once; like every projection target it is a rendering request and never alters which entailments hold."
msgstr "请求将答案渲染到 Datalog 表面的投影目标值。单个合约可一次命名的多个输出目标之一;如同每个投影目标,它是一次渲染请求,绝不改变哪些蕴涵成立。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Datarange|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:adultAge a logic:Datarange ; logic:onDatatype xsd:integer ; logic:withRestrictions ( [ xsd:minInclusive 18 ] ) ."
msgstr "示例：ex:adultAge a logic:Datarange ; logic:onDatatype xsd:integer ; logic:withRestrictions ( [ xsd:minInclusive 18 ] ) ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Datarange|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Facet records retain their native datatype-facet predicates inside the ordered restriction list."
msgstr "面记录在有序的限制列表内部保留其原生的数据类型面谓词。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/datumRecordedAt|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The xsd:dateTime at which the datum supporting a guarded precondition situation was recorded — the start of the age span a logic:FreshnessGuard measures against its logic:freshnessHorizon. Domain a precondition situation, range xsd:dateTime (stated in prose). Compared against logic:decisionTime in a single timescale; a missing value under a declared freshness guard is a hard error, never a silent pass."
msgstr "记录支撑某个受守卫前置条件情形的数据的 xsd:dateTime——logic:FreshnessGuard 相对其 logic:freshnessHorizon 度量的年龄跨度之起点。定义域为前置条件情形,值域为 xsd:dateTime(以散文陈述)。在单一时间刻度上与 logic:decisionTime 比较;在已声明的新鲜度守卫下缺失取值即为硬错误,绝非静默通过。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DeadlineWindowGoal|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:GoalExpressionKind for an achievement or maintenance target indexed to a bounding logic:deadlineWindow interval; the evaluation stays logic:GoalEvaluationUndetermined while the window is open and becomes conclusive once it closes. The single operand carries the windowed target sub-expression."
msgstr "用于绑定到界定性 logic:deadlineWindow 区间的达成或维持目标的 logic:GoalExpressionKind;窗口开启期间评估保持 logic:GoalEvaluationUndetermined,一旦关闭即成定论。单一操作数承载加窗的目标子表达式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/deadlineWindow|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a deadline-window logic:GoalExpression to the bounding interval after which its window closes — until the window closes the evaluation is logic:GoalEvaluationUndetermined, and once it closes the judgment becomes conclusive. Domain logic:GoalExpression (stated in prose); the range is the bounding interval, left open in this standalone module. The companion of the goal's operand (its achievement or maintenance target)."
msgstr "将一个截止窗口 logic:GoalExpression 关联到其窗口在其后关闭的界定区间——窗口关闭之前评估为 logic:GoalEvaluationUndetermined,一旦关闭判断即成定论。定义域 logic:GoalExpression(以散文陈述);值域为界定区间,在此独立模块中留空。目标操作数(其达成或维持目标)的伴随物。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/decidabilityClass|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The decidability-class guarantee a logic:EngineContract offers for one of its logic:supportedProfile presets — the termination/complexity token the engine promises for queries read under that preset (e.g. `terminating/PTIME-data` for the positive-Horn and stratified-negation presets, `three-valued/PTIME` for well-founded, `NP-hard` for stable-model, `operational/Turing-complete` for procedural Prolog, `probabilistic/#P-hard` for the probabilistic preset). Single-valued per preset. Domain logic:ReasoningPreset — a supported preset of the contract — (stated in prose). It draws from the SAME value vocabulary as logic:complexityClass but is carried in a DIFFERENT place for a different purpose: logic:complexityClass records the class of a lowering/projection alongside its preservation polarity in the loss ledger, whereas logic:decidabilityClass is the per-preset guarantee published on the runtime engine's capability manifest so a consumer reads it off the pinned contract. Decidability here is a projection guarantee bought by reasoning under a bounded preset, never a canonical-layer promise — the canonical layer is maximally expressive and only semi-decidable. Authored canonically in crates/logic (Rust); a lossy documentation projection (Principle 17)."
msgstr "logic:EngineContract 为其某个 logic:supportedProfile 预设所提供的可判定性类保证——引擎对在该预设下读取的查询所承诺的终止性/复杂度记号(例如正 Horn 与分层否定预设为 `terminating/PTIME-data`,良基语义为 `three-valued/PTIME`,稳定模型为 `NP-hard`,过程式 Prolog 为 `operational/Turing-complete`,概率预设为 `probabilistic/#P-hard`)。每个预设单值。定义域 logic:ReasoningPreset——合约的一个受支持预设——(以散文陈述)。它取自与 logic:complexityClass 相同的取值词汇,却出于不同目的置于不同之处:logic:complexityClass 在损失账本中记录某个下降/投影的类别及其保持极性,而 logic:decidabilityClass 是发布在运行时引擎能力清单上的逐预设保证,使消费者可从锁定的合约上读到它。此处的可判定性是通过在有界预设下推理换得的投影保证,绝非规范层的承诺——规范层最大程度可表达且仅半可判定。在 crates/logic(Rust)中规范地编写;一个有损的文档投影(原则 17)。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/decisionTime|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The xsd:dateTime a logic:GateProbe is judged at — the \"now\" against which a logic:FreshnessGuard measures the age of a precondition datum. Domain logic:GateProbe, range xsd:dateTime (stated in prose). When a probe gates a schema carrying a freshness guard, a missing logic:decisionTime is a hard error, never a silent pass: the age comparison has no reference point and the evaluator refuses to guess."
msgstr "对一个 logic:GateProbe 作出判定所在的 xsd:dateTime——logic:FreshnessGuard 据以度量前置条件数据年龄的“现在”。定义域 logic:GateProbe,值域 xsd:dateTime(以散文陈述)。当一次探测把关一个携带新鲜度守卫的模式时,缺失 logic:decisionTime 即为硬错误,绝非静默通过:年龄比较没有参照点,而求值器拒绝猜测。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/declaredIsolationLevel|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to the logic:IsolationLevel guarantee strength its concurrent transactions must meet. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:IsolationLevel (stated in prose); at most one per contract, from the closed isolation-level set (a value outside it is a hard error). It is kept DISTINCT from logic:declaredProtocol (the mechanism that would enforce the level) and from logic:serializabilityCriterion (a history property): an isolation level is the guarantee STRENGTH required, neither the mechanism that achieves it nor the property a particular history happens to have. The native evaluator classifies whether the witnessed schedule meets this declared strength and records the result as logic:isolationLevelAdequacy."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ReasoningContract 关联到其并发事务必须满足的 logic:IsolationLevel 保证强度。定义域 logic:ReasoningContract,值域 logic:IsolationLevel(以散文陈述);每份合约至多一个,取自封闭的隔离级别集合(集合之外的取值即为硬错误)。它与 logic:declaredProtocol(将强制施行该级别的机制)以及 logic:serializabilityCriterion(一种历史属性)保持区别:隔离级别是所要求的保证强度,既非达成它的机制,也非某个特定历史恰好具有的属性。原生求值器判定所见证的调度是否满足此已声明强度,并将结果记录为 logic:isolationLevelAdequacy。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/declaredProtocol|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to the logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol its concurrent transactions are to be enforced under — the IMPLEMENTATION MECHANISM (strict / strong-strict two-phase locking, timestamp ordering, or optimistic validation) declared for the run. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol (stated in prose); at most one per contract, from the closed protocol set (a value outside it is a hard error). It is kept DISTINCT from the guarantee strength the mechanism is meant to achieve (logic:declaredIsolationLevel) and from the history property it produces (logic:serializabilityCriterion): a protocol is HOW a guarantee is enforced, never the guarantee itself. The native evaluator classifies whether the witnessed schedule respects this protocol's discipline over the run's recorded protocol events and records the verdict as logic:protocolEnforced."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ReasoningContract 关联到其并发事务应在其下被强制施行的 logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol——为该次运行声明的实现机制(严格/强严格两阶段锁定、时间戳排序,或乐观校验)。定义域 logic:ReasoningContract,值域 logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol(以散文陈述);每份合约至多一个,取自封闭的协议集合(集合之外的取值即为硬错误)。它与该机制意在达成的保证强度(logic:declaredIsolationLevel)以及它所产生的历史属性(logic:serializabilityCriterion)保持区别:协议是保证被如何强制施行,绝非保证本身。原生求值器就该次运行所记录的协议事件,判定所见证的调度是否遵守此协议的纪律,并将裁决记录为 logic:protocolEnforced。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/declaresColumn|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ResultShape to a logic:ResultColumn it declares. Set-valued: a shape declares one column per SELECT variable it types. Domain logic:ResultShape, range logic:ResultColumn (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ResultShape 关联到它所声明的一个 logic:ResultColumn。集值:一个形状为其类型化的每个 SELECT 变量声明一列。定义域 logic:ResultShape,值域 logic:ResultColumn(以散文陈述)。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/defaultClosure|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to the logic:ClosureValue that is the default of its closure map — the open- or closed-world reading applied to any predicate or context key not overridden by a logic:closureEntry. The closure facet is a map; this is its default, normally open-world, with closed-world confined to keys inside a logic:WorldBoundary. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:ClosureValue (stated in prose, matching the module's convention)."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ReasoningContract 关联到作为其闭包映射默认值的 logic:ClosureValue——对任何未被 logic:closureEntry 覆盖的谓词或上下文键所施加的开放世界或封闭世界读法。闭包侧面是一个映射;此为其默认值,通常为开放世界,封闭世界则限于 logic:WorldBoundary 之内的键。定义域 logic:ReasoningContract,值域 logic:ClosureValue(以散文陈述,遵循模块惯例)。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/defaultLadderProfile|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The shipped default logic:LadderProjectionProfile the coarse-ladder projection rules read: awareness ≥ emerging emits gmeow:isAwareOf, declarative familiarity ≥ competent emits gmeow:knowsAbout, conceptual understanding ≥ competent emits gmeow:understands, and procedural competence ≥ strong together with transfer ≥ strong emit gmeow:hasMastered."
msgstr "粗阶梯投影规则所读取的、随附交付的默认 logic:LadderProjectionProfile:觉知 ≥ emerging 发出 gmeow:isAwareOf,陈述性熟悉度 ≥ competent 发出 gmeow:knowsAbout,概念性理解 ≥ competent 发出 gmeow:understands,而过程性胜任 ≥ strong 连同迁移 ≥ strong 发出 gmeow:hasMastered。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DefaultNegation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The negation-as-failure operator: a body literal that holds when its atom is not derivable. One member of the negation-operator set facet (which may also include logic:ExplicitNegation); a program using it requires at least the stratified-negation reading of the model-semantics facet rather than positive-Horn least-model semantics."
msgstr "失败即否定算子:当其原子不可导出时成立的一个体文字。否定算子集合侧面的一个成员(该集合也可包含 logic:ExplicitNegation);使用它的程序要求模型语义侧面至少采用分层否定读法,而非正 Horn 最小模型语义。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DefeasibleEvidence|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A reified declaration that one relation or fact (logic:evidenceProperty) is DEFEASIBLE — defeater-blockable — evidence for another (logic:evidenceFor), carrying its logic:defeasibleStrength, and explicitly NOT a strict entailment. The support can come apart: the evidence may hold while the supported claim fails (and conversely), so the engine never materializes the supported edge from the evidence under the default reasoning — only a consumer opting into defeasible reasoning under a declared contract draws it, defeated when a declared defeater holds. The central recast of any 'X is evidence for Y, not X entails Y' relationship; its first instance is gmeow:hasSkill as defeasible evidence for gmeow:knowsAbout."
msgstr "一份具体化声明,断言某个关系或事实(logic:evidenceProperty)是支持另一者(logic:evidenceFor)的可废止——可被反驳者阻断——证据,携带其 logic:defeasibleStrength,且明确并非严格蕴涵。支持可以脱节:证据可以成立而被支持的主张却失败(反之亦然),因此在默认推理下引擎绝不从该证据物化出被支持的边——唯有在已声明合约下选择加入可废止推理的消费者才引出它,并在已声明的反驳者成立时被废止。它是对任何“X 是 Y 的证据,而非 X 蕴涵 Y”关系的核心重铸;其首个实例是作为 gmeow:knowsAbout 的可废止证据的 gmeow:hasSkill。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/defeasibleStrength|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A solver-layer measure of how strongly a logic:DefeasibleEvidence supports its logic:evidenceFor target before any defeater — a ranking annotation, never asserted as a reasoned axiom and never a probability. Range is left open (an ordinal label or a numeric weight), stated in prose."
msgstr "求解器层的一种度量,表示在任何反驳者之前 logic:DefeasibleEvidence 对其 logic:evidenceFor 目标的支持强度——一个排名注记,绝不作为被推理的公理断言,也绝非概率。值域留空(一个序数标签或一个数值权重),以散文陈述。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DeleteUpdate|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "An elementary Transaction-Logic update of the `del(F)` kind: it retires one active support from the successor state while retaining the historical support in the path record. `del` is supersession, not physical erasure; state validity changes by moving to a successor snapshot, while displayability remains a separate disclosure decision."
msgstr "一次 `del(F)` 种类的初等 Transaction-Logic 更新:它从后继状态中退役一个活动支持,同时在路径记录中保留历史支持。`del` 是取代,而非物理擦除;状态有效性通过移动到后继快照而改变,而可显示性仍是一个单独的披露决定。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/del|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:DeleteUpdate to the support/fact it retires. The `del(F)` primitive removes F from the active support set of the successor state, records supersession provenance, and leaves the predecessor state and historical support intact."
msgstr "将一个 logic:DeleteUpdate 关联到它所退役的支持/事实。`del(F)` 原语从后继状态的活动支持集合中移除 F,记录取代来源,并使前驱状态与历史支持保持完好。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/demonstratesChaseWitness|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ExistentialChaseDemonstrand to the logic:ChaseWitnessLeaf witness that discharges its existential obligation — the `p` in the demonstrator's C ⊑ ∃p.D law. Domain logic:ExistentialChaseDemonstrand, range logic:ChaseWitnessLeaf (stated in prose). When a demonstrand instance asserts no such edge, the native existential chase invents a fresh Skolem witness (a gmeow:InventedWitness) and materializes the demonstratesChaseWitness edge to it; the property is the object-property head `p` whose someValuesFrom obligation makes the chase fire — an object property, never a datatype property, so its value is an invented individual, not a literal."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ExistentialChaseDemonstrand 关联到履行其存在性义务的 logic:ChaseWitnessLeaf 见证——即演示器 C ⊑ ∃p.D 法则中的 `p`。定义域 logic:ExistentialChaseDemonstrand,值域 logic:ChaseWitnessLeaf(以散文陈述)。当一个演示对象实例未断言任何此类边时,原生存在性追逐会发明一个新的 Skolem 见证(一个 gmeow:InventedWitness)并向它物化 demonstratesChaseWitness 边;该属性是其 someValuesFrom 义务触发追逐的对象属性头 `p`——一个对象属性,绝非数据类型属性,因此其取值是一个被发明的个体,而非字面量。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/demonstratesChaseWitness|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "logic:existentialChaseDemonstrandAlpha logic:demonstratesChaseWitness <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/skolem/9f2c> ."
msgstr "示例：logic:existentialChaseDemonstrandAlpha logic:demonstratesChaseWitness <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/skolem/9f2c> ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/deonticallyIdeal|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The typed deontic accessibility relation: a context is deontically ideal — an ought-world — relative to an issuer. Deontic reasoning is a USE of typed contexts, not a separate context type: a deontic claim is truth in the deontically-ideal accessible contexts of an issuer. Deontic accessibility is serial — every context from which an obligation is read has at least one accessible ideal context — so the 'satisfied in every ideal context' condition is never vacuously true; an empty ideal set yields undetermined rather than vacuous truth. logic:accessibleFrom is its generic superproperty in prose only — NOT asserted rdfs:subPropertyOf — so what is ideal never leaks into what is."
msgstr "带类型的道义可及关系:相对于一个发布者,某个上下文是道义理想的——一个应然世界。道义推理是对带类型上下文的一种运用,而非一种单独的上下文类型:一个道义主张即是在某发布者的道义理想可及上下文中的真。道义可及是串行的——读取义务所自的每个上下文都至少有一个可及的理想上下文——因此“在每个理想上下文中被满足”这一条件绝不空洞为真;空的理想集合产生未定,而非空洞的真。logic:accessibleFrom 仅在散文中是其通用超属性——并不断言 rdfs:subPropertyOf——从而理想之事绝不渗漏入实然之事。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/deonticallyIncompatible|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates two gmeow:Goals whose conjunction a norm makes impermissible even where it is physically reachable. Domain gmeow:Goal, range gmeow:Goal (stated in prose). One of seven conflict relations between independently-meaningful goals, weaker than gmeow:counterGoal (constitutive opposition). Deontic force arrives with the norms vocabulary, which ranges over goals — the dependency points toward the goal layer, never the reverse."
msgstr "关联两个 gmeow:Goals,其合取即便在物理上可达之处也被某条规范判为不可容许。定义域 gmeow:Goal,值域 gmeow:Goal(以散文陈述)。是独立有意义目标之间七种冲突关系之一,弱于 gmeow:counterGoal(构成性对立)。道义力量随规范词汇而来,规范词汇涵盖目标——依赖指向目标层,绝不反向。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DeonticFramework|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The normative framework: obligation, prohibition, permission, and recommendation evaluated against the deontic-ideal worlds of the typed context algebra, with issuer-indexed force (an ought is always according-to an authority, never bare) and serial deontic accessibility so the universal obligation condition is never vacuously satisfied (design/LOGIC-TELEOLOGY.md, the norms-and-deontic-force-over-goals section)."
msgstr "规范框架:义务、禁止、许可与推荐,针对带类型上下文代数的道义理想世界进行评估,力量按发布者索引(一个应然总是依据某个权威,绝不赤裸),且道义可及为串行,从而全称义务条件绝不空洞地被满足(design/LOGIC-TELEOLOGY.md,norms-and-deontic-force-over-goals 章节)。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DependencyModel|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A probability model carrying an EXPLICIT joint distribution over a correlated set of logic:probability facts: where logic:FullIndependence factorizes as a product, a dependency model substitutes a declared joint table (logic:correlates names the correlated facts; logic:jointOutcome enumerates the joint outcomes with their logic:jointProbability). Facts outside the correlated set remain independent and factorize as usual. The declared joint outcomes must be exhaustive and sum to one."
msgstr "一个概率模型,在一组相关的 logic:probability 事实上携带显式的联合分布:凡 logic:FullIndependence 因式分解为乘积之处,依赖模型代之以一张已声明的联合表(logic:correlates 命名相关事实;logic:jointOutcome 连同其 logic:jointProbability 枚举联合结果)。相关集合之外的事实仍保持独立并照常因式分解。已声明的联合结果必须穷尽且总和为一。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DerivationRule|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A head entailed from a body: the productive subset of the IR, where satisfying the antecedents derives the consequent. Distinct from logic:Constraint, whose violation is reported as a finding rather than producing new assertions."
msgstr "由体蕴涵出的头:IR 的生产性子集,其中满足前件即导出后件。区别于 logic:Constraint,后者的违反被报告为一项发现,而非产生新的断言。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/derivedHistory|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:TransactionOutcome of a logic:ConcurrentComposition run to the logic:ConcurrentHistory the native evaluator derived from the interleaved execution of its two legs. Domain logic:TransactionOutcome, range logic:ConcurrentHistory (stated in prose). It SEPARATES the executional-entailment verdict (the outcome — does a path exist) from the derived concurrency surface (the history — how the conflicting operations were ordered and whether that ordering is serializable): a concurrent run records BOTH, linked by this property, so neither the verdict nor the serializability finding is conflated with the other."
msgstr "将一次 logic:ConcurrentComposition 运行的 logic:TransactionOutcome 关联到原生求值器从其两条支路交错执行中导出的 logic:ConcurrentHistory。定义域 logic:TransactionOutcome,值域 logic:ConcurrentHistory(以散文陈述)。它把执行蕴涵裁决(结果——是否存在一条路径)与导出的并发表面(历史——冲突操作如何被排序、该排序是否可串行化)分离开:一次并发运行同时记录两者,由此属性相连,使得裁决与可串行化发现互不混淆。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DesignatedValueSet|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The facet value class of the designated-value set: which truth values count as designated (as holding) for the purpose of consequence. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract. It is one of the three independent components — truth algebra, admissible-valuation policy, designated values — that together separate FDE, LP, K3 and classical logic; collapsing any two of them erases exactly the choices that distinguish those logics."
msgstr "指定值集合的侧面值类:哪些真值在推论目的上算作被指定的(算作成立的)。在 ReasoningContract 上单值。它是三个独立成分之一——真值代数、可容许赋值策略、指定值——三者共同区分 FDE、LP、K3 与经典逻辑;将其中任意两者塌缩,恰好抹去区分这些逻辑的那些选择。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/designatedValues|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to the logic:DesignatedValueSet it selects — which truth values count as holding for consequence. Single-valued on the contract. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:DesignatedValueSet (stated in prose, matching the module's convention). One of the three independent truth-facet components; it must not be conflated with logic:admissibleValuation, since FDE and LP share a designated set and differ only in their admissible valuations."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ReasoningContract 关联到它所选择的 logic:DesignatedValueSet——哪些真值在推论上算作成立。在合约上单值。定义域 logic:ReasoningContract,值域 logic:DesignatedValueSet(以散文陈述,遵循模块惯例)。真值侧面的三个独立成分之一;不可与 logic:admissibleValuation 混淆,因为 FDE 与 LP 共享同一个指定集合,仅在其可容许赋值上有别。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DesignateTrueAndBoth|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The designated-value set that counts both true and both (the glut) as designated — i.e. as holding for the purpose of consequence. The designated set shared by FDE and LP in their standard presentations; what distinguishes FDE from LP is the admissible-valuation policy, not this designated set, so it is a formal error to attribute the FDE↔LP difference to the designated values."
msgstr "将 true 与 both(过剩)二者都算作被指定的——即在推论目的上算作成立的——指定值集合。FDE 与 LP 在其标准表述中共享的指定集合;区分 FDE 与 LP 的是可容许赋值策略,而非此指定集合,因此将 FDE↔LP 的差异归因于指定值是一个形式错误。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DesignateTrueOnly|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The designated-value set that counts only true as designated. The designated set of K3 and classical logic; combined with the admissible-valuation policy and truth algebra it fixes which logic a contract selects, the three components varying independently."
msgstr "仅将 true 算作被指定的指定值集合。K3 与经典逻辑的指定集合;与可容许赋值策略及真值代数结合,它确定一份合约选择哪种逻辑,三个成分各自独立地变化。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Determinacy|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The closed two-value axis recording whether the TARGET RELATIONSHIP a logic:Correspondence asserts is ontically crisp (logic:Crisp) or vague (logic:Vague). It is separate from logic:confidence: 'similar but not quite' is logic:Vague determinacy with a logic:AffineCorrespondence class, NOT a low-confidence logic:Equiv. Conflating the two destroys the distinction between an uncertain sharp claim and a confident fuzzy one. The set is closed, so a misspelt value names no declared determinacy and is rejected (design/LOGIC-CORRESPONDENCE.md, the quantitative-and-contextual-axes section)."
msgstr "记录一个 logic:Correspondence 所断言的目标关系在本体上是清晰的(logic:Crisp)还是模糊的(logic:Vague)的封闭二值轴。它与 logic:confidence 分离:“相似但不完全”是带 logic:AffineCorrespondence 类的 logic:Vague 确定性,而非低置信度的 logic:Equiv。将二者混淆会摧毁不确定的清晰主张与自信的模糊主张之间的区别。该集合封闭,因此拼写错误的取值不命名任何已声明的确定性并被拒绝(design/LOGIC-CORRESPONDENCE.md,quantitative-and-contextual-axes 章节)。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Dialect|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A named sub-language of the canonical logic: IR, in the MLIR sense of a dialect with its own node verifiers and progressive lowering (not an LLVM-style substrate). The one F1 dialect is logic:RelationalCore, the logical-to-physical lowering waist between the full IR and the native execution engine."
msgstr "规范 logic: IR 的一个具名子语言,采用 MLIR 意义上的方言,拥有自己的节点校验器与渐进式下降(而非 LLVM 式的基底)。唯一的 F1 方言是 logic:RelationalCore,即完整 IR 与原生执行引擎之间逻辑到物理的下降腰部。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/dimensionAwareness|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The awareness dimension: whether the agent registers the subject at all. The shallowest factored axis; the source of the gmeow:isAwareOf rung of the coarse knowledge ladder under a declared threshold."
msgstr "觉知维度:智能体是否根本注意到该主题。最浅的因子化轴;粗知识阶梯在已声明阈值下 gmeow:isAwareOf 阶级的来源。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/dimensionCalibration|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The calibration dimension: whether the agent's confidence matches its accuracy. Assessed against an explicit forecast protocol (a forecast/outcome series, a scoring rule, a reference class and observation window), kept apart from a single logic:confidence value and from the metacognition vocabulary's qualitative gmeow:CalibrationStatus."
msgstr "校准维度:智能体的置信度是否与其准确性相符。针对一个显式的预测协议(一个预测/结果序列、一条评分规则、一个参照类与观测窗口)评估,与单个 logic:confidence 值以及元认知词汇的定性 gmeow:CalibrationStatus 分开。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/dimensionConceptualUnderstanding|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The conceptual-understanding dimension: whether the agent grasps WHY — the structure behind the facts, beyond reciting them. The source of the gmeow:understands rung of the coarse knowledge ladder under a declared threshold."
msgstr "概念性理解维度:智能体是否把握“为什么”——事实背后的结构,超出对它们的复述。粗知识阶梯在已声明阈值下 gmeow:understands 阶级的来源。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/dimensionDeclarativeFamiliarity|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The declarative-familiarity dimension: what the agent knows THAT — the facts it can state about the subject. The source of the gmeow:knowsAbout rung of the coarse knowledge ladder under a declared threshold."
msgstr "陈述性熟悉度维度:智能体知道“何事为真”——它能就该主题陈述的事实。粗知识阶梯在已声明阈值下 gmeow:knowsAbout 阶级的来源。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/dimensionExplanatoryAbility|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The explanatory-ability dimension: whether the agent can produce an account others can follow and check — the seam to the solver-layer gmeow:explanatoryScore and gmeow:systematicity measurements, which feed this dimension but are never asserted as reasoned axioms."
msgstr "解释能力维度:智能体是否能产出他人可跟随并核查的陈述——通往求解器层 gmeow:explanatoryScore 与 gmeow:systematicity 度量的接缝,这些度量供养此维度,却绝不作为被推理的公理断言。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/dimensionMetacognition|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The metacognition dimension: whether the agent models its own competence, including the limits of its own knowledge. Reads the metacognition vocabulary's second-order posture — gmeow:awareOfNotKnowing, gmeow:epistemicSelfTrust, and reflection that can defeat one's own inference — as its subject."
msgstr "元认知维度:智能体是否对自身胜任力建模,包括自身知识的界限。它以元认知词汇的二阶姿态为其主题——gmeow:awareOfNotKnowing、gmeow:epistemicSelfTrust,以及能够击败自身推断的反思。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/dimensionProceduralCompetence|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The procedural-competence dimension: what the agent knows HOW to do — its working command of the subject. Read together with the transfer dimension, the source of the gmeow:hasMastered rung of the coarse knowledge ladder under a declared threshold."
msgstr "过程性胜任维度:智能体知道“如何做”——它对该主题的实操驾驭。与迁移维度一同读取,是粗知识阶梯在已声明阈值下 gmeow:hasMastered 阶级的来源。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/dimensionReliability|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The reliability dimension: how dependably an agent or engine reasons as a disposition, relative to a reference class (a task, domain, or distribution) and read from MANY results with their expected or observed outcomes — a metric over the series (accuracy, soundness-violation rate, recall, calibration, robustness) across a stated interval. Distinct from the single-run logic:ResultAssurance: a reliable reasoner may correctly return a contradiction verdict on contradictory input, and a completed internally-supported result may still be wrong, so reliability is never read from one result's assurance. The dimension design §Result assurance and reasoner reliability are distinct introduces alongside the eight factored dimensions."
msgstr "可靠性维度:一个智能体或引擎作为一种倾向推理得多么可靠,相对于一个参照类(一项任务、领域或分布),并从连同其预期或观测结果的众多结果中读取——是在一个所述区间上跨该系列的一个指标(准确率、可靠性违反率、召回率、校准、稳健性)。区别于单次运行的 logic:ResultAssurance:一个可靠的推理器可以在矛盾输入上正确返回矛盾裁决,而一个已完成且内部受支持的结果仍可能是错的,因此可靠性绝不从单个结果的保证中读取。维度设计 §Result assurance and reasoner reliability are distinct 将其与八个因子化维度一同引入。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DimensionThreshold|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "One row of a logic:LadderProjectionProfile: a logic:projectsLadderEdge ladder property paired with the logic:sourceDimension it reads and the minimum logic:thresholdLevel an assessment on that dimension must clear (by the logic:levelAtOrAbove order) for the edge to be emitted. The gmeow:hasMastered rung is the only one with two rows — procedural competence and transfer — both of which must clear, so mastery of one narrow task no longer implies broad command of a subject."
msgstr "一个 logic:LadderProjectionProfile 的一行:一个 logic:projectsLadderEdge 阶梯属性,配以它所读取的 logic:sourceDimension,以及该维度上的评估为发出该边必须跨过的最小 logic:thresholdLevel(依 logic:levelAtOrAbove 次序)。gmeow:hasMastered 阶级是唯一具有两行的——过程性胜任与迁移——二者都必须跨过,因此对一项狭窄任务的精通不再蕴涵对某主题的宽广驾驭。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/dimensionTransfer|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The transfer dimension: whether competence in one context carries to another — the axis a single ordinal ladder most conspicuously hides, since fluency in a narrow task says nothing about generalization. Read together with procedural competence, the source of the gmeow:hasMastered rung of the coarse knowledge ladder under a declared threshold."
msgstr "迁移维度:某一上下文中的胜任力是否延续到另一上下文——单一序数阶梯最显眼地掩盖的那个轴,因为在狭窄任务中的流利对泛化毫无所言。与过程性胜任一同读取,是粗知识阶梯在已声明阈值下 gmeow:hasMastered 阶级的来源。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/directType|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:focusGuard logic:directType ex:focus, ex:ReviewedClaim ."
msgstr "示例：ex:focusGuard logic:directType ex:focus, ex:ReviewedClaim ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/directType|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Direct type means an asserted rdf:type at the focus node, excluding subclass-derived membership."
msgstr "直接类型指焦点节点上断言的 rdf:type，排除由子类推导出的成员关系。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DischargeBoundedCorpus|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The discharge condition holding when the obligation is explicitly bounded to a declared corpus or mutation-test space and exhaustive checking within that bound is complete. Named in the closed set but not yet engine-backed. Wire value `bounded-corpus`."
msgstr "当义务被显式限定到一个已声明的语料或变异测试空间、且在该界限内的穷尽检查是完备的时成立的履行条件。已在封闭集合中命名,但尚未有引擎支撑。线值 `bounded-corpus`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DischargeCertifiedFragment|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The discharge condition holding when the check runs within a certified complete fragment (e.g. a Datalog stratum or EL profile over which the chase terminates and is complete). Named in the closed set but not yet engine-backed. Wire value `certified-fragment`."
msgstr "当检查在一个经认证的完备片段(例如一个 Datalog 层或一个追逐在其上终止且完备的 EL 剖面)内运行时成立的履行条件。已在封闭集合中命名,但尚未有引擎支撑。线值 `certified-fragment`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DischargeCondition|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The closed five-member value class of the logic:obligationDischargeCondition facet: the condition under which a logic:NonEntailmentObligation's absence-of-proof is conclusively checkable. Its individuals are logic:DischargeCertifiedFragment, logic:DischargeFiniteClosure, logic:DischargeSyntacticReachability, logic:DischargeConservativeExtension and logic:DischargeBoundedCorpus. The foundation engine wires logic:DischargeSyntacticReachability and logic:DischargeFiniteClosure; the other three are named but not yet engine-backed, so an obligation declaring one of them is a hard error rather than a silent pass. The set is closed, so a misspelt condition names no declared value and is rejected (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, §Typed formalization governance)."
msgstr "logic:obligationDischargeCondition 侧面的封闭五成员值类:一个 logic:NonEntailmentObligation 的无证明可被确定性核查所依据的条件。其个体为 logic:DischargeCertifiedFragment、logic:DischargeFiniteClosure、logic:DischargeSyntacticReachability、logic:DischargeConservativeExtension 与 logic:DischargeBoundedCorpus。基础引擎接线了 logic:DischargeSyntacticReachability 与 logic:DischargeFiniteClosure;其余三个已命名但尚未有引擎支撑,因此声明其中之一的义务是硬错误而非静默通过。该集合封闭,因此拼写错误的条件不命名任何已声明的取值并被拒绝(design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md,§Typed formalization governance)。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DischargeCondition|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "Use logic:DischargeFiniteClosure when a completed finite chase makes absence of the forbidden predicate decidable."
msgstr "当已完成的有限 chase 使被禁谓词的缺失变得可判定时，采用 logic:DischargeFiniteClosure。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DischargeConservativeExtension|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The discharge condition holding when a conservative-extension proof establishes the added axioms cannot introduce the forbidden conclusion. Named in the closed set but not yet engine-backed. Wire value `conservative-extension`."
msgstr "当一个保守扩张证明确立所添加的公理不能引入被禁止的结论时成立的履行条件。已在封闭集合中命名,但尚未有引擎支撑。线值 `conservative-extension`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DischargeFiniteClosure|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The discharge condition holding when a finite materialized derivation graph is available and complete: the obligation is discharged by checking the forbidden predicate is absent from that closure. Engine-backed (the foundation chase over an adversarial fixture). Wire value `finite-closure`."
msgstr "当一个有限的、已物化的推导图可用且完备时成立的履行条件:通过核查被禁止的谓词不在该闭包中来履行义务。有引擎支撑(在对抗性夹具上的基础追逐)。线值 `finite-closure`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/dischargeObligation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates an individual to an anti-rigid type it instantiates contingently, carrying the standing obligation to construct or cite a world of existence in which the individual lacks that type (the anti-rigidity witness). The instance-level diagnostic the anti-rigidity lowering emits under the witness-obligation policy (the default; LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md §Anti-rigidity needs a witness policy): for an individual x typed by an anti-rigid Role or Phase T in a world, a logic:dischargeObligation fact is entailed in that world. It is an obligation, NOT a violation — anti-rigid instantiation is licensed on the promise that the counter-world is satisfiable on demand (its construction happens on demand); the lighter schema-only policy emits nothing instance-level, the stricter witness-required policy emits logic:witnessRequiredViolation instead. Like the other derived diagnostics it is never asserted by hand."
msgstr "将一个个体关联到它偶然实例化的一个反刚性类型,携带常设义务,以构造或引用一个该个体缺乏此类型的存在世界(反刚性见证)。反刚性下降在见证义务策略(默认;LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md §Anti-rigidity needs a witness policy)下发出的实例级诊断:对于在某世界中被反刚性 Role 或 Phase T 类型化的个体 x,一个 logic:dischargeObligation 事实在该世界中被蕴涵。它是一项义务,而非一项违反——反刚性实例化在“反世界可按需满足”(其构造按需发生)的承诺上被许可;较轻的仅模式策略在实例级不发出任何东西,较严的要求见证策略则代之以发出 logic:witnessRequiredViolation。如同其他导出诊断,它绝不由手工断言。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/dischargesSectionObligation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:SectionAcceptanceWitness to the section obligation (an IRI) its executed get/put round-trip discharges. Domain logic:SectionAcceptanceWitness (stated in prose). Exactly the edge whose absence makes the discharge unfalsifiable: a section witness that names no obligation asserts a round-trip without saying which law it satisfies."
msgstr "将一个 logic:SectionAcceptanceWitness 关联到其已执行的 get/put 往返所履行的截面义务(一个 IRI)。定义域 logic:SectionAcceptanceWitness(以散文陈述)。恰恰是其缺席会使履行不可证伪的那条边:一个不命名任何义务的截面见证断言了一次往返,却未说出它满足哪条法则。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DischargeSyntacticReachability|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The discharge condition holding when a syntactic dependency/reachability analysis over the rule heads shows the forbidden predicate is unreachable — no rule head unifies with it, directly or through any chain of rule applications. Engine-backed (reachability over the foundation rule strata). Wire value `syntactic-reachability`."
msgstr "当对规则头进行的句法依赖/可达性分析表明被禁止的谓词不可达时成立的履行条件——没有任何规则头与它合一,无论是直接地还是经由任何规则应用链。有引擎支撑(在基础规则层上的可达性)。线值 `syntactic-reachability`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DischargeVerdict|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The closed three-value class of the logic:obligationDischargeVerdict facet: the result an obligation check returns. Its individuals are logic:ObligationDischarged, logic:ObligationUnknown (carried forward, never 'proved absent') and logic:ObligationViolated. The set is closed, so a misspelt verdict names no declared value and is rejected (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, §Typed formalization governance)."
msgstr "logic:obligationDischargeVerdict 侧面的封闭三值类:一次义务检查返回的结果。其个体为 logic:ObligationDischarged、logic:ObligationUnknown(向前携带,绝非“已证明缺席”)与 logic:ObligationViolated。该集合封闭,因此拼写错误的裁决不命名任何已声明的取值并被拒绝(design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md,§Typed formalization governance)。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DischargeVerdict|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A bounded check that exhausts its declared corpus without deriving the forbidden predicate returns logic:ObligationDischarged."
msgstr "一个有界检查若耗尽其声明的语料而未推导出被禁谓词，则返回 logic:ObligationDischarged。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Discipline|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A named OntoUML structural discipline a class can violate: the closed vocabulary of anti-patterns the foundation lowering checks (stereotype cardinality, identity overlap, free role, mixed rigidity, relator completeness). Its named individuals are the labels a logic:violation fact points at; the set is closed so a misspelt label names no declared discipline and is rejected rather than silently accepted."
msgstr "一个类可以违反的具名 OntoUML 结构纪律:基础下降所检查的反模式的封闭词汇(刻板印象基数、同一性重叠、自由角色、混合刚性、关系子完备性)。其具名个体是一个 logic:violation 事实所指向的标签;该集合封闭,因此拼写错误的标签不命名任何已声明的纪律,并被拒绝而非静默接受。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Disjoint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The negative pole of the correspondence-relation lattice: source and view share no instances, an asserted non-alignment. Lowers to owl:disjointWith. Distinct from the mereological relation logic:disjoint (two entities sharing no part); this records that two aligned patterns are deliberately kept apart."
msgstr "对应关系格的负极:源与视图不共享任何实例,一种被断言的非对齐。下降为 owl:disjointWith。区别于部分学关系 logic:disjoint(两个不共享任何部分的实体);此项记录两个已对齐模式被刻意分开。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/disjoint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Mereological disjointness: two entities share no part — the negation of logic:overlaps. A primitive notion of profiled mereology, settled (alongside logic:overlaps) before weak supplementation is stated, so logic:WeakSupplementation is never applied to wholes for which overlap is undefined. The 'another part disjoint from the first' clause of weak supplementation is read against this relation (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "部分学不相交:两个实体不共享任何部分——logic:overlaps 的否定。剖面化部分学的一个原始概念,在陈述弱补充之前(连同 logic:overlaps)即已确定,因此 logic:WeakSupplementation 绝不施加于重叠未定义的整体。弱补充中“与第一者不相交的另一部分”一句是针对此关系来读的(design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md,typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons 章节)。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/disjointWith|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:Continuant logic:disjointWith ex:Occurrent ."
msgstr "示例：ex:Continuant logic:disjointWith ex:Occurrent ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/disjointWith|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The assertion is symmetric at the class-extension level even when written in one direction."
msgstr "即使仅按单一方向书写，该断言在类外延层面也是对称的。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DisjunctiveGoal|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:GoalExpressionKind for a goal satisfied when ANY of its logic:operand sub-expressions is satisfied. The disjunctive combinator of the goal algebra; co-equal counterpart of logic:ConjunctiveGoal."
msgstr "用于当其 logic:operand 子表达式中任意一个被满足时即被满足的目标的 logic:GoalExpressionKind。目标代数的析取组合子;logic:ConjunctiveGoal 的同等对应物。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Disjunctive|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The residue shape tag for a formula in which a disjunction (logic:or) appears — a choice the single determinate body of a Horn rule cannot express. Disclosed when a Horn-fragment target carries such a formula as flagged unsupported residue."
msgstr "用于其中出现析取(logic:or)的公式的残余形状标记——一个 Horn 规则单一确定的体无法表达的选择。当一个 Horn 片段目标携带这样一条公式作为被标记的不受支持残余时予以披露。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Disposition|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A bearer-held tendency, power, or liability to manifest events of a characteristic type when triggered — a fragility, a solubility, a hazard's potential to harm — which remains fully real even while it never manifests. gUFO has no Disposition class and models such tendencies as a gufo:IntrinsicMode; logic: subsumes that by carrying the disposition as first-class, so an unmanifested tendency needs no counterfactual reification. A logic:Mode whose manifestations are logic:Events of the characteristic type (stated in prose, not as a subclass edge); the bearer relation is asserted with a domain property (Principle 5), never gufo:inheresIn."
msgstr "一个由承载者持有的、当被触发时显现某种特征类型事件的倾向、能力或倾向性——一种脆性、一种可溶性、一种危害致损的潜能——即便它从不显现也仍然完全真实。gUFO 没有 Disposition 类,而将此类倾向建模为 gufo:IntrinsicMode;logic: 通过将此倾向作为一等公民承载而涵盖之,因此一个未显现的倾向无需任何反事实具体化。一个 logic:Mode,其显现是该特征类型的 logic:Events(以散文陈述,而非作为子类边);承载者关系以一个域属性断言(原则 5),绝不用 gufo:inheresIn。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DistanceAnnotation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The external-relation annotation dimension for a metric or non-metric distance. A smaller or larger distance may affect provider order, but distance is not epistemic confidence."
msgstr "用于度量或非度量距离的外部关系注记维度。较小或较大的距离可能影响提供者次序,但距离并非认识论置信度。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/distinctBody|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment"
msgid "Inequality body guard of a logic:Rule. Default-absent: a rule that needs no inequality carries no logic:distinctBody, so the existing corpus is byte-identical."
msgstr "logic:Rule 的不等式体部守卫。默认缺省：无需不等式的规则不携带 logic:distinctBody，因此现有语料库在字节层面完全一致。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/distinctBody|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Rule to an inequality body guard: a reified node carrying rdf:subject and rdf:object (two rule variables, and — unlike logic:body — no rdf:predicate) that must bind to DISTINCT values for the rule to fire, projecting to the Datalog inequality constraint ?A != ?B. Parallel to logic:negatedBody as an additive rule-structural surface: it lets a rule detect 'at least two distinct values' (e.g. a class carrying more than one stereotype, or a relator mediating two distinct relata) that set-semantic Datalog cannot otherwise express. An inequality guard introduces no negative dependency edge, so it leaves a rule's stratification class unchanged."
msgstr "将一个 logic:Rule 关联到一个不等式体守卫:一个携带 rdf:subject 与 rdf:object(两个规则变量,且——不同于 logic:body——没有 rdf:predicate)的具体化节点,它们必须绑定到不同的取值,规则方可触发,投影为 Datalog 不等式约束 ?A != ?B。作为一种加性的规则结构表面,与 logic:negatedBody 平行:它使一条规则能够检测“至少两个不同取值”(例如一个携带多于一个刻板印象的类,或一个中介两个不同 relata 的关系子),这是集合语义的 Datalog 否则无法表达的。一个不等式守卫不引入任何负依赖边,因此它使一条规则的分层类保持不变。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/distinctnessRole|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:RelatumDistinctnessAssertion to one of the two roles that must bind distinct values on a focus node. Exactly two are asserted per record; the native coherence gate raises a violation when both roles bind the same value on one focus node. Domain logic:RelatumDistinctnessAssertion; two-valued."
msgstr "将一个 logic:RelatumDistinctnessAssertion 关联到必须在一个焦点节点上绑定不同取值的两个角色之一。每条记录恰好断言两个;当两个角色在一个焦点节点上绑定相同取值时,原生一致性门闸引发一项违反。定义域 logic:RelatumDistinctnessAssertion;二值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/distinctnessTarget|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:RelatumDistinctnessAssertion to the class whose focus nodes it constrains (the relator class). Read together with logic:distinctnessRole, it tells the native coherence gate which class bears the mutual-inequality condition. Domain logic:RelatumDistinctnessAssertion; single-valued."
msgstr "将 logic:RelatumDistinctnessAssertion 关联到其约束焦点节点的类（关系者类）。与 logic:distinctnessRole 一同解读时，它告知原生一致性门哪个类承载相互不等条件。定义域为 logic:RelatumDistinctnessAssertion；单值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/domain|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:memberOf logic:domain ex:Agent ."
msgstr "示例：ex:memberOf logic:domain ex:Agent ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/domain|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Multiple domain axioms are conjunctive entailments, not alternative allowed subject types."
msgstr "多条定义域公理是合取式的蕴涵，而非可供选择的许可主语类型。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DownwardConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The canonical relational construct of holonic governance: the downward (governing) face of a holon, a typed directed constraint a whole imposes on a named proper part — the whole limits which roles or states the part may take. This is downward CONSTRAINT, never material causation: the governing whole bounds the part's permissible state, it does not produce or compose the part. Reified with the role properties logic:constraintWhole, logic:constraintTarget, logic:constraintState, logic:constraintRegime, and logic:constraintOverride, and the engine derives its logic:constraintVerdict (logic:ConstraintBinding, logic:ConstraintOverridden, or logic:ConstraintUnknown). The constraint is structured and NON-TRANSITIVE by default (ME9): it applies to the explicitly named target and says nothing automatic about the target's own proper parts — there is no rule cascading the constraint down logic:properPartOf, exactly as no rule propagates logic:bearsProperty down it (mirroring logic:EmergenceAssessment / logic:HolonicPosition; design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "全体论治理的规范关系构造：一个全体的向下（治理）面，即一个整体对指定的真部分施加的类型化定向约束——整体限制该部分可承担的角色或状态。这是向下约束，绝非物质因果：治理整体限定部分的许可状态，它不产生也不构成该部分。通过角色属性 logic:constraintWhole、logic:constraintTarget、logic:constraintState、logic:constraintRegime 和 logic:constraintOverride 予以具体化，引擎据此导出其 logic:constraintVerdict（logic:ConstraintBinding、logic:ConstraintOverridden 或 logic:ConstraintUnknown）。该约束默认是结构化且非传递的（ME9）：它作用于显式命名的目标，对目标自身的真部分不作任何自动断言——没有规则沿 logic:properPartOf 向下级联该约束，正如没有规则沿其向下传播 logic:bearsProperty（映照 logic:EmergenceAssessment / logic:HolonicPosition；design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons 小节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/doxasticallyAccessible|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The typed doxastic accessibility relation between gmeow:EpistemicContexts — what an agent's beliefs hold accessible. It need not be reflexive (an agent may believe a falsehood); this character is documented in prose, not asserted as an OWL characteristic, matching the kernel convention. logic:accessibleFrom is its generic superproperty in prose only — NOT asserted rdfs:subPropertyOf — so the bare superproperty licenses no cross-type entailment and what is believed never leaks into what is true."
msgstr "gmeow:EpistemicContexts 之间的类型化信念可达关系——即一个主体的信念所认为可达者。它无需自反（一个主体可能相信一个谬误）；此特征以散文记录，而非断言为 OWL 特征，符合内核惯例。logic:accessibleFrom 仅在散文中是其通用超属性——并未断言 rdfs:subPropertyOf——因此裸超属性不授予任何跨类型蕴涵，被相信之物也绝不渗漏为为真之物。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/editionOfFunctionality|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Asserts on the canonical carrier that gmeow:editionOf is functional: an edition editions exactly one work, as its skos:definition states."
msgstr "在规范载体上断言 gmeow:editionOf 是函数性的：一个版本恰好版化一部作品，正如其 skos:definition 所述。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/effect|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ActionSchema to the change it introduces, expressed as the supersession primitives of the transaction layer (ins/del), NEVER as physical erasure — executing an occurrence is the elementary update whose ins/del a transaction path records. Domain logic:ActionSchema (stated in prose). One of the eight action-theory facets."
msgstr "将 logic:ActionSchema 关联到它所引入的变更，以事务层的取代原语（ins/del）表达，绝非物理擦除——执行一次发生即是其 ins/del 由事务路径记录的基本更新。定义域为 logic:ActionSchema（以散文陈述）。行动理论八个侧面之一。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ElementaryUpdate|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A single Transaction-Logic state-transition primitive over a path of WorldStore snapshots. Its two concrete forms are `ins(F)`, which makes a support hold in the successor state, and `del(F)`, which retires one active support in the successor state without deleting the historical assertion. Conflicting same-fact updates are resolved by the declared entrenchment ordering."
msgstr "在 WorldStore 快照路径上的单个事务逻辑状态转移原语。其两种具体形式为 `ins(F)`，使某支持在后继状态中成立；以及 `del(F)`，在后继状态中退役一个活动支持而不删除历史断言。同一事实的冲突更新由所声明的固着序解决。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/EmergenceAssessment|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The canonical relational construct of emergence: a tri-valued assessment of whether a whole's property is reducible to its proper parts, always made relative to a declared logic:ReductionTheory. Emergence is assessed, never asserted — the assessment is reified with the role properties logic:assessmentWhole, logic:assessmentProperty, and logic:assessmentReductionTheory, and the engine derives its logic:assessmentVerdict (logic:Aggregate, logic:Emergent, or logic:EmergenceUnknown). Failure to derive a property from the parts under one theory is not proof of irreducibility: because the assessment records the theory it is relative to, a later, stronger theory can overturn an logic:Emergent verdict without contradiction. The convenient unary reading 'P is emergent' is the lossy projection of this assessment, exactly as logic:Holon projects logic:HolonicPosition (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "涌现的规范关系构造：对一个整体的属性是否可还原为其真部分的三值评估，且始终相对于一个所声明的 logic:ReductionTheory 而作出。涌现是被评估的，绝非被断言——该评估通过角色属性 logic:assessmentWhole、logic:assessmentProperty 和 logic:assessmentReductionTheory 予以具体化，引擎据此导出其 logic:assessmentVerdict（logic:Aggregate、logic:Emergent 或 logic:EmergenceUnknown）。在某一理论下未能从部分导出某属性并不构成不可还原性的证明：因为该评估记录了它所相对的理论，一个更晚出、更强的理论可以无矛盾地推翻一个 logic:Emergent 裁决。便捷的一元读法「P 是涌现的」是此评估的有损投影，恰如 logic:Holon 投影 logic:HolonicPosition（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons 小节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/EmergenceUnknown|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The emergence-verdict value when the reducibility question cannot be posed: the whole bears the property under assessment, but the logic:EmergenceAssessment declares no logic:ReductionTheory (no logic:assessmentReductionTheory), so neither a part-reconstruction (logic:Aggregate) nor a theory-relative non-reduction (logic:Emergent) can be derived. ME9's first-class third value, kept distinct from logic:Aggregate and logic:Emergent so that a genuinely unclassifiable assessment is never silently read as emergence — failure-to-derive is not irreducibility, and a theory-free assessment is unknown, not emergent (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "当可还原性问题无法被提出时的涌现裁决值：整体承载受评估的属性，但 logic:EmergenceAssessment 未声明任何 logic:ReductionTheory（无 logic:assessmentReductionTheory），因而既无法导出一次部分重构（logic:Aggregate），也无法导出一次相对于理论的非还原（logic:Emergent）。ME9 的一等第三值，与 logic:Aggregate 和 logic:Emergent 保持区分，从而使一个真正无法归类的评估绝不被默默读作涌现——未能导出并非不可还原，而一个无理论的评估是未知的，而非涌现的（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons 小节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/EmergenceVerdict|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The closed class of emergence-assessment outcomes: the tri-valued result an logic:EmergenceAssessment receives via logic:assessmentVerdict. Its three named individuals are logic:Aggregate (part-reducible under the declared theory), logic:Emergent (borne by the whole but not part-reducible under that theory), and logic:EmergenceUnknown (the reducibility question cannot be posed). The set is closed, so a misspelt verdict names no declared value and is rejected rather than silently accepted, mirroring logic:MereologyConstraint (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "涌现评估结果的封闭类：一个 logic:EmergenceAssessment 经由 logic:assessmentVerdict 所接收的三值结果。其三个命名个体为 logic:Aggregate（在所声明理论下可还原为部分）、logic:Emergent（由整体承载但在该理论下不可还原为部分）以及 logic:EmergenceUnknown（可还原性问题无法被提出）。该集合是封闭的，因而一个拼写错误的裁决不指称任何所声明的值，会被拒绝而非默默接受，映照 logic:MereologyConstraint（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons 小节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Emergent|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The emergence-verdict value for a genuinely emergent whole property: under the declared logic:ReductionTheory of an logic:EmergenceAssessment, the whole bears the property but it is not reconstructible from the parts — the theory does not carry it in its logic:reductionBasis, or no proper part bears it — so the property does not propagate down logic:properPartOf and is not entailed by the parts' properties. The verdict is strictly theory-relative: it is reached by negation-as-failure over the aggregate derivation, never as a bare 'unflagged' default, and failure to derive under this theory is not proof of irreducibility — a stronger logic:ReductionTheory may reduce the same property under a different assessment without contradiction. Contrast logic:Aggregate and logic:EmergenceUnknown (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "针对一个真正涌现的整体属性的涌现裁决值：在一个 logic:EmergenceAssessment 所声明的 logic:ReductionTheory 之下，整体承载该属性，但它无法从部分重构——该理论未将其纳入其 logic:reductionBasis，或没有任何真部分承载它——因此该属性不沿 logic:properPartOf 向下传播，也不由各部分的属性所蕴涵。此裁决严格相对于理论：它经由对聚合导出的失败即否定而达成，绝非作为一个裸的「未标记」缺省，且在此理论下未能导出并非不可还原性的证明——一个更强的 logic:ReductionTheory 可在另一次评估下无矛盾地还原同一属性。与 logic:Aggregate 及 logic:EmergenceUnknown 相对照（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons 小节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Endurant|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A continuant: an individual that persists through time and is wholly present at each moment of its existence, enduring through change rather than unfolding through it. The counterpart of gufo:Endurant and the bearer side of the endurant/perdurant divide; contrast logic:Perdurant, which has temporal parts. Substantials and aspects are both endurants."
msgstr "一个延续者：一个贯穿时间而持存、在其存在的每一刻皆完整在场的个体，是历经变化而非在变化中展开者。gufo:Endurant 的对应物，是延续者/持续者划分的承载一侧；与具有时间部分的 logic:Perdurant 相对照。实体者与方面皆为延续者。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/EndurantType|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A logic:Type whose instances are logic:Endurants — the type whose extension (via logic:instanceOf) is drawn from continuants. The counterpart of gufo:EndurantType; the type-of-endurants branch under which the sortal and non-sortal foundation meta-types (logic:Kind, logic:Phase, logic:Role, logic:Category, …) ultimately fall. Stated in prose, not as a subclass edge. Contrast logic:Event and logic:Situation, which carry gUFO's EventType/SituationType roles per the down-projection."
msgstr "一个其实例为 logic:Endurants 的 logic:Type——即其外延（经由 logic:instanceOf）取自延续者的类型。gufo:EndurantType 的对应物；是延续者类型分支，可分类与非可分类的基础元类型（logic:Kind、logic:Phase、logic:Role、logic:Category、……）最终归属于此。以散文陈述，而非作为一条子类边。与 logic:Event 和 logic:Situation 相对照，后二者按下向投影承载 gUFO 的 EventType/SituationType 角色。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/EngineCapability|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A declared capability of a reasoning engine — the executional ability an actor must hold to execute a logic:ActionSchema, named as the object of logic:capability. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:EngineCapability only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "推理引擎的一项声明能力——一个行动者为执行 logic:ActionSchema 所必须持有的执行性能力，作为 logic:capability 的宾语被命名。它并非某个更宽、更窄或仅相关构造的可互换别名；仅在所陈述的同一性与验证条件下使用 logic:EngineCapability。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/engineContractDescriptorHash|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The framed-BLAKE3 content address computed over the WHOLE logic:EngineContract descriptor — the engine identity and version, the backward-source digest (logic:backwardSourceHash), the forward-contract digest (logic:forwardContractHash), and every supported preset with its logic:decidabilityClass. This is THE value a consumer pins at load: any change to any covered input moves it, and the projected contract's subject IRI is content-addressed on it. Single-valued. Domain logic:EngineContract (stated in prose). NON-CONFLATION: it pins the engine SOURCE identity (which engine could decide answers), NOT a single invocation — a per-query logic:contractHash on a logic:ReasoningResult pins the semantics/resource inputs of ONE dispatch, and two queries under different presets or budgets share this descriptor while carrying different per-query contracts, so recording 'answer X was minted under engine Y' needs both. Authored canonically in crates/logic (Rust); a lossy documentation projection (Principle 17)."
msgstr "在整个 logic:EngineContract 描述符之上计算的 framed-BLAKE3 内容地址——包括引擎同一性与版本、后向源摘要（logic:backwardSourceHash）、前向合约摘要（logic:forwardContractHash），以及每一个受支持的预设及其 logic:decidabilityClass。这是消费者在加载时锚定的那个值：任何受覆盖输入的任何改动都会使其变动，而被投影合约的主语 IRI 即以其为内容地址。单值。定义域为 logic:EngineContract（以散文陈述）。防混同：它锚定引擎的源同一性（哪个引擎能够裁决答案），而非单次调用——一个 logic:ReasoningResult 上的逐查询 logic:contractHash 锚定一次派发的语义/资源输入，而在不同预设或预算下的两次查询共享此描述符却承载不同的逐查询合约，故记录「答案 X 是在引擎 Y 下铸造的」需要二者兼备。在 crates/logic（Rust）中规范撰写；一个有损文档投影（原则 17）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/EngineContract|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The self-describing, content-addressed identity of the WHOLE gmeow-logic runtime engine — the runtime pin a signed-ledger consumer records at load and later refuses a drifted answer against. One descriptor covers BOTH engine directions at once: the forward EL/DL/RL chase reasoning-contract identity (logic:forwardContractHash) and the backward goal-resolution source surface (logic:backwardSourceHash), together with the engine identity and version (logic:engine) and the per-preset capability manifest (logic:supportedProfile, each supported logic:ReasoningPreset carrying its logic:decidabilityClass guarantee). Its own content address is logic:engineContractDescriptorHash — the single value a consumer pins; the projected instance's subject IRI is itself content-addressed on that hash, so there is no second copy of the identity that could drift. Conceptual sibling of the coherence-evidence family (logic:CoherenceCertificate / logic:CoherenceCheckAttestation): each is a content-addressed, to_nquads-projectable evidence object a consumer folds into its own (signed) ledger AS DATA — but a coherence outcome scopes ONE completed check over a bundle, whereas an engine contract pins the ENGINE that would decide any such check, and so is negotiated once at load rather than issued per run. DISTINCT from logic:ReasoningResult and its per-invocation logic:contractHash: a result records what one query decided, the engine contract records which engine was entitled to decide it. Authored canonically in crates/logic (Rust, crates/logic/src/runtime.rs); this is a lossy documentation projection (Principle 17). Normative in design/LOGIC-RUNTIME.md, §The compiler/runtime split."
msgstr "整个 gmeow-logic 运行时引擎的自描述、内容寻址同一性——即一个签名账本消费者在加载时记录、日后据以拒绝已漂移答案的运行时锚钉。单个描述符一次性覆盖引擎的两个方向：前向 EL/DL/RL 追逐推理合约同一性（logic:forwardContractHash）与后向目标求解源面（logic:backwardSourceHash），连同引擎同一性与版本（logic:engine）以及逐预设能力清单（logic:supportedProfile，每个受支持的 logic:ReasoningPreset 均携带其 logic:decidabilityClass 保证）。其自身内容地址为 logic:engineContractDescriptorHash——消费者锚定的那个单一值；被投影实例的主语 IRI 本身即以该散列为内容地址，故不存在可能漂移的同一性第二副本。它是一致性证据族（logic:CoherenceCertificate / logic:CoherenceCheckAttestation）的概念同胞：每一个都是内容寻址、可经 to_nquads 投影的证据对象，消费者将其作为数据折入自己的（签名）账本——但一致性结果的范围是对一个捆绑包所完成的一次检查，而引擎合约锚定的是会裁决任何此类检查的引擎，故其在加载时协商一次，而非每次运行签发。与 logic:ReasoningResult 及其逐调用 logic:contractHash 有别：结果记录一次查询裁决了什么，引擎合约记录哪个引擎有资格裁决它。在 crates/logic（Rust，crates/logic/src/runtime.rs）中规范撰写；这是一个有损文档投影（原则 17）。规范见 design/LOGIC-RUNTIME.md，§The compiler/runtime split。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/engine|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The engine identity + version that produced a logic:ReasoningResult, or — reusing the same property — that a logic:EngineContract pins as the engine entitled to produce one. Single-valued. Domain logic:ReasoningResult or logic:EngineContract (stated in prose)."
msgstr "产生某个 logic:ReasoningResult 的引擎同一性 + 版本，或——复用同一属性——某个 logic:EngineContract 锚定为有资格产生该结果的引擎。单值。定义域为 logic:ReasoningResult 或 logic:EngineContract（以散文陈述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/EntrenchmentRevision|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The revision-policy value under which conflicting information is absorbed by an AGM-style belief revision driven by a declared epistemic-entrenchment ordering: the least entrenched beliefs are surrendered to restore consistency. Contrast logic:MonotonicRevision (nothing retracted) and logic:TruthMaintenanceRevision (justification-tracked retraction)."
msgstr "修订策略值，在其下冲突信息由一次 AGM 式的信念修订所吸纳，该修订由一个所声明的认知固着序驱动：最不固着的信念被舍弃以恢复一致性。与 logic:MonotonicRevision（不撤回任何内容）及 logic:TruthMaintenanceRevision（按论证追踪的撤回）相对照。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Enumeration|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:trafficLightState a logic:Enumeration ; logic:oneOf ( ex:red ex:amber ex:green ) ."
msgstr "示例：ex:trafficLightState a logic:Enumeration ; logic:oneOf ( ex:red ex:amber ex:green ) ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Enumeration|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Enumeration denotes exactly the listed members; list order does not imply preference or rank."
msgstr "枚举恰好指称所列出的成员；列表顺序并不暗示偏好或等级。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/epistemicallyPossible|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The typed alethic accessibility relation between logic:PossibleWorlds — a world is epistemically (alethically) accessible from another. logic:accessibleFrom is its generic superproperty in prose only: it is NOT asserted rdfs:subPropertyOf logic:accessibleFrom, because the generic superproperty licenses no cross-type entailment and a subproperty edge would manufacture exactly that inference. The modal operators are the standard translation over THIS relation, never over a blurred union of accessibility relations. It asserts no OWL characteristic; its logical character is documented in prose, matching the kernel convention."
msgstr "logic:PossibleWorlds 之间的类型化真势可达关系——一个世界从另一个世界在认知（真势）上可达。logic:accessibleFrom 仅在散文中是其通用超属性：它并未被断言为 rdfs:subPropertyOf logic:accessibleFrom，因为该通用超属性不授予任何跨类型蕴涵，而一条子属性边恰会制造出那种推理。模态算子是在此关系之上的标准翻译，绝不在可达关系的模糊并集之上进行。它不断言任何 OWL 特征；其逻辑特征以散文记录，符合内核惯例。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/EpistemicConfidenceAnnotation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The external-relation annotation dimension used only when the provider genuinely supplies epistemic confidence. Similarity, rank, distance, and persistence values never project to this individual implicitly."
msgstr "仅在提供方确实供给认知置信度时才使用的外部关系注解维度。相似度、排名、距离和持久性的值绝不隐式投影到此个体。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/EpistemicFramework|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The knowledge, justification, and argumentation framework: doxastic accessibility (logic:doxasticallyAccessible), knowing-that that is factive only relative to a world and an epistemic standard, evidential warrant (logic:evidenceStrength), and defeasible argumentation resolved under a declared logic:ArgumentationSemantics with typed attacks. Factivity stays honest in a paraconsistent, world-indexed setting — knowing P in a world entails P in that world, never globally (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the argumentation-and-epistemic-standards section)."
msgstr "知识、辩护与论证框架：信念可达性（logic:doxasticallyAccessible）、仅相对于一个世界和一个认知标准才为事实性的知道—其为真、证据担保（logic:evidenceStrength），以及在一个所声明的、带类型化攻击的 logic:ArgumentationSemantics 下裁决的可废止论证。事实性在一个次协调、按世界索引的设定中保持诚实——在某个世界中知道 P 蕴涵 P 在该世界中成立，而绝不全局成立（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，argumentation-and-epistemic-standards 小节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/EqualityPolicy|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The facet value class of the equality facet: when two terms are taken to denote one entity. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract. Its individuals range from RDF equality through explicit (asserted) equality to an optional unique-name assumption."
msgstr "相等侧面的侧面值类：何时将两个词项视为指称同一个实体。在 ReasoningContract 上单值。其个体从 RDF 相等，经由显式（被断言的）相等，直至一个可选的唯一名称假设。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/equalityPolicy|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to the logic:EqualityPolicy it selects — when two terms denote one entity. Single-valued on the contract. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:EqualityPolicy (stated in prose, matching the module's convention)."
msgstr "将 logic:ReasoningContract 关联到它所选定的 logic:EqualityPolicy——何时两个词项指称同一个实体。在合约上单值。定义域为 logic:ReasoningContract，值域为 logic:EqualityPolicy（以散文陈述，符合模块惯例）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/equivalentClass|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:EveningStar logic:equivalentClass ex:MorningStarDescription ."
msgstr "示例：ex:EveningStar logic:equivalentClass ex:MorningStarDescription ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/equivalentClass|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Equivalence entails both subsumption directions and therefore requires stronger evidence than a bridge relation."
msgstr "等价蕴涵两个方向的包容关系，因此比桥接关系需要更强的证据。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/equivalentProperty|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:hasBiologicalMother logic:equivalentProperty ex:biologicalMotherRelation ."
msgstr "示例：ex:hasBiologicalMother logic:equivalentProperty ex:biologicalMotherRelation ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/equivalentProperty|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Equivalent properties entail identical ordered subject-object pair extensions."
msgstr "等价属性蕴涵相同的有序主语-宾语对外延。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Equiv|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The top of the correspondence-relation lattice: the source pattern and the view pattern denote one and the same extension. Lowers to sssom:exactMatch and (when the logic:MorphismClass and logic:LawClaim set support it) owl:equivalentClass; the strongest claim, never licensed for a commitment-shifting bridge."
msgstr "对应关系格的顶端：源模式与视图模式指称唯一且相同的外延。下沉为 sssom:exactMatch，并（当 logic:MorphismClass 与 logic:LawClaim 集合支持时）下沉为 owl:equivalentClass；这是最强的主张，绝不容许用于承诺迁移的桥。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/evaluatedAgainst|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:GoalEvaluation to the situation or world it is judged against. Domain logic:GoalEvaluation (stated in prose); the range ranges over a situation (logic:Situation) or a world/context, left open in this standalone module. One of the subjects in the identifying tuple of an evaluation."
msgstr "将 logic:GoalEvaluation 关联到据以评判它的情境或世界。定义域为 logic:GoalEvaluation（以散文陈述）；其值域覆盖一个情境（logic:Situation）或一个世界/语境，在此独立模块中保持开放。评估的标识元组中的主体之一。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/evaluatesGoal|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:GoalEvaluation to the gmeow:Goal it judges. Domain logic:GoalEvaluation, range gmeow:Goal (stated in prose). One of the subjects in the identifying tuple of an evaluation (goal, situation/world, evaluator, time, criterion)."
msgstr "将 logic:GoalEvaluation 关联到它所评判的 gmeow:Goal。定义域为 logic:GoalEvaluation，值域为 gmeow:Goal（以散文陈述）。评估的标识元组（目标、情境/世界、评估者、时间、准则）中的主体之一。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/EvaluationCompleted|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:EvaluationStatus value for a run that reached its natural end on the request — a conclusive evaluation. Wire value `completed`."
msgstr "针对在请求上抵达其自然终点的运行的 logic:EvaluationStatus 值——一次决定性的评估。传输值 `completed`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/evaluationCriterion|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:GoalEvaluation to the criterion applied in reaching its judgment — the standard against which satisfaction, feasibility, and the quantities are read. Domain logic:GoalEvaluation (stated in prose). One of the subjects in the identifying tuple of an evaluation; two evaluations differing only in criterion are distinct records."
msgstr "将 logic:GoalEvaluation 关联到达成其判断时所施用的准则——据以读取满足度、可行性及各数量的标准。定义域为 logic:GoalEvaluation（以散文陈述）。评估的标识元组中的主体之一；仅在准则上相异的两次评估是不同的记录。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/evaluationEvaluator|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:GoalEvaluation to the vantage holding the judgment — the evaluator the record is attributed to. Domain logic:GoalEvaluation (stated in prose). Aligns with gmeow:accordingTo: a goal evaluation is a vantage-indexed claim, never a global verdict, so two evaluators who disagree are two coexisting evaluations rather than one elected winner (Principle 9). One of the subjects in the identifying tuple of an evaluation."
msgstr "将 logic:GoalEvaluation 关联到持有该判断的视角——记录所归属的评估者。定义域为 logic:GoalEvaluation（以散文陈述）。与 gmeow:accordingTo 对齐：目标评估是一个按视角索引的主张，绝非全局裁决，因而两个意见相左的评估者构成两个共存的评估，而非一个被选定的胜者（原则 9）。评估的标识元组中的主体之一。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/EvaluationMode|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The closed value class of the evaluation strategy a logic:ReasoningProgram selects via logic:evaluationMode — which procedure resolves the SAME authored clause set. Its sole individual today is logic:BackwardEvaluation, the goal-directed SLG-WFS backward-resolution strategy; the set is closed and a misspelt or otherwise-unrecognized value is rejected. A forward chase over the identical clause shape is a future member of this same closed set, not a competing program kind, which is why evaluation strategy is carried as a selector value rather than a class distinction on logic:ReasoningProgram."
msgstr "一个 logic:ReasoningProgram 经由 logic:evaluationMode 所选定的评估策略的封闭值类——即哪种程序求解同一套已撰写的子句集。其今日唯一的个体是 logic:BackwardEvaluation，即目标导向的 SLG-WFS 后向求解策略；该集合是封闭的，拼写错误或以其他方式无法识别的值会被拒绝。在相同子句形态之上的一次前向追逐是这同一封闭集合的未来成员，而非一种相竞争的程序种类，这正是评估策略被作为选择器值而非 logic:ReasoningProgram 上的类区分来承载的原因。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/evaluationMode|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningProgram to the single logic:EvaluationMode strategy it selects to resolve its clause set. Functional: a program selects exactly one strategy, never a mix. An unrecognized or unsupported mode value is a HARD FAIL at compile time — explicit feature selection under the closed logic:EvaluationMode set, never a silent fallback to a weaker or default strategy."
msgstr "将 logic:ReasoningProgram 关联到它为求解其子句集所选定的唯一 logic:EvaluationMode 策略。函数性：一个程序恰好选定一种策略，绝非混合。无法识别或不受支持的模式值在编译期为硬失败——在封闭的 logic:EvaluationMode 集合下作显式特性选择，绝非默默退回到较弱或缺省策略。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/EvaluationStatus|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The closed value class of the logic:resultEvaluation field (the computation axis): what the engine was ABLE to do. Its individuals are logic:EvaluationCompleted, logic:BudgetExhausted, and logic:EvaluationUnsupported. The set is closed; a misspelt value is rejected (design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md, §The reasoning result)."
msgstr "logic:resultEvaluation 字段（计算轴）的封闭值类：引擎当时能够做什么。其个体为 logic:EvaluationCompleted、logic:BudgetExhausted 和 logic:EvaluationUnsupported。该集合是封闭的；拼写错误的值会被拒绝（design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md，§The reasoning result）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/evaluationTime|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The time of judgment component of the logic:GoalEvaluation identifying tuple: when this evaluation was made. Domain logic:GoalEvaluation (stated in prose); range xsd:dateTime (a full ISO-8601 instant, never xsd:date). Two evaluations of the same goal, situation, evaluator, and criterion made at different times are distinct records. When no explicit time is recorded the identifying tuple component is absent, not defaulted — absence means the time of judgment is unspecified rather than unknown."
msgstr "logic:GoalEvaluation 标识元组的「判断时间」成分：此评估是何时作出的。定义域为 logic:GoalEvaluation（以散文陈述）；值域为 xsd:dateTime（一个完整的 ISO-8601 瞬间，绝非 xsd:date）。对同一目标、同一情境、同一评估者和同一准则在不同时间作出的两次评估是不同的记录。当未记录显式时间时，该标识元组成分是缺席的，而非取默认值——缺席意味着判断时间是未指定的，而非未知的。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/EvaluationUnsupported|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:EvaluationStatus value for a request the engine has no defined procedure for (an unsupported contract, or a missing required model such as a probabilistic dependency model). Wire value `unsupported`; the information field is then logic:InfoNotEvaluated, never logic:InfoNeither."
msgstr "针对引擎没有既定程序可处理的请求（一个不受支持的合约，或一个缺失的必需模型，如概率依赖模型）的 logic:EvaluationStatus 值。传输值 `unsupported`；此时信息字段为 logic:InfoNotEvaluated，绝非 logic:InfoNeither。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Event|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A perdurant occurrence that happens in time and is composed of temporal parts: an action, a process, a happening that unfolds and is complete once it has occurred. Tokens it as an occurrence rather than an endurant; in the type-level world strata (risk, teleology, norms) the no-occurrence gate keeps reasoning over Event *types* without entailing any Event instance. Unitary: a proper temporal part of an event is not itself that event, and a completed (logic:Closed) event cannot vary — it bears no time-varying logic:Fluent (the change-asymmetry, logic:OccurrentChangeAsymmetry). An event is constituted by the process it is made of (logic:occurrentConstituent)."
msgstr "一个在时间中发生并由时间部分构成的持续性发生：一个行动、一个过程、一个展开且一旦发生便告完成的事件。将其例元化为一次发生而非一个延续者；在类型层世界层理（风险、目的论、规范）中，无发生门使推理得以在 Event *类型* 之上进行而不蕴涵任何 Event 实例。单一性：一个事件的一个真时间部分本身并非该事件，而一个已完成的（logic:Closed）事件不能变化——它不承载任何随时间变化的 logic:Fluent（变化不对称性，logic:OccurrentChangeAsymmetry）。一个事件由构成它的过程所构成（logic:occurrentConstituent）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/evidenceFor|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The relation or claim a logic:DefeasibleEvidence defeasibly supports — the 'to' side (e.g. gmeow:knowsAbout). Defeasible support, never strict entailment: the supported edge is not materialized from the evidence under the default reasoning. Range is left open (a property or a claim), stated in prose."
msgstr "一个 logic:DefeasibleEvidence 可废止地支持的关系或主张——「至」一侧（例如 gmeow:knowsAbout）。可废止的支持，绝非严格蕴涵：受支持的边在缺省推理下不由该证据物化。值域保持开放（一个属性或一个主张），以散文陈述。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/evidenceProperty|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The evidential relation a logic:DefeasibleEvidence declares to bear defeasibly on another — the 'from' side (e.g. gmeow:hasSkill). Range is left open (a property or a claim), stated in prose; the object is used by punning, the gmeow:pairsWith convention."
msgstr "一个 logic:DefeasibleEvidence 声明可废止地作用于另一者的证据关系——「自」一侧（例如 gmeow:hasSkill）。值域保持开放（一个属性或一个主张），以散文陈述；宾语经由双关（punning）使用，遵循 gmeow:pairsWith 惯例。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/evidenceStrength|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Evidential support for a statement, provenance-derived and reusing the evidence-slice warrant axes (source tier, evidence class): how well-warranted a claim is by its evidence. Normatively distinct from logic:probability, logic:confidence, and logic:weight — an evidential warrant is not a calibrated probability, an asserter's confidence, or a solver ranking, and is not interchangeable with any of them."
msgstr "对一个陈述的证据支持，源自出处并复用证据切片的担保轴（来源层级、证据类）：一个主张被其证据担保得有多充分。在规范上与 logic:probability、logic:confidence 和 logic:weight 相区别——一个证据担保不是一个已校准的概率、一个断言者的置信度，也不是一个求解器排名，且不与其中任何一者可互换。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/EvolutionMode|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The facet value class of the evolution facet: whether and how state changes over the course of reasoning. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract. Its individuals range from the static (one-state) default through state-transition to the Transaction-Logic transaction-path semantics; evolution is independent of the model-semantics facet, which is why state-change reasoning is a facet value, never a parallel profile. Commitment — whether a program's effects are committed or discarded — is a separate orthogonal facet (logic:ExecutionMode), not a value of this one: a program may be hypothetically executed (logic:HypotheticalExecution) under any evolution mode."
msgstr "演化侧面的侧面值类：在推理过程中状态是否以及如何变化。在 ReasoningContract 上单值。其个体从静态（单状态）缺省，经由状态转移，直至事务逻辑的事务路径语义；演化独立于模型语义侧面，这正是状态变化推理作为一个侧面值、而绝非一个并行剖面的原因。承诺——一个程序的效果是被提交还是被丢弃——是一个独立的正交侧面（logic:ExecutionMode），而非此侧面的一个值：一个程序可在任何演化模式下被假设性地执行（logic:HypotheticalExecution）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/evolution|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to the logic:EvolutionMode it selects — whether and how state changes. Single-valued on the contract. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:EvolutionMode (stated in prose, matching the module's convention). Evolution is independent of the model-semantics facet, which is why state-change reasoning (logic:TransactionPathEvolution) is a facet value, never a parallel profile."
msgstr "将 logic:ReasoningContract 关联到它所选定的 logic:EvolutionMode——状态是否以及如何变化。在合约上单值。定义域为 logic:ReasoningContract，值域为 logic:EvolutionMode（以散文陈述，符合模块惯例）。演化独立于模型语义侧面，这正是状态变化推理（logic:TransactionPathEvolution）作为一个侧面值、而绝非一个并行剖面的原因。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ExactPreservation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The projection yields the same answers as the canonical model for the declared query class: neither misses canonical answers nor adds spurious ones. The strongest preservation polarity, claimable only for a certified subfragment."
msgstr "对于所声明的查询类，该投影产生与规范模型相同的答案：既不遗漏规范答案，也不添加虚假答案。这是最强的保持极性，仅对一个经认证的子片段方可主张。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/executedAlongPath|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a program run — a logic:Plan or a logic:TransactionOutcome — to the logic:Path along which it executed: the executed history that realizes the program. Domain logic:Plan or logic:TransactionOutcome, range logic:Path (stated in prose). This is the one link the four-notion chain intention -> plan -> action -> transaction-path did not already have: intention reaches its goal and action through gmeow:intentionGoal / gmeow:motivates, a logic:Plan reaches the same goal through logic:planGoal, and an action occurrence reaches its type through logic:instantiatesSchema, but no existing term tied a program to the run that executed it. It CONNECTS the program to its path but does NOT subsume either: a plan is the program (what is intended to be done), a path is the executed run (how state actually changed); the link records that this program ran along that history without conflating the two."
msgstr "将一次程序运行——一个 logic:Plan 或一个 logic:TransactionOutcome——关联到它据以执行的 logic:Path：即实现该程序的已执行历史。定义域为 logic:Plan 或 logic:TransactionOutcome，值域为 logic:Path（以散文陈述）。这是四概念链 intention -> plan -> action -> transaction-path 此前尚未具备的那一环：意图经由 gmeow:intentionGoal / gmeow:motivates 抵达其目标与行动，一个 logic:Plan 经由 logic:planGoal 抵达同一目标，一次行动发生经由 logic:instantiatesSchema 抵达其类型，但既有词项无一将一个程序系于执行它的那次运行。它把程序与其路径连接起来，却不涵摄二者中的任何一个：计划是程序（意图去做之事），路径是已实现的运行（状态实际如何变化）；该链接记录此程序沿那段历史运行过，而不混同二者。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/executedHypotheticallyAs|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The content-addressed witness (a digest) of a hypothetical (sandbox) transaction run: present on a logic:TransactionOutcome exactly when the program executed under logic:HypotheticalExecution, recording the identity of the discarded run whose verdict (logic:transactionSucceeds) was computed without committing its effects. The run's effect substrate — the executed logic:Path, the per-step logic:TransactionStep records, and the supersession quads — is intentionally ABSENT, because the sandbox operator tests without committing; this digest is therefore the sole standing trace that the run occurred and what it ranged over. Nothing is asserted to be erased, only never emitted, so suppression-never-erasure holds for free. Single-valued. Domain logic:TransactionOutcome, range xsd:string (stated in prose). The committed counterpart (logic:CommittedExecution) emits the full effect substrate and carries no such witness."
msgstr "一次假设性（沙箱）事务运行的内容寻址见证（一个摘要）：恰当程序在 logic:HypotheticalExecution 下执行时出现于一个 logic:TransactionOutcome 之上，记录那次被丢弃运行的同一性，其裁决（logic:transactionSucceeds）是在不提交其效果的情况下计算的。该运行的效果基底——已执行的 logic:Path、逐步的 logic:TransactionStep 记录以及取代四元组——是有意缺席的，因为沙箱算子在不提交的情况下进行测试；故此摘要是该运行曾发生及其涉及范围的唯一留存痕迹。没有任何内容被断言为已擦除，只是从未发出，因而「抑制而非擦除」自然成立。单值。定义域为 logic:TransactionOutcome，值域为 xsd:string（以散文陈述）。已提交的对应物（logic:CommittedExecution）发出完整的效果基底，且不携带任何此类见证。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/executedUnderContract|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a transaction-program node — a transaction-program combinator root (logic:SerialConjunction, logic:Choice, logic:Fallback, or logic:Iteration) marked executable by logic:transitionFromState — to the logic:ReasoningContract it executes under, whose logic:executionMode selects whether the program's effects are committed (logic:CommittedExecution, the default) or discarded (logic:HypotheticalExecution, the sandbox operator). This is the link by which a program reaches the execution-commitment facet: without it the contract-level logic:executionMode could not select commit-versus-discard for a concrete run. Single-valued — a program names at most one governing contract; absence resolves to the default committed execution. Domain a transaction-program node, range logic:ReasoningContract (stated in prose, matching the module's domain/range convention)."
msgstr "将一个事务程序节点——一个由 logic:transitionFromState 标记为可执行的事务程序组合子根（logic:SerialConjunction、logic:Choice、logic:Fallback 或 logic:Iteration）——关联到它据以执行的 logic:ReasoningContract，后者的 logic:executionMode 选定该程序的效果是被提交（logic:CommittedExecution，缺省）还是被丢弃（logic:HypotheticalExecution，沙箱算子）。这是一个程序抵达执行承诺侧面所经由的链接：没有它，合约层的 logic:executionMode 便无法为一次具体运行选定提交对丢弃。单值——一个程序至多命名一个治理合约；缺席解析为缺省的已提交执行。定义域为一个事务程序节点，值域为 logic:ReasoningContract（以散文陈述，符合模块的定义域/值域惯例）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ExecutionMode|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The facet value class of the execution-commitment facet: whether a Transaction-Logic program's effects are committed or discarded. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract and ORTHOGONAL to the evolution facet — a program may be executed hypothetically under any logic:EvolutionMode, because commitment (commit vs. discard) and state-change shape are independent dimensions. Its individuals are logic:CommittedExecution (the default) and logic:HypotheticalExecution (the sandbox operator). The sandbox operator is DISTINCT from modal possibility (◇): ◇ is the standard translation over the appropriate typed accessibility relation — logic:epistemicallyPossible or logic:doxasticallyAccessible (an alethic or doxastic claim about what is possible), not over the bare logic:accessibleFrom superproperty — whereas hypothetical execution asserts a program can execute from here without committing; conflating them would let an execution sandbox masquerade as a statement about what is possible."
msgstr "执行承诺侧面的侧面值类：一个事务逻辑程序的效果是被提交还是被丢弃。在 ReasoningContract 上单值，且与演化侧面正交——一个程序可在任何 logic:EvolutionMode 下被假设性地执行，因为承诺（提交对丢弃）与状态变化形态是独立的维度。其个体为 logic:CommittedExecution（缺省）和 logic:HypotheticalExecution（沙箱算子）。沙箱算子与模态可能性（◇）有别：◇ 是在恰当的类型化可达关系之上的标准翻译——logic:epistemicallyPossible 或 logic:doxasticallyAccessible（一个关于何为可能的真势或信念主张），而非在裸的 logic:accessibleFrom 超属性之上——而假设性执行断言一个程序可从此处执行而不提交；混同二者会让一个执行沙箱冒充一个关于何为可能的陈述。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/executionMode|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to the logic:ExecutionMode it selects — whether transaction effects are committed (logic:CommittedExecution, the default) or discarded (logic:HypotheticalExecution, the sandbox operator). Single-valued on the contract. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:ExecutionMode (stated in prose, matching the module's domain/range convention). Independent of logic:evolution: a hypothetical run may compose with any evolution mode. This facet carries the sandbox operator, which is distinct from modal possibility — modal possibility is computed as the standard translation over the appropriate typed accessibility relation (logic:epistemicallyPossible / logic:doxasticallyAccessible), never over the bare logic:accessibleFrom superproperty and never reified as a possibility class."
msgstr "将 logic:ReasoningContract 关联到它所选定的 logic:ExecutionMode——事务效果是被提交（logic:CommittedExecution，缺省）还是被丢弃（logic:HypotheticalExecution，沙箱算子）。在合约上单值。定义域为 logic:ReasoningContract，值域为 logic:ExecutionMode（以散文陈述，符合模块的定义域/值域惯例）。独立于 logic:evolution：一次假设性运行可与任何演化模式组合。此侧面承载沙箱算子，它与模态可能性有别——模态可能性是作为在恰当的类型化可达关系（logic:epistemicallyPossible / logic:doxasticallyAccessible）之上的标准翻译来计算的，绝不在裸的 logic:accessibleFrom 超属性之上，也绝不具体化为一个可能性类。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/existentialChaseDemonstrandAlpha|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The first seeded demonstrand of the native existential chase: a logic:ExistentialChaseDemonstrand asserted with NO logic:demonstratesChaseWitness edge, so the chase must invent a fresh Skolem witness (a gmeow:InventedWitness) to satisfy its ∃demonstratesChaseWitness.ChaseWitnessLeaf obligation. Paired with logic:existentialChaseDemonstrandBeta so the chase mints two DISTINCT nulls, one per instance, in the same world."
msgstr "原生存在追逐的第一个种子被证物：一个未带任何 logic:demonstratesChaseWitness 边即被断言的 logic:ExistentialChaseDemonstrand，故追逐必须发明一个新鲜的 Skolem 见证（一个 gmeow:InventedWitness）以满足其 ∃demonstratesChaseWitness.ChaseWitnessLeaf 义务。与 logic:existentialChaseDemonstrandBeta 配对，以便追逐在同一世界中铸造两个不同的空值，每个实例一个。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/existentialChaseDemonstrandBeta|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The second seeded demonstrand of the native existential chase: a logic:ExistentialChaseDemonstrand asserted with NO logic:demonstratesChaseWitness edge, so the chase must invent a fresh Skolem witness (a gmeow:InventedWitness) to satisfy its ∃demonstratesChaseWitness.ChaseWitnessLeaf obligation. Paired with logic:existentialChaseDemonstrandAlpha so the chase mints two DISTINCT nulls, one per instance, in the same world."
msgstr "原生存在追逐的第二个种子被证物：一个未带任何 logic:demonstratesChaseWitness 边即被断言的 logic:ExistentialChaseDemonstrand，故追逐必须发明一个新鲜的 Skolem 见证（一个 gmeow:InventedWitness）以满足其 ∃demonstratesChaseWitness.ChaseWitnessLeaf 义务。与 logic:existentialChaseDemonstrandAlpha 配对，以便追逐在同一世界中铸造两个不同的空值，每个实例一个。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ExistentialChaseDemonstrand|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A narrow, self-describing existential obligation: a class each of whose instances carries the C ⊑ ∃p.D obligation `ExistentialChaseDemonstrand ⊑ ∃demonstratesChaseWitness.ChaseWitnessLeaf`, which the native existential chase MUST discharge by inventing a fresh Skolem witness (a gmeow:InventedWitness) for every instance that asserts no logic:demonstratesChaseWitness edge. It is deliberately narrow — ONLY the two seeded demonstrand individuals inhabit it — so the demonstration dogfoods the chase without cascading global inference over a widely-instantiated class. This is the native chase's own defining law made concrete and on-topic: an existential obligation entails a Skolem witness, and running the chase over this class is the minimal proof that GMEOW's own existential materializer actually fires."
msgstr "一个狭窄、自描述的存在义务：一个类，其每个实例均承载 C ⊑ ∃p.D 义务 `ExistentialChaseDemonstrand ⊑ ∃demonstratesChaseWitness.ChaseWitnessLeaf`，原生存在追逐必须通过为每个未断言任何 logic:demonstratesChaseWitness 边的实例发明一个新鲜的 Skolem 见证（一个 gmeow:InventedWitness）来履行该义务。它是刻意狭窄的——仅有两个种子被证物个体栖居其中——以便该演示自食其狗粮式地运用追逐，而不在一个被广泛实例化的类上级联全局推理。这是原生追逐自身的定义律被落实为具体且切题者：一个存在义务蕴涵一个 Skolem 见证，而在此类之上运行追逐是 GMEOW 自身的存在物化器确实触发的最小证明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ExistentialChaseDemonstrand|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "logic:existentialChaseDemonstrandAlpha a logic:ExistentialChaseDemonstrand ."
msgstr "示例：logic:existentialChaseDemonstrandAlpha a logic:ExistentialChaseDemonstrand ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ExistentialRulesFragment|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The formula-fragment facet value selecting the existential-rules (tuple-generating-dependency / Datalog±) class, admitting existential quantifiers in rule heads. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract; more expressive than logic:DatalogFragment (value invention) and the fragment over which acyclicity or guardedness conditions buy back decidability."
msgstr "选定存在规则（元组生成依赖 / Datalog±）类的公式片段侧面值，允许在规则头部使用存在量词。在 ReasoningContract 上单值；比 logic:DatalogFragment 更具表达力（值发明），并且是无环性或有界性条件在其上赎回可判定性的那个片段。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/exists|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates an existential-quantifier logic:Formula to its body formula. The bound variables are carried by logic:quantifiedVariable. Existential witnesses are Skolemized only at the evaluable-lowering layer; the AST node pins the binder and body, not the witness identity."
msgstr "将一个存在量词的 logic:Formula 关联到其主体公式。约束变量由 logic:quantifiedVariable 承载。存在见证仅在可求值下沉层被 Skolem 化；AST 节点锚定绑定符与主体，而非见证的同一性。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/exists|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "An existential node can bind y and point logic:exists to the atom ex:knows(x,y)."
msgstr "存在量词节点可以绑定 y 并将 logic:exists 指向原子 ex:knows(x,y)。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/expandsToFacet|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Links a logic:ReasoningPreset to a facet value it expands to. A preset's full facet selection is the set of its logic:expandsToFacet values plus any facet-specific properties; the compiler expands the preset to this bundle before reasoning, so a preset reference and its expanded facet set are interchangeable. Domain logic:ReasoningPreset (stated in prose, matching the module's convention)."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ReasoningPreset 链接到它所展开成的一个侧面值。一个预设的完整侧面选择是其 logic:expandsToFacet 值的集合加上任何侧面专属属性；编译器在推理之前将该预设展开为此捆绑，因而一个预设引用与其展开后的侧面集合可互换。定义域为 logic:ReasoningPreset（以散文陈述，符合模块惯例）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/expectsInputShape|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a query (or a competency question) to the logic:ResultShape its input is expected to satisfy. The producer feeding the query must satisfy this shape (structural input→output compatibility) BEFORE execution; a mismatch is a hard, surfaced error. Single-valued. Range logic:ResultShape (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将一个查询（或一个胜任力问题）关联到其输入被期望满足的 logic:ResultShape。为该查询供料的生产者在执行之前必须满足此形状（结构上输入→输出兼容）；不匹配是一个硬性的、被显现出来的错误。单值。值域为 logic:ResultShape（以散文陈述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ExplicitEqualityPolicy|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The equality-policy value under which two terms are one only when their identity is explicitly asserted (e.g. via owl:sameAs-style equality facts): no implicit unification beyond what is declared. Contrast logic:RdfEqualityPolicy (RDF node identity) and logic:UniqueNameEqualityPolicy (distinct names denote distinct entities)."
msgstr "相等策略值，在其下唯有当两个词项的同一性被显式断言时（例如经由 owl:sameAs 式的相等事实）二者方为一：不存在超出所声明范围的隐式合一。与 logic:RdfEqualityPolicy（RDF 节点同一性）及 logic:UniqueNameEqualityPolicy（不同的名称指称不同的实体）相对照。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ExplicitNegation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The strong (explicit) negation operator: an atom is asserted false, distinct from being merely not derivable. One member of the negation-operator set facet — a program may legitimately use explicit negation and logic:DefaultNegation together — which records the permitted operator set, not a single chosen operator."
msgstr "强（显式）否定算子：一个原子被断言为假，区别于仅仅不可导出。否定算子集合侧面的一个成员——一个程序可合法地同时使用显式否定与 logic:DefaultNegation——它记录被许可的算子集合，而非单一被选定的算子。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ExpressivenessBoundary|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The closed class naming which logical fragment a defining statement inhabits — the machine-readable first-order-vs-second-order axis of the loss ledger, distinct from logic:PreservationKind (answer polarity) and logic:FormulaShape (first-order constructs a Horn target cannot carry). Its individuals are logic:FirstOrder and logic:SecondOrder; the set is closed, so a misspelt value names no declared boundary."
msgstr "命名一个定义性陈述栖居于哪个逻辑片段的封闭类——即损失账本中机器可读的一阶对二阶轴，区别于 logic:PreservationKind（答案极性）与 logic:FormulaShape（一个 Horn 目标无法承载的一阶构造）。其个体为 logic:FirstOrder 和 logic:SecondOrder；该集合是封闭的，因而一个拼写错误的值不指称任何所声明的边界。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/expressivenessBoundary|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a defining law or a loss-ledger boundary record to the logic:ExpressivenessBoundary its statement inhabits."
msgstr "将一条定义性律或一条损失账本边界记录关联到其陈述所栖居的 logic:ExpressivenessBoundary。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RefutationPattern|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The closed class of decision-procedure schemata a certified-complete refutation family closes under. Several decided families may share one pattern (a cardinality count and an owl:hasSelf self-edge are both the counting pigeonhole). Its individuals are the state-of-the-art patterns the native kernel decides; the set is the projection of the Rust RefutationPattern enum."
msgstr "封闭类，列举一个已认证完备的反驳族据以归属的判定过程模式。多个已判定的族可以共享同一个模式（一次基数计数与一条 owl:hasSelf 自环边都属于计数鸽笼）。其个体是原生内核所判定的各个前沿模式；该集合是 Rust RefutationPattern 枚举的投影。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DecidedFragment|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A certified-complete construct family the native refutation kernel decides: it carries the logic:RefutationPattern it closes under (logic:decidesUnderPattern) and a technical completeness bound (logic:fragmentCompletenessBound). One individual per decided family; the set is the projection of the Rust decided_fragments() registry, outside which the kernel honestly withholds."
msgstr "原生反驳内核所判定的一个已认证完备的构造族：它携带其据以归属的 logic:RefutationPattern（通过 logic:decidesUnderPattern）以及一个技术性完备性界（logic:fragmentCompletenessBound）。每个已判定的族对应一个个体；该集合是 Rust decided_fragments() 注册表的投影，超出此范围内核则诚实地保留判定。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/decidesUnderPattern|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:DecidedFragment to the logic:RefutationPattern its family closes under."
msgstr "将一个 logic:DecidedFragment 关联到其所属族据以归属的 logic:RefutationPattern。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/fragmentCompletenessBound|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The technical completeness bound of a logic:DecidedFragment: the precise fragment characterization under which the kernel's decision is complete, free of any process reference."
msgstr "一个 logic:DecidedFragment 的技术性完备性界：内核的判定在其下完备的精确片段刻画，不含任何流程性指称。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/fragmentBoundaryReason|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The technical reason a retained-withhold record lies outside the certified-complete refutation fragment: the construct the kernel deliberately does not decide and why, free of any process reference."
msgstr "一条保留的弃判记录之所以落在已认证完备的反驳片段之外的技术原因：内核刻意不予判定的构造及其缘由，不含任何流程性指称。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/counting-pigeonhole|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A finite pigeonhole count of distinct fillers or edges against a numeric bound: the count exceeds (or collapses) the bound, so no model can satisfy it."
msgstr "针对一个数值界对不同的填充值或边进行的有限鸽笼计数：该计数超过（或压垮）该界，因而没有任何模型能够满足它。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/value-space-cardinality|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A finite datatype value-space cardinality bounding the distinct-literal count a cardinality restriction can force onto a datatype property."
msgstr "一种数据类型有限值空间的基数，用以限定一个基数限制能够施加于某数据类型属性之上的不同字面量数目。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/case-split-exhaustion|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "An exhaustive, terminating case-split over a bounded disjunction: every branch is refuted, so the disjunction as a whole is refuted."
msgstr "对一个有界析取进行的穷尽且可终止的按案例拆分：每个分支都被反驳，因而该析取整体被反驳。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/complement-clash|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A propositional complement clash: a class expression forced to inhabit both a class and its complement in a definition position, decided without model search."
msgstr "一种命题层面的补类冲突：一个类表达式在定义位置上被迫同时归属于某个类及其补类，无需模型搜索即可判定。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/arithmetic-equality-collapse|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "An equality / inequality arithmetic collapse over a finite set of named individuals: an (inverse-)functional identity forced against an asserted distinctness."
msgstr "在一个有限的具名个体集合上发生的相等/不等算术坍缩：一个（逆）函数性同一性被迫与一个已断言的相异性相抵触。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/malformed-metamodel|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A decidable metamodel malformation of the finite triple set, such as a structurally broken RDF list, adjudicated independently of object-level entailment."
msgstr "对有限三元组集合的一种可判定的元模型畸形，例如一个结构性损坏的 RDF 列表，其判定独立于对象层面的蕴涵。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/nominal-clash|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A finite closed-set intersection emptiness over nominal enumerations: an individual forced into two or more disjoint owl:oneOf sets."
msgstr "在标称枚举上发生的有限闭集交空性：一个个体被迫归入两个或更多互不相交的 owl:oneOf 集合。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/complement-refutation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The certified-complete complement-refutation family: a class constrained by a negated class expression forced unsatisfiable-yet-nonempty, decided under the complement clash pattern."
msgstr "已认证完备的补类反驳族：一个类受一个被否定的类表达式约束，被迫呈现为不可满足却又非空，在补类冲突模式下判定。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/number-cardinality-counting|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The certified-complete number/cardinality-counting family: min/max/exact (qualified) cardinality bounds decided by counting distinct fillers under the identity stance, under the counting pigeonhole pattern."
msgstr "已认证完备的数量／基数计数族：在给定同一性立场下通过对不同填充值计数来判定的最小/最大/精确（限定）基数界，属于计数鸽笼模式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/union-disjoint-case-split|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The certified-complete union-plus-disjoint refutation family: a bounded disjunctive membership every branch of which closes, under the case-split exhaustion pattern."
msgstr "已认证完备的并集加互斥反驳族：一种有界的析取归属关系，其每个分支都会收敛，属于案例穷举拆分模式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/nominal-enumeration-counting|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The certified-complete nominal-enumeration-counting family: a nominal pigeonhole across disjoint owl:oneOf enumerations, under the nominal clash pattern."
msgstr "已认证完备的标称枚举计数族：跨越互不相交的 owl:oneOf 枚举的一种标称鸽笼，属于标称冲突模式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/datatype-value-space|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The certified-complete datatype value-space family: a facet-restricted datatype whose finite value space is too small for the distinct values forced onto it, under the value-space cardinality pattern."
msgstr "已认证完备的数据类型值空间族：一种经面限制的数据类型，其有限值空间对于被迫施加于其上的不同值而言过小，属于值空间基数模式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/inverse-functional-identity-collapse|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The certified-complete inverse-functional / functional identity-collapse family: an (inverse-)functional property collapsing two distinct individuals, under the arithmetic equality collapse pattern."
msgstr "已认证完备的（逆）函数同一性坍缩族：一个（逆）函数性属性将两个不同个体坍缩为一，属于算术相等坍缩模式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/malformed-rdf-list|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The certified-complete malformed-rdf:List family: an rdf:nil node bearing a list edge, decided under the malformed metamodel pattern."
msgstr "已认证完备的畸形 rdf:List 族：一个承载列表边的 rdf:nil 节点，在畸形元模型模式下判定。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/has-self-membership|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The certified-complete owl:hasSelf membership-refutation family: a self-restriction in a disjointness position clashed by a self-edge, decided under the counting pigeonhole pattern."
msgstr "已认证完备的 owl:hasSelf 归属反驳族：一个处于互斥位置的自反限制被一条自环边冲突，属于计数鸽笼模式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/xsd-pattern-facet|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The retained-withhold record for xsd:pattern facets: a datatype value-space emptiness the kernel does not decide because it needs the XML-Schema regular-expression dialect rather than a host regex engine."
msgstr "针对 xsd:pattern 面的保留弃判记录：一种数据类型值空间空性，内核不予判定，因为它需要 XML Schema 的正则表达式方言，而非宿主正则引擎。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/non-binary-property-chain|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The retained-withhold record for non-binary property chains: an n-ary role composition the kernel does not certify because it does not reduce to the binary composition its deciders handle."
msgstr "针对非二元属性链的保留弃判记录：一种 n 元角色复合，内核不予认证，因为它无法归约为其判定器所处理的二元复合。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/entangled-existential-cardinality|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The retained-withhold record for entangled full-DL existential-plus-cardinality configurations: witness generation coupled with counting on one property, which the kernel certifies only in isolation."
msgstr "针对纠缠的全 DL 存在加基数配置的保留弃判记录：在同一属性上将见证生成与计数相耦合，内核只在两者各自独立时才予以认证。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/externalRelationAdmittedRows|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The number of unique, complete, validated provider rows admitted by an invocation or across a query receipt. Failed, incomplete, cancelled, over-budget, and malformed batches admit zero."
msgstr "一次调用或跨一份查询回执所接纳的唯一、完整、经验证的提供方行数。失败的、不完整的、已取消的、超预算的和格式错误的批次接纳零行。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/externalRelationAnnotationAlgebra|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Names the stable algebra identity a provider descriptor requires. Provider-aware dispatch hard-fails before execution when it differs from the selected logic:TupleAnnotationAlgebra identity."
msgstr "命名一个提供方描述符所要求的稳定代数同一性。当其与所选定的 logic:TupleAnnotationAlgebra 同一性相异时，提供方感知的派发在执行之前硬失败。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ExternalRelationAnnotationDimension|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The explicitly named semantic dimension of a provider tuple's opaque algebra element. The standard values distinguish similarity, rank, distance, persistence, and epistemic confidence; additional named dimensions remain possible, but none is silently relabelled as another."
msgstr "一个提供方元组的不透明代数元素的显式命名语义维度。标准值区分相似度、排名、距离、持久性和认知置信度；额外的命名维度仍属可能，但没有任何一个会被默默重新标记为另一个。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/externalRelationAnnotationDimension|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a descriptor or invocation to the logic:ExternalRelationAnnotationDimension carried by its tuple algebra element. This explicit edge prevents similarity, rank, distance, persistence, and epistemic confidence from collapsing into one score meaning."
msgstr "将一个描述符或一次调用关联到其元组代数元素所承载的 logic:ExternalRelationAnnotationDimension。此显式边防止相似度、排名、距离、持久性和认知置信度坍缩为单一的分数含义。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/externalRelationArgumentDatatype|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The optional absolute datatype IRI required by a literal-valued logic:ExternalRelationArgument. It is absent when any RDF literal datatype conforms."
msgstr "由取字面量值的 logic:ExternalRelationArgument 所要求的可选绝对数据类型 IRI。当任意 RDF 字面量数据类型均适用时，它缺省不存在。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/externalRelationArgumentKind|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates an logic:ExternalRelationArgument to its logic:TermKind, including native RDF 1.2 triple terms. Single-valued per argument entry."
msgstr "将 logic:ExternalRelationArgument 关联到其 logic:TermKind，包括原生的 RDF 1.2 三元组词项。每个参数条目取单一值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/externalRelationArgumentPosition|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The zero-based position of an logic:ExternalRelationArgument in its descriptor's ordered schema. Single-valued per argument entry."
msgstr "logic:ExternalRelationArgument 在其描述符有序模式中的从零开始的位置。每个参数条目取单一值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/externalRelationArgumentSchema|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates an logic:ExternalRelationProviderDescriptor to the ordered RDF list of logic:ExternalRelationArgument entries that types every positional RDF 1.2 value and determines relation arity."
msgstr "将 logic:ExternalRelationProviderDescriptor 关联到有序的 logic:ExternalRelationArgument 条目 RDF 列表，该列表为每个按位 RDF 1.2 值定型并确定关系的元数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ExternalRelationArgument|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "One positional entry of an external relation's RDF 1.2 argument schema, carrying its zero-based position, logic:TermKind, and optional literal datatype. The ordered list of these entries determines relation arity and is checked before any provider tuple enters evaluation."
msgstr "外部关系的 RDF 1.2 参数模式中的一个按位条目，携带其从零开始的位置、logic:TermKind 以及可选的字面量数据类型。这些条目的有序列表确定关系的元数，并在任何提供方元组进入求值之前接受检查。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/externalRelationArity|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The positive number of positional arguments in an external relation descriptor, equal to the length of its logic:externalRelationArgumentSchema list."
msgstr "外部关系描述符中按位参数的正整数个数，等于其 logic:externalRelationArgumentSchema 列表的长度。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/externalRelationArtifactGeneration|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Names the immutable index or artifact generation a provider descriptor pins and an invocation actually read. Generation mismatch or mid-call staleness is a typed non-result, never silently accepted data."
msgstr "命名提供方描述符所固定、且某次调用实际读取的不可变索引或工件世代。世代不匹配或调用中途的陈旧性属于一种带类型的非结果，绝不作为默默接受的数据。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ExternalRelationAscending|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The external-relation order direction in which smaller provider order keys precede larger keys; canonical RDF tuple order breaks equal keys. Wire value `ascending`."
msgstr "外部关系的排序方向，其中较小的提供方排序键位于较大键之前；规范的 RDF 元组顺序用于打破相等键的平局。线值 `ascending`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/externalRelationBounds|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The canonical positional encoding of bound and unbound RDF 1.2 arguments pushed to an invocation. The executable receipt retains the native typed values; this literal is their lossy ontology projection."
msgstr "推送给某次调用的已绑定与未绑定 RDF 1.2 参数的规范按位编码。可执行回执保留原生的带类型值；此字面量是它们的有损本体投影。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ExternalRelationBudgetExhausted|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The invocation status reached when the query's deterministic external call or unique-row governor would be exceeded. No over-budget batch is partially admitted. Wire value `budget-exhausted`."
msgstr "当查询的确定性外部调用或唯一行调节器将被超出时所达到的调用状态。任何超预算的批次都不会被部分接纳。线值 `budget-exhausted`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ExternalRelationBudget|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The deterministic operation-wide governor for external relations, carrying non-zero maximum provider-call and unique-admitted-row counts. Exhaustion is a typed incomplete non-result; it never turns a partial provider execution into a complete empty relation."
msgstr "面向外部关系的确定性、覆盖整个操作的调节器，携带非零的最大提供方调用次数与最大唯一接纳行数。耗尽是一种带类型的不完整非结果；它绝不会把提供方的部分执行变成一个完整的空关系。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/externalRelationBudget|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a provider manifest or query receipt to the logic:ExternalRelationBudget that governed every query-local invocation."
msgstr "将提供方清单或查询回执关联到管辖每次查询本地调用的 logic:ExternalRelationBudget。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ExternalRelationCacheHit|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The invocation status for reuse of an identical complete, validated batch from the same query-local cache. Reuse occurs before call or row budget charging. Wire value `cache-hit`."
msgstr "对来自同一查询本地缓存的、完全相同的完整且已校验批次进行复用时的调用状态。复用发生在计入调用预算或行预算之前。线值 `cache-hit`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/externalRelationCallBudget|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The maximum number of distinct provider calls allowed by an logic:ExternalRelationBudget. Query-local cache hits do not consume it."
msgstr "logic:ExternalRelationBudget 所允许的不同提供方调用的最大次数。查询本地缓存命中不会消耗它。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/externalRelationCallLimit|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The non-zero ordered-prefix row limit pushed on one external relation invocation. Provider over-production is a contract violation, not silently truncated output."
msgstr "推送到一次外部关系调用上的非零有序前缀行数限制。提供方的过量生产是一种契约违背，而非被默默截断的输出。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ExternalRelationCancelled|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The invocation status when operation cancellation is observed immediately before or after a provider call. A post-call cancellation discards the returned batch before admission. Wire value `cancelled`."
msgstr "在提供方调用之前或之后立即观察到操作取消时的调用状态。调用后取消会在接纳之前丢弃返回的批次。线值 `cancelled`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ExternalRelationComplete|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The invocation status for a provider batch that completed and passed generation, arity, RDF 1.2 schema, bound, limit, uniqueness, ordering, annotation, cancellation, and budget validation. Wire value `complete`."
msgstr "对于已完成并通过世代、元数、RDF 1.2 模式、绑定、限制、唯一性、排序、注解、取消及预算校验的提供方批次的调用状态。线值 `complete`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ExternalRelationContractViolation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The invocation status for provider output or a request that violates the pinned relation descriptor: wrong generation, arity, RDF 1.2 schema, bounds, limit, uniqueness, total order, or annotation consistency. The malformed batch is never cached or admitted. Wire value `contract-violation`."
msgstr "对于违反所固定关系描述符的提供方输出或请求的调用状态：错误的世代、元数、RDF 1.2 模式、边界、限制、唯一性、全序或注解一致性。畸形批次绝不会被缓存或接纳。线值 `contract-violation`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/externalRelationContributed|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Whether at least one tuple from an invocation occurs in a final answer derivation. An invoked but unused provider remains in operational evidence without being falsely named as a contributor."
msgstr "表示某次调用中是否至少有一个元组出现在最终答案的推导中。被调用却未被使用的提供方仍保留在操作性证据中，而不会被错误地列为贡献者。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/externalRelationDeliveredRows|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The number of rows a provider delivered before validation for an invocation or across a receipt. This structural counter makes demand pushdown inspectable without a wall-clock claim."
msgstr "提供方在校验之前为某次调用或在整份回执范围内所交付的行数。此结构性计数器使需求下推可供检视，而不作任何挂钟时间上的断言。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ExternalRelationDescending|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The external-relation order direction in which larger provider order keys precede smaller keys; canonical RDF tuple order breaks equal keys. Wire value `descending`."
msgstr "外部关系的排序方向，其中较大的提供方排序键位于较小键之前；规范的 RDF 元组顺序用于打破相等键的平局。线值 `descending`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/externalRelationDescriptor|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates an logic:ExternalRelationInvocation to the logic:ExternalRelationProviderDescriptor that governed it. The descriptor is immutable for the containing query."
msgstr "将 logic:ExternalRelationInvocation 关联到管辖它的 logic:ExternalRelationProviderDescriptor。对于包含它的查询而言，该描述符是不可变的。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ExternalRelationFailed|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The invocation status for an operational provider failure. It is a typed non-result, not a complete relation containing zero rows. Wire value `failed`."
msgstr "对于提供方运行性故障的调用状态。它是一种带类型的非结果，而不是一个包含零行的完整关系。线值 `failed`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ExternalRelationIncomplete|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The invocation status for a provider that cannot certify the requested ordered prefix, including provider-budget, stale-generation, or uncertified-universe cases. It is not semantic absence. Wire value `incomplete`."
msgstr "对于无法认证所请求有序前缀的提供方的调用状态，包括提供方预算、世代陈旧或宇宙未认证等情形。它并非语义上的缺失。线值 `incomplete`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ExternalRelationInvocation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The content-addressed evidence for one provider request or query-local cache reuse: it records descriptor identities, positional bounds, pushed limit and ordering, annotation dimension, terminal status, response digest, row counts, and whether a returned tuple contributed to an answer. No incomplete or invalid batch contributes tuples."
msgstr "对一次提供方请求或查询本地缓存复用的内容寻址证据：它记录描述符标识、按位边界、所推送的限制与排序、注解维度、终态状态、响应摘要、行数计数，以及某个返回元组是否为答案作出贡献。任何不完整或无效的批次都不贡献元组。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/externalRelationInvocation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates an logic:ExternalRelationQueryReceipt to each ordered logic:ExternalRelationInvocation it records, including complete calls, cache hits, and terminal failed attempts."
msgstr "将 logic:ExternalRelationQueryReceipt 关联到它所记录的每个有序的 logic:ExternalRelationInvocation，包括完整调用、缓存命中以及终态失败的尝试。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ExternalRelationInvocationStatus|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The closed terminal-status class for one external relation invocation: complete, cache hit, failed, incomplete, budget exhausted, cancelled, or contract violation. Only complete and cache-hit invocations may supply tuples to an answer."
msgstr "对一次外部关系调用的封闭终态状态类：完整、缓存命中、失败、不完整、预算耗尽、已取消或契约违背。只有完整调用和缓存命中调用才可为答案提供元组。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/externalRelationInvocationStatus|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates an logic:ExternalRelationInvocation to its single logic:ExternalRelationInvocationStatus terminal value."
msgstr "将 logic:ExternalRelationInvocation 关联到其单一的 logic:ExternalRelationInvocationStatus 终态值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/externalRelationModel|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Names the stable model or deterministic algorithm identity used by an external relation provider. It is kept distinct from provider identity and artifact generation in descriptors, lineage, and receipts."
msgstr "命名外部关系提供方所使用的稳定模型或确定性算法标识。在描述符、谱系和回执中，它与提供方标识及工件世代保持区分。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ExternalRelationOrderDirection|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The closed value class for the direction of an logic:ExternalRelationOrdering: logic:ExternalRelationAscending or logic:ExternalRelationDescending."
msgstr "logic:ExternalRelationOrdering 方向的封闭值类：logic:ExternalRelationAscending 或 logic:ExternalRelationDescending。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/externalRelationOrderDirection|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates an logic:ExternalRelationOrdering to its single logic:ExternalRelationOrderDirection value."
msgstr "将 logic:ExternalRelationOrdering 关联到其单一的 logic:ExternalRelationOrderDirection 值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/externalRelationOrderingCriterion|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Names the absolute IRI identifying the primary provider order-key criterion of an logic:ExternalRelationOrdering."
msgstr "命名标识 logic:ExternalRelationOrdering 主要提供方排序键判据的绝对 IRI。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ExternalRelationOrdering|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The total row-order contract pushed to an external relation provider: an identified criterion plus ascending or descending direction, with canonical RDF tuple order breaking equal provider keys. The engine validates the returned sequence rather than silently sorting malformed output."
msgstr "推送给外部关系提供方的全序行排序契约：一个已标识的判据加上升序或降序方向，并以规范的 RDF 元组顺序打破相等提供方键的平局。引擎会校验返回的序列，而非默默地对畸形输出进行排序。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/externalRelationOrdering|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a provider descriptor or invocation to the logic:ExternalRelationOrdering pushed into the call and validated over the returned batch."
msgstr "将提供方描述符或调用关联到被推入调用、并在返回批次上得到校验的 logic:ExternalRelationOrdering。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/externalRelationPredicate|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Names the predicate or relation IRI a provider exposes as a query-scoped physical EDB operator. Returned tuples satisfy this query relation only; this property does not promote them to asserted RDF facts."
msgstr "命名提供方作为查询范围的物理 EDB 运算符所暴露的谓词或关系 IRI。返回的元组仅满足此查询关系；此属性不会将它们提升为已断言的 RDF 事实。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/externalRelationPreservation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates an external relation descriptor or receipt to every logic:PreservationKind polarity disclosed by that provider input. Invoked provider claims merge into the query answer and cannot weaken or bypass the governing preservation ledger."
msgstr "将外部关系描述符或回执关联到该提供方输入所披露的每个 logic:PreservationKind 极性。被调用的提供方声明会并入查询答案，且不能削弱或绕过管辖它们的保持台账。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ExternalRelationProviderDescriptor|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The immutable declaration of one relation-valued physical EDB source available to a single query execution: it pins the provider, artifact generation, model, relation predicate, positional RDF 1.2 argument schema, annotation dimension and algebra, total ordering, and preservation claim. It describes derived query inputs, never asserted ontology facts, and it has no ambient mutable registry. Authored canonically in crates/logic (Rust); this class is a lossy documentation projection (Principle 17)."
msgstr "对单次查询执行可用的一个取关系值的物理 EDB 源的不可变声明：它固定提供方、工件世代、模型、关系谓词、按位 RDF 1.2 参数模式、注解维度与代数、全序以及保持声明。它描述派生的查询输入，绝非已断言的本体事实，并且没有任何环境可变注册表。在 crates/logic（Rust）中规范地编写；此类是一种有损的文档投影（原则 17）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/externalRelationProviderManifestHash|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The content address of every immutable query-local provider descriptor, per-call limit, and operation-wide call/row budget. It excludes ambient process state because no global registry participates."
msgstr "每个不可变的查询本地提供方描述符、每次调用限制以及覆盖整个操作的调用/行预算的内容地址。它排除环境进程状态，因为没有任何全局注册表参与其中。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/externalRelationProvider|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Names the stable IRI identity of the provider bound by an external relation descriptor or invocation receipt. This identity is part of the query-local provider manifest and request content address."
msgstr "命名由外部关系描述符或调用回执所绑定的提供方的稳定 IRI 标识。此标识是查询本地提供方清单及请求内容地址的一部分。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/externalRelationQueryContractHash|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The content address of the profile, reasoning budget, annotation contract and algebra, and provider manifest governing a provider-aware query. It is distinct from the whole-engine descriptor hash."
msgstr "管辖某个提供方感知查询的配置文件、推理预算、注解契约与代数以及提供方清单的内容地址。它与整个引擎的描述符哈希相区分。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ExternalRelationQueryReceipt|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The content-addressed success or failure evidence for one provider-aware query, binding its query contract, immutable provider manifest, RDF source generation, engine descriptor, ordered invocation evidence, structural access counters, preservation, and completeness. A success receipt accompanies a complete answer; a failure receipt accompanies a typed non-result and exposes no partial answer set."
msgstr "对一个提供方感知查询的内容寻址成功或失败证据，将其查询契约、不可变提供方清单、RDF 源世代、引擎描述符、有序调用证据、结构性访问计数器、保持以及完整性绑定在一起。成功回执伴随一个完整答案；失败回执伴随一个带类型的非结果，且不暴露任何部分答案集。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/externalRelationReceiptCompleteness|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates an logic:ExternalRelationQueryReceipt to the logic:CompletenessStatus derived from its typed boundary: a success receipt is complete for its pinned fragment, while failure, incompleteness, cancellation, exhaustion, or contract violation is incomplete and never semantic absence."
msgstr "将 logic:ExternalRelationQueryReceipt 关联到由其带类型边界所导出的 logic:CompletenessStatus：成功回执对于其所固定的片段是完整的，而失败、不完整、取消、耗尽或契约违背则是不完整的，且绝非语义缺失。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/externalRelationReceiptHash|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The canonical digest over an external relation query receipt, including source and engine identities, ordered invocation evidence, structural counters, contributors or terminal failure detail. Identical inputs and budgets produce the same value."
msgstr "对外部关系查询回执的规范摘要，包括源与引擎标识、有序调用证据、结构性计数器、贡献者或终态失败细节。相同的输入与预算产生相同的值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/externalRelationRequest|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Names the engine-minted, content-addressed request IRI for one external relation call, derived from the query contract, descriptor, positional bounds, pushed limit, and ordering."
msgstr "命名由引擎铸造、内容寻址的、用于一次外部关系调用的请求 IRI，它由查询契约、描述符、按位边界、所推送的限制以及排序派生而来。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/externalRelationResponseHash|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The canonical response digest of a complete validated provider batch, including descriptor identity, RDF 1.2 arguments, order keys, and algebra-canonical annotation elements. It is absent on non-complete attempts."
msgstr "对完整且已校验的提供方批次的规范响应摘要，包括描述符标识、RDF 1.2 参数、排序键以及按代数规范化的注解元素。在非完整的尝试上它缺省不存在。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/externalRelationRowBudget|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The maximum number of unique validated provider tuples an logic:ExternalRelationBudget permits the whole query to admit. A complete batch that would cross it is rejected atomically."
msgstr "logic:ExternalRelationBudget 允许整个查询接纳的、唯一且已校验的提供方元组的最大数量。会越过该上限的完整批次会被原子性地拒绝。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ExternalSignal|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A situation type the engine can learn of ONLY by external notification — a manual notification, a callback, a sensor reading, an external service response — never by computing it from the state. The thing a logic:NotificationWaitSchema logic:awaitsSignal: until the signal obtains (the engine is told), a wait on it is pending. It marks the descriptive-side input at the prescriptive-descriptive seam, distinct from a logic:precondition the engine evaluates over facts it already holds."
msgstr "引擎只能通过外部通知得知的一种情形类型——手动通知、回调、传感器读数、外部服务响应——绝不能由引擎从状态中计算得出。这正是 logic:NotificationWaitSchema 通过 logic:awaitsSignal 所等待的东西：在信号成立（引擎被告知）之前，针对它的等待处于挂起状态。它标记规定性-描述性接缝处描述侧的输入，区别于引擎在其已持有事实上求值的 logic:precondition。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Fallback|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The fallback program combinator: attempts the primary sub-program (logic:leftOperand); if it fails (the primary executional entailment does not hold from the current state), executes the alternate sub-program (logic:rightOperand). It is a PROGRAM combinator over the transaction layer path semantics, typed APART from action-level logic:compensation: a compensation undoes the EFFECT of an action that ran and reached an outcome, recovering from a realized nondeterministic outcome branch, while logic:Fallback is a STRUCTURAL OPERATOR that routes control to an alternate path when the primary program cannot succeed from the current state. The two sub-programs are binary, carried by logic:leftOperand (the primary) and logic:rightOperand (the alternate), reusing the same properties logic:SerialConjunction and logic:Choice use. A plan strong-cyclic success through recoverable failures is the quantification-level counterpart: logic:Fallback is the operator that makes recovery structurally expressible in the program body."
msgstr "回退程序组合子：它尝试主子程序（logic:leftOperand）；若其失败（主执行蕴涵从当前状态无法成立），则执行备用子程序（logic:rightOperand）。它是作用于事务层路径语义之上的一个程序组合子，其类型与动作级的 logic:compensation 相区隔：补偿撤销一个已运行并达到某结果的动作的效果，从一个已实现的非确定性结果分支中恢复，而 logic:Fallback 是一个结构性运算符，当主程序从当前状态无法成功时将控制路由到备用路径。这两个子程序是二元的，由 logic:leftOperand（主）与 logic:rightOperand（备）承载，复用 logic:SerialConjunction 与 logic:Choice 所用的相同属性。经由可恢复失败取得的计划强循环成功是量化层面的对应物：logic:Fallback 正是使恢复在程序体中结构性可表达的运算符。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FeasibilityStatus|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The closed value class of the feasibility axis of a logic:GoalEvaluation: whether the goal is reachable from the situation it is judged against. Its individuals are logic:Feasible (a path to the goal exists), logic:Blocked (no path exists in the current situation but the obstruction may lift), logic:Infeasible (no path exists in any reachable situation), and logic:FeasibilityUnknown (the feasibility question has not been settled). The set is closed; a misspelt value is rejected. This axis varies independently of satisfaction, lifecycle, and goal-evaluation status — a goal may be partial in satisfaction, blocked in feasibility, and active in lifecycle at once."
msgstr "logic:GoalEvaluation 可行性轴的封闭值类：目标从据以评判它的情形出发是否可达。其个体为 logic:Feasible（通往目标的路径存在）、logic:Blocked（当前情形中无路径存在但障碍可能解除）、logic:Infeasible（在任何可达情形中都无路径存在）以及 logic:FeasibilityUnknown（可行性问题尚未裁定）。该集合是封闭的；拼写错误的值会被拒绝。此轴与满足度、生命周期及目标评估状态相互独立地变化——一个目标可以同时在满足度上是部分的、在可行性上被阻塞、并在生命周期中处于活动状态。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/feasibilityStatus|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:GoalEvaluation to the logic:FeasibilityStatus it carries — the feasibility axis of the factored outcome. Domain logic:GoalEvaluation, range logic:FeasibilityStatus (stated in prose). Varies independently of satisfaction, lifecycle, and goal-evaluation status."
msgstr "将 logic:GoalEvaluation 关联到它所携带的 logic:FeasibilityStatus——分解结果的可行性轴。定义域 logic:GoalEvaluation，值域 logic:FeasibilityStatus（以散文陈述）。与满足度、生命周期及目标评估状态相互独立地变化。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FeasibilityUnknown|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:FeasibilityStatus value when the reachability question has not been settled — the engine has neither found a path nor proved none exists. The first-class fourth value, kept distinct from logic:Blocked so an unexamined goal is never silently read as obstructed."
msgstr "当可达性问题尚未裁定时的 logic:FeasibilityStatus 值——引擎既未找到路径，也未证明不存在路径。这是头等的第四个值，与 logic:Blocked 保持区分，以使未经检验的目标绝不会被默默解读为受阻。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Feasible|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:FeasibilityStatus value for a goal a path can reach from the situation it is judged against — the goal is achievable. Contrast logic:Blocked (no current path, but the obstruction may lift) and logic:Infeasible (no path in any reachable situation)."
msgstr "对于某条路径能从据以评判它的情形出发到达的目标的 logic:FeasibilityStatus 值——目标是可实现的。与 logic:Blocked（当前无路径，但障碍可能解除）及 logic:Infeasible（在任何可达情形中都无路径）形成对照。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FindingCategory|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The closed value class of a validator finding's KIND — an axis orthogonal to its severity, because not all findings are failures. Its individuals are logic:FindingDataShapeViolation, logic:FindingModelingDisciplineViolation, logic:FindingContradictionWitness, logic:FindingPermittedEpistemicConflict, logic:FindingUnsupportedSemanticFeature, logic:FindingIncompleteCheck, logic:FindingProjectionLoss, logic:FindingPolicyWarning, logic:FindingCorroboration and logic:FindingTransientChatter. The set is closed; a misspelt value names no declared kind and is rejected. The load-bearing case is logic:FindingPermittedEpistemicConflict: a disclosed, witnessed contradiction permitted by a glut-admitting contract is coherent and does NOT fail the gate; the mirror case is logic:FindingCorroboration, a native↔published agreement folded as non-blocking positive evidence rather than dropped; logic:FindingTransientChatter is the non-gating chatter kind for general-purpose logging witnesses (design/LOGIC-CONFORMANCE.md, §The coherence certificate)."
msgstr "验证器发现之种类的封闭值类——一个与其严重性正交的轴，因为并非所有发现都是失败。其个体为 logic:FindingDataShapeViolation、logic:FindingModelingDisciplineViolation、logic:FindingContradictionWitness、logic:FindingPermittedEpistemicConflict、logic:FindingUnsupportedSemanticFeature、logic:FindingIncompleteCheck、logic:FindingProjectionLoss、logic:FindingPolicyWarning、logic:FindingCorroboration 与 logic:FindingTransientChatter。该集合是封闭的；拼写错误的值不命名任何已声明的种类，会被拒绝。承重的情形是 logic:FindingPermittedEpistemicConflict：由一个容纳过剩的契约所许可的、经披露并有见证的矛盾是融贯的，且不会使该关卡失败；镜像情形是 logic:FindingCorroboration，一种被折叠为非阻塞正面证据而非被丢弃的原生↔已发布一致；logic:FindingTransientChatter 是用于通用日志见证的非把关闲谈种类（design/LOGIC-CONFORMANCE.md，§The coherence certificate）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FindingContradictionWitness|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:FindingCategory for a within-world contradiction (a logic:InfoBoth glut) that the governing contract FORBIDS — an unpermitted, integrity-violating inconsistency. A failure. Distinguished from logic:FindingPermittedEpistemicConflict purely by the contract's logic:contradictionPolicy. Wire value `contradiction-witness`."
msgstr "对于管辖契约所禁止的世界内矛盾（一个 logic:InfoBoth 过剩）的 logic:FindingCategory——一种不被许可、违反完整性的不一致。属于失败。它与 logic:FindingPermittedEpistemicConflict 的区分纯粹取决于契约的 logic:contradictionPolicy。线值 `contradiction-witness`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FindingCorroboration|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:FindingCategory for a native↔published AGREEMENT — the native reasoner's verdict matches the community-decided ground truth of an external-corpus case. NOT a failure and the exact opposite of a logic:FindingIncompleteCheck: it is positive corroborating evidence surfaced for the benchmark surface, coherent, and never blocks a logic:CoherenceCertificate. It is the honest, non-blocking kind an agreeing external-corpus comparison folds as, so agreements are retained as first-class findings rather than dropped. Wire value `corroboration`."
msgstr "对于原生↔已发布一致的 logic:FindingCategory——原生推理器的裁决与外部语料案例中由社区裁定的基准真值相符。它不是失败，而是 logic:FindingIncompleteCheck 的截然相反：它是为基准面呈现的正面佐证证据，融贯，且绝不阻塞 logic:CoherenceCertificate。它是一致的外部语料比较所折叠成的诚实、非阻塞种类，从而使一致被保留为头等发现而非被丢弃。线值 `corroboration`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FindingDataShapeViolation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:FindingCategory for a closed-world data-shape constraint breach — a SHACL shape an instance failed. A failure. Wire value `data-shape-violation`."
msgstr "对于闭世界数据形状约束破坏的 logic:FindingCategory——某实例未通过的一个 SHACL 形状。属于失败。线值 `data-shape-violation`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FindingIncompleteCheck|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:FindingCategory for a check that did not run to completion — a logic:BudgetExhausted or logic:Incomplete evaluation. Records that the search was bounded; it is the reason a bounded run yields a logic:CoherenceCheckAttestation rather than a logic:CoherenceCertificate. Not a failure of the data. Wire value `incomplete-check`."
msgstr "对于未运行至完成的检查的 logic:FindingCategory——一次 logic:BudgetExhausted 或 logic:Incomplete 求值。它记录该搜索是有界的；这正是有界运行产出 logic:CoherenceCheckAttestation 而非 logic:CoherenceCertificate 的原因。并非数据的失败。线值 `incomplete-check`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FindingModelingDisciplineViolation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:FindingCategory for an ontology modeling-discipline breach — a structural/gUFO-tier rule the vocabulary itself violates, or an unsatisfiable class surfaced by reasoning. A failure. Wire value `modeling-discipline-violation`."
msgstr "对于本体建模纪律破坏的 logic:FindingCategory——词汇表自身违反的一条结构性/gUFO 层级规则，或由推理呈现出的一个不可满足类。属于失败。线值 `modeling-discipline-violation`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FindingPermittedEpistemicConflict|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:FindingCategory for a disclosed, witnessed contradiction that a glut-admitting contract PERMITS — exactly the behaviour the paraconsistent contract anticipates. NOT a failure: it is coherent, surfaced for transparency, and does NOT block a logic:CoherenceCertificate. The load-bearing case for the principle that not all findings are failures. Wire value `permitted-epistemic-conflict`."
msgstr "对于一个容纳过剩的契约所许可的、经披露并有见证的矛盾的 logic:FindingCategory——恰是次协调契约所预期的行为。它不是失败：它是融贯的，为透明起见予以呈现，且不阻塞 logic:CoherenceCertificate。这是支撑并非所有发现都是失败这一原则的承重情形。线值 `permitted-epistemic-conflict`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FindingPolicyWarning|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:FindingCategory for a trust/policy advisory — an untrusted signer, a missing-but-not-required attestation, a soft governance note. Advisory, not a hard failure. Wire value `policy-warning`."
msgstr "对于信任/策略性提示的 logic:FindingCategory——一个不受信任的签名者、一份缺失但非必需的证明、一条柔性治理备注。属咨询性质，而非硬失败。线值 `policy-warning`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FindingProjectionLoss|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:FindingCategory for a construct a lowering could not carry exactly — a warning that an answer was produced through a projection whose preservation claim drops or approximates some constructs (the loss ledger). Not a failure; a fidelity disclosure. Wire value `projection-loss`."
msgstr "当某构造被降级无法精确承载时所用的 logic:FindingCategory ——一条警告，表明某答案是经由某投影产生的，而该投影的保持声明会丢弃或近似某些构造（损失账本）。这并非失败；而是一种保真度披露。线值 `projection-loss`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FindingTransientChatter|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The closed CHATTER logic:FindingCategory for general-purpose logging witnesses — the ordinary note/info stream a run emits to narrate its own progress. Never a failure and never a coherence stance: it is transient bookkeeping that carries no evidential weight, contributes nothing to the gate, and can never block a logic:CoherenceCertificate. The home category for a Note or Info witness that records what happened without asserting anything about the data. Wire value `transient-chatter`."
msgstr "用于通用日志见证的封闭 CHATTER logic:FindingCategory ——即一次运行为叙述自身进展而发出的普通注记/信息流。它绝非失败，也绝非一致性立场：它是一种瞬态记账，不承载任何证据分量，对门控毫无贡献，且永远无法阻断一个 logic:CoherenceCertificate。它是记录已发生之事而不对数据作任何断言的 Note 或 Info 见证的归属类别。线值 `transient-chatter`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FindingUnsupportedSemanticFeature|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:FindingCategory for a construct the engine has no defined procedure for under the governing contract — a logic:EvaluationUnsupported outcome on a feature outside the certified fragment. A disclosure, not a defect of the data. Wire value `unsupported-semantic-feature`."
msgstr "用于引擎在管辖契约下没有既定处理程序之构造的 logic:FindingCategory ——对已认证片段之外某特性给出的 logic:EvaluationUnsupported 结果。这是一次披露，而非数据的缺陷。线值 `unsupported-semantic-feature`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FirstOrder|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The expressiveness boundary of a defining statement authorable as a first-order logic:Formula (∀/∃ over individuals of the reified signature). First-order mathematical laws — continuity, connectedness, the T0–T4 separation axioms — sit here; the grounding peers author them as logic:Formula objects at this boundary."
msgstr "可作为一阶 logic:Formula 撰写的定义性陈述的表达力边界（对具体化签名的个体施加 ∀/∃）。一阶数学定律——连续性、连通性、T0–T4 分离公理——位于此处；接地对等体将它们撰写为处于此边界的 logic:Formula 对象。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FixedCollection|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A logic:Collection with fixed membership: its members (via logic:memberOf) do not change over its existence, so gaining or losing a member yields a different collection — a specific deck of 52 cards, the founding signatories of a treaty. The counterpart of gufo:FixedCollection. Stated in prose, not as a subclass edge. Because membership is invariant across worlds the membership relation reads rigidly; contrast logic:VariableCollection."
msgstr "具有固定成员资格的 logic:Collection：其成员（经由 logic:memberOf）在其存在期间不发生变化，因此获得或失去一个成员便产生一个不同的集合——例如某副确定的 52 张牌、一份条约的创始签署方。它是 gufo:FixedCollection 的对应物。以散文表述，而非作为子类边。由于成员资格跨世界保持不变，成员关系被读作刚性的；与 logic:VariableCollection 相对照。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FlagshipScenarioFailureClassConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Requires every logic:-namespaced failure class named by a flagship scenario to be a logic:LogicConformanceFailure or one of its subclasses. Namespace-scoped: the three grounding slices each contribute a failure-range gate over the ONE shared gmeow:FlagshipScenario class, so each validates exactly the failure classes it owns — an unscoped gate would demand every scenario reach every slice's root at once."
msgstr "要求由旗舰场景命名的每个 logic: 命名空间失败类都是一个 logic:LogicConformanceFailure 或其某个子类。按命名空间限定：三个接地切片各自在那唯一共享的 gmeow:FlagshipScenario 类上贡献一个失败值域门控，因此各自恰好校验它所拥有的失败类——一个不限定的门控会要求每个场景同时抵达每个切片的根。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/flowFrom|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a reified flow edge (logic:ControlFlowEdge or logic:DataFlowEdge) to its source process node — the predecessor in a control-flow edge, the producer in a dataflow edge. Domain a flow edge, range a process node (stated in prose). Paired with logic:flowTo; the two mediation legs that make a flow edge a well-formed Relator."
msgstr "将一条具体化的流边（logic:ControlFlowEdge 或 logic:DataFlowEdge）关联到其源过程节点——在控制流边中即前驱，在数据流边中即生产者。定义域为一条流边，值域为一个过程节点（以散文表述）。与 logic:flowTo 配对；这两条中介支腿使一条流边成为良构的 Relator。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/flowTo|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a reified flow edge (logic:ControlFlowEdge or logic:DataFlowEdge) to its target process node — the successor in a control-flow edge, the consumer in a dataflow edge. Domain a flow edge, range a process node (stated in prose). Paired with logic:flowFrom."
msgstr "将一条具体化的流边（logic:ControlFlowEdge 或 logic:DataFlowEdge）关联到其目标过程节点——在控制流边中即后继，在数据流边中即消费者。定义域为一条流边，值域为一个过程节点（以散文表述）。与 logic:flowFrom 配对。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Fluent|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A value or relation indexed to time (and world): a time-varying property whose truth changes across moments — an object's location, an account's balance, a temperature reading. The native temporal-fluent construct of the four-dimensional treatment (criticism 3), pairing with Principle-11 frame-relativity so each temporal value lives in an explicit reference system rather than as a bare literal."
msgstr "一个按时间（及世界）索引的值或关系：一种随时间变化的属性，其真值跨时刻改变——某对象的位置、某账户的余额、一次温度读数。这是四维处理（批评 3）的原生时序流量构造，与原则 11 的参照系相对性相配对，使每个时序值驻留于一个显式参照系中，而非作为裸字面量。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FOLFragment|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The formula-fragment facet value selecting unrestricted first-order formulae. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract; the most expressive (and only semi-decidable) fragment, against which the Horn, Datalog, and existential-rules values are the decidability-bought restrictions."
msgstr "选定无限制一阶公式的公式片段侧面值。在 ReasoningContract 上为单值；这是表达力最强（且仅为半可判定）的片段，相较之下 Horn、Datalog 与存在规则各值是以牺牲可判定性换取的限制。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/forall|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a universal-quantifier logic:Formula to its body formula. The bound variables are carried by logic:quantifiedVariable; their block order is significant. Universal quantification ranges over individuals in the domain of discourse (the object level stays first-order). It is not iteration over RDF serialization order or a higher-order predicate binder."
msgstr "将一个全称量词 logic:Formula 关联到其主体公式。被约束变量由 logic:quantifiedVariable 承载；其块次序具有意义。全称量化遍历论域中的个体（对象层级保持一阶）。它既不是对 RDF 序列化次序的迭代，也不是高阶谓词绑定器。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/forall|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A universal node can bind x and point logic:forall to person(x) implies mortal(x)."
msgstr "全称量词节点可以绑定 x 并将 logic:forall 指向 person(x) implies mortal(x)。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/forbiddenPredicate|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The forbidden predicate of a logic:ForbiddenPatternConstraint: the focus must carry no value on this predicate (or, when logic:forbiddenValue is present, not that specific value)."
msgstr "一个 logic:ForbiddenPatternConstraint 的被禁谓词：焦点在该谓词上不得携带任何值（或者，当 logic:forbiddenValue 存在时，不得携带那个特定值）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/forbiddenValue|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "An optional fixed object value that narrows a logic:ForbiddenPatternConstraint to forbid only forbiddenPredicate(this, value) rather than any value on the predicate. An IRI or a literal."
msgstr "一个可选的固定对象值，它收窄一个 logic:ForbiddenPatternConstraint，使其仅禁止 forbiddenPredicate(this, value)，而非该谓词上的任意值。可为一个 IRI 或一个字面量。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/forbiddenViolationWitness|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a coherence outcome to a within-world contradiction the contract FORBIDS (a logic:FindingContradictionWitness) — MULTI-valued. A NON-EMPTY set blocks issuance: a logic:CoherenceCertificate is issued only when this set is empty. Domain logic:CoherenceCertificate or logic:CoherenceCheckAttestation (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将一个一致性结果关联到契约所禁止的一个世界内矛盾（一个 logic:FindingContradictionWitness）——多值。一个非空集合会阻断签发：仅在此集合为空时才签发一个 logic:CoherenceCertificate。定义域为 logic:CoherenceCertificate 或 logic:CoherenceCheckAttestation（以散文表述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ForbidGapAndGlut|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The admissible-valuation policy that forbids both the neither gap and the both glut, leaving exactly true and false. It carves classical logic out of the Belnap algebra; combined with logic:DesignateTrueOnly it recovers ordinary two-valued entailment."
msgstr "禁止「二者皆非」空隙与「二者兼有」过剩、恰好留下真与假的可容许赋值策略。它从 Belnap 代数中切分出经典逻辑；与 logic:DesignateTrueOnly 结合，它恢复了普通的二值蕴涵。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ForbidGap|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The admissible-valuation policy that forbids the neither gap while admitting the both glut — every atom is at least true or false, but may be both. It carves out the Logic of Paradox (LP). FDE and LP share the designated set true,both; LP differs from FDE by forbidding the gap, not by its designated values — reducing the FDE↔LP difference to designated values is a formal error."
msgstr "禁止「二者皆非」空隙而容许「二者兼有」过剩的可容许赋值策略——每个原子至少为真或为假，但可以二者兼有。它切分出悖论逻辑（LP）。FDE 与 LP 共享指定集合 真,二者；LP 与 FDE 的区别在于禁止空隙，而非在于其指定值——把 FDE↔LP 的差异归结为指定值是一个形式错误。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ForbidGlut|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The admissible-valuation policy that forbids the both glut while admitting the neither gap — every atom is at most true or false, but may be neither. It carves out Strong Kleene logic (K3), the dual restriction to logic:ForbidGap; the difference between K3 and the gap-admitting logics lies in this admissible-valuation set, not in the designated values."
msgstr "禁止「二者兼有」过剩而容许「二者皆非」空隙的可容许赋值策略——每个原子至多为真或为假，但可以二者皆非。它切分出强 Kleene 逻辑（K3），即 logic:ForbidGap 的对偶限制；K3 与容许空隙的逻辑之间的区别在于此可容许赋值集合，而非在于指定值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FormalizationCandidate|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A typed, reviewable proposal to turn a prose constraint into a formal axiom: the governed unit of the prose-to-axiom transition. It carries its source-text hash (logic:candidateSourceHash), extraction provenance (logic:candidateExtractionProvenance), intended scope (logic:candidateScope) and reasoning contract (logic:candidateContract, ME1), its logic:FormalizationCategory, its logic:CandidateLifecycleState and reviewer decision (logic:reviewedBy), a positive competency case and a negative countermodel (logic:candidatePositiveCase / logic:candidateNegativeCase), any required logic:NonEntailmentObligation (logic:candidateNonEntailment), its projection behaviour (logic:candidateProjectionBehavior) and its logic:SemanticRiskClass. An LLM extraction always enters as a candidate, never directly as an accepted axiom; only a candidate promoted through review becomes canonical (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, §Typed formalization governance)."
msgstr "一个带类型的、可审阅的提案，用以将一条散文约束转化为形式公理：即散文到公理转变过程中受治理的单元。它携带其源文本哈希（logic:candidateSourceHash）、抽取来源（logic:candidateExtractionProvenance）、拟定范围（logic:candidateScope）与推理契约（logic:candidateContract，ME1）、其 logic:FormalizationCategory、其 logic:CandidateLifecycleState 及审阅者裁决（logic:reviewedBy）、一个正向胜任案例与一个负向反模型（logic:candidatePositiveCase / logic:candidateNegativeCase）、任何所需的 logic:NonEntailmentObligation（logic:candidateNonEntailment）、其投影行为（logic:candidateProjectionBehavior）以及其 logic:SemanticRiskClass。一次 LLM 抽取始终作为候选进入，绝不直接作为已接受的公理；唯有经审阅晋升的候选才成为规范（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，§Typed formalization governance）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FormalizationCategory|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The closed eleven-member value class of the logic:candidateCategory facet: the kind of force a prose constraint was meant to carry. Its individuals are logic:CategoryEquivalenceDefinition, logic:CategoryNecessaryCondition, logic:CategorySufficientCondition, logic:CategoryIntegrityConstraint, logic:CategoryDerivationRule, logic:CategoryDefeasibleDefault, logic:CategoryTypicality, logic:CategoryRecommendation, logic:CategoryNonEntailmentObligation, logic:CategoryDeliberateOverlap and logic:CategoryDocumentationOnly. The set is closed and atomic (Principle 9: necessary and sufficient are two categories, not one), so a misspelt label names no declared category and is rejected rather than silently accepted (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, §Typed formalization governance)."
msgstr "logic:candidateCategory 侧面的封闭十一成员值类：一条散文约束本应承载的力度种类。其个体为 logic:CategoryEquivalenceDefinition、logic:CategoryNecessaryCondition、logic:CategorySufficientCondition、logic:CategoryIntegrityConstraint、logic:CategoryDerivationRule、logic:CategoryDefeasibleDefault、logic:CategoryTypicality、logic:CategoryRecommendation、logic:CategoryNonEntailmentObligation、logic:CategoryDeliberateOverlap 以及 logic:CategoryDocumentationOnly。该集合是封闭且原子的（原则 9：必要与充分是两个类别，而非一个），因此拼写错误的标签不命名任何已声明的类别，会被拒绝而非被默默接受（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，§Typed formalization governance）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/formalizes|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A bridge annotation from a logic: foundational term to the gmeow: domain concept it formalizes: the central reasoning vocabulary (argumentation semantics, Belnap information states) names the domain construct that mirrors it, so the domain term's documentation can surface the formalization without the domain slice ever asserting a logic: triple. Subject is a logic: term, object a gmeow: term, both stated in prose; an annotation property, never a reasoned axiom, so it carries no DL or EL profile weight."
msgstr "从一个 logic: 基础词项到它所形式化的 gmeow: 领域概念的一条桥接注解：核心推理词汇（论证语义、Belnap 信息状态）命名映照它的领域构造，从而领域词项的文档可以呈现该形式化，而领域切片却从不断言任何 logic: 三元组。主语是一个 logic: 词项，宾语是一个 gmeow: 词项，二者均以散文表述；这是一个注解属性，绝非经推理的公理，因此它不承载任何 DL 或 EL 规格分量。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FormulaFragment|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The facet value class of the formula-fragment facet: the syntactic class of formulae a rule set is admitted from. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract. Its individuals range from unrestricted first-order through Horn and Datalog to existential rules, fixing both expressivity and the decidability ceiling."
msgstr "公式片段侧面的侧面值类：一个规则集所准入的公式的句法类别。在 ReasoningContract 上为单值。其个体自无限制一阶，经 Horn 与 Datalog，直至存在规则，同时确定表达力与可判定性上限。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/formulaFragment|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to the logic:FormulaFragment it selects — the syntactic class of admitted formulae. Single-valued on the contract. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:FormulaFragment (stated in prose, matching the module's convention)."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ReasoningContract 关联到它所选定的 logic:FormulaFragment ——即被准入公式的句法类别。在该契约上为单值。定义域为 logic:ReasoningContract，值域为 logic:FormulaFragment（以散文表述，遵循该模块的约定）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FormulaShape|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The closed class of first-order shape tags a Horn-fragment projection target discloses when it cannot represent a logic:Formula. Each individual names one construct that pushes a formula beyond the binary Horn+NAF fragment, so the loss ledger records which constructs were carried-and-flagged in the canonical logic: layer instead of one opaque note. The set is closed — its individuals are logic:Disjunctive, logic:Nested, logic:Quantified, logic:StrongNegation, and logic:Variadic — so a misspelt tag names no declared value."
msgstr "当一个 Horn 片段投影目标无法表示某 logic:Formula 时所披露的一阶形状标签的封闭类。每个个体命名一种将公式推出二元 Horn+NAF 片段之外的构造，因此损失账本记录哪些构造在规范的 logic: 层中被承载并标记，而非记为一条不透明的注记。该集合是封闭的——其个体为 logic:Disjunctive、logic:Nested、logic:Quantified、logic:StrongNegation 与 logic:Variadic ——因此拼写错误的标签不命名任何已声明的值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FormulaShape|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A formula containing logic:or receives logic:Disjunctive in a Horn projection's residue ledger."
msgstr "包含 logic:or 的公式在 Horn 投影的残差账本中会获得 logic:Disjunctive。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Formula|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A first-order formula node: the reified AST node a non-Horn logic: statement compiles into. A logic:Formula is a quantifier (carrying logic:forall or logic:exists over a body and one or more logic:quantifiedVariable bindings), a connective (logic:and, logic:or, logic:not, logic:antecedent with logic:consequent, or logic:iff over sub-formulae), or an atomic predication (logic:relation over ordered logic:argument terms). It is the unified full-FOL core of which Horn+NAF derivation rules are a recognized sub-fragment; the canonical RDF 1.2 serialization round-trips it losslessly, while weaker projections carry any formula they cannot express as flagged unsupported residue."
msgstr "一个一阶公式节点：一条非 Horn 的 logic: 陈述所编译成的具体化 AST 节点。一个 logic:Formula 是一个量词（在一个主体及一个或多个 logic:quantifiedVariable 绑定上承载 logic:forall 或 logic:exists）、一个联结词（在子公式上承载 logic:and、logic:or、logic:not、logic:antecedent 配合 logic:consequent，或 logic:iff），或一个原子谓述（在有序的 logic:argument 词项上承载 logic:relation）。它是统一的完整 FOL 核心，Horn+NAF 派生规则是其一个公认的子片段；规范的 RDF 1.2 序列化对它无损往返，而较弱的投影则将它们无法表达的任何公式作为被标记的不受支持残余加以承载。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Formula|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The tree for every person knows someone is a logic:forall node whose body is a logic:exists node containing a logic:relation atom."
msgstr "「every person knows someone」的语法树是一个 logic:forall 节点，其主体是一个包含 logic:relation 原子的 logic:exists 节点。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/forwardContractHash|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The content-addressed identity of the FORWARD reasoning contract — the EL/DL/RL materialization (chase) engine's own contract hash — folded into a logic:EngineContract so ONE descriptor pins both engine directions. It is the same value a forward reasoning run records as logic:contractHash on its logic:ReasoningResult: the engine contract carries the forward identity so a consumer can pin the materializer without first executing a query. Single-valued. Domain logic:EngineContract (stated in prose). NON-CONFLATION with logic:backwardSourceHash (the independent backward goal-resolution surface) and with logic:engineContractDescriptorHash (the whole-descriptor address that FOLDS this value in among others). Authored canonically in crates/logic (Rust); a lossy documentation projection (Principle 17). Normative in design/LOGIC-RUNTIME.md, §The forward materialization ↔ backward resolution seam."
msgstr "前向（FORWARD）推理契约的内容寻址身份——即 EL/DL/RL 物化（chase）引擎自身的契约哈希——被折叠进一个 logic:EngineContract，从而单个描述符即钉住引擎的两个方向。它与一次前向推理运行在其 logic:ReasoningResult 上记录为 logic:contractHash 的值相同：引擎契约携带前向身份，使消费者无需先执行查询即可钉住物化器。单值。定义域为 logic:EngineContract（以散文表述）。不得与 logic:backwardSourceHash（独立的后向目标求解面）以及 logic:engineContractDescriptorHash（把此值连同其他值一并折叠进去的整描述符地址）相混淆。在 crates/logic（Rust）中规范地撰写；这是一个有损的文档投影（原则 17）。规范见于 design/LOGIC-RUNTIME.md，§The forward materialization ↔ backward resolution seam。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FreeRole|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The OntoUML FreeRole anti-pattern: an anti-rigid sortal (Role or Phase) must specialize a rigid sortal from which to inherit a principle of identity. An anti-rigid sortal with no rigid (Kind/SubKind) ancestor violates it. One half of the lowering of reasoning_lint.anti_rigidity_discipline."
msgstr "OntoUML 的 FreeRole 反模式：一个反刚性可数类元（Role 或 Phase）必须特化一个刚性可数类元，以从中继承同一性原则。一个没有刚性（Kind/SubKind）祖先的反刚性可数类元违反了它。这是 reasoning_lint.anti_rigidity_discipline 降级的一半。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FreshnessGuard|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A valid-time currency guard on an action-schema precondition. It declares that the datum supporting a logic:precondition (via logic:guardsPrecondition) is relied upon only when it passes TWO INDEPENDENT valid-time axes. (1) AGE HORIZON: the datum's age — the span from its logic:datumRecordedAt to the probe's logic:decisionTime — is within a declared logic:freshnessHorizon (an xsd:duration ceiling on how OLD the value may be). (2) EXPLICIT VALID-TIME WINDOW: when the guard declares a logic:freshnessWindow, the probe's logic:decisionTime must fall inside the closed absolute interval [logic:freshnessWindowStart, logic:freshnessWindowEnd] — the datum is authoritative only WITHIN that named bounding interval (e.g. 'the current episode'), regardless of how recently it was recorded. The two axes are ORTHOGONAL and neither implies the other: a datum can pass the age horizon yet fall outside the window, or vice versa. Each axis is OPTIONAL and imposes no constraint when absent (a guard may carry horizon only, window only, both, or neither). Outside either bound the datum is undetermined, not stale-but-used: the action gate yields logic:GateUndetermined rather than admitting on an out-of-window / out-of-date value or denying on a value that merely aged or is off-episode. This is GMEOW's native, canonical generalization of a decision-rule 'currency' annotation (max age → horizon) AND its 'time_window' annotation (an explicit named bounding interval → window) — the valid-time freshness discipline the typed context algebra applies, executed at the action gate."
msgstr "作用于动作模式前置条件上的一个有效时间时效守卫。它声明：支撑某 logic:precondition 的基准数据（经由 logic:guardsPrecondition）仅在其通过两条互相独立的有效时间轴时才被采信。(1) 年龄视界：该基准数据的年龄——自其 logic:datumRecordedAt 至探针的 logic:decisionTime 之间的跨度——处于一个已声明的 logic:freshnessHorizon 之内（一个 xsd:duration 上限，规定该值最多可有多旧）。(2) 显式有效时间窗口：一旦守卫声明了一个 logic:freshnessWindow，探针的 logic:decisionTime 便须落入闭合的绝对区间 [logic:freshnessWindowStart, logic:freshnessWindowEnd] 之内——该基准数据仅在那个具名的界定区间（例如「当前情节」）内部才具权威性，而不论其记录有多近。这两条轴是正交的，彼此互不蕴含：一条基准数据可以通过年龄视界却落于窗口之外，反之亦然。每条轴都是可选的，缺席时不施加任何约束（一个守卫可以仅带视界、仅带窗口、二者皆带或二者皆无）。一旦超出任一边界，该基准数据即为未定，而非过期仍用：动作门控产出 logic:GateUndetermined，而不是在一个窗外/过期的值上准入，也不是在一个仅仅变旧或脱离情节的值上拒绝。这是 GMEOW 对决策规则「currency」注解（最大年龄 → 视界）以及其「time_window」注解（一个显式具名的界定区间 → 窗口）的原生、规范推广——即带类型上下文代数所施加、在动作门控处执行的有效时间时效纪律。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/freshnessGuard|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ActionSchema to a logic:FreshnessGuard it carries — the valid-time currency guard on one of its preconditions. Domain logic:ActionSchema, range logic:FreshnessGuard (stated in prose). MULTI-valued: a schema may guard several preconditions, each with its own horizon."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ActionSchema 关联到它所携带的一个 logic:FreshnessGuard ——即作用于其某个前置条件上的有效时间时效守卫。定义域为 logic:ActionSchema，值域为 logic:FreshnessGuard（以散文表述）。多值：一个模式可守护若干前置条件，各自拥有自身的视界。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FreshnessGuardWindowBoundsConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A closed-world integrity constraint: a logic:FreshnessGuard declaring a logic:freshnessWindow carries both a logic:freshnessWindowStart and a logic:freshnessWindowEnd — a half-declared window gates on an ill-defined interval."
msgstr "一条闭世界完整性约束：一个声明了 logic:freshnessWindow 的 logic:FreshnessGuard 同时携带一个 logic:freshnessWindowStart 与一个 logic:freshnessWindowEnd ——一个半声明的窗口会在一个界定不清的区间上进行门控。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/freshnessHorizon|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The maximum admissible age of a guarded precondition datum, as an xsd:duration measured from the datum's logic:datumRecordedAt to the probe's logic:decisionTime. Domain logic:FreshnessGuard, range xsd:duration (stated in prose). Only fixed-length designators are admissible (weeks / days / hours / minutes / seconds); a nominal-length designator (years / months, which are not fixed spans) is a hard error, because the age comparison would be ill-defined."
msgstr "被守护的前置条件基准数据的最大可容许年龄，作为一个 xsd:duration，自该基准数据的 logic:datumRecordedAt 度量至探针的 logic:decisionTime。定义域为 logic:FreshnessGuard，值域为 xsd:duration（以散文表述）。仅固定长度的指示符可容许（周／日／时／分／秒）；名义长度的指示符（年／月，它们并非固定跨度）是硬错误，因为年龄比较将界定不清。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/freshnessWindowEnd|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The inclusive upper bound of a logic:FreshnessGuard's explicit valid-time logic:freshnessWindow, as an xsd:dateTime. Domain logic:FreshnessGuard, range xsd:dateTime (stated in prose). Together with logic:freshnessWindowStart it defines the closed absolute interval [start, end] within which the guarded datum is authoritative; a probe's logic:decisionTime after this end falls outside the window and yields logic:GateUndetermined. This axis is DISTINCT from the age ceiling logic:freshnessHorizon — it bounds WHEN the decision may be taken, not how OLD the datum may be. Required exactly once when a window is declared (paired with logic:freshnessWindowStart); a declared window with a missing bound, a malformed xsd:dateTime, or end before start is a hard error. When no window is declared this bound is absent and the window axis imposes no constraint."
msgstr "一个 logic:FreshnessGuard 的显式有效时间 logic:freshnessWindow 的含端上界，作为一个 xsd:dateTime。定义域为 logic:FreshnessGuard，值域为 xsd:dateTime（以散文表述）。它与 logic:freshnessWindowStart 一同界定闭合的绝对区间 [start, end]，被守护的基准数据在其内部具权威性；探针的 logic:decisionTime 若晚于此终点则落于窗口之外并产出 logic:GateUndetermined。此轴有别于年龄上限 logic:freshnessHorizon ——它界定决策可在何时作出，而非该基准数据最多可有多旧。声明窗口时须恰好出现一次（与 logic:freshnessWindowStart 配对）；一个声明的窗口若缺失某边界、含格式错误的 xsd:dateTime，或终点早于起点，即为硬错误。若未声明任何窗口，则此边界缺席且窗口轴不施加任何约束。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/freshnessWindow|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Marks that a logic:FreshnessGuard carries an EXPLICIT absolute valid-time interval — the closed [logic:freshnessWindowStart, logic:freshnessWindowEnd] window within which the guarded datum is authoritative, DISTINCT from and orthogonal to the age ceiling logic:freshnessHorizon. This is GMEOW's native subsumption of an openEHR decision-rule 'time_window' annotation (a named bounding interval such as 'the current episode'), as opposed to 'currency' (a max age → logic:freshnessHorizon). Domain logic:FreshnessGuard, range a string literal naming the window (stated in prose); the interval bounds are carried by logic:freshnessWindowStart / logic:freshnessWindowEnd. The property is OPTIONAL: ABSENT-WINDOW SEMANTICS impose NO constraint on this axis — a guard with no logic:freshnessWindow is gated by its logic:freshnessHorizon alone (or, if it declares neither, by nothing). When PRESENT, a probe whose logic:decisionTime falls OUTSIDE the closed interval yields logic:GateUndetermined (not admitted, not denied) — the datum is undetermined off-window, never stale-but-used — with a logic:gateUndeterminedReason naming the window bounds and the decision time. Independent of the age horizon: a datum can be within its horizon yet outside its window, or vice versa; the first axis to fail is reported."
msgstr "标记一个 logic:FreshnessGuard 携带一个显式的绝对有效时间区间——即闭合的 [logic:freshnessWindowStart, logic:freshnessWindowEnd] 窗口，被守护的基准数据在其内部具权威性；它有别于年龄上限 logic:freshnessHorizon 并与之正交。这是 GMEOW 对一条 openEHR 决策规则「time_window」注解（一个具名界定区间，例如「当前情节」）的原生涵摄，与「currency」（一个最大年龄 → logic:freshnessHorizon）相对。定义域为 logic:FreshnessGuard，值域为一个命名该窗口的字符串字面量（以散文表述）；区间边界由 logic:freshnessWindowStart / logic:freshnessWindowEnd 承载。该属性是可选的：窗口缺席语义在此轴上不施加任何约束——一个没有 logic:freshnessWindow 的守卫仅由其 logic:freshnessHorizon 单独门控（或者，若二者皆未声明，则不受任何约束）。当其存在时，一个 logic:decisionTime 落于闭合区间之外的探针产出 logic:GateUndetermined（既不准入也不拒绝）——该基准数据在窗外为未定，绝非过期仍用——并附带一个命名窗口边界与决策时刻的 logic:gateUndeterminedReason。它独立于年龄视界：一条基准数据可以处于其视界之内却在其窗口之外，反之亦然；首先失败的那条轴会被报告。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/freshnessWindowStart|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The inclusive lower bound of a logic:FreshnessGuard's explicit valid-time logic:freshnessWindow, as an xsd:dateTime. Domain logic:FreshnessGuard, range xsd:dateTime (stated in prose). Together with logic:freshnessWindowEnd it defines the closed absolute interval [start, end] within which the guarded datum is authoritative; a probe's logic:decisionTime before this start falls outside the window and yields logic:GateUndetermined. This axis is DISTINCT from the age ceiling logic:freshnessHorizon — it bounds WHEN the decision may be taken, not how OLD the datum may be. Required exactly once when a window is declared (paired with logic:freshnessWindowEnd); a declared window with a missing bound, a malformed xsd:dateTime, or end before start is a hard error. When no window is declared this bound is absent and the window axis imposes no constraint."
msgstr "一个 logic:FreshnessGuard 的显式有效时间 logic:freshnessWindow 的含端下界，作为一个 xsd:dateTime。定义域为 logic:FreshnessGuard，值域为 xsd:dateTime（以散文表述）。它与 logic:freshnessWindowEnd 一同界定闭合的绝对区间 [start, end]，被守护的基准数据在其内部具权威性；探针的 logic:decisionTime 若早于此起点则落于窗口之外并产出 logic:GateUndetermined。此轴有别于年龄上限 logic:freshnessHorizon ——它界定决策可在何时作出，而非该基准数据最多可有多旧。声明窗口时须恰好出现一次（与 logic:freshnessWindowEnd 配对）；一个声明的窗口若缺失某边界、含格式错误的 xsd:dateTime，或终点早于起点，即为硬错误。若未声明任何窗口，则此边界缺席且窗口轴不施加任何约束。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FullIndependence|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The well-known probability model under which every logic:probability fact is an independent Bernoulli variable — the ProbLog default, made explicit rather than assumed. The probability of a total choice is the product over the chosen facts of their probabilities times the product over the unchosen of their complements; a query's marginal is the sum of total-choice probabilities over the choices whose least Herbrand model derives it."
msgstr "众所周知的概率模型，据此每个 logic:probability 事实都是一个独立的 Bernoulli 变量——即 ProbLog 的默认设定，被显式给出而非默认假定。一个全选择的概率等于被选事实之概率的乘积，乘以未被选事实之补的乘积；一个查询的边缘概率是那些其最小 Herbrand 模型能导出它的选择上全选择概率之和。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FunctionalComplex|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A whole whose parts play distinct functional roles — a car (engine, wheels, chassis), an organism (organs), an organization (departments): a complex object, not a mere collection of like members. The counterpart of gufo:FunctionalComplex; its parts relate to it via logic:properPartOf (mereological parthood) rather than logic:memberOf, and each part contributes a different function. Stated in prose, not as a subclass edge. Contrast logic:Collection (uniform members) and logic:Quantity (homogeneous stuff)."
msgstr "一个整体，其各部分扮演互不相同的功能角色——一辆汽车（引擎、车轮、底盘）、一个有机体（器官）、一个组织（各部门）：这是一个复合对象，而非同类成员的单纯集合。它是 gufo:FunctionalComplex 的对应物；其各部分经由 logic:properPartOf（部分论意义上的部分关系）而非 logic:memberOf 与其相关联，且每个部分贡献一种不同的功能。以散文表述，而非作为子类边。与 logic:Collection（同质成员）以及 logic:Quantity（均质物料）相对照。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/functionalProperty|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic: property-characteristic marker for functionality: a property P such that P(a,b) ∧ P(a,c) entails b = c. The logic: analogue of owl:FunctionalProperty, minted standalone so the characteristic can be asserted on the canonical reasoning carrier alongside the others; functionality is already lifted into the foundation chase for the relator-mediation count, so a functional carrier records the characteristic centrally rather than adding a second enforcement path."
msgstr "针对函数性的 logic: 属性特征标记：一个属性 P，使得 P(a,b) ∧ P(a,c) 蕴涵 b = c。它是 owl:FunctionalProperty 的 logic: 类比物，被独立铸造，以便该特征能与其他特征一并在规范的推理载体上加以断言；函数性已为关系子中介计数而被提升进基础 chase，因此一个函数性载体集中记录该特征，而非增添第二条强制执行路径。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FunctionSymbolConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Requires every declared logic:FunctionTerm to carry a logic:functionSymbol. Paired with the owl:FunctionalProperty declaration on logic:functionSymbol (which caps it at one), it makes a function term bear EXACTLY one reified function symbol. It is not the argument-list check: a function term's operands are separate logic:argument term-carriers."
msgstr "要求每个已声明的 logic:FunctionTerm 都携带一个 logic:functionSymbol。它与作用于 logic:functionSymbol 上的 owl:FunctionalProperty 声明（把它上限定为一）相配对，使一个函数项恰好承载一个具体化的函数符号。它不是参数列表检查：一个函数项的操作数是各自独立的 logic:argument 词项载体。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FunctionSymbolConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A logic:FunctionTerm with two logic:argument carriers but no logic:functionSymbol violates this constraint."
msgstr "一个带有两个 logic:argument 载体但没有 logic:functionSymbol 的 logic:FunctionTerm 违反此约束。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/functionSymbol|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:FunctionTerm to the single function symbol it applies, over its ordered logic:argument terms. The symbol is reified as a logic:Type individual, exactly mirroring how logic:relation reifies an atomic predication's relation (the HiLog reflection — see logic:instanceOf and logic:orderedType): applying a reified function-symbol individual keeps the object level first-order rather than admitting a function variable, so no separate function-symbol class is minted. Functional: a function term applies exactly one symbol."
msgstr "将一个 logic:FunctionTerm 关联到它在其有序 logic:argument 词项上所施用的单一函数符号。该符号被具体化为一个 logic:Type 个体，恰好映照 logic:relation 具体化一个原子谓述之关系的方式（HiLog 反射——参见 logic:instanceOf 与 logic:orderedType）：施用一个具体化的函数符号个体使对象层级保持一阶，而非准入一个函数变量，因此不铸造单独的函数符号类。函数性的：一个函数项恰好施用一个符号。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FunctionTermArityConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Requires every declared logic:FunctionTerm to carry at least one logic:argument term-carrier: a nullary application is forbidden, because a 0-ary function symbol is a constant and belongs on a carrier's logic:termIri, so an empty-argument function term would give one constant two spellings. It is not the ordinal check: zero-based uniqueness and contiguity of the argument carriers are verified across all siblings by the typed-IR frontend."
msgstr "要求每个已声明的 logic:FunctionTerm 至少携带一个 logic:argument 词项载体：零元应用被禁止，因为一个 0 元函数符号是一个常量，应归于某载体的 logic:termIri，因此一个空参数函数项会给一个常量两种写法。它不是序数检查：参数载体的从零起编号的唯一性与连续性由带类型 IR 前端在所有同级之间加以验证。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FunctionTermArityConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A logic:FunctionTerm with a logic:functionSymbol but no logic:argument violates this constraint."
msgstr "一个带有 logic:functionSymbol 但没有 logic:argument 的 logic:FunctionTerm 违反此约束。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FunctionTerm|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A compound function-term application node: a single reified function symbol (logic:functionSymbol, a logic:Type individual) applied to a non-empty, ordered list of logic:argument term-carriers, denoting a first-order term such as cons(H, T) or s(X). It mirrors the atomic-predication pattern (logic:relation over ordered logic:argument), but predicates a FUNCTION symbol producing a term rather than a relation producing a truth value; reifying the symbol as a logic:Type individual keeps the object level first-order, so there is no function-variable. An argument carrier may itself carry logic:termApplication, so a nested term such as cons(H, cons(1, nil)) round-trips. It is not itself a logic:Formula: it is a term, referenced from a carrier's logic:termApplication, never asserted as a sentence."
msgstr "一个复合的函数项应用节点：一个具体化的单一函数符号（logic:functionSymbol，一个 logic:Type 个体）施用于一个非空、有序的 logic:argument 词项载体列表，指称一个一阶词项，例如 cons(H, T) 或 s(X)。它映照原子谓述模式（在有序的 logic:argument 上承载 logic:relation），但它谓述一个产生词项的函数符号，而非一个产生真值的关系；将该符号具体化为一个 logic:Type 个体使对象层级保持一阶，因此不存在函数变量。一个参数载体本身也可以承载 logic:termApplication，因此一个嵌套词项如 cons(H, cons(1, nil)) 可无损往返。它本身并非一个 logic:Formula：它是一个词项，从某载体的 logic:termApplication 处被引用，绝不作为语句被断言。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FunctionTerm|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "cons(H, cons(1, nil)) is a logic:FunctionTerm whose logic:functionSymbol is ex:cons and whose second logic:argument carries logic:termApplication onto the inner cons(1, nil) function term."
msgstr "cons(H, cons(1, nil)) 是一个 logic:FunctionTerm，其 logic:functionSymbol 为 ex:cons，其第二个 logic:argument 将 logic:termApplication 承载至内层的函数项 cons(1, nil)。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FuzzyMeasure|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The uncertainty measure carrying fuzzy (degree-of-truth) membership values. One member of the uncertainty-measure set facet, which may carry several measures at once; distinct from logic:ProbabilisticMeasure (a calibrated probability) and logic:WeightedRankingMeasure (a solver preference order)."
msgstr "承载模糊（真度）隶属值的不确定性度量。它是不确定性度量集合侧面的一个成员，该侧面可同时承载若干度量；它区别于 logic:ProbabilisticMeasure（一个经校准的概率）与 logic:WeightedRankingMeasure（一个求解器偏好次序）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GateAdmitted|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:gateVerdict value for an action the gate admits: every precondition holds, every capability is available, every invariant is preserved, and every required resource is available."
msgstr "针对门控准入之动作的 logic:gateVerdict 值：每个前置条件皆成立，每项能力皆可用，每个不变式皆得保持，且每项所需资源皆可用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/gateCompensation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a denied logic:GateProbe to the logic:compensation (rollback) the schema would run on denial. Domain logic:GateProbe, range the compensation action (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将一个被拒的 logic:GateProbe 关联到该模式在被拒时会执行的 logic:compensation（回滚）。定义域为 logic:GateProbe，值域为该补偿动作（以散文表述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/gateDenialReason|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A human-readable reason on a denied logic:GateProbe naming the failing gate — the unmet precondition, the unavailable capability, the breached invariant, or the unavailable resource. Domain logic:GateProbe, range a string literal (stated in prose). A breach is a surfaced verdict, never a silent pass."
msgstr "一个被拒的 logic:GateProbe 上的人类可读原因，命名失败的门控——未满足的前置条件、不可用的能力、被违反的不变式，或不可用的资源。定义域为 logic:GateProbe，值域为一个字符串字面量（以散文表述）。违反是一个被呈现的裁决，绝非一次静默放行。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GateDenied|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:gateVerdict value for an action the gate denies: a precondition, capability, invariant, or resource gate failed. The probe carries a logic:gateDenialReason naming the failing gate and, when declared, the logic:gateCompensation rollback."
msgstr "针对门控拒绝之动作的 logic:gateVerdict 值：一个前置条件、能力、不变式或资源门控失败了。该探针携带一个命名失败门控的 logic:gateDenialReason，并且在已声明时，携带 logic:gateCompensation 回滚。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GateProbe|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A node pairing a logic:ActionSchema (via logic:probesSchema) with the state (via logic:probesState) the action-gate verdict is computed against, plus the capabilities the state makes available (logic:capabilityAvailable). The native evaluator emits a logic:gateVerdict — logic:GateAdmitted or logic:GateDenied — surfacing the precondition, capability, invariant-breach, and resource-exhaustion gates as recorded findings rather than silent passes."
msgstr "一个节点，将一个 logic:ActionSchema（经由 logic:probesSchema）与用以计算动作门控裁决的状态（经由 logic:probesState）相配对，外加该状态所提供的能力（logic:capabilityAvailable）。原生求值器发出一个 logic:gateVerdict —— logic:GateAdmitted 或 logic:GateDenied ——将前置条件、能力、不变式违反与资源耗尽门控作为被记录的发现加以呈现，而非静默放行。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/gateUndeterminedReason|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A human-readable reason on a logic:GateUndetermined logic:GateProbe naming the specific cause of the withheld judgment: for a logic:FreshnessGuard failure, WHICH valid-time axis failed and its bounds — either the age exceeding the logic:freshnessHorizon, or the logic:decisionTime falling outside the [logic:freshnessWindowStart, logic:freshnessWindowEnd] logic:freshnessWindow interval (the two axes are independent and the reason names whichever failed first). Domain logic:GateProbe, range a string literal (stated in prose). The undetermined verdict is surfaced, never a silent pass or a spurious denial."
msgstr "一个 logic:GateUndetermined 的 logic:GateProbe 上的人类可读原因，命名判断被搁置的具体缘由：对于一次 logic:FreshnessGuard 失败，即哪一条有效时间轴失败及其边界——要么是年龄超过了 logic:freshnessHorizon，要么是 logic:decisionTime 落于 logic:freshnessWindow 区间 [logic:freshnessWindowStart, logic:freshnessWindowEnd] 之外（这两条轴互相独立，原因命名先失败的那一条）。定义域为 logic:GateProbe，值域为一个字符串字面量（以散文表述）。未定裁决会被呈现，绝非一次静默放行或一次虚假拒绝。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GateUndetermined|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:gateVerdict value for an action whose gate is neither admitted nor denied because the judgment is withheld on insufficient information — a single conclusiveness value with two causes. (1) A precondition datum fails its logic:FreshnessGuard on EITHER of two independent valid-time axes: (1a) the AGE HORIZON — the datum was recorded too long before the logic:decisionTime, its age exceeding the guard's logic:freshnessHorizon; or (1b) the EXPLICIT VALID-TIME WINDOW — the logic:decisionTime falls outside the closed [logic:freshnessWindowStart, logic:freshnessWindowEnd] interval the guard declares (an off-episode / out-of-window decision). Either way the datum is treated as undetermined rather than stale-but-usable, carrying a logic:gateUndeterminedReason that names the failing axis. The two axes are orthogonal: a datum may fail one and pass the other. (2) A logic:NotificationWaitSchema is still awaiting its logic:ExternalSignal: the engine has not been told the wait completed, carrying a logic:awaitingSignal witness. Both mirror the logic:GoalEvaluationUndetermined conclusiveness axis of goal evaluation: a judgment the evaluator declines to make on insufficient input rather than guessing — NOT a denial, since the datum may refresh or the signal may arrive."
msgstr "针对某动作的 logic:gateVerdict 值，其门控既不准入也不拒绝，因为在信息不足的情况下判断被搁置——这是一个具有两种成因的单一定论性值。(1) 一条前置条件基准数据在两条独立有效时间轴的任一条上未能通过其 logic:FreshnessGuard：(1a) 年龄视界——该基准数据的记录时间早于 logic:decisionTime 过久，其年龄超过守卫的 logic:freshnessHorizon；或 (1b) 显式有效时间窗口—— logic:decisionTime 落于守卫所声明的闭合区间 [logic:freshnessWindowStart, logic:freshnessWindowEnd] 之外（一次脱离情节／窗外的决策）。无论哪种情形，该基准数据都被视为未定而非过期仍可用，并携带一个命名失败轴的 logic:gateUndeterminedReason。这两条轴是正交的：一条基准数据可以在一条上失败而在另一条上通过。(2) 一个 logic:NotificationWaitSchema 仍在等待其 logic:ExternalSignal：引擎尚未被告知等待已完成，携带一个 logic:awaitingSignal 见证。二者皆映照目标评估的 logic:GoalEvaluationUndetermined 定论性轴：即求值器在输入不足时拒绝作出判断而非臆测——这并非一次拒绝，因为该基准数据可能刷新，或该信号可能到达。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/gateVerdict|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:GateProbe to its action-gate verdict, one of logic:GateAdmitted, logic:GateDenied, or logic:GateUndetermined. Domain logic:GateProbe (stated in prose). The materialized verdict of the precondition / capability / invariant / resource / freshness gate."
msgstr "将一个 logic:GateProbe 关联到其动作门控裁决，为 logic:GateAdmitted、logic:GateDenied 或 logic:GateUndetermined 之一。定义域为 logic:GateProbe（以散文表述）。这是前置条件／能力／不变式／资源／时效门控的已物化裁决。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GenericDependence|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A probability model for a GENERIC (unstructured) stochastic dependence between random variables: the lowering target for a math:MarkovKernel via math:probabilityModelLowering, whose conditional structure is not further factored into an explicit joint table (logic:DependencyModel) or a full-independence product (logic:FullIndependence). It records that a dependence exists without committing to its internal structure. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:GenericDependence only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "一个概率模型，描述随机变量之间一种通用（无结构）的随机依赖：即经由 math:probabilityModelLowering 对一个 math:MarkovKernel 的降级目标，其条件结构不再被进一步分解为一张显式联合表（logic:DependencyModel）或一个完全独立乘积（logic:FullIndependence）。它记录一种依赖存在，而不对其内部结构作出承诺。它并非某个更宽、更窄或仅仅相关之构造的可互换别名；仅在所述的同一性与校验条件下才可采用 logic:GenericDependence。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/genericQuality|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Quality to the basic generic quality it instantiates — length, mass, pressure, temperature: the frame-independent kind of quality, prior to any bearer-context or role. The frame-independent leg of the generic-quality/quality-role ladder (Principle 11: the structure invariant across frames), paired with logic:qualityRole (the anti-rigid logic:Role that generic quality plays in a bearer-context — height being length in a body-context). A quality that plays a logic:qualityRole must instantiate its logic:genericQuality, or it is the logic:QualityRoleWithoutGeneric violation. Domain logic:Quality (stated in prose, matching the module's convention)."
msgstr "将一个 logic:Quality 关联到它所例示的基本通用质——长度、质量、压强、温度：即与参照系无关的那类质，先于任何承载者上下文或角色。它是通用质／质角色阶梯中与参照系无关的那条支腿（原则 11：跨参照系不变的结构），与 logic:qualityRole 相配对（通用质在某承载者上下文中所扮演的反刚性 logic:Role ——高度即身体上下文中的长度）。一个扮演某 logic:qualityRole 的质必须例示其 logic:genericQuality，否则即为 logic:QualityRoleWithoutGeneric 违反。定义域为 logic:Quality（以散文表述，遵循该模块的约定）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/getLeg|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Lens to the logic:TransactionProgram that realizes its get leg — the down-projection get : S → V from the GMEOW source to the external view. Reuses the transaction layer's path semantics and logic:PathShape; no new pattern language. Domain logic:Lens, range logic:TransactionProgram."
msgstr "将一个 logic:Lens 关联到实现其 get 支腿的 logic:TransactionProgram ——即从 GMEOW 源到外部视图的下投影 get : S → V。它复用事务层的路径语义与 logic:PathShape；不引入新的模式语言。定义域为 logic:Lens，值域为 logic:TransactionProgram。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GetPut|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The lens law put(get(s), s) = s: getting a view from a source and immediately putting it back leaves the source unchanged. Claimable from the logic:WellBehavedLens rung upward; the acquisition-stability law."
msgstr "透镜定律 put(get(s), s) = s：从一个源取得一个视图并随即将其放回，会使该源保持不变。自 logic:WellBehavedLens 这一级及以上可加以主张；即获取稳定性定律。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GoalEvaluationCompleted|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:GoalEvaluationStatus value for a goal evaluation that has reached a conclusive judgment. Together with satisfaction status logic:Satisfied it is the condition under which a gmeow:satisfiedBy edge is generated. A maintenance or avoidance goal reaches this only when its window closes (satisfied) or its target fails (violated)."
msgstr "针对已达成定论判断之目标评估的 logic:GoalEvaluationStatus 值。它连同满足状态 logic:Satisfied 一起，构成生成一条 gmeow:satisfiedBy 边的条件。一个维持性或规避性目标仅在其窗口关闭（满足）或其目标失败（被违反）时才达成此状态。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GoalEvaluation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The reified, vantage-indexed record of whether a goal is met: one logic:GoalEvaluation per (goal, situation or world it is judged against, evaluator holding the judgment, time of judgment, criterion applied), identified by that tuple of subjects and attributed through gmeow:accordingTo. Its outcome is factored into independent axes rather than one collapsed label — logic:satisfactionStatus, logic:feasibilityStatus, logic:lifecycleStatus, logic:goalEvaluationStatus, and the logic:satisfactionDegree quantity — each varying independently. The binary gmeow:satisfiedBy edge is the conclusive projection of this record: an edge is generated from each evaluation whose satisfaction status is logic:Satisfied and whose goal-evaluation status is logic:GoalEvaluationCompleted, and a directly authored gmeow:satisfiedBy edge deterministically expands into a default such evaluation under the asserting vantage, so the flat and reified records never disagree. Two evaluators who disagree are two coexisting evaluations, each retained rather than reconciled (Principle 9)."
msgstr "关于某目标是否达成的、具体化且按视角索引的记录：每一个（目标、据以评判它的情境或世界、持有该判断的评估者、判断时刻、所施用的准则）对应一个 logic:GoalEvaluation，由该主体元组标识，并经由 gmeow:accordingTo 加以归属。其结果被分解为若干独立的轴，而非一个坍缩的单一标签—— logic:satisfactionStatus、logic:feasibilityStatus、logic:lifecycleStatus、logic:goalEvaluationStatus，以及 logic:satisfactionDegree 量——各自独立变化。二元的 gmeow:satisfiedBy 边是此记录的定论性投影：从每个满足状态为 logic:Satisfied 且目标评估状态为 logic:GoalEvaluationCompleted 的评估生成一条边，而一条直接撰写的 gmeow:satisfiedBy 边会在断言视角下确定性地展开为一个如此的默认评估，因此扁平记录与具体化记录永不相悖。两个意见相左的评估者即两个并存的评估，各自被保留而非被调和（原则 9）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GoalEvaluationStatus|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The closed value class of the goal-evaluation-completeness axis of a logic:GoalEvaluation: whether the evaluation has reached a conclusive judgment. Its individuals are logic:GoalEvaluationCompleted (a conclusive judgment), logic:GoalEvaluationUndetermined (not yet conclusive — a maintenance or avoidance goal whose window has not closed holds so far but is not yet conclusively satisfied), and logic:GoalEvaluationUnsupported (the evaluator has no defined procedure for the judgment). The set is closed; a misspelt value is rejected. DISTINCT from logic:EvaluationStatus, the engine-computation axis of a logic:ReasoningResult (what the engine was able to do): the two are orthogonal and must never be conflated — one factors a goal judgment's conclusiveness, the other a reasoning run's computational completion."
msgstr "一个 logic:GoalEvaluation 的目标评估完备性轴的封闭值类：即该评估是否已达成定论判断。其个体为 logic:GoalEvaluationCompleted（一个定论判断）、logic:GoalEvaluationUndetermined（尚未定论——一个窗口尚未关闭的维持性或规避性目标迄今成立，但尚未定论性地被满足），以及 logic:GoalEvaluationUnsupported（评估者对该判断没有既定程序）。该集合是封闭的；拼写错误的值会被拒绝。它有别于 logic:EvaluationStatus ——一个 logic:ReasoningResult 的引擎计算轴（引擎能够做到什么）：二者正交，绝不可混为一谈——前者分解一个目标判断的定论性，后者分解一次推理运行的计算完成度。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/goalEvaluationStatus|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:GoalEvaluation to the logic:GoalEvaluationStatus it carries — whether the evaluation is conclusive. Domain logic:GoalEvaluation, range logic:GoalEvaluationStatus (stated in prose). Together with satisfaction status logic:Satisfied, the value logic:GoalEvaluationCompleted is the condition under which a gmeow:satisfiedBy edge is generated. DISTINCT from logic:resultEvaluation, which carries the engine-computation logic:EvaluationStatus of a logic:ReasoningResult."
msgstr "将一个 logic:GoalEvaluation 关联到它所承载的 logic:GoalEvaluationStatus ——即该评估是否为定论。定义域为 logic:GoalEvaluation，值域为 logic:GoalEvaluationStatus（以散文表述）。连同满足状态 logic:Satisfied，值 logic:GoalEvaluationCompleted 构成生成一条 gmeow:satisfiedBy 边的条件。它有别于 logic:resultEvaluation ——后者承载一个 logic:ReasoningResult 的引擎计算 logic:EvaluationStatus。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GoalEvaluationUndetermined|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:GoalEvaluationStatus value for a goal evaluation not yet conclusive — most characteristically a maintenance or avoidance goal whose bounding window has not closed: holding so far is not conclusive satisfaction. Distinct from logic:GoalEvaluationUnsupported (no procedure exists): here the procedure exists but the judgment is open."
msgstr "针对尚未定论之目标评估的 logic:GoalEvaluationStatus 值——最典型地即一个界定窗口尚未关闭的维持性或规避性目标：迄今成立并非定论性满足。它区别于 logic:GoalEvaluationUnsupported（不存在任何程序）：此处程序存在，但判断仍悬而未决。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GoalEvaluationUnsupported|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:GoalEvaluationStatus value for a goal evaluation the evaluator has no defined procedure for — the judgment cannot be made under the applicable criterion. Distinct from logic:GoalEvaluationUndetermined (the procedure exists but the judgment is open)."
msgstr "针对评估者对其没有既定程序之目标评估的 logic:GoalEvaluationStatus 值——依据适用准则无法作出该判断。它区别于 logic:GoalEvaluationUndetermined（程序存在，但判断仍悬而未决）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GoalExpressionKind|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The closed value class of the node kind of a logic:GoalExpression — which of the nine compositional variants the expression is, read by the engine to evaluate it. Its individuals are logic:AtomicGoal (a named situation type obtains), logic:ConjunctiveGoal and logic:DisjunctiveGoal (all, or any, operand sub-expressions hold), logic:AchievementGoal (the target first obtains along a path), logic:MaintenanceGoal (the target holds at every state of an interval, violated at the first failure), logic:AvoidanceGoal (the dual — a proscribed situation never obtains), logic:OptimizationGoal (directed at a measure, satisfied to a degree rather than crisply), logic:ConditionalGoal (a target applying only when a guard situation holds), and logic:DeadlineWindowGoal (an achievement or maintenance target indexed to a bounding interval after which the window closes). The set is closed; a misspelt kind names no declared variant and is rejected."
msgstr "一个 logic:GoalExpression 的节点种类的封闭值类——即该表达式是九种组合变体中的哪一种，由引擎读取以对其求值。其个体为 logic:AtomicGoal（一个具名情境类型成立）、logic:ConjunctiveGoal 与 logic:DisjunctiveGoal（全部、或任一操作数子表达式成立）、logic:AchievementGoal（目标沿某路径首次成立）、logic:MaintenanceGoal（目标在某区间的每个状态上皆成立，一旦首次失败即被违反）、logic:AvoidanceGoal（其对偶——一个被禁止的情境永不成立）、logic:OptimizationGoal（指向某度量，按程度而非分明地被满足）、logic:ConditionalGoal（一个仅在某守卫情境成立时才适用的目标），以及 logic:DeadlineWindowGoal（一个索引到某界定区间、区间之后窗口即关闭的达成或维持目标）。该集合是封闭的；拼写错误的种类不命名任何已声明的变体，会被拒绝。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/goalExpressionKind|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:GoalExpression to its logic:GoalExpressionKind — which of the nine compositional variants it is. Domain logic:GoalExpression, range logic:GoalExpressionKind (stated in prose). The engine reads this to dispatch the compositional evaluation."
msgstr "将 logic:GoalExpression 关联到其 logic:GoalExpressionKind——即它属于九种组合变体中的哪一种。定义域 logic:GoalExpression，值域 logic:GoalExpressionKind（以散文陈述）。引擎读取此项以分派组合式求值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GoalExpression|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The typed IR term carrying the compositional structure of a goal's target so the engine can evaluate it compositionally, attached to a gmeow:Goal through logic:hasGoalCondition. Its node kind is one of nine variants: atomic (satisfied when a named situation type obtains), conjunctive and disjunctive (satisfied when all, or any, sub-expressions are), achievement (satisfied once the target first obtains along a path), maintenance (satisfied only while the target holds at every state of an interval, violated at the first failure), avoidance (the dual of maintenance — satisfied while a proscribed situation never obtains), optimization (directed at a measure, satisfied to the degree the measure is extremized rather than by a crisp boundary), conditional (a target applying only when a guard situation holds), and deadline-window (an achievement or maintenance target indexed to a bounding interval after which the window closes). Identity is STRUCTURAL: two expressions with the same node kind, operands, and bound situation type are the same term, so a goal condition is data the engine reads and writes rather than prose. The flat gmeow:hasGoal and conclusive gmeow:satisfiedBy edges are the surface views this richer form generates; projections that cannot hold the structure record the loss in the preservation ledger."
msgstr "承载目标之标的组合结构的类型化 IR 词项，使引擎得以对其进行组合式求值，经由 logic:hasGoalCondition 附着于 gmeow:Goal。其节点种类为九种变体之一：原子（当某具名情形类型成立时得到满足）、合取与析取（当全部或任一子表达式满足时得到满足）、达成（一旦标的沿某路径首次成立即得到满足）、维持（仅当标的在某区间的每个状态皆成立时得到满足，首次失败即被违反）、规避（维持之对偶——只要被禁止的情形从不成立即得到满足）、优化（指向某度量，按度量被极值化的程度而非按清晰边界得到满足）、条件（仅当守卫情形成立时才适用的标的），以及截止窗口（索引到某界定区间的达成或维持标的，超过该区间窗口即关闭）。同一性为结构性：具有相同节点种类、操作数与所绑定情形类型的两个表达式即为同一词项，故目标条件乃引擎读写的数据而非散文。扁平的 gmeow:hasGoal 与终结性的 gmeow:satisfiedBy 边是此更丰富形式所生成的表层视图；无法保有该结构的投影在保持账本中记录其损失。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/goalWellFoundedModel|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The success criterion of the well-founded materializer's phase plan: the total (two-valued) well-founded model of the rules over every world is computed and its derived non-EDB rows emitted. The gmeow:Goal logic:wellFoundedMaterializerPlan is arranged to reach; a partial model is a hard failure, never a partial success."
msgstr "良基物化器阶段规划的成功判据：计算规则在每个世界上的完全（二值）良基模型，并发出其派生的非-EDB 行。此即 logic:wellFoundedMaterializerPlan 所设定要达到的 gmeow:Goal；部分模型为硬性失败，绝非部分成功。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GovernanceRegime|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A declared scope within which a logic:DownwardConstraint is active, relative to which its logic:constraintVerdict is read. It carries, via logic:activationBasis, the constrained states it activates as binding — a constraint binds only when its constrained state is in the regime's basis. Governance is always regime-relative: the same whole may bind a part's state under one GovernanceRegime and leave it logic:ConstraintUnknown under another, and a binding can be quieted by a different regime without contradiction precisely because the constraint records which regime it is relative to. The holonic-governance analogue of a logic:ReductionTheory (which scopes the emergence calculus) and a logic:MereologyProfile (which scopes weak supplementation) — it scopes the downward-constraint calculus rather than asserting governance foundation-wide (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "一个已声明的范围，在其内 logic:DownwardConstraint 处于活跃状态，并相对于它读取其 logic:constraintVerdict。它经由 logic:activationBasis 承载它所激活为具约束力的受约束状态——某约束仅当其受约束状态位于该体制的基底中时才具约束力。治理始终相对于体制：同一整体可能在某 GovernanceRegime 下约束部分的状态，而在另一体制下将其留为 logic:ConstraintUnknown，且一项约束力可被另一体制平息而无矛盾，恰恰因为该约束记录了它相对于哪个体制。它是 logic:ReductionTheory（界定涌现演算）与 logic:MereologyProfile（界定弱补充）在全息治理上的类比物——它界定向下约束演算，而非在整个基础范围内断言治理（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons 章节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/granularityAgent|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The coarsest grain of an assessment subject: the reasoner as a whole — the grain at which a reliability assessment of an agent or engine is made."
msgstr "评估主体的最粗粒度：作为整体的推理机——在此粒度上对一个智能体或引擎作出可靠性评估。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/granularityBodyOfReasoning|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "An intermediate grain of an assessment subject: a connected body of reasoning — a derivation, a proof, an episode of inference — judged as a whole rather than one step."
msgstr "评估主体的中间粒度：一个连贯的推理体——一次推导、一个证明、一段推理片段——作为整体而非单一步骤加以判断。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/granularityDomain|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A broad grain of an assessment subject: a domain of competence — the agent's standing in a field rather than on any one episode."
msgstr "评估主体的宽粒度：一个能力域——智能体在某领域中的地位，而非在任一片段上的表现。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/granularityInference|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The finest grain of an assessment subject: a single inference — one logic:InferenceProcess or commitment being judged."
msgstr "评估主体的最细粒度：单次推理——被判断的一个 logic:InferenceProcess 或承诺。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GroundedArgumentation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The grounded Dung argumentation semantics: the unique, sceptical, least fixed point of the characteristic function — an argument is accepted only when every attack on it is defeated by an accepted argument. The argumentation-facet value that resolves conflict deterministically; contrast logic:PreferredArgumentation, which admits multiple maximal admissible sets."
msgstr "接地的 Dung 论辩语义：特征函数唯一的、怀疑的、最小不动点——某论证仅当针对它的每一次攻击都被某个被接受的论证击败时才被接受。此论辩侧面值以确定性方式化解冲突；与 logic:PreferredArgumentation 相对照，后者容许多个极大可接纳集。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GroundingCorrespondence|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:bridge a logic:GroundingCorrespondence ; logic:sourceEndpoint logic:Restriction ; logic:targetEndpoint owl:Restriction ."
msgstr "示例：ex:bridge a logic:GroundingCorrespondence ; logic:sourceEndpoint logic:Restriction ; logic:targetEndpoint owl:Restriction ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GroundingCorrespondence|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Grounding correspondences are shipped correspondence-law data; they do not import or canonize the external target vocabulary."
msgstr "接地对应是随附交付的对应律数据；它们既不导入也不规范化外部目标词汇表。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/groupKey|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment"
msgid "A group-by key variable of a reduce rule. Default-absent on ordinary Horn rules; multi-valued for a multi-key grouping."
msgstr "归约规则的分组键变量。在普通 Horn 规则上默认缺省；对于多键分组则为多值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/groupKey|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A group-by variable (a ?-prefixed string) over which a reduce rule partitions its body bindings before aggregating: logic:aggregateFunction is computed once per distinct tuple of logic:groupKey values. The group keys are set-semantic (their order does not change meaning); the SHACL-AF reduce surface realizes a single-group-key reduce as the focus node ($this) of a GROUP-BY sub-SELECT."
msgstr "一个分组变量（以 ? 为前缀的字符串），归约规则据其在聚合之前对其主体绑定进行分区：logic:aggregateFunction 对每个不同的 logic:groupKey 值元组计算一次。分组键具集合语义（其顺序不改变含义）；SHACL-AF 归约表层将单一分组键归约实现为 GROUP-BY 子-SELECT 的焦点节点（$this）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/guardSituation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a conditional logic:GoalExpression to the logic:Situation type that guards it — the goal's target (its operand) applies only when the guard holds (via logic:situationObtains). Domain logic:GoalExpression, range logic:Situation (stated in prose). When the guard is false the conditional goal prescribes nothing: the evaluation reflects does-not-apply rather than asserting satisfied or violated."
msgstr "将条件性 logic:GoalExpression 关联到守卫它的 logic:Situation 类型——该目标的标的（其操作数）仅当守卫成立（经由 logic:situationObtains）时才适用。定义域 logic:GoalExpression，值域 logic:Situation（以散文陈述）。当守卫为假时，条件目标不作任何规定：求值反映不适用，而非断言已满足或已违反。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/guardsPrecondition|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:FreshnessGuard to the logic:precondition situation it guards — the situation whose supporting datum must be current for the gate to admit. Domain logic:FreshnessGuard, range the guarded precondition situation (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将 logic:FreshnessGuard 关联到它所守卫的 logic:precondition 情形——其支撑数据必须为最新、闸门方予放行的那个情形。定义域 logic:FreshnessGuard，值域为被守卫的前置条件情形（以散文陈述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/happensBefore|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A schedule-order edge of a logic:ConcurrentHistory: 'earlier happensBefore later' records that the earlier logic:TransactionStep is scheduled before the later one in the witnessed index-order interleaving AND the two conflict (they share a situation that at least one writes). Domain and range logic:TransactionStep (stated in prose). Emitted only for CROSS-transaction conflicting pairs — the schedule order between the two legs' operations that view- and conflict-serializability both read. It is the step-level witnessed-order companion to logic:readsFrom; it is kept DISTINCT from logic:precedes, which lifts conflict order to the TRANSACTION level for cycle detection, and from logic:temporallySucceeds, which orders the states of a single executed path rather than operations across legs."
msgstr "logic:ConcurrentHistory 的一条调度序边：earlier happensBefore later 记录较早的 logic:TransactionStep 在见证的索引序交错中被调度于较晚者之前，且二者发生冲突（它们共享一个至少一方写入的情形）。定义域与值域皆为 logic:TransactionStep（以散文陈述）。仅对跨事务的冲突对发出——视图可串行化与冲突可串行化二者都读取的、两条支路操作之间的调度序。它是 logic:readsFrom 在步骤级见证序上的伙伴；它与 logic:precedes 保持区分，后者将冲突序提升到事务级以进行环路检测，也与 logic:temporallySucceeds 区分，后者对单条已执行路径的状态排序，而非跨支路的操作排序。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/hasDeterminacy|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Correspondence to its logic:Determinacy — whether the target relationship is ontically logic:Crisp or logic:Vague. Kept separate from logic:confidence so a vague-but-confident alignment is not mis-recorded as a low-confidence equivalence. Range logic:Determinacy (domain stated in prose)."
msgstr "将 logic:Correspondence 关联到其 logic:Determinacy——即目标关系在本体上是 logic:Crisp 还是 logic:Vague。与 logic:confidence 分开保持，以免将模糊但有把握的对齐误记为低置信度的等价。值域 logic:Determinacy（定义域以散文陈述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/hasFormula|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a program or container to a top-level logic:Formula it asserts. Top-level formulae are reached by this property; sub-formulae are reached by the connective and quantifier properties, so a formula referenced as another's component is not also a top-level assertion."
msgstr "将某程序或容器关联到它所断言的顶层 logic:Formula。顶层公式经由此属性抵达；子公式经由联结词与量词属性抵达，故被引用为另一公式之组成部分的公式并非同时也是顶层断言。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/hasGoalCondition|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a gmeow:Goal to the logic:GoalExpression carrying the compositional structure of its target. Domain gmeow:Goal, range logic:GoalExpression (stated in prose, matching the module's domain/range convention). The flat gmeow:hasGoal and conclusive gmeow:satisfiedBy edges are the surface views this richer condition generates; gmeow:intentionGoal stays functional and ranges over gmeow:Goal — goal structure lives on the goal through this property, leaving the functional edge untouched."
msgstr "将 gmeow:Goal 关联到承载其标的组合结构的 logic:GoalExpression。定义域 gmeow:Goal，值域 logic:GoalExpression（以散文陈述，符合本模块的定义域/值域约定）。扁平的 gmeow:hasGoal 与终结性的 gmeow:satisfiedBy 边是此更丰富条件所生成的表层视图；gmeow:intentionGoal 保持为函数性并以 gmeow:Goal 为值域——目标结构经由此属性驻留于目标之上，使函数性边不受触动。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/hasHolonicPosition|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The derived marker that an entity occupies at least one logic:HolonicPosition within a holarchy. Never asserted by hand; it is entailed by the foundation lowering, settling in stratum 1 the moment any logic:positionEntity reifier names the entity. It is the negation-as-failure target that arms the logic:HolonicLevelIncoherence rule (a profiled holon occupying NO position is incoherent), and the positive companion to logic:multiplyPositioned (which fires when an entity occupies SEVERAL distinct positions). It tracks compositional positioning only and is orthogonal to the HiLog logic:orderedType instantiation tower — the two axes never feed one another."
msgstr "表示某实体在某全息架构内占据至少一个 logic:HolonicPosition 的派生标记。绝不手工断言；它由基础下降蕴涵而来，一旦任何 logic:positionEntity 具体化器命名该实体，即在第 1 层稳定下来。它是武装 logic:HolonicLevelIncoherence 规则的失败即否定标的（未占据任何位置的已剖面化全息子是不融贯的），并是 logic:multiplyPositioned 的正向伙伴（当某实体占据若干不同位置时触发）。它仅追踪组合性定位，与 HiLog 的 logic:orderedType 实例化塔正交——两条轴从不彼此供给。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/hasLawClaim|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Correspondence to a logic:LawClaim it makes — a claimed logic:CorrespondenceLaw with its discharge state. Multi-valued: a correspondence may claim several laws, each capped by its logic:MorphismClass rung. Range logic:LawClaim (domain stated in prose)."
msgstr "将 logic:Correspondence 关联到它所提出的 logic:LawClaim——一条带其了结状态的、被主张的 logic:CorrespondenceLaw。多值：一个对应可主张若干条律，每条以其 logic:MorphismClass 层级封顶。值域 logic:LawClaim（定义域以散文陈述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/hasLens|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Correspondence to the logic:Lens that is its executable get / put core. Single-valued: each correspondence wraps exactly one lens, around which it adds the relation, axes, law claims and standpoint envelope. Range logic:Lens (domain stated in prose, matching the module's convention)."
msgstr "将 logic:Correspondence 关联到作为其可执行 get / put 内核的 logic:Lens。单值：每个对应恰包裹一个 lens，并围绕它添加关系、轴、律主张与立场包络。值域 logic:Lens（定义域以散文陈述，符合本模块约定）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/hasThresholdRow|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:LadderProjectionProfile to one of its logic:DimensionThreshold rows. Range logic:DimensionThreshold (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将 logic:LadderProjectionProfile 关联到其某一 logic:DimensionThreshold 行。值域 logic:DimensionThreshold（以散文陈述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/hasValue|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:activeRestriction logic:hasValue ex:active ."
msgstr "示例：ex:activeRestriction logic:hasValue ex:active ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/hasValue|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The required filler is one concrete RDF term rather than a class of possible fillers."
msgstr "所要求的填充项是一个具体的 RDF 词项，而非一类可能的填充项。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Holarchy|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The bounded logic:properPartOf strict partial order viewed as a nested whole/part structure — a holarchy in Koestler's sense. Because logic:properPartOf is transitive, asymmetric, and irreflexive, a holarchy is a directed acyclic graph (a DAG, not a strict ladder): an entity may be a proper part of several wholes along several paths. It is the structure over which a logic:HolonicPosition is read and logic:holonicLevel is measured (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "被视为嵌套整体/部分结构的有界 logic:properPartOf 严格偏序——即 Koestler 意义上的全息架构。由于 logic:properPartOf 是传递的、非对称的且非自反的，全息架构是一个有向无环图（DAG，而非严格阶梯）：一个实体可沿若干路径成为若干整体的真部分。它是读取 logic:HolonicPosition 与度量 logic:holonicLevel 所依据的结构（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons 章节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/HolonicAgencyProfile|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A declared profile of holonic agency that a holarchy may adopt, relative to which an logic:AgencyAssessment is made. It carries, via logic:selfAssertiveBasis and logic:integrativeBasis, the property-values that respectively evidence a holon's self-assertive (autonomy-as-a-whole) and integrative (subordination-as-a-part) tendencies — Koestler's two co-equal Janus faces, neither primary (Principle 9). Holonic agency is always relative to such a profile: it is a named profile a holarchy adopts, NOT a universal well-formedness rule every holon must satisfy — a bolt, a file-segment, or a process-phase needs no autonomy and is simply outside the profile. The Koestlerian-agency analogue of a logic:ReductionTheory (which scopes the emergence calculus) and a logic:GovernanceRegime (which scopes downward constraint) — it scopes the autonomy/integration calculus rather than asserting agency foundation-wide (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "一个已声明的全息能动性剖面，某全息架构可采纳之，logic:AgencyAssessment 相对于它作出。它经由 logic:selfAssertiveBasis 与 logic:integrativeBasis，分别承载佐证某全息子之自我肯定（作为整体的自主）与整合（作为部分的从属）倾向的属性值——Koestler 的两副对等的雅努斯面孔，二者皆非首要（原则 9）。全息能动性始终相对于这样一个剖面：它是某全息架构所采纳的具名剖面，而非每个全息子都要满足的普遍良构规则——一枚螺栓、一段文件片段或一个流程阶段无需任何自主，只是处于该剖面之外。它是 logic:ReductionTheory（界定涌现演算）与 logic:GovernanceRegime（界定向下约束）在 Koestler 式能动性上的类比物——它界定自主/整合演算，而非在整个基础范围内断言能动性（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons 章节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/HolonicFramework|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The compositional / systems-theory framework: the contextual, path-relative parthood of logic:HolonicPosition, the Koestlerian self-assertive/integrative assessment of logic:AgencyAssessment, emergence over a declared reduction theory, and non-transitive downward governance. Holon-ness is a position an entity occupies in a holarchy under a context over an interval, never a bare unary type (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "组合性 / 系统论框架：logic:HolonicPosition 的情境性、路径相对的部分关系，logic:AgencyAssessment 的 Koestler 式自我肯定/整合评估，在某已声明还原理论之上的涌现，以及非传递的向下治理。全息子性是某实体在某情境下、于某区间内在某全息架构中占据的位置，绝非一个裸露的一元类型（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons 章节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/HolonicLevelIncoherence|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The coherence violation raised for a holon — an entity that occupies a holonic position (both a proper part of some whole and itself having a proper part) — that is DECLARED UNDER a logic:MereologyProfile (via logic:underMereologyProfile) yet occupies no logic:HolonicPosition. A holon's logic:holonicLevel is read off its logic:HolonicPosition, the canonical relational construct of which logic:Holon and a level are lossy projections; a profiled holon with no declared position has no path along which its compositional depth can be coherently measured, so its level is incoherent. It is enforced only within the profile a holon is declared under, never across all holons: a holon outside any logic:MereologyProfile is never charged, mirroring logic:WeakSupplementation. Parthood is profiled, not universal, and a holonic level is path-relative (recorded per path, e.g. as a min/max band), so a position is required only when a profile demands it. Note explicitly the non-conflation with the instantiation tower: logic:holonicLevel records mereological compositional depth in a whole/part DAG, whereas logic:orderedType is the HiLog deep-instantiation order numbering logic:instanceOf chains (an order-n type instantiates an order-(n+1) type); the two axes are orthogonal and must not be conflated. An entity high in the instantiation tower (via logic:instanceOf / logic:orderedType) but occupying no holonic position still fires this violation. Enforced by the stratified NAF rule in crates/logic/src/foundation.rs (C5; design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "为某全息子——占据全息位置的实体（既是某整体的真部分，自身又拥有真部分）——所引发的融贯性违规，该全息子在某 logic:MereologyProfile 下被声明（经由 logic:underMereologyProfile），却未占据任何 logic:HolonicPosition。全息子的 logic:holonicLevel 读自其 logic:HolonicPosition，后者为规范的关系性构造，logic:Holon 与层级皆为其有损投影；已剖面化而无已声明位置的全息子，没有任何路径能沿之融贯地度量其组合深度，故其层级不融贯。它仅在某全息子被声明所处的剖面内实施，绝不跨全体全息子：处于任何 logic:MereologyProfile 之外的全息子从不被追究，与 logic:WeakSupplementation 相呼应。部分关系是被剖面化的、并非普遍，且全息层级是路径相对的（按路径记录，例如作为 min/max 带），故仅当某剖面要求时才需要位置。明确注意与实例化塔不相混淆：logic:holonicLevel 记录整体/部分 DAG 中的部分论组合深度，而 logic:orderedType 是对 logic:instanceOf 链编号的 HiLog 深度实例化序（一个 n 阶类型实例化一个 (n+1) 阶类型）；两条轴正交，不得相混淆。在实例化塔中位置很高（经由 logic:instanceOf / logic:orderedType）却未占据任何全息位置的实体，仍会触发此违规。由 crates/logic/src/foundation.rs 中的分层 NAF 规则实施（C5；design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons 章节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/holonicLevelMax|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The deepest of the logic:holonicLevel values an entity carries across all the logic:HolonicPositions it occupies within a holarchy — the upper endpoint of the path-relative depth band. Because holarchies are DAGs, a single intrinsic level is ill-defined, so the band (min..max) is stored instead of one value. NOTE — honest scope: this endpoint is operator-asserted, NOT engine-verified. The all-IRI logic:StratifiedNAFProfile foundation chase cannot compare or aggregate the integer literals, so it cannot derive or check that this value is the true maximum of the borne per-position levels; the engine grounds only that a non-trivial band exists, via the derived marker logic:multiplyPositioned (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "某实体在其于某全息架构内占据的全体 logic:HolonicPositions 上所承载的 logic:holonicLevel 值中最深者——路径相对深度带的上端点。由于全息架构是 DAG，单一的内在层级并无良好定义，故存储的是带（min..max）而非单一值。注——诚实的范围界定：此端点由操作者断言，而非由引擎验证。全 IRI 的 logic:StratifiedNAFProfile 基础追逐无法比较或聚合整数字面量，故它既不能推导也不能核验此值确为所承载各位置层级的真正最大值；引擎仅经由派生标记 logic:multiplyPositioned 确立存在一条非平凡的带（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons 章节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/holonicLevelMin|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The shallowest of the logic:holonicLevel values an entity carries across all the logic:HolonicPositions it occupies within a holarchy — the lower endpoint of the path-relative depth band. Because holarchies are DAGs, a single intrinsic level is ill-defined, so the band (min..max) is stored instead of one value. NOTE — honest scope: this endpoint is operator-asserted, NOT engine-verified. The all-IRI logic:StratifiedNAFProfile foundation chase cannot compare or aggregate the integer literals, so it cannot derive or check that this value is the true minimum of the borne per-position levels; the engine grounds only that a non-trivial band exists, via the derived marker logic:multiplyPositioned (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "某实体在其于某全息架构内占据的全体 logic:HolonicPositions 上所承载的 logic:holonicLevel 值中最浅者——路径相对深度带的下端点。由于全息架构是 DAG，单一的内在层级并无良好定义，故存储的是带（min..max）而非单一值。注——诚实的范围界定：此端点由操作者断言，而非由引擎验证。全 IRI 的 logic:StratifiedNAFProfile 基础追逐无法比较或聚合整数字面量，故它既不能推导也不能核验此值确为所承载各位置层级的真正最小值；引擎仅经由派生标记 logic:multiplyPositioned 确立存在一条非平凡的带（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons 章节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/holonicLevel|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The compositional depth at which an entity sits within a holarchy, measured along one path: how many proper-part steps lie between the entity and a root whole. It is a literal read off a logic:HolonicPosition (hence rdfs:domain logic:HolonicPosition), never an intrinsic attribute of the entity — holarchies are DAGs, so an entity has no single global level; two paths may place the same entity at different depths and both are correct, and the level is therefore recorded per position (per path). The per-entity min/max band across an entity's positions is materialized separately as logic:holonicLevelMin and logic:holonicLevelMax. Distinct from logic:orderedType: logic:orderedType is the HiLog deep-instantiation order (an order-n type instantiates an order-(n+1) type), a property of the instantiation tower, whereas logic:holonicLevel is mereological compositional depth in a whole/part DAG; the two must not be conflated (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "某实体在某全息架构内所处的组合深度，沿单一路径度量：该实体与某根整体之间隔着多少真部分步。它是读自某 logic:HolonicPosition 的字面量（因而 rdfs:domain logic:HolonicPosition），绝非该实体的内在属性——全息架构是 DAG，故实体没有单一的全局层级；两条路径可将同一实体置于不同深度，二者皆正确，因而层级按位置（按路径）记录。跨某实体各位置的按实体 min/max 带被单独物化为 logic:holonicLevelMin 与 logic:holonicLevelMax。与 logic:orderedType 相区别：logic:orderedType 是 HiLog 深度实例化序（一个 n 阶类型实例化一个 (n+1) 阶类型），属实例化塔的属性，而 logic:holonicLevel 是整体/部分 DAG 中的部分论组合深度；二者不得相混淆（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons 章节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/HolonicPosition|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The canonical relational construct of holon-ness: an entity occupies a holonic position in a particular holarchy, under a particular context, over a particular interval, along a particular path (entity, holarchy, context, interval, path). Whether an entity is a holon is read off this position, never asserted of the entity alone; the unary logic:Holon is its lossy projection. It is reified with the role properties logic:positionEntity, logic:positionHolarchy, logic:positionContext, logic:positionInterval, and logic:positionPath, because the foundation relation is five-place and the arity-bounded reasoning surface carries it as an objectified position (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "全息子性的规范关系性构造：某实体在某特定全息架构中、某特定情境下、某特定区间内、沿某特定路径占据一个全息位置（实体、全息架构、情境、区间、路径）。某实体是否为全息子读自此位置，绝不单就实体断言；一元的 logic:Holon 是其有损投影。它以角色属性 logic:positionEntity、logic:positionHolarchy、logic:positionContext、logic:positionInterval 与 logic:positionPath 加以具体化，因为该基础关系是五元的，而元数受限的推理表层将其承载为一个对象化的位置（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons 章节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/HolonIntegral|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The agency-verdict value for a holon that exhibits both Janus tendencies: under the declared logic:HolonicAgencyProfile of an logic:AgencyAssessment, the holon bears (logic:bearsProperty) both a logic:selfAssertiveBasis value (it asserts itself as a whole) and a logic:integrativeBasis value (it subordinates itself as a part) — Koestler's balanced holon. The positive, derivation-grounded verdict, reached by an actual two-face conjunction rather than by negation; the two faces are co-equal, neither privileged (Principle 9). Contrast logic:AutonomyDeficient and logic:IntegrationDeficient (one face collapsed) and logic:AgencyUnknown (neither evidenced) (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "对同时展现雅努斯两种倾向的全息子所给出的能动性裁定值：在某 logic:AgencyAssessment 已声明的 logic:HolonicAgencyProfile 下，该全息子既承载（logic:bearsProperty）一个 logic:selfAssertiveBasis 值（它作为整体肯定自身），又承载一个 logic:integrativeBasis 值（它作为部分从属自身）——Koestler 的均衡全息子。这一正向的、以推导为依据的裁定，经由真正的两面合取而非经由否定得出；两面对等，皆无优先（原则 9）。与 logic:AutonomyDeficient 及 logic:IntegrationDeficient（一面坍缩）以及 logic:AgencyUnknown（皆无佐证）相对照（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons 章节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Holon|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The lossy unary projection of logic:HolonicPosition: an entity that, within some holarchy, is simultaneously a whole and a part — both a proper part of some larger whole and itself having a proper part. Holon-ness is never a bare property of the entity; it is a position occupied in a particular holarchy, context, interval, and path, so logic:Holon is the convenient, lossy projection of that relational logic:HolonicPosition, exactly as the standpoint-modality view projects finer axes (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section). Root wholes and atomic leaves are not holons."
msgstr "logic:HolonicPosition 的有损一元投影：某实体在某全息架构内同时既是整体又是部分——既是某更大整体的真部分，自身又拥有真部分。全息子性绝非该实体的裸属性；它是在某特定全息架构、情境、区间与路径中占据的位置，故 logic:Holon 是那个关系性 logic:HolonicPosition 便利而有损的投影，正如立场-模态视图投影更细的轴一般（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons 章节）。根整体与原子叶子并非全息子。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/HornFragment|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The formula-fragment facet value selecting Horn clauses (at most one positive literal per clause). Single-valued on a ReasoningContract; the rule fragment over which least-model semantics is well-defined and, for the function-free case, terminating — the base on which the positive-Horn, stratified-negation and procedural presets build."
msgstr "选取 Horn 子句（每子句至多一个正文字）的公式片段侧面值。在 ReasoningContract 上为单值；此规则片段之上最小模型语义有良好定义，且在无函数情形下可终止——它是正-Horn、分层否定与过程性预设所构筑其上的基底。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/HypotheticalExecution|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The execution-mode value realizing the sandbox/hypothetical operator: a transaction program is executed to test whether it WOULD succeed, with its effects discarded rather than committed. It asserts that a program can execute from here without committing, and is NOT modal possibility (◇) — ◇ is the standard translation over the appropriate typed accessibility relation, logic:epistemicallyPossible or logic:doxasticallyAccessible (an alethic or doxastic claim), not over the bare logic:accessibleFrom superproperty; the two share construction machinery but are separate typed operators with separate meanings. The sandbox operator of the Transaction-Logic design, kept apart from the alethic/doxastic possibility of the context algebra."
msgstr "实现沙箱/假设算子的执行模式值：执行某事务程序以测试它是否会成功，其效果被丢弃而非提交。它断言某程序可从此处执行而不提交，且并非模态可能性（◇）——◇ 是在恰当的类型化可及关系 logic:epistemicallyPossible 或 logic:doxasticallyAccessible（一项真势或信念主张）之上的标准翻译，而非在裸露的 logic:accessibleFrom 超属性之上；二者共享构造机制，但为意义各异的独立类型化算子。它是 Transaction-Logic 设计的沙箱算子，与情境代数的真势/信念可能性保持分离。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/iff|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a biconditional logic:Formula to each of its two operand sub-formulae. The biconditional is commutative, so the canonical identity is insensitive to which operand is which — unlike the ordered logic:antecedent / logic:consequent of an implication."
msgstr "将双条件 logic:Formula 关联到其两个操作数子公式中的每一个。双条件是可交换的，故规范同一性对哪个操作数是哪个并不敏感——不同于蕴涵中有序的 logic:antecedent / logic:consequent。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/iff|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A definition can connect triangle(x) and polygonWithThreeSides(x) as the two logic:iff operands."
msgstr "一个定义可以将 triangle(x) 和 polygonWithThreeSides(x) 连接为两个 logic:iff 操作数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/imports|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Common Logic importation between logic:Modules: the importing module has, as part of its own theory, every sentence of the imported module. The module-to-module edge onto which the Common Logic (cl-imports …) directive maps. Importation composes transitively in the Common Logic reading, but this is documented in prose rather than asserted as owl:TransitiveProperty, matching the kernel convention that logic: relations carry no OWL characteristics and state their logical character in prose; the engine, not an OWL entailment, closes the import graph."
msgstr "logic:Modules 之间的 Common Logic 导入：导入方模块将被导入模块的每一个语句作为其自身理论的一部分而拥有。这是 Common Logic 的 (cl-imports …) 指令所映射到的模块到模块之边。在 Common Logic 的读法中导入以传递方式复合，但此点以散文记述而非断言为 owl:TransitiveProperty，符合内核约定：logic: 关系不携带任何 OWL 特性，并以散文陈述其逻辑性格；闭合导入图的是引擎，而非某项 OWL 蕴涵。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/imports|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:geometry logic:imports ex:orders makes the imported module's sentences visible in ex:geometry."
msgstr "ex:geometry logic:imports ex:orders 使被导入模块的语句在 ex:geometry 中可见。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/IncompleteClosure|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The failure raised when a logic:ClosureAcceptanceWitness — the acceptance record of an EL→RL→DL reasoning closure — declares no logic:closureEntailedAtom, i.e. names no atom the closure entails beyond its asserted EDB. A closure that adds nothing is either trivial or truncated; the flagship's guarantee is that the native reason_all closure genuinely derives new entailed atoms, so a witness carrying none is ill-formed and the gate rejects it."
msgstr "当某 logic:ClosureAcceptanceWitness——一次 EL→RL→DL 推理闭包的接受记录——未声明任何 logic:closureEntailedAtom 时所引发的失败，即未命名任何该闭包在其断言的 EDB 之外所蕴涵的原子。不添加任何东西的闭包要么平凡要么被截断；旗舰的保证在于原生 reason_all 闭包确实推导出新的被蕴涵原子，故不携带任何此类原子的见证是不良构的，闸门将其拒绝。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Incomplete|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:CompletenessStatus value for an answer whose search did not exhaust the space (a budget, answer cap, or depth bound was hit, or a DL construct was undecided). Wire value `incomplete`."
msgstr "对应其搜索未穷尽空间之答案的 logic:CompletenessStatus 值（命中了某预算、答案上限或深度界限，或某 DL 构造未决）。线值 `incomplete`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/InconsistencyPreserving|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A canonical inconsistency appears as an inconsistency in the projection: the projection does not silently mask a contradiction present in the canonical model. The inconsistency-direction polarity guaranteeing canonical → projection visibility."
msgstr "一个规范的不一致在投影中呈现为一个不一致：投影不会悄然掩盖规范模型中存在的矛盾。这是保证规范 → 投影可见性的不一致方向极性。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/InconsistencyReflecting|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "An inconsistency in the projection implies an inconsistency in the canonical model: the projection raises no spurious contradiction absent from the canonical model. The inconsistency-direction polarity guaranteeing projection → canonical soundness, dual to logic:InconsistencyPreserving."
msgstr "投影中的一个不一致蕴涵规范模型中的一个不一致：投影不会引发规范模型中不存在的虚假矛盾。这是保证投影 → 规范可靠性的不一致方向极性，与 logic:InconsistencyPreserving 对偶。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/IndirectContributorNotAttributionObligation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The standing non-entailment obligation that a derived gmeow:indirectContributor edge stays EVIDENCE, never ENTAILMENT, of direct responsibility: the foundation must never derive gmeow:wasAttributedTo (asserted authorship, ownership, or accountability) from the generation chain that surfaces indirect contribution. Enforced by syntactic reachability over the rule strata (no rule head produces the predicate) and finite closure over the materialized derivation graph (the predicate appears in no DERIVED edge). Guards the provenance credit model against collapsing indirect production into direct responsibility."
msgstr "长期成立的非蕴涵义务：派生的 gmeow:indirectContributor 边始终是直接责任的证据，绝非其蕴涵：基础绝不可从浮现间接贡献的生成链推导出 gmeow:wasAttributedTo（被断言的著作权、所有权或问责）。由规则层上的句法可达性（没有任何规则头产生该谓词）与物化推导图上的有限闭包（该谓词不出现在任何派生边中）加以实施。它守护出处归功模型，防止将间接产出坍缩为直接责任。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Individual|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A particular: an entity that is NOT a logic:Type — it is instantiated by types (via logic:instanceOf) but has no instances of its own, sitting at the bottom of every instantiation chain (logic:orderedType 0). The counterpart of gufo:Individual; the root complementing logic:Type. Specialized by logic:ConcreteIndividual (in spacetime) and logic:AbstractIndividual (outside it). Stated in prose, not as a subclass edge."
msgstr "一个个别者：一个并非 logic:Type 的实体——它被类型实例化（经由 logic:instanceOf），但自身没有任何实例，位于每条实例化链的底端（logic:orderedType 0）。它是 gufo:Individual 的对应物；补足 logic:Type 的根。由 logic:ConcreteIndividual（处于时空之内）与 logic:AbstractIndividual（处于其外）加以特化。以散文陈述，而非作为子类边。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Infeasible|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:FeasibilityStatus value for a goal no path can reach from any reachable situation — permanently unachievable, not merely currently obstructed. The strongest infeasibility reading; contrast logic:Blocked (the obstruction may lift)."
msgstr "对应任何路径都无法从任何可达情形抵达之目标的 logic:FeasibilityStatus 值——永久无法达成，而非仅仅当前受阻。这是最强的不可行性读法；与 logic:Blocked（阻碍可能解除）相对照。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/inferencePremiseConclusionDistinctness|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Asserts that a gmeow:InferenceCommitment's gmeow:premise and gmeow:conclusion must be distinct: an argument cannot assume what it proves — no premise is also the conclusion. The native coherence gate raises a violation when a premise coincides with the conclusion; the generated SHACL constraint surface is its projection."
msgstr "断言某 gmeow:InferenceCommitment 的 gmeow:premise 与 gmeow:conclusion 必须相异：论证不能假定它所证明者——没有任何前提同时也是结论。当某前提与结论重合时，原生融贯闸门引发一项违规；所生成的 SHACL 约束表层是其投影。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/InfoBoth|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:InformationState value when a proof AND a counterproof exist — a witnessed contradiction (glut) within one context, carried with its logic:contradictionWitness graph. Wire value `both`. A correct `both` is HIGH-assurance about a contradictory input, not a defect, and is local to its world — never globalized to owl:Nothing."
msgstr "当证明与反证同时存在时的 logic:InformationState 值——某单一情境内一个被见证的矛盾（过盈），随其 logic:contradictionWitness 图一并携带。线值 `both`。一个正确的 `both` 是关于矛盾输入的高确信，而非缺陷，且局限于其世界——绝不全局化为 owl:Nothing。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/InfoNeither|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:InformationState value when neither proof nor counterproof exists, established by a CONCLUSIVE evaluation (a completed run or a complete-for-the-fragment answer) — a real four-valued verdict. Wire value `neither`. NEVER interchangeable with logic:InfoUndetermined (no verdict reached) or logic:InfoNotEvaluated (the engine could not look)."
msgstr "当证明与反证均不存在、且由一次终结性求值（一次已完成的运行或一个就片段而言完备的答案）确立时的 logic:InformationState 值——一个真正的四值裁定。线值 `neither`。绝不与 logic:InfoUndetermined（未得出裁定）或 logic:InfoNotEvaluated（引擎无法查看）互换。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/InfoNotEvaluated|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:InformationState value when no information semantics were available — the engine COULD NOT look (an unsupported contract, or a missing required model such as a probabilistic dependency model). Wire value `not-evaluated`. NOT the conclusive logic:InfoNeither."
msgstr "当无任何信息语义可用时的 logic:InformationState 值——引擎无法查看（一份不受支持的契约，或一个缺失的必需模型，例如概率依赖模型）。线值 `not-evaluated`。并非终结性的 logic:InfoNeither。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/InfoOpposed|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:InformationState value when there is a counterproof and no proof — the FDE/paraconsistent evidence for the explicit negation. Wire value `opposed`."
msgstr "当存在反证而无证明时的 logic:InformationState 值——支持显式否定的 FDE/次协调证据。线值 `opposed`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/InformationState|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The closed value class of the logic:resultInformation field (the information axis): the four-valued Belnap verdict about the queried proposition plus two explicit non-results. Its individuals are logic:InfoSupported, logic:InfoOpposed, logic:InfoBoth, logic:InfoNeither (the Belnap four), logic:InfoUndetermined, and logic:InfoNotEvaluated. The three non-positive states are NEVER interchangeable: logic:InfoNeither requires a conclusive evaluation; logic:InfoUndetermined means no verdict was reached; logic:InfoNotEvaluated means the engine could not look. The set is closed; a misspelt value is rejected (design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md, §The reasoning result)."
msgstr "logic:resultInformation 字段（信息轴）的封闭值类：关于被查询命题的四值 Belnap 裁定，外加两个显式的非结果。其个体为 logic:InfoSupported、logic:InfoOpposed、logic:InfoBoth、logic:InfoNeither（Belnap 四值）、logic:InfoUndetermined 与 logic:InfoNotEvaluated。三个非肯定状态绝不互换：logic:InfoNeither 要求一次终结性求值；logic:InfoUndetermined 意为未得出裁定；logic:InfoNotEvaluated 意为引擎无法查看。该集合是封闭的；拼写有误的值被拒绝（design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md，§The reasoning result）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/InfoSupported|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:InformationState value when there is a proof and no counterproof. Wire value `supported`. Provisional when the evaluation is not conclusive (logic:Incomplete); conclusive within the fragment otherwise."
msgstr "当存在证明而无反证时的 logic:InformationState 值。线值 `supported`。当求值非终结性时（logic:Incomplete）为暂定；否则在该片段内为终结性。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/InfoUndetermined|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:InformationState value when the evaluation did not reach a conclusive verdict — the search did not finish (budget exhausted), a partial-order tie, or a graded semantics with no discretization policy. Wire value `undetermined`. NOT the conclusive logic:InfoNeither."
msgstr "当求值未达成终结性裁定时的 logic:InformationState 值——搜索未结束（预算耗尽）、一次偏序平局，或一种没有离散化策略的分级语义。线值 `undetermined`。并非终结性的 logic:InfoNeither。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/inhabitationIntervalFrameRequirement|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Asserts that every gmeow:TimeInterval a gmeow:InhabitationTenure scopes via gmeow:duringInterval must declare at least one gmeow:hasTemporalFrame — an interval asserted without its frame is ill-formed (Principle 11: the interval carries its frame). The native coherence gate raises a violation when a scoping interval lacks a frame."
msgstr "断言某 gmeow:InhabitationTenure 经由 gmeow:duringInterval 所界定的每个 gmeow:TimeInterval 都必须声明至少一个 gmeow:hasTemporalFrame——不带其框架而被断言的区间是不良构的（原则 11：区间承载其框架）。当某界定区间缺少框架时，原生融贯闸门引发一项违规。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/inModule|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a statement (an axiom or rule, carried on its reifier) to the logic:Module it is asserted in — the per-statement carrier of the module context axis, parallel to how logic:standpoint carries the world axis. A statement with no logic:inModule belongs to the top-level module. It never licenses cross-module entailment on its own: importation (logic:imports) governs which modules' sentences a module sees, and the bare membership edge is index and provenance, not an inference-bearing relation. It asserts no OWL characteristic; its logical character is documented in prose, matching the kernel convention."
msgstr "将某语句（一条公理或规则，承载于其具体化器之上）关联到它所被断言于其中的 logic:Module——模块情境轴的按语句载体，与 logic:standpoint 承载世界轴的方式相平行。没有 logic:inModule 的语句属于顶层模块。它单凭自身绝不许可跨模块蕴涵：导入（logic:imports）支配一个模块能看到哪些模块的语句，而裸露的成员边只是索引与出处，并非承载推理的关系。它不断言任何 OWL 特性；其逻辑性格以散文记述，符合内核约定。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/inModule|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A reified axiom can carry logic:inModule ex:geometry without changing the standpoint under which it holds."
msgstr "一个具体化的公理可以携带 logic:inModule ex:geometry，而不改变其成立所依据的立场。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/InputInvalid|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:InputStatus value for an ill-formed request: no reasoning was attempted and the other four fields are vacuous. Wire value `invalid`."
msgstr "对应格式不良请求的 logic:InputStatus 值：未尝试任何推理，其余四个字段皆为空。线值 `invalid`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/InputStatus|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The closed value class of the logic:resultInput field: was the request well-formed? Its individuals are logic:InputValid and logic:InputInvalid. The set is closed, so a misspelt value names no declared value and is rejected (design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md, §The reasoning result)."
msgstr "logic:resultInput 字段的封闭值类：请求是否格式良好？其个体为 logic:InputValid 与 logic:InputInvalid。该集合是封闭的，故拼写有误的值不指称任何已声明的值并被拒绝（design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md，§The reasoning result）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/InputValid|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:InputStatus value for a request whose sources parsed and type-checked: reasoning was attempted. Wire value `valid`."
msgstr "对应其来源已解析并通过类型检查之请求的 logic:InputStatus 值：已尝试推理。线值 `valid`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/InsertUpdate|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "An elementary Transaction-Logic update of the `ins(F)` kind: it asserts one support into the successor state of a path. Insertion advances the path by materializing the support in the successor snapshot; it does not mutate the predecessor state."
msgstr "一种 `ins(F)` 类的基本 Transaction-Logic 更新：它向某路径的后继状态断言一个支撑。插入通过在后继快照中物化该支撑来推进路径；它不改动前驱状态。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ins|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:InsertUpdate to the support/fact it asserts. The `ins(F)` primitive makes F active in the successor state while leaving the predecessor state untouched."
msgstr "将某 logic:InsertUpdate 关联到它所断言的支撑/事实。`ins(F)` 原语使 F 在后继状态中活跃，同时使前驱状态保持不动。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/instanceOf|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "HiLog deep instantiation: relates an individual or a type to a (possibly higher-order) type it instantiates, across any number of meta-levels. The first-class multi-level primitive that replaces OWL punning (criticism 5): types are reified as first-order individuals so 'an instance of a type that is itself an instance of a metatype' is ordinary first-order quantification rather than a punning trick. The general relation of which logic:suppliesIdentity is the identity-supplying specialization."
msgstr "HiLog 深度实例化：将某个别者或某类型关联到它跨任意数目元层级所实例化的一个（可能为高阶的）类型。这是取代 OWL 双关（批评 5）的头等多层级原语：类型被具体化为一阶个别者，从而「某个本身即是某元类型之实例的类型的一个实例」成为寻常的一阶量化，而非双关把戏。它是 logic:suppliesIdentity 作为其提供同一性之特化所归属的一般关系。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/instanceOf|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:Fido logic:instanceOf ex:Dog and ex:Dog logic:instanceOf logic:Kind form two levels of one deep-instantiation chain."
msgstr "ex:Fido logic:instanceOf ex:Dog 与 ex:Dog logic:instanceOf logic:Kind 构成一条深度实例化链的两个层级。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/instantiatesFramework|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a term to the closed logic:LogicalFramework discipline(s) it traffics in — the reasoning machinery the term belongs to (logic:HolonicPosition instantiates logic:HolonicFramework; gmeow:Norm instantiates logic:DeonticFramework). Multi-valued: a term may inhabit several frameworks (a logic:GoalEvaluation that ranges over deontic-ideal worlds is both teleological and deontic). Classifying metadata, orthogonal to the logic:ReasoningContract facets that configure a particular evaluation; the range is the closed class, so an undeclared value is rejected. Absence is meaningful — a plain domain term that traffics in no special discipline carries no framework, and none is asserted (design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md, the unified-logic-core section)."
msgstr "将某词项关联到它所涉足的封闭 logic:LogicalFramework 学科——该词项所归属的推理机制（logic:HolonicPosition 实例化 logic:HolonicFramework；gmeow:Norm 实例化 logic:DeonticFramework）。多值：一个词项可栖居于若干框架（一个遍历道义-理想世界的 logic:GoalEvaluation 既是目的论的又是道义的）。这是分类性元数据，与配置某特定求值的 logic:ReasoningContract 侧面正交；值域为封闭类，故未声明的值被拒绝。缺席是有意义的——一个不涉足任何特殊学科的普通领域词项不携带任何框架，也不断言任何框架（design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md，unified-logic-core 章节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/instantiatesPlan|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates an executed action occurrence — a materialized logic:TransactionStep (a gmeow:Event minted per run position) — to the logic:Plan program it was executed under. Domain the occurrence, range logic:Plan (stated in prose). It is the plan-level companion of logic:instantiatesSchema: where that link records the reusable type an occurrence instantiates (Event to ActionSchema), this records the whole plan the occurrence realizes (Event to Plan). The pair is a load-bearing in-band recovery witness — the executed record carries, in band, a back-reference to both the schema and the plan it instantiates — so a correspondence's put leg can recover the planned skeleton from an execution record (the mnemomorphism's in-band complement at the process layer) rather than synthesizing a plausible plan. Without it the descriptive run and the prescriptive plan are only externally related; with it the planned portion round-trips."
msgstr "将某已执行的动作发生——一个被物化的 logic:TransactionStep（按运行位置铸造的 gmeow:Event）——关联到它在其下被执行的 logic:Plan 程序。定义域为该发生，值域 logic:Plan（以散文陈述）。它是 logic:instantiatesSchema 在计划层面的伙伴：该链接记录某发生所实例化的可复用类型（Event 到 ActionSchema），而此项记录该发生所实现的整个计划（Event 到 Plan）。这一对是承重的带内恢复见证——已执行记录在带内携带一个回指，既指向其所实例化的模式又指向其所实例化的计划——从而某对应的 put 支路能从某执行记录恢复计划好的骨架（记忆态射在流程层的带内补足），而非合成一个貌似合理的计划。若无它，描述性的运行与规定性的计划仅在外部相关；有了它，计划好的部分得以往返。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/instantiatesSchema|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a gmeow:Event (an action occurrence — a particular event executed along a particular path) to the logic:ActionSchema it instantiates. Domain gmeow:Event, range logic:ActionSchema (stated in prose). The occurrence is the same perdurant an intentional moment links to through gmeow:motivates; the schema is the reusable type it instantiates. The schema names what an action does; the path records that it was done and what changed."
msgstr "将某 gmeow:Event（一个动作发生——沿某特定路径执行的某特定事件）关联到它所实例化的 logic:ActionSchema。定义域 gmeow:Event，值域 logic:ActionSchema（以散文陈述）。该发生即某意向性时刻经由 gmeow:motivates 所联系到的同一个延续体；模式是它所实例化的可复用类型。模式命名一个动作做什么；路径记录它已被做以及发生了什么改变。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/InstitutionMorphism|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A satisfaction-preserving morphism between theories presented as institutions: truth in the source maps to truth in the view, so logical alignment axioms (up to owl:equivalentClass when the rung allows) are licensed. The morphism kind of a faithful down-projection."
msgstr "在以机构（institution）形式呈现的理论之间的一个保满足态射：源中的真映射为视图中的真，因而逻辑对齐公理（在阶梯允许时可达 owl:equivalentClass）获得许可。它是一种忠实下投影的态射种类。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/IntegrationDeficient|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The agency-verdict value for the second Koestlerian pathology — a 'whole' that refuses to integrate: under the declared logic:HolonicAgencyProfile, the holon bears an logic:selfAssertiveBasis value (it asserts itself as a whole) but bears no logic:integrativeBasis value, so its integrative (subordination-as-a-part) face has collapsed. Reached by negation-as-failure over the integrative marker while the self-assertive marker holds, so the verdict is profile-relative, never a bare default. The co-equal counterpart of logic:AutonomyDeficient (the opposite collapse); contrast logic:HolonIntegral (both faces) and logic:AgencyUnknown (neither evidenced) (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "第二种科斯特勒式病态的能动性裁定值——一个拒绝整合的「整体」：在所声明的 logic:HolonicAgencyProfile 下，该全子（holon）承载一个 logic:selfAssertiveBasis 值（它将自身断言为整体），却不承载任何 logic:integrativeBasis 值，因而其整合（作为部分的从属）面已坍缩。它经由对整合标记的失败即否定、同时自我肯定标记成立而得出，故裁定相对于剖面，绝非赤裸的默认。它是 logic:AutonomyDeficient（相反的坍缩）的对等对应物；与 logic:HolonIntegral（两面俱全）及 logic:AgencyUnknown（两者皆无佐证）相对照（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons 一节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/integrativeBasis|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:HolonicAgencyProfile to a property-value that evidences the integrative tendency: the profile holds that a holon bearing this value (logic:bearsProperty) subordinates itself as a part to a larger whole — Koestler's integrative face. The carrier that makes integration profile-relative, the co-equal twin of logic:selfAssertiveBasis (neither privileged, Principle 9). Without a borne integrative value a holon's integration face is not evidenced, contributing — together with the self-assertive face — to the logic:AgencyVerdict (logic:IntegrationDeficient or logic:HolonIntegral). The integration analogue of logic:reductionBasis and logic:activationBasis (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "把一个 logic:HolonicAgencyProfile 关联到一个佐证整合倾向的属性值：该剖面认为承载此值（logic:bearsProperty）的全子将自身作为部分从属于更大的整体——科斯特勒的整合面。它是使整合相对于剖面的载体，是 logic:selfAssertiveBasis 的对等孪生（两者皆不优先，原则 9）。若未承载整合值，则全子的整合面无佐证，从而——连同自我肯定面——共同促成 logic:AgencyVerdict（logic:IntegrationDeficient 或 logic:HolonIntegral）。它是 logic:reductionBasis 与 logic:activationBasis 的整合类比（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons 一节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/integrity|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Constraint to its closed-world integrity condition: the reified logic:Formula whose violation is a finding, not a derivation. Reuses the realized full-FOL formula core verbatim — the condition is an outer range-restricted universal (logic:forall over a bound focus) whose logic:antecedent guard names the class or predicate the focus ranges over and whose logic:consequent is the per-focus condition — so a constraint needs no bespoke shape DSL. The focus target (a class, or the subjects/objects of a predicate) is derived from that guard, never authored twice."
msgstr "把一个 logic:Constraint 关联到其闭世界完整性条件：其违反是一个发现而非一次推导的具体化 logic:Formula。它逐字复用已实现的全 FOL 公式内核——该条件是一个外层受值域限制的全称式（在受限焦点上的 logic:forall），其 logic:antecedent 守卫命名焦点所遍历的类或谓词，其 logic:consequent 是逐焦点条件——因而约束无需任何定制的形状 DSL。焦点目标（一个类，或一个谓词的主体/客体）由该守卫派生，绝不二次撰写。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/IntentNotFromDeceptionObligation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The standing non-entailment obligation that the presence of a held≠projected gap is EVIDENCE, never ENTAILMENT, of deceptive intent: the foundation must never derive gmeow:deceptiveIntentClaim (an attributed, defeasible standpoint claim) from a structural deception gap. Enforced by syntactic reachability over the rule strata (no rule head produces the predicate) and finite closure over the materialized derivation graph (the predicate appears in no DERIVED edge). Guards the deception slice held/projected model (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, §Typed formalization governance)."
msgstr "一项常设的非蕴涵义务：存在一处 held≠projected 缺口只是欺骗意图的证据、绝非其蕴涵：基础绝不可从结构性欺骗缺口推导出 gmeow:deceptiveIntentClaim（一个可归属、可被否决的立场主张）。它由规则层上的句法可达性（无任何规则头产出该谓词）与对已物化推导图的有限闭包（该谓词不出现在任何 DERIVED 边中）来强制执行。它守护欺骗切片的 held/projected 模型（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，§Typed formalization governance）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/invariant|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ActionSchema to what the action must preserve across its execution — the condition that holds before, during, and after. Domain logic:ActionSchema (stated in prose). One of the eight action-theory facets, distinct from logic:precondition (what must hold to begin) and logic:effect (what changes)."
msgstr "把一个 logic:ActionSchema 关联到该动作在其执行全程必须保持之物——在之前、期间与之后都成立的条件。定义域 logic:ActionSchema（以散文陈述）。它是八个动作理论切面之一，区别于 logic:precondition（开始所须成立者）与 logic:effect（所变者）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/inverseFunctionalProperty|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:identifiedBy a logic:inverseFunctionalProperty ."
msgstr "示例：ex:identifiedBy a logic:inverseFunctionalProperty ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/inverseFunctionalProperty|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Inverse functionality identifies subjects that share one object and can trigger equality reasoning."
msgstr "逆函数性识别共享同一宾语的主语，并可触发相等性推理。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/inverseOf|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:parentOf logic:inverseOf ex:childOf ."
msgstr "示例：ex:parentOf logic:inverseOf ex:childOf ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/inverseOf|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The declaration is symmetric between the two property names while reversing each related pair."
msgstr "该声明在两个属性名称之间是对称的，同时反转每一个相关联的对。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/invokesBuiltin|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Rule to a logic:Builtin it calls in its body: the dependency edge recording that a rule uses a native computational primitive, and therefore requires logic:ProceduralPrologProfile (where builtins are gated). Lets the compiler check that a rule invoking a builtin declares the procedural profile and records the loss when such a rule is projected to a declarative semantics."
msgstr "把一个 logic:Rule 关联到它在体内调用的一个 logic:Builtin：这条依赖边记录某规则使用了一个原生计算原语，因而要求 logic:ProceduralPrologProfile（内建在此受门控）。它让编译器得以核查调用内建的规则已声明程序化剖面，并在此类规则被投影到声明式语义时记录损失。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/invokesPathShape|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:PathInvocation to the logic:PathShape it applies by name: the dependency edge recording which reusable traversal a parametric call instantiates. Paired with logic:pathDepthArg, which supplies the concrete bound for the shape's logic:pathDepthParam."
msgstr "把一个 logic:PathInvocation 关联到它按名应用的 logic:PathShape：这条依赖边记录一次参数化调用实例化了哪条可复用遍历。与 logic:pathDepthArg 配对，后者为该形状的 logic:pathDepthParam 提供具体界限。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/irreflexiveProperty|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic: property-characteristic marker for irreflexivity: a property P such that P(a,a) holds for no a. The logic: analogue of owl:IrreflexiveProperty, used together with logic:transitiveProperty and logic:asymmetricProperty to make logic:properPartOf a genuine strict partial order (criticism 7)."
msgstr "表示非自反性的 logic: 属性特征标记：一个属性 P，使得对任何 a 都不成立 P(a,a)。它是 owl:IrreflexiveProperty 的 logic: 类比，与 logic:transitiveProperty 及 logic:asymmetricProperty 一同使用，以使 logic:properPartOf 成为一个真正的严格偏序（批评 7）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/isHolon|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The derived marker that projects holon-ness onto an entity: it holds of an entity that, within a holarchy, is simultaneously a proper part of some whole and itself has a proper part. It is the reasoning-surface marker (mirroring logic:isClass-style stereotype markers) from which the unary logic:Holon class is the OWL projection; the faithful construct is the relational logic:HolonicPosition, of which both are lossy projections. Never asserted by hand; it is entailed by the foundation lowering."
msgstr "把全子性投影到实体上的派生标记：它对某实体成立，该实体在一个全阶层（holarchy）内同时既是某整体的真部分、其自身又拥有一个真部分。它是推理面标记（仿照 logic:isClass 式的定型标记），一元的 logic:Holon 类是其 OWL 投影；忠实的构造是关系性的 logic:HolonicPosition，两者皆为其有损投影。绝不手工断言；它由基础降型所蕴涵。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/isolationInadequacyReason|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A human-readable description of WHY a logic:ConcurrentHistory's witnessed schedule fails to meet its declared logic:IsolationLevel — present exactly when logic:isolationLevelAdequacy is false. Domain logic:ConcurrentHistory, range xsd:string (stated in prose). In the snapshot-isolation model this is the case of a schedule that is not conflict-serializable (a write-skew or lost-update cycle) declared under logic:SerializableIsolation or logic:OpacityIsolation, and the reason names that: the schedule is not conflict-serializable, so it does not meet the declared strength. It is a guarantee-level finding, never a claim of logical contradiction within a state."
msgstr "一段人类可读的描述，说明为何一个 logic:ConcurrentHistory 的见证调度未能达到其所声明的 logic:IsolationLevel——恰在 logic:isolationLevelAdequacy 为假时呈现。定义域 logic:ConcurrentHistory，值域 xsd:string（以散文陈述）。在快照隔离模型中，这是这样一种情形：一个非冲突可串行化的调度（一个写偏斜或更新丢失环）被声明在 logic:SerializableIsolation 或 logic:OpacityIsolation 之下，而该理由指明：该调度非冲突可串行化，故未达到所声明的强度。它是保证级别的发现，绝非对某状态内逻辑矛盾的主张。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/isolationLevelAdequacy|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The boolean verdict of classifying a logic:ConcurrentHistory's witnessed schedule against the logic:IsolationLevel its run declared (logic:declaredIsolationLevel): true iff the schedule meets that declared guarantee strength. Domain logic:ConcurrentHistory, range xsd:boolean (stated in prose); present only when a level is declared. Because the concurrent evaluator realizes snapshot isolation, every level up to logic:SnapshotIsolation is adequate by construction; logic:SerializableIsolation and logic:OpacityIsolation are adequate iff the schedule is conflict-serializable — a write-skew cycle (which snapshot admits) is adequate for snapshot yet INADEQUATE for serializability. A false verdict carries a logic:isolationInadequacyReason. It is guarantee-strength adequacy, kept distinct from logic:protocolEnforced (mechanism soundness) and logic:satisfiesCriterion (the history property)."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ConcurrentHistory 的见证调度对照其运行所声明的 logic:IsolationLevel（logic:declaredIsolationLevel）进行分类所得的布尔裁定：当且仅当该调度达到所声明的保证强度时为真。定义域 logic:ConcurrentHistory，值域 xsd:boolean（以散文陈述）；仅在声明了级别时呈现。由于并发求值器实现的是快照隔离，直至 logic:SnapshotIsolation 的每个级别皆按构造充分；logic:SerializableIsolation 与 logic:OpacityIsolation 当且仅当调度冲突可串行化时充分——一个写偏斜环（快照容许之）对快照充分，却对可串行性不充分。假裁定携带一个 logic:isolationInadequacyReason。它是保证强度充分性，与 logic:protocolEnforced（机制健全性）及 logic:satisfiesCriterion（历史属性）保持区分。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/IsolationLevel|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The declared GUARANTEE STRENGTH a schedule must meet — not a history property and not an implementation mechanism. The closed value class spanning the standard isolation spectrum up to and including full serializability and opacity. Its individuals are logic:ReadUncommittedIsolation, logic:ReadCommittedIsolation, logic:RepeatableReadIsolation, logic:SnapshotIsolation, logic:SerializableIsolation, and logic:OpacityIsolation — the strongest, under which even aborted or in-flight transactions never observe an inconsistent state, strictly stronger than serializability. The set is closed; a misspelt value is rejected. This is one of three distinct, separately-declared concurrency concerns that must NOT be conflated: a logic:IsolationLevel is a guarantee strength, a logic:SerializabilityCriterion is a property of a history, and a logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol is an implementation mechanism."
msgstr "一个调度必须达到的所声明保证强度——既非历史属性也非实现机制。这个封闭值类涵盖标准隔离谱系，直至并包含完全可串行性与不透明性。其个体为 logic:ReadUncommittedIsolation、logic:ReadCommittedIsolation、logic:RepeatableReadIsolation、logic:SnapshotIsolation、logic:SerializableIsolation 与 logic:OpacityIsolation——其中最强者之下，即使已中止或在途的事务也绝不观察到不一致状态，严格强于可串行性。该集合封闭；拼写有误之值被拒。它是三个必须区分、分别声明、不可混同的并发关切之一：logic:IsolationLevel 是保证强度，logic:SerializabilityCriterion 是历史的一项属性，logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol 是一种实现机制。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Isomorphism|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The top rung: an iso, get ∘ put = id and put ∘ get = id, a full round-trip in both directions. The only rung that licenses a confidence-1.0 equivalence. Caps: both round-trip laws claimable."
msgstr "最高阶梯：一个同构，get ∘ put = id 且 put ∘ get = id，双向的完整往返。这是唯一许可置信度 1.0 等价的阶梯。上限：两条往返定律皆可主张。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/iterationBody|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Iteration combinator to the sub-program that constitutes its loop body — the program executed on each iteration pass. Domain logic:Iteration, range a transaction-program node (stated in prose). Paired with logic:iterationCondition, which carries the guard situation checked before each pass. Distinct from logic:leftOperand / logic:rightOperand (binary co-equal operands of serial, choice, concurrent, and fallback combinators): a loop body is not co-equal with a loop condition."
msgstr "把一个 logic:Iteration 组合子关联到构成其循环体的子程序——每一遍迭代所执行的程序。定义域 logic:Iteration，值域一个事务程序节点（以散文陈述）。与 logic:iterationCondition 配对，后者携带每遍之前所核查的守卫情形。区别于 logic:leftOperand / logic:rightOperand（串行、选择、并发与回退组合子的二元对等操作数）：循环体与循环条件并不对等。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/iterationCondition|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Iteration combinator to the situation type that gates each pass of the loop body — the loop is executed while this situation obtains at the current state; when it does not hold the iteration terminates. Domain logic:Iteration, range logic:Situation (stated in prose). Paired with logic:iterationBody. Reuses the situation-type pattern of logic:guardSituation and logic:boundSituationType: the engine reads this against the current path state via logic:situationObtains."
msgstr "把一个 logic:Iteration 组合子关联到对循环体每一遍设门的情形类型——当此情形在当前状态获得时循环即执行；当它不再成立，迭代终止。定义域 logic:Iteration，值域 logic:Situation（以散文陈述）。与 logic:iterationBody 配对。它复用 logic:guardSituation 与 logic:boundSituationType 的情形类型模式：引擎经由 logic:situationObtains 对照当前路径状态读取它。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Iteration|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The iteration program combinator: repeats a body sub-program while a loop condition holds. The body is carried by logic:iterationBody and the loop condition by logic:iterationCondition. Binary left/right operand semantics do not fit iteration — a loop has a body and a separate condition, not two co-equal operands — so logic:iterationBody and logic:iterationCondition are minted as dedicated properties rather than repurposing logic:leftOperand / logic:rightOperand. A logic:Iteration is the program-level counterpart of the loop/retry structure logic:StrongCyclicPlanSuccess quantifies over: a strong-cyclic plan succeeds when every fair execution of a loop through recoverable failures terminates at the goal in finitely many steps. The loop condition is a situation type checked before each body execution; when it does not hold the iteration terminates. Typed APART from recursive goal structures and from plain goal decomposition, which carry satisfaction dependency rather than control flow."
msgstr "迭代程序组合子：当一个循环条件成立时反复执行一个体子程序。体由 logic:iterationBody 携带，循环条件由 logic:iterationCondition 携带。二元左/右操作数语义不适配迭代——循环有一个体和一个独立条件，而非两个对等操作数——故 logic:iterationBody 与 logic:iterationCondition 被铸为专用属性，而非挪用 logic:leftOperand / logic:rightOperand。一个 logic:Iteration 是 logic:StrongCyclicPlanSuccess 所量化的循环/重试结构在程序层面的对应物：当一个循环穿越可恢复失败的每一次公平执行都在有限步内于目标终止时，一个强循环计划成功。循环条件是每次执行体之前所核查的情形类型；当它不再成立，迭代终止。它与递归目标结构以及朴素目标分解相区隔，后者携带满足依赖而非控制流。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/joinAggregateComparison|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The reified relation an expanded logic:JoinAggregateConstraint carries as its honest FOL integrity: joinAggregateComparison(this, function, comparator, threshold). The realized FOL formula core has neither an aggregate nor a join node, so this predication makes the multi-hop-join product-aggregate meaning complete in the FOL canon while the structured join-aggregate satellite (the ordered leg chain) drives the real multi-hop-join GROUP BY/HAVING SPARQL projection. It carries only the scalar core, not the leg chain, which lives in the satellite."
msgstr "一个展开的 logic:JoinAggregateConstraint 作为其诚实 FOL 完整性所携带的具体化关系：joinAggregateComparison(this, function, comparator, threshold)。已实现的 FOL 公式内核既无聚合节点亦无连接节点，故此谓述使多跳连接积聚合之义在 FOL 正典中得以完整，而结构化的连接聚合卫星（有序的分段链）驱动真正的多跳连接 GROUP BY/HAVING SPARQL 投影。它仅携带标量内核，而非分段链，后者驻留于卫星中。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/JoinAggregateConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Compact sugar for a multi-hop-join product-aggregate constraint (P9): a logic:onClass focus, an ordered logic:joinPath of at least two logic:JoinLeg records (each a reified relation with a logic:legSource / logic:legTarget / logic:legValue predicate and an optional logic:legRecordType), a logic:aggFunction (SUM for ∂²), a logic:aggComparator invariant, and a fixed literal logic:aggThreshold. Each leg hops from an already-bound endpoint through a record to the next endpoint, chaining leg[k].target into leg[k+1].source (the shared join variable); the aggregate is applied to the PRODUCT of the joined leaf values, GROUPED BY the (focus, far-endpoint) tuple, and a violation fires when a group value fails the invariant. It GENERALIZES logic:AggregateConstraint from a single-predicate focus aggregate to a chained-join product aggregate, and is the sanctioned home of the general-CW ∂²=0 conformance check (a SUM of incidence-sign products over composable cells that must equal 0). Expands to a canonical logic:Constraint carrying both the honest reified FOL integrity and a structured join-aggregate satellite, lowered to a SELECT $this ?far … GROUP BY $this ?far HAVING(…) sh:SPARQLConstraint whose join order uses the incidence index and scales with the number of records, never cells². It is not a single-predicate aggregate (use logic:AggregateConstraint), not a derivation rule (a reduce head belongs on logic:aggregateFunction), and not a cartesian product over cells. Frontend-only authoring shortcut."
msgstr "多跳连接积聚合约束的紧凑语法糖（P9）：一个 logic:onClass 焦点，一个由至少两条 logic:JoinLeg 记录组成的有序 logic:joinPath（每条是一个带 logic:legSource / logic:legTarget / logic:legValue 谓词及可选 logic:legRecordType 的具体化关系），一个 logic:aggFunction（对 ∂² 用 SUM），一个 logic:aggComparator 不变式，以及一个固定的字面 logic:aggThreshold。每条分段从一个已绑定的端点经一条记录跳到下一个端点，把 leg[k].target 链入 leg[k+1].source（共享连接变量）；聚合施加于所连接叶值的乘积（PRODUCT），按 (焦点, 远端点) 元组分组（GROUPED BY），当某组值未通过不变式时触发违反。它把 logic:AggregateConstraint 从单谓词焦点聚合泛化为链式连接积聚合，并且是通用 CW ∂²=0 一致性检查（可复合胞元上关联符号积的一个必须等于 0 的 SUM）获批准的归处。它展开为一个既携带诚实具体化 FOL 完整性又携带结构化连接聚合卫星的规范 logic:Constraint，降型为一个 SELECT $this ?far … GROUP BY $this ?far HAVING(…) 的 sh:SPARQLConstraint，其连接顺序采用关联索引并随记录数量伸缩，绝不按胞元²。它不是单谓词聚合（请用 logic:AggregateConstraint），不是推导规则（归约头属于 logic:aggregateFunction），也不是胞元上的笛卡尔积。仅前端的撰写捷径。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/JoinAggregateConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:boundarySquareZero a logic:JoinAggregateConstraint ; logic:onClass ex:TopCell ; logic:aggFunction \"SUM\" ; logic:aggComparator \"=\" ; logic:aggThreshold 0 ; logic:joinPath ( [ logic:legRecordType ex:Incidence ; logic:legSource ex:incidenceCoface ; logic:legTarget ex:incidenceFace ; logic:legValue ex:incidenceSign ] [ logic:legRecordType ex:Incidence ; logic:legSource ex:incidenceCoface ; logic:legTarget ex:incidenceFace ; logic:legValue ex:incidenceSign ] ) ; logic:formalizes ex:BoundaryOperator ."
msgstr "示例：ex:boundarySquareZero a logic:JoinAggregateConstraint ; logic:onClass ex:TopCell ; logic:aggFunction \"SUM\" ; logic:aggComparator \"=\" ; logic:aggThreshold 0 ; logic:joinPath ( [ logic:legRecordType ex:Incidence ; logic:legSource ex:incidenceCoface ; logic:legTarget ex:incidenceFace ; logic:legValue ex:incidenceSign ] [ logic:legRecordType ex:Incidence ; logic:legSource ex:incidenceCoface ; logic:legTarget ex:incidenceFace ; logic:legValue ex:incidenceSign ] ) ; logic:formalizes ex:BoundaryOperator ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/JoinLeg|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "One hop (leg) of a logic:JoinAggregateConstraint's logic:joinPath: a reified relation record whose logic:legSource predicate reaches this leg's source endpoint, whose logic:legTarget predicate reaches its target endpoint, and whose logic:legValue predicate carries the numeric leaf value multiplied into the group product; an optional logic:legRecordType types the record for the index-anchored join. The legs are ORDERED (the list order is semantic) and chain leg[k].target into leg[k+1].source, so a leg is a hop specification, not a data record — it names the predicates the projected SPARQL joins on, never an incidence itself."
msgstr "一个 logic:JoinAggregateConstraint 的 logic:joinPath 的一跳（分段）：一条具体化关系记录，其 logic:legSource 谓词到达此分段的源端点，其 logic:legTarget 谓词到达其目标端点，其 logic:legValue 谓词携带被乘入组乘积的数值叶值；一个可选的 logic:legRecordType 为索引锚定的连接给该记录定类型。分段是有序的（列表次序具语义），并把 leg[k].target 链入 leg[k+1].source，故一条分段是一个跳规格，而非一条数据记录——它命名被投影 SPARQL 所连接的谓词，绝非关联本身。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/JoinLeg|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "[ logic:legRecordType ex:Incidence ; logic:legSource ex:incidenceCoface ; logic:legTarget ex:incidenceFace ; logic:legValue ex:incidenceSign ]"
msgstr "示例：[ logic:legRecordType ex:Incidence ; logic:legSource ex:incidenceCoface ; logic:legTarget ex:incidenceFace ; logic:legValue ex:incidenceSign ]"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/joinPath|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The ordered join specification of a logic:JoinAggregateConstraint: an rdf:List of at least two logic:JoinLeg records whose target/source predicates chain the endpoints (leg[k].target is the shared join variable leg[k+1].source re-binds). The list order is SEMANTIC — it is the composition order of the hops — so a joinPath is a traversal specification, not an unordered set of predicates; a single-element list is not a JOIN and is rejected."
msgstr "一个 logic:JoinAggregateConstraint 的有序连接规格：一个至少含两条 logic:JoinLeg 记录的 rdf:List，其目标/源谓词把端点相链（leg[k].target 是共享连接变量，leg[k+1].source 重新绑定它）。列表次序具语义——它是各跳的复合次序——故一个 joinPath 是一个遍历规格，而非无序的谓词集合；单元素列表不是连接（JOIN），会被拒。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/JointOutcome|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "One row of a logic:DependencyModel's explicit joint table: a single joint assignment of truth values to the model's correlated facts, together with logic:jointProbability for that assignment. The facts asserted true in this outcome are named by logic:outcomeAssignment; correlated facts not named are taken to be false in this outcome."
msgstr "一个 logic:DependencyModel 的显式联合表的一行：对模型相关事实的真值的一次单一联合赋值，连同该赋值的 logic:jointProbability。在此结果中断言为真的事实由 logic:outcomeAssignment 命名；未被命名的相关事实在此结果中被视为假。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/jointOutcome|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:DependencyModel to one logic:JointOutcome of its explicit joint table. The outcomes a model declares must be mutually exclusive and exhaustive over the assignments to its logic:correlates set, and their logic:jointProbability values must sum to one."
msgstr "把一个 logic:DependencyModel 关联到其显式联合表的一个 logic:JointOutcome。一个模型所声明的结果必须在对其 logic:correlates 集合的赋值上互斥且穷尽，且其 logic:jointProbability 值必须和为一。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/jointProbability|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The probability mass a logic:DependencyModel assigns to one logic:JointOutcome — the joint probability of that exact assignment of truth values to the model's correlated facts. Distinct from logic:probability (a per-fact marginal): the joint outcomes of a model partition its correlated sample space and their logic:jointProbability values sum to one. The range is intentionally left open (no rdfs:range), matching the other quantitative axes (logic:probability, logic:confidence, logic:weight, logic:evidenceStrength), which this standalone module declares without an xsd range: the value is a unit-interval decimal."
msgstr "一个 logic:DependencyModel 赋予一个 logic:JointOutcome 的概率质量——即对模型相关事实真值的那一确切赋值的联合概率。区别于 logic:probability（逐事实的边缘概率）：一个模型的联合结果划分其相关样本空间，且其 logic:jointProbability 值和为一。值域有意留空（无 rdfs:range），与其他定量轴（logic:probability、logic:confidence、logic:weight、logic:evidenceStrength）一致，此独立模块声明它们时均不带 xsd 值域：其值是一个单位区间小数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Kind|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A rigid sortal that supplies a principle of identity to its instances and applies necessarily across every world in which an instance exists: an ultimate sortal under which an object falls for its whole existence. Every object instantiates exactly one ultimate Kind. Rigid (rigidlyAppliesTo) and identity-supplying (suppliesIdentity); contrast the anti-rigid Role and Phase."
msgstr "一个刚性种别（sortal），为其实例提供同一性原则，并在实例存在的每个世界中必然适用：一个物体终其存在都归属其下的终极种别。每个物体恰好实例化一个终极 Kind。刚性（rigidlyAppliesTo）且提供同一性（suppliesIdentity）；与反刚性的 Role 和 Phase 相对照。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/LadderProjectionProfile|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A declared per-dimension threshold profile governing the generated coarse projection of the multidimensional logic:CognitiveAssessment onto the gmeow:isAwareOf … gmeow:hasMastered knowledge ladder: a set of logic:DimensionThreshold rows (logic:hasThresholdRow), each binding a ladder edge to its source dimension and the minimum logic:AssessmentLevel an assessment must clear for the edge to be emitted. Making the thresholds an explicit profile keeps the ordinal chain a projection a consumer that needs one number can read, while the factored assessment stays canonical — the ladder never re-establishes mastery, understanding, knowledge and awareness as a single ordinal entailment chain in place of the independent dimensions."
msgstr "一个所声明的逐维阈值剖面，管辖将多维 logic:CognitiveAssessment 生成投影到 gmeow:isAwareOf … gmeow:hasMastered 知识阶梯的粗投影：一组 logic:DimensionThreshold 行（logic:hasThresholdRow），每行把一条阶梯边绑定到其源维度以及一次评估须清过、该边方得发出的最小 logic:AssessmentLevel。把阈值做成显式剖面，使序数链保持为一个需要单一数字的消费者可读的投影，同时因子化的评估仍为规范——阶梯绝不把掌握、理解、知识与觉知重建为一条单一序数蕴涵链以取代各独立维度。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ladderRowAwareness|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The default-profile row emitting gmeow:isAwareOf when the awareness dimension reaches logic:levelEmerging."
msgstr "当觉知维度达到 logic:levelEmerging 时发出 gmeow:isAwareOf 的默认剖面行。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ladderRowConceptual|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The default-profile row emitting gmeow:understands when the conceptual-understanding dimension reaches logic:levelCompetent."
msgstr "当概念理解维度达到 logic:levelCompetent 时发出 gmeow:understands 的默认剖面行。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ladderRowDeclarative|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The default-profile row emitting gmeow:knowsAbout when the declarative-familiarity dimension reaches logic:levelCompetent."
msgstr "当陈述性熟悉维度达到 logic:levelCompetent 时发出 gmeow:knowsAbout 的默认剖面行。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ladderRowProceduralMastery|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The procedural half of the default-profile gmeow:hasMastered rung: procedural competence must reach logic:levelStrong. Read together with logic:ladderRowTransferMastery — both must clear for gmeow:hasMastered."
msgstr "默认剖面 gmeow:hasMastered 阶梯的程序性一半：程序性胜任须达到 logic:levelStrong。与 logic:ladderRowTransferMastery 一并阅读——两者皆须清过方得 gmeow:hasMastered。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ladderRowTransferMastery|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The transfer half of the default-profile gmeow:hasMastered rung: transfer must reach logic:levelStrong. Read together with logic:ladderRowProceduralMastery — both must clear for gmeow:hasMastered, so mastery of one narrow task never implies broad command."
msgstr "默认剖面 gmeow:hasMastered 阶梯的迁移一半：迁移须达到 logic:levelStrong。与 logic:ladderRowProceduralMastery 一并阅读——两者皆须清过方得 gmeow:hasMastered，故对一项狭窄任务的掌握绝不蕴涵宽广的驾驭。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/lawClaimed|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:LawClaim to the logic:CorrespondenceLaw it asserts (logic:GetPut, logic:PutGet, logic:PutPut or logic:SectionLaw). Domain logic:LawClaim, range logic:CorrespondenceLaw."
msgstr "把一个 logic:LawClaim 关联到它所断言的 logic:CorrespondenceLaw（logic:GetPut、logic:PutGet、logic:PutPut 或 logic:SectionLaw）。定义域 logic:LawClaim，值域 logic:CorrespondenceLaw。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/LawClaim|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A claim that a logic:Correspondence satisfies a particular logic:CorrespondenceLaw (named by logic:lawClaimed), together with the discharge state of that claim: a logic:DischargeVerdict via logic:lawDischargeVerdict and, when applicable, the logic:DischargeCondition under which it was checked via logic:lawDischargeCondition. It reuses the foundation's executable discharge vocabulary rather than a parallel status enum: a law proved within a certified fragment is logic:ObligationDischarged under logic:DischargeCertifiedFragment; a refuted law is logic:ObligationViolated with its countermodel; an authored-but-unchecked or inconclusive law is logic:ObligationUnknown, carried forward. The overclaim gate fires when a correspondence claims a law its lowered legs do not satisfy (design/LOGIC-CORRESPONDENCE.md, the preservation-is-the-lens-law-framework section)."
msgstr "一个主张：某个 logic:Correspondence 满足某条特定的 logic:CorrespondenceLaw（由 logic:lawClaimed 命名），连同该主张的清偿状态：经 logic:lawDischargeVerdict 的一个 logic:DischargeVerdict，以及在适用时经 logic:lawDischargeCondition 所核查之下的 logic:DischargeCondition。它复用基础的可执行清偿词汇，而非另设一个并行的状态枚举：在一个已认证片段内证明的定律为 logic:DischargeCertifiedFragment 之下的 logic:ObligationDischarged；被反驳的定律为携带反模型的 logic:ObligationViolated；一条已撰写但未核查或未决的定律为 logic:ObligationUnknown，被向前携带。当一个对应主张其降型分段并不满足的定律时，过度主张门被触发（design/LOGIC-CORRESPONDENCE.md，preservation-is-the-lens-law-framework 一节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/lawDischargeCondition|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:LawClaim to the logic:DischargeCondition under which its logic:lawDischargeVerdict is conclusively checkable (for example logic:DischargeCertifiedFragment for a law proved within a certified complete fragment). Optional: a law carrying logic:ObligationUnknown with no condition is an authored-but-unverified claim. Reuses the foundation's discharge-condition value class. Domain logic:LawClaim, range logic:DischargeCondition."
msgstr "把一个 logic:LawClaim 关联到其 logic:lawDischargeVerdict 得以确定性可核查之下的 logic:DischargeCondition（例如对在一个已认证完整片段内证明的定律用 logic:DischargeCertifiedFragment）。可选：一条携带 logic:ObligationUnknown 而无条件的定律是一个已撰写但未验证的主张。复用基础的清偿条件值类。定义域 logic:LawClaim，值域 logic:DischargeCondition。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/lawDischargeVerdict|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:LawClaim to the logic:DischargeVerdict its check returned — logic:ObligationDischarged, logic:ObligationUnknown or logic:ObligationViolated. Reuses the foundation's discharge-verdict value class (the law-claim analogue of logic:obligationDischargeVerdict, which is domain-locked to logic:NonEntailmentObligation): an unchecked or inconclusive law is logic:ObligationUnknown, never silently passed. Domain logic:LawClaim, range logic:DischargeVerdict."
msgstr "把一个 logic:LawClaim 关联到其核查所返回的 logic:DischargeVerdict——logic:ObligationDischarged、logic:ObligationUnknown 或 logic:ObligationViolated。复用基础的清偿裁定值类（它是 logic:obligationDischargeVerdict 在定律主张层面的类比，后者被域锁定于 logic:NonEntailmentObligation）：一条未核查或未决的定律为 logic:ObligationUnknown，绝不静默通过。定义域 logic:LawClaim，值域 logic:DischargeVerdict。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/LeastModelSemantics|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The model-semantics facet value selecting the unique least Herbrand model of a positive (or stratified) program. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract; the monotonic semantics underlying the positive-Horn and stratified-negation presets, contrasted with the well-founded and stable-model values for unstratified negation."
msgstr "选取一个正（或分层）程序唯一最小埃尔布朗模型的模型语义切面值。在一个 ReasoningContract 上为单值；它是正 Horn 与分层否定预设所依托的单调语义，与用于非分层否定的良基与稳定模型值相对照。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/leftOperand|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a binary transaction-program combinator (for example a logic:SerialConjunction) to its left/prefix operand — the program that holds over the prefix of the executing path. Range a transaction-program node (stated in prose). Paired with logic:rightOperand."
msgstr "把一个二元事务程序组合子（例如一个 logic:SerialConjunction）关联到其左/前缀操作数——在执行路径的前缀上成立的程序。值域一个事务程序节点（以散文陈述）。与 logic:rightOperand 配对。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/legRecordType|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The optional class typing the reified relation record a logic:JoinLeg traverses (e.g. an incidence-record class), emitted as an index-anchoring `?record a <Type>` triple in the projected join and a well-formedness guard. Optional: a leg with no logic:legRecordType is bound solely by its role and value predicates. It types the RECORD node, not the endpoints the leg connects."
msgstr "对一个 logic:JoinLeg 所遍历的具体化关系记录定类型的可选类（例如一个关联记录类），在被投影的连接中作为一个索引锚定的 `?record a <Type>` 三元组以及一个良构守卫而发出。可选：无 logic:legRecordType 的分段仅由其角色谓词与值谓词绑定。它给记录节点定类型，而非分段所连接的端点。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/legSource|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The predicate from a logic:JoinLeg's record to this leg's SOURCE endpoint (record → from). The first leg's source binds to the focus $this; every later leg's source binds to the preceding leg's logic:legTarget (the shared join variable). It names a role PREDICATE the projected SPARQL anchors the join on, never an endpoint node."
msgstr "从一个 logic:JoinLeg 的记录到此分段源端点的谓词（记录 → 源端）。第一条分段的源绑定到焦点 $this；其后每条分段的源绑定到前一条分段的 logic:legTarget（共享连接变量）。它命名被投影 SPARQL 用以锚定连接的一个角色谓词，绝非一个端点节点。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/legTarget|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The predicate from a logic:JoinLeg's record to this leg's TARGET endpoint (record → to). The intermediate legs' targets are aggregated away (summed over); the LAST leg's target is the far endpoint of the (focus, far-endpoint) group key. It names a role PREDICATE the join binds the next endpoint on, never an endpoint node."
msgstr "从一个 logic:JoinLeg 的记录到此分段目标端点的谓词（记录 → 目标端）。中间各分段的目标被聚合掉（被求和）；最末一条分段的目标是 (焦点, 远端点) 组键的远端点。它命名连接用以绑定下一端点的一个角色谓词，绝非一个端点节点。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/legValue|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The predicate from a logic:JoinLeg's record to the numeric leaf value multiplied into the group product (record → value). For the ∂² check it is the incidence sign; the projected SPARQL computes the PRODUCT of every leg's leaf value inside the aggregate. It names the value PREDICATE, not the value literal itself."
msgstr "从一个 logic:JoinLeg 的记录到被乘入组乘积的数值叶值的谓词（记录 → 值）。对 ∂² 检查它是关联符号；被投影的 SPARQL 在聚合内部计算每条分段叶值的乘积（PRODUCT）。它命名值谓词，而非值字面本身。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Lens|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The executable asymmetric core a logic:Correspondence wraps: a get / put leg pair between a rich source S and a derived view V, with get : S → V the down-projection and put : V × S → S the up-projection. GMEOW is always the source S and the external vocabulary the view V, so down-projection (GMEOW → external) is the get leg and up-projection (external → GMEOW) is the put leg. The view is the smaller, derived thing; put folds a possibly-fresh view back into the rich source, and the ingest-with-no-prior-state case (S empty) is exactly where a witness must travel in the view — the mnemomorphism a logic:Correspondence records with logic:mnemomorphic. Both legs are logic:TransactionProgram bodies over the path semantics of the transaction layer and logic:PathShape — no new pattern language is introduced. It is not the logic:Correspondence envelope, which separately carries the relation, quantitative axes, law claims, and standpoint (design/LOGIC-CORRESPONDENCE.md, the orientation-convention section)."
msgstr "一个 logic:Correspondence 所包裹的可执行非对称内核：在一个丰富源 S 与一个派生视图 V 之间的一对 get / put 分段，其中 get : S → V 为下投影、put : V × S → S 为上投影。GMEOW 始终是源 S 而外部词汇是视图 V，故下投影（GMEOW → 外部）是 get 分段、上投影（外部 → GMEOW）是 put 分段。视图是较小的、派生之物；put 把一个或许全新的视图折回丰富源，而无先前状态的摄入情形（S 为空）恰是一个见证必须在视图中携行之处——即一个 logic:Correspondence 以 logic:mnemomorphic 记录的记忆态射。两条分段皆为事务层路径语义与 logic:PathShape 之上的 logic:TransactionProgram 体——不引入新的模式语言。它不是 logic:Correspondence 封套，后者另行携带关系、定量轴、定律主张与立场（design/LOGIC-CORRESPONDENCE.md，orientation-convention 一节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Lens|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:alignment logic:hasLens ex:roundTripLens . ex:roundTripLens logic:getLeg ex:downProjection ; logic:putLeg ex:upProjection ."
msgstr "示例：ex:alignment logic:hasLens ex:roundTripLens . ex:roundTripLens logic:getLeg ex:downProjection ; logic:putLeg ex:upProjection ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/levelAtOrAbove|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Orders the ordinal assessment scale: relates a logic:AssessmentLevel to itself and to every level it surpasses (logic:levelStrong logic:levelAtOrAbove logic:levelCompetent). Reflexive-and-transitive on the levels, so the coarse-ladder projection can test 'the assessed level is at or above the threshold level' by a single body atom, with no numeric comparison (which would force a procedural profile). The full reflexive-transitive closure is asserted on the level individuals so the test needs no transitive computation in the rule engine."
msgstr "为序数评估尺度定序：把一个 logic:AssessmentLevel 关联到其自身及其所超越的每个级别（logic:levelStrong logic:levelAtOrAbove logic:levelCompetent）。在各级别上自反且传递，故粗阶梯投影可用单一体原子测试「所评级别处于阈值级别或以上」，无需数值比较（那会强制程序化剖面）。完整的自反传递闭包被断言在各级别个体上，故该测试在规则引擎中无需任何传递计算。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/levelCompetent|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The third ordinal assessment level: the dimension is solidly evidenced. Surpasses logic:levelEmerging and logic:levelNone on the logic:levelAtOrAbove order."
msgstr "第三个序数评估级别：该维度得到扎实佐证。在 logic:levelAtOrAbove 序上超越 logic:levelEmerging 与 logic:levelNone。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/levelEmerging|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The second ordinal assessment level: the dimension is weakly evidenced. Surpasses logic:levelNone on the logic:levelAtOrAbove order."
msgstr "第二个序数评估级别：该维度得到微弱佐证。在 logic:levelAtOrAbove 序上超越 logic:levelNone。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/levelNone|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The lowest ordinal assessment level: the dimension is not evidenced at all. Clears no ladder rung's threshold."
msgstr "最低的序数评估级别：该维度全无佐证。不清过任何阶梯级的阈值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/levelStrong|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The highest ordinal assessment level: the dimension is strongly evidenced. Surpasses every lower level on the logic:levelAtOrAbove order."
msgstr "最高的序数评估级别：该维度得到强力佐证。在 logic:levelAtOrAbove 序上超越每个更低级别。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/LifecycleActive|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:LifecycleStatus value for a goal currently held and pursued — its adoption tenure open. Contrast logic:LifecycleRetired (tenure closed) and logic:LifecycleSuperseded (replaced)."
msgstr "用于一个当前持有并追求之目标的 logic:LifecycleStatus 值——其采纳任期开放。与 logic:LifecycleRetired（任期关闭）及 logic:LifecycleSuperseded（被替换）相对照。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/LifecycleRetired|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:LifecycleStatus value for a goal no longer pursued, its adoption tenure closed by supersession rather than erased — the abandoned goal remains auditable. Contrast logic:LifecycleSuperseded, where a specific replacement goal takes its place."
msgstr "用于一个不再追求之目标的 logic:LifecycleStatus 值，其采纳任期因被取代而关闭、而非被抹除——被放弃的目标仍可审计。与 logic:LifecycleSuperseded 相对照，后者有一个具体的替换目标取而代之。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/LifecycleStatus|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The closed value class of the lifecycle axis of a logic:GoalEvaluation: where the goal stands in its adoption history. Its individuals are logic:LifecycleActive (currently held), logic:LifecycleRetired (no longer pursued, its tenure closed), and logic:LifecycleSuperseded (replaced by another goal). The set is closed; a misspelt value is rejected. This axis varies independently of satisfaction and feasibility — goal revision is supersession, never erasure, so a retired or superseded goal remains an auditable closed tenure."
msgstr "一个 logic:GoalEvaluation 之生命周期轴的封闭值类：该目标在其采纳历史中所处之位。其个体为 logic:LifecycleActive（当前持有）、logic:LifecycleRetired（不再追求，其任期关闭）与 logic:LifecycleSuperseded（被另一目标替换）。该集合封闭；拼写有误之值被拒。此轴独立于满足与可行性而变化——目标修订是取代、绝非抹除，故一个已退役或已被取代的目标仍是一段可审计的关闭任期。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/lifecycleStatus|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:GoalEvaluation to the logic:LifecycleStatus it carries — the lifecycle axis of the factored outcome. Domain logic:GoalEvaluation, range logic:LifecycleStatus (stated in prose). Varies independently of satisfaction, feasibility, and goal-evaluation status."
msgstr "把一个 logic:GoalEvaluation 关联到它所携带的 logic:LifecycleStatus——即因子化结果的生命周期轴。定义域 logic:GoalEvaluation，值域 logic:LifecycleStatus（以散文陈述）。独立于满足、可行性与目标评估状态而变化。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/LifecycleSuperseded|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:LifecycleStatus value for a goal replaced by another — a closed tenure standing under a successor goal. Distinct from logic:LifecycleRetired (closed with no successor named)."
msgstr "用于一个被另一目标替换之目标的 logic:LifecycleStatus 值——一段立于一个后继目标之下的关闭任期。区别于 logic:LifecycleRetired（关闭而未命名后继）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/linkNextAcyclicity|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Asserts on the canonical carrier that gmeow:linkNext is acyclic: a causal-cascade walk never reaches itself through gmeow:linkNext, as the Cascade prose states. linkNext is deliberately NOT transitive (it names the immediate next link, not every downstream one), so the native coherence gate enforces this with an internal reachability walk that raises a violation on any cycle, never by materialising the closure; the generated SHACL constraint surface is its projection."
msgstr "在规范载体上断言 gmeow:linkNext 是无环的：一次因果级联行走绝不经由 gmeow:linkNext 到达自身，正如 Cascade 散文所述。linkNext 有意并非传递（它命名紧邻的下一个链接，而非每一个下游链接），故原生一致性门以一次内部可达性行走来强制此点，对任何环抛出违反，绝不物化闭包；所生成的 SHACL 约束面是其投影。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/loadBearing|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Types an annotation as load-bearing (true) or droppable (false, the default). A droppable annotation — a display hint or scope note — must never carry correctness: dropping it only pessimizes a result, so a lowering may drop it silently. A load-bearing annotation — an in-band complement or a quantitative axis — is needed by the inverse leg for put after get to equal the identity, so a lowering must either preserve it or record its loss in the ledger. Without this bit a section / retraction (perfect-subsumption) claim cannot be verified, which is why it is part of the node from the start."
msgstr "把一个注解定类型为承载性（true）或可弃性（false，默认值）。一个可弃注解——一个显示提示或一条范围注记——绝不可承载正确性：弃之只会使结果变悲观，故一次降型可静默弃之。一个承载性注解——一个带内补足项或一个定量轴——为逆分段所需，以使 get 之后的 put 等于恒等，故一次降型要么保持它、要么把其损失记入账本。若无此位，一个截面/收回（完美包摄）主张便无法核验，这正是它从一开始就是节点之一部分的缘由。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/loadBearing|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A witness needed to reconstruct a richer source is logic:loadBearing true, while a display hint is false."
msgstr "重建更丰富来源所需的见证物其 logic:loadBearing 为 true，而显示提示则为 false。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/lockAcquired|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Records that the action a transaction step performs ACQUIRES an exclusive lock on a situation — a recorded event of a two-phase-locking protocol. Declared on the action schema (logic:ActionSchema) a step instantiates, range the locked situation (stated in prose); the native evaluator reads the acquire/release events in each leg's step order to classify the lock discipline. Under logic:StrictTwoPhaseLocking the schedule is well-formed iff each leg is two-phase (no acquire follows any release within the leg); under logic:StrongStrictTwoPhaseLocking, additionally, no lock is released before the leg's final (commit) step. It is a recorded protocol EVENT the classifier reads, kept distinct from logic:lockReleased (its releasing counterpart) and from the situation-validity vocabulary (logic:situationObtains), which is about what holds, not what is locked."
msgstr "记录一个事务步所执行的动作在一个情形上获取了一个排他锁——一个两阶段锁定协议的被记录事件。声明在一个步所实例化的动作模式（logic:ActionSchema）上，值域被锁定的情形（以散文陈述）；原生求值器按每个分段的步序读取获取/释放事件以对锁定纪律分类。在 logic:StrictTwoPhaseLocking 下，当且仅当每个分段皆为两阶段（分段内无任何获取跟在任一释放之后）时调度良构；在 logic:StrongStrictTwoPhaseLocking 下，此外，任何锁都不在分段的最终（提交）步之前被释放。它是一个分类器所读取的被记录协议事件，与 logic:lockReleased（其释放对应物）以及情形有效性词汇（logic:situationObtains，涉及何者成立而非何者被锁）保持区分。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/lockReleased|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Records that the action a transaction step performs RELEASES its exclusive lock on a situation — the releasing counterpart of logic:lockAcquired and a recorded event of a two-phase-locking protocol. Declared on the action schema (logic:ActionSchema) a step instantiates, range the released situation (stated in prose). The native evaluator reads releases in each leg's step order: a release before any remaining acquire breaks the two-phase discipline (logic:StrictTwoPhaseLocking), and a release before the leg's final step breaks the held-to-commit discipline (logic:StrongStrictTwoPhaseLocking). It is a recorded protocol EVENT the classifier reads, never a derived verdict."
msgstr "记录一个事务步所执行的动作在一个情形上释放了其排他锁——logic:lockAcquired 的释放对应物，一个两阶段锁定协议的被记录事件。声明在一个步所实例化的动作模式（logic:ActionSchema）上，值域被释放的情形（以散文陈述）。原生求值器按每个分段的步序读取释放：一个释放先于任何剩余获取即破坏两阶段纪律（logic:StrictTwoPhaseLocking），一个释放先于分段最终步即破坏持有至提交的纪律（logic:StrongStrictTwoPhaseLocking）。它是一个分类器所读取的被记录协议事件，绝非一个派生裁定。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/LogicalFramework|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The closed class of reasoning disciplines the canonical logic: core formalizes — each a self-contained body of constructs, axioms, and operational semantics co-resident in logic:. Its nine named individuals are logic:HolonicFramework, logic:MereologicalFramework, logic:DeonticFramework, logic:TeleologicalFramework, logic:TemporalFramework, logic:ModalFramework, logic:EpistemicFramework, logic:ProbabilisticFramework, and logic:ParaconsistentFramework. A term declares the disciplines it traffics in via logic:instantiatesFramework, and may instantiate several; absence is meaningful — a plain domain term that traffics in no special discipline carries no framework. The value names WHICH reasoning machinery a term belongs to, orthogonal to the logic:ReasoningContract facets, which describe HOW a particular evaluation is configured rather than which discipline a term inhabits. The set is closed, so a misspelt framework names no declared value and is rejected rather than silently accepted, mirroring logic:AgencyVerdict and logic:EmergenceVerdict (design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md, the unified-logic-core section)."
msgstr "规范 logic: 内核所形式化的推理学科封闭类——每一者皆为一个自足的构造、公理与操作语义之体，共驻于 logic:。其九个具名个体为 logic:HolonicFramework、logic:MereologicalFramework、logic:DeonticFramework、logic:TeleologicalFramework、logic:TemporalFramework、logic:ModalFramework、logic:EpistemicFramework、logic:ProbabilisticFramework 与 logic:ParaconsistentFramework。一个词项经 logic:instantiatesFramework 声明其所涉的学科，且可实例化数者；缺席具有意义——一个不涉任何特殊学科的朴素领域词项不承载框架。该值命名一个词项归属于哪套推理机制，与 logic:ReasoningContract 各切面正交，后者描述一次特定求值如何配置、而非一个词项栖居于哪个学科。该集合封闭，故一个拼写有误的框架不命名任何已声明值，会被拒而非静默接受，仿照 logic:AgencyVerdict 与 logic:EmergenceVerdict（design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md，unified-logic-core 一节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/LogicConformanceFailure|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The root of the logic grounding layer's typed conformance-failure lattice: every well-formedness violation the logic: slice detects is an instance of one of its subclasses, so a failure is a first-class queryable object rather than an out-of-band error string. Its five bedrock subclasses cover the flagship acceptance scenarios — an incomplete EL/RL/DL closure, a violated correspondence section obligation, an unentrenched counterfactual, an unwitnessed refutation, and an uncertified chase — plus logic:UnwiredFlagshipScenario for an acceptance scenario that does not bind all its realizing/enforcing artifacts."
msgstr "逻辑接地层的类型化一致性失败格之根：logic: 切片所检出的每一个良构违反都是其某个子类的实例，故一次失败是一个一等的可查询对象，而非一个带外的错误字符串。其五个基石子类涵盖旗舰验收场景——一个不完整的 EL/RL/DL 闭包、一个被违反的对应截面义务、一个未确立的反事实、一次无见证的反驳，以及一次未认证的追逐（chase）——外加 logic:UnwiredFlagshipScenario，用于一个未绑定其全部实现/强制工件的验收场景。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/lossCode|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The stable machine code of a logic:ProjectionLoss — reifier-layer-dropped, annotation-layer-dropped, or standpoint-scope-dropped — naming exactly which structure the projection shed. The codes are shared verbatim with the conversion loss ledger so in-band and contract-level loss declarations agree."
msgstr "一个 logic:ProjectionLoss 的稳定机器码——reifier-layer-dropped、annotation-layer-dropped 或 standpoint-scope-dropped——确切命名投影所舍弃的是哪种结构。这些码与转换损失账本逐字共享，以使带内的与合约级的损失声明彼此一致。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/LossyLens|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A lens with non-injective get: one direction is faithful but the inverse needs a witness, a co-authored put-with-claim, or declared defaults. Most schema.org / FOAF downcasts live here. Caps: a single faithful direction; the put leg may not claim recovery without a logic:mnemomorphic witness."
msgstr "一个 get 非单射的透镜：一个方向忠实，但其逆需要一个见证、一个共同撰写的带主张 put，或所声明的默认值。多数 schema.org / FOAF 降型栖居于此。上限：仅一个忠实方向；put 分段不可在无 logic:mnemomorphic 见证时主张恢复。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/lostReifies|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Points from a logic:ProjectionLoss to the RDF-1.2 triple term whose reifier (and any annotations) the projection dropped, so a consumer can recover which statement lost its reification layer. The object is a quoted triple term; its range is intentionally left open (stated in prose) to keep the OWL down-projection DL-clean."
msgstr "从 logic:ProjectionLoss 指向投影所丢弃其具体化器（及任何注解）的 RDF-1.2 三元组词项，以便消费者能够恢复哪条陈述失去了其具体化层。其对象是被引用的三元组词项；其值域被有意保持开放（以散文形式说明），以使 OWL 下投影保持 DL 洁净。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/lowerPriorityUnderPolicy|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates two gmeow:Goals where, under a governing priority ordering established by an applicable policy, one goal is deprioritised in favour of the other — a conflict resolved by policy precedence rather than by logical, temporal, or deontic impossibility. Domain gmeow:Goal, range gmeow:Goal (stated in prose). One of seven conflict relations between independently-meaningful goals, weaker than gmeow:counterGoal (constitutive opposition). Distinct from logic:deonticallyIncompatible: the conjunction is not normatively impermissible — it is merely ranked lower by the policy ordering; and distinct from logic:competesForResource: the deprioritisation is a priority decision, not an exhaustion of supply."
msgstr "关联两个 gmeow:Goals，其中在适用策略确立的支配性优先级排序下，一个目标为了另一个而被降低优先级——这是一种由策略优先次序而非逻辑、时间或道义不可能性所解决的冲突。定义域 gmeow:Goal，值域 gmeow:Goal（以散文形式说明）。这是独立有意义目标之间七种冲突关系之一，弱于 gmeow:counterGoal（构成性对立）。区别于 logic:deonticallyIncompatible：其合取并非规范上不可容许——它只是被优先级排序排得更低；也区别于 logic:competesForResource：降低优先级是一项优先级决策，而非供给的耗尽。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/MaintenanceGoal|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:GoalExpressionKind for a goal satisfied only while its logic:boundSituationType holds at EVERY state of the interval, violated at the FIRST state it fails; while the bounding window is still open the evaluation is logic:GoalEvaluationUndetermined, not conclusively satisfied. The dual of logic:AvoidanceGoal."
msgstr "logic:GoalExpressionKind，用于仅当其 logic:boundSituationType 在区间的每一个状态都成立时才被满足的目标，在其失败的第一个状态即被违反；只要限界窗口仍然开放，评估结果就是 logic:GoalEvaluationUndetermined，而非确定性地被满足。它是 logic:AvoidanceGoal 的对偶。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/MaterialRelationshipType|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A logic:RelationshipType whose instances are material relations — relations founded on a logic:Relator that mediates the relata (marriage, employment, enrolment). The counterpart of gufo:MaterialRelationshipType; the relation it types holds in virtue of the mediating Relator existing (logic:mediates), so its instances are reducible to the relator and its mediation links. Stated in prose, not as a subclass edge. Contrast logic:ComparativeRelationshipType, which needs no relator."
msgstr "一种 logic:RelationshipType，其实例是物质关系——建立在中介其相关项的 logic:Relator 之上的关系（婚姻、雇佣、注册）。它是 gufo:MaterialRelationshipType 的对应物；它所类型化的关系凭借中介性 Relator 的存在（logic:mediates）而成立，因此其实例可归约为该 relator 及其中介链接。以散文形式说明，而非作为子类边。与 logic:ComparativeRelationshipType 相对照，后者不需要任何 relator。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/maxCardinality|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:primaryContactRestriction logic:maxCardinality 1 ."
msgstr "示例：ex:primaryContactRestriction logic:maxCardinality 1 ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/maxCardinality|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The count ranges over all distinct fillers of the selected property."
msgstr "计数遍及所选属性的全部不同填充项。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/maxInclusiveBound|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The inclusive upper literal bound of a logic:ValueRangeConstraint: every value on the constraint's logic:valuePath must be less than or equal to this literal (projected to sh:maxInclusive on the target class shape). At least one of the two inclusive bounds must be present."
msgstr "logic:ValueRangeConstraint 的包含式字面量上界：约束的 logic:valuePath 上的每个值都必须小于或等于该字面量（投影到目标类形状上的 sh:maxInclusive）。两个包含式界限中至少必须存在一个。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/maxQualifiedCardinality|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:leadRestriction logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass ex:Lead ."
msgstr "示例：ex:leadRestriction logic:maxQualifiedCardinality 1 ; logic:onClass ex:Lead ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/maxQualifiedCardinality|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The upper bound applies only to fillers satisfying the one declared qualifier."
msgstr "上界仅适用于满足所声明的那个限定词的填充项。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/McpActionSchema|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A logic:ActionSchema that grounds an MCP (Model Context Protocol) tool action — the opt-in marker subtype that brings an action schema under the stricter MCP-action governance profile (logic:McpActionPolicyShape). Beyond the facets every action schema carries it must always declare a logic:compensation (rollback) because an MCP tool that mutates external state must be recoverable: the dogfood case where the canonical process model governs the agent's own tool calls. A plain logic:ActionSchema is NOT required to carry compensation; typing it logic:McpActionSchema is the explicit declaration that the governance profile applies."
msgstr "一种为 MCP（Model Context Protocol）工具动作提供接地的 logic:ActionSchema——这是使动作模式纳入更严格的 MCP 动作治理配置（logic:McpActionPolicyShape）的选择性加入标记子类型。除了每个动作模式所携带的各面之外，它必须始终声明一个 logic:compensation（回滚），因为一个改变外部状态的 MCP 工具必须是可恢复的：这正是规范进程模型治理智能体自身工具调用的自食其果案例。一个普通的 logic:ActionSchema 并不被要求携带补偿；将其类型化为 logic:McpActionSchema 就是关于治理配置适用的显式声明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/measuredValue|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The frame-relative magnitude of a measurement: the numeric value a measured quantity takes once expressed in a unit and reference frame — the 37 of 37 °C, the 120 of 120 mmHg. The frame-relative leg of the true-quantity/measured-value seam (Principle 11), paired with logic:referenceFrame: the value is meaningful only together with the frame it is expressed in, so a logic:measuredValue asserted without a logic:referenceFrame is the logic:MeasurementFrameMissing violation. Contrast logic:trueQuantity, the frame-independent magnitude the value measures. The foundation-level seam predicate the domain property gmeow:value grounds onto by sub-property, so a domain measurement lifts into the constraint's scope. The range is intentionally left open (no rdfs:range), matching the module's quantitative-axis convention."
msgstr "测量的相对于参照系的量值：一个被测量在以单位和参照系表达之后所取的数值——37 °C 中的 37，120 mmHg 中的 120。它是真量/测量值接缝（原则 11）中相对于参照系的一支，与 logic:referenceFrame 配对：该值仅在与其所表达的参照系一起时才有意义，因此在没有 logic:referenceFrame 的情况下断言的 logic:measuredValue 即构成 logic:MeasurementFrameMissing 违规。与 logic:trueQuantity 相对照，后者是该值所测量的、与参照系无关的量值。这是基础层接缝谓词，域属性 gmeow:value 通过子属性接地到它，从而使域测量提升进入该约束的范围。其值域被有意保持开放（无 rdfs:range），符合模块的定量轴约定。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/MeasurementFrameMissing|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The frame-completeness axiom as a quality constraint: a value expressed in a unit must not be asserted without the reference frame it is read in — a measurement bearing a logic:unit but no logic:referenceFrame is ill-formed. A bare magnitude is frame-independent (a logic:trueQuantity), but the moment a value is given it is expressed in a unit and frame; a value asserted without its frame is meaningless, not merely under-specified (Principle 11: separate the frame-independent structure from the frame-relative value, and never assert the value without the frame). Because the foundation chase is all-IRI, the rule keys on logic:unit — the IRI-valued witness that a framed value exists — rather than on the literal logic:measuredValue it qualifies. A unit-bearing measurement lacking a frame is the logic:violation, entailed by the foundation lowering rather than asserted by hand."
msgstr "作为质量约束的参照系完整性公理：以单位表达的值不得在缺少其被读取所在的参照系的情况下被断言——携带 logic:unit 但没有 logic:referenceFrame 的测量是格式错误的。裸量值与参照系无关（一个 logic:trueQuantity），但一旦给出某个值，它便是以单位和参照系表达的；缺少其参照系而被断言的值是无意义的，而不仅仅是欠规定（原则 11：将与参照系无关的结构同相对于参照系的值分离，且切勿在没有参照系的情况下断言该值）。由于基础追踪全部为 IRI，该规则以 logic:unit 为键——即证明存在框定值的 IRI 值证据——而非以它所限定的字面量 logic:measuredValue 为键。携带单位却缺失参照系的测量即为 logic:violation，由基础下降蕴含得出，而非手工断言。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/MediatedPropertyRequirementAssertion|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A central record asserting that, on a target class, every value a focus node reaches through a mediating property must itself declare at least one value of a required property — the interval that scopes a situation must carry its temporal frame (Principle 11). It names the class with logic:mediatedRequirementTarget, the mediating property with logic:mediatedRequirementVia, and the demanded property with logic:mediatedRequirementProperty; the native coherence gate joins them to raise a violation when a mediated value lacks the required property. Carries a logic:formalizes back-reference to the domain property whose prose it encodes."
msgstr "一条中心记录，断言在某个目标类上，焦点节点通过中介属性所到达的每个值本身都必须声明某个必需属性的至少一个值——为情形界定范围的区间必须携带其时间参照系（原则 11）。它用 logic:mediatedRequirementTarget 命名该类，用 logic:mediatedRequirementVia 命名中介属性，用 logic:mediatedRequirementProperty 命名所要求的属性；原生一致性门将它们连接起来，以便在某个被中介的值缺少必需属性时引发违规。它携带一个 logic:formalizes 回引用，指向其所编码散文的域属性。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/mediatedRequirementProperty|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:MediatedPropertyRequirementAssertion to the property each mediated value must declare at least once. Domain logic:MediatedPropertyRequirementAssertion; single-valued."
msgstr "将 logic:MediatedPropertyRequirementAssertion 关联到每个被中介的值都至少必须声明一次的属性。定义域 logic:MediatedPropertyRequirementAssertion；单值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/mediatedRequirementTarget|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:MediatedPropertyRequirementAssertion to the class whose focus nodes it constrains. Domain logic:MediatedPropertyRequirementAssertion; single-valued."
msgstr "将 logic:MediatedPropertyRequirementAssertion 关联到其所约束焦点节点的类。定义域 logic:MediatedPropertyRequirementAssertion；单值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/mediatedRequirementVia|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:MediatedPropertyRequirementAssertion to the mediating property whose values must carry the required property. Domain logic:MediatedPropertyRequirementAssertion; single-valued."
msgstr "将 logic:MediatedPropertyRequirementAssertion 关联到其值必须携带必需属性的中介属性。定义域 logic:MediatedPropertyRequirementAssertion；单值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/mediates|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a Relator to a mediation role — the relationship between an objectified relation and each of its relata, on which the Relator existentially depends. A Relator must mediate at least two distinct entities (the relator-mediation discipline, RelComp), reached either through two distinct roles or through a single non-functional role; the material relation the Relator grounds holds in virtue of these mediation links."
msgstr "将 Relator 关联到一个中介角色——即被对象化的关系与其每个相关项之间的关系，Relator 在存在上依赖于它。一个 Relator 必须中介至少两个不同的实体（relator 中介纪律，RelComp），这些实体或通过两个不同角色、或通过单个非功能性角色到达；Relator 所接地的物质关系凭借这些中介链接而成立。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/memberOf|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The member-collection relation: relates a member to a logic:Collection it belongs to, where the members are the relevant units of the whole. Distinct from logic:partOf and logic:properPartOf: collection membership is not mereological parthood — a team member is a member of, not a proper part of, the team, and membership does not inherit parthood's transitivity through the collection."
msgstr "成员-集合关系：将成员关联到它所属的 logic:Collection，其中成员是整体的相关单元。区别于 logic:partOf 和 logic:properPartOf：集合成员资格不是部分学意义上的部分关系——一名队员是球队的成员，而非球队的真部分，且成员资格不会通过集合继承部分关系的传递性。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/MereologicalFramework|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The part-whole framework: strict parthood (logic:properPartOf, a transitive, asymmetric, irreflexive order), overlap and disjointness, and weak supplementation scoped to a declared logic:MereologyProfile rather than imposed universally. Parthood is profiled, not universal — supplementation is true of functional complexes and quantities but false of singleton collectives and in-progress assemblies (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "部分-整体框架：严格部分关系（logic:properPartOf，一个传递、反对称、非自反的序）、重叠与不相交，以及被界定到一个已声明的 logic:MereologyProfile 而非普遍强加的弱补充。部分关系是被配置的、而非普遍的——补充对功能性复合体和量成立，但对单元素集合体和进行中的装配不成立（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons 一节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/MereologyConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A named profiled-mereology axiom a whole can violate — the family of mereological well-formedness constraints (weak supplementation and its kin) that hold only within a declared logic:MereologyProfile. Distinct from logic:Discipline, the closed set of OntoUML structural anti-patterns: mereology constraints are scoped to a profile, not asserted foundation-wide. Its named individuals are the labels a logic:violation fact may point at; the set is closed so a misspelt label names no declared constraint and is rejected rather than silently accepted."
msgstr "一条整体可以违反的、具名的配置化部分学公理——部分学良构约束族（弱补充及其同类），它们仅在已声明的 logic:MereologyProfile 之内成立。区别于 logic:Discipline，即 OntoUML 结构反模式的封闭集合：部分学约束被界定到某个配置，而非在整个基础范围内断言。它的具名个体是 logic:violation 事实可以指向的标签；该集合是封闭的，因此拼写错误的标签不命名任何已声明的约束，会被拒绝而非被无声接受。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/MereologyProfile|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A declared scope within which the strong mereological axioms — weak supplementation above all — are taken to hold. Parthood is profiled, not universal: weak supplementation is true of functional complexes and quantities but false of many legitimate wholes (singleton-membered collectives, abstract aggregates, in-progress assemblies), so logic: scopes it to the MereologyProfile a whole is declared under (via logic:underMereologyProfile) rather than asserting it across all logic:properPartOf. A whole outside any profile is never charged with a logic:WeakSupplementation violation (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "一个被声明的范围，强部分学公理——首先是弱补充——在其内被视为成立。部分关系是被配置的、而非普遍的：弱补充对功能性复合体和量成立，但对许多合法整体（单成员集合体、抽象聚合、进行中的装配）不成立，因此 logic: 将其界定到某个整体所声明所属的 MereologyProfile（经由 logic:underMereologyProfile），而非在所有 logic:properPartOf 上断言它。任何配置之外的整体永远不会被指控 logic:WeakSupplementation 违规（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons 一节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/message|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The advisory human-readable message a logic:Constraint violation attaches (projected to sh:message). Presentation-only and load-bearing-false: it carries no identity, so two constraints differing only in their message are the same constraint. Absent means no message."
msgstr "logic:Constraint 违规所附加的、供参考的人类可读消息（投影到 sh:message）。仅用于呈现且不承载：它不携带任何标识，因此仅在消息上不同的两个约束是同一个约束。缺席意味着没有消息。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/MetaLevelFormula|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A formula about formulas: a statement that quotes or ranges over other propositions, distinct from the propositions it mentions. Kept apart from the object level so a meta-level quotation cannot collapse into the object-level assertion it quotes; any holds or truth predicate over it is stratified so the IR cannot encode a self-referential paradox by accident."
msgstr "关于公式的公式：一个引用其他命题或在其上取值的陈述，区别于它所提及的命题。与对象层分隔开来，使得元层引用不能坍缩成它所引用的对象层断言；作用于它之上的任何成立谓词或真值谓词都是分层的，从而使中间表示不会偶然编码自指悖论。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/minCardinality|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:teamRestriction logic:minCardinality 1 ."
msgstr "示例：ex:teamRestriction logic:minCardinality 1 ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/minCardinality|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The count ranges over all distinct fillers of the selected property."
msgstr "计数遍及所选属性的全部不同填充项。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/minInclusiveBound|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The inclusive lower literal bound of a logic:ValueRangeConstraint: every value on the constraint's logic:valuePath must be greater than or equal to this literal (projected to sh:minInclusive on the target class shape). At least one of the two inclusive bounds must be present."
msgstr "logic:ValueRangeConstraint 的包含式字面量下界：约束的 logic:valuePath 上的每个值都必须大于或等于该字面量（投影到目标类形状上的 sh:minInclusive）。两个包含式界限中至少必须存在一个。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/minQualifiedCardinality|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:committeeRestriction logic:minQualifiedCardinality 2 ; logic:onClass ex:Member ."
msgstr "示例：ex:committeeRestriction logic:minQualifiedCardinality 2 ; logic:onClass ex:Member ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/minQualifiedCardinality|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The lower bound applies only to fillers satisfying the one declared qualifier."
msgstr "下界仅适用于满足所声明的那个限定词的填充项。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/MixIden|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The OntoUML MixIden anti-pattern: a sortal inherits its principle of identity from exactly one Kind. A Kind specializing another Kind, or a non-Kind sortal tracing to zero or to two-or-more Kinds, violates it. The lowering of reasoning_lint.identity_overlap."
msgstr "OntoUML MixIden 反模式：一个 sortal 恰好从一个 Kind 继承其身份原则。一个特化另一个 Kind 的 Kind，或者一个追溯到零个或两个及以上 Kind 的非 Kind sortal，都会违反它。它是 reasoning_lint.identity_overlap 的下降。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Mixin|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A semi-rigid non-sortal that classifies instances of several Kinds, applying rigidly to some instances and anti-rigidly to others: a dispersive type whose rigidity is mixed across its extension. Identity-dispersive like a Category, but semi-rigid rather than uniformly rigid."
msgstr "一种半刚性非 sortal，它对多个 Kind 的实例进行分类，对某些实例刚性地适用、对另一些反刚性地适用：一种其刚性在其外延上混杂的分散型类型。像 Category 一样在身份上分散，但半刚性而非一致刚性。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/MixRig|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The OntoUML MixRig anti-pattern: a rigid sortal (Kind or SubKind) must never specialize an anti-rigid type (Phase, Role, PhaseMixin, RoleMixin, Mixin), because a rigid type cannot inherit contingent instantiation. A rigid sortal with an anti-rigid-type ancestor violates it. The other half of the lowering of reasoning_lint.anti_rigidity_discipline."
msgstr "OntoUML MixRig 反模式：一个刚性 sortal（Kind 或 SubKind）绝不可特化一个反刚性类型（Phase、Role、PhaseMixin、RoleMixin、Mixin），因为刚性类型不能继承偶然实例化。一个具有反刚性类型祖先的刚性 sortal 会违反它。它是 reasoning_lint.anti_rigidity_discipline 下降的另一半。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/mnemomorphic|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Whether a logic:Correspondence's forward get leg retains a source witness — factoring through the graph of the correspondence so that put is obtained by projecting along the retained witness rather than synthesizing a plausible source. The bit is orthogonal to the logic:MorphismClass rung but is what lets a correspondence climb it: a retained witness is what discharges put ∘ get = id (the logic:SectionLaw), the dividing line between recoverable subsumption and reconstructed approximation. True or false (default false); a false value bars any section / retraction claim. Range xsd:boolean (domain left open, like logic:loadBearing)."
msgstr "表示某个 logic:Correspondence 的前向 get 支是否保留了一个源证据——通过对应的图进行分解，从而使 put 是沿着所保留的证据投影得到的，而非合成一个貌似合理的源。该位与 logic:MorphismClass 阶梯正交，但正是它让一个对应能够攀升该阶梯：保留的证据正是履行 put ∘ get = id（logic:SectionLaw）的东西，是可恢复的包含与重构的近似之间的分界线。真或假（默认为假）；假值禁止任何截面/收缩主张。值域 xsd:boolean（定义域保持开放，如同 logic:loadBearing）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ModalFramework|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The alethic-modality and rigidity framework: logic:World / logic:PossibleWorld with typed accessibility, and the modal notion of rigidity (logic:rigidlyAppliesTo, lowering to the constraint that a rigid type held in one world of an individual's existence is held in all). Kripke semantics realized over GMEOW's contextual index — the modal distinctions full UFO needs and OWL cannot hold (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the criticism-ledger section; design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md, the operational-semantics-modality-and-identity-supply section)."
msgstr "真势模态与刚性框架：带类型化可达性的 logic:World / logic:PossibleWorld，以及刚性的模态概念（logic:rigidlyAppliesTo，下降为如下约束：在某个体存在的一个世界中成立的刚性类型在所有世界中都成立）。在 GMEOW 的语境索引之上实现的 Kripke 语义——完整 UFO 所需要而 OWL 无法承载的模态区分（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，criticism-ledger 一节；design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md，operational-semantics-modality-and-identity-supply 一节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ModelSemantics|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The facet value class of the model-semantics facet: which models of a program are selected as authoritative. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract. Its individuals are classical entailment, the least model, the well-founded model, and the stable models — the choice that settles which entailments hold over a rule program."
msgstr "模型语义面的面值类：一个程序的哪些模型被选为权威。在 ReasoningContract 上单值。它的个体是经典蕴含、最小模型、良基模型和稳定模型——这一选择决定了在一个规则程序上哪些蕴含成立。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/modelSemantics|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to the logic:ModelSemantics it selects — which models are authoritative. Single-valued on the contract. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:ModelSemantics (stated in prose, matching the module's convention). Probabilistic reasoning is never a value here — graded belief is carried on logic:uncertaintyMeasure alongside whatever model semantics is in force."
msgstr "将 logic:ReasoningContract 关联到它所选择的 logic:ModelSemantics——哪些模型是权威的。在合约上单值。定义域 logic:ReasoningContract，值域 logic:ModelSemantics（以散文形式说明，符合模块约定）。概率推理在此处永远不是一个值——分级信念由 logic:uncertaintyMeasure 携带，与当前生效的任何模型语义并列。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Mode|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "An aspect that is NOT directly measurable in a quality space — a belief, a skill, an intention, a symptom — whether intrinsic to a single bearer or relational across several. The counterpart of gufo:IntrinsicMode and gufo:ExtrinsicMode generalized: a logic:Aspect lacking a quality value (stated in prose, not as a subclass edge). Contrast logic:Quality, which is measurable."
msgstr "一个在质量空间中不可直接测量的方面——一个信念、一项技能、一个意图、一个症状——无论它是内在于单个承载者的，还是跨若干承载者关系性的。它是 gufo:IntrinsicMode 与 gufo:ExtrinsicMode 的推广对应物：一个缺少质量值的 logic:Aspect（以散文形式说明，而非作为子类边）。与 logic:Quality 相对照，后者是可测量的。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ModuleContextAxis|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The module index axis of the multi-dimensional context facet: a statement is relative to the logic:Module (Common Logic theory) it is asserted in. A theory-structuring axis that coexists with the world, standpoint, time, and path axes and indexes the same result simultaneously — orthogonal to them, never an alternative value of the world or standpoint slot. Its per-statement carrier is logic:inModule; module-to-module importation is logic:imports."
msgstr "多维语境面的模块索引轴：一个陈述相对于它被断言所在的 logic:Module（Common Logic 理论）。这是一个理论结构化轴，它与世界、立场、时间和路径轴共存，并同时索引同一结果——与它们正交，绝不是世界槽或立场槽的替代值。它的逐陈述载体是 logic:inModule；模块到模块的导入是 logic:imports。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ModuleContextAxis|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "One result can be indexed simultaneously by ex:geometry as its module and ex:analystView as its standpoint."
msgstr "同一个结果可以同时以 ex:geometry 作为其模块、以 ex:analystView 作为其立场进行索引。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Module|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A named Common Logic module — a body of sentences grouped as a reusable theory, with its own local vocabulary and importation. The theory-structuring context of a statement, ORTHOGONAL to the epistemic logic:World / gmeow:Standpoint dimension: a module says WHERE a sentence lives (which theory), never UNDER WHOSE perspective it holds, so a module must never be conflated with a world or a standpoint — that conflation is exactly the category error the context algebra forbids. Per-statement membership is carried by logic:inModule and module-to-module importation by logic:imports; the top-level (unnamed) module is the absence of any logic:inModule. It is the construct the ingested and emitted Common Logic dialects (CLIF, CGIF, XCL) map their (module …) and (cl-imports …) forms onto."
msgstr "一个具名的 Common Logic 模块——一组作为可复用理论分组的语句，拥有自己的局部词汇和导入。它是一个陈述的理论结构化语境，与认知性的 logic:World / gmeow:Standpoint 维度正交：一个模块说的是一条语句存在于何处（哪个理论），绝不说它在谁的视角下成立，因此一个模块绝不可与一个世界或一个立场相混同——这种混同正是语境代数所禁止的范畴错误。逐陈述的成员资格由 logic:inModule 携带，模块到模块的导入由 logic:imports 携带；顶层（无名）模块即任何 logic:inModule 的缺席。它是被摄入和被发出的 Common Logic 方言（CLIF、CGIF、XCL）将其 (module …) 与 (cl-imports …) 形式映射到的构造。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Module|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A Common Logic theory named ex:geometry can import ex:orders while remaining in the same epistemic world."
msgstr "名为 ex:geometry 的 Common Logic 理论可以导入 ex:orders，同时仍处于同一个认知世界中。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/MonotonicRevision|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The revision-policy value under which new information only adds conclusions and never retracts them: there is nothing to revise because no conclusion is ever defeated. The degenerate revision policy of monotonic reasoning (the positive-Horn preset), contrasted with logic:EntrenchmentRevision and logic:TruthMaintenanceRevision, which absorb defeating information."
msgstr "修订策略值，在其下新信息只添加结论而绝不撤回它们：没有什么需要修订，因为没有任何结论会被击败。这是单调推理的退化修订策略（正 Horn 预设），与 logic:EntrenchmentRevision 和 logic:TruthMaintenanceRevision 相对照，后两者吸收击败性信息。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/MorphismClass|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The ordered law-spine of a logic:Correspondence: how much invertibility it may lawfully claim, where each rung caps the laws the correspondence may assert. From strongest to floor the seven rungs are logic:Isomorphism, logic:SectionRetraction, logic:WellBehavedLens, logic:LossyLens, logic:Prism, logic:AffineCorrespondence and logic:BridgeView. The spine fuses the profunctor-optic lattice with the categorical subobject notion; composition can only weaken the rung, never strengthen it, and a logic:mnemomorphic witness is what lets a correspondence climb it. The set is closed, so a misspelt class names no declared rung and is rejected (design/LOGIC-CORRESPONDENCE.md, the ordered-law-spine section)."
msgstr "一个 logic:Correspondence 的有序法则脊柱：它可以合法地主张多少可逆性，其中每一阶梯为该对应可以断言的法则设定上限。从最强到底层，七个阶梯是 logic:Isomorphism、logic:SectionRetraction、logic:WellBehavedLens、logic:LossyLens、logic:Prism、logic:AffineCorrespondence 和 logic:BridgeView。该脊柱将 profunctor 光学格与范畴论子对象概念融合；复合只能削弱阶梯，绝不能加强它，而一个 logic:mnemomorphic 证据正是让一个对应攀升它的东西。该集合是封闭的，因此拼写错误的类不命名任何已声明的阶梯，会被拒绝（design/LOGIC-CORRESPONDENCE.md，ordered-law-spine 一节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/morphismClass|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Correspondence to its rung on the ordered law-spine (logic:MorphismClass), which caps the logic:CorrespondenceLaw values it may claim. Composition can only weaken this rung. Range logic:MorphismClass (domain stated in prose)."
msgstr "将一个 logic:Correspondence 关联到它在有序法则脊柱（logic:MorphismClass）上的阶梯，该阶梯为它可以主张的 logic:CorrespondenceLaw 值设定上限。复合只能削弱这一阶梯。值域 logic:MorphismClass（定义域以散文形式说明）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/MorphismKind|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The closed two-value qualifier, orthogonal to the logic:MorphismClass rung, recording the institution-theoretic split between a satisfaction-preserving morphism (logic:InstitutionMorphism) and a commitment-shifting bridge (logic:CommitmentShiftingBridge). This is the distinction the foundation already draws between a truth-preserving down-projection and a by-reference bridge; the loss ledger refuses owl:equivalentClass for the bridge kind. The set is closed, so a misspelt kind names no declared value and is rejected (design/LOGIC-CORRESPONDENCE.md, the ordered-law-spine section)."
msgstr "封闭的二值限定符，与 logic:MorphismClass 阶梯正交，记录了保持满足性的态射（logic:InstitutionMorphism）与转移承诺的桥（logic:CommitmentShiftingBridge）之间的机构理论式分野。这正是基础在保持真值的下投影与按引用的桥之间已经划出的区分；损失账本对桥类型拒绝 owl:equivalentClass。该集合是封闭的，因此拼写错误的类型不命名任何已声明的值，会被拒绝（design/LOGIC-CORRESPONDENCE.md，ordered-law-spine 一节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/morphismKind|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Correspondence to its logic:MorphismKind — the satisfaction-preserving / commitment-shifting split orthogonal to the rung. A logic:CommitmentShiftingBridge value makes the loss ledger refuse owl:equivalentClass. Range logic:MorphismKind (domain stated in prose)."
msgstr "将一个 logic:Correspondence 关联到它的 logic:MorphismKind——与阶梯正交的保持满足性/转移承诺分野。一个 logic:CommitmentShiftingBridge 值会使损失账本拒绝 owl:equivalentClass。值域 logic:MorphismKind（定义域以散文形式说明）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/multiplyPositioned|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The derived marker that an entity occupies two or more distinct logic:HolonicPositions — the structural signature of a DAG node sitting on multiple paths through a holarchy, the ground on which a non-trivial path-relative depth band (logic:holonicLevelMin .. logic:holonicLevelMax) exists. It is the positive companion to logic:HolonicLevelIncoherence: where the incoherence violation fires for a profiled holon that occupies NO position, this marker certifies that a holon occupies SEVERAL, so its level is genuinely path-relative rather than single-valued. Never asserted by hand; it is entailed by the foundation lowering by negation-of-equality over the position set (two distinct positionEntity reifiers for the same entity), all-IRI and without any numeric comparison. It grounds only the band's existence, not its endpoint values, which the logic:StratifiedNAFProfile chase cannot compute (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "派生标记，表示一个实体占据两个或更多不同的 logic:HolonicPositions——一个 DAG 节点坐落于穿过全子层级的多条路径上的结构特征，是非平凡的相对于路径的深度带（logic:holonicLevelMin .. logic:holonicLevelMax）得以存在的根基。它是 logic:HolonicLevelIncoherence 的正向伴随物：不一致违规针对占据零个位置的被配置全子而触发，而这个标记则证明某个全子占据了若干个位置，因此其层级是真正相对于路径的、而非单值的。它绝不手工断言；它由基础下降通过对位置集合的相等性否定（同一实体的两个不同的 positionEntity 具体化器）蕴含得出，全部为 IRI 且不含任何数值比较。它只为该带的存在提供接地，而非其端点值，后者是 logic:StratifiedNAFProfile 追踪无法计算的（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons 一节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/MultiversionConcurrencyControl|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol under which each transaction reads from a consistent version snapshot taken at its start and writes new versions independently, so readers never block writers. Its strongest enforced guarantee is logic:SnapshotIsolation — it still admits WRITE SKEW and so does NOT enforce logic:SerializableIsolation, which is exactly why declaring it under a serializable-or-stronger level is inadequate. This engine realizes snapshot isolation by construction, so a multiversion run needs no lock or timestamp events. A mechanism, not a guarantee."
msgstr "logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol，在其下每个事务从其开始时所取的一致版本快照中读取，并独立地写入新版本，从而使读者永不阻塞写者。它所强制的最强保证是 logic:SnapshotIsolation——它仍然允许 WRITE SKEW，因此并不强制 logic:SerializableIsolation，这正是为何将其声明在可串行化或更强的级别之下是不充分的原因。此引擎在构造上实现快照隔离，因此一次多版本运行不需要任何锁或时间戳事件。它是一种机制，而非一种保证。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/namesContradictionWitness|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:RefutationAcceptanceWitness to the concrete logic:ContradictionWitness (an IRI) its refutation rests on — the individual forced to owl:Nothing and the jointly-inconsistent premises. Domain logic:RefutationAcceptanceWitness (stated in prose). A refutation naming no witness is an unreplayable assertion, not a proof."
msgstr "将一个 logic:RefutationAcceptanceWitness 关联到其反驳所依据的具体 logic:ContradictionWitness（一个 IRI）——被强制为 owl:Nothing 的个体以及联合不一致的前提。定义域 logic:RefutationAcceptanceWitness（以散文形式说明）。不命名任何证据的反驳是一个不可重放的断言，而非一个证明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/naryArg0|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a reifier node to the term in argument position 0 of the n-ary tuple it reifies. The flat-binary positional predicate the evaluable lowering emits for the first argument of a fixed-arity n-ary atom Rel(a₀,…): logic:naryArg0(R, a₀) beside logic:instanceOf(R, Rel). Directly evaluable in the binary relational core; the zero-based position is fixed in the predicate itself so no separate index carrier is needed. It is not a logic:argument AST-carrier edge."
msgstr "将一个具体化器节点关联到它所具体化的 n 元元组中位于参数位置 0 的词项。这是可求值下降为固定元数 n 元原子 Rel(a₀,…) 的第一个参数所发出的扁平二元位置谓词：logic:naryArg0(R, a₀)，与 logic:instanceOf(R, Rel) 并列。它在二元关系核心中直接可求值；从零开始的位置固定在谓词本身之中，因此不需要单独的索引载体。它不是一条 logic:argument 抽象语法树载体边。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/naryArg0|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The lowering of ex:between(a,b,c) links its tuple reifier to a through logic:naryArg0."
msgstr "ex:between(a,b,c) 的降级通过 logic:naryArg0 将其元组具体化物连接到 a。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/naryArg1|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a reifier node to the term in argument position 1 of the n-ary tuple it reifies. The flat-binary positional predicate the evaluable lowering emits for the second argument of a fixed-arity n-ary atom; companion to logic:naryArg0. Directly evaluable in the binary relational core. It is not the first position and is not a logic:argument AST-carrier edge."
msgstr "将一个具体化器节点关联到它所具体化的 n 元元组中位于参数位置 1 的词项。这是可求值下降为固定元数 n 元原子的第二个参数所发出的扁平二元位置谓词；是 logic:naryArg0 的伴随物。它在二元关系核心中直接可求值。它不是第一个位置，也不是一条 logic:argument 抽象语法树载体边。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/naryArg1|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The lowering of ex:between(a,b,c) links its tuple reifier to b through logic:naryArg1."
msgstr "ex:between(a,b,c) 的降级通过 logic:naryArg1 将其元组具体化物连接到 b。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/naryArg2|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a reifier node to the term in argument position 2 of the n-ary tuple it reifies. The flat-binary positional predicate the evaluable lowering emits for the third argument of a fixed-arity n-ary atom; companion to logic:naryArg0 and logic:naryArg1. Directly evaluable in the binary relational core. The enumerated positional predicates run 0 … N for the maximum fixed arity in play (ternary here); a higher arity extends the closed set with the next positional predicate. It is not emitted for a binary atom and is not a logic:argument AST-carrier edge."
msgstr "将一个具体化器节点关联到它所具体化的 n 元元组中位于参数位置 2 的词项。这是可求值下降为固定元数 n 元原子的第三个参数所发出的扁平二元位置谓词；是 logic:naryArg0 和 logic:naryArg1 的伴随物。它在二元关系核心中直接可求值。枚举的位置谓词从 0 到 N 覆盖当前在用的最大固定元数（此处为三元）；更高的元数以下一个位置谓词扩展该封闭集合。它不会为二元原子发出，也不是一条 logic:argument 抽象语法树载体边。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/naryArg2|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The lowering of ex:between(a,b,c) links its tuple reifier to c through logic:naryArg2."
msgstr "ex:between(a,b,c) 的降级通过 logic:naryArg2 将其元组具体化物连接到 c。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/necessaryFor|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a sub-gmeow:Goal that must be satisfied for a gmeow:Goal to be satisfied. Domain gmeow:Goal, range gmeow:Goal (stated in prose). The relation an logic:AndDecomposition groups: all necessary sub-goals must hold together. One of the four decomposition relations carrying satisfaction dependency, typed apart from gmeow:properPartOf (structural part-hood) — the satisfaction dependency planning needs that part-hood alone does not express."
msgstr "关联一个为使某个 gmeow:Goal 得以满足而必须被满足的子 gmeow:Goal。定义域 gmeow:Goal，值域 gmeow:Goal（以散文形式说明）。这是 logic:AndDecomposition 所分组的关系：所有必需的子目标必须一同成立。它是承载满足依赖的四种分解关系之一，与 gmeow:properPartOf（结构性部分关系）分开类型化——这是规划所需要、而单凭部分关系无法表达的满足依赖。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/negatedBody|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment"
msgid "Negation-as-failure body atom of a logic:Rule. Default-absent: a positive Horn rule has only logic:body atoms and no logic:negatedBody, so the existing positive corpus is unaffected."
msgstr "logic:Rule 的失败即否定体部原子。默认缺省：正的 Horn 规则仅有 logic:body 原子而无 logic:negatedBody，因此现有的正语料库不受影响。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/negatedBody|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Rule to a negated (negation-as-failure) body atom: the antecedent literal that must NOT be derivable for the rule to fire. Parallel to logic:body (the positive antecedent atoms) but read under closed-world negation, so a rule with any logic:negatedBody atom requires at least logic:StratifiedNAFProfile rather than logic:PositiveHornProfile. The atom itself is a reified rdf:subject/rdf:predicate/rdf:object triple exactly as for logic:body; only its polarity differs."
msgstr "将一条 logic:Rule 关联到一个被否定的（否定即失败）体原子：为使规则触发而必须不可推导的前件文字。它与 logic:body（正前件原子）平行，但在封闭世界否定下被读取，因此含有任何 logic:negatedBody 原子的规则至少需要 logic:StratifiedNAFProfile，而非 logic:PositiveHornProfile。该原子本身是一个被具体化的 rdf:subject/rdf:predicate/rdf:object 三元组，与 logic:body 完全一致；仅其极性不同。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/negationOperator|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to a logic:NegationOperator its programs may use. Set-valued on the contract: a program may legitimately use explicit (strong) negation and negation-as-failure together, so this records the permitted operator set, not a single chosen operator. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:NegationOperator (stated in prose, matching the module's convention)."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ReasoningContract 关联到其程序可以使用的一个 logic:NegationOperator。在合约上取集合值：一个程序可以合法地同时使用显式（强）否定和否定即失败，因此这里记录的是被允许的算子集合，而非单个被选定的算子。定义域 logic:ReasoningContract，值域 logic:NegationOperator（以散文形式说明，符合模块约定）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Nested|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The residue shape tag for a formula that is a connective or quantifier tree rather than a flat predication — it carries logical structure (logic:and, logic:or, logic:not, an implication, logic:iff, or a quantifier) that the flat body of a Horn rule cannot hold. Disclosed when a Horn-fragment target carries such a formula as flagged unsupported residue."
msgstr "残余形状标签，用于一个是连接词或量词树而非扁平谓述的公式——它携带 Horn 规则的扁平体所不能容纳的逻辑结构（logic:and、logic:or、logic:not、一个蕴涵、logic:iff 或一个量词）。当一个 Horn 片段目标携带这样一个公式作为被标记的不受支持残余时，它被披露。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/nextActionSchema|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a policy to the logic:ActionSchema its selected branch invokes — the next action chosen from what an observation revealed. Domain a policy, range logic:ActionSchema (stated in prose). Surfaced by the native evaluator alongside logic:selectedBranch so a policy reading is possible from the materialized output."
msgstr "将一个策略关联到其被选定分支所调用的 logic:ActionSchema——从某次观察所揭示的内容中选出的下一个动作。定义域为一个策略，值域 logic:ActionSchema（以散文形式说明）。由原生求值器与 logic:selectedBranch 一并浮现，以便能够从物化输出中进行策略解读。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/NoArgumentation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The argumentation-facet value selecting no argumentation layer: conflicts are not resolved by an argumentation semantics. The default for contracts whose conflict resolution is handled by the model semantics or revision policy alone, contrasted with the grounded, preferred, and policy-specific argumentation values."
msgstr "选择无论证层的论证面值：冲突不由某种论证语义来解决。这是那些其冲突解决仅由模型语义或修订策略处理的合约的默认值，与有基础的、优先的以及特定于策略的论证值相对照。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/NodeKind|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The typed-sum tag every node of the canonical logic: IR declares. The IR is a typed sum, not an untyped triple bag: each node names its kind, and the kind governs what may be done with it — keeping a constraint distinct from a derivation rule, a query operator from a program operator, and a meta-level quotation from the object-level assertion it quotes. Its individuals are the object-level formula, the meta-level formula, the constraint, the derivation rule, the query, the transaction program, the action schema, the validation shape, the law-bearing correspondence, and the lifted RDFS/SKOS annotation."
msgstr "规范 logic: 中间表示的每个节点所声明的类型化和标签。该中间表示是一个类型化和，而非无类型的三元组袋：每个节点命名其种类，而种类支配可以对它做什么——使一个约束区别于一条推导规则、一个查询算子区别于一个程序算子、一个元层引用区别于它所引用的对象层断言。它的个体是对象层公式、元层公式、约束、推导规则、查询、事务程序、动作模式、验证形状、承载法则的对应，以及被提升的 RDFS/SKOS 注解。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/nondeterministicOutcome|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ActionSchema to one of its alternative effects, each reified as a logic:Outcome node naming via logic:outcomeSituation the distinct successor situation it reaches — multi-valued, so an action whose result is not fixed is represented faithfully rather than collapsed to a single effect. The outcome set this enumerates is why plan success must be quantified (logic:planSuccessMode) and why compensation is outcome-indexed: each logic:Outcome branch carries its own logic:compensation. Domain logic:ActionSchema, range logic:Outcome (stated in prose). One of the eight action-theory facets."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ActionSchema 关联到它的一种备选效果，每种效果都被具体化为一个 logic:Outcome 节点，经由 logic:outcomeSituation 命名它所到达的不同后继情形——多值，因此一个结果不固定的动作被忠实地表示，而非坍缩为单一效果。这里所枚举的结果集合正是计划成功必须被量化（logic:planSuccessMode）以及补偿按结果索引的原因：每个 logic:Outcome 分支携带自己的 logic:compensation。定义域 logic:ActionSchema，值域 logic:Outcome（以散文形式说明）。它是八个动作理论面之一。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/NonEntailmentObligation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A first-class, executable record of a conclusion the foundation must NEVER draw: a deliberate non-assertion the engine is held to, not a comment the axioms happen to respect. It names the forbidden predicate (logic:obligationForbiddenPredicate), the logic:DischargeCondition under which absence-of-proof is conclusively checkable, and the logic:DischargeVerdict the check returns. Because the canonical logic is semi-decidable, an obligation is conclusively discharged only within a stated fragment or bound; outside it the verdict is logic:ObligationUnknown, carried forward, never 'proved absent'. The two standing obligations are 'intent must not be derived from structural deception' and 'counterpart must not become transitive' (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, §Typed formalization governance)."
msgstr "一条关于基础绝不可得出的结论的一等、可执行记录：这是引擎被约束遵守的一项蓄意的非断言，而非公理碰巧遵守的一条注释。它命名被禁止的谓词（logic:obligationForbiddenPredicate）、在其下证明之缺席可被确定性检查的 logic:DischargeCondition，以及该检查返回的 logic:DischargeVerdict。由于规范逻辑是半可判定的，一项义务只有在某个明示的片段或界限之内才被确定性地履行；在其之外，裁决为 logic:ObligationUnknown，被向前携带，绝不是「已证明缺席」。两项常设义务是「意图不得从结构性欺骗中推导得出」以及「对应物不得变为传递的」（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，§Typed formalization governance）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/NonRigidType|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A logic:Type that is not rigid: either anti-rigid (logic:AntiRigidType) or semi-rigid (logic:SemiRigidType). The counterpart of gufo:NonRigidType; the meta-type that is the union complement of logic:RigidType over the sorts — its instances are logic:Phase, logic:Role, logic:RoleMixin, logic:PhaseMixin (anti-rigid) and logic:Mixin (semi-rigid). Stated in prose, not as a subclass edge. The negation of logic:RigidType, used where a discipline only needs 'not necessarily applying' rather than the stronger 'contingent for every instance'."
msgstr "一个非刚性的 logic:Type：要么反刚性（logic:AntiRigidType），要么半刚性（logic:SemiRigidType）。它是 gufo:NonRigidType 的对应物；是在各分类上 logic:RigidType 的并集补的元类型——它的实例是 logic:Phase、logic:Role、logic:RoleMixin、logic:PhaseMixin（反刚性）以及 logic:Mixin（半刚性）。以散文形式说明，而非作为子类边。它是 logic:RigidType 的否定，用于某纪律只需要「不必然适用」、而非更强的「对每个实例都偶然」之处。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/NonSortal|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A logic:Type that aggregates instances of several different logic:Sortals and supplies NO principle of identity of its own — it spans Kinds dispersively. The counterpart of gufo:NonSortal; the meta-type whose instances are the dispersive sorts: logic:Category, logic:Mixin, logic:RoleMixin, logic:PhaseMixin. Stated in prose, not as a subclass edge. Identity-dispersive (logic:suppliesIdentity holds for none of its instances); contrast logic:Sortal."
msgstr "一个 logic:Type，它聚合多个不同 logic:Sortals 的实例，并且不提供自己的任何身份原则——它分散地横跨各 Kind。它是 gufo:NonSortal 的对应物；是其实例为分散型分类的元类型：logic:Category、logic:Mixin、logic:RoleMixin、logic:PhaseMixin。以散文形式说明，而非作为子类边。在身份上分散（logic:suppliesIdentity 对它的任何实例都不成立）；与 logic:Sortal 相对照。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/NotificationWaitSchema|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A logic:ActionSchema whose completion the engine learns of ONLY by being externally told: it does not fire until a logic:ExternalSignal it logic:awaitsSignal obtains in the state — a manual-notification or callback-driven completion, the prescriptive-descriptive epistemic boundary where what the engine knows of the real world is limited to what it is informed of. The opt-in marker subtype that brings an action schema under the wait-well-formedness profile (logic:NotificationWaitShape, which requires a logic:awaitsSignal). At the action gate a wait whose signal has not obtained is neither admitted nor denied but logic:GateUndetermined, carrying a logic:awaitingSignal witness — the wait is pending (the engine has not been told), a judgment withheld rather than a failure; in a plan a wait step blocks the path until the signal is received."
msgstr "一个 logic:ActionSchema，引擎仅通过被外部告知才得知其完成：它在其 logic:awaitsSignal 的某个 logic:ExternalSignal 于状态中实现之前不会触发——一种手动通知或回调驱动的完成，是规定性-描述性的认知边界，在其中引擎对真实世界的所知仅限于它被告知的内容。这是使一个动作模式纳入等待良构配置（logic:NotificationWaitShape，它要求一个 logic:awaitsSignal）的选择性加入标记子类型。在动作门处，一个信号尚未实现的等待既不被准入也不被拒绝，而是 logic:GateUndetermined，携带一个 logic:awaitingSignal 证据——该等待处于挂起状态（引擎尚未被告知），是一个被搁置的判断而非一次失败；在计划中，一个等待步骤会阻塞路径，直到信号被接收。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/not|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a strong-negation logic:Formula to its single negated sub-formula. This is explicit (classical) negation and is kept distinct from negation-as-failure, which is a body-literal flag on a derivation rule (logic:negatedBody): the two are never conflated."
msgstr "将一个强否定 logic:Formula 关联到它唯一的被否定子公式。这是显式（经典）否定，与否定即失败保持区分，后者是推导规则上的一个体文字标志（logic:negatedBody）：二者从不混同。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/not|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A formula node with logic:not ex:licensed represents the strong negation of the ex:licensed formula."
msgstr "带有 logic:not ex:licensed 的公式节点表示 ex:licensed 公式的强否定。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/NoUncertainty|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The uncertainty-measure value carrying no graded belief: reasoning is categorical. The default of the uncertainty set facet (the empty selection), contrasted with logic:ProbabilisticMeasure, logic:WeightedRankingMeasure, and logic:FuzzyMeasure, any combination of which may be in force at once."
msgstr "不携带任何分级信念的不确定性度量值：推理是断然的。它是不确定性集合面的默认值（空选择），与 logic:ProbabilisticMeasure、logic:WeightedRankingMeasure 和 logic:FuzzyMeasure 相对照，这些中的任意组合都可以同时生效。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/objectiveDirection|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates an optimization-goal logic:GoalEvaluation to the direction and unit/frame against which its logic:objectiveValue is read — whether the measure is to be maximized or minimized, and in what units the value is stated. Domain logic:GoalEvaluation (stated in prose); the range is left open so the direction/unit-frame may be carried as a structured value. The companion of logic:objectiveValue: a value without its direction and frame is uninterpretable."
msgstr "将一个优化目标的 logic:GoalEvaluation 关联到读取其 logic:objectiveValue 所依据的方向和单位/参照系——即该度量是要被最大化还是被最小化，以及该值以何种单位陈述。定义域 logic:GoalEvaluation（以散文形式说明）；值域被保持开放，以便方向/单位参照系可以作为结构化值携带。它是 logic:objectiveValue 的伴随物：一个缺少其方向和参照系的值是不可解释的。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/objectiveValue|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The measured quantity an optimization goal extremizes, carried on a logic:GoalEvaluation. Domain logic:GoalEvaluation (stated in prose). The range is intentionally left open (no rdfs:range), matching the module's quantitative axes; its direction and unit/frame are carried by logic:objectiveDirection. NEVER folded into a truth value and never into an uncertainty measure — DISTINCT from logic:confidence, logic:probability, logic:weight, logic:evidenceStrength, from logic:satisfactionDegree, and from logic:utility. A probability over outcomes is never the objective value being optimized."
msgstr "一个优化目标所极值化的被测量量，携带在一个 logic:GoalEvaluation 上。定义域 logic:GoalEvaluation（以散文形式说明）。值域被有意保持开放（无 rdfs:range），符合模块的定量轴；其方向和单位/参照系由 logic:objectiveDirection 携带。绝不折叠为真值，也绝不折叠为不确定性度量——区别于 logic:confidence、logic:probability、logic:weight、logic:evidenceStrength，区别于 logic:satisfactionDegree，也区别于 logic:utility。对各结果的概率绝不是正在被优化的目标值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ObjectLevelFormula|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "An ordinary first-order formula over the domain of discourse: the object-level node kind. Its quantifiers range over individuals in the domain, some of which may be reified predicates or types, so the object level stays first-order even where it expresses what reads as quantification over predicates or types."
msgstr "一个在论域之上的普通一阶公式：对象层节点种类。它的量词在论域中的个体上取值，其中某些可能是被具体化的谓词或类型，因此对象层即使在表达读起来像是对谓词或类型的量化之处也保持一阶。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Object|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A substantial endurant that bears its own principle of identity and does not inhere in another individual — a person, an organization, a physical artefact. The counterpart of gufo:Object: an independent endurant, contrasted with the aspects that existentially depend on it. Every Object is a logic:Substantial and a logic:Endurant (stated in prose, not as a subclass edge)."
msgstr "一个实体性延续体，它承载自己的身份原则且不寓于另一个体之中——一个人、一个组织、一件物理制品。它是 gufo:Object 的对应物：一个独立的延续体，与那些在存在上依赖于它的方面相对照。每一个 Object 都是一个 logic:Substantial 和一个 logic:Endurant（以散文形式说明，而非作为子类边）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/obligationDischargeCondition|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:NonEntailmentObligation to the logic:DischargeCondition under which its absence-of-proof is conclusively checkable. An obligation declaring a condition the engine does not wire (anything other than logic:DischargeSyntacticReachability or logic:DischargeFiniteClosure) is a hard error, never a silent pass. Domain logic:NonEntailmentObligation, range logic:DischargeCondition."
msgstr "将一个 logic:NonEntailmentObligation 关联到在其下其证明之缺席可被确定性检查的 logic:DischargeCondition。一项声明了引擎未接线条件（除 logic:DischargeSyntacticReachability 或 logic:DischargeFiniteClosure 之外的任何条件）的义务是一个硬错误，绝不是一次无声通过。定义域 logic:NonEntailmentObligation，值域 logic:DischargeCondition。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ObligationDischarged|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The discharge verdict for an obligation conclusively checked within its declared logic:DischargeCondition: the forbidden conclusion is provably not drawn within the stated fragment or bound. Wire value `discharged`."
msgstr "在其声明的 logic:DischargeCondition 内被确定性核查后得出的义务解除裁决：可证明在所指定的片段或界限内不会推出被禁止的结论。线值 `discharged`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/obligationDischargeVerdict|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:NonEntailmentObligation to the logic:DischargeVerdict the check returned — logic:ObligationDischarged, logic:ObligationUnknown or logic:ObligationViolated. Computed by the engine, not asserted by hand. Domain logic:NonEntailmentObligation, range logic:DischargeVerdict."
msgstr "将 logic:NonEntailmentObligation 关联到核查所返回的 logic:DischargeVerdict —— logic:ObligationDischarged、logic:ObligationUnknown 或 logic:ObligationViolated。由引擎计算得出，并非手工断言。定义域 logic:NonEntailmentObligation，值域 logic:DischargeVerdict。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/obligationForbiddenPredicate|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The IRI of the predicate a logic:NonEntailmentObligation forbids the closure from ever containing (and forbids any rule head from producing). The check reads this IRI, then either proves it unreachable over the rule strata (logic:DischargeSyntacticReachability) or absent from the materialized closure (logic:DischargeFiniteClosure). Single-valued, xsd:anyURI. Domain logic:NonEntailmentObligation."
msgstr "logic:NonEntailmentObligation 禁止闭包永远包含（并禁止任何规则头产生）的谓词的 IRI。核查读取此 IRI，随后或者证明其在规则分层上不可达（logic:DischargeSyntacticReachability），或者证明其不出现在已物化的闭包中（logic:DischargeFiniteClosure）。单值，xsd:anyURI。定义域 logic:NonEntailmentObligation。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ObligationUnknown|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The discharge verdict outside any wired discharge condition: not 'proved absent' but not-yet-discharged, carried forward to the next evaluation cycle or stronger fragment. The honest verdict the semi-decidable canonical logic demands. Wire value `unknown`."
msgstr "处于任何已接线解除条件之外的解除裁决：并非『已证明缺席』，而是尚未解除，被结转至下一个求值周期或更强的片段。半可判定的规范逻辑所要求的诚实裁决。线值 `unknown`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ObligationViolated|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The discharge verdict when the forbidden predicate IS reachable or present in the closure: the obligation is broken and the check is a hard error. Wire value `violated`."
msgstr "当被禁止的谓词在闭包中确实可达或存在时的解除裁决：该义务被破坏，核查为硬错误。线值 `violated`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/observation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ActionSchema to what executing the action reveals — the seam to the cognitive layer (design/LOGIC-COGNITION.md). A plan whose next action is chosen from what an earlier action's observation reveals is a policy. Domain logic:ActionSchema (stated in prose). One of the eight action-theory facets; a NEW facet, not a reuse of any cognition term."
msgstr "将 logic:ActionSchema 关联到执行该动作所揭示的内容 —— 通向认知层的接缝（design/LOGIC-COGNITION.md）。若某计划的下一动作是依据先前动作观察所揭示的内容而选取的，则该计划是一种策略。定义域 logic:ActionSchema（以散文表述）。八个动作理论切面之一；一个全新切面，而非对任何认知词项的复用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/OccurrentBoundaryMismatch|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The boundary-exclusivity axiom as an occurrent constraint: a perdurant must not be both on-going and completed — it must not carry both logic:occurrentBoundary logic:Open and logic:occurrentBoundary logic:Closed. The two halves of the action(open)/event(closed) distinction are mutually exclusive at a single standpoint; an occurrent bearing both is the logic:violation, entailed by the foundation lowering rather than asserted by hand."
msgstr "作为发生物约束的边界互斥公理：一个延续物不得既进行中又已完成 —— 它不得同时携带 logic:occurrentBoundary logic:Open 与 logic:occurrentBoundary logic:Closed。action(open)/event(closed) 区分的两半在单一立场下互斥；同时承载二者的发生物即为 logic:violation，由基础降解蕴含而得，而非手工断言。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/OccurrentBoundary|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The closed class of perdurant boundary values: the two-valued result a perdurant receives via logic:occurrentBoundary. Its named individuals are logic:Open (an on-going action over an open interval — the arriving) and logic:Closed (a completed unitary event over a closed interval — the arrival). The set is closed, so a misspelt value names no declared boundary and is rejected rather than silently accepted, mirroring logic:EmergenceVerdict and logic:ConstraintVerdict. The carrier of the YAMATO/Galton action(open)/event(closed) distinction as a value, not a subclass (Principle 9)."
msgstr "延续物边界值的封闭类：延续物经由 logic:occurrentBoundary 所接收的二值结果。其具名个体为 logic:Open（在开区间上进行中的动作 —— 正在到达）与 logic:Closed（在闭区间上已完成的单一事件 —— 已到达）。该集合封闭，故拼写错误的值命名不到任何已声明的边界，会被拒绝而非被静默接受，与 logic:EmergenceVerdict 及 logic:ConstraintVerdict 相仿。作为一个值而非子类来承载 YAMATO/Galton 的 action(open)/event(closed) 区分的载体（原则 9）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/occurrentBoundary|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a perdurant to its boundary value — logic:Open (an on-going action, an open temporal interval: the arriving) or logic:Closed (a completed unitary event, a closed interval: the arrival). The action(open)/event(closed) typing of the YAMATO/Galton refinement, carried as a VALUE rather than a subclass (Principle 9): the same occurrence is open while it unfolds and closed once whole, so boundedness is an indexed value, not a rigid kind. The formal name for the prescriptive-to-descriptive seam — an open action is the doing, the closed event its done record. An occurrent bearing both logic:Open and logic:Closed is the logic:OccurrentBoundaryMismatch violation."
msgstr "将延续物关联到其边界值 —— logic:Open（进行中的动作，一段开放时间区间：正在到达）或 logic:Closed（已完成的单一事件，一段闭区间：已到达）。这是 YAMATO/Galton 精化的 action(open)/event(closed) 定型，作为一个值而非子类来承载（原则 9）：同一发生在展开之际为开、一旦整全即为闭，故有界性是一个带索引的值，而非刚性的种类。它是规约性到描述性接缝的正式名称 —— 开放的动作是行动本身，闭合的事件是其已完成记录。同时承载 logic:Open 与 logic:Closed 的发生物即为 logic:OccurrentBoundaryMismatch 违规。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/OccurrentChangeAsymmetry|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The change-asymmetry axiom as an occurrent constraint: a completed unitary occurrent (logic:occurrentBoundary logic:Closed) must not vary — it must bear no time-varying logic:Fluent. Processes and on-going actions may change; an event, once whole, cannot (the YAMATO/Galton process-not-equal-event refinement, restoring the UFO-B four-dimensional account). A Closed occurrent that bears a logic:Fluent is the logic:violation, entailed by the foundation lowering rather than asserted by hand."
msgstr "作为发生物约束的变化不对称公理：一个已完成的单一发生物（logic:occurrentBoundary logic:Closed）不得变化 —— 它不得承载任何随时间变化的 logic:Fluent。过程与进行中的动作可以变化；而事件一旦整全便不能（YAMATO/Galton 的过程不等于事件精化，恢复了 UFO-B 的四维论述）。承载 logic:Fluent 的 Closed 发生物即为 logic:violation，由基础降解蕴含而得，而非手工断言。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/occurrentConstituent|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a unitary occurrent to a process that constitutes it: the change-stuff an event is made of — a marathon is constituted by the running, a fermentation-event by the fermenting. The constitutive reading of the YAMATO/Galton dictum that events are made of processes: distinct from temporal parthood (logic:temporalPartOf) and from causal parthood (logic:causalPartOf), and carries NO parthood-subsumption rule, so an event's constituting process is not thereby asserted a temporal part of it — constitution, not parthood. The bridge from the unitary, completed logic:Event to the dissective logic:Process whose unfolding it bounds."
msgstr "将单一发生物关联到构成它的过程：事件由之构成的变化材料 —— 马拉松由奔跑构成，发酵事件由发酵过程构成。这是 YAMATO/Galton『事件由过程构成』格言的构成性解读：区别于时间部分关系（logic:temporalPartOf）与因果部分关系（logic:causalPartOf），且不携带任何部分—包含规则，故一个事件的构成过程并不因此被断言为它的时间部分 —— 是构成，而非部分关系。从单一、已完成的 logic:Event 通向其展开为之界定的可分割 logic:Process 的桥梁。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/OccurrentConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A named occurrent well-formedness axiom a perdurant can violate — the family of constraints governing the process/event change-asymmetry and the action(open)/event(closed) boundary. Distinct from logic:Discipline (the closed set of OntoUML structural anti-patterns) and from logic:MereologyConstraint (profiled-mereology axioms): occurrent constraints govern the four-dimensional semantics of perdurants. Its named individuals are the labels a logic:violation fact may point at; the set is closed so a misspelt label names no declared constraint and is rejected rather than silently accepted."
msgstr "一个延续物可违反的具名发生物良构公理 —— 治理过程/事件变化不对称以及 action(open)/event(closed) 边界的约束族。区别于 logic:Discipline（OntoUML 结构反模式的封闭集）与 logic:MereologyConstraint（配置化的部分学公理）：发生物约束治理延续物的四维语义。其具名个体是 logic:violation 事实可指向的标签；该集合封闭，故拼写错误的标签命名不到任何已声明的约束，会被拒绝而非被静默接受。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/onClass|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The class parameter of a canonical logic: construct. On compact constraint sugar it names the focus class whose instances the expanded logic:Constraint ranges over (rdf:type(this, C) becomes the range-restricting universal guard); on a qualified logic:Restriction it names the class whose values are counted. The latter use lowers to owl:onClass."
msgstr "规范 logic: 构件的类参数。在紧凑约束语法糖上，它命名焦点类，展开后的 logic:Constraint 遍历该类的实例（rdf:type(this, C) 成为限定值域的全称守卫）；在带限定的 logic:Restriction 上，它命名其值被计数的类。后一种用法降解为 owl:onClass。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/onDataRange|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:scoreRestriction logic:onDataRange xsd:decimal ."
msgstr "示例：ex:scoreRestriction logic:onDataRange xsd:decimal ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/onDataRange|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This qualifier selects datatype-valued fillers counted by a qualified cardinality predicate."
msgstr "此限定词选择由带限定基数谓词计数的、取数据类型值的填充项。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/onDatatype|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:adultAge logic:onDatatype xsd:integer ."
msgstr "示例：ex:adultAge logic:onDatatype xsd:integer ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/onDatatype|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The base datatype supplies the lexical and value space before facet restrictions narrow it."
msgstr "基础数据类型提供词法空间与值空间，之后由面限制将其收窄。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/oneOf|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:binaryState logic:oneOf ( ex:on ex:off ) ."
msgstr "示例：ex:binaryState logic:oneOf ( ex:on ex:off ) ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/oneOf|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The RDF list is closed and exhaustive for the enumeration's extension."
msgstr "对于枚举的外延而言，该 RDF 列表是封闭且穷尽的。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/onProperty|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:memberRestriction logic:onProperty ex:member ."
msgstr "示例：ex:memberRestriction logic:onProperty ex:member ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/onProperty|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Each restriction selects one property before stating its value or cardinality condition."
msgstr "每条限制先选定一个属性，然后陈述其值或基数条件。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/OpacityIsolation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:IsolationLevel guarantee under which even aborted or in-flight transactions never observe an inconsistent state — the strongest level, STRICTLY STRONGER than serializability (logic:SerializableIsolation), which constrains only committed transactions. Engine note: under the committed-only, snapshot-isolation execution model of the native evaluator, no aborted or in-flight transactions arise; opacity's additional constraints are therefore vacuously satisfied, and the isolation-adequacy verdict for logic:OpacityIsolation coincides with that of logic:SerializableIsolation by construction — both are met exactly when the witnessed schedule is conflict-serializable."
msgstr "一种 logic:IsolationLevel 保证，在其之下即使被中止或飞行中的事务也绝不观察到不一致状态 —— 最强级别，严格强于可串行化（logic:SerializableIsolation），后者仅约束已提交的事务。引擎注记：在原生求值器仅提交、快照隔离的执行模型下，不会出现被中止或飞行中的事务；因此不透明性的额外约束被空洞地满足，logic:OpacityIsolation 的隔离充分性裁决在构造上与 logic:SerializableIsolation 的裁决一致 —— 二者恰在被证见的调度可冲突串行化时同时得到满足。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Open|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The occurrent-boundary value for an on-going action: a perdurant unfolding over an open temporal interval, not yet a completed whole — the arriving, the running, the prescribed-but-unexecuted plan. The action half of the YAMATO/Galton action(open)/event(closed) distinction; an occurrent that varies (bears a logic:Fluent) is properly Open, since only the unfinished can still change. Contrast logic:Closed."
msgstr "进行中动作的发生物边界值：一个在开放时间区间上展开、尚未成为已完成整体的延续物 —— 正在到达、正在奔跑、已规约但未执行的计划。YAMATO/Galton 的 action(open)/event(closed) 区分中的动作那一半；发生变化（承载 logic:Fluent）的发生物恰为 Open，因为惟有未完成者仍能变化。与 logic:Closed 相对照。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/OpenWorldClosure|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The open-world value of the closure map: for the predicate or context key it is bound to, absence of a fact means unknown rather than false. The default for any key not explicitly closed; the closure facet is a map, so this value is read per key, with logic:ClosedWorldClosure applied only inside a logic:WorldBoundary."
msgstr "闭包映射的开放世界值：对于它所绑定的谓词或上下文键，某事实的缺席意味着未知而非假。任何未被显式闭合之键的默认值；闭包切面是一个映射，故此值按键读取，logic:ClosedWorldClosure 仅在 logic:WorldBoundary 内部适用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/operand|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a compositional logic:GoalExpression (conjunctive, disjunctive, conditional, or deadline-window) to one of its sub-expressions — multi-valued, so a conjunction or disjunction over several sub-goals is carried faithfully. Domain logic:GoalExpression, range logic:GoalExpression (stated in prose). For a conjunctive goal every operand must be satisfied; for a disjunctive goal any one suffices; a conditional or deadline-window goal carries its single guarded/windowed target as its operand."
msgstr "将一个组合式 logic:GoalExpression（合取、析取、条件式或截止窗口式）关联到它的一个子表达式 —— 多值，故对若干子目标的合取或析取被忠实承载。定义域 logic:GoalExpression，值域 logic:GoalExpression（以散文表述）。对合取目标，各操作数皆需被满足；对析取目标，任一即足；条件式或截止窗口式目标以其单一受守卫/受窗口约束的目标作为其操作数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/OptimisticValidation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol that lets transactions run without locking and validates for conflicts at commit time, aborting and retrying on a detected conflict. A mechanism, not a guarantee."
msgstr "一种 logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol，让事务在不加锁的情况下运行，并在提交时校验冲突，检测到冲突则中止并重试。一种机制，而非一项保证。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/OptimizationGoal|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:GoalExpressionKind for a goal directed at a logic:objectiveValue read in a logic:objectiveDirection, satisfied to the DEGREE the measure is extremized (carried as logic:satisfactionDegree) rather than by a crisp boundary. Its outcome is recorded as a degree, never folded into a crisp truth value."
msgstr "针对某个 logic:objectiveValue（按 logic:objectiveDirection 读取）的目标的 logic:GoalExpressionKind，其满足取决于该度量被极值化的程度（承载为 logic:satisfactionDegree），而非取决于一个明确边界。其结果被记录为一个程度，绝不折叠为一个明确真值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/OrDecomposition|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The decomposition of a gmeow:Goal under which any one sufficient sub-goal settles the parent on its own — a disjunctive node of the and-or goal graph means–end search runs over. It groups the logic:sufficientFor sub-goals of the parent: satisfying any one settles it. The co-equal counterpart of logic:AndDecomposition (all necessary sub-goals must hold together); the two compose into the and-or goal graph. Like all decomposition it carries satisfaction dependency and is typed apart from the generic mereology spine, which carries only structural part-hood."
msgstr "gmeow:Goal 的一种分解，在其下任一充分子目标即可独自决定父目标 —— 手段—目的搜索所遍历的与或目标图中的一个析取节点。它归组父目标的 logic:sufficientFor 子目标：满足任一即决定它。logic:AndDecomposition（所有必要子目标须共同成立）的对等对应物；二者合成为与或目标图。如同一切分解，它携带满足依赖，并与仅携带结构部分关系的一般部分学主干分型开来。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/orderedType|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a type to its order (level) in the multi-level hierarchy: a first-order type is order 1, a type whose instances are first-order types is order 2, and so on. Makes the deep-instantiation level explicit so logic:instanceOf chains can be checked for level coherence (an order-n type instantiates an order-(n+1) type), the well-formedness condition that keeps HiLog multi-level modeling stratified."
msgstr "将一个类型关联到它在多层级层次结构中的阶（级别）：一阶类型的阶为 1，其实例为一阶类型的类型阶为 2，依此类推。它使深度实例化级别显式化，从而可对 logic:instanceOf 链核查级别一致性（一个 n 阶类型实例化一个 n+1 阶类型），此即使 HiLog 多层建模保持分层的良构条件。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/or|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a disjunction logic:Formula to each of its operand sub-formulae (multi-valued, two or more). Disjunction is commutative and associative, so the canonical identity flattens nested disjunctions and is insensitive to operand order. It is not a program-choice operator and does not select one branch for execution."
msgstr "将一个析取 logic:Formula 关联到它的每个操作数子公式（多值，两个或更多）。析取满足交换律与结合律，故规范恒等式会展平嵌套的析取并对操作数顺序不敏感。它不是程序选择算子，也不为执行选取某一分支。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/or|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A covering formula can link ex:Cat(x), ex:Dog(x), and ex:Bird(x) through three logic:or edges."
msgstr "一个覆盖公式可以通过三条 logic:or 边连接 ex:Cat(x)、ex:Dog(x) 和 ex:Bird(x)。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/outcomeAssignment|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:JointOutcome to a correlated logic:probability fact (the reified base triple) that is TRUE in this outcome. Correlated facts of the model that are not named by any logic:outcomeAssignment of an outcome are false in that outcome — the assignment is read as the positive set, the complement against the model's logic:correlates support. The range is intentionally left open (no rdfs:range), for the same reason as logic:correlates: its object is a reified logic:probability statement, which carries no dedicated class in this standalone module."
msgstr "将一个 logic:JointOutcome 关联到在此结果中为真的、相关的 logic:probability 事实（具体化的基础三元组）。模型中未被某结果的任何 logic:outcomeAssignment 命名的相关事实在该结果中为假 —— 该赋值被读作正集，即相对于模型 logic:correlates 支撑的补集。值域被有意留空（无 rdfs:range），原因与 logic:correlates 相同：其对象是一个具体化的 logic:probability 陈述句，在此独立模块中不携带专属类。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/outcomeOfProgram|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:TransactionOutcome to the transaction program whose execution it records — a transaction-program combinator node (logic:SerialConjunction, logic:Choice, logic:Fallback, or logic:Iteration). Domain logic:TransactionOutcome, range a transaction-program node (stated in prose). It ties the verdict back to the program that produced it without conflating the outcome (a run record) with the program (the structure that was run)."
msgstr "将一个 logic:TransactionOutcome 关联到其执行被它记录的事务程序 —— 一个事务程序组合子节点（logic:SerialConjunction、logic:Choice、logic:Fallback 或 logic:Iteration）。定义域 logic:TransactionOutcome，值域一个事务程序节点（以散文表述）。它把裁决绑回产生它的程序，同时不将结果（一次运行记录）与程序（被运行的结构）混同起来。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/outcomeSituation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Outcome (one branch of an action schema's nondeterministic outcome set) to the successor logic:Situation it reaches. Domain logic:Outcome, range logic:Situation (stated in prose). The branch's own logic:compensation recovers from this specific successor, so recovery is outcome-indexed rather than a single generic undo."
msgstr "将一个 logic:Outcome（某动作模式非确定性结果集的一个分支）关联到它所到达的后继 logic:Situation。定义域 logic:Outcome，值域 logic:Situation（以散文表述）。该分支自身的 logic:compensation 从此特定后继中恢复，故恢复按结果索引，而非单一的通用撤销。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Outcome|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "One branch of the nondeterministic outcome set of a logic:ActionSchema: a single alternative result, naming via logic:outcomeSituation the successor situation it reaches and via the reused logic:compensation the action that recovers from THIS branch specifically. Reifying each branch as an Outcome is what lets compensation be outcome-indexed rather than a single generic undo across the schema, and what lets plan-success quantification (logic:planSuccessMode) range over the branches. A logic:ActionSchema points at its branches through logic:nondeterministicOutcome."
msgstr "logic:ActionSchema 非确定性结果集的一个分支：单一的备选结果，经由 logic:outcomeSituation 命名它所到达的后继情境，并经由被复用的 logic:compensation 命名专门从此分支恢复的动作。将每个分支具体化为一个 Outcome，正是使补偿按结果索引而非在整个模式上单一通用撤销之所以可能的原因，也是使计划成功量化（logic:planSuccessMode）得以遍历各分支的原因。logic:ActionSchema 经由 logic:nondeterministicOutcome 指向其各分支。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Overlaps|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Source and view share instances without either subsuming the other: a partial, caveated alignment. Lowers to sssom:closeMatch (an OWL equivalence is unsupported and the overclaim gate refuses one). Below the directional band, above logic:RelatedMatch. Distinct from the mereological relation logic:overlaps (shared parts of one whole); this is a relation between two aligned patterns."
msgstr "源与视图共享实例而彼此均不包含对方：一种部分的、附带保留条件的对齐。降解为 sssom:closeMatch（OWL 等价不受支持，越权门也会拒绝之）。位于有向带之下、logic:RelatedMatch 之上。区别于部分学关系 logic:overlaps（同一整体的共享部分）；此为两个已对齐模式之间的关系。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/overlaps|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Mereological overlap: two entities share a common part. The primitive sharing notion that must be settled before disjointness or weak supplementation can be stated — logic:disjoint is its negation, and logic:WeakSupplementation is never applied where overlap is undefined. It is derived from logic:properPartOf: entities that share a proper part overlap, and a proper part overlaps its whole. Symmetric in intent (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "部分学重叠：两个实体共享一个公共部分。这是在可陈述不相交性或弱补充之前必须先确定的原初共享概念 —— logic:disjoint 是它的否定，而 logic:WeakSupplementation 绝不在重叠未定义处应用。它由 logic:properPartOf 导出：共享一个真部分的实体重叠，且一个真部分与其整体重叠。在意图上对称（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，分型化且带上下文的部分学与全体子一节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/overridesIrreflexivity|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Asserts on the canonical carrier that gmeow:overrides is irreflexive: a norm never overrides itself, as its skos:definition states. The native coherence gate reads this to raise a violation for a norm asserted to override itself; the generated SHACL constraint surface is its projection."
msgstr "在规范载体上断言 gmeow:overrides 是非自反的：如其 skos:definition 所述，一条规范绝不覆盖自身。原生一致性门读取此项，为被断言覆盖自身的规范抛出一个违规；生成的 SHACL 约束表面是其投影。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/OwlProjection|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The projection-target value requesting the answer be rendered to an OWL surface (e.g. an EL or DL profile). One of several output targets a single contract may name at once; like every projection target it is a rendering request and never alters which entailments hold."
msgstr "请求将答案渲染到某个 OWL 表面（例如 EL 或 DL 配置）的投影目标值。单个契约可同时命名的若干输出目标之一；如同各投影目标，它是一次渲染请求，绝不改变哪些蕴含成立。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ParaconsistentFramework|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The multi-valued-truth framework: the logic:BelnapBilattice (true, false, both/glut, neither/gap), the admissible-valuation policy (logic:AdmissibleValuationPolicy — the gap/glut choice distinguishing FDE, LP, K3, classical) and designated-value set carried on a logic:TruthAlgebra, and context-indexed entailment so a contradiction is localized to the contexts that disagree, witnessed explicitly, and reasoned around rather than exploding the model (design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md, the unified-logic-core section; design/LOGIC-CONTRACT.md, the truth-values-admissible-valuations-and-the-designated-value-policy section)."
msgstr "多值真理框架：logic:BelnapBilattice（真、假、二者兼有/过剩、二者皆非/空缺）、可接纳赋值策略（logic:AdmissibleValuationPolicy——区分 FDE、LP、K3、经典逻辑的空缺/过剩选择）以及承载于 logic:TruthAlgebra 上的指定值集，还有按上下文索引的蕴含，从而使矛盾被局部化到相互抵触的上下文、被显式证见、并被绕过推理，而非使模型爆炸（design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md，unified-logic-core 一节；design/LOGIC-CONTRACT.md，真值、可接纳赋值与指定值策略 一节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PartiallySatisfied|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:SatisfactionStatus value for a goal met in part, its extent carried as a logic:satisfactionDegree quantity. Held apart from a low logic:confidence in a logic:Satisfied evaluation: partial satisfaction is how much of the goal is achieved, never how sure the evaluator is. Contrast logic:Unsatisfied (no positive progress) and logic:Violated (a target has failed)."
msgstr "部分被满足之目标的 logic:SatisfactionStatus 值，其程度承载为一个 logic:satisfactionDegree 数量。它与 logic:Satisfied 评估中的低 logic:confidence 区分开来：部分满足是指目标被达成了多少，绝非评估者有多确定。与 logic:Unsatisfied（无正向进展）及 logic:Violated（某目标已失败）相对照。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Participation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The reified involvement of an endurant in a perdurant — an actor's participation in an event, a reactant's participation in a reaction. The counterpart of gufo:Participation: a relator-like reified link binding a logic:Endurant to the logic:Perdurant it takes part in, so the role and temporal scope of the involvement can be carried on the participation itself."
msgstr "端续物在延续物中被具体化的卷入 —— 一个行动者对一个事件的参与，一个反应物对一个反应的参与。gufo:Participation 的对应物：一个类关系子的具体化链接，将一个 logic:Endurant 绑定到它所参与的 logic:Perdurant，从而卷入的角色与时间范围可承载于参与本身之上。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/partOf|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The general (reflexive) parthood relation: relates an entity to a whole it is part of, where every entity is trivially part of itself. The mereological base relation over which logic:properPartOf is the strict (irreflexive) restriction. Distinct from logic:memberOf, which relates a member to a collection without the part being a part of the whole in the mereological sense."
msgstr "一般（自反）部分关系：将一个实体关联到它作为部分所属的整体，其中各实体平凡地是其自身的部分。logic:properPartOf 作为其严格（非自反）限制所依据的部分学基础关系。区别于 logic:memberOf，后者将成员关联到集合，而该部分并非部分学意义上整体的部分。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/partOfTransitivity|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Asserts on the canonical carrier that gmeow:partOf is transitive: the universal part-to-whole spine its skos:definition names as transitive and intentionally broad. The native coherence gate reads this to close the parthood spine."
msgstr "在规范载体上断言 gmeow:partOf 是可传递的：其 skos:definition 命名为可传递且有意宽泛的普遍部分—整体主干。原生一致性门读取此项以闭合该部分关系主干。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PathContextAxis|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The path index axis of the multi-dimensional context facet: a truth is relative to a transaction or execution path. One of several context axes that coexist on a single result — world, standpoint, time, and path index the same result simultaneously rather than being alternative values of one slot."
msgstr "多维上下文切面的路径索引轴：一个真值相对于某个事务或执行路径而言。并存于单一结果上的若干上下文轴之一 —— 世界、立场、时间与路径同时对同一结果进行索引，而非同一槽位的备选值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/pathDepthArg|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The concrete depth bound supplied at a logic:PathInvocation for the named depth parameter of the invoked logic:PathShape (its logic:pathDepthParam): the value of ?maxDepth in :name(?maxDepth := 2). Bounds the traversal to at most this many hops for this invocation without altering the shape itself."
msgstr "在 logic:PathInvocation 处为被调用的 logic:PathShape 的具名深度参数（其 logic:pathDepthParam）所提供的具体深度界限：:name(?maxDepth := 2) 中 ?maxDepth 的值。它将本次调用的遍历界定为至多这么多跳，而不改变形状本身。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/pathDepthParam|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The name of the depth parameter a logic:PathShape exposes for parametric invocation — 'maxDepth' in :nearbyOrgs(?maxDepth := 2). A logic:PathInvocation binds this parameter with logic:pathDepthArg. Default-absent: a shape with a fixed depth and no exposed parameter carries no logic:pathDepthParam and is invoked without an argument."
msgstr "logic:PathShape 为参数化调用所暴露的深度参数之名 —— :nearbyOrgs(?maxDepth := 2) 中的 'maxDepth'。logic:PathInvocation 以 logic:pathDepthArg 绑定此参数。默认缺席：具有固定深度且不暴露参数的形状不携带 logic:pathDepthParam，调用时不带实参。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PathInvocation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A by-name application of a logic:PathShape with concrete depth arguments — the canonical, reified form of a parametric call such as :nearbyOrgs(?maxDepth := 2). It carries logic:invokesPathShape (the shape applied) and logic:pathDepthArg (the value bound to the shape's logic:pathDepthParam), so a named, reusable traversal is instantiated at a specific bound without rewriting the shape. The surface syntax :name(?param := value) is a rendering of this individual, not a separate construct (Principle 17)."
msgstr "logic:PathShape 的一次按名应用，带有具体的深度实参 —— 诸如 :nearbyOrgs(?maxDepth := 2) 这类参数化调用的规范、具体化形式。它携带 logic:invokesPathShape（被应用的形状）与 logic:pathDepthArg（绑定到形状 logic:pathDepthParam 的值），从而一个具名、可复用的遍历在特定界限处被实例化，而无需重写形状。表层语法 :name(?param := value) 是此个体的一种渲染，而非独立构件（原则 17）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/pathMaxDepth|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The inclusive upper bound on the traversal length of a logic:PathShape — the n in a bounded {min,n} path. Default-absent: a shape with no logic:pathMaxDepth is unbounded (the SPARQL-+ / transitive-closure reading), traversing arbitrarily many hops. When present it makes the path a bounded {1,n} traversal, which SPARQL 1.1 §9 cannot express directly."
msgstr "logic:PathShape 遍历长度的含端上界 —— 有界 {min,n} 路径中的 n。默认缺席：无 logic:pathMaxDepth 的形状是无界的（SPARQL-+ / 传递闭包解读），遍历任意多跳。存在时它使路径成为一个有界 {1,n} 遍历，而这是 SPARQL 1.1 §9 无法直接表达的。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/pathMinDepth|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The inclusive lower bound on the traversal length of a logic:PathShape — the min in a bounded {min,max} path. Default-absent: a shape with no logic:pathMinDepth starts at one hop (min = 1). Must not exceed logic:pathMaxDepth when both are present; a minimum above the maximum is a malformed shape and is rejected by the frontend, not silently repaired."
msgstr "logic:PathShape 遍历长度的含端下界 —— 有界 {min,max} 路径中的 min。默认缺席：无 logic:pathMinDepth 的形状从一跳起（min = 1）。二者皆存在时不得超过 logic:pathMaxDepth；下限高于上限是一个畸形形状，会被前端拒绝，而非被静默修复。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/pathNamespaceScope|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A predicate-namespace IRI prefix that scopes a wildcard step of a logic:PathShape: when logic:pathWildcard is true, only predicates whose IRI begins with this namespace are traversed. Bounds the fan-out of an otherwise any-predicate walk to a single vocabulary. Default-absent on a wildcard shape: the wildcard matches predicates in any namespace."
msgstr "界定 logic:PathShape 某通配步的谓词命名空间 IRI 前缀：当 logic:pathWildcard 为真时，仅遍历其 IRI 以此命名空间开头的谓词。它把一次否则为任意谓词的游走的扇出界定到单一词汇表。在通配形状上默认缺席：通配匹配任意命名空间中的谓词。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PathShape|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A named, parametric predicate-path traversal specification: a reusable description of how to walk the graph, invocable by name with a depth parameter. A PathShape carries a base step — either a named predicate (logic:pathStepPredicate) or a predicate wildcard (logic:pathWildcard true, optionally scoped by logic:pathNamespaceScope) — together with a bounded depth range (logic:pathMinDepth … logic:pathMaxDepth; an absent maximum means unbounded) and a declared depth parameter name (logic:pathDepthParam) bound at each logic:PathInvocation. It SUBSUMES and EXTENDS SPARQL 1.1 property paths (§9), which are fixed strings with no predicate wildcard, no bounded depth {1,n}, and no named or parameterized reuse: 'all nodes within n hops, by any predicate' becomes a first-class, reusable term. The PathShape is the canonical logic: form; an extended SPARQL property path and a depth-bounded Datalog program are its projections (Principle 17), and the native Datalog least-model fixpoint is its runtime."
msgstr "一个具名、参数化的谓词路径遍历规范：如何游走图的可复用描述，可按名以深度参数调用。PathShape 携带一个基础步 —— 或为具名谓词（logic:pathStepPredicate），或为谓词通配（logic:pathWildcard 为真，可选地由 logic:pathNamespaceScope 界定）—— 连同一个有界深度范围（logic:pathMinDepth … logic:pathMaxDepth；缺席的上界意味无界）以及一个声明的深度参数名（logic:pathDepthParam），后者在每次 logic:PathInvocation 处被绑定。它包容并扩展 SPARQL 1.1 属性路径（§9），后者是固定字符串，无谓词通配、无有界深度 {1,n}、无具名或参数化复用：『n 跳内所有节点，按任意谓词』成为一个头等、可复用的词项。PathShape 是规范的 logic: 形式；一条扩展 SPARQL 属性路径与一个深度有界的 Datalog 程序是其投影（原则 17），而原生 Datalog 最小模型不动点是其运行时。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Path|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "An ordered run of states — a history — over which the typed accessibility relation logic:temporallySucceeds is read; the typed context of the context algebra that carries the Transaction-Logic state sequence, whose edges logic:transitionFromState and logic:transitionToState walk and whose positions are gmeow:State configurations, each realizing a logic:Situation. 'History' is the documented synonym. One of the distinct typed contexts (alongside logic:PossibleWorld, gmeow:EpistemicContext, gmeow:Standpoint, gmeow:Scenario, gmeow:State, gmeow:ReferenceFrame, gmeow:NarrativeReferenceFrame); no inference may cross into it by walking the bare logic:accessibleFrom superproperty, and its relation to states and situations is stated in prose, not as a subclass edge."
msgstr "一段有序的状态运行 —— 一段历史 —— 分型化可达关系 logic:temporallySucceeds 在其上被读取；承载事务逻辑状态序列的上下文代数分型化上下文，其边 logic:transitionFromState 与 logic:transitionToState 在其中游走，其位置为 gmeow:State 配置，各自实现一个 logic:Situation。『历史』是有据可查的同义词。诸个不同分型化上下文之一（与 logic:PossibleWorld、gmeow:EpistemicContext、gmeow:Standpoint、gmeow:Scenario、gmeow:State、gmeow:ReferenceFrame、gmeow:NarrativeReferenceFrame 并列）；任何推理不得经由游走裸的 logic:accessibleFrom 超属性而越入其中，且它与状态和情境的关系以散文表述，而非作为子类边。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/pathStepPredicate|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The named predicate that each hop of a logic:PathShape traverses. Present on a named-predicate path; absent on a wildcard path (where logic:pathWildcard is true instead). A shape that carries BOTH a logic:pathStepPredicate and logic:pathWildcard true is malformed — the base step is a named predicate XOR a wildcard — and is rejected by the frontend rather than silently resolved."
msgstr "logic:PathShape 每一跳所遍历的具名谓词。存在于具名谓词路径上；在通配路径上缺席（此时改为 logic:pathWildcard 为真）。同时携带 logic:pathStepPredicate 与 logic:pathWildcard 为真的形状是畸形的 —— 基础步是具名谓词与通配二者取其一 —— 会被前端拒绝，而非被静默消解。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/pathWildcard|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Marks a logic:PathShape whose step matches ANY predicate rather than one named predicate — the 'any predicate within n hops' traversal that SPARQL 1.1 §9 property paths cannot express. When true the step is unconstrained except by an optional logic:pathNamespaceScope; mutually exclusive with logic:pathStepPredicate. Default-absent (false): the path follows the named logic:pathStepPredicate."
msgstr "标记一个 logic:PathShape，其步匹配任意谓词而非某个具名谓词 —— SPARQL 1.1 §9 属性路径无法表达的『n 跳内任意谓词』遍历。为真时该步除受一个可选的 logic:pathNamespaceScope 约束外不受约束；与 logic:pathStepPredicate 互斥。默认缺席（假）：路径跟随具名的 logic:pathStepPredicate。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Perdurant|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "An occurrent: an individual that unfolds in time by accumulating temporal parts, so that at any single moment only a part of it is present. The four-dimensional counterpart of the endurant; logic:Event and logic:Process are perdurants (every Event is a Perdurant — the supertype relation is stated here in prose rather than as an rdfs:subClassOf edge, matching how the foundation sorts are authored). Contrast logic:Endurant, which is wholly present at each moment."
msgstr "一个发生物：随时间通过累积时间部分而展开的个体，故在任何单一时刻惟其一部分在场。端续物的四维对应物；logic:Event 与 logic:Process 是延续物（每个 Event 都是 Perdurant —— 此上位关系在此以散文表述，而非作为 rdfs:subClassOf 边，与基础种类的编写方式一致）。与 logic:Endurant 相对照，后者在每一时刻完整在场。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/permittedConflictWitness|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a coherence outcome to a disclosed, witnessed contradiction the contract PERMITS (a logic:FindingPermittedEpistemicConflict) — MULTI-valued. Present permitted witnesses do NOT block a logic:CoherenceCertificate; they are surfaced for transparency. Domain logic:CoherenceCertificate or logic:CoherenceCheckAttestation (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将一个一致性结果关联到契约所许可的、被披露且被证见的矛盾（一个 logic:FindingPermittedEpistemicConflict）—— 多值。在场的被许可证见不会阻断 logic:CoherenceCertificate；它们为透明起见而被呈现。定义域 logic:CoherenceCertificate 或 logic:CoherenceCheckAttestation（以散文表述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PersistenceAnnotation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The external-relation annotation dimension for topological persistence or another explicitly identified persistence measure. It is not epistemic confidence."
msgstr "面向拓扑持久性或另一种被显式标识的持久性度量的外部关系标注维度。它不是认知置信度。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PhaseMixin|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "An anti-rigid non-sortal that abstracts an intrinsically-determined phase shared across instances of several Kinds — living thing (a person or an animal in its living phase). Anti-rigid and identity-dispersive: a Phase generalized to span multiple Kinds without supplying identity."
msgstr "一个反刚性非分类子，它抽象出跨若干 Kind 的实例所共享的、由内在决定的相位 —— 生物（一个人或一只动物在其存活相位中）。反刚性且身份离散：一个 Phase 被推广以跨越多个 Kind，而不提供身份。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Phase|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "An anti-rigid sortal an instance falls under during a stage of its existence determined by a change in its own intrinsic state — child, adult, vacant, occupied. Anti-rigid: there is a world of existence in which the instance lacks the Phase (the anti-rigidity witness). Contrast Role, whose change is relational rather than intrinsic."
msgstr "一个反刚性分类子，实例在其存在的某个阶段内落入其下，该阶段由其自身内在状态的一次变化所决定 —— 儿童、成人、空置、占用。反刚性：存在一个存在世界，实例在其中缺乏该 Phase（反刚性证见）。与 Role 相对照，后者的变化是关系性的而非内在的。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/planBody|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Plan to the ROOT node of its program TREE — the structured-program form an interpreter walks, distinct from logic:planFlowEdge, which gathers the binary-edge FLOW-GRAPH form the Tarjan acyclicity certifier runs over. The root is normally a transaction-program combinator (logic:SerialConjunction, logic:Choice, logic:ConcurrentComposition, logic:Fallback, or logic:Iteration), but a single-step plan roots directly at a logic:ActionSchema leaf — no synthetic wrapper combinator is required. Single-valued: a plan has one program root, from which the whole tree is reachable through logic:leftOperand / logic:rightOperand / logic:iterationBody / logic:iterationCondition. A plan whose program tree carries a logic:Iteration loop is OUTSIDE the certified acyclic DAG fragment by construction — the loop is legitimate canonical program structure, not a well-formedness defect — so such a plan does NOT run logic:executedUnderContract the DAG-workflow profile. Domain logic:Plan, range a transaction-program combinator node OR a logic:ActionSchema leaf (stated in prose, matching the module's domain/range convention)."
msgstr "将一个 logic:Plan 关联到其程序树的根节点 —— 解释器所游走的结构化程序形式，区别于 logic:planFlowEdge，后者汇集 Tarjan 无环性证明器所运行的二元边流图形式。根通常是一个事务程序组合子（logic:SerialConjunction、logic:Choice、logic:ConcurrentComposition、logic:Fallback 或 logic:Iteration），但单步计划直接以一个 logic:ActionSchema 叶为根 —— 无需合成的包装组合子。单值：一个计划有一个程序根，整棵树经由 logic:leftOperand / logic:rightOperand / logic:iterationBody / logic:iterationCondition 从中可达。其程序树携带 logic:Iteration 循环的计划在构造上处于被认证的无环 DAG 片段之外 —— 该循环是合法的规范程序结构，而非良构缺陷 —— 故此类计划不 logic:executedUnderContract DAG 工作流配置。定义域 logic:Plan，值域一个事务程序组合子节点或一个 logic:ActionSchema 叶（以散文表述，与模块的定义域/值域约定一致）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/planBranch|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a plan to one of its observation-conditioned branches. A plan that carries logic:planBranch branches whose choice depends on what an earlier action's logic:observation reveals is a POLICY — a reading of a plan, not a separate class (see logic:Plan). Domain a plan, range a branch (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将一个计划关联到它的一条观察条件化分支。若某计划所携带的 logic:planBranch 分支之选择取决于先前动作的 logic:observation 所揭示的内容，则该计划是一种策略 —— 是对计划的一种解读，而非独立类（见 logic:Plan）。定义域一个计划，值域一条分支（以散文表述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/planCertification|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Plan to the logic:ReasoningResult recording its DAG-workflow certification verdict — the result the acyclicity certifier emits when the plan runs logic:executedUnderContract a contract requesting logic:DagWorkflowResource. The result carries logic:resultEvaluation (logic:EvaluationCompleted on an acyclic plan, logic:EvaluationUnsupported on a cyclic one) and logic:resultCompleteness (logic:CompleteForFragment when certified), and on a cyclic plan it discloses the offending cycle members through logic:dagCycleWitness — so the `unsupported` verdict and its witness are reachable from the plan rather than computed and discarded. Domain logic:Plan, range logic:ReasoningResult (stated in prose). The plan stays valid canonically under a non-DAG contract; this link records only what the DAG profile certified over it."
msgstr "将一个 logic:Plan 关联到记录其 DAG 工作流认证裁决的 logic:ReasoningResult —— 当计划 logic:executedUnderContract 一个请求 logic:DagWorkflowResource 的契约时无环性证明器所发出的结果。该结果携带 logic:resultEvaluation（无环计划上为 logic:EvaluationCompleted，有环计划上为 logic:EvaluationUnsupported）与 logic:resultCompleteness（认证时为 logic:CompleteForFragment），并在有环计划上经由 logic:dagCycleWitness 披露犯规的循环成员 —— 从而 `unsupported` 裁决及其证见可从计划到达，而非被计算后丢弃。定义域 logic:Plan，值域 logic:ReasoningResult（以散文表述）。该计划在非 DAG 契约下于规范上仍然有效；此链接仅记录 DAG 配置对它认证了什么。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/planFlowEdge|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Plan to a reified flow edge (logic:ControlFlowEdge or logic:DataFlowEdge) that constitutes its FLOW-GRAPH — the binary-edge form the DAG-workflow acyclicity certifier runs Tarjan SCC over, each edge mediating a source (logic:flowFrom) and a target (logic:flowTo) process node. MULTI-valued: a plan gathers all the control-flow and dataflow edges of its process graph. The canonical-plan counterpart of the build pipeline's gmeow:hasStage stage-membership — where a pipeline gathers gmeow:PipelineStage members whose gmeow:dataflowConsumes edges form its graph, a logic:Plan gathers its reified flow edges directly — so a plan's flow graph is reachable from the plan rather than left as free-standing edges. A plan whose planFlowEdge closure is acyclic is certified logic:CompleteForFragment under logic:DagWorkflowResource; a cyclic closure resolves to the `unsupported` verdict (logic:EvaluationUnsupported) with the offending members disclosed by logic:dagCycleWitness, never silently truncated. Domain logic:Plan, range logic:ControlFlowEdge or logic:DataFlowEdge (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将一个 logic:Plan 关联到构成其流图的一条被具体化的流边（logic:ControlFlowEdge 或 logic:DataFlowEdge）—— DAG 工作流无环性证明器对之运行 Tarjan 强连通分量算法的二元边形式，每条边中介一个源（logic:flowFrom）与一个目标（logic:flowTo）过程节点。多值：一个计划汇集其过程图的所有控制流与数据流边。它是构建管线 gmeow:hasStage 阶段成员关系的规范计划对应物 —— 管线汇集其 gmeow:dataflowConsumes 边构成其图的 gmeow:PipelineStage 成员，而 logic:Plan 直接汇集其被具体化的流边 —— 从而计划的流图可从计划到达，而非被留作游离的边。planFlowEdge 闭包为无环的计划在 logic:DagWorkflowResource 下被认证为 logic:CompleteForFragment；有环闭包解析为 `unsupported` 裁决（logic:EvaluationUnsupported），犯规成员由 logic:dagCycleWitness 披露，绝不被静默截断。定义域 logic:Plan，值域 logic:ControlFlowEdge 或 logic:DataFlowEdge（以散文表述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/planGoal|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Plan to the gmeow:Goal that is its success criterion — the goal the plan's steps, invoking action schemas, are arranged to reach. Domain logic:Plan, range gmeow:Goal (stated in prose). The plan's success against this goal is quantified over nondeterministic outcomes through logic:planSuccessMode."
msgstr "将一个 logic:Plan 关联到作为其成功判据的 gmeow:Goal —— 计划的各步骤（调用动作模式）被安排以达成的目标。定义域 logic:Plan，值域 gmeow:Goal（以散文表述）。计划相对于此目标的成功经由 logic:planSuccessMode 在非确定性结果上被量化。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Plan|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A transaction program (a logic:TransactionProgram-kind node) whose primitive operations invoke action schemas and whose success criterion is a goal expression. As a program it carries the structure a decomposed goal alone cannot — ordering and serial composition, guards, branching, concurrency, loops, and fallback — all in the operators of the transaction layer. A POLICY is a plan whose branches are conditioned on what an earlier action's observation reveals rather than fixed in advance; this is a reading of a plan, NOT a separate class. Plan adoption and revision are recorded as an intention is: a plan is held over an interval and revised by suppression, never mutated. Because an action schema may carry a nondeterministic outcome set, plan success is quantified over those outcomes through logic:planSuccessMode rather than left to the bare executional-success reading. On the foundational spine a logic:Plan is a gmeow:SocialObject (a description, not a physical thing), grounded in prose per the logic-core convention rather than by a subclass edge; a process surface that specializes logic:Plan therefore also asserts its own gmeow:SocialObject or gmeow:InformationObject sort directly, since the prose grounding licenses no DL inference of it."
msgstr "一个事务程序（一个 logic:TransactionProgram 类别的节点），其原始操作调用动作模式，其成功判据是一个目标表达式。作为程序它承载被分解目标本身无法承载的结构 —— 排序与串行组合、守卫、分支、并发、循环与回退 —— 全部处于事务层的算子之中。策略是这样一种计划，其分支条件化于先前动作观察所揭示的内容，而非预先固定；这是对计划的一种解读，而非独立类。计划的采纳与修订如同一个意图那样被记录：一个计划在一段区间上被持有，并通过抑制被修订，绝不被就地变异。由于一个动作模式可携带一个非确定性结果集，计划成功经由 logic:planSuccessMode 在那些结果上被量化，而非留给裸的执行成功解读。在基础主干上，一个 logic:Plan 是一个 gmeow:SocialObject（一个描述，而非物理事物），依逻辑核心约定以散文接地而非经由子类边；因此，一个特化 logic:Plan 的过程表面还需直接断言其自身的 gmeow:SocialObject 或 gmeow:InformationObject 类别，因为散文接地不许可对它作任何 DL 推断。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PlanSuccessMode|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The closed value class of the success quantification a logic:Plan declares over the nondeterministic outcomes of its action schemas. Its individuals are logic:WeakPlanSuccess (some outcome path reaches the goal), logic:StrongPlanSuccess (every outcome path reaches it), and logic:StrongCyclicPlanSuccess (every fair execution is guaranteed to reach it in finitely many steps, allowing retried loops through recoverable failures). The set is closed; a misspelt value is rejected. The quantification exists because the bare executional-success reading of the transaction layer would count the mere existence of one favourable path as success."
msgstr "一个 logic:Plan 就其动作模式的非确定性结果所声明的成功量化的封闭值类。其个体为 logic:WeakPlanSuccess（某条结果路径到达目标）、logic:StrongPlanSuccess（每条结果路径都到达它）与 logic:StrongCyclicPlanSuccess（每次公平执行都保证在有限步内到达它，允许经由可恢复失败而重试的循环）。该集合封闭；拼写错误的值被拒绝。此量化之所以存在，是因为事务层裸的执行成功解读会把一条有利路径的仅仅存在计为成功。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/planSuccessMode|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Plan to the logic:PlanSuccessMode quantifying its success over the nondeterministic outcomes of its action schemas. Domain logic:Plan, range logic:PlanSuccessMode (stated in prose). The quantification exists because the bare executional-success reading of the transaction layer would count one favourable path as success; this declares whether some, every, or every fair execution must reach the goal."
msgstr "将一个 logic:Plan 关联到就其动作模式的非确定性结果量化其成功的 logic:PlanSuccessMode。定义域 logic:Plan，值域 logic:PlanSuccessMode（以散文表述）。此量化之所以存在，是因为事务层裸的执行成功解读会把一条有利路径计为成功；此项声明是否需某条、每条或每次公平执行都到达目标。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PolicySpecificArgumentation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The argumentation-facet value selecting a domain- or policy-specific conflict-resolution semantics rather than a standard Dung semantics — e.g. a declared preference or priority ordering proper to a normative or legal register. Contrast logic:GroundedArgumentation and logic:PreferredArgumentation, the standard abstract-argumentation semantics."
msgstr "选择领域特定或策略特定的冲突消解语义而非标准 Dung 语义的论辩切面值 —— 例如某个恰当归属于规范或法律语域的、被声明的偏好或优先序。与 logic:GroundedArgumentation 及 logic:PreferredArgumentation 即标准抽象论辩语义相对照。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/positionContext|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The context role of a logic:HolonicPosition: the context under which the position is occupied. Holon-ness is contextual — an entity that is a holon under one context need not be under another. One of the five role properties (with logic:positionEntity, logic:positionHolarchy, logic:positionInterval, logic:positionPath) that reify the five-place holonic-position relation onto the arity-bounded reasoning surface."
msgstr "logic:HolonicPosition 的上下文角色：位置被占据时所处的上下文。全子性是上下文相关的——某实体在一个上下文中是全子，在另一个上下文中未必如此。这是将五元全子位置关系具化到元数受限推理面上的五个角色属性之一（另有 logic:positionEntity、logic:positionHolarchy、logic:positionInterval、logic:positionPath）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/positionEntity|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The entity role of a logic:HolonicPosition: the individual that occupies the holonic position — the thing that is a holon along the position's path. One of the five role properties (with logic:positionHolarchy, logic:positionContext, logic:positionInterval, logic:positionPath) that reify the five-place holonic-position relation onto the arity-bounded reasoning surface."
msgstr "logic:HolonicPosition 的实体角色：占据该全子位置的个体——沿位置路径而言充当全子的那个事物。这是将五元全子位置关系具化到元数受限推理面上的五个角色属性之一（另有 logic:positionHolarchy、logic:positionContext、logic:positionInterval、logic:positionPath）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/positionHolarchy|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The holarchy role of a logic:HolonicPosition: the logic:Holarchy within which the position is occupied. Holon-ness is always relative to a holarchy; the same entity may occupy holonic positions in several holarchies. One of the five role properties (with logic:positionEntity, logic:positionContext, logic:positionInterval, logic:positionPath) that reify the five-place holonic-position relation."
msgstr "logic:HolonicPosition 的全子层级角色：位置被占据于其中的 logic:Holarchy。全子性总是相对于某个全子层级而言；同一实体可在多个全子层级中占据全子位置。这是具化五元全子位置关系的五个角色属性之一（另有 logic:positionEntity、logic:positionContext、logic:positionInterval、logic:positionPath）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/positionInterval|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The interval role of a logic:HolonicPosition: the interval over which the position is occupied. Holon-ness is temporally bounded — an entity may occupy a holonic position over one interval and not another. One of the five role properties (with logic:positionEntity, logic:positionHolarchy, logic:positionContext, logic:positionPath) that reify the five-place holonic-position relation."
msgstr "logic:HolonicPosition 的区间角色：位置被占据所跨越的区间。全子性受时间限定——某实体可在一个区间内占据全子位置而在另一区间内不占据。这是具化五元全子位置关系的五个角色属性之一（另有 logic:positionEntity、logic:positionHolarchy、logic:positionContext、logic:positionPath）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/positionPath|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The path role of a logic:HolonicPosition: the path through the holarchy along which the position is read. Holarchies are DAGs, so a holonic position — and the logic:holonicLevel measured at it — is meaningful only relative to a path; two paths may place the same entity at different depths, and both are correct. One of the five role properties (with logic:positionEntity, logic:positionHolarchy, logic:positionContext, logic:positionInterval) that reify the five-place holonic-position relation."
msgstr "logic:HolonicPosition 的路径角色：沿其读取该位置、穿过全子层级的路径。全子层级是 DAG，因此全子位置——以及在该处测得的 logic:holonicLevel——仅相对于某条路径才有意义；两条路径可将同一实体置于不同深度，且两者皆正确。这是具化五元全子位置关系的五个角色属性之一（另有 logic:positionEntity、logic:positionHolarchy、logic:positionContext、logic:positionInterval）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PositiveHornProfile|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The monotonic Horn-rule semantics: least-model semantics over positive (negation-free) rules, always terminating for the function-free fragment. The base case against which every richer profile adds expressivity and cost."
msgstr "单调 Horn 规则语义：正（无否定）规则之上的最小模型语义，对无函数片段总是终止。它是每个更丰富配置在其上叠加表达力与代价的基准情形。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PossibleWorld|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A typed alethic context — a logic:World of alethic possibility, one of the distinct typed contexts of the context algebra (alongside the doxastic gmeow:EpistemicContext, the perspectival gmeow:Standpoint, the hypothesized gmeow:Scenario, the gmeow:State along a logic:Path, the gmeow:ReferenceFrame, and the gmeow:NarrativeReferenceFrame). The contexts its typed accessibility relation logic:epistemicallyPossible ranges over; the modal operators (necessity, possibility) are the standard translation over that typed relation, never over a blurred union. It is a logic:World of the alethic world-type (stated in prose, not as a subclass edge), so no inference may cross into it by walking the bare logic:accessibleFrom superproperty."
msgstr "一种带类型的真势上下文——真势可能性的 logic:World，是上下文代数中若干不同带类型上下文之一（此外还有信念型 gmeow:EpistemicContext、视角型 gmeow:Standpoint、假设型 gmeow:Scenario、沿 logic:Path 的 gmeow:State、gmeow:ReferenceFrame 以及 gmeow:NarrativeReferenceFrame）。它是其带类型可达关系 logic:epistemicallyPossible 所涵盖的诸上下文；模态算子（必然、可能）是在该带类型关系之上的标准翻译，绝不在模糊的并集之上。它是真势世界类型的 logic:World（以散文表述，而非作为子类边），因此任何推理都不得通过遍历那裸的 logic:accessibleFrom 超属性而跨入其中。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/precedenceTenureDistinctness|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Asserts that a gmeow:PrecedenceTenure's gmeow:precedenceHigher and gmeow:precedenceLower norms must be distinct: a norm does not take precedence over itself. The native coherence gate raises a violation when they coincide."
msgstr "断言某 gmeow:PrecedenceTenure 的 gmeow:precedenceHigher 与 gmeow:precedenceLower 规范必须相异：一条规范不优先于其自身。当二者重合时，原生一致性闸会引发一个违规。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/precedes|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A conflict (precedence) edge in a logic:ConcurrentHistory: 'from precedes to' orders the conflicting operation of transaction 'from' before that of transaction 'to' in the witnessed schedule. Two operations conflict when they touch the same item and at least one writes it; the edge direction records which came first in the interleaving. Domain and range are transaction-program nodes (stated in prose). A CYCLE over logic:precedes is a serialization anomaly (logic:SerializationAnomaly) — between two transactions it requires edges in BOTH directions, the write-skew / lost-update shape — and is NEVER a logical contradiction (logic:contradictionWitness): it is a property of the history, not of any single state."
msgstr "logic:ConcurrentHistory 中的一条冲突（优先）边：其方向在被见证的调度中将源事务的冲突操作排在目标事务的冲突操作之前。当两个操作触及同一数据项且至少有一个对其写入时，它们发生冲突；边的方向记录了在交错中谁先发生。定义域与值域为事务程序节点（以散文表述）。logic:precedes 上的一个环是序列化异常（logic:SerializationAnomaly）——在两个事务之间它要求双向都有边，即写偏斜／丢失更新的形态——且绝非逻辑矛盾（logic:contradictionWitness）：它是历史的性质，而非任何单一状态的性质。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/precondition|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ActionSchema to the situation that must hold for the action to apply — the gate on the elementary state transition the schema grounds. Domain logic:ActionSchema (stated in prose, matching the module's domain/range convention). One of the eight action-theory facets means–end reasoning reads."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ActionSchema 关联到该动作得以适用所须成立的情形——即该图式所接地的基本状态转移之上的闸。定义域为 logic:ActionSchema（以散文表述，与模块的定义域／值域约定一致）。它是手段—目的推理所读取的八个动作理论面向之一。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PreferredArgumentation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The preferred Dung argumentation semantics: acceptance over the maximal (with respect to set inclusion) admissible sets of arguments. The credulous counterpart of logic:GroundedArgumentation — a framework may have several preferred extensions, so it admits genuine choice where the grounded semantics is uniquely sceptical."
msgstr "优选的 Dung 论辩语义：在（就集合包含而言）极大的可容许论证集之上进行接受判定。它是 logic:GroundedArgumentation 的轻信对应物——一个框架可有多个优选扩展，因此在有据语义唯一地持怀疑之处，它容许真正的选择。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PreservationKind|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The polarity of guarantee a reasoning projection makes about its answers relative to the canonical logic: model: the answer-preservation classification recorded in the loss ledger for each projection, distinct from and complementary to the complexity/decidability class. Its individuals range from exact preservation through sound under-approximation and complete over-approximation to validation-only, the unsupported floor (the construct cannot be expressed in the target at all), and the two inconsistency-direction kinds."
msgstr "一个推理投影相对于规范 logic: 模型对其答案所作保证的极性：为每个投影记录在损失账本中的答案保持分类，它与复杂度／可判定性类别相区别且互补。其个体从精确保持，经健全的欠近似与完备的过近似，直至仅验证、无支持的下限（该构造在目标中根本无法表达），以及两种不一致方向的种类。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/preservationKind|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a projection (or projection-report entry) to the logic:PreservationKind it claims: the machine-readable preservation polarity in the loss ledger. Lets a report say not just 'dropped modality' but, e.g., 'OWL-EL is a logic:SoundUnderApproximation for subclass entailments under profile X; PTIME'. The projections conformance category checks that each emitted projection matches its declared preservation kind."
msgstr "将一个投影（或投影报告条目）关联到它所声称的 logic:PreservationKind：损失账本中机器可读的保持极性。它使报告不仅能说“掉了模态”，还能说例如“OWL-EL 在配置 X 下对子类蕴涵是 logic:SoundUnderApproximation；PTIME”。投影一致性类别会检查每个发出的投影是否与其所声明的保持种类相符。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/preventsGoal|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates two gmeow:Goals where achieving one closes the path to the other. Domain gmeow:Goal, range gmeow:Goal (stated in prose). One of seven conflict relations between independently-meaningful goals, weaker than gmeow:counterGoal (constitutive opposition). Distinct from logic:contradictoryGoal: prevention closes a path, it does not entail violation in every world."
msgstr "关联两个 gmeow:Goal，其中达成其一即封闭通往另一者的路径。定义域为 gmeow:Goal，值域为 gmeow:Goal（以散文表述）。这是独立且各具意义的目标之间的七种冲突关系之一，弱于 gmeow:counterGoal（构成性对立）。与 logic:contradictoryGoal 相区别：阻断封闭一条路径，并不蕴涵在每个世界中都发生违反。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Prism|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A partial map S → V + S that matches and builds only on the in-focus case of a sum or optional: the optic for 'this correspondence applies when the source is of a particular variant, otherwise it passes through.' Caps: match / build laws on the in-focus case only. Paired with logic:AffineCorrespondence as the partial-alignment band below logic:LossyLens."
msgstr "一个部分映射 S → V + S，仅在和类型或可选类型的聚焦分支上进行匹配与构建：即“该对应仅当源为某个特定变体时适用，否则原样穿过”的光学器件。上限：匹配／构建律仅施于聚焦分支。它与 logic:AffineCorrespondence 配对，作为 logic:LossyLens 之下的部分对齐带。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ProbabilisticFramework|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The uncertainty framework: logic:probability as a graded-belief measure over a declared logic:ProbabilityModel (an independence or dependency model), with marginals computed by weighted model counting. A measure on the uncertainty facet, never a model-semantics value, and kept strictly distinct from logic:confidence (epistemic metadata), logic:weight (solver ranking), and logic:evidenceStrength (warrant) — the four are not interchangeable (design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md, the confidence-probability-weight-and-evidence section)."
msgstr "不确定性框架：以 logic:probability 作为在所声明的 logic:ProbabilityModel（一个独立性或依赖性模型）之上的分级信念度量，其边缘概率由加权模型计数算得。它是不确定性面向上的一种度量，绝非模型语义值，并与 logic:confidence（认知元数据）、logic:weight（求解器排序）以及 logic:evidenceStrength（凭据）严格区分——四者不可互换（design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md，confidence-probability-weight-and-evidence 一节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ProbabilisticMeasure|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The uncertainty measure carrying calibrated probabilities, requiring a declared logic:ProbabilityModel. One member of the uncertainty-measure set facet (it may coexist with logic:WeightedRankingMeasure or logic:FuzzyMeasure); it is a measure carried alongside the chosen model semantics, never a model-semantics value of its own, and never the default reading of a logic:confidence number."
msgstr "承载经校准概率的不确定性度量，需要一个已声明的 logic:ProbabilityModel。它是不确定性度量集合面向中的一员（可与 logic:WeightedRankingMeasure 或 logic:FuzzyMeasure 并存）；它是与所选模型语义并行承载的一种度量，本身绝非模型语义值，也绝不作为某个 logic:confidence 数值的默认读法。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ProbabilisticProfile|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Probabilistic inference over logic:probability, ProbLog-style: requires an explicit independence or dependency model. Probabilistic inference is available only in this profile — it is not the default reading of every confidence number, and a logic:confidence annotation is never interpreted as a probability unless an explicit mapping to logic:probability is declared."
msgstr "在 logic:probability 之上的概率推理，ProbLog 风格：需要显式的独立性或依赖性模型。概率推理仅在此配置中可用——它并非每个置信数值的默认读法，且一个 logic:confidence 标注绝不被解释为概率，除非声明了到 logic:probability 的显式映射。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ProbabilityModel|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A declared independence or dependency model governing probabilistic inference for a rule set or world. Probabilistic inference under logic:ProbabilisticProfile is available ONLY when such a model is declared via logic:probabilityModel: the model fixes the joint distribution over the logic:probability facts so that marginals are well-defined. Absent a declared model the profile refuses to infer probabilities — it never silently assumes independence, because treating un-modelled confidence metadata as a probability model is the named failure mode this vocabulary exists to prevent."
msgstr "一个已声明的独立性或依赖性模型，为某规则集或世界的概率推理提供支配。在 logic:ProbabilisticProfile 之下，只有当经由 logic:probabilityModel 声明了此类模型时，概率推理才可用：该模型固定 logic:probability 事实之上的联合分布，使边缘概率有良好定义。若无已声明的模型，该配置拒绝推断概率——它绝不悄然假定独立性，因为把未建模的置信元数据当作概率模型正是本词汇表存在以防止的那种失败模式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/probabilityModel|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Links a rule set or world to the logic:ProbabilityModel that governs its probabilistic inference. Required for any probabilistic query under logic:ProbabilisticProfile: with no logic:probabilityModel declared, probabilistic inference returns unknown rather than assuming independence over the logic:probability facts."
msgstr "将一个规则集或世界链接到支配其概率推理的 logic:ProbabilityModel。对 logic:ProbabilisticProfile 之下的任何概率查询都必需：若未声明 logic:probabilityModel，概率推理返回未知，而不假定 logic:probability 事实之上的独立性。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/probability|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A calibrated probability under probabilistic fact/event semantics, requiring an explicit independence or dependency model. Distinct from logic:confidence, logic:weight, and logic:evidenceStrength and not interchangeable with them: probabilistic inference is available only in logic:ProbabilisticProfile. A logic:confidence annotation is NOT a probability unless an explicit mapping to this property is declared."
msgstr "在概率性事实／事件语义下的一个经校准概率，需要显式的独立性或依赖性模型。它与 logic:confidence、logic:weight 及 logic:evidenceStrength 相区别且不可互换：概率推理仅在 logic:ProbabilisticProfile 中可用。一个 logic:confidence 标注不是概率，除非声明了到此属性的显式映射。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/probesSchema|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:GateProbe to the logic:ActionSchema it gates. Domain logic:GateProbe, range logic:ActionSchema (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将一个 logic:GateProbe 关联到它所把守的 logic:ActionSchema。定义域为 logic:GateProbe，值域为 logic:ActionSchema（以散文表述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/probesState|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:GateProbe to the state the schema is gated against — the state whose logic:situationObtains and logic:resourceSupply facts the gate reads. Domain logic:GateProbe, range a state (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将一个 logic:GateProbe 关联到该图式所把守的状态——即闸所读取其 logic:situationObtains 与 logic:resourceSupply 事实的那个状态。定义域为 logic:GateProbe，值域为一个状态（以散文表述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ProceduralExecution|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The operational-execution property of a resource policy: the closed set of native derivational builtins is permitted alongside declarative rules. This facet licenses checked arithmetic and comparison evaluation; it does not license search-control constructs. Cut is retired and rejected under every profile. Only the procedural preset expands to this facet, while a budget-bounded contract does not imply procedural execution."
msgstr "资源策略的操作性执行属性：在声明式规则之外，还许可那组封闭的原生派生内建。此面向许可经检查的算术与比较求值；它不许可搜索控制构造。cut 已退役并在每个配置下被拒绝。只有过程式预设展开到此面向，而预算受限的合约并不意味着过程式执行。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ProceduralPrologProfile|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The retained preset name for budget-bounded native derivational builtins: checked arithmetic and comparison operators evaluated by the native physical core alongside declarative rules. It does not provide an embedded Prolog runtime or license cut; cut syntax is retired and rejected before evaluation."
msgstr "为预算受限的原生派生内建保留的预设名称：由原生物理核心在声明式规则之外求值的、经检查的算术与比较算子。它不提供嵌入式 Prolog 运行时，也不许可 cut；cut 语法已退役并在求值前被拒绝。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Process|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A perdurant with internal dynamics: an occurrent composed of sub-processes and phases that unfold over its temporal extent — a manufacturing run, a negotiation, a fermentation. A logic:Perdurant richer than a punctual event (stated in prose, not as a subclass edge); part of the native four-dimensional treatment that restores the UFO-B account gUFO scales back (criticism 3). Dissective: any temporal part of a process is itself that same process, and a process MAY vary over its extent (it bears time-varying logic:Fluents) — the change-bearing half of the process-not-equal-event asymmetry."
msgstr "具有内部动态的续断者：一个由子过程与阶段构成、在其时间延展上展开的发生者——一次制造运行、一场谈判、一场发酵。它是比瞬时事件更丰富的 logic:Perdurant（以散文表述，而非作为子类边）；是原生四维处理的一部分，恢复了 gUFO 缩减的 UFO-B 解释（批评 3）。可分性：过程的任一时间部分本身就是同一个过程，且过程可在其延展上变化（它承载随时间变化的 logic:Fluent）——即过程不等于事件这一非对称性中承载变化的那一半。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/producesResultShape|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a query (or a competency question) to the logic:ResultShape its result set is guaranteed to satisfy. The query's bindings are validated against this shape after execution; a mismatch is a hard, surfaced error. Single-valued. Range logic:ResultShape (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将一个查询（或一道胜任力问题）关联到其结果集被保证满足的 logic:ResultShape。查询的绑定在执行后依此形状校验；不匹配即为一个硬性、被显式暴露的错误。单值。值域为 logic:ResultShape（以散文表述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/programQuery|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningProgram to the single goal atom it resolves against its clause set. Functional: a program declares exactly one goal (logic:ReasoningProgramQueryConstraint requires it; the owl:FunctionalProperty declaration caps it at one). The goal's logic:termVariable term-carriers are the answer variables the engine binds and returns, distinct from a logic:verdictProbe atom's three-valued verdict projection."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ReasoningProgram 关联到它针对其子句集求解的单个目标原子。函数式：一个程序恰好声明一个目标（logic:ReasoningProgramQueryConstraint 要求之；owl:FunctionalProperty 声明将其上限定为一）。该目标的 logic:termVariable 词项载体是引擎绑定并返回的答案变量，区别于 logic:verdictProbe 原子的三值裁决投影。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ProjectionLoss|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "An in-band declaration that a lossy projection dropped structure its source carried — emitted into the projected graph itself, never a sidecar. GTS stays lossless; loss is declared only at the exit gate (Principle 17 / Principle 4). A loss-aware SPARQL CONSTRUCT mints one when its template omits an RDF-1.2 reification layer that its WHERE matched, so a downstream consumer of the projection can see exactly what was shed."
msgstr "一个带内声明，表明有损投影丢弃了其源所承载的结构——它被发出到投影图本身之中，绝非旁挂文件。GTS 保持无损；损失仅在出口闸处声明（原则 17／原则 4）。当一个损失感知的 SPARQL CONSTRUCT 模板略去其匹配图式所命中的 RDF-1.2 具体化层时，会铸造一个此类声明，以便投影的下游消费者能确切看到被剥去了什么。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/projectionLoss|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Names a loss-ledger code carried on a logic:CoherenceCertificate / logic:CoherenceCheckAttestation payload — MULTI-valued. Distinct from logic:unsupportedConstruct (which names the undecided DL construct): logic:projectionLoss records the ledger code of a lossy projection (Principle 17) that co-held when the coherence artifact was issued."
msgstr "命名承载于一个 logic:CoherenceCertificate／logic:CoherenceCheckAttestation 载荷上的损失账本代码——多值。与 logic:unsupportedConstruct（命名未判定的 DL 构造）相区别：logic:projectionLoss 记录在一致性工件签发时并存的某个有损投影（原则 17）的账本代码。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ProjectionTarget|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The facet value class of a projection target: a surface the answer is rendered to. The projection facet is an output request that may name one or more targets (canonical, OWL, Datalog, Common Logic, validation-only) at once; it is a standing request, not a semantic selection, and never alters which entailments hold."
msgstr "一个投影目标的面向值类：答案被渲染到其上的一个表面。投影面向是一个输出请求，可同时命名一个或多个目标（规范、OWL、Datalog、Common Logic、仅验证）；它是一个常设请求，而非语义选择，且绝不改变哪些蕴涵成立。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/projectionTarget|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to a logic:ProjectionTarget it requests the answer be rendered to. A standing output request, possibly naming several targets at once (canonical, OWL, Datalog, Common Logic, validation-only); it is not a semantic selection and never alters which entailments hold. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:ProjectionTarget (stated in prose, matching the module's convention)."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ReasoningContract 关联到它请求把答案渲染至其上的一个 logic:ProjectionTarget。一个常设输出请求，可能同时命名若干目标（规范、OWL、Datalog、Common Logic、仅验证）；它不是语义选择，且绝不改变哪些蕴涵成立。定义域为 logic:ReasoningContract，值域为 logic:ProjectionTarget（以散文表述，与模块约定一致）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ProjectionTarget|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A contract may request both logic:CanonicalProjection and logic:CommonLogicProjection for one canonical answer."
msgstr "一份合约可以为同一个规范答案同时请求 logic:CanonicalProjection 和 logic:CommonLogicProjection。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/projectsLadderEdge|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The ladder property a logic:DimensionThreshold row emits when its dimension clears its threshold: gmeow:isAwareOf, gmeow:knowsAbout, gmeow:understands or gmeow:hasMastered. Range is left open (the gmeow: ladder properties), stated in prose to keep the OWL down-projection clean."
msgstr "当一个 logic:DimensionThreshold 行的维度越过其阈值时，它所发出的阶梯属性：gmeow:isAwareOf、gmeow:knowsAbout、gmeow:understands 或 gmeow:hasMastered。值域保持开放（即 gmeow: 阶梯属性），以散文表述以保持 OWL 下投影的整洁。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/projectsToVerdict|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The machine-readable image of the SZS→conformance-verdict collapse: relates a logic:SzsStatus individual to the logic:ConformanceVerdict its outcome projects onto. Domain logic:SzsStatus, range logic:ConformanceVerdict (stated in prose). This is the dogfooded, on-gate-checkable form of the native crates/conformance/src/external/status.rs::outcome_for_szs table — the monotone map whose lossiness (many statuses to one verdict) is declared by logic:corrSzsToVerdict and whose per-status edges the no-drift gate compares against the Rust table so the ontology and the code can never disagree."
msgstr "SZS→一致性裁决坍缩的机器可读映像：将一个 logic:SzsStatus 个体关联到其结果所投影至的 logic:ConformanceVerdict。定义域为 logic:SzsStatus，值域为 logic:ConformanceVerdict（以散文表述）。这是原生 crates/conformance/src/external/status.rs::outcome_for_szs 表的、被自吃狗粮且可在闸上核查的形式——那个单调映射，其有损性（多个状态对一个裁决）由 logic:corrSzsToVerdict 声明，其逐状态边由无漂移闸与该 Rust 表比对，从而使本体与代码永不相悖。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/properPartOf|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "STRICT parthood: relates an entity to a whole it is part of but NOT identical to. Transitive, asymmetric, and irreflexive — a genuine strict partial order (proper-part-of, ancestor). This exact combination is illegal in OWL 2 DL, which globally forbids a property being both transitive and asymmetric (criticism 7, LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md §OWL 2 criticisms); logic: imposes no such global restriction and reasons over it completely, recovering decidability by projection rather than by crippling the canon. The deliberate OWL-2-criticism demonstrator."
msgstr "严格部分关系：将一个实体关联到它是其部分但与之不同一的整体。传递、反对称且反自反——一个真正的严格偏序（真部分关系、祖先）。这一确切组合在 OWL 2 DL 中非法，后者全局禁止一个属性同时为传递与反对称（批评 7，LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md §OWL 2 批评）；logic: 不施加此类全局限制并对其完全推理，通过投影而非阉割正典来恢复可判定性。它是那个刻意的 OWL-2-批评示范者。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PropertyCharacteristicAssertion|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A central record asserting that a named property bears a characteristic sort — one of logic:transitiveProperty, logic:symmetricProperty, logic:irreflexiveProperty, logic:asymmetricProperty or logic:functionalProperty. It names the property with logic:characterizes and the sort with logic:characteristicSort, the pair the native coherence gate joins to enforce the characteristic, and carries a logic:formalizes back-reference to the domain property whose prose it encodes. This is the canonical logic: carrier of a property characteristic: the domain slice keeps the OWL-facing declaration, the reasoning authority names and enforces it here."
msgstr "一条中心记录，断言某个具名属性承载一种特征种类——logic:transitiveProperty、logic:symmetricProperty、logic:irreflexiveProperty、logic:asymmetricProperty 或 logic:functionalProperty 之一。它以 logic:characterizes 命名该属性，以 logic:characteristicSort 命名该种类，二者构成原生一致性闸为强制该特征而连接的配对，并携带一个 logic:formalizes 回指，指向其散文被它编码的那个领域属性。这是属性特征的规范 logic: 载体：领域切片保留面向 OWL 的声明，而推理权威在此命名并强制它。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PropertyPathProjection|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The projection-target value requesting that a logic:PathShape (or a rule's path-structured body) be rendered to a SPARQL property-path surface — extended by GMEOW past SPARQL 1.1 §9 with bounded depth {n,m} and a predicate wildcard. One of several output targets a single contract may name at once; like every projection target it is a rendering request and never alters which entailments hold. A consumer restricted to standard SPARQL §9 receives the unrolled or approximated form, and that loss is declared in the loss ledger rather than hidden."
msgstr "投影目标值，请求把一个 logic:PathShape（或某规则的路径结构化主体）渲染到 SPARQL 属性路径表面——由 GMEOW 在 SPARQL 1.1 §9 之外扩展，加入有界深度 {n,m} 与谓词通配符。它是单个合约可同时命名的若干输出目标之一；如同每个投影目标，它是一个渲染请求，绝不改变哪些蕴涵成立。一个受限于标准 SPARQL §9 的消费者会收到展开或近似的形式，而该损失被声明在损失账本中，而非被隐藏。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ProseFieldAvoidWhen|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:ProseField for a term's gmeow:avoidWhen — the anti-pattern or non-applicability guidance a candidate formalized. Wire value `avoid-when`."
msgstr "对应某词项 gmeow:avoidWhen 的 logic:ProseField——候选者所形式化的反模式或不适用性指引。线路值 `avoid-when`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ProseFieldDefinition|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:ProseField for a term's skos:definition — the definitional or descriptive prose a candidate formalized. Wire value `definition`."
msgstr "对应某词项 skos:definition 的 logic:ProseField——候选者所形式化的定义性或描述性散文。线路值 `definition`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/proseFieldProperty|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Names the annotation property a logic:ProseField value stands for — the exact term-level field (skos:definition, gmeow:useWhen or gmeow:avoidWhen) whose prose a harvested candidate formalizes. An annotation property, so the closed logic:ProseField set links to the real field IRI without punning it into the reasoned core."
msgstr "命名一个 logic:ProseField 值所代表的标注属性——即某个被采集的候选者所形式化的散文所属的确切词项级字段（skos:definition、gmeow:useWhen 或 gmeow:avoidWhen）。它是一个标注属性，因此封闭的 logic:ProseField 集合链接到真实字段 IRI，而不将其双关进被推理的核心。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ProseField|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The closed three-member value class of the logic:candidateSourceField facet: which annotation field of a term's prose a logic:FormalizationCandidate harvested its axiom from. Its individuals are logic:ProseFieldDefinition, logic:ProseFieldUseWhen and logic:ProseFieldAvoidWhen, each naming the annotation property it stands for via logic:proseFieldProperty (skos:definition, gmeow:useWhen and gmeow:avoidWhen respectively). The set is closed and atomic (Principle 9), so a misspelt field names no declared value and is rejected rather than silently accepted. Read with logic:candidateFormalizes (which term) it makes harvest coverage queryable in both directions — from a harvested axiom to the exact prose field it formalizes, and from a prose field to the axioms that formalize it (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, §Typed formalization governance)."
msgstr "logic:candidateSourceField 面向的封闭三成员值类：一个 logic:FormalizationCandidate 从某词项散文的哪个标注字段采集其公理。其个体为 logic:ProseFieldDefinition、logic:ProseFieldUseWhen 与 logic:ProseFieldAvoidWhen，各自经由 logic:proseFieldProperty 命名它所代表的标注属性（分别为 skos:definition、gmeow:useWhen 与 gmeow:avoidWhen）。该集合封闭且原子（原则 9），因此拼错的字段不命名任何已声明的值，会被拒绝而非悄然接受。与 logic:candidateFormalizes（哪个词项）合读，它使采集覆盖在两个方向上均可查询——从被采集的公理到它所形式化的确切散文字段，以及从一个散文字段到形式化它的诸公理（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，§Typed formalization governance）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ProseFieldUseWhen|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:ProseField for a term's gmeow:useWhen — the applicability guidance a candidate formalized. Wire value `use-when`."
msgstr "对应于某词项的 gmeow:useWhen 的 logic:ProseField——某候选者所形式化的适用性指引。线路值 `use-when`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/protocolEnforced|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The boolean verdict of classifying a logic:ConcurrentHistory's witnessed schedule against the logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol its run declared (logic:declaredProtocol): true iff the schedule respects that protocol's discipline over the run's recorded protocol events (timestamps for logic:TimestampOrdering; lock acquire/release events for the two-phase-locking protocols; cross-leg read-write disjointness for logic:OptimisticValidation). Domain logic:ConcurrentHistory, range xsd:boolean (stated in prose); present only when a protocol is declared. A false verdict carries a human-readable logic:protocolViolationReason. This is HOW-a-guarantee-is-enforced verification, kept distinct from logic:satisfiesCriterion (the history property the schedule satisfies) and logic:isolationLevelAdequacy (whether the schedule meets a declared guarantee strength); a declared protocol whose required events are absent is a hard error, never a false-by-default."
msgstr "针对一个 logic:ConcurrentHistory 被见证的调度，就其运行所声明的 logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol（logic:declaredProtocol）进行分类所得的布尔裁决：当且仅当该调度在运行所记录的协议事件上遵守该协议的纪律时为真（对 logic:TimestampOrdering 为时间戳；对两阶段锁定协议为加锁／解锁事件；对 logic:OptimisticValidation 为跨腿读写不相交）。定义域为 logic:ConcurrentHistory，值域为 xsd:boolean（以散文表述）；仅当声明了协议时存在。为假的裁决携带一段人类可读的 logic:protocolViolationReason。这是关于保证如何被强制的验证，与 logic:satisfiesCriterion（调度所满足的历史性质）及 logic:isolationLevelAdequacy（调度是否达到所声明的保证强度）保持区分；一个所声明协议若其所需事件缺失，则为硬性错误，绝非默认为假。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/protocolLevelAdequacy|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The boolean verdict of classifying whether the logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol a run declares (logic:declaredProtocol) is strong enough to guarantee the logic:IsolationLevel it also declares (logic:declaredIsolationLevel): true iff the protocol's guaranteed ceiling level is at least the declared level. Domain logic:ConcurrentHistory, range xsd:boolean (stated in prose); present only when a run declares BOTH a protocol and a level — otherwise there is no pairing to judge. The guaranteed ceilings are logic:SnapshotIsolation for logic:MultiversionConcurrencyControl and logic:SerializableIsolation (coincident with logic:OpacityIsolation for committed-only histories) for logic:StrictTwoPhaseLocking, logic:StrongStrictTwoPhaseLocking, logic:TimestampOrdering, and logic:OptimisticValidation. The one inadequate pairing this vocabulary admits is logic:MultiversionConcurrencyControl declared under logic:SerializableIsolation or logic:OpacityIsolation, since its snapshot ceiling still admits write skew; a false verdict carries a logic:protocolLevelInadequacyReason. It is a CONSISTENCY CROSS-CHECK between two declarations — kept distinct from logic:protocolEnforced (whether the witnessed schedule respects the mechanism) and logic:isolationLevelAdequacy (whether the witnessed schedule meets the strength) — and never infers the level from the protocol nor the protocol from the level."
msgstr "分类判定运行所声明的 logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol（logic:declaredProtocol）是否足够强以保证它同时声明的 logic:IsolationLevel（logic:declaredIsolationLevel）所得的布尔裁决：当且仅当协议所保证的天花板级别至少达到所声明级别时为真。定义域为 logic:ConcurrentHistory，值域为 xsd:boolean（以散文表述）；仅当一次运行同时声明了协议与级别时存在——否则没有可判定的配对。所保证的天花板为：logic:MultiversionConcurrencyControl 对应 logic:SnapshotIsolation；logic:StrictTwoPhaseLocking、logic:StrongStrictTwoPhaseLocking、logic:TimestampOrdering 与 logic:OptimisticValidation 对应 logic:SerializableIsolation（对仅提交的历史与 logic:OpacityIsolation 重合）。本词汇表所承认的唯一不足配对是 logic:MultiversionConcurrencyControl 在 logic:SerializableIsolation 或 logic:OpacityIsolation 之下声明，因为其快照天花板仍容许写偏斜；为假的裁决携带一段 logic:protocolLevelInadequacyReason。它是两个声明之间的一致性交叉核对——与 logic:protocolEnforced（被见证的调度是否遵守机制）及 logic:isolationLevelAdequacy（被见证的调度是否达到强度）保持区分——且绝不从协议推断级别，也不从级别推断协议。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/protocolLevelInadequacyReason|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A human-readable description of WHY a run's declared logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol cannot guarantee its declared logic:IsolationLevel — present exactly when logic:protocolLevelAdequacy is false. Domain logic:ConcurrentHistory, range xsd:string (stated in prose). In this vocabulary the case is logic:MultiversionConcurrencyControl declared under logic:SerializableIsolation or logic:OpacityIsolation, and the reason names it: the protocol's guaranteed ceiling is snapshot isolation, which admits write skew, so it does not reach the declared serializable-or-stronger level. It is a declaration-consistency finding, never a claim of logical contradiction within a state."
msgstr "一段人类可读的描述，说明为何一次运行所声明的 logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol 无法保证其所声明的 logic:IsolationLevel——恰在 logic:protocolLevelAdequacy 为假时存在。定义域为 logic:ConcurrentHistory，值域为 xsd:string（以散文表述）。在本词汇表中，该情形是 logic:MultiversionConcurrencyControl 在 logic:SerializableIsolation 或 logic:OpacityIsolation 之下声明，理由即指明：协议所保证的天花板是快照隔离，它容许写偏斜，故达不到所声明的可序列化或更强级别。它是一项声明一致性发现，绝非在某一状态之内主张逻辑矛盾。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/protocolViolationReason|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A human-readable description of WHY a logic:ConcurrentHistory's witnessed schedule fails the concurrency-control protocol its run declared — present exactly when logic:protocolEnforced is false. Domain logic:ConcurrentHistory, range xsd:string (stated in prose). It names the discipline the schedule breaks (a non-two-phase lock order, a lock released before commit, a conflict edge against timestamp order, or a cross-leg read-write conflict that optimistic validation would abort), so a protocol failure is surfaced with its cause rather than as a bare boolean. It is a description of a mechanism-level finding, never a claim of logical contradiction within a state."
msgstr "一段人类可读的描述，说明为何一个 logic:ConcurrentHistory 被见证的调度未通过其运行所声明的并发控制协议——恰在 logic:protocolEnforced 为假时存在。定义域为 logic:ConcurrentHistory，值域为 xsd:string（以散文表述）。它指明调度所违背的纪律（非两阶段的锁序、在提交前释放的锁、与时间戳序相悖的冲突边，或乐观验证会中止的跨腿读写冲突），使协议失败连同其成因一并被暴露，而非作为一个裸布尔。它是对机制级发现的描述，绝非在某一状态之内主张逻辑矛盾。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PutGet|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The lens law get(put(v, s)) = v: putting a view into a source and reading it back yields exactly that view. Claimable from the logic:WellBehavedLens rung upward; the update-faithfulness law."
msgstr "透镜律 get(put(v, s)) = v：将一个视图放入源再读回，恰好得到该视图。可自 logic:WellBehavedLens 这一级向上主张；即更新忠实性律。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/putLeg|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Lens to the logic:TransactionProgram that realizes its put leg — the up-projection put : V × S → S folding a view back into the rich GMEOW source. A lawful put comes only from a logic:mnemomorphic witness or a co-authored put-with-claim; naive backward execution of the get leg is a candidate preimage, never a lawful put. Domain logic:Lens, range logic:TransactionProgram."
msgstr "将一个 logic:Lens 关联到实现其 put 腿的 logic:TransactionProgram——即上投影 put : V × S → S，将视图折回丰富的 GMEOW 源。合法的 put 只来自一个 logic:mnemomorphic 见证或一个共同撰写的带主张 put；对 get 腿的朴素反向执行是候选原像，绝非合法 put。定义域为 logic:Lens，值域为 logic:TransactionProgram。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PutPut|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The very-well-behaved lens law put(v2, put(v1, s)) = put(v2, s): a later put overwrites an earlier one with no residue. Optional even at the logic:WellBehavedLens rung; claimed only by correspondences whose put leg is genuinely history-free."
msgstr "极良行为透镜律 put(v2, put(v1, s)) = put(v2, s)：后一次 put 覆盖前一次而无残留。即便在 logic:WellBehavedLens 这一级也是可选的；仅由其 put 腿真正无历史的诸对应所主张。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/qualifiedCardinality|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:reviewRestriction logic:qualifiedCardinality 2 ; logic:onClass ex:Reviewer ."
msgstr "示例：ex:reviewRestriction logic:qualifiedCardinality 2 ; logic:onClass ex:Reviewer ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/qualifiedCardinality|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Exactly one qualifier, logic:onClass or logic:onDataRange, determines which fillers are counted."
msgstr "恰好一个限定词，logic:onClass 或 logic:onDataRange，决定对哪些填充项进行计数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/QualityConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A named quality/quantity well-formedness axiom a quality or measured value can violate — the family of constraints governing the generic-quality/quality-role ladder and the true-quantity/measured-value seam. Distinct from logic:OccurrentConstraint (the four-dimensional perdurant axioms) and logic:MereologyConstraint (profiled-mereology axioms): quality constraints govern the stratification of a quality into a frame-independent generic quality, the anti-rigid role it plays in a bearer-context, and a frame-relative measured value. Its named individuals are the labels a logic:violation fact may point at; the set is closed so a misspelt label names no declared constraint and is rejected rather than silently accepted."
msgstr "一条具名的品质／数量良构公理，品质或测量值可违反它——支配通用品质／品质角色阶梯以及真数量／测量值接缝的那族约束。与 logic:OccurrentConstraint（四维续断者公理）及 logic:MereologyConstraint（配置化部分论公理）相区别：品质约束支配一个品质被分层为一个与框架无关的通用品质、它在承载者上下文中所扮演的反刚性角色，以及一个与框架相关的测量值。其具名个体是一个 logic:violation 事实可指向的标签；该集合封闭，故拼错的标签不命名任何已声明的约束，会被拒绝而非悄然接受。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/qualityRole|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Quality to the anti-rigid logic:Role its generic quality plays in a bearer-context — height being length playing a role in a human-body context, systolic pressure being pressure playing a role in the arterial-blood-pressure context. The frame-relative leg of the generic-quality/quality-role ladder (Principle 11 stated in role terms), paired with logic:genericQuality: the role contextualizes the frame-independent generic quality, and reuses the existing anti-rigid logic:Role machinery rather than minting a parallel one. A quality bearing a logic:qualityRole with no logic:genericQuality is the logic:QualityRoleWithoutGeneric violation. Domain logic:Quality, range logic:Role (stated in prose, matching the module's convention)."
msgstr "将一个 logic:Quality 关联到其通用品质在承载者上下文中所扮演的反刚性 logic:Role——身高是长度在人体上下文中扮演角色、收缩压是压力在动脉血压上下文中扮演角色。这是通用品质／品质角色阶梯与框架相关的那条腿（以角色术语表述的原则 11），与 logic:genericQuality 配对：角色将与框架无关的通用品质情境化，并复用既有的反刚性 logic:Role 机制而非另铸一套。一个品质承载 logic:qualityRole 却无 logic:genericQuality，即 logic:QualityRoleWithoutGeneric 违规。定义域为 logic:Quality，值域为 logic:Role（以散文表述，与模块约定一致）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/QualityRoleWithoutGeneric|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The ladder-completeness axiom as a quality constraint: a quality that plays a quality-role must also instantiate the generic quality that role contextualizes — a logic:Quality with a logic:qualityRole but no logic:genericQuality is ill-formed. The generic quality (length, pressure) is the frame-independent structure; the quality-role (height, systolic pressure) is that structure playing an anti-rigid logic:Role in a bearer-context, and the role presupposes the generic it specializes (Principle 11 in role terms: the frame-relative value cannot stand without the frame-independent structure it refines). A quality bearing a role with no generic is the logic:violation, entailed by the foundation lowering rather than asserted by hand."
msgstr "作为品质约束的阶梯完备性公理：一个扮演品质角色的品质，也必须实例化该角色所情境化的通用品质——一个带 logic:qualityRole 却无 logic:genericQuality 的 logic:Quality 是不良构的。通用品质（长度、压力）是与框架无关的结构；品质角色（身高、收缩压）是该结构在承载者上下文中扮演一个反刚性 logic:Role，而角色预设了它所特化的通用品质（以角色术语表述的原则 11：与框架相关的值离不开它所精炼的与框架无关的结构）。一个承载角色却无通用品质的品质即为该 logic:violation，由基础下投影蕴涵得出，而非手工断言。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Quality|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "An aspect whose value is a point or region in a quality space — a mass, a temperature, a colour hue — an intrinsic, directly measurable moment. The counterpart of gufo:Quality; a logic:Aspect that takes a logic:QualityValue in a logic:QualitySpace (stated in prose, not as a subclass edge). Contrast logic:Mode, which is not directly measurable. A logic:Quality is persistent: it inheres in a bearer and endures while its measured values change, so dated observations attach to one enduring quality (by reference) rather than minting a fresh value each time. It instantiates a frame-independent generic quality via logic:genericQuality and may play an anti-rigid quality-role in a bearer-context via logic:qualityRole over logic:Role — the generic-quality/quality-role ladder (Principle 11)."
msgstr "一个方面，其值是品质空间中的一个点或区域——一个质量、一个温度、一个色相——一个内在的、可直接测量的瞬态。它是 gufo:Quality 的对应物；一个在 logic:QualitySpace 中取一个 logic:QualityValue 的 logic:Aspect（以散文表述，而非作为子类边）。与不可直接测量的 logic:Mode 相对照。一个 logic:Quality 是持续的：它内在于一个承载者并在其测量值变化时持存，因此有日期的观测按引用附着于同一个持续品质，而非每次铸造一个新值。它经由 logic:genericQuality 实例化一个与框架无关的通用品质，并可经由 logic:qualityRole 在 logic:Role 之上于承载者上下文中扮演一个反刚性品质角色——即通用品质／品质角色阶梯（原则 11）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/QualitySpace|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The structured space of possible values for a kind of quality — the mass scale, the temperature scale, a colour solid — within which a logic:Quality's logic:QualityValue is located. The conceptual-space structure (ordering, metric, dimensions) against which quality values are compared; it supplies the geometry a bare value would lack."
msgstr "某类品质可能值的结构化空间——质量标度、温度标度、一个颜色立体——某个 logic:Quality 的 logic:QualityValue 定位于其中。它是品质值据以比较的概念空间结构（序、度量、维度）；它提供了一个裸值所缺的几何。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/QualityValue|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A point or region within a quality space that a logic:Quality takes as its value — 80 kg, 37 °C, the hue at coordinate (h,s,v). The counterpart of gufo:QualityValue; a logic:AbstractIndividual situated in a logic:QualitySpace (stated in prose, not as a subclass edge)."
msgstr "品质空间内一个 logic:Quality 取作其值的点或区域——80 kg、37 °C、坐标 (h,s,v) 处的色相。它是 gufo:QualityValue 的对应物；一个置于 logic:QualitySpace 中的 logic:AbstractIndividual（以散文表述，而非作为子类边）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Quantified|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The residue shape tag for a formula in which an explicit quantifier (logic:forall or logic:exists) appears — quantification nested or alternating beyond the implicit universal closure of a Horn rule. Disclosed when a Horn-fragment target carries such a formula as flagged unsupported residue."
msgstr "某公式的残余形状标签，其中出现一个显式量词（logic:forall 或 logic:exists）——量化嵌套或交替，超出 Horn 规则的隐式全称闭包。当一个 Horn 片段目标承载此类公式作为被标记的无支持残余时予以披露。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/quantifiedVariable|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a quantifier logic:Formula to one of its bound-variable term-carriers. Each carrier fixes its position in the binder block with logic:termIndex and its name with logic:termVariable; block order is significant, because bound-variable renaming preserves meaning but reordering a quantifier prefix does not."
msgstr "将一个量词 logic:Formula 关联到它的某个约束变量词项载体。每个载体以 logic:termIndex 固定其在绑定块中的位置、以 logic:termVariable 固定其名称；块序有意义，因为约束变量重命名保持含义，而重排量词前缀则不然。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/quantifiedVariable|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A two-variable quantifier links carriers at indices 0 and 1 with logic:termVariable values 'x' and 'y'."
msgstr "一个双变量量词以 logic:termVariable 值 'x' 和 'y' 将索引 0 和 1 处的载体连接起来。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Quantity|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "An amount of stuff individuated by its constitution rather than by a count of members — a portion of water, a lump of clay, a quantity of gold. The counterpart of gufo:Quantity; its identity tracks the matter that constitutes it (maximally self-connected portions of a substance), not a number of discrete units. Contrast logic:Collection, individuated by its members."
msgstr "一份由其构成而非由成员计数个体化的物料——一份水、一团黏土、一定量的黄金。它是 gufo:Quantity 的对应物；其同一性追踪构成它的物质（某物质的极大自连通份额），而非离散单位的数目。与由其成员个体化的 logic:Collection 相对照。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Query|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A goal to be resolved, carried together with its answer shape: the node kind that asks a question of the IR rather than asserting or deriving. Distinct from logic:DerivationRule and logic:TransactionProgram so a query operator is never read as a program operator."
msgstr "一个待求解的目标，连同其答案形状一并承载：向 IR 提出一个问题、而非断言或派生的那种节点种类。它与 logic:DerivationRule 及 logic:TransactionProgram 相区别，使查询算子绝不被读作程序算子。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/query|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The canonical query text a logic:ReasoningResult answers — part of the proof certificate. Single-valued. Domain logic:ReasoningResult (stated in prose)."
msgstr "一个 logic:ReasoningResult 所回答的规范查询文本——证明证书的一部分。单值。定义域为 logic:ReasoningResult（以散文表述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/range|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:memberOf logic:range ex:Organization ."
msgstr "示例：ex:memberOf logic:range ex:Organization ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/range|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Multiple range axioms are conjunctive entailments, not alternative allowed object types."
msgstr "多条值域公理是合取式的蕴涵，而非可供选择的许可宾语类型。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RankAnnotation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The external-relation annotation dimension for an explicitly declared ordinal rank. Rank is neither distance nor epistemic confidence."
msgstr "为一个显式声明的序数等级提供的外部关系注解维度。等级既不是距离，也不是认识论上的置信度。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/rawStatusToken|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The verbatim external result-status token carried as provenance, so the coarse logic:ConformanceVerdict projection never discards the distinction the community source drew. Domain a logic:SzsStatus individual or a conformance comparison, range xsd:string (stated in prose): the exact SZS token (e.g. \"ContradictoryAxioms\") or W3C manifest kind before the lossy collapse. This realizes maximal information flow — logic:SzsContradictoryAxioms and logic:SzsUnsatisfiable both project to logic:ConfInconsistent, yet stay distinguishable on the folded individual through this token (design/LOGIC-CONFORMANCE.md, the external FOL soundness oracle)."
msgstr "作为来源信息携带的、逐字的外部结果状态令牌，从而使粗粒度的 logic:ConformanceVerdict 投影永不丢弃社区来源所作出的区分。定义域为一个 logic:SzsStatus 个体或一次一致性比较，值域为 xsd:string（以散文形式给出）：即在有损坍缩之前的精确 SZS 令牌（例如 \"ContradictoryAxioms\"）或 W3C 清单类别。这实现了最大化的信息流——logic:SzsContradictoryAxioms 与 logic:SzsUnsatisfiable 都投影为 logic:ConfInconsistent，但通过此令牌在折叠后的个体上仍可区分（design/LOGIC-CONFORMANCE.md，外部 FOL 可靠性预言机）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RdfEqualityPolicy|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The equality-policy value under which term identity is RDF node identity — two IRIs are equal exactly when they are the same node, and distinct IRIs are not assumed to co-refer absent an asserted equality. The baseline graph reading; contrast logic:ExplicitEqualityPolicy and logic:UniqueNameEqualityPolicy."
msgstr "一种相等策略取值，在其之下词项同一性即 RDF 节点同一性——两个 IRI 恰好在它们是同一节点时相等，而在缺少已断言的相等关系时，相异的 IRI 不被假定共指。这是基线的图读法；与 logic:ExplicitEqualityPolicy 及 logic:UniqueNameEqualityPolicy 相对照。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ReadCommittedIsolation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:IsolationLevel guarantee under which a transaction observes only committed writes, but successive reads of the same item may differ — dirty reads excluded, non-repeatable reads still admitted."
msgstr "logic:IsolationLevel 保证，在其之下一次事务仅观察到已提交的写入，但对同一条目的连续读取可能不同——排除脏读，仍允许不可重复读。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/readsFrom|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A read-dependency edge of a logic:ConcurrentHistory: 'reader readsFrom writer' records that the reading logic:TransactionStep observed, for a situation in its read set (its schema's logic:precondition), the value written by the writer logic:TransactionStep — the last step to write that situation before the reader in the witnessed interleaving. Domain and range logic:TransactionStep (stated in prose). Emitted only for CROSS-transaction read dependencies (a step reading from the OTHER leg's write), which is where the read-from relation can differ from a serial order and therefore where it carries view-serializability information; intra-leg read dependencies are fixed by the leg's own order and carry none. Together with logic:happensBefore it is the view-serializability surface, kept DISTINCT from logic:precedes, which is the transaction-level conflict edge over which conflict-serializability is decided."
msgstr "logic:ConcurrentHistory 的一条读依赖边：「reader readsFrom writer」记录了执行读取的 logic:TransactionStep 针对其读集合中的某个情形（其模式的 logic:precondition）观察到了由执行写入的 logic:TransactionStep 所写入的值——即在被见证的交错序列中，在该读者之前最后写入该情形的步骤。定义域与值域均为 logic:TransactionStep（以散文形式给出）。仅为跨事务的读依赖（某步骤读取另一分支的写入）而生成，因为正是在此处「读自」关系可能偏离串行次序，从而携带视图可串行化信息；分支内的读依赖由该分支自身的次序所固定，不携带任何此类信息。它与 logic:happensBefore 一起构成视图可串行化界面，并与 logic:precedes 保持区分，后者是事务级别的冲突边，冲突可串行化据此判定。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ReadUncommittedIsolation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:IsolationLevel guarantee under which a transaction may observe uncommitted writes of others — the weakest level of the standard spectrum, admitting dirty reads."
msgstr "logic:IsolationLevel 保证，在其之下一次事务可以观察到他者尚未提交的写入——标准谱系中最弱的级别，允许脏读。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ReasoningContract|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A compositional specification of the reasoning semantics a rule set is interpreted under: an independent selection across orthogonal facets (formula fragment, model semantics, truth/inconsistency semantics, negation operators, closure, context, evolution, uncertainty, argumentation, revision, equality) plus two standing requests (resource policy, projection targets). The canonical form GMEOW reasons over; the historical named profiles are presets that expand to a full facet selection. Replaces the single monolithic semantic-profile axis: 'sound' is meaningless until the full contract is fixed."
msgstr "对某规则集所依据的推理语义的组合式规范：在多个正交面向（公式片段、模型语义、真值/不一致语义、否定算子、闭包、语境、演化、不确定性、论辩、修订、相等）上的独立选择，外加两项常设请求（资源策略、投影目标）。这是 GMEOW 所据以推理的规范形式；历史上的具名剖面只是展开为完整面向选择的预设。它取代了单一而整体的语义剖面轴：在完整契约被固定之前，「可靠」一词毫无意义。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ReasoningPreset|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A named ReasoningContract that fixes a common, supported facet selection — sugar the compiler expands to the full facet bundle before reasoning. The historical profile names (positive-Horn, stratified-negation, well-founded, stable-model, procedural, probabilistic) survive only as presets, not as indivisible alternatives."
msgstr "一个具名的 ReasoningContract，它固定了一种常见且受支持的面向选择——是编译器在推理之前展开为完整面向束的语法糖。历史上的剖面名称（positive-Horn、stratified-negation、well-founded、stable-model、procedural、probabilistic）仅作为预设留存，而非不可分割的备选项。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ReasoningProgramClauseConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Requires every declared logic:ReasoningProgram to carry at least one logic:clause. A program with no clauses has nothing to resolve its goal against and is malformed. It is not the query check: the required goal atom is validated separately by logic:ReasoningProgramQueryConstraint."
msgstr "要求每个已声明的 logic:ReasoningProgram 至少携带一条 logic:clause。没有任何子句的程序无从对其目标进行归结，因而格式不良。它不是查询检查：所需的目标原子由 logic:ReasoningProgramQueryConstraint 单独验证。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ReasoningProgramClauseConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A logic:ReasoningProgram with a logic:programQuery but no logic:clause violates this constraint."
msgstr "带有 logic:programQuery 但没有 logic:clause 的 logic:ReasoningProgram 违反此约束。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ReasoningProgramQueryConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Requires every declared logic:ReasoningProgram to carry a logic:programQuery. Paired with the owl:FunctionalProperty declaration on logic:programQuery (which caps it at one), it makes a program bear EXACTLY one goal atom. It is not the clause-set check: a program's facts and rules are validated separately by logic:ReasoningProgramClauseConstraint."
msgstr "要求每个已声明的 logic:ReasoningProgram 携带一个 logic:programQuery。与 logic:programQuery 上的 owl:FunctionalProperty 声明（将其上限限定为一个）相配合，使一个程序恰好携带一个目标原子。它不是子句集检查：程序的事实与规则由 logic:ReasoningProgramClauseConstraint 单独验证。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ReasoningProgramQueryConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A logic:ReasoningProgram with logic:clause facts but no logic:programQuery violates this constraint."
msgstr "带有 logic:clause 事实但没有 logic:programQuery 的 logic:ReasoningProgram 违反此约束。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ReasoningProgram|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A named clause set evaluated under a selected strategy: the authored surface that drives the native reasoning engine directly from slice content. A logic:ReasoningProgram carries a set of logic:clause atoms — facts and Horn rules, the SAME logic:Formula clause shape the forward relational-core lane already consumes, so there is no separate clause language — exactly one logic:programQuery goal atom whose logic:termVariable term-carriers are the answer variables the engine binds, zero or more logic:verdictProbe atoms whose three-valued well-founded verdict is projected independently of the query's bindings, and exactly one logic:evaluationMode selecting the evaluation strategy. 'Backward' resolution is a STRATEGY over a clause set, not a kind of program: keeping the mode a selector on a shared clause set, rather than splitting programs into forward and backward kinds, is what lets the SAME authored clauses later be evaluated forward once a chase strategy is added, without re-authoring."
msgstr "一个具名子句集，依据所选策略进行求值：即直接从切片内容驱动原生推理引擎的作者化界面。一个 logic:ReasoningProgram 携带一组 logic:clause 原子——事实与 Horn 规则，与前向关系核心通道已消费的 logic:Formula 子句形态完全相同，因此并不存在单独的子句语言——恰好一个 logic:programQuery 目标原子，其 logic:termVariable 词项载体即引擎所绑定的答案变量，零个或多个 logic:verdictProbe 原子，其三值良基裁决独立于查询绑定而被投影，以及恰好一个用于选定求值策略的 logic:evaluationMode。「后向」归结是施加于子句集之上的一种策略，而非一类程序：把模式保持为共享子句集上的选择器，而不是把程序拆分为前向与后向两类，正是这样才能让同一批作者化子句在日后加入 chase 策略后被前向求值，无需重新编写。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ReasoningProgram|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A program with two logic:clause facts, a rule concluding path(X,Z) from edge(X,Y) and path(Y,Z), one logic:programQuery path(a, V), and logic:evaluationMode logic:BackwardEvaluation resolves V by goal-directed SLG-WFS backward resolution over the clause set."
msgstr "一个包含两个 logic:clause 事实、一条由 edge(X,Y) 和 path(Y,Z) 推出 path(X,Z) 的规则、一个 logic:programQuery path(a, V) 以及 logic:evaluationMode logic:BackwardEvaluation 的程序，通过在子句集上进行目标导向的 SLG-WFS 后向求解来解出 V。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ReasoningResult|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The single shared result a reasoning run produces and every consumer reads (ME2): a compositional status carrying FIVE orthogonal fields, each ranging over its own value class — logic:resultInput (well-formedness), logic:resultEvaluation (what the engine could do), logic:resultCompleteness (relative to what the answer is complete), logic:resultPreservation (the set of answer-preservation polarities the lowering claims, plus the constructs it could not carry), and logic:resultInformation (the four-valued Belnap verdict plus two explicit non-results). Several fields hold at once. It additionally carries the provenance bundle: logic:contractHash, logic:query/logic:conclusion, logic:resultProof/logic:resultCounterproof, the world/standpoint/time/path context, logic:engine, logic:consumedBudget, logic:certifiedFragment, logic:contradictionWitness, and logic:resultAssumption. Authored canonically in crates/logic (Rust); this is a lossy documentation projection (Principle 17). Normative in design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md, §The reasoning result."
msgstr "一次推理运行所产生、并由每个消费者读取的唯一共享结果（ME2）：一个组合式状态，携带五个正交字段，各自在其自身的值类上取值——logic:resultInput（良构性）、logic:resultEvaluation（引擎所能做到的）、logic:resultCompleteness（相对于何者而言答案是完整的）、logic:resultPreservation（该下降所主张的答案保持极性集合，外加它无法承载的构造），以及 logic:resultInformation（四值 Belnap 裁决外加两种显式的非结果）。多个字段可同时成立。它另外携带来源信息束：logic:contractHash、logic:query/logic:conclusion、logic:resultProof/logic:resultCounterproof、世界/立场/时间/路径语境、logic:engine、logic:consumedBudget、logic:certifiedFragment、logic:contradictionWitness 以及 logic:resultAssumption。在 crates/logic（Rust）中规范化编写；此为有损的文档投影（原则 17）。规范见 design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md，§The reasoning result。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RecoveryCase|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A first-class executable query-class case that decides whether a logic:Correspondence genuinely recovers its source. Its logic:recoveryTransform is an ordered universally quantified source-to-view logic:Formula. The native correspondence executor instantiates the complete source pattern, computes the declared view, derives the candidate inverse, and compares the recovered source graph with the original. A recovery case is neutral evidence rather than a positive assertion: it may discharge a genuine section/retraction or deliberately refute a lossy mapping by retaining a source distinction absent from the view. Every logic:mnemomorphic true correspondence that claims logic:SectionLaw requires executable complete recovery evidence: an atomic one-triple leg may synthesize its complete case, while a composite leg requires an authored logic:RecoveryCase. A structural inverse or a declared boolean alone is never proof (design/LOGIC-CORRESPONDENCE.md, genuine recovery cases)."
msgstr "一个头等的、可执行的查询类案例，用以判定某个 logic:Correspondence 是否真正恢复其源。其 logic:recoveryTransform 是一个有序的、全称量化的、从源到视图的 logic:Formula。原生对应执行器实例化完整的源模式，计算所声明的视图，推导候选逆，并将恢复出的源图与原图相比较。恢复案例是中性证据，而非肯定性断言：它既可兑现一个真正的截面/收回，也可通过保留视图中缺失的某个源区分来蓄意驳斥一个有损映射。每一个主张 logic:SectionLaw 的 logic:mnemomorphic 真对应都需要可执行的完整恢复证据：一条仅含单个三元组的原子分支可综合出其完整案例，而复合分支则需要一份作者化的 logic:RecoveryCase。仅有结构性的逆或一个已声明的布尔值绝不构成证明（design/LOGIC-CORRESPONDENCE.md，genuine recovery cases）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/recoveryCase|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Correspondence to one of the logic:RecoveryCase nodes whose complete source pattern is executed to decide its source-recovery claim. Multi-valued and conjunctive: every attached case must recover for a mnemomorphic Section Law to discharge; one countermodel refutes the claim. A lossy correspondence may attach a refuting case so changing only its rung or logic:mnemomorphic flag cannot manufacture a proof. Domain logic:Correspondence, range logic:RecoveryCase."
msgstr "将一个 logic:Correspondence 关联到某个 logic:RecoveryCase 节点，其完整的源模式被执行以判定该对应的源恢复主张。多值且合取式：每一个附加的案例都必须成功恢复，一条记忆同态截面律方能兑现；单个反模型即可驳斥该主张。有损对应可附加一个用于反驳的案例，从而仅更改其等级或 logic:mnemomorphic 标志无法伪造出一份证明。定义域 logic:Correspondence，值域 logic:RecoveryCase。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/recoveryTransform|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The exactly-one ordered source-to-view logic:Formula executed for a logic:RecoveryCase. The supported discharge fragment is a universally quantified implication whose antecedent and consequent are positive conjunctions of binary RDF atoms: the antecedent is the complete source graph pattern and the consequent is the projected view pattern. The order is semantic — reversing the implication changes which information must be recovered — while conjunction order remains immaterial under the formula's canonical identity. Domain logic:RecoveryCase, range logic:Formula."
msgstr "为一个 logic:RecoveryCase 所执行的、恰好唯一的、有序的、从源到视图的 logic:Formula。受支持的兑现片段是一个全称量化的蕴涵，其前件与后件均为二元 RDF 原子的正合取：前件是完整的源图模式，后件是投影出的视图模式。次序具有语义——反转该蕴涵会改变必须恢复哪些信息——而在该公式的规范同一性之下，合取的次序仍无关紧要。定义域 logic:RecoveryCase，值域 logic:Formula。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/recoveryTransformValuesAreFormulae|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "For every recovery case and transform value, if the case is a logic:RecoveryCase and bears that value through logic:recoveryTransform, then the value is a logic:Formula. This canonical first-order axiom grounds the OWL all-values-from projection used by validation."
msgstr "对于每一个恢复案例及其变换取值，若该案例是一个 logic:RecoveryCase 且通过 logic:recoveryTransform 承载该取值，则该取值是一个 logic:Formula。这条规范的一阶公理为验证所采用的 OWL all-values-from 投影提供接地。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/reductionBasis|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReductionTheory to a property-value it treats as part-reducible: the theory holds that a whole bearing this property has it in virtue of its proper parts bearing it, so under that theory the property is an logic:Aggregate rather than an emergent one. The carrier that makes emergence theory-relative — a property in one theory's reduction basis and absent from another's receives opposite verdicts with no contradiction. Without a matching basis entry, a borne whole property is assessed logic:Emergent under the theory (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ReductionTheory 关联到它视为可部分还原的属性取值：该理论主张，承载此属性的整体之所以拥有它，是凭借其真部分对其的承载，因而在该理论之下此属性是一个 logic:Aggregate 而非涌现属性。它正是使涌现相对于理论的载体——一个属性在一种理论的还原基中、却不在另一种理论的还原基中，会得到相反的裁决而不产生矛盾。若缺少相匹配的基项，一项被承载的整体属性在该理论之下被评定为 logic:Emergent（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ReductionTheory|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A declared theory of part-whole reducibility, relative to which an logic:EmergenceAssessment is made. It carries, via logic:reductionBasis, the property-values it treats as part-reducible — reconstructible from the proper parts that bear them. Emergence is always relative to such a theory: the same whole property may be logic:Aggregate under one ReductionTheory and logic:Emergent under another, and an logic:Emergent verdict can be overturned by a later, stronger theory without contradiction precisely because the assessment records which theory it was relative to. The systems-theory analogue of a logic:MereologyProfile — it scopes the emergence calculus rather than asserting reducibility foundation-wide (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "一种已声明的部分-整体可还原性理论，某个 logic:EmergenceAssessment 相对于它而作出。它经由 logic:reductionBasis 承载其视为可部分还原的属性取值——可由承载它们的真部分重构。涌现始终相对于这样一种理论：同一整体属性在一种 ReductionTheory 之下可为 logic:Aggregate，而在另一种之下为 logic:Emergent，并且一个 logic:Emergent 裁决可被日后更强的理论推翻而不产生矛盾，恰恰因为该评定记录了它相对于哪一种理论。它是 logic:MereologyProfile 在系统论中的对应物——它为涌现演算划定范围，而非在整个基础层面断言可还原性（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/referenceFrame|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a measurement to the reference frame its logic:measuredValue is expressed in — the coordinate system, datum, unit system, or platform space that fixes what the value means. The frame leg of the true-quantity/measured-value seam (Principle 11: a value asserted without its frame is ill-formed); a logic:measuredValue with no logic:referenceFrame is the logic:MeasurementFrameMissing violation. The foundation-level seam predicate the domain property gmeow:referenceFrame grounds onto by sub-property, so a domain measurement lifts into the constraint's scope. Domain a measurement, range a reference frame (stated in prose, matching the module's convention)."
msgstr "将一次测量关联到其 logic:measuredValue 所表达于的参考系——即固定该值含义的坐标系、基准、单位制或平台空间。它是真量/测量值接缝的参考系分支（原则 11：一个不带其参考系而被断言的值是格式不良的）；缺少 logic:referenceFrame 的 logic:measuredValue 即构成 logic:MeasurementFrameMissing 违规。它是基础层面的接缝谓词，领域属性 gmeow:referenceFrame 经由子属性接地于其上，从而使一次领域测量提升进入该约束的范围。定义域为一次测量，值域为一个参考系（以散文形式给出，与模块惯例一致）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/refinesGoal|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a sub-gmeow:Goal to a coarser gmeow:Goal it makes precise. Domain gmeow:Goal, range gmeow:Goal (stated in prose). One of the four decomposition relations carrying satisfaction dependency, typed apart from gmeow:properPartOf (structural part-hood): a sub-goal may be both a proper part and refine its parent, yet part-hood alone does not express the refinement."
msgstr "将一个子 gmeow:Goal 关联到它所精确化的一个更粗粒度的 gmeow:Goal。定义域 gmeow:Goal，值域 gmeow:Goal（以散文形式给出）。它是携带满足依赖的四种分解关系之一，与 gmeow:properPartOf（结构性部分关系）分开定型：一个子目标既可以是真部分又可以精化其父目标，然而仅凭部分关系并不表达该精化。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/reflexiveProperty|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:connectedTo a logic:reflexiveProperty ."
msgstr "示例：ex:connectedTo a logic:reflexiveProperty ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/reflexiveProperty|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Reflexivity is a global semantic characteristic of the property over the interpretation domain."
msgstr "自反性是该属性在解释域上的一种全局语义特征。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RefutationAcceptanceWitness|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The acceptance record that a symmetric φ/¬φ conjecture test resolved to a refutation carrying a concrete contradiction witness, executed natively by gmeow_logic::conjecture::conjecture_test. It names, through logic:namesContradictionWitness, the logic:ContradictionWitness the refutation rests on. The flagship producer runs the native test and pins that a refutation case yields Some(witness) while a corroboration case yields None; this witness is the ontological twin the thin logic:RefutationAcceptanceWitnessShape gates."
msgstr "接受记录，证明一次对称的 φ/¬φ 猜想测试解析为一个携带具体矛盾见证的驳斥，由 gmeow_logic::conjecture::conjecture_test 原生执行。它经由 logic:namesContradictionWitness 命名该驳斥所依据的 logic:ContradictionWitness。旗舰生产者运行原生测试，并钉定驳斥情形产出 Some(witness) 而佐证情形产出 None；此见证即为轻量的 logic:RefutationAcceptanceWitnessShape 所把关的本体论孪生。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RelatedMatch|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The weakest positive relation: source and view are associated (curatorially relevant) but neither equivalent, subsuming nor reliably overlapping. Lowers to sssom:relatedMatch only; no logical alignment axiom is emitted. The floor of the positive lattice, above only the negative pole logic:Disjoint."
msgstr "最弱的正向关系：源与视图相关联（在编目意义上相关），但既不等价、也不包含、亦非可靠地重叠。仅下降为 sssom:relatedMatch；不发出任何逻辑对齐公理。它是正向格的底层，仅高于负向极点 logic:Disjoint。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RelationalCore|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logical-to-physical lowering waist of the correspondence calculus: a first-class Datalog±-with-stratified-negation sub-language (with aggregation and existentials — the chase) between the full-FOL logic: IR and the native execution engine. Every execution strategy, the incremental layer and the semiring annotation that carries the quantitative axes target this one dialect, so a get leg compiles to a join plan and a put / chase to a semi-naive fixpoint with existentials over the same core (design/LOGIC-CORRESPONDENCE.md and design/LOGIC-IR.md, the IR-commitments section)."
msgstr "对应演算中逻辑到物理的下降腰部：一个头等的 Datalog±-带分层否定的子语言（带聚合与存在量词——即 chase），位于完整 FOL 的 logic: IR 与原生执行引擎之间。每一种执行策略、增量层以及承载各定量轴的半环注解都以这一种方言为目标，因而一条 get 分支编译为连接计划，而一次 put / chase 编译为在同一核心之上带存在量词的半朴素不动点（design/LOGIC-CORRESPONDENCE.md 与 design/LOGIC-IR.md，the IR-commitments section）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RelationalCore|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A fixed-arity atom lowers to logic:instanceOf plus logic:naryArg0 through logic:naryArg2 before the native chase evaluates it."
msgstr "一个固定元数的原子在本地 chase 对其求值之前，降级为 logic:instanceOf 加上 logic:naryArg0 至 logic:naryArg2。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RelationshipType|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A logic:Type whose instances are relationships (relators or comparative relations): the type-level classifier of how two or more entities are related. The counterpart of gufo:RelationshipType; specialized by logic:MaterialRelationshipType (founded on a logic:Relator) and logic:ComparativeRelationshipType (grounded in the relata's qualities, with no relator). Stated in prose, not as a subclass edge."
msgstr "一个 logic:Type，其实例为关系（关系体或比较关系）：即在类型层面对两个或多个实体如何相关联进行分类的分类器。它是 gufo:RelationshipType 的对应物；由 logic:MaterialRelationshipType（奠基于一个 logic:Relator）与 logic:ComparativeRelationshipType（接地于关系项各自的质、无关系体）加以特化。以散文形式给出，而非作为子类边。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/relation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates an atomic-predication logic:Formula to the relation it predicates, over its ordered logic:argument terms. The relation is reified as a logic:Type individual per the HiLog reflection (see logic:instanceOf and logic:orderedType): predicating over a reified relation individual keeps the object level first-order rather than admitting a predicate variable, so no separate relation or predicate class is minted."
msgstr "将一个原子谓述的 logic:Formula 关联到它在其有序的 logic:argument 词项上所谓述的关系。依据 HiLog 反射，该关系被具体化为一个 logic:Type 个体（参见 logic:instanceOf 与 logic:orderedType）：在一个已具体化的关系个体上进行谓述，使对象层保持一阶，而不引入谓词变量，因此不会铸造出单独的关系类或谓词类。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/relation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "An atomic formula for ex:knows(alice,bob) carries ex:knows as its sole logic:relation."
msgstr "ex:knows(alice,bob) 的原子公式以 ex:knows 作为其唯一的 logic:relation。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Relator|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A truthmaker of a material relation: an objectified relationship — a marriage, an employment, an enrolment — that mediates two or more relata and existentially depends on each of them. A Relator must mediate at least two distinct entities (the relator-mediation discipline, RelComp); the relation it grounds holds in virtue of the Relator existing."
msgstr "一个物质关系的真值制造者：一个被对象化的关系——一场婚姻、一份雇佣、一次注册——它中介两个或更多的关系项，并在存在上依赖于其中每一个。一个关系体必须中介至少两个相异的实体（关系体中介纪律，RelComp）；它所奠基的关系凭借该关系体的存在而成立。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RelatumDistinctnessAssertion|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A central record asserting that, on a target class, two named roles must bind DISTINCT values on any one focus node — the mutual-inequality integrity condition of a relator whose relata must differ (a Commitment's committed agent and beneficiary, a Criterion's reward and penalty poles). It names the class with logic:distinctnessTarget and the two roles with logic:distinctnessRole, the triple the native coherence gate joins to raise a violation when the roles coincide, and carries a logic:formalizes back-reference to the domain property whose prose it encodes. The reasoning authority names and enforces it here; the domain slice keeps the OWL-facing role declarations."
msgstr "一条中心记录，断言在某个目标类上，两个具名角色在任一焦点节点上必须绑定相异的值——即一个其关系项必须不同的关系体的相互不等完整性条件（一个承诺的受托主体与受益者，一个准则的奖励极与惩罚极）。它以 logic:distinctnessTarget 命名该类，以 logic:distinctnessRole 命名这两个角色——原生一致性门在这个三元组上进行连接，以便在两角色重合时抛出违规——并携带一个 logic:formalizes 反向引用，指向它所编码其散文的领域属性。推理权威在此处命名并强制执行它；领域切片保留面向 OWL 的角色声明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RelComp|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The OntoUML RelComp anti-pattern: a concrete Relator must mediate at least two distinct entities. Mediation is read by entity count — a relator reaches two entities either through two distinct mediation roles, or through a single non-functional role (which connects two or more entities on its own). A concrete Relator (one with no logic: subclass to defer its mediations to) that reaches fewer than two entities — a single functional role, or none — violates it. The native foundation lowering enforces it over the whole ontology; the gUFO downcast is a lossy projection of it."
msgstr "OntoUML 的 RelComp 反模式：一个具体的关系体必须中介至少两个相异的实体。中介以实体计数来判读——一个关系体要么通过两个相异的中介角色、要么通过单一的非函数角色（其自身即连接两个或更多实体）来触及两个实体。一个触及少于两个实体的具体关系体（即没有 logic: 子类可将其中介推延过去者）——单一的函数角色，或一个都没有——即违反它。原生基础下降在整个本体上强制执行它；gUFO 向下转换是它的一个有损投影。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RepeatableReadIsolation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:IsolationLevel guarantee under which re-reads of an item a transaction has read return the same value — non-repeatable reads excluded, phantom rows still admitted."
msgstr "logic:IsolationLevel 保证，在其之下对一次事务已读取的条目再次读取会返回相同的值——排除不可重复读，仍允许幻影行。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/requires|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A required companion predicate of a logic:GuardedImplicationConstraint: when the guard holds, ∃ a value on this predicate is required. Multi-valued (a conjunction of existentials)."
msgstr "一个 logic:GuardedImplicationConstraint 的必需伴随谓词：当卫式成立时，本谓词上 ∃ 一个取值是必需的。多值（存在量词的合取）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/resourceExhausted|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A boolean marker on a resource that has been depleted: a resource flagged logic:resourceExhausted \"true\" is unavailable even where a state supplies it (logic:resourceSupply), so an action requiring it via logic:actionResource is gated. Domain a resource, range xsd:boolean (stated in prose). The depletion half of the representation-level resource facet, kept distinct from engine-budget exhaustion."
msgstr "施加于一个已被耗尽资源上的布尔标记：被标为 logic:resourceExhausted \"true\" 的资源即便在某状态提供它（logic:resourceSupply）之处也不可用，因而经由 logic:actionResource 需要它的一个动作会被门控。定义域为一个资源，值域为 xsd:boolean（以散文形式给出）。它是表征层资源面向的「耗尽」一半，与引擎预算耗尽保持区分。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ResourcePolicy|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The facet value class of the resource facet: the engine's execution discipline. It is a structured execution policy holding several independent properties together — whether a certified-complete, terminating fragment is required AND what budget or bound applies — not a single complete-vs-bounded toggle, and not a semantic selection. A contract may carry both a certified-fragment requirement and a budget at once."
msgstr "资源面向的面向值类：即引擎的执行纪律。它是一种结构化的执行策略，同时持有若干互相独立的属性——即是否需要一个经认证完备且可终止的片段，以及适用何种预算或界限——而非单一的完备与有界二选一开关，也非语义选择。一个契约可以同时携带一项认证片段要求与一份预算。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/resourcePolicy|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to the logic:ResourcePolicy it requests — the engine's execution discipline. A standing request, not a semantic selection; the resource policy holds several independent properties together (a certified-fragment requirement AND a budget), so a contract may carry both logic:CertifiedFragmentResource and logic:BudgetBoundedResource. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:ResourcePolicy (stated in prose, matching the module's convention)."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ReasoningContract 关联到它所请求的 logic:ResourcePolicy——即引擎的执行纪律。这是一项常设请求，而非语义选择；资源策略同时持有若干互相独立的属性（一项认证片段要求以及一份预算），因而一个契约可以同时携带 logic:CertifiedFragmentResource 与 logic:BudgetBoundedResource。定义域 logic:ReasoningContract，值域 logic:ResourcePolicy（以散文形式给出，与模块惯例一致）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/resourceSupply|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a state to a resource it supplies, recording resource availability at that state for the logic:actionResource facet. The native evaluator gates an action whose required logic:actionResource a state does not supply (or that is flagged logic:resourceExhausted). Domain a state, range the supplied resource (stated in prose). This is the representation-level resource seam to logic:competesForResource — it evaluates the represented resource facet only and is NOT a real build engine-lock."
msgstr "将一个状态关联到它所提供的一项资源，为 logic:actionResource 面向记录该状态处的资源可用性。原生求值器会门控这样一个动作：其所需的 logic:actionResource 未被某状态提供（或被标为 logic:resourceExhausted）。定义域为一个状态，值域为所提供的资源（以散文形式给出）。这是表征层通向 logic:competesForResource 的资源接缝——它仅评估被表征的资源面向，并非真正的构建引擎锁。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Restriction|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:memberRestriction a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty ex:member ; logic:someValuesFrom ex:Person ."
msgstr "示例：ex:memberRestriction a logic:Restriction ; logic:onProperty ex:member ; logic:someValuesFrom ex:Person ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Restriction|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "A restriction is a class expression in the canonical logic graph, even when projected as an OWL blank node."
msgstr "限制是规范逻辑图中的一个类表达式，即使被投影为 OWL 空白节点也是如此。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/resultAssumption|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A declared closure/identity/revision/witness-policy assumption a logic:ReasoningResult rests on (e.g. closed-world, unique-name, entrenchment-revision, skolem-witness) — MULTI-valued. Domain logic:ReasoningResult (stated in prose)."
msgstr "一个 logic:ReasoningResult 所依据的、已声明的闭包/同一性/修订/见证策略假设（例如封闭世界、唯一命名、根深度修订、skolem 见证）——多值。定义域 logic:ReasoningResult（以散文形式给出）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ResultAssurance|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A reified assessment that targets one logic:ReasoningResult (via logic:assuresResult) and reads its fields JOINTLY: logic:InfoSupported with logic:Incomplete is provisional, whereas logic:InfoSupported with logic:CompleteForFragment is conclusive within that fragment; a correctly returned logic:InfoBoth is high-assurance about a contradictory input, not a defect. A result assurance is DISTINCT from a reliability assessment of the reasoner: the former judges one result, the latter judges a series of runs (a logic:CognitiveAssessment). Authored canonically in crates/logic (Rust); lossy documentation projection (Principle 17). Normative in design/LOGIC-COGNITION.md."
msgstr "一个被具体化的评定，它针对一个 logic:ReasoningResult（经由 logic:assuresResult）并联合读取其各字段：logic:InfoSupported 配 logic:Incomplete 为暂定的，而 logic:InfoSupported 配 logic:CompleteForFragment 在该片段内为定论；一个被正确返回的 logic:InfoBoth 是对矛盾输入的高保证，而非缺陷。结果保证与推理器的可靠性评定相区分：前者裁断一个结果，后者裁断一系列运行（一个 logic:CognitiveAssessment）。在 crates/logic（Rust）中规范化编写；有损的文档投影（原则 17）。规范见 design/LOGIC-COGNITION.md。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ResultColumn|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "One typed column of a logic:ResultShape: a declared SELECT variable (logic:columnVariable), its term-kind (logic:columnTermKind, mandatory — an untyped column is the bag this contract eliminates), an optional pinned datatype for literal columns (logic:columnDatatype), and whether it is bound in every row (logic:columnBinding). Authored canonically in crates/logic (Rust); this is a lossy documentation projection (Principle 17)."
msgstr "一个 logic:ResultShape 的一个定型列：一个已声明的 SELECT 变量（logic:columnVariable）、其词项种类（logic:columnTermKind，必需——一个未定型的列正是本契约所消除的袋）、字面量列的一个可选的钉定数据类型（logic:columnDatatype），以及它是否在每一行中都被绑定（logic:columnBinding）。在 crates/logic（Rust）中规范化编写；此为有损的文档投影（原则 17）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/resultCompleteness|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningResult to the logic:CompletenessStatus of its answer. Single-valued. Domain logic:ReasoningResult, range logic:CompletenessStatus (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ReasoningResult 关联到其答案的 logic:CompletenessStatus。单值。定义域 logic:ReasoningResult，值域 logic:CompletenessStatus（以散文形式给出）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/resultCounterproof|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningResult to the derivation that proves the explicit negation of its conclusion (the same machinery as logic:resultProof), present iff the negation is derivable. A result carrying BOTH a proof and a counterproof is logic:InfoBoth. Domain logic:ReasoningResult (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ReasoningResult 关联到证明其结论的显式否定的那个推导（与 logic:resultProof 同一套机制），当且仅当该否定可推导时存在。一个同时携带证明与反证明的结果即为 logic:InfoBoth。定义域 logic:ReasoningResult（以散文形式给出）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/resultEvaluation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningResult to the logic:EvaluationStatus the engine reached (the computation axis). Single-valued. Domain logic:ReasoningResult, range logic:EvaluationStatus (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ReasoningResult 关联到引擎所达到的 logic:EvaluationStatus（计算轴）。单值。定义域 logic:ReasoningResult，值域 logic:EvaluationStatus（以散文形式给出）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/resultInformation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningResult to the logic:InformationState verdict about the queried proposition (the information axis). Single-valued. Domain logic:ReasoningResult, range logic:InformationState (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ReasoningResult 关联到关于被查询命题的 logic:InformationState 裁决（信息轴）。单值。定义域 logic:ReasoningResult，值域 logic:InformationState（以散文形式给出）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/resultInput|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningResult to the logic:InputStatus it received. Single-valued. Domain logic:ReasoningResult, range logic:InputStatus (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ReasoningResult 关联到它所接收的 logic:InputStatus。单值。定义域 logic:ReasoningResult，值域 logic:InputStatus（以散文形式给出）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/resultPreservation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningResult to each logic:PreservationKind polarity that co-holds for it — MULTI-valued, because the preservation field is a SET of polarities, not a single choice (logic:ValidationOnly is excluded; it names a lowering's purpose, not an answer-preservation polarity). Domain logic:ReasoningResult, range logic:PreservationKind (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ReasoningResult 关联到对它共同成立的每一个 logic:PreservationKind 极性——多值，因为保持字段是一个极性集合，而非单一选择（logic:ValidationOnly 被排除；它命名的是一个下降的目的，而非答案保持极性）。定义域 logic:ReasoningResult，值域 logic:PreservationKind（以散文形式给出）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/resultProof|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningResult to the derivation that proves its conclusion (a content-addressed handle into the explanation/proof tree), present iff the conclusion is derivable. Domain logic:ReasoningResult (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ReasoningResult 关联到证明其结论的那个推导（一个指向解释/证明树的内容寻址句柄），当且仅当该结论可推导时存在。定义域 logic:ReasoningResult（以散文形式给出）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/resultRowSchema|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningResult to the logic:ResultShape its bindings are contracted to — the row-schema facet of the typed result. Single-valued; absent for surfaces with no row schema (e.g. a pure DL-consistency verdict). The schema is the caller's DECLARED contract, validated against the bindings, never synthesised from them. Domain logic:ReasoningResult, range logic:ResultShape (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ReasoningResult 关联到其绑定所约定于的 logic:ResultShape——即定型结果的行模式面向。单值；对于没有行模式的界面（例如一个纯 DL 一致性裁决）则缺失。该模式是调用方所声明的契约，针对绑定进行验证，而绝不从绑定中综合得出。定义域 logic:ReasoningResult，值域 logic:ResultShape（以散文形式给出）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ResultShape|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A schema-level type contract on a SPARQL SELECT result set: the declared columns it carries (logic:declaresColumn) and the row-set cardinality (logic:shapeCardinality, with logic:shapeRowCount in count mode). The same construct types a query's expected INPUT (logic:expectsInputShape) and its guaranteed OUTPUT (logic:producesResultShape), so a query's input→output contract is checkable before execution. It generalises the test-DSL example-row idiom: an ExpectedRow is an example-instance of the ResultShape its competency question declares. Authored canonically in crates/logic (Rust); this is a lossy documentation projection (Principle 17). Normative in design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md, §The result row schema."
msgstr "一个施加于 SPARQL SELECT 结果集之上的模式层类型契约：它所携带的已声明列（logic:declaresColumn）以及行集基数（logic:shapeCardinality，在计数模式下配以 logic:shapeRowCount）。同一构造既为一个查询期望的输入（logic:expectsInputShape）定型，也为其被保证的输出（logic:producesResultShape）定型，因而一个查询的输入→输出契约在执行前即可检查。它推广了测试 DSL 的示例行惯用法：一个 ExpectedRow 是其胜任力问题所声明的 ResultShape 的一个示例实例。在 crates/logic（Rust）中规范化编写；此为有损的文档投影（原则 17）。规范见 design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md，§The result row schema。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/retiredByTransaction|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a retired support/reified assertion to the elementary update or transaction-path step that retired it. It is transition provenance: it explains why the support no longer holds in the successor state without deleting the support from the historical path."
msgstr "将一个被退役的支持/具体化断言关联到退役它的那个基本更新或事务路径步骤。它是转移来源信息：它解释了为何该支持在后继状态中不再成立，而不将该支持从历史路径中删除。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/reveals|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates the observation value an action schema names through logic:observation to the situation that executing the action reveals. The native evaluator surfaces the revealed situation in the materialized output so a policy can branch on it. Domain the logic:observation value, range the revealed logic:Situation (stated in prose). The reading half of the observation facet's seam to the cognitive layer (design/LOGIC-COGNITION.md)."
msgstr "将一个动作模式经由 logic:observation 命名的观测值关联到执行该动作所揭示的情形。原生求值器在物化输出中呈现被揭示的情形，以便策略能据此分支。定义域为 logic:observation 值，值域为被揭示的 logic:Situation（以散文形式给出）。它是观测面向通向认知层接缝的「读取」一半（design/LOGIC-COGNITION.md）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/reviewedBy|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:FormalizationCandidate to the reviewer decision that promoted it — a provenance/agent individual recording who reviewed it and when (range stated in prose, a reviewer provenance node, so the keystone gate is machine-auditable rather than trusting a free literal). Its presence is what a logic:CandidateAccepted candidate is checked against. Single-valued. Domain logic:FormalizationCandidate."
msgstr "将一个 logic:FormalizationCandidate 关联到晋升它的评审决定——一个来源/主体个体，记录谁在何时评审了它（值域以散文形式给出，一个评审者来源节点，从而使这一关键门可由机器审计，而非信任一个自由字面量）。它的存在正是一个 logic:CandidateAccepted 候选被据以核查者。单值。定义域 logic:FormalizationCandidate。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/reviewerLogicFoundation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The reviewer-decision provenance node the logic foundation records against an accepted logic:FormalizationCandidate: an auditable IRI (never a free literal) standing for the maintainer authority that adjudicated the prose-to-axiom promotion, so the reviewer gate is machine-checkable."
msgstr "逻辑基础针对一个被接受的 logic:FormalizationCandidate 所记录的评审决定来源节点：一个可审计的 IRI（绝非自由字面量），代表裁定散文到公理晋升的维护者权威，从而使评审门可由机器核查。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RevisionPolicy|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The facet value class of the revision facet: how a body of conclusions absorbs change. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract. Its individuals range from monotonic (nothing retracted) through entrenchment-ordered belief revision to truth-maintenance."
msgstr "修订面向的面向值类：即一批结论如何吸纳变化。在一个 ReasoningContract 上为单值。它的个体从单调（无任何撤回）经由按根深度排序的信念修订直至真值维护。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/revision|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to the logic:RevisionPolicy it selects — how change is absorbed. Single-valued on the contract. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:RevisionPolicy (stated in prose, matching the module's convention)."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ReasoningContract 关联到它所选定的 logic:RevisionPolicy——即变化如何被吸纳。在该契约上为单值。定义域 logic:ReasoningContract，值域 logic:RevisionPolicy（以散文形式给出，与模块惯例一致）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/rightOperand|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a binary transaction-program combinator (for example a logic:SerialConjunction) to its right/suffix operand — the program that holds over the suffix of the executing path. Range a transaction-program node (stated in prose). Paired with logic:leftOperand."
msgstr "将一个二元事务程序组合子（例如一个 logic:SerialConjunction）关联到其右/后缀操作数——即在执行路径的后缀上成立的那个程序。值域为一个事务程序节点（以散文形式给出）。与 logic:leftOperand 配对。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/rigidityViolation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates an individual to a rigid type it fails to persist as across worlds: the derived diagnostic of the positive cross-world rigidity discipline (the fourth OntoUML discipline, the one the type-only lint cannot express). For an individual x and a rigid type T, if x instantiates T in some world but still exists in another world where it is NOT typed T, a logic:rigidityViolation fact is entailed in that other world. Unlike logic:violation it is not produced by an in-world Datalog rule — rigidity quantifies over pairs of worlds and the chase is world-local, so it is evaluated by bounded closure over the finite materialized world set (LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md §Operational semantics). It is never asserted by hand; its presence is a machine-checkable proof that a rigid type's instantiation did not carry over to a world where the individual persists."
msgstr "将一个个体关联到它未能跨世界持续所属的一个刚性类型：即正向跨世界刚性纪律（第四条 OntoUML 纪律，也是纯类型静态检查无法表达的那一条）的派生诊断。对于一个个体 x 与一个刚性类型 T，若 x 在某个世界中实例化 T，却在另一个世界中仍然存在而不被定型为 T，则在那另一个世界中蕴涵出一个 logic:rigidityViolation 事实。与 logic:violation 不同，它并非由世界内的 Datalog 规则产生——刚性对成对的世界进行量化，而 chase 是世界局部的，因此它通过在有限的已物化世界集合上的有界闭包来求值（LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md §Operational semantics）。它绝不由人手断言；它的存在是一份可由机器核查的证明，表明某个刚性类型的实例化未能延续到该个体持续存在的一个世界。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/rigidlyAppliesTo|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a rigid type to the individuals it necessarily classifies: for every individual and every pair of worlds in which the individual exists, if it instantiates the type in one world it instantiates it in the other. The modal rigidity constraint; a Kind rigidly applies to its instances, an anti-rigid Role or Phase does not (the same constraint negated). Lowered to a universally quantified, world-indexed rule evaluated by closure over the finite materialized world set, needing no native modal operator."
msgstr "将一个刚性类型关联到它必然分类的那些个体：对于每一个个体以及该个体存在于其中的每一对世界，若它在一个世界中实例化该类型，则它在另一个世界中也实例化它。这是模态刚性约束；一个 Kind 刚性地应用于其实例，而一个反刚性的 Role 或 Phase 则不然（即同一约束的否定）。被下降为一条全称量化的、按世界索引的规则，通过在有限的已物化世界集合上的闭包来求值，无需任何原生模态算子。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RigidType|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A logic:Type that applies necessarily to each of its instances — in every world in which an instance exists it instantiates the type (logic:rigidlyAppliesTo holds for all its instances). The counterpart of gufo:RigidType; the meta-type whose instances are the rigid sorts: logic:Kind and logic:SubKind are each a logic:RigidType and a logic:Sortal, logic:Category is a logic:RigidType and a logic:NonSortal. Stated in prose, not as a subclass edge. Contrast logic:AntiRigidType."
msgstr "一个 logic:Type，它必然应用于其每一个实例——在实例存在的每一个世界中它都实例化该类型（logic:rigidlyAppliesTo 对其所有实例成立）。它是 gufo:RigidType 的对应物；是其实例为刚性种类的元类型：logic:Kind 与 logic:SubKind 各自既是一个 logic:RigidType 又是一个 logic:Sortal，logic:Category 既是一个 logic:RigidType 又是一个 logic:NonSortal。以散文形式给出，而非作为子类边。与 logic:AntiRigidType 相对照。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RiskAdvisory|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The semantic-risk class for a candidate with no entailment consequence at all — advisory content, the lightest review. Wire value `advisory`."
msgstr "针对完全没有任何蕴涵后果的候选的语义风险类别——咨询性内容，最轻量的评审。线上取值 `advisory`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RiskCoreContaminating|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The semantic-risk class for a candidate whose wrong formalization would corrupt the reasoned core — the highest risk, demanding the strictest review. Wire value `core-contaminating`."
msgstr "针对这样一种候选的语义风险类别：其错误的形式化会污损被推理的核心——最高的风险，要求最严格的评审。线上取值 `core-contaminating`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RiskProjectionOnly|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The semantic-risk class for a candidate whose blast radius is confined to a lossy projection surface, leaving the reasoned core intact. Wire value `projection-only`."
msgstr "针对这样一种候选的语义风险类别：其影响半径被限定在一个有损投影界面之内，使被推理的核心保持完好。线上取值 `projection-only`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/roleA|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The first role predicate of a logic:CrossNodeConstraint (paired with logic:roleB under logic:crossMode)."
msgstr "一个 logic:CrossNodeConstraint 的第一个角色谓词（在 logic:crossMode 之下与 logic:roleB 配对）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/roleB|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The second role predicate of a logic:CrossNodeConstraint (paired with logic:roleA under logic:crossMode)."
msgstr "logic:CrossNodeConstraint 的第二个角色谓词（依 logic:crossMode 与 logic:roleA 配对）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RoleCompositionExclusionAssertion|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A central record asserting that, on a target class, the value bound by a whole role must not also be — via any of a set of composition properties — the value bound by a part role on the same focus node: a relator whose one relatum composes the other is ill-formed (an argument does not attack its own component). It names the class with logic:compositionExclusionTarget, the whole and part roles with logic:compositionExclusionWhole and logic:compositionExclusionPart, and the composition steps with logic:compositionExclusionVia; the native coherence gate joins them to raise a violation. Carries a logic:formalizes back-reference to the domain property whose prose it encodes."
msgstr "一条中心记录，断言在某目标类上，由整体角色绑定的值不得同时——经由一组合成属性中的任意一个——成为在同一焦点节点上由部分角色绑定的值：某个关联子，其一个关联项合成了另一个，即为畸形（一个论证不攻击其自身的组成部分）。它用 logic:compositionExclusionTarget 命名该类，用 logic:compositionExclusionWhole 和 logic:compositionExclusionPart 命名整体角色与部分角色，用 logic:compositionExclusionVia 命名合成步骤；原生一致性门将它们连接以引发一次违规。携带一条 logic:formalizes 回引，指向其散文所编码的领域属性。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RoleMixin|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "An anti-rigid non-sortal that abstracts a relationally-acquired property shared across instances of several Kinds — customer (a person or an organization), insured party. Anti-rigid and identity-dispersive: a Role generalized to span multiple Kinds without supplying identity."
msgstr "一个反刚性的非分类共相，抽象出跨若干种类（Kind）实例所共享的、经关系获得的属性——顾客（一个人或一个组织）、被保险方。反刚性且身份弥散：一个被泛化以横跨多个种类而不提供身份的角色（Role）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Role|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "An anti-rigid sortal an instance falls under contingently, by virtue of a relation it bears to some other entity — student, employee, defendant. Anti-rigid: there is a world of existence in which the instance lacks the Role (the anti-rigidity witness). Identity-dependent on the underlying Kind; contrast Phase, whose change is intrinsic rather than relational."
msgstr "一个反刚性的分类共相，实例因其对某其他实体所持有的关系而偶然地归于其下——学生、雇员、被告。反刚性：存在一个实例缺乏该角色（Role）的存在世界（反刚性见证）。在身份上依赖于底层种类（Kind）；与相（Phase）相对照，后者的变化是内在的而非关系性的。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RowCardinality|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The closed value class of the logic:shapeCardinality facet: the row-set contract a result shape declares. Its individuals are logic:RowsExact (the declared example rows are the complete set), logic:RowsContains (the declared rows must all appear; extras permitted) and logic:RowsCount (only the count is pinned, via logic:shapeRowCount). The set is closed, so a misspelt value names no declared mode and is rejected."
msgstr "logic:shapeCardinality 侧面的封闭值类：结果形状所声明的行集合契约。其个体为 logic:RowsExact（所声明的示例行即为完整集合）、logic:RowsContains（所声明的行必须全部出现；允许额外行）以及 logic:RowsCount（仅经由 logic:shapeRowCount 固定计数）。该集合是封闭的，故拼写错误的值不命名任何已声明模式并被拒绝。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RowsContains|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:RowCardinality value requiring the declared example rows to all appear, with extra rows permitted. Wire value `contains`."
msgstr "logic:RowCardinality 的值，要求所声明的示例行全部出现，并允许额外行。传输值 `contains`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RowsCount|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:RowCardinality value pinning only the result row count (carried by logic:shapeRowCount), with no per-row content contract. Wire value `count`."
msgstr "logic:RowCardinality 的值，仅固定结果行计数（由 logic:shapeRowCount 携带），不含逐行内容契约。传输值 `count`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RowsExact|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:RowCardinality value pinning the declared example rows as the complete, exact result set. Wire value `exact`."
msgstr "logic:RowCardinality 的值，将所声明的示例行固定为完整、精确的结果集合。传输值 `exact`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleClusterRoot|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Emits gmeow:clusterRoot(root, root) whenever some finding gmeow:findingRootCause a root: the root-keyed cluster node carries its shared root once. Positive Horn (logic:PositiveHornProfile); monotone; materialized natively. The self-edge follows from identifying the cluster with its root finding — the cluster node (the root) names R exactly once, matching every member's gmeow:findingRootCause."
msgstr "每当某个发现项 gmeow:findingRootCause 一个根时，发出 gmeow:clusterRoot(root, root)：以根为键的簇节点一次性携带其共享的根。正型 Horn（logic:PositiveHornProfile）；单调；原生物化。该自环源于将簇与其根发现项相认同——簇节点（根）恰好一次命名 R，与每个成员的 gmeow:findingRootCause 相匹配。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleCrossNodeGlut|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Emits gmeow:crossNodeGlutWith(f1, f2) whenever two DISTINCT findings share one gmeow:findingAnchor that is a gmeow:NonTrivialAnchor, f1's gmeow:findingCategory has gmeow:categoryPolarity logic:InfoSupported, and f2's has logic:InfoOpposed: an opposing-polarity Belnap clash at one real source position, the cross-code coherence conflict the same-fingerprint merge (which keys on the code) cannot see. Positive Horn (logic:PositiveHornProfile) with a logic:distinctBody inequality guard (f1 ≠ f2) and the gmeow:NonTrivialAnchor guard that keeps it off the shared empty anchor of locationless findings; monotone; materialized natively (logic:ExactPreservation). Because the reified-Horn chase cannot mint a fresh witness node, the glut is carried as this directed edge (Supported → Opposed) rather than a minted gmeow:CrossNodeGlutWitness."
msgstr "每当两个不同（DISTINCT）的发现项共享一个作为 gmeow:NonTrivialAnchor 的 gmeow:findingAnchor，且 f1 的 gmeow:findingCategory 具有 gmeow:categoryPolarity logic:InfoSupported，而 f2 的具有 logic:InfoOpposed 时，发出 gmeow:crossNodeGlutWith(f1, f2)：在一个真实源位置上出现极性相反的 Belnap 冲突，即以代码为键的同指纹合并所无法看见的跨代码一致性冲突。正型 Horn（logic:PositiveHornProfile），带一个 logic:distinctBody 不等式守卫（f1 ≠ f2）以及使其避开无位置发现项之共享空锚的 gmeow:NonTrivialAnchor 守卫；单调；原生物化（logic:ExactPreservation）。由于具体化 Horn 追逐无法铸造一个新的见证节点，该 glut 以此有向边（Supported → Opposed）携带，而非一个被铸造的 gmeow:CrossNodeGlutWitness。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleFindingCluster|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Emits gmeow:findingCluster(finding, root) whenever a finding gmeow:findingRootCause a root: the finding's membership in the cluster keyed by that shared root. Positive Horn (logic:PositiveHornProfile) over the root-cause output (stratified above it); monotone; materialized natively. The cluster node is the root finding itself (fresh-node minting is not expressible in the reified-Horn chase), so gmeow:findingCluster points at the shared root, which logic:ruleFindingClusterType types gmeow:FindingCluster and logic:ruleClusterRoot links to itself."
msgstr "每当一个发现项 gmeow:findingRootCause 一个根时，发出 gmeow:findingCluster(finding, root)：该发现项在以那个共享根为键的簇中的成员资格。在根因输出之上的正型 Horn（logic:PositiveHornProfile）（分层于其上）；单调；原生物化。簇节点即根发现项本身（新节点铸造在具体化 Horn 追逐中不可表达），故 gmeow:findingCluster 指向共享根，logic:ruleFindingClusterType 将其类型化为 gmeow:FindingCluster，logic:ruleClusterRoot 将其连向自身。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleFindingClusterType|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Emits rdf:type(root, gmeow:FindingCluster) whenever some finding gmeow:findingRootCause a root: the root-keyed grouping node is a gmeow:FindingCluster. Positive Horn (logic:PositiveHornProfile); monotone; materialized natively. Types the shared root as the cluster it heads, so the readable 'N findings share root R' surface is a first-class typed node."
msgstr "每当某个发现项 gmeow:findingRootCause 一个根时，发出 rdf:type(root, gmeow:FindingCluster)：以根为键的分组节点是一个 gmeow:FindingCluster。正型 Horn（logic:PositiveHornProfile）；单调；原生物化。将共享根类型化为它所统领的簇，从而可读的『N 个发现项共享根 R』表层是一个头等的类型化节点。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleFindingHasAntecedent|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Emits the self-edge gmeow:findingHasAntecedent(finding, finding) whenever a finding gmeow:findingAntecedent anything: the positive one-place marker of a non-root finding, carried on a DEDICATED relation (not rdf:type). Positive Horn (logic:PositiveHornProfile); monotone; materialized natively. It exists so the stratified root-cause rule can express 'has no antecedent of its own' as a single negation-as-failure over gmeow:findingHasAntecedent — the marker settles in a lower stratum than the NAF that reads it. Its own relation (rather than rdf:type) is load-bearing: negating rdf:type would form a negative cycle with the downstream rules that derive rdf:type from gmeow:findingRootCause, breaking stratification."
msgstr "每当一个发现项 gmeow:findingAntecedent 任何东西时，发出自环 gmeow:findingHasAntecedent(finding, finding)：非根发现项的正型一元标记，承载于一条专用（DEDICATED）关系（非 rdf:type）上。正型 Horn（logic:PositiveHornProfile）；单调；原生物化。它存在，是为了让分层的根因规则能把『没有自身的前件』表达为对 gmeow:findingHasAntecedent 的单一失败即否定——该标记落定于比读取它的 NAF 更低的层。它自有的关系（而非 rdf:type）承重：否定 rdf:type 将与那些从 gmeow:findingRootCause 派生 rdf:type 的下游规则形成一个负环，破坏分层。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleFindingRootCause|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Emits gmeow:findingRootCause(finding, root) whenever a finding gmeow:findingTraces a root that is NOT a gmeow:findingHasAntecedent of itself — i.e. the finding reaches the root up the witness DAG and the root has no antecedent of its own. The negation-as-failure over gmeow:findingHasAntecedent makes this logic:StratifiedNAFProfile (the marker is derived in a lower stratum than this rule reads it); materialized natively (logic:ExactPreservation). Honestly the shared ROOT antecedent, not a lowest-common-dominator: it names a childless root the finding derives from, without claiming uniqueness."
msgstr "每当一个发现项 gmeow:findingTraces 一个并非其自身之 gmeow:findingHasAntecedent 的根时——即该发现项沿见证 DAG 向上到达该根，且该根没有自身的前件——发出 gmeow:findingRootCause(finding, root)。对 gmeow:findingHasAntecedent 的失败即否定使其成为 logic:StratifiedNAFProfile（该标记派生于比此规则读取它更低的层）；原生物化（logic:ExactPreservation）。诚实地为共享的根（ROOT）前件，而非最小公共支配者：它命名该发现项所派生自的一个无子女根，而不宣称唯一性。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleFindingTracesBase|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Emits gmeow:findingTraces(finding, antecedent) whenever a finding gmeow:findingAntecedent an antecedent: the base case of the transitive closure of the witness-DAG derivation edge. Positive Horn (logic:PositiveHornProfile); monotone; materialized natively (logic:ExactPreservation). Paired with logic:ruleFindingTracesStep, which closes it recursively up the chain."
msgstr "每当一个发现项 gmeow:findingAntecedent 一个前件时，发出 gmeow:findingTraces(finding, antecedent)：见证 DAG 派生边之传递闭包的基例。正型 Horn（logic:PositiveHornProfile）；单调；原生物化（logic:ExactPreservation）。与 logic:ruleFindingTracesStep 配对，后者沿链条递归地将其闭合。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleFindingTracesStep|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Emits gmeow:findingTraces(finding, root) whenever a finding gmeow:findingAntecedent an intermediate finding that gmeow:findingTraces the root: the recursive step that closes gmeow:findingTraces transitively up the witness DAG. Positive Horn (logic:PositiveHornProfile); monotone recursion the native chase settles to fixpoint; materialized natively (logic:ExactPreservation). Paired with logic:ruleFindingTracesBase."
msgstr "每当一个发现项 gmeow:findingAntecedent 一个中间发现项，而后者 gmeow:findingTraces 该根时，发出 gmeow:findingTraces(finding, root)：沿见证 DAG 向上将 gmeow:findingTraces 传递闭合的递归步骤。正型 Horn（logic:PositiveHornProfile）；原生追逐稳定至不动点的单调递归；原生物化（logic:ExactPreservation）。与 logic:ruleFindingTracesBase 配对。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleGateFatalVerdict|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Emits gmeow:findingGateVerdict(finding, gmeow:gateFatal) whenever a finding's gmeow:findingSeverity is gmeow:severityError, its gmeow:findingCategory's gmeow:categoryBlocking projection is gmeow:blockingBlocking, and its gmeow:findingStandpoint is gmeow:standpointBinding: the principal up-set ↑(Error, Blocking, Binding) of the truth ordering, the meet of three monotone axis-maps. The RDF-side derivation of the single Rust gmeow_errors::grade::gate() policy morphism. Positive Horn; monotone; materialized natively (logic:ExactPreservation). Because Fatal is reachable only from the top of all three axes, an advisory-standpoint or Coherent-category finding is structurally unable to be derived Fatal — the two never-gate theorems fall out of the up-set construction, not a special case."
msgstr "每当一个发现项的 gmeow:findingSeverity 为 gmeow:severityError、其 gmeow:findingCategory 的 gmeow:categoryBlocking 投影为 gmeow:blockingBlocking、且其 gmeow:findingStandpoint 为 gmeow:standpointBinding 时，发出 gmeow:findingGateVerdict(finding, gmeow:gateFatal)：真值序的主上集 ↑(Error, Blocking, Binding)，三个单调轴映射之交。单一 Rust 策略态射 gmeow_errors::grade::gate() 的 RDF 侧派生。正型 Horn；单调；原生物化（logic:ExactPreservation）。由于 Fatal 仅可从全部三个轴的顶端到达，一个咨询立场或 Coherent 类别的发现项在结构上无法被派生为 Fatal——两条永不设门的定理由上集构造导出，而非特例。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleIndirectContributor|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Emits gmeow:indirectContributor(entity, agent) whenever the entity gmeow:wasGeneratedBy an activity that gmeow:wasAssociatedWith the agent: the productive composition wasGeneratedBy ∘ wasAssociatedWith that surfaces the agents behind an entity's production. Positive Horn; monotone; materialized natively. It never derives gmeow:wasAttributedTo — indirect contribution is a reasoned consequence, not asserted direct responsibility."
msgstr "每当实体 gmeow:wasGeneratedBy 一个活动，而该活动 gmeow:wasAssociatedWith 该行动者时，发出 gmeow:indirectContributor(entity, agent)：产出式合成 wasGeneratedBy ∘ wasAssociatedWith，它使一个实体产出背后的行动者浮现。正型 Horn；单调；原生物化。它从不派生 gmeow:wasAttributedTo——间接贡献是经推理得出的后果，而非所断言的直接责任。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleInstantiatesWork|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Emits gmeow:instantiatesWork(item, work) whenever an Item gmeow:exemplifies a Manifestation that gmeow:embodies an Expression that gmeow:realizes the Work: the productive composition exemplifies ∘ embodies ∘ realizes that links a concrete copy directly to the abstract Work it carries. Positive Horn; monotone; materialized natively. The conjunction of all three R-relations means a broken spine (a missing tier) derives nothing."
msgstr "每当一个 Item gmeow:exemplifies 一个 Manifestation，后者 gmeow:embodies 一个 Expression，后者 gmeow:realizes 该 Work 时，发出 gmeow:instantiatesWork(item, work)：产出式合成 exemplifies ∘ embodies ∘ realizes，它把一份具体副本直接连向它所承载的抽象 Work。正型 Horn；单调；原生物化。三条 R 关系的合取意味着断裂的脊柱（缺失的一层）不派生任何东西。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RuleNoClosedWorldInCounterfactual|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The compatibility rule forbidding logic:ClosedWorldClosure — whether the contract's logic:defaultClosure or any per-key closure entry value — together with counterfactual entrenchment revision (logic:EntrenchmentRevision is the contract-internal indicator that counterfactual closest-world states are generated). The counterfactual states are open-ended, so reading absence as falsehood inside them is unsound; a contract that names both is unsupported. Authored canonically in crates/logic (Rust); this individual is a lossy documentation projection (Principle 17)."
msgstr "禁止 logic:ClosedWorldClosure——无论作为契约的 logic:defaultClosure 还是任何逐键闭包条目的值——与反事实固守修正（logic:EntrenchmentRevision 是契约内部指示反事实最近世界状态被生成的标志）并存的兼容性规则。反事实状态是开放式的，故在其内部把缺失读作虚假是不健全的；同时命名两者的契约不受支持。在 crates/logic（Rust）中规范撰写；此个体是一份有损的文档投影（原则 17）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RuleNoParaconsistentCounterfactualRevision|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The compatibility rule forbidding a paraconsistent valuation — a gap/glut-admitting logic:admissibleValuation (logic:AdmitAllFour, logic:ForbidGap, or logic:ForbidGlut) OR the logic:BelnapBilattice truth algebra — together with counterfactual entrenchment revision (logic:EntrenchmentRevision, the contract-internal indicator of counterfactual closest-world generation). The closest-world selection that generates the counterfactual states is not defined over gappy or glutty valuations; a contract that names both is unsupported. Authored canonically in crates/logic (Rust); this individual is a lossy documentation projection (Principle 17)."
msgstr "禁止一个亚一致赋值——一个容许 gap/glut 的 logic:admissibleValuation（logic:AdmitAllFour、logic:ForbidGap 或 logic:ForbidGlut）或 logic:BelnapBilattice 真值代数——与反事实固守修正（logic:EntrenchmentRevision，契约内部指示反事实最近世界生成的标志）并存的兼容性规则。生成反事实状态的最近世界选择在有裂隙或有过剩的赋值上没有定义；同时命名两者的契约不受支持。在 crates/logic（Rust）中规范撰写；此个体是一份有损的文档投影（原则 17）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RuleNoProbabilisticStableModel|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The compatibility rule forbidding logic:ProbabilisticMeasure in the uncertainty-measure set together with logic:StableModelSemantics as the model semantics. A calibrated probability mass is not well-defined over the multiple incomparable answer sets the stable-model semantics admits; a contract that names both is unsupported. Authored canonically in crates/logic (Rust); this individual is a lossy documentation projection (Principle 17)."
msgstr "禁止不确定性度量集合中的 logic:ProbabilisticMeasure 与作为模型语义的 logic:StableModelSemantics 并存的兼容性规则。一个校准过的概率质量在稳定模型语义所容许的多个不可比答案集上没有良定义；同时命名两者的契约不受支持。在 crates/logic（Rust）中规范撰写；此个体是一份有损的文档投影（原则 17）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleOrgMembershipPropagation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Emits gmeow:memberOf(agent, parent) whenever the agent gmeow:memberOf an organization that is gmeow:subOrganizationOf the parent: membership climbs the organizational part/whole hierarchy, so a department member is a member of the containing organization. Positive Horn and recursive on gmeow:memberOf — one rule carries membership up an arbitrarily deep nest of sub-organizations without needing gmeow:subOrganizationOf transitivity. Monotone; materialized natively. The native-chase form of the propagation the gmeow:memberOf owl:propertyChainAxiom ( gmeow:memberOf gmeow:subOrganizationOf ) expresses for the OWL 2 RL closure — the same inference in the logic: engine, not a divergent reading."
msgstr "每当行动者 gmeow:memberOf 一个组织，而该组织 gmeow:subOrganizationOf 该父级时，发出 gmeow:memberOf(agent, parent)：成员资格沿组织的部分/整体层级向上攀升，故一个部门成员即包含它的组织的成员。正型 Horn 且在 gmeow:memberOf 上递归——单一规则将成员资格向上带过任意深的子组织嵌套，而无需 gmeow:subOrganizationOf 的传递性。单调；原生物化。这是 gmeow:memberOf owl:propertyChainAxiom ( gmeow:memberOf gmeow:subOrganizationOf ) 为 OWL 2 RL 闭包所表达之传播的原生追逐形式——在 logic: 引擎中的同一推理，而非有分歧的解读。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RuleProbabilisticRequiresModel|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The graph-dependent compatibility rule requiring that whenever a contract carries logic:ProbabilisticMeasure, the source graph declares a logic:ProbabilityModel (via logic:probabilityModel or an individual typed logic:ProbabilityModel). Absent a declared model the contract is unsupported: a probabilistic measure is never inferred from confidence metadata and independence is never silently assumed. Because it inspects the surrounding graph it is enforced in the front-end rather than the contract-internal rule table; authored canonically in crates/logic (Rust), projected here lossily (Principle 17)."
msgstr "依赖于图的兼容性规则，要求每当契约携带 logic:ProbabilisticMeasure 时，源图声明一个 logic:ProbabilityModel（经由 logic:probabilityModel 或一个类型为 logic:ProbabilityModel 的个体）。在没有已声明模型的情况下，契约不受支持：概率度量从不从置信元数据推断，独立性也从不被无声地假定。由于它检视周围的图，它在前端而非契约内部规则表中强制执行；在 crates/logic（Rust）中规范撰写，在此有损地投影（原则 17）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleProjectHasMastered|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Emits gmeow:hasMastered only when BOTH a procedural-competence assessment and a transfer assessment of the same agent on the same subject clear their gmeow:hasMastered rows, where both rows belong to the SAME logic:LadderProjectionProfile. The two-row conjunction is why mastery of one narrow task no longer implies broad command — transfer must clear too — and the shared-profile join is why a procedural threshold from one profile can never be mixed with a transfer threshold from another. Positive Horn; thresholds read from the profile."
msgstr "仅当同一行动者在同一主题上的一次程序性能力评估与一次迁移评估都通过其 gmeow:hasMastered 行、且两行同属于同一个（SAME）logic:LadderProjectionProfile 时，才发出 gmeow:hasMastered。两行合取正是为何对一项狭窄任务的掌握不再蕴含宽广的驾驭能力——迁移也必须通过——而共享档案的连接正是为何来自一个档案的程序性阈值绝不能与来自另一个档案的迁移阈值相混。正型 Horn；阈值从档案读取。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleProjectIsAwareOf|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Emits gmeow:isAwareOf from an assessment whose dimension and level clear the gmeow:isAwareOf row of a logic:LadderProjectionProfile. Positive Horn; the threshold is read from the profile, not hard-coded."
msgstr "从一个其维度与层级通过 logic:LadderProjectionProfile 之 gmeow:isAwareOf 行的评估中发出 gmeow:isAwareOf。正型 Horn；阈值从档案读取，而非硬编码。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleProjectKnowsAbout|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Emits gmeow:knowsAbout from an assessment whose dimension and level clear the gmeow:knowsAbout row of a logic:LadderProjectionProfile. Positive Horn; the threshold is read from the profile. The canonical source of a gmeow:knowsAbout edge — never gmeow:hasSkill."
msgstr "从一个其维度与层级通过 logic:LadderProjectionProfile 之 gmeow:knowsAbout 行的评估中发出 gmeow:knowsAbout。正型 Horn；阈值从档案读取。一条 gmeow:knowsAbout 边的规范来源——绝非 gmeow:hasSkill。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleProjectUnderstands|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Emits gmeow:understands from an assessment whose dimension and level clear the gmeow:understands row of a logic:LadderProjectionProfile. Positive Horn; the threshold is read from the profile."
msgstr "从一个其维度与层级通过 logic:LadderProjectionProfile 之 gmeow:understands 行的评估中发出 gmeow:understands。正型 Horn；阈值从档案读取。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleRootFinding|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Emits rdf:type(root, gmeow:RootFinding) whenever some finding gmeow:findingRootCause a root: the childless root antecedent surfaced as a one-place marker. Positive Horn (logic:PositiveHornProfile) over the root-cause output (stratified above it); monotone; materialized natively (logic:ExactPreservation). Authored as the third member of the diagnostic meta-fold to demonstrate that a new meta-finding is added by tagging a rule gmeow:DiagnosticMetaRule — the reasoner discovers and runs it by TYPE, with no engine change."
msgstr "每当某个发现项 gmeow:findingRootCause 一个根时，发出 rdf:type(root, gmeow:RootFinding)：无子女的根前件作为一元标记浮现。在根因输出之上的正型 Horn（logic:PositiveHornProfile）（分层于其上）；单调；原生物化（logic:ExactPreservation）。作为诊断元折叠的第三个成员撰写，以示范只需给一条规则打上 gmeow:DiagnosticMetaRule 标签即可添加一个新的元发现项——推理器按类型（TYPE）发现并运行它，无需引擎改动。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleTenureClaimObservedFeature|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Emits gmeow:observedFeature(claim, position) whenever a gmeow:StandpointTenure gmeow:standpointClaim a claim and gmeow:tenurePosition a position: the tenure's held position becomes the observedFeature of its generated gmeow:StandpointClaim observation, so 'what is claimed' reads uniformly on the observation spine. Positive Horn; monotone; materialized natively."
msgstr "每当一个 gmeow:StandpointTenure gmeow:standpointClaim 一个主张并 gmeow:tenurePosition 一个立场时，发出 gmeow:observedFeature(claim, position)：该任期所持的立场成为其所生成的 gmeow:StandpointClaim 观测的 observedFeature，从而『所主张者为何』在观测脊柱上被统一读取。正型 Horn；单调；原生物化。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleTenureClaimVantage|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Emits gmeow:vantage(claim, standpoint) whenever a gmeow:StandpointTenure gmeow:standpointClaim a claim and gmeow:tenureStandpoint a standpoint: the tenure's frame becomes the vantage of its generated gmeow:StandpointClaim observation, so 'whose frame' reads uniformly across tenures and bare observations. Positive Horn; monotone; materialized natively."
msgstr "每当一个 gmeow:StandpointTenure gmeow:standpointClaim 一个主张并 gmeow:tenureStandpoint 一个视角时，发出 gmeow:vantage(claim, standpoint)：该任期的框架成为其所生成的 gmeow:StandpointClaim 观测的视点，从而『谁的框架』在各任期与裸观测之间被统一读取。正型 Horn；单调；原生物化。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/satisfactionDegree|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The quantity carried on a logic:GoalEvaluation for a goal met to a degree rather than crisply — how much of the goal is achieved. Domain logic:GoalEvaluation (stated in prose). The range is intentionally left open (no rdfs:range), matching the other quantitative axes (logic:confidence, logic:probability, logic:weight, logic:evidenceStrength): the value is a unit-interval decimal. DISTINCT from those uncertainty measures and from logic:objectiveValue and logic:utility — how much of the goal is met is never how sure the evaluator is, never the measure an optimization goal extremizes, and never how desirable the outcome is; none substitutes for another."
msgstr "承载于一个 logic:GoalEvaluation 上的量，用于按某种程度而非干脆达成的目标——目标被实现了多少。定义域 logic:GoalEvaluation（以散文陈述）。值域有意保持开放（无 rdfs:range），与其他定量轴（logic:confidence、logic:probability、logic:weight、logic:evidenceStrength）一致：其值为单位区间小数。与那些不确定性度量以及与 logic:objectiveValue 和 logic:utility 相区别——目标被达成了多少绝非评估者有多确信，绝非一个优化目标所极值化的度量，也绝非结果有多可欲；三者互不替代。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SatisfactionStatus|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The closed value class of the satisfaction axis of a logic:GoalEvaluation: to what extent the goal is met against the situation it is judged against. Its individuals are logic:Satisfied (fully met), logic:PartiallySatisfied (met in part — held apart from a low logic:confidence in a satisfied evaluation, which is a different question), logic:Violated (a maintenance or avoidance target has failed), and logic:Unsatisfied (not met, with no positive partial progress recorded). The set is closed; a misspelt value is rejected. Together with logic:GoalEvaluationCompleted, logic:Satisfied is the condition under which a gmeow:satisfiedBy edge is generated."
msgstr "一个 logic:GoalEvaluation 之满足轴的封闭值类：相对于目标所被判断的情境，目标被达成到何种程度。其个体为 logic:Satisfied（完全达成）、logic:PartiallySatisfied（部分达成——须与一次满足评估中较低的 logic:confidence 区分开，那是另一个问题）、logic:Violated（一个维持或规避目标已失败）以及 logic:Unsatisfied（未达成，且未记录任何正向的部分进展）。该集合是封闭的；拼写错误的值被拒绝。与 logic:GoalEvaluationCompleted 一起，logic:Satisfied 是生成一条 gmeow:satisfiedBy 边所依据的条件。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/satisfactionStatus|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:GoalEvaluation to the logic:SatisfactionStatus it carries — the satisfaction axis of the factored outcome. Domain logic:GoalEvaluation, range logic:SatisfactionStatus (stated in prose). Varies independently of feasibility, lifecycle, and goal-evaluation status."
msgstr "将一个 logic:GoalEvaluation 关联到它所携带的 logic:SatisfactionStatus——所分解结果的满足轴。定义域 logic:GoalEvaluation，值域 logic:SatisfactionStatus（以散文陈述）。独立于可行性、生命周期与目标评估状态而变化。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SatisfiedByBackedByEvaluationConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A closed-world integrity constraint: a conclusive gmeow:satisfiedBy edge is backed by a vantage-scoped logic:GoalEvaluation that evaluatesGoal this goal, was evaluatedAgainst the situation, and is Satisfied and completed."
msgstr "一条闭世界完整性约束：一条确定性的 gmeow:satisfiedBy 边由一个具有视点范围的 logic:GoalEvaluation 支撑，后者 evaluatesGoal 此目标、曾 evaluatedAgainst 该情境，且为 Satisfied 并已完成。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Satisfied|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:SatisfactionStatus value for a goal fully met against the situation it is judged against. Together with goal-evaluation status logic:GoalEvaluationCompleted it is the condition that generates a gmeow:satisfiedBy edge. Distinct from a high logic:confidence in a satisfied evaluation — how met is not how sure."
msgstr "logic:SatisfactionStatus 的值，用于相对于目标所被判断的情境完全达成的目标。与目标评估状态 logic:GoalEvaluationCompleted 一起，它是生成一条 gmeow:satisfiedBy 边的条件。与一次满足评估中较高的 logic:confidence 相区别——达成程度不是确信程度。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/satisfiesCriterion|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ConcurrentHistory to each logic:SerializabilityCriterion its witnessed schedule actually SATISFIES — the classification RESULT, as opposed to logic:serializabilityCriterion, which names the criterion the history is judged against. The native evaluator emits logic:ConflictSerializability when the logic:precedes conflict graph is acyclic and logic:ViewSerializability when the witnessed interleaving is view-equivalent to one of the two serial orders of its legs. Domain logic:ConcurrentHistory, range logic:SerializabilityCriterion (stated in prose); multi-valued. Because conflict-serializability is strictly stronger, a history that satisfies logic:ConflictSerializability always also satisfies logic:ViewSerializability; a conflict-CYCLIC history may satisfy logic:ViewSerializability alone. Absence of a criterion here is the honest record that the schedule does not satisfy it — the corresponding logic:SerializationAnomaly finding carries the violated criterion — never a silent linearization."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ConcurrentHistory 关联到其所见证的调度实际满足（SATISFIES）的每一个 logic:SerializabilityCriterion——分类的结果（RESULT），与 logic:serializabilityCriterion 相对，后者命名该历史所被判断依据的准则。当 logic:precedes 冲突图无环时，原生评估器发出 logic:ConflictSerializability；当所见证的交错与其各分支两种串行序之一视图等价时，发出 logic:ViewSerializability。定义域 logic:ConcurrentHistory，值域 logic:SerializabilityCriterion（以散文陈述）；多值。由于冲突可串行化严格更强，一个满足 logic:ConflictSerializability 的历史总是也满足 logic:ViewSerializability；一个冲突有环（CYCLIC）的历史可能仅满足 logic:ViewSerializability。此处某准则的缺席是调度不满足它的诚实记录——相应的 logic:SerializationAnomaly 发现项携带被违反的准则——绝非一次无声的线性化。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SecondOrder|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The expressiveness boundary of a defining statement that genuinely exceeds first-order logic — quantification over families/subsets or an appeal to finiteness (e.g. compactness's 'every open cover has a finite subcover'). Not authorable as a logic:Formula; carried in the loss ledger as an honest boundary with logic:preservationKind logic:Unsupported, never as a fake first-order formula."
msgstr "一个真正超出一阶逻辑的定义性陈述的表达力边界——对族/子集的量化，或对有限性的诉求（例如紧致性的『每个开覆盖都有有限子覆盖』）。不可作为 logic:Formula 撰写；作为一条诚实的边界携带于损失账本中，带 logic:preservationKind logic:Unsupported，绝不作为一个伪造的一阶公式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SectionAcceptanceWitness|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The acceptance record that a correspondence get/put leg pair discharges its section law (put ∘ get = identity), executed natively by gmeow_logic::correspondence_exec::leg_pair_verdict. It names, through logic:dischargesSectionObligation, the section obligation the executed round-trip discharges. The flagship producer runs the native discharge and pins that a genuine inverse yields DischargeVerdict::ObligationDischarged while a broken section does not; this witness is the ontological twin the thin logic:SectionAcceptanceWitnessShape gates."
msgstr "一份接受记录，证明一对对应的 get/put 分支履行其截面律（put ∘ get = 恒等），由 gmeow_logic::correspondence_exec::leg_pair_verdict 原生执行。它经由 logic:dischargesSectionObligation 命名所执行的往返所履行的截面义务。旗舰产出器运行原生履行，并钉定一个真正的逆产出 DischargeVerdict::ObligationDischarged，而破损的截面则不会；此见证是纤薄的 logic:SectionAcceptanceWitnessShape 所把关的本体论孪生体。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SectionLaw|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The perfect-subsumption law put ∘ get = id_S: the source is recovered exactly from its view because the in-band complement retained everything the retraction needs (a logic:mnemomorphic witness). Claimable only at the logic:SectionRetraction rung or above; the CI-checkable form of 'GMEOW perfectly subsumes this vocabulary.'"
msgstr "完美归摄律 put ∘ get = id_S：源恰好从其视图中被恢复，因为带内补量保留了收缩所需的一切（一个 logic:mnemomorphic 见证）。仅在 logic:SectionRetraction 阶或更高处可主张；『GMEOW 完美归摄此词汇表』的可 CI 检查形式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SectionObligationViolated|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The failure raised when a logic:SectionAcceptanceWitness — the acceptance record of a correspondence section-law discharge — names no logic:dischargesSectionObligation edge, i.e. claims a get/put leg pair round-trips without pointing at the section obligation it discharges. The section law (put ∘ get = identity) is the correspondence's teeth; a witness that discharges no obligation is unfalsifiable, so the gate rejects it (LOGIC-CORRESPONDENCE.md)."
msgstr "当一个 logic:SectionAcceptanceWitness——一次对应截面律履行的接受记录——不命名任何 logic:dischargesSectionObligation 边时，即在没有指向它所履行的截面义务的情况下声称一对 get/put 分支往返，所引发的失败。截面律（put ∘ get = 恒等）是对应的牙齿；一个不履行任何义务的见证是不可证伪的，故门将其拒绝（LOGIC-CORRESPONDENCE.md）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SectionRetraction|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Perfect subsumption: a split mono with put ∘ get = id_S and get ∘ put idempotent on V ⊕ complement. The source embeds losslessly into the view, the augmentation being S ∖ im(get) carried in the in-band complement. Caps: the section law (lossless source recovery), but not full bidirectional iso."
msgstr "完美归摄：一个分裂单态，满足 put ∘ get = id_S 且 get ∘ put 在 V ⊕ 补量上幂等。源无损地嵌入视图，其扩增为承载于带内补量中的 S ∖ im(get)。上限为：截面律（无损的源恢复），但非完整的双向同构。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/selectedBranch|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a policy to the branch the native evaluator selected because its logic:branchGuard matched the situation an earlier action's observation revealed (logic:reveals). Domain a policy, range the selected branch (stated in prose). The materialized record of an observation-conditioned policy decision."
msgstr "将一个策略关联到原生评估器所选择的分支，因为其 logic:branchGuard 匹配了较早一个动作的观测所揭示（logic:reveals）的情境。定义域为一个策略，值域为所选分支（以散文陈述）。一个由观测所条件化的策略决策的物化记录。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/selectedByEntrenchment|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:CounterfactualAcceptanceWitness to the outcome (an IRI) the entrenchment ranking deterministically selected when resolving the counterfactual antecedent. Domain logic:CounterfactualAcceptanceWitness (stated in prose). Its absence marks an unentrenched, arbitrary counterfactual: an outcome chosen without a recorded ordering is a silent guess."
msgstr "将一个 logic:CounterfactualAcceptanceWitness 关联到固守排序在解析反事实前件时确定性地选择的结果（一个 IRI）。定义域 logic:CounterfactualAcceptanceWitness（以散文陈述）。其缺席标示一个未固守的、任意的反事实：一个在没有已记录排序的情况下所选择的结果是一次无声的猜测。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/selfAssertiveBasis|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:HolonicAgencyProfile to a property-value that evidences the self-assertive (autonomy) tendency: the profile holds that a holon bearing this value (logic:bearsProperty) asserts itself as a whole — Koestler's self-assertive face. The carrier that makes autonomy profile-relative, the co-equal twin of logic:integrativeBasis (neither privileged, Principle 9). Without a borne self-assertive value a holon's autonomy face is not evidenced, contributing — together with the integrative face — to the logic:AgencyVerdict (logic:AutonomyDeficient or logic:HolonIntegral). The autonomy analogue of logic:reductionBasis and logic:activationBasis (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "将一个 logic:HolonicAgencyProfile 关联到一个见证自我肯定（自治）倾向的属性值：该档案主张一个持有此值（logic:bearsProperty）的完子作为一个整体肯定自身——Koestler 的自我肯定面向。使自治相对于档案的载体，logic:integrativeBasis 的对等孪生体（二者均不被优先，原则 9）。若无一个被承载的自我肯定值，一个完子的自治面向便未被见证，从而——与整合面向一起——贡献于 logic:AgencyVerdict（logic:AutonomyDeficient 或 logic:HolonIntegral）。logic:reductionBasis 与 logic:activationBasis 的自治类比物（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，类型化与语境化的部分论与完子章节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SemanticRiskClass|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The closed value class of the logic:candidateSemanticRisk facet: how far a wrong formalization of a candidate would propagate, which makes the reviewer gate proportionate. Its individuals are logic:RiskCoreContaminating, logic:RiskProjectionOnly and logic:RiskAdvisory. The set is closed, so a misspelt class names no declared value and is rejected (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, §Typed formalization governance)."
msgstr "logic:candidateSemanticRisk 侧面的封闭值类：一个候选项的错误形式化会传播多远，这使得评审者门与之相称。其个体为 logic:RiskCoreContaminating、logic:RiskProjectionOnly 与 logic:RiskAdvisory。该集合是封闭的，故拼写错误的类不命名任何已声明值并被拒绝（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，§Typed formalization governance）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SemiRigidType|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A logic:Type that is rigid for some of its instances and anti-rigid for others — logic:rigidlyAppliesTo holds for part of its extension and fails for the rest. The counterpart of gufo:SemiRigidType; its sole foundation instance is logic:Mixin (a logic:SemiRigidType and a logic:NonSortal). Stated in prose, not as a subclass edge. A logic:SemiRigidType is a logic:NonRigidType but not a logic:AntiRigidType (which requires contingency for every instance)."
msgstr "一个 logic:Type，对其某些实例是刚性的、对另一些是反刚性的——logic:rigidlyAppliesTo 对其外延的一部分成立而对其余部分失败。gufo:SemiRigidType 的对应物；其唯一的基础实例是 logic:Mixin（一个 logic:SemiRigidType 且一个 logic:NonSortal）。以散文陈述，而非作为一条子类边。一个 logic:SemiRigidType 是一个 logic:NonRigidType 但不是一个 logic:AntiRigidType（后者要求每个实例都具偶然性）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SequenceMarker|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A variadic argument placeholder (the Common Logic '…x' form) that binds a sequence of terms rather than a single term, generalizing the fixed arity-three atom to predications of any arity. A term-carrier argument whose value is a logic:termSequenceMarker denotes one; keeping it a distinct kind stops a single-term variable from being mistaken for a sequence one."
msgstr "一个可变元参数占位符（Common Logic 的 '…x' 形式），它绑定一个词项序列而非单个词项，将固定三元原子推广至任意元数的谓述。一个其值为 logic:termSequenceMarker 的词项载体参数指代一个这样的占位符；将其保持为一个独立种类，可防止单词项变量被误认为序列变量。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SequenceMarker|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:restCarrier logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termSequenceMarker \"rest\" ."
msgstr "示例：ex:restCarrier logic:termIndex 1 ; logic:termSequenceMarker \"rest\" ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SerialConjunction|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The serial-conjunction program combinator (⊗, 'do φ then ψ'): the path along which the program executes splits so that φ holds over a prefix and ψ holds over the remaining suffix. It is a PROGRAM combinator over the transaction layer's path semantics, typed APART from ordinary (at-a-state) logical conjunction — a program operator is never conflated with the logical connective that holds at a single state, matching the formula-versus-program operator typing of the IR. Its two operands are carried by logic:leftOperand (the prefix program) and logic:rightOperand (the suffix program). The base relations of the layer are elementary state transitions, this serial conjunction, and executional entailment."
msgstr "串行合取程序组合子（⊗，『先做 φ 再做 ψ』）：程序沿之执行的路径被拆分，使得 φ 在一个前缀上成立而 ψ 在其余后缀上成立。它是事务层路径语义之上的一个程序（PROGRAM）组合子，与普通的（处于单一状态的）逻辑合取分开（APART）类型化——一个程序算子绝不与在单一状态成立的逻辑联结词混同，与 IR 的公式对程序算子类型化相一致。它的两个操作数由 logic:leftOperand（前缀程序）与 logic:rightOperand（后缀程序）携带。该层的基关系是基本状态迁移、此串行合取以及执行性蕴涵。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SerializabilityCriterion|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A correctness property OF A HISTORY — not a protocol and not a guarantee strength. The closed value class of serializability criteria for a concurrent transaction history. Its individuals are logic:ConflictSerializability (an equivalent serial order exists reachable with no swap of conflicting operations) and logic:ViewSerializability (some serial order has the same read-from and final-write relationships). The set is closed; a misspelt value is rejected. This is one of three distinct, separately-declared concurrency concerns that must NOT be conflated: a logic:SerializabilityCriterion is a property of a history, a logic:IsolationLevel is a declared guarantee strength, and a logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol is an implementation mechanism — keeping them apart is required because they are not interchangeable and an implicit assumption about any one of them is a defect."
msgstr "一个历史（HISTORY）的正确性属性——既非协议，也非保证强度。一个并发事务历史的可串行化准则的封闭值类。其个体为 logic:ConflictSerializability（存在一个可在不交换冲突操作的情况下到达的等价串行序）与 logic:ViewSerializability（某个串行序具有相同的读自与最终写关系）。该集合是封闭的；拼写错误的值被拒绝。这是三个必须不（NOT）被混同的、各自分别声明的并发关切之一：一个 logic:SerializabilityCriterion 是历史的属性，一个 logic:IsolationLevel 是一个已声明的保证强度，而一个 logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol 是一个实现机制——将它们分开是必需的，因为它们不可互换，而对其中任一者的隐含假定都是一个缺陷。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/serializabilityCriterion|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ConcurrentHistory to the logic:SerializabilityCriterion its schedule is classified against — logic:ConflictSerializability (the default when none is stated) or logic:ViewSerializability. Domain logic:ConcurrentHistory, range logic:SerializabilityCriterion (stated in prose). This is the history-property dimension only: it is kept SEPARATE from logic:IsolationLevel (a declared guarantee strength) and logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol (an implementation mechanism), the two other concurrency concerns the layer never conflates. The criterion a detected anomaly violates is recorded on the finding through logic:violatedCriterion."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ConcurrentHistory 关联到其调度所被分类依据的 logic:SerializabilityCriterion——logic:ConflictSerializability（未陈述时的默认）或 logic:ViewSerializability。定义域 logic:ConcurrentHistory，值域 logic:SerializabilityCriterion（以散文陈述）。这仅是历史属性维度：它被与 logic:IsolationLevel（一个已声明的保证强度）和 logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol（一个实现机制）保持分开（SEPARATE），后二者是该层从不混同的另两个并发关切。一个被检测出的异常所违反的准则经由 logic:violatedCriterion 记录在发现项上。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SerializableIsolation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:IsolationLevel guarantee under which the schedule is equivalent to some serial execution of the committed transactions — full serializability. Strictly weaker than logic:OpacityIsolation, which additionally constrains aborted and in-flight transactions."
msgstr "logic:IsolationLevel 保证，在其下调度等价于已提交事务的某种串行执行——完整可串行化。严格弱于 logic:OpacityIsolation，后者另外约束已中止与在途的事务。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SerializationAnomaly|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A HISTORY-LEVEL finding: a pattern of conflicting operations, read-from edges, and happens-before arcs in a transaction history that admits no equivalent serial execution under the declared policy. Lost updates, write skew, and read/write anomalies are findings of this kind. It is DISTINCT from a contradiction witness (logic:contradictionWitness, which asserts ⊥ within a single state) and must NOT be modelled as one: the final state after a non-serializable schedule may be perfectly logically consistent while the schedule still has no equivalent serial execution, so a serialization anomaly is a property of the history, never a logical contradiction inside a state. It is surfaced as a finding with its dependency cycle or violated isolation level described; a non-serializable schedule is never silently linearized."
msgstr "一个历史级（HISTORY-LEVEL）发现项：事务历史中冲突操作、读自边与先于弧的一种模式，在已声明策略下不容许任何等价的串行执行。丢失更新、写偏斜以及读/写异常都是此类发现项。它与矛盾见证（logic:contradictionWitness，它在单一状态内断言 ⊥）相区别，且不得（NOT）被建模为矛盾见证：一个不可串行化调度之后的最终状态在逻辑上可能完全一致，而该调度仍无任何等价的串行执行，故一个串行化异常是历史的属性，绝非一个状态内部的逻辑矛盾。它作为一个发现项浮现，并描述其依赖环或被违反的隔离级别；一个不可串行化的调度绝不被无声地线性化。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/severity|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The severity a logic:Constraint violation reports at, as one of the SHACL local names 'Violation', 'Warning', or 'Info'. Absent means the SHACL default 'Violation'. Carried on the canonical constraint so the projected sh:SPARQLConstraint reproduces the authored sh:severity rather than re-deriving one."
msgstr "一个 logic:Constraint 违规所报告的严重度，为 SHACL 局部名 'Violation'、'Warning' 或 'Info' 之一。缺席即意味 SHACL 默认的 'Violation'。承载于规范约束上，从而所投影的 sh:SPARQLConstraint 复现所撰写的 sh:severity，而非重新派生一个。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/shapeCardinality|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ResultShape to the logic:RowCardinality it declares — the row-set contract. Single-valued. Domain logic:ResultShape, range logic:RowCardinality (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ResultShape 关联到它所声明的 logic:RowCardinality——行集合契约。单值。定义域 logic:ResultShape，值域 logic:RowCardinality（以散文陈述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/shapeRowCount|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The pinned result row count for a logic:ResultShape in logic:RowsCount mode. Single-valued, xsd:nonNegativeInteger. Domain logic:ResultShape (stated in prose)."
msgstr "logic:RowsCount 模式下一个 logic:ResultShape 的所固定结果行计数。单值，xsd:nonNegativeInteger。定义域 logic:ResultShape（以散文陈述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/sharpensTransitivity|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Asserts on the canonical carrier that gmeow:sharpens is transitive: the standpoint refinement order its skos:definition names (Standpoint Logic's coverage relation). The native coherence gate reads this to close the refinement order."
msgstr "在规范载体上断言 gmeow:sharpens 是传递的：其 skos:definition 所命名的立场精化序（立场逻辑的覆盖关系）。原生一致性门读取此断言以闭合该精化序。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SimilarityAnnotation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The external-relation annotation dimension for lexical, vector, or another explicitly declared similarity measure. It is a retrieval score, not epistemic confidence."
msgstr "用于词汇、向量或另一种明确声明的相似性度量的外部关系注解维度。它是一个检索得分，而非认知置信度。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/situationObtains|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a gmeow:State (a configuration along a logic:Path) to a logic:Situation type that obtains at it — the engine reads this to decide whether an atomic goal's logic:boundSituationType, or a conditional goal's logic:guardSituation, holds at a given state. Domain gmeow:State, range logic:Situation (stated in prose). It records that a situation type is realized at a state without mutating that state, mirroring the prose 'each gmeow:State realizes a logic:Situation' on logic:Path."
msgstr "将一个 gmeow:State（沿一个 logic:Path 的一种配置）关联到一个在其处成立的 logic:Situation 类型——引擎读取此关联以判定一个原子目标的 logic:boundSituationType，或一个条件目标的 logic:guardSituation，是否在给定状态成立。定义域 gmeow:State，值域 logic:Situation（以散文陈述）。它记录一个情境类型在某状态被实现，而不改变该状态，呼应 logic:Path 上的散文『每个 gmeow:State 实现一个 logic:Situation』。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Situation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A reified configuration of entities and their properties standing in a state of affairs at a time — the DOLCE Description-and-Situation sense: a snapshot of how things are that can satisfy a described state (a goal-world realized by a Situation). The static counterpart of the dynamic Event."
msgstr "一个实体及其属性的具体化配置，在某一时刻处于某种事态之中——DOLCE 描述与情境（Description-and-Situation）之义：事物如何存在的一个快照，可满足一个被描述的状态（一个由情境实现的目标世界）。动态事件（Event）的静态对应物。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/skillEvidenceForKnowsAbout|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The shipped declaration recasting expertise's former gmeow:hasSkill ⊑ gmeow:knowsAbout: possessing a skill in a subject is DEFEASIBLE evidence that the agent knows about it, not a strict subproperty entailment — tacit competence and descriptive, fact-level knowing-about come apart. The supported gmeow:knowsAbout edge is never materialized from gmeow:hasSkill under the default reasoning (its only shipped source is the declarative-familiarity ladder projection); a consumer opting into defeasible reasoning draws it, defeated when the competence is purely tacit."
msgstr "已交付的声明，将专业能力原有的 gmeow:hasSkill ⊑ gmeow:knowsAbout 重新表述：在某主题上具备技能构成智能体了解该主题的可废止证据，而非严格的子属性蕴涵——隐性胜任力与描述性的、事实层面的了解相互分离。在默认推理下，受支持的 gmeow:knowsAbout 边永远不会由 gmeow:hasSkill 物化（其唯一交付来源是声明式熟悉度阶梯投影）；选择启用可废止推理的消费者会推出该边，当胜任力纯属隐性时该边被击败。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SnapshotIsolation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:IsolationLevel guarantee under which a transaction reads from a consistent snapshot taken at its start — strong against most anomalies yet still admitting write skew, so strictly weaker than logic:SerializableIsolation."
msgstr "一种 logic:IsolationLevel 保证，事务在其中从启动时拍摄的一致性快照读取——对大多数异常具有较强防护，但仍容许写偏斜（write skew），因而严格弱于 logic:SerializableIsolation。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/someValuesFrom|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:parentRestriction logic:someValuesFrom ex:Person ."
msgstr "示例：ex:parentRestriction logic:someValuesFrom ex:Person ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/someValuesFrom|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The restriction entails the existence of at least one qualifying filler."
msgstr "该限制蕴涵至少存在一个符合条件的填充项。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Sortal|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A logic:Type that carries a principle of identity for its instances — it answers what counts as the same instance over time. The counterpart of gufo:Sortal; the meta-type whose instances are the identity-bearing sorts: logic:Kind (which supplies identity, via logic:suppliesIdentity), logic:SubKind, logic:Phase, and logic:Role (which inherit it). Stated in prose, not as a subclass edge. Contrast logic:NonSortal, which supplies no identity."
msgstr "一种为其实例携带同一性原则的 logic:Type——它回答什么算作跨时间的同一实例。它是 gufo:Sortal 的对应物；其实例为携带同一性的种类的元类型：logic:Kind（经由 logic:suppliesIdentity 供给同一性）、logic:SubKind、logic:Phase 与 logic:Role（后者继承之）。以散文陈述，而非作为子类边。与不供给任何同一性的 logic:NonSortal 相对照。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SoundUnderApproximation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Anything the projection entails is canonically valid, but the projection may miss canonical answers: sound but incomplete. The projection never overclaims a derivation; it may under-derive."
msgstr "投影所蕴涵的任何内容都是规范有效的，但投影可能遗漏规范答案：可靠但不完备。投影从不对推导过度声称；它可能推导不足。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/sourceDimension|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:AssessmentDimension a logic:DimensionThreshold row reads: the factored axis whose assessment level is tested against the row's logic:thresholdLevel. Range logic:AssessmentDimension (stated in prose)."
msgstr "某一 logic:DimensionThreshold 行所读取的 logic:AssessmentDimension：其评估级别与该行 logic:thresholdLevel 相比较的被因子化的轴。值域为 logic:AssessmentDimension（以散文陈述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/sourceEndpoint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:bridge logic:sourceEndpoint logic:Restriction ."
msgstr "示例：ex:bridge logic:sourceEndpoint logic:Restriction ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/sourceEndpoint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "For external grounding bridges the source endpoint is always in lang:, math:, or logic:."
msgstr "对于外部接地桥，源端点始终位于 lang:、math: 或 logic: 之中。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/sparqlTarget|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:focusGuard logic:sparqlTarget ex:focus, \"SELECT ?this WHERE { ?this ex:reviewed true }\" ."
msgstr "示例：ex:focusGuard logic:sparqlTarget ex:focus, \"SELECT ?this WHERE { ?this ex:reviewed true }\" ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/sparqlTarget|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The SELECT text defines focus selection only and is removed from the projected violation condition."
msgstr "SELECT 文本仅定义焦点选择，并会从投影出的违规条件中移除。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/StableModelProfile|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Answer-set / stable-model semantics: a program may have several stable models (possibly none), and entailment is over those models. NP-hard in the worst case; the profile that admits genuine non-determinism and disjunctive reasoning."
msgstr "回答集／稳定模型语义：一个程序可能拥有若干稳定模型（也可能没有），蕴涵则遍及这些模型。最坏情况下为 NP 困难；这是容许真正非确定性与析取推理的配置。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/StableModelSemantics|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The model-semantics facet value selecting answer-set (stable-model) semantics: a program may have several stable models, or none, and entailment is taken over that model set. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract; the non-deterministic, NP-hard semantics for unstratified negation, contrasted with the unique well-founded model and the unique least model."
msgstr "选择回答集（稳定模型）语义的 model-semantics 面值：一个程序可能拥有若干稳定模型或一个也没有，蕴涵取自该模型集合。在 ReasoningContract 上取单值；用于非分层否定的非确定性、NP 困难语义，与唯一的良基模型及唯一的最小模型相对照。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/StandpointContextAxis|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The standpoint index axis of the multi-dimensional context facet: a truth is relative to a standpoint (a perspective in the sharpening poset). One of several context axes that coexist on a single result — world, standpoint, time, and path index the same result simultaneously rather than being alternative values of one slot."
msgstr "多维上下文面的立场索引轴：真理相对于某一立场（锐化偏序集中的一个视角）。它是共存于单一结果之上的若干上下文轴之一——世界、立场、时间与路径同时索引同一结果，而非作为单一槽位的可替换取值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/StateTransitionEvolution|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The evolution-facet value under which state changes across discrete transitions between successive states, each a configuration reasoned over in turn. The state-change mode between the static default and the full transaction-path semantics; independent of the model-semantics facet."
msgstr "一种 evolution 面值，状态在其中通过相继状态之间的离散转移而改变，每个状态都是被依次推理的一种配置。它是介于静态默认与完整事务路径语义之间的状态变更模式；独立于 model-semantics 面。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/StaticEvolution|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The evolution-facet value under which no state change occurs — reasoning is over a single, degenerate one-state path. The default evolution mode; contrast logic:StateTransitionEvolution and logic:TransactionPathEvolution."
msgstr "一种 evolution 面值，其中不发生任何状态变更——推理遍及单一的、退化的单状态路径。它是默认的演化模式；与 logic:StateTransitionEvolution 及 logic:TransactionPathEvolution 相对照。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/StereotypeCardinality|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The discipline that every class carries exactly one stereotype: a class with no meta-class pun, or with two or more distinct meta-class puns, violates it. The lowering of reasoning_lint.exactly_one_stereotype — the precondition every other discipline assumes."
msgstr "要求每个类恰好携带一个构造型的纪律：没有元类双关、或带有两个及以上相异元类双关的类，均违反之。它是 reasoning_lint.exactly_one_stereotype 的下降——其他每一项纪律都预设的前置条件。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/StratifiedNAFProfile|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Negation-as-failure under stratification: a unique perfect model with PTIME data complexity, where negated literals are evaluated only over strata already settled. Adds well-behaved negation without the multiple models of the stable-model semantics."
msgstr "分层下的失败即否定：具有 PTIME 数据复杂度的唯一完美模型，其中被否定的文字仅在已确定的层上求值。它加入了行为良好的否定，而不产生稳定模型语义那样的多重模型。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/StrictTwoPhaseLocking|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol that holds all EXCLUSIVE (write) locks until the transaction commits or aborts, preventing cascading aborts on writes. Contrast logic:StrongStrictTwoPhaseLocking, which additionally holds shared (read) locks to commit."
msgstr "一种 logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol，持有所有排他（写）锁直至事务提交或中止，从而防止写操作上的级联中止。与 logic:StrongStrictTwoPhaseLocking 相对照，后者还额外持有共享（读）锁直至提交。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/StrongCyclicPlanSuccess|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:PlanSuccessMode value under which a plan succeeds when every FAIR execution is guaranteed to reach the goal in finitely many steps, allowing retried loops through recoverable failures — the reading that tolerates cyclic recovery a strong plan forbids while still guaranteeing eventual success a weak plan does not. Between logic:WeakPlanSuccess and logic:StrongPlanSuccess in strength."
msgstr "一种 logic:PlanSuccessMode 取值，当每次公平执行都保证在有限步内到达目标时该计划即成功，允许经由可恢复失败的重试循环——这种解读容忍强计划所禁止的循环恢复，同时仍保证弱计划所不保证的最终成功。其强度介于 logic:WeakPlanSuccess 与 logic:StrongPlanSuccess 之间。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/StrongNegation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The residue shape tag for a formula in which strong (explicit, classical) negation (logic:not) appears — distinct from negation-as-failure, which a Horn rule body already carries. Disclosed when a Horn-fragment target carries such a formula as flagged unsupported residue."
msgstr "用于标记出现强（显式、经典）否定（logic:not）的公式的残余形状标签——区别于 Horn 规则体已经承载的失败即否定。当某个 Horn 片段目标承载这样一条公式并作为被标记的、不受支持的残余时予以披露。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/StrongPlanSuccess|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:PlanSuccessMode value under which a plan succeeds when EVERY outcome path reaches the goal — the universal reading, guaranteeing the goal regardless of how nondeterminism resolves. Contrast logic:WeakPlanSuccess (some path) and logic:StrongCyclicPlanSuccess (every fair execution, allowing retried loops)."
msgstr "一种 logic:PlanSuccessMode 取值，当每一条结果路径都到达目标时该计划即成功——全称解读，无论非确定性如何消解都保证达成目标。与 logic:WeakPlanSuccess（某条路径）及 logic:StrongCyclicPlanSuccess（每次公平执行，允许重试循环）相对照。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/StrongStrictTwoPhaseLocking|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol that holds ALL locks — both shared (read) and exclusive (write) — until commit or abort, yielding the strongest, strictest two-phase-locking discipline. The strong-strict variant the design names distinctly from the strict variant (logic:StrictTwoPhaseLocking), which releases shared locks earlier."
msgstr "一种 logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol，持有全部锁——共享（读）与排他（写）皆然——直至提交或中止，从而产生最强、最严格的两阶段锁定纪律。这是设计中与严格变体（logic:StrictTwoPhaseLocking）明确区分命名的强严格变体，后者较早释放共享锁。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/subClassOf|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:Cat logic:subClassOf ex:Animal ."
msgstr "示例：ex:Cat logic:subClassOf ex:Animal ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/subClassOf|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The edge carries extensional implication from subject class to object class."
msgstr "该边承载从主语类到宾语类的外延蕴涵。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/subEventOfTransitivity|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Asserts on the canonical carrier that gmeow:subEventOf is transitive: a part of a part is a part — the reading its own skos:definition commits to (CIDOC-CRM P9). The native coherence gate reads this to close the sub-event relation."
msgstr "在规范载体上断言 gmeow:subEventOf 是传递的：部分的部分即是部分——这是其自身 skos:definition 所承诺的解读（CIDOC-CRM P9）。原生一致性关卡读取此项以闭合子事件关系。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SubjectGranularity|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The value-vocabulary class of the grain of a logic:CognitiveAssessment's subject, named via logic:subjectGranularity: a single inference, a body of reasoning, a domain of competence, or the reasoner as a whole. An OPEN value vocabulary (individuals, never subclasses), since competence is judged at different grains and a new grain is a new individual."
msgstr "某 logic:CognitiveAssessment 主体之粒度的值词汇类，经由 logic:subjectGranularity 命名：单次推理、一整套推理、一个胜任力领域，或整体的推理者。这是一个开放的值词汇（个体，绝非子类），因为胜任力在不同粒度上被判定，且一个新粒度即是一个新个体。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/subjectGranularity|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:CognitiveAssessment to the logic:SubjectGranularity individual recording the grain of its logic:assessmentSubject (inference, body-of-reasoning, domain, or agent). Range logic:SubjectGranularity (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将某 logic:CognitiveAssessment 关联到记录其 logic:assessmentSubject 之粒度（推理、一整套推理、领域或智能体）的 logic:SubjectGranularity 个体。值域为 logic:SubjectGranularity（以散文陈述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SubKind|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A rigid sortal that specializes a Kind without supplying its own independent principle of identity: it carries the identity criterion inherited from the Kind it specializes. Rigid like a Kind, but identity-dependent rather than identity-supplying."
msgstr "一种刚性 sortal，它特化某个 Kind 而不供给自身独立的同一性原则：它携带从所特化的 Kind 继承而来的同一性判据。像 Kind 一样刚性，但依赖同一性而非供给同一性。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/subPropertyOf|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:biologicalParentOf logic:subPropertyOf ex:parentOf ."
msgstr "示例：ex:biologicalParentOf logic:subPropertyOf ex:parentOf ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/subPropertyOf|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Every subject-object pair in the narrower relation is entailed in the broader relation."
msgstr "较窄关系中的每一个主语-宾语对都在较宽关系中被蕴涵。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Substantial|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "An endurant that does NOT inhere in another individual: an independent bearer that can exist on its own and onto which aspects inhere. The complement of logic:Aspect within the endurant category; every logic:Object is a Substantial (stated in prose, not as a subclass edge)."
msgstr "一种不寓于另一个体的续存物：一个能够自行存在、并且诸方面寓于其上的独立承载者。它是续存物范畴内 logic:Aspect 的补；每个 logic:Object 都是 Substantial（以散文陈述，而非作为子类边）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SubsumedBy|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The source pattern is narrower than the view: every source instance is a view instance but not conversely. Lowers to sssom:narrowMatch and an owl:subClassOf with the source as the subclass. The converse direction of logic:Subsumes, the second mid-lattice relation under logic:Equiv."
msgstr "源模式比视图更窄：每个源实例都是视图实例，反之则不然。下降为 sssom:narrowMatch 以及一条以源为子类的 owl:subClassOf。它是 logic:Subsumes 的相反方向，是 logic:Equiv 之下第二条格中层关系。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Subsumes|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The source pattern is broader than the view: every view instance is a source instance but not conversely. Lowers to sssom:broadMatch and an owl:subClassOf with the view as the subclass. One of the two mid-lattice directional relations under logic:Equiv."
msgstr "源模式比视图更宽：每个视图实例都是源实例，反之则不然。下降为 sssom:broadMatch 以及一条以视图为子类的 owl:subClassOf。它是 logic:Equiv 之下两条格中层有向关系之一。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/sufficientFor|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a sub-gmeow:Goal whose satisfaction settles a gmeow:Goal on its own. Domain gmeow:Goal, range gmeow:Goal (stated in prose). The relation an logic:OrDecomposition groups: any one sufficient sub-goal settles the parent. One of the four decomposition relations carrying satisfaction dependency, distinct from gmeow:properPartOf (structural part-hood)."
msgstr "关联一个子 gmeow:Goal，其满足即可独自了结某个 gmeow:Goal。定义域为 gmeow:Goal，值域为 gmeow:Goal（以散文陈述）。这是 logic:OrDecomposition 所归组的关系：任一充分子目标即可了结其父目标。它是承载满足依赖的四种分解关系之一，区别于 gmeow:properPartOf（结构性部分论）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/summarizesResult|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a coherence outcome (logic:CoherenceCertificate or logic:CoherenceCheckAttestation) to the single logic:ReasoningResult whose completion status, contract (logic:contractHash), certified fragment (logic:certifiedFragment), consumed budget (logic:consumedBudget), assumptions (logic:resultAssumption) and preservation losses it certifies over. The completeness gate (certificate vs attestation) reads this result's logic:resultEvaluation and logic:resultCompleteness. Single-valued. Domain logic:CoherenceCertificate or logic:CoherenceCheckAttestation, range logic:ReasoningResult (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将某一致性结果（logic:CoherenceCertificate 或 logic:CoherenceCheckAttestation）关联到它据以认证的单个 logic:ReasoningResult——其完成状态、合约（logic:contractHash）、被认证片段（logic:certifiedFragment）、已消耗预算（logic:consumedBudget）、假设（logic:resultAssumption）以及保持损失。完备性关卡（证书对证明）读取该结果的 logic:resultEvaluation 与 logic:resultCompleteness。取单值。定义域为 logic:CoherenceCertificate 或 logic:CoherenceCheckAttestation，值域为 logic:ReasoningResult（以散文陈述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/supersededBy|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a retired support/reified assertion version to the update or successor support that supersedes it in the append-only store. It is the missing counterpart that, together with logic:activeInState, logic:validUntilState, and logic:retiredByTransaction, makes every `del` a supersession rather than an erasure: the retired version is never removed, it is recorded as superseded by the version that took its place. The substrate therefore stays monotonic and append-only — a superseded assertion remains recoverable, and the supersession chain reconstructs the full history of what replaced what. Suppression-not-erasure: `del` removes a support, it does not destroy the historical record. Domain a retired support/reified assertion version, range the superseding update or successor support (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将一个已退役的支持／具体化断言版本关联到在仅追加存储中取代它的更新或后继支持。它是缺失的对应物，与 logic:activeInState、logic:validUntilState 及 logic:retiredByTransaction 一同，使每一次 `del` 成为取代而非抹除：已退役的版本从不被移除，而是被记录为已被取而代之的版本所取代。因此底层保持单调且仅追加——被取代的断言仍可恢复，取代链重建何者替换何者的完整历史。抑制而非抹除：`del` 移除一个支持，它并不摧毁历史记录。定义域为已退役的支持／具体化断言版本，值域为取代性更新或后继支持（以散文陈述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/supersededTerm|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a supersession logic:Correspondence to the old term it records as superseded — the source endpoint of a greenfield migration crossing (e.g. a removed class or property the correspondence maps onto its replacement at a rung). Names the endpoint so the supersession ledger is queryable by the migrated-from term. Domain logic:Correspondence, range any term (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将一个取代性的 logic:Correspondence 关联到它记录为被取代的旧词项——greenfield 迁移交叉的源端点（例如一个被移除的类或属性，对应关系在某一档级上将其映射到其替代物）。为端点命名，使取代账本可按迁移来源词项查询。定义域为 logic:Correspondence，值域为任意词项（以散文陈述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/supersedingTerm|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a supersession logic:Correspondence to the replacement term it records as superseding the old one — the target endpoint of a greenfield migration crossing. Paired with logic:supersededTerm, it makes the correspondence's rung (logic:morphismClass) queryable per migrated term. Domain logic:Correspondence, range any term (stated in prose)."
msgstr "将一个取代性的 logic:Correspondence 关联到它记录为取代旧词项的替代词项——greenfield 迁移交叉的目标端点。与 logic:supersededTerm 配对，使对应关系的档级（logic:morphismClass）可按被迁移词项查询。定义域为 logic:Correspondence，值域为任意词项（以散文陈述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/suppliesIdentity|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates an ultimate sortal to an individual whose principle of identity it supplies: the second-order identity-supply relation, reified as a first-order relation over punned type individuals (HiLog/F-logic style) so that 'every object instantiates exactly one ultimate sortal' becomes a first-order counting constraint. Kinds supply identity; SubKinds, Roles, and Phases inherit it; non-sortals (Category, Mixin, RoleMixin, PhaseMixin) supply none."
msgstr "将一个终极 sortal 关联到一个由它供给同一性原则的个体：二阶的同一性供给关系，被具体化为一条作用于双关型个体的一阶关系（HiLog/F-logic 风格），从而使『每个对象恰好实例化一个终极 sortal』成为一条一阶计数约束。Kind 供给同一性；SubKind、Role 与 Phase 继承之；非 sortal（Category、Mixin、RoleMixin、PhaseMixin）则一概不供给。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/supportedProfile|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:EngineContract to a logic:ReasoningPreset the runtime dispatch surface recognizes — one edge per entry of the capability manifest, MULTI-valued. It lets a consumer NEGOTIATE capability up front (does this engine support the preset my query needs?) instead of discovering an unsupported preset as a runtime refusal (a typed Err, never a silent empty answer). Each linked preset carries, via logic:decidabilityClass, the decidability guarantee the engine offers for it, so the manifest pairs recognition with its termination promise. Domain logic:EngineContract, range logic:ReasoningPreset (stated in prose, matching the module's convention). Authored canonically in crates/logic (Rust); a lossy documentation projection (Principle 17)."
msgstr "将一个 logic:EngineContract 关联到运行时派发面所识别的一个 logic:ReasoningPreset——能力清单每一条目对应一条边，取多值。它让消费者得以在前期协商能力（本引擎是否支持我的查询所需的预设？），而不是把不受支持的预设当作运行时拒绝才发现（一个带类型的 Err，绝非静默的空答案）。每个被链接的预设经由 logic:decidabilityClass 携带引擎为其提供的可判定性保证，因此清单将识别与其终止承诺配成一对。定义域为 logic:EngineContract，值域为 logic:ReasoningPreset（以散文陈述，与该模块惯例一致）。在 crates/logic（Rust）中规范撰写；一种有损的文档投影（原则 17）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/supportSelfSupportExclusion|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Asserts that a gmeow:Support's gmeow:supportSource and gmeow:supportTarget must be distinct: support is irreflexive — a structure does not support itself. The native coherence gate raises a violation when they coincide; the generated SHACL constraint surface is its projection."
msgstr "断言一个 gmeow:Support 的 gmeow:supportSource 与 gmeow:supportTarget 必须相异：支持是非自反的——一个结构不支持它自身。当二者重合时，原生一致性关卡会引发一处违规；生成的 SHACL 约束面即是它的投影。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/survivesCounterexample|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The Lakatos survival edge: relates a refined successor conjecture to the logic:ContradictionWitness that refuted its predecessor and which the successor now EXCLUDES — the evidence that the refinement did real work, not just relabelled the claim. Paired with logic:conjectureRefinedFrom, it lets the corpus show a refinement chain where each successor demonstrably survives a witness that killed its parent. Domain logic:Conjecture, range logic:ContradictionWitness."
msgstr "Lakatos 存活边：将一个经精炼的后继猜想关联到曾反驳其前驱、而后继现将其排除的 logic:ContradictionWitness——这是精炼确实做了实事、而非仅仅给论断重贴标签的证据。与 logic:conjectureRefinedFrom 配对，它让语料库得以展示一条精炼链，其中每个后继都可证地存活于曾杀死其父的见证之下。定义域为 logic:Conjecture，值域为 logic:ContradictionWitness。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/symmetricProperty|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic: property-characteristic marker for symmetry: a property P such that P(a,b) entails P(b,a). The logic: analogue of owl:SymmetricProperty, minted standalone so the characteristic can be asserted on the canonical reasoning carrier alongside the others and reasoned over natively — including together with logic:irreflexiveProperty, for a constitutive-opposition relation that holds both ways but never of a thing and itself."
msgstr "表示对称性的 logic: 属性特征标记：一个属性 P 使得 P(a,b) 蕴涵 P(b,a)。它是 owl:SymmetricProperty 的 logic: 类似物，独立铸造，以便该特征能够与其他特征一并在规范推理载体上被断言并原生地被推理——包括与 logic:irreflexiveProperty 一同用于一种构成性对立关系，该关系双向成立，却绝不成立于某物与其自身之间。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SzsContradictoryAxioms|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The SZS status asserting the axioms are themselves contradictory (unsatisfiable independent of any conjecture). Projects to logic:ConfInconsistent, and logic:szsStrengthens logic:SzsUnsatisfiable — it is the strictly stronger outcome, entailing unsatisfiability while additionally locating the inconsistency in the axiom set. This is precisely the distinction the coarse three-bucket collapse loses, preserved verbatim as logic:rawStatusToken. A logic:SzsSuccess status."
msgstr "断言诸公理本身相互矛盾（独立于任何猜想即不可满足）的 SZS 状态。投影为 logic:ConfInconsistent，并且 logic:szsStrengthens logic:SzsUnsatisfiable——它是严格更强的结果，蕴涵不可满足性，同时还将不一致定位于公理集合之中。这正是粗糙的三桶坍缩所丢失的区分，被原样保留为 logic:rawStatusToken。一个 logic:SzsSuccess 状态。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SzsCounterSatisfiable|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The SZS status asserting the conjecture is not entailed — a counter-model exists (the negated conjecture is satisfiable together with the axioms). Projects to logic:ConfConsistent, the entailment-fails twin of the W3C mf:NegativeEntailment kind. This is the distinction from logic:SzsSatisfiable the coarse collapse loses, preserved as logic:rawStatusToken. A logic:SzsSuccess status."
msgstr "断言猜想不被蕴涵的 SZS 状态——存在一个反模型（被否定的猜想与诸公理一同可满足）。投影为 logic:ConfConsistent，即 W3C mf:NegativeEntailment 种类的『蕴涵失败』孪生体。这是与 logic:SzsSatisfiable 之间、粗糙坍缩所丢失的区分，被保留为 logic:rawStatusToken。一个 logic:SzsSuccess 状态。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SzsGaveUp|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The SZS status asserting the prover abandoned the attempt without a decision. Projects to logic:ConfIncomplete. A logic:SzsNoSuccess status."
msgstr "断言证明器未作出裁决即放弃尝试的 SZS 状态。投影为 logic:ConfIncomplete。一个 logic:SzsNoSuccess 状态。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SzsNoSuccess|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The SZS no-success sort: the statuses under which the prover did NOT reach a decision — it gave up, timed out, ran out of resources, or returned an explicit unknown. Its members (logic:SzsUnknown, logic:SzsGaveUp, logic:SzsTimeout, logic:SzsResourceOut) project onto the least-informative join logic:ConfIncomplete, kept strictly distinct from a native capability gap (a hard fail, never an incomplete swallowed into agreement). The undecided half of the logic:SzsStatus partition, complement of logic:SzsSuccess."
msgstr "SZS 的『无成功』类别：证明器未能达成裁决的那些状态——它放弃、超时、资源耗尽或返回一个显式的未知。其成员（logic:SzsUnknown、logic:SzsGaveUp、logic:SzsTimeout、logic:SzsResourceOut）投影到信息量最少的连接 logic:ConfIncomplete，并与原生能力缺口严格区分（一个硬失败，绝不把不完备吞入认同之中）。它是 logic:SzsStatus 划分中未定的一半，是 logic:SzsSuccess 的补。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SzsResourceOut|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The SZS status asserting the prover exhausted a resource bound (memory, inferences) before deciding. Projects to logic:ConfIncomplete. A logic:SzsNoSuccess status; the resource-bounded outcome."
msgstr "断言证明器在作出裁决前耗尽某一资源界限（内存、推理次数）的 SZS 状态。投影为 logic:ConfIncomplete。一个 logic:SzsNoSuccess 状态；受资源限制的结果。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SzsSatisfiable|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The SZS status asserting the axiom set has a model. Projects to logic:ConfConsistent. A logic:SzsSuccess status; the decided-negative outcome for a consistency question."
msgstr "断言公理集合拥有一个模型的 SZS 状态。投影为 logic:ConfConsistent。一个 logic:SzsSuccess 状态；针对一致性问题的裁决为否的结果。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SzsStatus|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The TPTP SZS result-status ontology, subsumed by reference (Principle 5 — no vendored axioms) as a first-class logic: vocabulary rather than parsed and discarded. An SZS status is the community-decided ground-truth outcome a problem carries in the external FOL soundness corpus. The vocabulary is partitioned by rdfs:subClassOf into logic:SzsSuccess (the prover decided) and logic:SzsNoSuccess (the prover did not), and the intra-branch strength order is carried by logic:szsStrengthens (logic:SzsContradictoryAxioms strengthens logic:SzsUnsatisfiable). The coarse three-bucket runner view (logic:ConformanceVerdict) is a monotone lossy projection of this ordered structure — a logic:SoundUnderApproximation that collapses distinctions the raw token preserves via logic:rawStatusToken (design/LOGIC-CONFORMANCE.md, the external FOL soundness oracle)."
msgstr "TPTP 的 SZS 结果状态本体，经由引用被归纳（原则 5——不内置任何公理）为一等的 logic: 词汇，而非解析后即弃。一个 SZS 状态是某问题在外部 FOL 可靠性语料库中所承载的、由社区裁定的基准真相结果。该词汇经 rdfs:subClassOf 划分为 logic:SzsSuccess（证明器已裁决）与 logic:SzsNoSuccess（证明器未裁决），而分支内的强度次序由 logic:szsStrengthens 承载（logic:SzsContradictoryAxioms 强化 logic:SzsUnsatisfiable）。粗糙的三桶运行器视图（logic:ConformanceVerdict）是此有序结构的一个单调有损投影——一个 logic:SoundUnderApproximation，它坍缩了原始令牌经由 logic:rawStatusToken 所保留的诸区分（design/LOGIC-CONFORMANCE.md，外部 FOL 可靠性判定源）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/szsStrengthens|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The strength order over logic:SzsStatus: relates a status to a weaker status it entails (logic:SzsContradictoryAxioms szsStrengthens logic:SzsUnsatisfiable — contradictory axioms entail, and are strictly stronger than, bare unsatisfiability). Domain and range logic:SzsStatus (stated in prose); transitive. The intra-branch partial order that makes the SZS vocabulary an ordered structure rather than a flat token set, mirroring gmeow:coarserThan over granularity levels; the ordering the monotone logic:ConformanceVerdict projection respects."
msgstr "logic:SzsStatus 之上的强度次序：将一个状态关联到它所蕴涵的较弱状态（logic:SzsContradictoryAxioms szsStrengthens logic:SzsUnsatisfiable——矛盾的公理蕴涵裸的不可满足性，且严格强于它）。定义域与值域皆为 logic:SzsStatus（以散文陈述）；传递。它是使 SZS 词汇成为有序结构而非扁平令牌集的分支内偏序，与 gmeow:coarserThan 之于粒度级别相仿；单调的 logic:ConformanceVerdict 投影所尊重的次序。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SzsSuccess|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The SZS success sort: the statuses under which the prover reached a decision about the problem — the axiom set's satisfiability or the conjecture's entailment was settled. Its members (logic:SzsTheorem, logic:SzsUnsatisfiable, logic:SzsContradictoryAxioms, logic:SzsSatisfiable, logic:SzsCounterSatisfiable) project onto the two informative logic:ConformanceVerdict meet-elements. The decided half of the logic:SzsStatus partition, complement of logic:SzsNoSuccess."
msgstr "SZS 的『成功』类别：证明器已对问题作出裁决的那些状态——公理集合的可满足性或猜想的蕴涵已被了结。其成员（logic:SzsTheorem、logic:SzsUnsatisfiable、logic:SzsContradictoryAxioms、logic:SzsSatisfiable、logic:SzsCounterSatisfiable）投影到 logic:ConformanceVerdict 的两个有信息量的交元素。它是 logic:SzsStatus 划分中已裁决的一半，是 logic:SzsNoSuccess 的补。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SzsTheorem|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The SZS status asserting the conjecture is a theorem of the axioms — entailment holds. Projects to logic:ConfInconsistent (the negated-conjecture reduction is unsatisfiable). A logic:SzsSuccess status; the canonical positive-entailment outcome, the SZS twin of the W3C mf:PositiveEntailment kind."
msgstr "断言猜想是诸公理之定理的 SZS 状态——蕴涵成立。投影为 logic:ConfInconsistent（否定猜想的归约不可满足）。一个 logic:SzsSuccess 状态；规范的正向蕴涵结果，W3C mf:PositiveEntailment 种类的 SZS 孪生体。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SzsTimeout|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The SZS status asserting the prover exhausted its wall-clock budget before deciding. Projects to logic:ConfIncomplete. A logic:SzsNoSuccess status; the budget-tripped outcome."
msgstr "断言证明器在作出裁决前耗尽其挂钟时间预算的 SZS 状态。投影为 logic:ConfIncomplete。一个 logic:SzsNoSuccess 状态；因预算被触发的结果。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SzsUnknown|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The SZS status asserting the prover could not determine the result. Projects to logic:ConfIncomplete. A logic:SzsNoSuccess status; the explicit undecided outcome, distinct from a native capability gap."
msgstr "断言证明器无法确定结果的 SZS 状态。投影为 logic:ConfIncomplete。一个 logic:SzsNoSuccess 状态；显式的未定结果，区别于原生能力缺口。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SzsUnsatisfiable|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The SZS status asserting the axiom set has no model. Projects to logic:ConfInconsistent. A logic:SzsSuccess status; strengthened by logic:SzsContradictoryAxioms (which additionally asserts the inconsistency is intrinsic to the axioms, not conjecture-relative)."
msgstr "断言公理集合没有任何模型的 SZS 状态。投影为 logic:ConfInconsistent。一个 logic:SzsSuccess 状态；由 logic:SzsContradictoryAxioms 强化（后者还额外断言该不一致是公理所固有的，而非相对于某猜想的）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/targetEndpoint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:bridge logic:targetEndpoint owl:Restriction ."
msgstr "示例：ex:bridge logic:targetEndpoint owl:Restriction ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/targetEndpoint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The target endpoint identifies a view term by reference and confers no authority on its external TBox."
msgstr "目标端点通过引用来标识一个视图词项，并不赋予其外部 TBox 任何权威性。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TeleologicalFramework|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The goal-and-action framework: structured logic:GoalExpression (atomic through achievement, maintenance, avoidance, optimization, conditional, and deadline forms), the reified multi-axis logic:GoalEvaluation, and logic:ActionSchema with its precondition / effect / invariant / capability / outcome / observation / compensation facets — the structure that motivates and evaluates transactions, kept distinct from how state changes (design/LOGIC-TELEOLOGY.md, the why-goals-and-action-are-their-own-layer section)."
msgstr "目标与行动框架：结构化的 logic:GoalExpression（从原子形式到达成、维持、规避、优化、条件与截止期形式），被具体化的多轴 logic:GoalEvaluation，以及带有前置条件／效果／不变式／能力／结果／观察／补偿诸面的 logic:ActionSchema——这是激励并评估事务的结构，与状态如何变更相区分（design/LOGIC-TELEOLOGY.md，为何目标与行动自成一层的章节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TemporalFramework|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The 4D / path framework: logic:State and logic:Path with the ordered transaction history, logic:TransactionStep instantiation from predecessor to successor, and frame-relative truth where a formula's truth is a property of the path it executes along. Time is one independent index axis of the typed context algebra, coexisting with world, standpoint, and path on a single result (design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md, the worlds-modality-and-counterfactuals section; design/LOGIC-TRANSACTION.md, the path-semantics section)."
msgstr "四维／路径框架：带有有序事务历史的 logic:State 与 logic:Path、从前驱到后继的 logic:TransactionStep 实例化，以及帧相对真理——公式的真值是它沿之执行的路径的一个属性。时间是有类型上下文代数的一条独立索引轴，与世界、立场和路径共存于单一结果之上（design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md，世界-模态-与反事实章节；design/LOGIC-TRANSACTION.md，路径语义章节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/temporallyIncompatible|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates two gmeow:Goals each achievable on its own but not within the windows both require. Domain gmeow:Goal, range gmeow:Goal (stated in prose). One of seven conflict relations between independently-meaningful goals, weaker than gmeow:counterGoal (constitutive opposition); the conflict is in the scheduling, not in the goals' content."
msgstr "关联两个各自单独可实现、却无法在二者都要求的时间窗内同时实现的 gmeow:Goals。定义域为 gmeow:Goal，值域为 gmeow:Goal（以散文陈述）。这是独立有意义的目标之间七种冲突关系之一，弱于 gmeow:counterGoal（构成性对立）；冲突在于调度，而非目标的内容。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/temporallySucceeds|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The typed temporal accessibility relation along a logic:Path: one gmeow:State succeeds another in the ordered run of states. A strict order (irreflexive and transitive) — its character is documented in prose, not asserted as OWL characteristics, matching the kernel convention. logic:accessibleFrom is its generic superproperty in prose only — NOT asserted rdfs:subPropertyOf — so the bare superproperty licenses no cross-type entailment across context types."
msgstr "沿某 logic:Path 的有类型时间可达关系：在状态的有序运行中，一个 gmeow:State 承接另一个。一种严格序（非自反且传递）——其性质在散文中记载，而非作为 OWL 特征断言，与内核惯例一致。logic:accessibleFrom 仅在散文中是其通用超属性——并未断言为 rdfs:subPropertyOf——因而这条裸超属性不许可跨上下文类型的任何跨类型蕴涵。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/temporalPartOf|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Parthood among perdurants: relates a temporal part of an occurrent to the larger occurrent it is a phase of — the first act is a temporal part of the play. The four-dimensional parthood relation, distinct from the endurant parthood of logic:partOf / logic:properPartOf: it carves a perdurant along its temporal extent into sub-occurrents."
msgstr "延续物之间的部分论：将一个发生物的时间部分关联到它作为其一个阶段的更大发生物——第一幕是该剧的一个时间部分。这是四维的部分论关系，区别于 logic:partOf／logic:properPartOf 的续存物部分论：它沿一个延续物的时间跨度将其切分为子发生物。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/termApplication|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Carries a compound function-term value on an argument term-carrier: the argument is the logic:FunctionTerm this property points at (a function symbol applied to ordered sub-terms), rather than a single atomic value. The fifth of the five mutually exclusive term-value properties; exactly one is present on each carrier. Because a logic:FunctionTerm's own logic:argument carriers may again bear logic:termApplication, a nested compound term round-trips recursively. It is not an IRI constant, variable, literal, or sequence marker — those are single-node values, while this points at a sub-tree."
msgstr "在一个参数词项载体上承载一个复合函数项值：该参数是本属性所指向的 logic:FunctionTerm（一个应用于有序子词项的函数符号），而非单个原子值。这是五个互斥的词项值属性中的第五个；每个载体上恰好存在一个。由于一个 logic:FunctionTerm 自身的 logic:argument 载体可再度承载 logic:termApplication，嵌套的复合词项得以递归往返。它不是 IRI 常量、变量、文字或序列标记——那些是单节点值，而它指向一棵子树。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/termDistinct|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A comparison relation the procedural-constraint SPARQL fragment lowers to a FILTER ( ?a != ?b ) over two already-bound terms (rather than a triple pattern). The inequality peer of logic:termEqual; it binds nothing, only tests inequality."
msgstr "一种比较关系，过程式约束的 SPARQL 片段将其下降为作用于两个已绑定词项之上的 FILTER ( ?a != ?b )（而非一个三元组模式）。它是 logic:termEqual 的不等式对应物；它不绑定任何东西，只测试不等。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/termEqual|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A comparison relation the procedural-constraint SPARQL fragment lowers to a FILTER ( ?a = ?b ) over two already-bound terms (rather than a triple pattern). Used by the cross-node inequality expansion; it binds nothing, only tests equality."
msgstr "一种比较关系，过程式约束的 SPARQL 片段将其下降为作用于两个已绑定词项之上的 FILTER ( ?a = ?b )（而非一个三元组模式）。由跨节点不等式展开所使用；它不绑定任何东西，只测试相等。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/termHasLang|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A language-tag presence relation the procedural-constraint SPARQL fragment lowers to a unary FILTER ( LANG(x) != \"\" ) over a bound term. The companion to logic:termLangMatches: it restricts a language-tag check to genuinely tagged literals, so a plain or typed literal is never swept into a tag-pattern violation."
msgstr "一种语言标签存在关系，过程式约束的 SPARQL 片段将其下降为作用于一个已绑定词项之上的一元 FILTER ( LANG(x) != \"\" )。它是 logic:termLangMatches 的伴随物：它将语言标签检查限定于真正带标签的文字，从而使一个普通或带类型的文字绝不会被卷入标签模式违规。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/termIndex|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The zero-based ordinal of a term-carrier within its ordered list — an argument within an atomic predication, or a bound variable within a quantifier block. Fixing position explicitly makes the variadic, order-significant lists round-trip independent of RDF statement order. It is not an RDF statement position, which has no graph semantics."
msgstr "一个词项载体在其有序列表中以零为起点的序数——原子谓述中的一个参数，或量词块中的一个约束变量。显式固定位置使得可变长、次序有意义的列表能够独立于 RDF 语句次序而往返。它不是 RDF 语句位置，后者不具备任何图语义。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/termIndex|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The object argument of a binary atom uses logic:termIndex 1 after its subject argument at index 0."
msgstr "二元原子的宾语参数在其位于索引 0 的主语参数之后使用 logic:termIndex 1。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/termIn|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:membershipGuard logic:termIn ex:status, ex:active, ex:pending ."
msgstr "示例：ex:membershipGuard logic:termIn ex:status, ex:active, ex:pending ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/termIn|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Argument order is semantic: the tested term precedes the finite set of permitted values."
msgstr "参数顺序具有语义意义：被测词项位于有限的许可值集合之前。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/termIri|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Carries an IRI-constant term value on an argument term-carrier: the argument is an individual (or a reified relation or type) named by this IRI. One of the four mutually exclusive term-value properties; exactly one is present on each carrier. It is not a variable name, lexical literal, or sequence-marker string."
msgstr "在一个参数词项载体上承载一个 IRI 常量词项值：该参数是由此 IRI 命名的一个个体（或一个被具体化的关系或类型）。这是四个互斥的词项值属性之一；每个载体上恰好存在一个。它不是变量名、词法文字或序列标记字符串。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/termIri|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A constant argument naming ex:Alice is carried as logic:termIri ex:Alice."
msgstr "一个命名 ex:Alice 的常量参数以 logic:termIri ex:Alice 的形式承载。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TermKindBlankNode|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:TermKind value for a column whose values are blank nodes. Wire value `blank-node`."
msgstr "用于其值为空白节点的列的 logic:TermKind 值。线上值 `blank-node`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TermKindIri|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:TermKind value for a column whose values are IRIs (named nodes). Wire value `iri`."
msgstr "用于其值为 IRI（命名节点）的列的 logic:TermKind 值。线上值 `iri`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TermKindLiteral|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:TermKind value for a column whose values are literals. A literal column may further pin its datatype with logic:columnDatatype; absent that, any literal conforms. Wire value `literal`."
msgstr "logic:TermKind 中用于某列（其值为字面量）的取值。字面量列可以进一步通过 logic:columnDatatype 固定其数据类型；若缺少该项，则任何字面量都符合。传输值 `literal`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TermKind|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The closed value class of the logic:columnTermKind facet: the RDF 1.2 term kind a result column binds. Its individuals are logic:TermKindIri, logic:TermKindLiteral, logic:TermKindBlankNode and logic:TermKindTripleTerm. The set is closed, so a misspelt value names no declared kind and is rejected (design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md, §The result row schema)."
msgstr "logic:columnTermKind 特征的封闭取值类：结果列所绑定的 RDF 1.2 词项种类。其个体为 logic:TermKindIri、logic:TermKindLiteral、logic:TermKindBlankNode 和 logic:TermKindTripleTerm。该集合是封闭的，因此拼写错误的取值不指称任何已声明的种类，会被拒绝（design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md，§The result row schema）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TermKindTripleTerm|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:TermKind value for a column whose values are RDF 1.2 triple terms. Wire value `triple-term`."
msgstr "logic:TermKind 中用于某列（其值为 RDF 1.2 三元组词项）的取值。传输值 `triple-term`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/termLangMatches|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A language-tag introspection relation the procedural-constraint SPARQL fragment lowers to a case-insensitive FILTER ( REGEX(LANG(x), 'pattern', 'i') ) over a bound term (rather than a triple pattern). It mirrors logic:termRegex but matches against the value's LANGUAGE TAG rather than its lexical form; it binds nothing, only tests the tag against a literal pattern."
msgstr "一种语言标签内省关系，过程式约束的 SPARQL 片段将其下降为对已绑定词项（而非三元组模式）执行的不区分大小写的 FILTER ( REGEX(LANG(x), 'pattern', 'i') )。它镜像 logic:termRegex，但比对的是值的语言标签而非其词法形式；它不绑定任何内容，仅按字面量模式测试该标签。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/termLiteralDatatype|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Carries the datatype IRI of a literal term value on an argument term-carrier that also bears logic:termLiteral. Absent for a plain literal. Held separately from the literal so the typed-literal term round-trips losslessly regardless of how an intermediate reader handles literal datatypes. It is not the lexical literal and cannot occur on a non-literal carrier."
msgstr "在同时承载 logic:termLiteral 的参数词项载体上，携带某个字面量词项值的数据类型 IRI。对于普通字面量则不存在。与字面量分开保存，使得带类型的字面量词项无论中间读取器如何处理字面量数据类型都能无损往返。它不是词法字面量，也不能出现在非字面量载体上。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/termLiteralDatatype|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A carrier for the lexical value '2026-07-12' can use logic:termLiteralDatatype xsd:date."
msgstr "词法值 '2026-07-12' 的载体可以使用 logic:termLiteralDatatype xsd:date。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/termLiteral|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Carries a data-literal term value (its lexical form) on an argument term-carrier; the term's datatype rides on the companion logic:termLiteralDatatype. One of the four mutually exclusive term-value properties. It is not an IRI constant, variable, or datatype declaration by itself."
msgstr "在参数词项载体上携带一个数据字面量词项值（其词法形式）；该词项的数据类型则搭载于配套的 logic:termLiteralDatatype 上。四个互斥的词项值属性之一。它本身不是 IRI 常量、变量或数据类型声明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/termLiteral|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The integer lexical value 42 is carried with logic:termLiteral '42' and logic:termLiteralDatatype xsd:integer."
msgstr "整数词法值 42 以 logic:termLiteral '42' 和 logic:termLiteralDatatype xsd:integer 承载。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/termRegex|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:codeGuard logic:termRegex ex:code, \"^[A-Z]{2}$\" ."
msgstr "示例：ex:codeGuard logic:termRegex ex:code, \"^[A-Z]{2}$\" ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/termRegex|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Regex syntax and flags remain target-dialect-sensitive projection residue."
msgstr "正则表达式的语法与标志仍是对目标方言敏感的投影残留物。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/termSequenceMarker|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Carries a sequence-marker term value (the authored marker name) on an argument term-carrier: the argument is a logic:SequenceMarker binding a sequence of terms rather than a single one. One of the five mutually exclusive term-value properties."
msgstr "在参数词项载体上携带一个序列标记词项值（所撰写的标记名称）：该参数是一个绑定词项序列而非单个词项的 logic:SequenceMarker。五个互斥的词项值属性之一。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/termSequenceMarker|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A variadic carrier can use logic:termSequenceMarker 'rest' to bind the remaining argument sequence."
msgstr "一个可变参数载体可以使用 logic:termSequenceMarker 'rest' 来绑定其余的参数序列。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/termVariable|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Carries a variable term value (the authored variable name, without a sigil) on a term-carrier: a single-term variable, bound by an enclosing quantifier or free. One of the four mutually exclusive term-value properties. It is not an IRI constant or a variadic sequence marker."
msgstr "在词项载体上携带一个变量词项值（所撰写的变量名，不含标记符号）：一个单词项变量，由外围量词绑定或为自由变量。四个互斥的词项值属性之一。它不是 IRI 常量，也不是可变元序列标记。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/termVariable|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A carrier with logic:termVariable 'person' represents the authored variable name without a question-mark sigil."
msgstr "带有 logic:termVariable 'person' 的载体表示所撰写的变量名，不带问号标记。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/thresholdLevel|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The minimum logic:AssessmentLevel an assessment on a row's logic:sourceDimension must reach — by the logic:levelAtOrAbove order — for the row's logic:projectsLadderEdge to be emitted. Range logic:AssessmentLevel (stated in prose)."
msgstr "为使某行的 logic:projectsLadderEdge 得以发出，对该行的 logic:sourceDimension 所作评估必须（按 logic:levelAtOrAbove 顺序）达到的最低 logic:AssessmentLevel。值域为 logic:AssessmentLevel（以散文陈述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TimeContextAxis|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The time index axis of the multi-dimensional context facet: a truth is relative to a time (a narrative or temporal reference frame). One of several context axes that coexist on a single result — world, standpoint, time, and path index the same result simultaneously rather than being alternative values of one slot."
msgstr "多维上下文特征的时间索引轴：真值相对于某个时间（一个叙事或时间参照系）而言。共存于单一结果之上的若干上下文轴之一——世界、立场、时间与路径同时索引同一结果，而非同一槽位的可替换取值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TimestampOrdering|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol that assigns each transaction a timestamp and orders conflicting operations by it, aborting any operation that would violate the timestamp order. A mechanism, not a guarantee."
msgstr "为每个事务分配一个时间戳并据此对冲突操作进行排序的 logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol，会中止任何违反时间戳顺序的操作。这是一种机制，而非一种保证。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TransactionOutcome|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The recorded result of executing a transaction program from a start state under executional entailment: the program succeeds iff there exists a path from the start state along which it holds, and failure leaves the start state untouched. It carries logic:outcomeOfProgram (the program executed), logic:transactionStart (the state it started from), and logic:transactionSucceeds (the boolean verdict); on success it is linked by logic:executedAlongPath to the logic:Path of states the run traversed and the per-step support is recorded as supersession. Typed APART from logic:GoalEvaluation, which records at-a-state satisfaction of a goal, and from logic:PlanSuccessMode, which classifies a plan's success mode over its nondeterministic outcome set: a logic:TransactionOutcome records ONE concrete executed run's success or failure under executional entailment, not a satisfaction judgement and not a mode classification."
msgstr "在执行蕴含下，从起始状态执行事务程序所记录的结果：程序成功当且仅当存在一条自起始状态出发、沿途程序成立的路径，而失败则使起始状态保持不变。它携带 logic:outcomeOfProgram（所执行的程序）、logic:transactionStart（其出发的状态）以及 logic:transactionSucceeds（布尔判决）；成功时通过 logic:executedAlongPath 关联到该次运行所遍历状态的 logic:Path，每一步的支持则记录为取代（supersession）。它与 logic:GoalEvaluation 分开定型——后者记录某目标在某状态处的满足——也与 logic:PlanSuccessMode 分开——后者在计划的非确定性结果集合上对其成功模式进行分类：一个 logic:TransactionOutcome 记录的是执行蕴含下一次具体执行运行的成功或失败，而非满足判断，也非模式分类。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TransactionPathEvolution|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The evolution-facet value selecting the Transaction-Logic state-change semantics of LOGIC-TRANSACTION.md — serial conjunction (⊗), executional entailment over a path of states, and elementary updates as supersession. It is a facet value, never a seventh profile, and is independent of the model-semantics facet; its full semantics are specified in LOGIC-TRANSACTION.md."
msgstr "选择 LOGIC-TRANSACTION.md 中事务逻辑状态变更语义的演化特征取值——串行合取（⊗）、状态路径上的执行蕴含，以及作为取代（supersession）的基本更新。它是一个特征取值，绝非第七种配置档，且独立于模型语义特征；其完整语义在 LOGIC-TRANSACTION.md 中规定。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TransactionProgram|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A state-changing composite over the path semantics of the transaction layer — insertion, deletion, hypothetical execution, and supersession rather than erasure. Its combinators are typed apart from formula connectives: serial composition is not conjunction, so a program operator is never confused with a logical one."
msgstr "在事务层路径语义之上进行状态变更的复合体——插入、删除、假设性执行以及取代（supersession）而非擦除。其组合子与公式连接词分开定型：串行组合不是合取，因此程序算子绝不会与逻辑算子相混淆。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/transactionStart|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:TransactionOutcome to the gmeow:State the program executed from — the start state of the executional-entailment run. Domain logic:TransactionOutcome, range gmeow:State (stated in prose). On failure the start state is left untouched (no successor is materialized); on success it is the first state of the logic:executedAlongPath path. The input side marks the executable program root with logic:transitionFromState; logic:transactionStart records, on the outcome, the start the verdict was computed from."
msgstr "将 logic:TransactionOutcome 关联到程序所从之执行的 gmeow:State——执行蕴含运行的起始状态。定义域为 logic:TransactionOutcome，值域为 gmeow:State（以散文陈述）。失败时起始状态保持不变（不物化任何后继）；成功时它是 logic:executedAlongPath 路径的第一个状态。输入侧用 logic:transitionFromState 标记可执行程序的根；logic:transactionStart 则在结果上记录计算该判决所依据的起始状态。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TransactionStep|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "An elementary update / transaction-path step that instantiates an action schema (logic:instantiatesSchema) and carries the path edge from a predecessor state (logic:transitionFromState) to a successor state (logic:transitionToState). The native evaluator applies the schema's logic:effect over the step, computing the successor situation's support as ins/del supersession: inserted supports become active, deleted supports are recorded via the append-only supersession quartet (logic:activeInState, logic:validUntilState, logic:retiredByTransaction, logic:supersededBy) and never erased."
msgstr "一个基本更新／事务路径步骤，它实例化一个动作模式（logic:instantiatesSchema），并承载从前驱状态（logic:transitionFromState）到后继状态（logic:transitionToState）的路径边。本机求值器在该步骤上应用模式的 logic:effect，将后继情形的支持计算为 ins/del 取代：插入的支持变为活动，删除的支持通过仅追加的取代四元组（logic:activeInState、logic:validUntilState、logic:retiredByTransaction、logic:supersededBy）予以记录，绝不擦除。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/transactionSucceeds|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The boolean executional-entailment verdict of a logic:TransactionOutcome: true iff there exists a path from logic:transactionStart along which the program holds, false otherwise. Domain logic:TransactionOutcome, range xsd:boolean (stated in prose). Kept distinct from goal satisfaction (logic:satisfactionStatus over a logic:GoalEvaluation) and from plan success mode (logic:planSuccessMode): it is the bare 'a path exists from the start' reading of the transaction layer, and a false verdict is honest total failure rather than a weak or partial success."
msgstr "一个 logic:TransactionOutcome 的布尔执行蕴含判决：为真当且仅当存在一条自 logic:transactionStart 出发、沿途程序成立的路径，否则为假。定义域为 logic:TransactionOutcome，值域为 xsd:boolean（以散文陈述）。与目标满足（logic:GoalEvaluation 上的 logic:satisfactionStatus）以及计划成功模式（logic:planSuccessMode）保持区分：它是事务层「存在一条自起点出发的路径」的裸读法，而一个假判决是诚实的彻底失败，而非弱成功或部分成功。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/transactionTimestamp|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The start-order timestamp assigned to a transaction (a concurrent-composition leg) under a timestamp-ordering protocol — the recorded event a logic:TimestampOrdering verification classifies the witnessed schedule against. Domain a transaction-program node (a logic:ConcurrentComposition leg), range xsd:integer (stated in prose); single-valued. Under logic:TimestampOrdering the schedule is well-formed iff every logic:precedes conflict edge runs from the earlier timestamp to the later one; a run declaring logic:TimestampOrdering that omits a leg's timestamp is a hard error. It is a recorded protocol EVENT — an input the classifier reads — not a derived verdict, and it is distinct from logic:temporallySucceeds, which orders the STATES of an executed path rather than the transactions of a schedule."
msgstr "在时间戳排序协议下分配给某事务（并发组合的一条支路）的启动顺序时间戳——即 logic:TimestampOrdering 验证据以对所观测调度进行分类的已记录事件。定义域为事务程序节点（一条 logic:ConcurrentComposition 支路），值域为 xsd:integer（以散文陈述）；单值。在 logic:TimestampOrdering 之下，调度良构当且仅当每一条 logic:precedes 冲突边都由较早的时间戳指向较晚的时间戳；声明了 logic:TimestampOrdering 却遗漏某支路时间戳的运行是硬错误。它是一个已记录的协议事件——分类器读取的输入——而非派生判决，并且区别于 logic:temporallySucceeds，后者对已执行路径的状态而非调度中的事务进行排序。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/transitionFromState|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates an elementary update or transaction-path step to the predecessor state snapshot from which it starts. States are WorldStore named-graph snapshots; this relation records the path edge's source state without mutating that state."
msgstr "将一个基本更新或事务路径步骤关联到它所从之出发的前驱状态快照。状态是 WorldStore 命名图快照；此关系记录路径边的源状态，而不改变该状态。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/transitionToState|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates an elementary update or transaction-path step to the successor state snapshot it materializes. The successor is a new named graph produced by the transition oracle from the predecessor plus the effective `ins`/`del` updates."
msgstr "将一个基本更新或事务路径步骤关联到它所物化的后继状态快照。后继是由转换预言机根据前驱加上有效的 `ins`/`del` 更新所产生的一个新命名图。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/transitiveProperty|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic: property-characteristic marker for transitivity: a property P such that P(a,b) ∧ P(b,c) entails P(a,c). The logic: analogue of owl:TransitiveProperty, minted standalone so logic: can combine it with logic:asymmetricProperty — a combination OWL 2 DL forbids globally (criticism 7) but logic: reasons over fully."
msgstr "logic: 中表示传递性的属性特征标记：一个属性 P 使得 P(a,b) ∧ P(b,c) 蕴含 P(a,c)。它是 owl:TransitiveProperty 的 logic: 对应物，独立铸造，以便 logic: 能将其与 logic:asymmetricProperty 组合——OWL 2 DL 在全局上禁止这种组合（批评 7），但 logic: 能对其完整地进行推理。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/trigger|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The trigger predicate of a logic:GuardedImplicationConstraint: the antecedent condition (optionally pinned to a logic:triggerValue) that, together with the target class, guards the required companion."
msgstr "一个 logic:GuardedImplicationConstraint 的触发谓词：前件条件（可选地固定到某个 logic:triggerValue），它与目标类一同守卫所要求的伴随项。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/triggerValue|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "An optional fixed object value that pins a logic:GuardedImplicationConstraint's trigger to trigger(this, value) rather than the mere presence of the trigger predicate. An IRI or a literal."
msgstr "一个可选的固定对象值，它将 logic:GuardedImplicationConstraint 的触发条件固定为 trigger(this, value)，而不仅仅是触发谓词的存在。可以是一个 IRI 或一个字面量。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/trueQuantity|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a measurement to its frame-independent magnitude: the quantity that exists independent of any unit or frame — the pressure itself, prior to its expression in mmHg or kPa. The frame-independent leg of the true-quantity/measured-value seam (Principle 11): logic:trueQuantity carries the unit-independent magnitude while logic:measuredValue and logic:referenceFrame carry the frame-relative value, so the same true quantity round-trips across unit systems without re-identifying the magnitude. The domain property gmeow:trueQuantity grounds onto this, pointing at a gmeow:Magnitude. Stated in prose, matching the module's domain/range convention."
msgstr "将一次测量关联到其与参照系无关的量值：独立于任何单位或参照系而存在的量——压强本身，先于其以 mmHg 或 kPa 的表达。真量／测得值接缝（原则 11）中与参照系无关的一支：logic:trueQuantity 承载与单位无关的量值，而 logic:measuredValue 与 logic:referenceFrame 承载相对于参照系的值，因此同一真量能在各单位制之间往返而无需重新标识该量值。定义域属性 gmeow:trueQuantity 接地于此，指向一个 gmeow:Magnitude。以散文陈述，符合本模块的定义域／值域约定。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TruthAlgebra|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The facet value class of the truth algebra: the lattice of truth values over which valuations range. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract. It is one of the three independent components of the truth/inconsistency facet — algebra, admissible-valuation policy, designated values — that together separate FDE, LP, K3 and classical logic; its values are the four-valued Belnap bilattice and the classical two-valued algebra."
msgstr "真值代数的特征取值类：赋值在其上取值的真值格。在 ReasoningContract 上为单值。它是真值／不一致性特征三个独立组成部分之一——代数、可容许赋值策略、指定值——三者共同区分 FDE、LP、K3 与经典逻辑；其取值为四值 Belnap 双格与经典二值代数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/truthAlgebra|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to the logic:TruthAlgebra it selects — the lattice of truth values over which valuations range. Single-valued on the contract. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:TruthAlgebra (stated in prose, matching the module's convention). One of the three independent truth-facet components, selected separately from logic:admissibleValuation and logic:designatedValues."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ReasoningContract 关联到它所选择的 logic:TruthAlgebra——赋值在其上取值的真值格。在合约上为单值。定义域为 logic:ReasoningContract，值域为 logic:TruthAlgebra（以散文陈述，符合本模块约定）。真值特征三个独立组成部分之一，与 logic:admissibleValuation 及 logic:designatedValues 分别选择。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TruthMaintenanceRevision|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The revision-policy value under which derived conclusions are tracked by their justifications, so retracting a premise automatically retracts the conclusions that depended on it (a truth-maintenance system). The dependency-directed counterpart of logic:EntrenchmentRevision; contrast logic:MonotonicRevision, which never retracts."
msgstr "一种修订策略取值，在其下派生结论按其依据被追踪，因此撤回某前提会自动撤回依赖于它的结论（一个真值维护系统）。它是 logic:EntrenchmentRevision 的依赖导向对应物；与从不撤回的 logic:MonotonicRevision 形成对照。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TupleAnnotationAlgebra|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The caller-selected algebra that composes annotations inside the native relational fixpoint: multiplication combines positive premises of one derivation and addition combines alternative derivations of the same tuple. Its stable identity and canonical element encoding participate in contract and receipt hashes; an undeclared algebraic approximation is refused rather than demoted to post-hoc scoring."
msgstr "由调用方选择的代数，在本机关系不动点内部对标注进行组合：乘法组合同一推导的正前提，加法组合同一元组的可替换推导。其稳定标识与规范元素编码参与合约与回执哈希；未声明的代数近似会被拒绝，而不会被降格为事后打分。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Type|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A universal: a type whose instances share a common feature, reified as a first-order individual so it can itself be the object of logic:instanceOf and carry a logic:orderedType. The counterpart of gufo:Type; first-order (its instances are logic:Individuals, logic:orderedType 1) or higher-order (its instances are themselves types). The root of the type taxonomy, complementing logic:Individual; every foundation sort (logic:Kind, logic:Role, …) and every meta-type below is a logic:Type. It is not an OWL class-punning shortcut: its deep-instantiation role is explicit first-order data."
msgstr "一个共相：一种类型，其实例共享某一共同特征，被具体化为一阶个体，从而它本身能作为 logic:instanceOf 的对象并携带一个 logic:orderedType。它是 gufo:Type 的对应物；可为一阶（其实例是 logic:Individuals，logic:orderedType 为 1）或高阶（其实例本身即类型）。它是类型分类法的根，与 logic:Individual 互补；每一个基础种别（logic:Kind、logic:Role、……）以及其下每一个元类型都是 logic:Type。它不是 OWL 类双关的捷径：其深度实例化角色是显式的一阶数据。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Type|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "logic:Kind is reified as a logic:Type so it can classify entity types through logic:instanceOf."
msgstr "logic:Kind 被具体化为 logic:Type，以便它能通过 logic:instanceOf 对实体类型进行分类。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/UncertaintyMeasure|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The facet value class of the uncertainty facet: how graded belief is carried. Set-valued on a ReasoningContract — several measures (probabilistic, weighted/ranking, fuzzy) may be in force on the same result at once, or none. Its individuals record the measures in force, not a single chosen one."
msgstr "不确定性特征的特征取值类：分级信念如何被承载。在 ReasoningContract 上为集合值——多种度量（概率型、加权／排名型、模糊型）可同时在同一结果上生效，也可以一个都没有。其个体记录生效中的各度量，而非单一选定的一种。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/uncertaintyMeasure|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to a logic:UncertaintyMeasure it carries — how graded belief is recorded. Set-valued on the contract: probabilistic, weighted/ranking, and fuzzy measures may coexist on the same result, so this records the set of measures in force, not one. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:UncertaintyMeasure (stated in prose, matching the module's convention)."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ReasoningContract 关联到它所承载的某个 logic:UncertaintyMeasure——分级信念如何被记录。在合约上为集合值：概率型、加权／排名型与模糊型度量可在同一结果上共存，因此这记录的是生效中度量的集合，而非单一一种。定义域为 logic:ReasoningContract，值域为 logic:UncertaintyMeasure（以散文陈述，符合本模块约定）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/UncertifiedChase|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The failure raised when a logic:ChaseAcceptanceWitness — the acceptance record of an existential-rule chase materialization — carries no logic:carriesTerminationCertificate, i.e. reports a materialized closure without the weak-acyclicity termination certificate that admits it. An uncertified chase may not terminate; the flagship's guarantee is that materialize_existential_rules surfaces the ChaseAdmission termination certificate as a first-class gmeow:Finding, so a chase acceptance record with no certificate is ill-formed (LOGIC-RUNTIME.md)."
msgstr "当一个 logic:ChaseAcceptanceWitness——存在性规则 chase 物化的接受记录——不携带任何 logic:carriesTerminationCertificate 时所引发的失败，即报告了一个已物化闭包，却没有据以承认它的弱无环性终止证书。未认证的 chase 可能不终止；旗舰的保证是 materialize_existential_rules 将 ChaseAdmission 终止证书作为一等的 gmeow:Finding 呈现出来，因此没有证书的 chase 接受记录是不良构的（LOGIC-RUNTIME.md）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/underMereologyProfile|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a whole to the logic:MereologyProfile it is declared under — the scope within which the strong mereological axioms (weak supplementation) hold for it. A whole carries no logic:WeakSupplementation obligation unless declared under a profile via this relation; parthood is profiled, not universal (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "将一个整体关联到它所被声明所依据的 logic:MereologyProfile——强部分论公理（弱补充）对它成立的范围。除非通过此关系在某配置档下声明，否则一个整体不承担任何 logic:WeakSupplementation 义务；部分关系是按配置档划定的，而非普遍的（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons 一节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/UnentrenchedCounterfactual|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The failure raised when a logic:CounterfactualAcceptanceWitness — the acceptance record of a Stratum-C counterfactual resolution — names no logic:selectedByEntrenchment outcome, i.e. resolves an antecedent without recording the entrenchment-ranked selection that made the result deterministic. A counterfactual whose outcome is not tied to an entrenchment ordering is a silent, arbitrary choice; the flagship's guarantee is a deterministic entrenchment-ranked selection, so a witness with none is ill-formed (LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md)."
msgstr "当一个 logic:CounterfactualAcceptanceWitness——某个 Stratum-C 反事实消解的接受记录——未指名任何 logic:selectedByEntrenchment 结果时所引发的失败，即消解了一个前件，却没有记录使结果确定化的、按固守度排序的选择。结果未与固守度排序相绑定的反事实是一种无声的、任意的选择；旗舰的保证是一个确定性的、按固守度排序的选择，因此缺少它的见证是不良构的（LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/UniqueLangConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Compact sugar for a per-property unique-language constraint: a logic:onClass target and a logic:valuePath predicate whose language-tagged literal values must each carry a DISTINCT language tag (no two values on that path share a tag). Expands declaratively to a sh:uniqueLang true property component on the target class node shape; a language-tagged prose predicate localizes at most once per language. Frontend-only authoring shortcut with no ShEx form (the uniqueLang facet is a disclosed ShEx drop)."
msgstr "针对每属性的唯一语言约束的紧凑糖衣：一个 logic:onClass 目标和一个 logic:valuePath 谓词，其带语言标签的字面量值各自必须携带一个互不相同的语言标签（该路径上没有两个值共享同一标签）。声明式地展开为目标类节点形状上的 sh:uniqueLang true 属性组件；带语言标签的散文谓词对每种语言至多本地化一次。仅前端的撰写捷径，没有 ShEx 形式（uniqueLang 特征是一处已披露的 ShEx 舍弃）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/UniqueLangConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:oneNamePerLang a logic:UniqueLangConstraint ; logic:onClass ex:Place ; logic:valuePath ex:localName ."
msgstr "示例：ex:oneNamePerLang a logic:UniqueLangConstraint ; logic:onClass ex:Place ; logic:valuePath ex:localName ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/UniqueNameEqualityPolicy|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The equality-policy value imposing the unique-name assumption: distinct names denote distinct entities unless equality is explicitly asserted. The optional strengthening of logic:RdfEqualityPolicy; contrast logic:ExplicitEqualityPolicy, which neither assumes distinctness nor unifies beyond what is declared."
msgstr "施加唯一名称假设的相等性策略取值：不同的名称指称不同的实体，除非相等性被显式断言。它是 logic:RdfEqualityPolicy 的可选强化；与 logic:ExplicitEqualityPolicy 形成对照，后者既不假设相异性，也不在已声明范围之外进行合一。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/unit|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a measurement to the unit its logic:measuredValue is expressed in — a QUDT unit by reference (Principle 5), held on the measurement rather than on the frame-independent magnitude. The unit leg of the true-quantity/measured-value seam (Principle 11): the unit belongs to the measurement, not the quantity, so the same logic:trueQuantity round-trips across unit systems. Because the foundation chase is all-IRI, logic:unit is the IRI-valued witness that a framed value exists, and is the predicate the logic:MeasurementFrameMissing constraint keys on — a value expressed in a unit but lacking its logic:referenceFrame is the violation. The domain property gmeow:unit grounds onto this by sub-property. Domain a measurement, range a unit (stated in prose, matching the module's convention)."
msgstr "将一次测量关联到其 logic:measuredValue 所用以表达的单位——按引用的 QUDT 单位（原则 5），承载于测量之上而非与参照系无关的量值之上。真量／测得值接缝（原则 11）中的单位一支：单位属于测量，而非量，因此同一 logic:trueQuantity 能在各单位制之间往返。由于基础 chase 全为 IRI，logic:unit 是「存在一个带参照系的值」的 IRI 值见证，也是 logic:MeasurementFrameMissing 约束据以索引的谓词——一个以某单位表达却缺少其 logic:referenceFrame 的值即为违规。定义域属性 gmeow:unit 通过子属性接地于此。定义域为一次测量，值域为一个单位（以散文陈述，符合本模块约定）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Unsatisfied|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:SatisfactionStatus value for a goal not met, with no positive partial progress recorded. Distinct from logic:Violated (an active breach of a maintenance or avoidance target) and from logic:PartiallySatisfied (some progress made)."
msgstr "针对未达成目标的 logic:SatisfactionStatus 取值，且未记录任何正向的部分进展。区别于 logic:Violated（对某维持或规避目标的活跃违反）以及 logic:PartiallySatisfied（已取得一些进展）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/unsupportedConstruct|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Names a construct the lowering could not carry at all, carried on a logic:ReasoningResult's preservation field — MULTI-valued. A query whose constructs intersect this set is loss-affected (a derived diagnostic, never a stored field). Domain logic:ReasoningResult (stated in prose)."
msgstr "指名下降完全无法承载的一个构造，承载于某 logic:ReasoningResult 的保持字段上——多值。若某查询的构造与此集合相交，则受损失影响（一个派生诊断，绝非存储字段）。定义域为 logic:ReasoningResult（以散文陈述）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Unsupported|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The weakest preservation polarity: the construct cannot be expressed in the target at all. A formula that lowers to unsupported is carried and flagged in the loss ledger, never silently dropped, and every result downstream of the lowering discloses which formulas the target did not evaluate. The legalization floor — a lowering is a total function into legal output plus flagged residue, and an unsupported construct is residue, never loss in silence."
msgstr "最弱的保持极性：该构造在目标中根本无法表达。一个下降为不支持的公式会被承载并在损失账本中被标记，绝不会被无声丢弃，而下降下游的每个结果都会披露目标未曾求值的是哪些公式。合法化下限——一次下降是一个映入合法输出加上被标记残余的全函数，一个不支持的构造是残余，绝非无声的损失。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/UnwiredFlagshipScenario|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The failure raised when a gmeow:FlagshipScenario in the logic grounding layer is not fully wired: it is missing its worked example (gmeow:demonstratedByExample), its competency question (gmeow:demonstratedByCompetency), its producer (gmeow:demonstratedByProducer), its counter-example (gmeow:guardedByCounterExample), or its enforcing failure class (gmeow:enforcesFailureClass); or the class it names as enforcing is not a logic:LogicConformanceFailure subclass. The depth bar is a contract, not a suggestion: an acceptance scenario that does not bind all realizing/enforcing artifacts cannot claim the scenario is met, and the gate rejects it. This layer's concrete realization of the shared gmeow:UnwiredFlagshipScenario marker (enforced uniformly by the shared gmeow:FlagshipScenarioShape); it subclasses ONLY the slice failure root (never the spec-layer gmeow:UnwiredFlagshipScenario marker), so it is a typed, queryable object in this layer's own failure lattice."
msgstr "当逻辑接地层中的一个 gmeow:FlagshipScenario 未被完全接线时所引发的失败：它缺少其可运行示例（gmeow:demonstratedByExample）、其胜任力问题（gmeow:demonstratedByCompetency）、其生产者（gmeow:demonstratedByProducer）、其反例（gmeow:guardedByCounterExample），或其实施用失败类（gmeow:enforcesFailureClass）；又或者它指名为实施用的类并非 logic:LogicConformanceFailure 的子类。深度门槛是一份合约，而非一条建议：未绑定全部实现／实施制品的接受场景不能宣称场景已满足，门禁会将其拒绝。这是本层对共享的 gmeow:UnwiredFlagshipScenario 标记的具体实现（由共享的 gmeow:FlagshipScenarioShape 统一实施）；它仅子类化本切片的失败根（绝不子类化规范层的 gmeow:UnwiredFlagshipScenario 标记），因此它是本层自身失败格中一个带类型、可查询的对象。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/UnwitnessedRefutation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The failure raised when a logic:RefutationAcceptanceWitness — the acceptance record of a symmetric φ/¬φ conjecture test whose verdict is a refutation — names no logic:namesContradictionWitness, i.e. claims the conjecture was refuted without pointing at the concrete logic:ContradictionWitness that carries the clash. A refutation with no replayable witness is an assertion, not a proof; the flagship's guarantee is that conjecture_test returns a concrete witness on a refutation, so a witness-less refutation record is ill-formed (LOGIC-CONTRACT.md)."
msgstr "当一个 logic:RefutationAcceptanceWitness——某个对称 φ/¬φ 猜想检验（其判决为反驳）的接受记录——未指名任何 logic:namesContradictionWitness 时所引发的失败，即宣称该猜想已被反驳，却未指向承载该冲突的具体 logic:ContradictionWitness。没有可重放见证的反驳是一项断言，而非一项证明；旗舰的保证是 conjecture_test 在反驳时返回一个具体见证，因此无见证的反驳记录是不良构的（LOGIC-CONTRACT.md）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/utility|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The preference quantity carried on a logic:GoalEvaluation — how desirable an outcome is. The ONE preference term: utility and preference are one concept here, so no separate preference property is minted. Domain logic:GoalEvaluation (stated in prose). The range is intentionally left open (no rdfs:range), matching the module's quantitative axes. DISTINCT from the uncertainty measures (logic:confidence, logic:probability, logic:weight, logic:evidenceStrength) and from logic:satisfactionDegree and logic:objectiveValue — desirability is never sureness, never how much of the goal is met, and never the measure an optimization goal extremizes; none substitutes for another."
msgstr "承载于某 logic:GoalEvaluation 上的偏好量——某结果有多合意。唯一的偏好词项：在此效用与偏好是同一个概念，因此不铸造单独的偏好属性。定义域为 logic:GoalEvaluation（以散文陈述）。值域被有意留空（无 rdfs:range），以符合本模块的量化轴。它与不确定性度量（logic:confidence、logic:probability、logic:weight、logic:evidenceStrength）以及 logic:satisfactionDegree 和 logic:objectiveValue 相区分——合意度绝非确定度，绝非目标被达成的程度，也绝非某个优化目标所极值化的度量；彼此皆不可相互替代。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Vague|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The target relationship is ontically fuzzy: it holds to a degree or only on a shared component, with genuine borderline cases. Paired with a logic:AffineCorrespondence class for the 'similar but not quite' alignment — vagueness in the world, not uncertainty in the curator."
msgstr "目标关系在本体上是模糊的：它仅在某种程度上或仅在某个共享成分上成立，且存在真正的边界情形。与一个 logic:AffineCorrespondence 类配对，用于「相似但不尽然」的对齐——是世界中的模糊，而非策展者的不确定。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ValidationOnlyProjection|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The projection-target value requesting a validation-only surface: it detects ill-formedness without computing canonical consequences (the honest output for bridge views that constrain but do not reason). One of several output targets a single contract may name at once; it never alters which entailments hold."
msgstr "请求仅验证表面的投影目标取值：它检测不良构而不计算规范后果（对于施加约束却不进行推理的桥接视图而言，这是诚实的输出）。同一合约可同时指名的若干输出目标之一；它绝不改变哪些蕴含成立。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ValidationOnly|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The projection detects some invalidity but is not an entailment relation: it can flag ill-formedness without computing canonical consequences. The honest label for bridge views (e.g. BFO/DOLCE) that constrain but do not reason; they carry this or no preservation claim, never logic:ExactPreservation."
msgstr "该投影检测出某些无效性，但它不是一种蕴含关系：它能标记不良构而不计算规范后果。对于施加约束却不进行推理的桥接视图（例如 BFO/DOLCE）而言，这是诚实的标签；它们要么携带此标签，要么不作任何保持声称，绝不携带 logic:ExactPreservation。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ValidationShape|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A closed-world data-shape condition: the SHACL-shaped subset of the IR, evaluated against a dataset rather than as an open-world entailment. The node kind for conditions checked under the closed-world reading where absence may be read as falsity."
msgstr "一个封闭世界数据形状条件：IR 中由 SHACL 塑形的子集，针对某数据集进行求值，而非作为开放世界蕴含。用于在封闭世界读法下检查的条件的节点种类，在该读法下缺失可被读作假。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/validUntilState|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a support/reified assertion to the successor state at which it stops holding as an active support. It is the path-state counterpart of temporal valid-until metadata: a `del` records the state boundary where the support is retired, while the historical support remains retained."
msgstr "将一个支持／具体化断言关联到它不再作为活动支持成立的后继状态。它是时间性「有效截至」元数据在路径状态上的对应物：一个 `del` 记录支持被退役的状态边界，而历史支持仍予以保留。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/valueClass|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The required value class of a logic:PathValueTypeConstraint: the class every value on logic:valuePath must belong to."
msgstr "一个 logic:PathValueTypeConstraint 所要求的值类：logic:valuePath 上每个值都必须属于的类。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/valueObject|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The fixed object of a logic:PathValueTypeConstraint's fixed-value variant: the required object (an IRI or a literal) of logic:valuePredicate on every value reached by logic:valuePath."
msgstr "一个 logic:PathValueTypeConstraint 固定值变体的固定对象：在 logic:valuePath 所到达的每个值上，logic:valuePredicate 所要求的对象（一个 IRI 或一个字面量）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/valuePath|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The path predicate of a logic:PathValueTypeConstraint: every value the focus carries on this predicate must be an instance of logic:valueClass."
msgstr "一个 logic:PathValueTypeConstraint 的路径谓词：焦点在此谓词上承载的每个值都必须是 logic:valueClass 的一个实例。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/valuePredicate|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The fixed check predicate of a logic:PathValueTypeConstraint's fixed-value variant: every value the focus carries on logic:valuePath must itself carry this predicate with object logic:valueObject (Q(v, o)), rather than being an instance of a logic:valueClass. Paired with logic:valueObject; mutually exclusive with logic:valueClass."
msgstr "一个 logic:PathValueTypeConstraint 固定值变体的固定检查谓词：焦点在 logic:valuePath 上承载的每个值本身都必须以 logic:valueObject 为对象携带此谓词（Q(v, o)），而非作为某个 logic:valueClass 的实例。与 logic:valueObject 配对；与 logic:valueClass 互斥。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ValueRangeConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Compact sugar for a numeric value-range constraint (P8): a logic:onClass target, a logic:valuePath predicate, and an inclusive lower (logic:minInclusiveBound) and/or upper (logic:maxInclusiveBound) literal bound every value on that path must satisfy. Expands to a canonical logic:Constraint ∀this,v. C(this) ∧ P(this,v) → min ≤ v ∧ v ≤ max and lowers declaratively to sh:minInclusive/sh:maxInclusive on the target class shape. It is the decidable, validation-only home of a bounded range — NOT an OWL faceted-datatype axiom, which the native reasoner cannot decide once a literal is asserted on the constrained path: it validates and never entails. Frontend-only authoring shortcut."
msgstr "数值取值范围约束（P8）的紧凑糖衣：一个 logic:onClass 目标、一个 logic:valuePath 谓词，以及该路径上每个值都必须满足的包含式下界（logic:minInclusiveBound）和／或上界（logic:maxInclusiveBound）字面量界限。展开为一个规范的 logic:Constraint ∀x,v. C(x) ∧ P(x,v) → min ≤ v ∧ v ≤ max，并声明式地下降为目标类形状上的 sh:minInclusive/sh:maxInclusive。它是有界范围可判定、仅验证的归属——而非 OWL 分面数据类型公理，后者一旦有字面量被断言到受约束路径上，本机推理器便无法判定：它进行验证，绝不蕴含。仅前端的撰写捷径。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ValueRangeConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:unitInterval a logic:ValueRangeConstraint ; logic:onClass ex:Probability ; logic:valuePath ex:magnitude ; logic:minInclusiveBound 0 ; logic:maxInclusiveBound 1 ."
msgstr "示例：ex:unitInterval a logic:ValueRangeConstraint ; logic:onClass ex:Probability ; logic:valuePath ex:magnitude ; logic:minInclusiveBound 0 ; logic:maxInclusiveBound 1 ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/VariableCollection|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A logic:Collection whose membership may change over time while the collection retains its identity — a club whose roster gains and loses members, a playlist edited over the years. The counterpart of gufo:VariableCollection. Stated in prose, not as a subclass edge. Its time-varying logic:memberOf is naturally carried as a logic:Fluent (membership indexed to time/world) rather than as the static membership of a logic:FixedCollection — the four-dimensional treatment of changing membership."
msgstr "一个 logic:Collection，其成员资格可随时间改变，而该集合保持其同一性——一个成员有进有出的俱乐部，一份多年间被编辑的播放列表。它是 gufo:VariableCollection 的对应物。以散文陈述，而非作为子类边。其随时间变化的 logic:memberOf 自然地被承载为一个 logic:Fluent（成员资格按时间／世界索引），而非作为 logic:FixedCollection 的静态成员资格——对变化成员资格的四维处理。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/variableSort|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Assigns an order-sort to a variable term-carrier: the reasoned class (any math:, logic:, or domain-slice owl:Class, not only the numeric tower) the term-carrier's bound variable ranges over, consumed to build the order-sorted unification context a backward-resolution engine unifies structured terms under. It is ONE case of a general sort-assignment pattern, not a variable-only special case: logic:variableSort is the named extension point where a future logic:functionSort (assigning a rank/sort signature to a function symbol rather than a variable) slots in, so nothing here precludes rank-sorted compound terms later. It is not a value restriction on an ordinary OWL property; it is metadata the typed-IR frontend reads to seed sort-checked unification."
msgstr "为一个变量词项载体指派一个序种别：词项载体的绑定变量所遍及的被推理的类（任何 math:、logic: 或领域切片的 owl:Class，不仅是数值塔），用以构建后向消解引擎据以对结构化词项进行合一的序种别合一上下文。它是一般种别指派模式的一个情形，而非仅限变量的特例：logic:variableSort 是命名的扩展点，未来的 logic:functionSort（为函数符号而非变量指派一个秩／种别签名）便嵌入于此，因此此处并不排除日后的秩种别复合词项。它不是对普通 OWL 属性的值限制；它是带类型 IR 前端读取以引导经种别检查合一的元数据。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Variadic|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The residue shape tag for an atomic predication whose argument arity is not the binary Horn shape: it carries a logic:SequenceMarker or a non-binary (unary or n-ary) argument list — the generalization beyond the fixed arity-three triple. Disclosed when a Horn-fragment target carries such a formula as flagged unsupported residue."
msgstr "针对某原子谓述的残余形状标记，其参数元数不是二元 Horn 形状：它携带一个 logic:SequenceMarker 或一个非二元（一元或 n 元）的参数列表——超越固定三元数三元组的推广。当某个 Horn 片段目标将这样一个公式作为被标记的不支持残余而携带时予以披露。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/VerdictEngineProduced|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The verdict-provenance value for a conjecture whose positive/negative cases were produced by a scoped reasoning run over the standpoint, not asserted by a reviewer: the defining mark of a logic:Conjecture against a plain logic:FormalizationCandidate. Wire value `engine-produced`."
msgstr "针对某猜想的判决出处取值，其正／负例是由针对该立场的、有界的推理运行所产生，而非由审阅者断言：这是 logic:Conjecture 相对于普通 logic:FormalizationCandidate 的定义性标志。传输值 `engine-produced`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/verdictProbe|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningProgram to zero or more atoms whose three-valued (true/false/undefined) well-founded verdict is projected as a standalone win/move-style check, rather than an answer-variable binding. Distinct from logic:programQuery: a probe reports which of the three verdicts an atom carries under the well-founded model, while the query resolves variable bindings for its single goal. Multi-valued; a program may carry no probes at all."
msgstr "将一个 logic:ReasoningProgram 关联到零个或多个原子，其三值（真／假／未定义）良基判决被投影为一个独立的胜负／走子式检查，而非答案变量绑定。区别于 logic:programQuery：探针报告某原子在良基模型下承载三种判决中的哪一种，而查询为其单一目标解析变量绑定。多值；一个程序也可以完全不携带任何探针。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/VerdictProvenanceKind|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The closed two-member value class of the logic:verdictProvenance facet: the one genuinely-new axis a logic:Conjecture adds over a plain logic:FormalizationCandidate — whether a candidate's positive/negative cases were ENGINE-PRODUCED by a scoped reasoning run or REVIEWER-ASSERTED by hand. Its individuals are logic:VerdictEngineProduced and logic:VerdictReviewerAsserted. The set is closed, so a misspelt provenance names no declared value and is rejected (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the conjecture-and-refutation section)."
msgstr "logic:verdictProvenance 特征的封闭双成员取值类：logic:Conjecture 相对于普通 logic:FormalizationCandidate 所增加的唯一真正新的轴——即某候选的正／负例是由有界推理运行引擎产生的，还是由审阅者手工断言的。其个体为 logic:VerdictEngineProduced 与 logic:VerdictReviewerAsserted。该集合是封闭的，因此拼写错误的出处不指称任何已声明取值，会被拒绝（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，conjecture-and-refutation 一节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/verdictProvenance|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Conjecture to the logic:VerdictProvenanceKind recording whether its cases were engine-produced or reviewer-asserted — the one genuinely-new axis the conjecture library adds over the candidate spine. Single-valued and REQUIRED. Domain logic:Conjecture, range logic:VerdictProvenanceKind."
msgstr "将一个 logic:Conjecture 关联到记录其各例是引擎产生还是审阅者断言的 logic:VerdictProvenanceKind——这是猜想库相对于候选脊柱所增加的唯一真正新的轴。单值且必需。定义域为 logic:Conjecture，值域为 logic:VerdictProvenanceKind。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/VerdictReviewerAsserted|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The verdict-provenance value for cases a reviewer asserted by hand rather than an engine deriving — the plain-candidate default, retained on the closed set so a conjecture may honestly record a hand-adjudicated case (e.g. a withdrawal) without pretending it was engine-produced. Wire value `reviewer-asserted`."
msgstr "用于由审阅者手工断言而非引擎推导的情形的判定溯源值——即纯候选默认值，保留在封闭集合上，使得某个猜想能够诚实地记录一个手工裁决的情形（例如撤回），而不假装它是由引擎产生的。线上值 `reviewer-asserted`。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/versionOfFunctionality|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Asserts on the canonical carrier that gmeow:versionOf is functional: a version belongs to exactly one lineage, as its skos:definition states."
msgstr "在规范载体上断言 gmeow:versionOf 是函数式的：一个版本恰好属于一条谱系，正如其 skos:definition 所述。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ViewSerializability|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:SerializabilityCriterion value satisfied when some serial order has the same read-from and final-write relationships as the history — equivalent on what each read observed and which write was last. A history property, not a protocol. Strictly weaker than logic:ConflictSerializability is not implied; the two are distinct criteria a history may satisfy."
msgstr "当某个串行顺序与历史具有相同的读自关系和最终写关系时所满足的 logic:SerializabilityCriterion 值——在每次读所观察到的内容以及哪次写是最后一次这两方面等价。它是历史的一个属性，而非协议。它比 logic:ConflictSerializability 严格更弱这一点并不成立；二者是历史可能满足的不同判据。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/violatedCriterion|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:SerializationAnomaly finding to the logic:SerializabilityCriterion it violates — the criterion (logic:ConflictSerializability or logic:ViewSerializability) under which the history admits no equivalent serial execution. Domain logic:SerializationAnomaly, range logic:SerializabilityCriterion (stated in prose). It names WHICH history property the anomaly breaches; it does not assert a logical contradiction (the schedule's final state may be perfectly consistent), keeping the finding a property of the history rather than of any state."
msgstr "将一个 logic:SerializationAnomaly 发现关联到它所违反的 logic:SerializabilityCriterion——即历史在其下不容许任何等价串行执行的判据（logic:ConflictSerializability 或 logic:ViewSerializability）。定义域 logic:SerializationAnomaly，值域 logic:SerializabilityCriterion（以散文陈述）。它指明该异常违背了历史的哪一个属性；它并不断言逻辑矛盾（该调度的最终状态可能完全一致），从而使该发现保持为历史的属性而非任何状态的属性。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Violated|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:SatisfactionStatus value for a goal whose target has failed — a maintenance goal that failed at some state of its interval, or an avoidance goal whose proscribed situation obtained. Stronger than logic:Unsatisfied: a violation is an active breach, not mere non-achievement."
msgstr "用于目标点已失败的目标的 logic:SatisfactionStatus 值——即在其区间某个状态失败的维持型目标，或其被禁止情形已发生的规避型目标。比 logic:Unsatisfied 更强：违反是一种主动的破坏，而非仅仅是未达成。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/violation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates an offending entity to the constraint it violates — a logic:Discipline (an OntoUML structural anti-pattern), a logic:MereologyConstraint (a profiled-mereology axiom such as logic:WeakSupplementation), a logic:OccurrentConstraint (an occurrent well-formedness axiom such as logic:OccurrentChangeAsymmetry), or a logic:QualityConstraint (a quality/quantity well-formedness axiom such as logic:MeasurementFrameMissing): the derived diagnostic the foundation lowering materializes, the logic: analogue of a reasoning_lint message. A logic:violation fact is never asserted by hand; it is entailed by the lowering rules over the stereotype, subsumption, mediation and parthood facts, so its presence is a machine-checkable proof that the entity breaks the named constraint."
msgstr "将一个违规实体关联到它所违反的约束——某个 logic:Discipline（一种 OntoUML 结构反模式）、某个 logic:MereologyConstraint（一条剖面化部件论公理，例如 logic:WeakSupplementation）、某个 logic:OccurrentConstraint（一条历现良构公理，例如 logic:OccurrentChangeAsymmetry），或某个 logic:QualityConstraint（一条质量/数量良构公理，例如 logic:MeasurementFrameMissing）：即基础下沉所物化的派生诊断，是 reasoning_lint 消息的 logic: 类比物。logic:violation 事实绝不由手工断言；它由下沉规则在构造型、包摄、中介与部件事实之上蕴含，因而其存在是一份机器可核验的证明，表明该实体破坏了所命名的约束。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/WeakPlanSuccess|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:PlanSuccessMode value under which a plan succeeds when SOME outcome path reaches the goal — the existential reading. The weakest of the three; contrast logic:StrongPlanSuccess (every path) and logic:StrongCyclicPlanSuccess (every fair execution, allowing loops)."
msgstr "使得当某个结果路径抵达目标时计划即成功的 logic:PlanSuccessMode 值——即存在性解读。三者中最弱的一个；与 logic:StrongPlanSuccess（每条路径）以及 logic:StrongCyclicPlanSuccess（每次公平执行，允许循环）形成对照。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/WeakSupplementation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The weak-supplementation axiom as a profiled-mereology constraint: a whole with a proper part must have another proper part disjoint from the first. It is enforced only within the logic:MereologyProfile a whole is declared under (logic:underMereologyProfile), never across all parthood; a whole with a lone proper part and no disjoint co-part, declared under a profile, is the logic:violation. The prerequisites logic:overlaps and logic:disjoint are settled first, so the axiom is never applied where overlap is undefined (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "作为剖面化部件论约束的弱补充公理：一个具有真部件的整体必须还有另一个与第一个不相交的真部件。它仅在整体被声明所属的 logic:MereologyProfile 之内强制实施（logic:underMereologyProfile），绝不跨越全部部件关系；一个在某剖面下声明、只有单一真部件且没有不相交共部件的整体，即构成 logic:violation。前提 logic:overlaps 与 logic:disjoint 先行确定，因此该公理绝不会在重叠未定义之处被应用（design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md，typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons 章节）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/WeightedRankingMeasure|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The uncertainty measure carrying weighted or ranking preferences over derivations. One member of the uncertainty-measure set facet (it may coexist with logic:ProbabilisticMeasure or logic:FuzzyMeasure); distinct from a calibrated probability — a ranking weight carries no probabilistic meaning unless one is separately declared."
msgstr "承载对推导的加权或排序偏好的不确定性度量。它是不确定性度量集合面的一个成员（可与 logic:ProbabilisticMeasure 或 logic:FuzzyMeasure 共存）；与经校准的概率不同——一个排序权重不承载任何概率含义，除非另行分别声明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/weight|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A solver or ranking weight — a numeric preference used to order or score derivations — not necessarily probabilistic and not an epistemic confidence. Normatively distinct from logic:probability, logic:confidence, and logic:evidenceStrength: a ranking weight carries no calibrated probabilistic or evidential meaning unless one is separately and explicitly declared."
msgstr "一种求解器或排序权重——用于对推导进行排序或评分的数值偏好——不一定是概率性的，也不是认知置信度。规范上与 logic:probability、logic:confidence 及 logic:evidenceStrength 相区分：一个排序权重不承载任何经校准的概率或证据含义，除非另行明确分别声明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/WellBehavedLens|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "An asymmetric lens: a structured-to-flat downcast with sound update. Caps: logic:GetPut and logic:PutGet claimable (logic:PutPut optional). The workhorse rung for a faithful but non-embedding projection."
msgstr "一种非对称透镜：从结构化到扁平的向下投射，并带有健全的更新。能力：可主张 logic:GetPut 与 logic:PutGet（logic:PutPut 可选）。是忠实但非嵌入投影的主力档位。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/wellFoundedMaterializerPlan|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The AUTHORED MODEL of the intra-engine phase sequence the native well-founded-semantics evaluator runs per world (crates/logic/src/wellfounded.rs materialize()): the canonical process model applied one scale down from the build pipeline (gmeow:pipeline-build) — an intra-engine pass sequence rather than an inter-stage DAG. Its logic:planBody is the root combinator logic:wfPhaseSequence, whose left-first walk yields the three phases materialize (logic:wfMaterializeEdb) ; resolve* (the logic:Iteration logic:wfResolveLoop over logic:wfResolveFixpoint, gated by logic:wfFixpointNotReached) ; construct (logic:wfConstructModel) — matching gmeow_logic::WELL_FOUNDED_PHASES. Because the middle phase is a logic:Iteration (a loop), this plan is OUTSIDE the certified acyclic DAG fragment by construction; that is correct and expected, so it does NOT run logic:executedUnderContract logic:DagWorkflowContract. Principle 12 BOUNDARY: this plan is authored SOURCE the parity gate crates/pipeline/tests/wellfounded_plan_parity.rs checks the Rust runtime against — the reasoner NEVER parses this RDF at scheduling or runtime; the native loop is the runtime, the plan is its declared twin. As a logic:Plan it asserts its own gmeow:SocialObject sort directly, the prose grounding of logic:Plan licensing no DL inference of it."
msgstr "本地良基语义求值器按世界运行的引擎内相位序列的作者化模型（crates/logic/src/wellfounded.rs materialize()）：即在构建流水线（gmeow:pipeline-build）之下一个尺度上应用的规范过程模型——是一条引擎内的遍历序列，而非跨阶段 DAG。其 logic:planBody 是根组合子 logic:wfPhaseSequence，其左优先遍历产出三个相位 materialize（logic:wfMaterializeEdb）；resolve*（凌驾于 logic:wfResolveFixpoint 之上、由 logic:wfFixpointNotReached 把关的 logic:Iteration logic:wfResolveLoop）；construct（logic:wfConstructModel）——与 gmeow_logic::WELL_FOUNDED_PHASES 相匹配。由于中间相位是一个 logic:Iteration（一个循环），此计划在构造上处于已认证无环 DAG 片段之外；这是正确且预期的，因此它并不运行 logic:executedUnderContract logic:DagWorkflowContract。原则 12 边界：此计划是作者化的源，奇偶门 crates/pipeline/tests/wellfounded_plan_parity.rs 据此对照校验 Rust 运行时——推理器在调度或运行时绝不解析此 RDF；本地循环才是运行时，计划是其声明的孪生体。作为一个 logic:Plan，它直接断言自身的 gmeow:SocialObject 类别，logic:Plan 的散文接地不许可对它作任何 DL 推断。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/WellFoundedProfile|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The well-founded semantics: a three-valued (true/false/undefined), total, polynomial-time semantics for normal logic programs that assigns a unique well-founded model even with unstratified negation, leaving genuinely circular literals undefined rather than branching."
msgstr "良基语义：一种针对普通逻辑程序的三值（真/假/未定义）、全域、多项式时间语义，即使在非分层否定下也赋予唯一的良基模型，将真正循环的文字保留为未定义而不进行分支。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/WellFoundedSemantics|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The model-semantics facet value selecting the well-founded semantics: a unique, three-valued (true/false/undefined), total, polynomial-time model for normal programs, leaving genuinely circular literals undefined rather than branching. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract; the deterministic counterpart of the non-deterministic logic:StableModelSemantics for unstratified negation."
msgstr "选定良基语义的模型语义面值：针对普通程序的唯一、三值（真/假/未定义）、全域、多项式时间模型，将真正循环的文字保留为未定义而不进行分支。在 ReasoningContract 上是单值的；是非分层否定情形下非确定性 logic:StableModelSemantics 的确定性对应物。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/wfConstructModel|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Phase 3 of the well-founded materializer (crates/logic/src/wellfounded.rs materialize()): the final reduct against the converged well-founded model W — least_model_of_reduct(reference = W), a HARD FAIL if the result's fact-key set differs from W (an undefined/partial model, unsupported in v1), then emit the derived non-EDB rows stamped with the world graph. The last elementary phase transition of the intra-engine plan."
msgstr "良基物化器的第 3 相位（crates/logic/src/wellfounded.rs materialize()）：针对已收敛良基模型 W 的最终归约——least_model_of_reduct(reference = W)，若结果的事实键集合与 W 有别（即一个未定义/部分模型，v1 不支持）则硬失败，随后发出以世界图盖印的派生非 EDB 行。是引擎内计划的最后一次基本相位转换。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/wfFixpointNotReached|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The loop-guard situation of the alternating-fixpoint phase: the double-reduct step has not yet converged — the new under-estimate K2 differs from the previous K by fact-key set (K2.key_set() != K.key_set() in crates/logic/src/wellfounded.rs). The logic:iterationCondition of logic:wfResolveLoop: the loop body re-runs while this obtains, and the iteration terminates when it ceases (K2 == K), at which point W = K is the well-founded model's set of true atoms."
msgstr "交替不动点相位的循环守卫情形：双重归约步骤尚未收敛——新的下估计 K2 在事实键集合上不同于先前的 K（crates/logic/src/wellfounded.rs 中的 K2.key_set() != K.key_set()）。它是 logic:wfResolveLoop 的 logic:iterationCondition：循环体在此情形成立期间反复运行，并在其停止（K2 == K）时迭代终止，此时 W = K 即良基模型的真原子集合。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/wfMaterializeEdb|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Phase 1 of the well-founded materializer (crates/logic/src/wellfounded.rs materialize()): seed the per-world EDB — collect world_edb_facts, echo the asserted rows, and load them (sorted-key order) into the seed FactStore that the alternating fixpoint starts from. The first elementary phase transition of the intra-engine plan; its successor is the alternating-fixpoint resolution."
msgstr "良基物化器的第 1 相位（crates/logic/src/wellfounded.rs materialize()）：为每个世界播种 EDB——收集 world_edb_facts，回显已断言的行，并将它们（按已排序键顺序）加载到交替不动点由此起步的种子 FactStore 中。是引擎内计划的第一次基本相位转换；其后继是交替不动点求解。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/wfPhaseSequence|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The ROOT logic:SerialConjunction of the well-founded materializer's phase plan: do the EDB-seeding phase (logic:leftOperand logic:wfMaterializeEdb), THEN the resolve-then-build suffix (logic:rightOperand logic:wfResolveThenBuild). Walked left-first, the combinator tree yields the execution order materialize ; resolve* ; construct — the program twin of crates/logic/src/wellfounded.rs materialize() and of gmeow_logic::WELL_FOUNDED_PHASES. The program root logic:wellFoundedMaterializerPlan reaches it through logic:planBody."
msgstr "良基物化器相位计划的根 logic:SerialConjunction：先执行 EDB 播种相位（logic:leftOperand logic:wfMaterializeEdb），随后执行先求解后构建的后缀（logic:rightOperand logic:wfResolveThenBuild）。以左优先遍历，该组合子树产出执行顺序 materialize ; resolve* ; construct——是 crates/logic/src/wellfounded.rs materialize() 以及 gmeow_logic::WELL_FOUNDED_PHASES 的程序孪生体。程序根 logic:wellFoundedMaterializerPlan 经由 logic:planBody 抵达它。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/wfReductEngineCapability|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The executional precondition on the actor the well-founded materializer's phase action schemas carry as their logic:capability: the least-model-of-reduct engine (crate::rule_ir::least_model_of_reduct) is available to evaluate a reduct against a reference fact set. The generic ability the native engine must hold to run any of the three phases — distinct from logic:wfWorldSeeded, which is a precondition on the world state, not on the engine."
msgstr "良基物化器的相位动作模式作为其 logic:capability 所携带的、针对行动者的执行前置条件：最小归约模型引擎（crate::rule_ir::least_model_of_reduct）可用于针对参照事实集合求值一个归约。是本地引擎运行三个相位中任何一个所必须持有的通用能力——与 logic:wfWorldSeeded 相区分，后者是针对世界状态而非针对引擎的前置条件。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/wfResolveFixpoint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Phase 2 of the well-founded materializer (crates/logic/src/wellfounded.rs materialize()): the alternating fixpoint of van Gelder — the double-reduct step U = least_model_of_reduct(reference = K) then K2 = least_model_of_reduct(reference = U), repeated until K2 and K have the same fact-key set. The body of the logic:Iteration logic:wfResolveLoop; the loop runs while logic:wfFixpointNotReached obtains and converges on W = K, the well-founded model's set of true atoms. The single ITERATED phase of the plan — why the plan is outside the acyclic DAG fragment."
msgstr "良基物化器的第 2 相位（crates/logic/src/wellfounded.rs materialize()）：van Gelder 的交替不动点——双重归约步骤 U = least_model_of_reduct(reference = K)，再 K2 = least_model_of_reduct(reference = U)，反复进行直到 K2 与 K 具有相同的事实键集合。是 logic:Iteration logic:wfResolveLoop 的循环体；循环在 logic:wfFixpointNotReached 成立期间运行，并收敛于 W = K，即良基模型的真原子集合。是计划中唯一被迭代的相位——也是计划处于无环 DAG 片段之外的缘由。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/wfResolveLoop|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The logic:Iteration combinator wrapping the alternating-fixpoint phase of the well-founded materializer: its logic:iterationBody is logic:wfResolveFixpoint (the double-reduct step) and its logic:iterationCondition is logic:wfFixpointNotReached (K2 != K). The loop is the program-level twin of the `loop { … break when K2.key_set() == K.key_set() }` of crates/logic/src/wellfounded.rs — the back-edge that places logic:wellFoundedMaterializerPlan outside the certified acyclic DAG fragment."
msgstr "包裹良基物化器交替不动点相位的 logic:Iteration 组合子：其 logic:iterationBody 是 logic:wfResolveFixpoint（双重归约步骤），其 logic:iterationCondition 是 logic:wfFixpointNotReached（K2 != K）。该循环是 crates/logic/src/wellfounded.rs 中 `loop { … break when K2.key_set() == K.key_set() }` 的程序级孪生体——是使 logic:wellFoundedMaterializerPlan 处于已认证无环 DAG 片段之外的回边。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/wfResolveThenBuild|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The inner logic:SerialConjunction of the well-founded materializer's phase plan: do the alternating-fixpoint loop (logic:leftOperand logic:wfResolveLoop), THEN construct the final model (logic:rightOperand logic:wfConstructModel). The suffix program of the plan's outer serial conjunction."
msgstr "良基物化器相位计划的内层 logic:SerialConjunction：先执行交替不动点循环（logic:leftOperand logic:wfResolveLoop），随后构建最终模型（logic:rightOperand logic:wfConstructModel）。是该计划外层串行合取的后缀程序。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/wfWorldSeeded|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The situation gate the well-founded materializer's phase action schemas ground on: the per-world store is selected and its asserted EDB facts are reachable (the sorted worlds list of crates/logic/src/wellfounded.rs materialize()). The shared logic:precondition of the three intra-engine phase schemas — the elementary phase transition applies only once a world is in scope."
msgstr "良基物化器的相位动作模式所依据的情形闸门：每个世界的存储已被选定且其已断言的 EDB 事实可达（crates/logic/src/wellfounded.rs materialize() 的已排序世界列表）。是三个引擎内相位模式共享的 logic:precondition——基本相位转换仅在某个世界进入作用域后才适用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/withdrawalReason|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The author's free-text rationale recorded when a logic:Conjecture is retired to logic:ConjectureWithdrawn — the human note explaining WHY testing stopped, carried on the compensating author-withdrawal segment appended to the append-only conjecture library. Distinct from a found counterexample (which a refutation names through logic:conjectureRefutationWitness): a withdrawal is a deliberate authoring decision to stop testing, so this reason is a reviewer-asserted datum (the withdrawal carries logic:verdictProvenance logic:VerdictReviewerAsserted), NEVER engine-produced. Optional and single-valued; present exactly when a withdrawal names a reason. Domain logic:Conjecture, range xsd:string."
msgstr "当一个 logic:Conjecture 被退役为 logic:ConjectureWithdrawn 时所记录的作者自由文本理由——即解释为何停止测试的人工注记，承载于追加到仅追加猜想库的补偿性作者撤回区段之上。与所找到的反例相区分（反例由某次反驳经 logic:conjectureRefutationWitness 命名）：撤回是一项有意的作者决定，旨在停止测试，因此此理由是审阅者断言的数据（该撤回携带 logic:verdictProvenance logic:VerdictReviewerAsserted），绝非引擎产生。可选且单值；恰在某次撤回命名了一个理由时出现。定义域 logic:Conjecture，值域 xsd:string。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/withRestrictions|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:adultAge logic:withRestrictions ( [ xsd:minInclusive 18 ] ) ."
msgstr "示例：ex:adultAge logic:withRestrictions ( [ xsd:minInclusive 18 ] ) ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/withRestrictions|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Each list member is a facet record interpreted against the base named by logic:onDatatype."
msgstr "列表中的每个成员都是一条面记录，依据由 logic:onDatatype 命名的基础进行解释。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/witnessIndividual|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The individual a logic:ContradictionWitness records as forced to owl:Nothing — the entity whose type became unsatisfiable under the conjectured formula, identifying exactly where the contradiction bit. Single-valued, xsd:string (the individual's IRI as a string). Domain logic:ContradictionWitness."
msgstr "logic:ContradictionWitness 记录为被迫归于 owl:Nothing 的个体——即在所猜想公式之下其类型变得不可满足的实体，精确标明矛盾在何处咬合。单值，xsd:string（个体的 IRI 作为字符串）。定义域 logic:ContradictionWitness。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/witnessPremise|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A premise that participated in the contradiction a logic:ContradictionWitness records — one serialized triple (subject predicate object) per value, MULTI-valued because a refutation typically rests on several jointly-inconsistent facts. Together the premises are the minimal derivation the reader can replay to see why the formula is refuted from the standpoint. Multi-valued, xsd:string. Domain logic:ContradictionWitness."
msgstr "参与了 logic:ContradictionWitness 所记录矛盾的一个前提——每个值一条序列化三元组（主语 谓语 宾语），因一次反驳通常依赖若干共同不一致的事实而为多值。这些前提合在一起即读者可重放的最小推导，以看清为何该公式从该立场被反驳。多值，xsd:string。定义域 logic:ContradictionWitness。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/witnessRequiredViolation|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates an individual to an anti-rigid type it instantiates with no materialized counter-world to witness the anti-rigidity: the instance-level diagnostic the anti-rigidity lowering emits under the strict witness-required policy (LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md §Anti-rigidity needs a witness policy). For an individual x typed by an anti-rigid Role or Phase T in a world, if there is no other materialized world in which x exists but is NOT typed T, a logic:witnessRequiredViolation fact is entailed in the typing world; a counter-world that witnesses x existing untyped by T discharges the obligation and no violation is emitted. Unlike the default witness-obligation policy (which emits logic:dischargeObligation, an obligation rather than a violation) this policy treats a missing counter-world as a hard failure; the construction of the witness world itself happens on demand. It is never asserted by hand; its presence is a machine-checkable proof that an anti-rigid instantiation lacks the world of existence its anti-rigidity requires."
msgstr "将一个个体关联到它所实例化的、却没有物化反世界来见证其反刚性的反刚性类型：即反刚性下沉在严格的见证者必需策略下发出的实例级诊断（LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md §Anti-rigidity needs a witness policy）。对于在某世界中由反刚性角色或相位 T 定型的个体 x，若不存在另一个 x 存在但未被 T 定型的物化世界，则在定型世界中蕴含一条 logic:witnessRequiredViolation 事实；一个见证 x 存在且未被 T 定型的反世界会清偿该义务，从而不发出违反。与默认的见证-义务策略（它发出 logic:dischargeObligation，是义务而非违反）不同，此策略将缺失的反世界视为硬失败；见证世界本身的构造按需发生。它绝不由手工断言；其存在是一份机器可核验的证明，表明某个反刚性实例化缺少其反刚性所要求的存在世界。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/witnessWorld|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The world IRI the logic:ContradictionWitness was found in — the modal/context world within the conjecture's standpoint where the contradiction was realized, so the refutation stays world-scoped rather than asserted across all worlds. Single-valued, xsd:string (the world IRI as a string). Domain logic:ContradictionWitness."
msgstr "找到 logic:ContradictionWitness 所在的世界 IRI——即在猜想立场之内实现矛盾的模态/语境世界，从而使反驳保持局限于一个世界，而非跨所有世界断言。单值，xsd:string（世界 IRI 作为字符串）。定义域 logic:ContradictionWitness。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/WorldBoundary|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A scoped region within which the closed-world assumption applies: it demarcates where what is not derivable may be read as false, leaving the rest of the model under the open-world assumption. The scoping construct of the hybrid open/closed feature (LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md §Greenfield feature map): the closed-world (CWA) lane realized by the built-in SHACL is confined to what a WorldBoundary encloses, while logic: outside it stays open-world. Enforcement is seamed to the engine."
msgstr "封闭世界假设在其内适用的一块限定区域：它划定了不可推导之物可被读作假的所在，而将模型的其余部分置于开放世界假设之下。是开放/封闭混合特性的作用域构造（LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md §Greenfield feature map）：由内置 SHACL 实现的封闭世界（CWA）通道被限定于某个 WorldBoundary 所围合之物，而其外的 logic: 保持开放世界。强制实施与引擎缝合。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/WorldContextAxis|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The world index axis of the multi-dimensional context facet: a truth is relative to a logic:World (a Kripke-style possible world in the materialized contextual index). One of several context axes that coexist on a single result — world, standpoint, time, and path index the same result simultaneously rather than being alternative values of one slot."
msgstr "多维语境面的世界索引轴：一条真理相对于一个 logic:World（物化语境索引中一个 Kripke 式可能世界）。是共存于单一结果之上的若干语境轴之一——世界、立场、时间与路径同时对同一结果编制索引，而非某个单一槽位的互斥取值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/World|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A reified, named context relative to which truth is evaluated — a possible world in the Kripke sense, realized by GMEOW's materialized contextual index (standpoints, narrative reference frames, goal-, ought-, feared-, and counterfactual-worlds). Truth is world-relative and entailment is world-indexed: a contradiction within one world is a witness, a contradiction across worlds is not an inconsistency in the model. Carries a world-type taxonomy (epistemic, doxastic, telic, deontic, alethic, representational, counterfactual)."
msgstr "一个具体化的、有名称的语境，真理相对于它被求值——是 Kripke 意义上的一个可能世界，由 GMEOW 的物化语境索引实现（立场、叙事参照框架、目标世界、应然世界、畏惧世界与反事实世界）。真理是相对于世界的，蕴含是按世界编制索引的：一个世界之内的矛盾是一个见证，跨世界的矛盾并非模型中的不一致。承载一套世界类型分类法（认知的、信念的、目的的、道义的、真势的、表征的、反事实的）。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/BareEntitySortalAdviceConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "prefer a specific sortal over bare gmeow:Entity"
msgstr "优先使用具体的 sortal 而非裸 gmeow:Entity"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/BareEntitySortalAdviceConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The advisory logic:Constraint that fires a deonticRecommendation Note when an individual is typed bare gmeow:Entity without a more-specific top sortal (gmeow:Agent, gmeow:InformationObject, gmeow:PhysicalObject or gmeow:SocialObject). Its data-matching guard formalizes gmeow:Entity, and its logic:message is that term's gmeow:avoidWhen prose surfaced verbatim (bound by logic:adviceSourceField logic:ProseFieldAvoidWhen); authored at logic:severity \"Info\" — the never-gating advisory tier."
msgstr "当某个个体被类型化为裸 gmeow:Entity 而缺少更具体的顶层 sortal（gmeow:Agent、gmeow:InformationObject、gmeow:PhysicalObject 或 gmeow:SocialObject）时，触发 deonticRecommendation Note 的建议性 logic:Constraint。其数据匹配守卫形式化 gmeow:Entity，其 logic:message 是该术语的 gmeow:avoidWhen 散文按原样呈现（由 logic:adviceSourceField logic:ProseFieldAvoidWhen 绑定）；以 logic:severity \"Info\" 撰写——永不阻断的建议层级。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/EndurantAsEventAdviceConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "avoid typing an endurant as a gmeow:Event"
msgstr "避免将 endurant 类型化为 gmeow:Event"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/EndurantAsEventAdviceConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The advisory logic:Constraint that fires a deonticRecommendation Note when an individual is typed both gmeow:Event and gmeow:Entity — an endurant (a person, document or place) mistyped as an occurrence. Its data-matching guard formalizes gmeow:Event, and its logic:message is that term's gmeow:avoidWhen prose surfaced verbatim (bound by logic:adviceSourceField logic:ProseFieldAvoidWhen); authored at logic:severity \"Info\" — the never-gating advisory tier."
msgstr "当某个个体同时被类型化为 gmeow:Event 和 gmeow:Entity 时，触发 deonticRecommendation Note 的建议性 logic:Constraint——即一个 endurant（人、文档或地点）被错误地类型化为一次发生。其数据匹配守卫形式化 gmeow:Event，其 logic:message 是该术语的 gmeow:avoidWhen 散文按原样呈现（由 logic:adviceSourceField logic:ProseFieldAvoidWhen 绑定）；以 logic:severity \"Info\" 撰写——永不阻断的建议层级。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AdviceGuidance|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Advice Guidance"
msgstr "建议指导"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AdviceGuidance|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A first-class positive-guidance carrier: a queryable object that makes a term's gmeow:useWhen applicability prose machine-active, the useWhen peer of the avoidWhen anti-pattern logic:Constraint. It logic:formalizes the term it advises, names the harvested field with logic:adviceSourceField (logic:ProseFieldUseWhen), and surfaces the VERBATIM useWhen prose as its logic:message — bound to the source prose by the native check_advice_message_prose_binding gate. Unlike a logic:Constraint it carries no data-matching guard: positive applicability is not an anti-pattern to detect but guidance to surface when authoring the term's domain. The advice-coverage slice-quality axis counts a term's useWhen cell as covered exactly when such a carrier logic:formalizes it."
msgstr "一种一等的正向指导载体：一个可查询的对象，它使某术语的 gmeow:useWhen 适用性散文对机器生效，是 avoidWhen 反模式 logic:Constraint 的 useWhen 对应物。它 logic:formalizes 它所建议的术语，用 logic:adviceSourceField（logic:ProseFieldUseWhen）命名收割的字段，并将 VERBATIM 的 useWhen 散文作为其 logic:message 呈现——由原生的 check_advice_message_prose_binding 门绑定到源散文。与 logic:Constraint 不同，它不携带数据匹配守卫：正向适用性不是要检测的反模式，而是在编写该术语的域时要呈现的指导。当且仅当这样的载体 logic:formalizes 某术语时，advice-coverage 切片质量轴才将该术语的 useWhen 单元格计为已覆盖。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/adviceSourceField|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "advice source field"
msgstr "建议来源字段"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/adviceSourceField|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The soft-advice peer of logic:candidateSourceField, borne by a realized advice carrier — an advisory logic:Constraint (avoidWhen) or a logic:AdviceGuidance (useWhen) — rather than a governance candidate: names which annotation field of the carrier's logic:formalizes term (a logic:ProseField from the closed set) the carrier's logic:message must surface VERBATIM. The native verify gate check_advice_message_prose_binding resolves that field's current @x-gmeow-english prose and hard-fails on any divergence, so the machine-active advice can never silently drift from the prose it formalizes. A direct string binding, not a stored digest, because the message IS the prose. Deliberately domain-free — it is shared by both advice-carrier kinds, so it must not entail either type (an rdfs:domain would). Single-valued, range logic:ProseField."
msgstr "logic:candidateSourceField 的软建议对应物，由一个已实现的建议载体承载——一个建议性的 logic:Constraint（avoidWhen）或一个 logic:AdviceGuidance（useWhen）——而非治理候选：指明载体的 logic:formalizes 术语的哪个注解字段（来自封闭集合的 logic:ProseField）必须由载体的 logic:message 按 VERBATIM 呈现。原生验证门 check_advice_message_prose_binding 解析该字段当前的 @x-gmeow-english 散文，并在任何偏离时硬失败，因此机器生效的建议永远不会悄然偏离它所形式化的散文。这是一个直接的字符串绑定，而非存储的摘要，因为该消息就是那段散文。刻意不设域——它由两种建议载体共享，因此不得蕴含任一类型（rdfs:domain 会那样做）。单值，值域为 logic:ProseField。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/EntityUniversalDomainAdvice|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "use gmeow:Entity as the universal domain"
msgstr "将 gmeow:Entity 用作通用域"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/EntityUniversalDomainAdvice|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The positive-guidance carrier that makes gmeow:Entity's gmeow:useWhen applicability prose machine-active: use gmeow:Entity as the universal domain for anything that persists and can bear properties. Its logic:message is that term's useWhen prose surfaced verbatim (bound by logic:adviceSourceField logic:ProseFieldUseWhen); the useWhen peer of gmeow:BareEntitySortalAdviceConstraint."
msgstr "使 gmeow:Entity 的 gmeow:useWhen 适用性散文对机器生效的正向指导载体：将 gmeow:Entity 用作任何持续存在且能承载属性之物的通用域。其 logic:message 是该术语的 useWhen 散文按原样呈现（由 logic:adviceSourceField logic:ProseFieldUseWhen 绑定）；是 gmeow:BareEntitySortalAdviceConstraint 的 useWhen 对应物。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/EventUniversalOccurrentAdvice|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "use gmeow:Event as the universal occurrent"
msgstr "将 gmeow:Event 用作通用发生体"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/EventUniversalOccurrentAdvice|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The positive-guidance carrier that makes gmeow:Event's gmeow:useWhen applicability prose machine-active: use gmeow:Event as the universal occurrent whenever something happens that bears participants, a time, a location, or sub-events. Its logic:message is that term's useWhen prose surfaced verbatim (bound by logic:adviceSourceField logic:ProseFieldUseWhen); the useWhen peer of gmeow:EndurantAsEventAdviceConstraint."
msgstr "使 gmeow:Event 的 gmeow:useWhen 适用性散文对机器生效的正向指导载体：每当发生某件带有参与者、时间、地点或子事件之事时，将 gmeow:Event 用作通用发生体。其 logic:message 是该术语的 useWhen 散文按原样呈现（由 logic:adviceSourceField logic:ProseFieldUseWhen 绑定）；是 gmeow:EndurantAsEventAdviceConstraint 的 useWhen 对应物。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AggregateConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Aggregate Constraint"
msgstr "聚合约束"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AggregateConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Compact sugar for an aggregate-comparison constraint (P6): a logic:onClass target, an aggregate over a path (logic:aggFunction, optional logic:aggDistinct, logic:aggPath), a logic:aggComparator, and a logic:aggCompareTo right-hand side (a compared property IRI, or a literal). Expands to a canonical logic:Constraint carrying both the honest reified FOL integrity and a structured aggregate satellite, lowered to a SELECT $this … GROUP BY $this HAVING(…) sh:SPARQLConstraint. Frontend-only authoring shortcut."
msgstr "聚合比较约束（P6）的紧凑语法糖：包含一个 logic:onClass 目标、路径上的聚合（logic:aggFunction、可选的 logic:aggDistinct 与 logic:aggPath）、logic:aggComparator，以及作为被比较属性 IRI 或字面量的右端 logic:aggCompareTo。它展开为规范的 logic:Constraint，同时携带忠实具象化的 FOL 完整性条件与结构化聚合附属结构，并降低为带分组和聚合条件的 sh:SPARQLConstraint。它只是前端创作捷径。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AggregateConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:minimumMembers a logic:AggregateConstraint ; logic:onClass ex:Team ; logic:aggFunction \"COUNT\" ; logic:aggPath ex:member ; logic:aggComparator \">=\" ; logic:aggCompareTo 2 ."
msgstr "例如：ex:minimumMembers a logic:AggregateConstraint ; logic:onClass ex:Team ; logic:aggFunction \"COUNT\" ; logic:aggPath ex:member ; logic:aggComparator \">=\" ; logic:aggCompareTo 2 ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ChoiceGroupConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Choice Group Constraint"
msgstr "选择组约束"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ChoiceGroupConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Compact sugar for a choice-group cardinality constraint (P1): a logic:onClass target, a set of logic:choicePredicate predicates, and a logic:choiceMode ('exactly-one', 'at-most-one', or the 'exactly-one-of-N' alias of 'exactly-one'). The compiler expands it into a canonical logic:Constraint whose integrity is the XOR / at-most formula over the ∃-requiredness of each predicate. Frontend-only: it is not a new node kind, only an authoring shortcut."
msgstr "选择组基数约束（P1）的紧凑语法糖：包含一个 logic:onClass 目标、一组 logic:choicePredicate 谓词，以及 logic:choiceMode（'exactly-one'、'at-most-one'，或作为 'exactly-one' 别名的 'exactly-one-of-N'）。编译器将其展开为规范的 logic:Constraint，其完整性条件是各谓词存在性要求之上的异或或至多公式。它仅供前端创作使用，不是新的节点类型。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ChoiceGroupConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:contactChoice a logic:ChoiceGroupConstraint ; logic:onClass ex:Contact ; logic:choicePredicate ex:email, ex:phone ; logic:choiceMode \"exactly-one\" ."
msgstr "例如：ex:contactChoice a logic:ChoiceGroupConstraint ; logic:onClass ex:Contact ; logic:choicePredicate ex:email, ex:phone ; logic:choiceMode \"exactly-one\" ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConstraintSugar|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Constraint Sugar"
msgstr "约束语法糖"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConstraintSugar|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "An authoring descriptor that the logic frontend expands into one canonical logic:Constraint with a reified integrity formula. A constraint-sugar record names a closed validation pattern and its parameters; it is not itself a logic:Formula AST node, so formula constructor checks never mistake validation metadata for an object-level sentence."
msgstr "一种创作描述符，逻辑前端会将其展开为一个带有具象化完整性公式的规范 logic:Constraint。约束语法糖记录为封闭验证模式及其参数命名；它本身不是 logic:Formula 抽象语法树节点，因此公式构造器检查不会把验证元数据误当作对象层语句。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConstraintSugar|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A logic:ChoiceGroupConstraint record can require exactly one of two predicates without being treated as either operand of the formula it compiles."
msgstr "一条 logic:ChoiceGroupConstraint 记录可以要求两个谓词中恰好出现一个，而不会被视为其所编译公式的任一操作数。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConversionTarget|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Conversion Target"
msgstr "转换目标"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConversionTarget|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A legal output language for a lowering: every emitted construct must inhabit this target, while anything it cannot express remains explicit flagged residue. It is not a logic:ProjectionTarget, which requests a presentation of an answer; a conversion target instead delimits the IR or dialect into which canonical content may be legalized."
msgstr "降低过程所面向的合法输出语言：每个发出的构造都必须属于该目标，而无法表达的内容仍作为显式标记的残留保留。它不是请求答案呈现形式的 logic:ProjectionTarget；转换目标限定的是规范内容可被合法化到的 IR 或方言。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConversionTarget|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "logic:RelationalCore a logic:ConversionTarget ."
msgstr "例如：logic:RelationalCore a logic:ConversionTarget ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CrossNodeConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Cross Node Constraint"
msgstr "跨节点约束"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CrossNodeConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Compact sugar for a cross-node co-occurrence / inequality constraint (P5): a logic:onClass target and two roles (logic:roleA, logic:roleB) that must, per logic:crossMode, either 'co-occur' (be present together) or 'differ' (never bind the same value). Expands to a canonical logic:Constraint whose integrity is the bi-implication (co-occur) or the join + inequality (differ, via the logic:termEqual filter relation). Frontend-only authoring shortcut."
msgstr "跨节点共现或不等约束（P5）的紧凑语法糖：包含一个 logic:onClass 目标和两个角色（logic:roleA、logic:roleB）；依照 logic:crossMode，它们必须或者 'co-occur'（共同出现），或者 'differ'（永不绑定同一值）。它展开为规范的 logic:Constraint，其完整性条件是双蕴含（co-occur），或通过 logic:termEqual 过滤关系形成的连接加不等式（differ）。它只是前端创作捷径。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CrossNodeConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:reviewRoles a logic:CrossNodeConstraint ; logic:onClass ex:Review ; logic:roleA ex:author ; logic:roleB ex:reviewer ; logic:crossMode \"differ\" ."
msgstr "例如：ex:reviewRoles a logic:CrossNodeConstraint ; logic:onClass ex:Review ; logic:roleA ex:author ; logic:roleB ex:reviewer ; logic:crossMode \"differ\" ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DisjunctiveRequirednessConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Disjunctive Requiredness Constraint"
msgstr "析取必需性约束"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DisjunctiveRequirednessConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Compact sugar for a disjunctive-requiredness constraint (P3): a logic:onClass target and a set of logic:anyOf predicates, at least one of which is required. Expands to a canonical logic:Constraint ∀this. C(this) → (∃p1 ∨ … ∨ ∃pn). Frontend-only authoring shortcut."
msgstr "析取必需性约束（P3）的紧凑语法糖：包含一个 logic:onClass 目标和一组 logic:anyOf 谓词，其中至少一个必须存在。它展开为规范的 logic:Constraint：∀x. C(x) → (∃p1 ∨ … ∨ ∃pn)。它只是前端创作捷径。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DisjunctiveRequirednessConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:contactRoute a logic:DisjunctiveRequirednessConstraint ; logic:onClass ex:Contact ; logic:anyOf ex:email, ex:phone ."
msgstr "例如：ex:contactRoute a logic:DisjunctiveRequirednessConstraint ; logic:onClass ex:Contact ; logic:anyOf ex:email, ex:phone ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ForbiddenPatternConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Forbidden Pattern Constraint"
msgstr "禁用模式约束"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ForbiddenPatternConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Compact sugar for a forbidden-pattern constraint (P7): a logic:onClass target and a logic:forbiddenPredicate (optionally pinned to a logic:forbiddenValue). Expands to a canonical logic:Constraint ∀this. C(this) → ¬∃b. forbidden(this,b) (or the pinned-value form ¬ forbidden(this, value)). Frontend-only authoring shortcut."
msgstr "禁用模式约束（P7）的紧凑语法糖：包含一个 logic:onClass 目标和一个可固定到 logic:forbiddenValue 的 logic:forbiddenPredicate。它展开为规范的 logic:Constraint：∀x. C(x) → ¬∃b. forbidden(x,b)，或固定值形式 ¬ forbidden(x, value)。它只是前端创作捷径。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ForbiddenPatternConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:noDeprecatedCode a logic:ForbiddenPatternConstraint ; logic:onClass ex:Submission ; logic:forbiddenPredicate ex:deprecatedCode ."
msgstr "例如：ex:noDeprecatedCode a logic:ForbiddenPatternConstraint ; logic:onClass ex:Submission ; logic:forbiddenPredicate ex:deprecatedCode ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FormulaConstructorConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Formula Constructor Constraint"
msgstr "公式构造器约束"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FormulaConstructorConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Requires every logic:Formula to select exactly one constructor family: atomic relation, strong negation, conjunction, disjunction, material implication (keyed by logic:antecedent), biconditional, universal quantification, or existential quantification. It does not choose among serialized operands; it prevents one node from having two incompatible logical meanings."
msgstr "要求每个 logic:Formula 恰好选择一个构造器族：原子关系、强否定、合取、析取、实质蕴含（由 logic:antecedent 标识）、双条件、全称量化或存在量化。它不在已序列化的操作数之间作选择；它防止同一节点同时具有两种不相容的逻辑含义。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FormulaConstructorConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A node with both logic:relation and logic:not violates this constraint because it cannot be both an atom and a negation."
msgstr "同时具有 logic:relation 与 logic:not 的节点违反此约束，因为它不能既是原子又是否定。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GuardedImplicationConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Guarded Implication Constraint"
msgstr "受守卫蕴含约束"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GuardedImplicationConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Compact sugar for a guarded-implication constraint (P2): a logic:onClass target, a logic:trigger predicate (optionally pinned to a logic:triggerValue), and one or more logic:requires companion predicates. Expands to a canonical logic:Constraint ∀this. C(this) ∧ trigger(this, …) → ∃ companion. Frontend-only authoring shortcut."
msgstr "受守卫蕴含约束（P2）的紧凑语法糖：包含一个 logic:onClass 目标、一个可由 logic:triggerValue 固定的 logic:trigger 谓词，以及一个或多个 logic:requires 伴随谓词。它展开为规范的 logic:Constraint：∀x. C(x) ∧ trigger(x, …) → ∃y。它只是前端创作捷径。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GuardedImplicationConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:datedApproval a logic:GuardedImplicationConstraint ; logic:onClass ex:Submission ; logic:trigger ex:approved ; logic:requires ex:approvalDate ."
msgstr "例如：ex:datedApproval a logic:GuardedImplicationConstraint ; logic:onClass ex:Submission ; logic:trigger ex:approved ; logic:requires ex:approvalDate ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ImplicationAntecedentConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Implication Antecedent Constraint"
msgstr "蕴含前件约束"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ImplicationAntecedentConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Requires a logic:Formula carrying logic:consequent to carry logic:antecedent as the ordered first operand of the same material implication. It is not an inverse entailment from conclusion to premise; it is the reverse structural completeness check for the serialized pair."
msgstr "要求携带 logic:consequent 的 logic:Formula 同时携带 logic:antecedent，作为同一实质蕴含中有序的第一个操作数。它不是从结论到前提的逆向蕴涵，而是对已序列化有序对进行的反向结构完整性检查。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ImplicationAntecedentConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A formula node with a consequent formula but no antecedent formula violates this constraint."
msgstr "具有后件公式但没有前件公式的公式节点违反此约束。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ImplicationConsequentConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Implication Consequent Constraint"
msgstr "蕴含后件约束"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ImplicationConsequentConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Requires a logic:Formula carrying logic:antecedent to carry logic:consequent as the ordered second operand of the same material implication. It is not a rule that derives a consequent; it is a structural integrity condition on the implication node."
msgstr "要求携带 logic:antecedent 的 logic:Formula 同时携带 logic:consequent，作为同一实质蕴含中有序的第二个操作数。它不是推导后件的规则，而是施加于蕴含节点的结构完整性条件。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ImplicationConsequentConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "An implication node with an antecedent atom but no consequent formula violates this constraint."
msgstr "具有前件原子但没有后件公式的蕴含节点违反此约束。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/LiteralDatatypeConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Literal Datatype Constraint"
msgstr "字面量数据类型约束"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/LiteralDatatypeConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Requires a carrier with logic:termLiteralDatatype to carry logic:termLiteral, so a datatype IRI can never float without the lexical literal it types. It does not require a datatype for every literal; absence denotes a plain literal."
msgstr "要求具有 logic:termLiteralDatatype 的载体同时携带 logic:termLiteral，从而避免数据类型 IRI 脱离其所类型化的词法字面量而孤立存在。它不要求每个字面量都有数据类型；缺省表示普通字面量。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/LiteralDatatypeConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A carrier with logic:termLiteralDatatype xsd:integer but no logic:termLiteral violates this constraint."
msgstr "具有 logic:termLiteralDatatype xsd:integer 但没有 logic:termLiteral 的载体违反此约束。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PathValueTypeConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Path Value Type Constraint"
msgstr "路径值类型约束"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PathValueTypeConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Compact sugar for a path-value type-membership constraint (P4): a logic:onClass target, a logic:valuePath predicate, and a required logic:valueClass. Expands to a canonical logic:Constraint ∀this. C(this) → ∀v. P(this,v) → D(v). Frontend-only authoring shortcut."
msgstr "路径值类型成员约束（P4）的紧凑语法糖：包含一个 logic:onClass 目标、一个 logic:valuePath 谓词和必需的 logic:valueClass。它展开为规范的 logic:Constraint：∀x. C(x) → ∀v. P(x,v) → D(v)。它只是前端创作捷径。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PathValueTypeConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "ex:memberType a logic:PathValueTypeConstraint ; logic:onClass ex:Team ; logic:valuePath ex:member ; logic:valueClass ex:Person ."
msgstr "例如：ex:memberType a logic:PathValueTypeConstraint ; logic:onClass ex:Team ; logic:valuePath ex:member ; logic:valueClass ex:Person ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Rule|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Rule"
msgstr "规则"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Rule|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A productive Horn or stratified-negation derivation whose logic:head is entailed when every positive logic:body atom holds, every logic:negatedBody atom is absent in its declared closure, and every guard succeeds. It is not a general logic:Formula or an integrity logic:Constraint: constructs outside the rule fragment remain formula trees and are carried as projection residue rather than approximated."
msgstr "一种能产生结论的 Horn 或分层否定推导：当每个正向 logic:body 原子成立、每个 logic:negatedBody 原子在其声明的闭包中均不存在且所有守卫都成功时，其 logic:head 被蕴涵。它既不是一般的 logic:Formula，也不是完整性 logic:Constraint；规则片段之外的构造仍保留为公式树，并作为投影残留携带，而不会被近似替代。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Rule|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A rule can derive ex:ancestor(x,z) from ex:parent(x,y) and ex:ancestor(y,z), with its variables bound positively in the body."
msgstr "一条规则可以由 ex:parent(x,y) 与 ex:ancestor(y,z) 推导 ex:ancestor(x,z)，其中变量在规则体中被正向绑定。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TermCarrier|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Term Carrier"
msgstr "词项载体"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TermCarrier|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "An atom's second argument can be represented by a carrier with logic:termIndex 1 and logic:termVariable 'object'."
msgstr "一个原子的第二个论元可以由携带 logic:termIndex 1 与 logic:termVariable 'object' 的载体表示。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TermCarrierIndexConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Term Carrier Index Constraint"
msgstr "词项载体索引约束"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TermCarrierIndexConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Requires every declared logic:TermCarrier to carry a logic:termIndex. It is not the list-level ordering check: uniqueness and zero-based contiguity are verified across all sibling carriers by the typed-IR frontend."
msgstr "要求每个已声明的 logic:TermCarrier 都携带 logic:termIndex。它不是列表层级的排序检查；类型化 IR 前端会跨所有同级载体验证索引的唯一性以及从零开始的连续性。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TermCarrierIndexConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A logic:TermCarrier with logic:termVariable 'x' but no logic:termIndex violates this constraint."
msgstr "具有 logic:termVariable 'x' 但没有 logic:termIndex 的 logic:TermCarrier 违反此约束。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TermCarrierValueConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Term Carrier Value Constraint"
msgstr "词项载体值约束"

